window.AKK_BEAUTIFUL_MOTHER_FORCE_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_BEAUTIFUL_MOTHER_FORCE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1","paragraphs":["\"Hey, wake up... Is she dead? Why don’t you check her breathing?\"","\"Qin Ji, you’re always egging me on to do such filthy things. I won’t do it.\"","\"I heard the other day that the Prefect brought back a group of Hu dancers from the Northern Governor. Those Hu women are stunningly beautiful, with snow-white skin and exotic attire—this girl matches the description. Could she be one of them?\"","\"Probably not. I’ve seen a few Hu dancers from afar, and their hair wasn’t pure black. Anyway, whether she’s a Hu dancer or not, we shouldn’t meddle. The estate’s been bustling with cleaning these past few days—must mean an important guest is coming. Maybe she’s already here, and this girl was discarded after being played to death by some noble. She was weak—just bad luck.\"","Qin Ji lowered her gaze at the woman lying half-submerged at the edge of the pond and fell silent.","The woman’s thick, unbound black hair spilled over her face, revealing only the graceful curve of her jaw. She lay face-down on the pond’s edge, her ink-dark tresses fanning out, while the hem of her ankle-length skirt floated in the water, exposing a slender, pale calf.","She was motionless, like the most vibrant lotus blooming by the pond.","The dancer lifted her eyes. \"Let’s go. No need to bother with this ‘beautiful corpse.’ Someone will come to deal with it later.\"","In these times, even commoners with their own households were as worthless as weeds—let alone concubines who could be traded like gifts.","A noble playing a woman to death? So what if she died?","\"Steward Sun has been harping on us not to slack in our performances, or we’ll face consequences. Given his urgency, I’d say the guest is no ordinary figure.\"","\"Prefect Jiang is one of the most powerful men in Nankang Commandery. For him to be this tense, the visitor must outrank him.\"","\"I hope it’s someone truly grand. Even the scraps from their fingers could feed us for ages—not to mention if one of us catches their eye...\"","The two dancers chatted as they walked away, completely missing the slight twitch of the \"beautiful corpse’s\" fingers.","Dai Li felt as though she were floating among clouds until voices became threads, pulling her downward.","She heard people speaking.","At first, the words were distant and muffled, but gradually they sharpened—though they still felt unreal.","Governor? Hu dancers? Nankang Commandery?","As the voices faded, the threads yanked sharply, slamming her drifting consciousness back into her body. The surreal weightlessness solidified into reality.","A chill seeped into her bones. Groggily, Dai Li crawled out of the pond and looked around.","Birdsong mingled with distant chatter. Before her stood artificial hills, exotic flowers, and a vast pond dotted with lotus blooms, spanned by a winding pavilion bridge.","Everything was utterly unfamiliar, like a bizarre dream.","Dai Li pinched her palm and whispered in disbelief, \"How...?\"","Three years ago, after her husband died in a plane crash, she had raised their son alone, sending him from kindergarten to elementary school.","She remembered the day her son died—the sky had been heavy with dark clouds, threatening to collapse, though it hadn’t rained at first. She’d walked the little boy, his red scarf tied neatly, to the school bus and handed him to the teacher, promising as always, \"Mom will wait for you at home.\"","Soon after the bus left, the downpour came, hammering the earth like it meant to shatter it. A strange unease had prickled at her, but she’d brushed it off—until news came of the bus plunging from the river-crossing bridge.","The bright red scarf remained vivid, but its young owner would never return. When Dai Li jumped from that bridge, she’d felt only relief. She would follow the strange dreams to reunite with Zhou Zhou.","The sky was too dark, and you got lost. Mom couldn’t wait for you to come home, so she went to find you.","She’d thought it was the end. Yet now, the surreal surroundings and the sharp pain in her palm told her this dreamlike world was real.","Was there truly another world beneath the river?","Or could the dead carry their memories and bodies elsewhere?","Dai Li had no answers.","But a thought swept through her like a storm, like a spring rain reviving all that was withered—","If she could wake here, maybe her child could too. Those strange, recurring dreams might have been omens after all.","My son must be here!","The possibility sent a shiver through her, a surge of determination straightening her spine and piecing her shattered mind back together.","A breeze brushed her damp skin, and she sneezed. The pond’s chill had seeped into her bones. Shivering, she staggered to her feet. Her limbs were stiff, but her foggy mind cleared slightly.","Had those voices been real? If so, her situation was dire...","Hu dancers, performances, guests, nobles.","They hadn’t been frightened by a \"corpse,\" only startled and annoyed. Were they unafraid of death, or was it just commonplace?","Dai Li suspected the latter.","That was a bad sign. If even delicate performers could dismiss a body so casually, what of guards or servants?","This might be a ruthless era.","Her shoes and the lower half of her dress were soaked. Dai Li wrung out the skirt and stomped her feet. In her original world, it had been summer—she’d worn emerald-green lace-up sandals with leather soles. Now water squelched out with each step.","\"I need to change clothes. This outfit stands out too much.\" She glanced down.","The skirt was fine, long enough to cover her ankles, but her short-sleeved blouse was undeniably modern—not even close to the \"new Chinese\" style.","Recalling the direction the two women had gone, Dai Li reasoned they’d returned to practice. She could head toward the women’s quarters.","The garden was enormous, clearly frequented by the estate’s ladies—along the path, she spotted an apricot-colored handkerchief fluttering on a potted plant.","Dai Li’s eyes lit up. She snatched the cloth and secured it over her face with two black hairpins.","It wasn’t perfect, but it would do.","After a moment’s thought, she smudged dirt on her forehead. Now she looked like a dancer who’d fallen into the pond, too embarrassed to show her face.","Disguise complete, she pressed on. Her plan was sound, but as she left the garden, she realized she’d underestimated the estate’s scale.","The garden connected to a transitional courtyard with four arched gateways—one behind her where she stood, and three others ahead, to the left, and to the right, each shaped like a crescent moon.","Dai Li frowned and immediately dismissed the forward arch, focusing only on the left and right paths. Common sense dictated that gardens were typically situated at the rear of estates, so proceeding straight ahead would likely lead to the reception hall.","Left or right?","In ancient times, the precedence of left or right was not fixed. For instance, the Western Han dynasty revered the right, while the Qin dynasty and Eastern Han favored the left. Moreover, determining left or right required a point of reference—something she lacked.","Dai Li took a deep breath.","Fine, she’d go right.","Pavilions, winding corridors, and eaves soaring like beaks—the further she walked, the more astonished she became. This estate was far more opulent than she had imagined, suggesting its owner was not merely wealthy but also of noble standing.","Whether by luck or because the household was preoccupied with other matters, she encountered no one as she traversed two long corridors.","A stroke of fortune.","After walking further, she arrived at the entrance of a pavilion courtyard. The buildings she had seen thus far were grand, and this was no exception. Dai Li couldn’t determine whether this was the women’s quarters.","A breeze brushed past, lifting the hem of her damp skirt against her calves. Pressing her lips together, she stepped inside.","Before entering, she had braced herself to encounter others and prepared an excuse. Yet, to her surprise, the vast, elegant courtyard was eerily silent—save for a few birds chirping, there was no other sound.","Dai Li scanned her surroundings again. \"No one? Something feels off...\"","But at this point, she had no choice. The absence of people suited her just fine. She quickly crossed the pavilion’s front courtyard.","The courtyard appeared to be a single-section estate. Beyond the front courtyard, low buildings flanked both sides, framing the central main hall.","Dai Li bypassed the main hall and headed toward the right-side building. The door was unlocked, and with a gentle push, a faint creak revealed the interior.","Inside, a square table stood in the center, paintings adorned the walls, and a half-height vase in the corner held vibrant fresh flowers. A beaded curtain draped over a small arched doorway leading to the inner chamber. The air carried a pleasant fragrance, faintly floral.","This was undoubtedly a meticulously arranged residence.","Silence stretched, the birdsong outside now muffled. Dai Li quietly closed the door and ventured further inside. The inner chamber was a sleeping area, and given the care taken with the outer furnishings, she suspected spare clothing might be stored here.","The clothing chests were easy to locate. She opened them all, only to find robes in shades of gray, black, and blue—straight or curved hemlines, accompanied by headwear, belts adorned with jade pendants, and even boots and socks.","From head to toe, nothing was overlooked—but every item was men’s attire.","Dai Li’s delicate brows furrowed as she hesitated.","The clothes were clean, but if she were caught wearing men’s garments, it would be an unmistakable sign of her suspicious identity.","With distinguished guests arriving at the estate, an unknown figure appearing at this critical moment would at the very least warrant her arrest.","Just as she wavered, she suddenly heard voices outside.","Footsteps, chatter—not just one or two people, but what sounded like a group approaching.","\"My lord, the carriages and luggage have been arranged in the neighboring courtyard. Both this residence and the adjacent one were prepared by my elder brother for your stay. You and your retinue have traveled far—please rest here. Servants will arrive shortly for your convenience, though you may dismiss them if they displease you. As for your Xuanxiao Cavalry stationed outside the city, my brother has dispatched provisions, including a hundred sheep, to ensure your soldiers are well-fed and rested. The evening banquet is set for the end of the Shen hour. My brother and I will await your esteemed presence in the main hall.\" The speaker paused, as if feeling his words insufficient, then added, \"Should there be any oversight in our hospitality, we humbly ask for your guidance.\"","His tone bordered on obsequious, sending a chill down Dai Li’s spine—not only because of the approaching crowd but also due to the title used.","Straight and curved robes were attire from the Qin and Han dynasties, and this era followed the twenty-rank nobility system, with the highest rank being \"Liehou\" (Marquis). However, not all marquises were addressed as \"Junhou\" (Lord Marquis)—only those with monumental achievements or those who had risen to the position of chancellor merited the title.","It was then that Dai Li realized why this lavishly decorated courtyard was empty.","The household had cleared the premises to welcome their esteemed guest, ensuring no unnecessary personnel remained.","As for whether servants would be retained, that was entirely up to the guest. Given the absence of any attendants, Prefect Jiang likely assumed the lord would decline his offer.","\"Prefect Jiang has gone to great lengths. Please convey my gratitude to him,\" a deep male voice replied with practiced courtesy, his laughter ambiguous. \"Servants won’t be necessary. I’ve grown unaccustomed to being waited on during my travels.\"","Jiang Chongjiang nodded hastily. The smile on the towering man’s lips did nothing to ease the tension coiled in his chest. He only wished to fulfill his elder brother’s task and leave as swiftly as possible.","This man was no Dong Zhou, the chancellor who had clawed his way to power through political maneuvering in Chang’an.","No, this man had earned his highest rank through sheer military prowess.","The northern territories had once been plagued by chaos—Xiongnu, Xianbei, Wuhuan, and other barbarians descended like specters in the night. The northern reaches of Youzhou and Bingzhou had been dismissed by rulers as \"chicken ribs.\"","Chicken ribs—tasteless when eaten, yet a pity to discard. The land had been so barren that even the greediest mosquitoes could scarcely draw blood from it.","Yet who could have foreseen that such a desolate wasteland would nurture the fiercest of tigers? With jaws agape, this tiger had devoured the northern demons, his robust warhorses fueling the growth of his Xuanxiao Cavalry and laying the foundation for his forceful \"provisional\" takeover of Bingzhou a year prior.","Without exaggeration, much of the northern frontier now bore the surname \"Qin\"—his Qin, Qin Shaozong’s Qin.","A man of such ruthless ambition and iron-fisted methods was someone Jiang Chongjiang, who preferred a life of leisure, kept at a respectful distance. After exchanging a few more pleasantries to conclude the interaction, Jiang Chongjiang departed with his entourage.","Dai Li listened as the footsteps faded, but her tension didn’t ease—moments later, voices sounded again outside.","\"Jiang Chonghai is quite the smooth talker. Not a fool, it seems,\" someone remarked with a chuckle.","\"His family only rose to prominence in his father’s generation. For Jiang Chonghai to become a leader in Nankang Commandery, he must have some skill.\"","Dai Li’s nerves tightened. These men were clearly entering the courtyard, and from their conversation, there were at least three of them. The leader would undoubtedly take the main hall, leaving the other two to occupy the side chambers.","Her room would soon have an occupant.","Her gaze dropped to the men’s robes in her hands. Earlier, she had hesitated—now, the choice was no longer hers.","There wasn’t enough time to change.","Setting the clothes aside, she turned toward the open window on the other side of the room, intending to slip out.","But as she took her first step, a faint \"squeak\" escaped from her waterlogged sandals.","She froze.","Surely they hadn’t heard. She had closed the door, and she was in the inner chamber while voices still carried outside. She tried to reassure herself.","After steeling her nerves, she resumed her path toward the window.","One step, two steps, three...","The carved wooden window drew nearer.","Just as she was two steps away from it, the outer door suddenly swung open. Dai Li's pupils constricted slightly, but before she could seize the moment to flee, a deep male voice erupted like thunder beside her ear:","\"Who's in there? Come out.\"","Dai Li felt as if she had plunged into an abyss.","She had been discovered? Even with a door between them, how had he sensed someone inside...","Footsteps sounded outside as if the person was checking whether the intruder was in the outer chamber.","\"Refusing a toast only to be forced to drink a forfeit.\"","A flash of silver shot inward, slicing through the beaded curtain with such force that it severed a string of hanging pearls, embedding both blade and beads into the wall behind the small door.","The dagger hummed with vibration. Turning at the sound, Dai Li caught her own terrified reflection in the cold, gleaming steel."]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2","paragraphs":["The blade hummed with vibration, and Dai Li's nerves trembled like a tightly drawn bowstring.","The curtain separating the inner and outer rooms was broken, leaving the space unobstructed, but she stood by the window on the opposite side, so she remained out of sight of the man in the outer chamber.","He could enter at any moment. Without hesitation, Dai Li slipped into the role of a servant: \"Forgive my intrusion, my lord. I am no trespasser—I was sent by the master of the house to tidy the bedchamber. I lost track of time and overstayed. There are still unfinished tasks inside. Please grant me a moment longer.\"","Unseen by her, the man in the outer room slowly arched a brow at her first words.","Her voice was pleasant—unusually so. It carried a natural, soothing gentleness, like warm water or a spring breeze. Though strained with tension, it was undeniably captivating.","Qin Shaozong stepped into the inner chamber without a word.","It was midday, and the sun blazed fiercely outside. The woman stood with her back to him, clad in a short top and long skirt. Sunlight streamed through the window, casting its glow on her nearly bare arms, revealing skin as pale as fresh cream—so white it nearly dazzled the eyes.","Her hands pressed against the windowsill, elbows slightly bent, as if she were about to climb out.","Just as Dai Li prepared to leap, a surge of overwhelming danger crashed over her already taut nerves, sending an inexplicable chill down her spine.","In the next instant, a large, well-defined hand reached from behind and clamped onto her upper arm.","The grip was firm, the man’s fingers splaying before tightening, causing the soft flesh of her arm to swell slightly between his knuckles.","Dai Li’s pupils constricted sharply. The last thread of composure in her mind snapped with an almost audible ping, freezing her in place.","His rough palm burned like a brand, searing her skin and scorching away most of her rationality.","I’ve been caught...","In moments of extreme fear, words often fail. Dai Li’s throat felt stuffed with dry straw—every breath scraped painfully, and no excuse would come.","\"Where were you planning to go?\" The man’s deep voice gave nothing away.","Dai Li stood motionless, silent. The hand gripping her arm did not loosen.","When no answer came, Qin Shaozong turned her around with a firm twist.","Her skirt fluttered as their gazes met across the scant distance of less than an arm’s length. Both froze for a fleeting instant—one in sheer terror, the other in stunned admiration.","Dai Li stood at 168 centimeters, not short for a woman, but this man towered over her by nearly a head, easily 188 centimeters or more.","Clad in black robes, his hair bound high, he had a sharply defined face with deep-set eyes. A small break in his left eyebrow lent him a fiercer air than most.","Faint lines at the corners of his eyes spoke of years beyond reckless youth, yet time had not dulled him. Instead, it had honed his presence into something deep and inscrutable—like the ocean’s abyss. His amber-brown eyes, fixed unblinkingly on their target, held the predatory stillness of a stalking tiger.","The sheer height difference pressed down on Dai Li’s chest like a weight. He loomed like a colossal tower, his shadow swallowing her whole.","She recognized his voice. Earlier, someone outside had fawned, addressing him as \"Lord Marquis,\" before he replied.","Of all people, I had to run into their leader. How do I talk my way out of this?","From Qin Shaozong’s perspective, this strangely dressed woman was nothing short of a surprise. She possessed striking peach-blossom eyes—dark as ink, whites pure as fresh snow—with a pronounced crease along the upper lid, forming a delicate pink fold.","Modern women’s short-sleeved tops often featured fitted waists, and Dai Li’s was no exception. The collar dipped into a small V, revealing a crescent of collarbone.","The snug garment outlined her figure clearly—curves lush and graceful, neither too slender nor too full. Her damp skirt clung slightly, droplets occasionally gathering at the hem before falling onto her shoes, which were little more than interlaced green straps and leather.","Her toenails were painted a vivid red, like blooming plum blossoms against snow. Noticing his gaze, her pale feet shifted back slightly, as if trying to hide in the shadow of her skirt.","The moment stretched, each second elongating as if time itself had slowed. All surrounding sounds seemed to fade away.","The man’s scrutiny swept over her from head to toe. Dai Li felt his gaze was peculiar—intensely invasive, as if it had sharpened into a blade, and she were meat laid bare on a cutting board.","His grip on her arm remained unyielding—rough, scorching, impossible to ignore. A man of his martial build could likely snap her neck with one hand.","Dai Li dared not move, rigid as stone.","How do I explain my \"bizarre\" attire and my presence in a guest’s chamber with soiled clothes?","If I’m mistaken for an assassin or spy and dragged off for interrogation, how do I justify my origins?","Zhou Zhou is waiting for me. I can’t die here.","Before she could devise a plan, a sharp tug at her hair sent pain shooting through her scalp—the kerchief pinned with a clip was yanked away.","Qin Shaozong had assumed she wore the covering to downplay her striking eyes. He hadn’t expected much when pulling it aside, merely acting on curiosity.","The reveal, however, caught him off guard.","A straight, delicate nose. Lips red without rouge. Against flawless skin, her features were like a masterfully painted portrait—vibrant, breathtaking. Unlike the youthful charm of girls in their teens or twenties, she was a peony in full bloom: opulent, mature, stunning. There was a languid grace about her, as if such beauty were second nature.","Yet perfection bore a flaw. Qin Shaozong suddenly raised his hand.","Dai Li recoiled instinctively, her back meeting the cold edge of the windowsill—nowhere left to retreat. Trapped between the unyielding sill and the imposing man, she was caged in a tiny space.","When his hand neared her neck, she flinched. But instead of the expected lethal twist, his calloused thumb brushed over her forehead, wiping away the dirt that had smudged her face.","Cleansed, the woman’s features gleamed—and at the center of her brow sat a vermilion beauty mark.","If before she had been a dazzling peony atop a golden pedestal, that crimson dot elevated her further, adding an untouchable, icy allure.","Qin Shaozong’s eyes narrowed slowly.","The friction against her forehead was rough. Dai Li’s nape prickled with goosebumps. His touch burned, yet she felt as though she’d been plunged into an icehouse.","Meeting his gaze, she recognized something in those dark, swirling depths—something not entirely unfamiliar. And with a jolt, she realized:","I misjudged this from the start.","Perhaps due to this era’s disregard for women, or his own confidence in his strength, he hadn’t categorized her as an assassin or spy.","No—that look in his eyes wasn’t suspicion toward an enemy.","It was the gaze of a man appraising a woman.","Dai Li had never been subjected to such an intense, devouring stare—one that seemed intent on consuming her whole.","Back in her school days, the boys had been fervent yet innocent—whenever she caught them staring, they'd shyly avert their eyes. Later, at work, the men in her professional circle were refined and well-educated, their admiration always restrained and polite.","Qin Shaozong hooked a few stray strands of hair behind her ear, his fingers deliberately grazing the soft curve of her earlobe. \"Just took a tumble in the pond?\"","Dai Li struggled to articulate the whirlwind of emotions that surged within her—like a sliver of sunlight piercing through storm-heavy clouds, or an island rising beneath her feet to lift her from the abyss after a tsunami.","She had thought of a plan, a lifeline to escape unscathed—for now.","Lowering her lashes to avoid the intensity of his brown eyes, Dai Li murmured, \"Word of your esteemed presence spread through the manor. Everyone wished to serve you, so... a minor disagreement arose today. This humble one had no choice but to dirty your honored quarters. I beg your forgiveness.\"","Qin Shaozong towered over her. As the woman before him bowed her head, her ink-black hair cascaded like water over one shoulder, revealing a sliver of pale neck.","Utterly submissive. Utterly controllable.","Instead of withdrawing his hand, he let it slide from her ear down to the nape of her neck, measuring, caressing—like soothing a skittish animal. \"If you don’t get along with them, you needn’t return.\"","A shiver ran through Dai Li—this time, unfeigned. The weight of his palm against her neck felt like a shackle. Had she not kept her head down, the panic on her face would have been unmistakable.","She dug her nails into her palm, steadying herself before timidly meeting his gaze. \"But... this humble one overheard you say you dislike having attendants nearby.\"","A soft chuckle escaped him—whether at her transparent ploy or her supposed naivety, she couldn’t tell.","\"Exceptions exist,\" Qin Shaozong said, withdrawing his hand. His thumb brushed against his fingertips, as if savoring the lingering warmth of her skin. \"Your name?\"","\"Feng Chun,\" Dai Li lied.","Slaves had no registered names; masters bestowed them as they pleased. She was certain he wouldn’t question it.","His gaze swept over her once more, a brow quirking slightly. \"Feng Chun—'meeting spring.' A fortunate name. Wait in the main chamber. You’ll serve me later.\"","They were adults. In this context, Dai Li knew exactly what \"serve\" entailed.","\"Thank you for your favor. This humble one will strive to please you tonight.\" Her smile was radiant, brightening the room like spring sunshine—though it faded quickly. \"My robes are soiled. May I change and freshen up before returning?\"","\"Granted.\"","The weight in her chest lifted. She didn’t hide her relief, her eyes crinkling with genuine delight, coldness melting into dazzling allure.","Qin Shaozong watched her a beat longer.","With permission secured, Dai Li hurried toward the door. As she passed him, the delicate scent of freesia wafted in her wake.","The damp hem of her skirt brushed lightly against his black boots, leaving a faint droplet behind.","Just as she stepped beyond the threshold, his voice halted her.","\"Stop.\"","Dai Li froze. Her heart, barely settled, leapt back into her throat. Sweat slicked her palms.","Had he caught her lie? Changed his mind? Or had she slipped up somewhere...?"]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3","paragraphs":["Invisible serrations seemed to scrape against her taut nerves, and in that instant, Dai Li’s mind raced through a series of dreadful conjectures, each one enough to send chills down her spine.","One breath, two breaths...","Dai Li slowly turned around, her head lowered. \"May I ask what instructions you have for me?\"","A shadowy figure loomed over her, nearly enveloping her entirely. Startled, Dai Li barely stifled a gasp as soft fabric brushed against her cheek, carrying the faint scent of sandalwood.","It was a robe—he had thrown a long robe at her.","\"Put this on before you leave,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Dai Li drew a deep breath, exhaling silently. Fortunately, the robe had covered her face, hiding the storm of emotions that had just played across her features.","Outside the room.","Mo Yanyun and Yan San waited, exchanging idle chatter:","\"Why did His Lordship suddenly go inside? Is there something unusual about this place? Or did Jiang Chonghai secretly tell him about some treasure hidden here?\" Without waiting for Yan San’s reply, Mo Yanyun stroked his chin and added, \"But that doesn’t make sense. Offering treasures isn’t a bad thing—why be so secretive? Unless there’s an assassin inside.\"","Yan San shot him a sidelong glance. \"Are you the fool, or is Jiang Chonghai the fool?\"","Mo Yanyun bristled. \"Hey, what’s with you? Why must you mimic His Lordship’s way of speaking? Is it because you’ve been by his side since childhood, marinating in his influence until you’ve turned out like this?\"","Yan San responded with a cold glare.","\"Who’s in there? Come out... You refuse a toast only to be forced to drink a forfeit.\"","The two men tensed, about to rush in, when a soft feminine voice drifted faintly from within.","Mo Yanyun halted, clicking his tongue. \"And here I thought some reckless fool had dared to trespass. Turns out it’s just a woman offering herself. Hah, wasted effort. His Lordship has no mind for indulgence on this trip. Even if he did, he’d favor the handpicked beauties presented by Jiang Chonghai—what could some random woman possibly achieve?\"","Yan San loosened his grip on his sword hilt. But after a few moments, his sharp instincts kicked in. \"Why hasn’t she come out yet?\"","Mo Yanyun belatedly realized the same. \"Right, why is it taking so long? Usually, it’s over in a word. Yan San, why don’t you go in and check?\"","Yan San ignored his prodding. A mere woman was no threat—certainly no assassin.","After a while, the two men finally saw a figure emerge. When they got a clear look, both froze.","The woman appeared to be in her thirties, yet she carried an extraordinary grace—elegant, gentle, with a touch of cool detachment, like a peony in full bloom atop a lofty pedestal. She wore an unbound quju robe, its dark fabric draping over her like a sheer veil, yet failing to dull her striking radiance.","Dai Li had known there were others outside, and seeing the two burly men confirmed they were subordinates of the man inside.","She had no intention of engaging with them. With a slight bow as a perfunctory greeting, she swiftly walked past them and out of the courtyard.","Mo Yanyun’s gaze followed her until she disappeared, muttering to himself, \"No wonder. They say the greatest beauties hail from Luoyang and Chang’an, praised as peerless treasures found nowhere else. But in my eyes, this humble Nanjun County hides the real gems. Even the most celebrated beauties of the capital would pale beside her. Yan San, do you think that woman has any sisters?\"","Yan San remained expressionless. \"Lust leads to ruin. Just half a year ago, you were swindled by a female thief, left penniless and borrowing meal money from the rest of us. Have you saved enough silver already to make the same mistake?\"","Mo Yanyun waved it off. \"I’m not like that miser Jin Duole, clutching every coin like a lifeline. Gold and silver are meant to be spent—why not use them to win a beauty’s smile? Ah, His Lordship is coming out...\"","Even after leaving the guest pavilion, Dai Li’s heart continued to pound wildly.","She was out—she’d made it!","Though she remembered the way back, she chose a different path. Now that she had a \"legitimate\" identity, she needed to explore more of the estate.","\"Stop! Who’s wandering around here?\"","At first, Dai Li didn’t realize the call was meant for her—until a man in a blue robe hurried over. But the moment he saw her, his expression shifted from irritation to bewilderment. \"Who are you? Why are you roaming freely? Are you one of the new dancers from the West Pavilion? No, that can’t be—the West Pavilion only houses foreign performers.\"","As he scrutinized her, Dai Li studied him in return. His attire was simple, neither luxurious nor shabby—likely a steward or attendant, not the master of the house.","Such men were easy to handle. A name-drop of the right authority would silence them.","\"I am His Lordship’s concubine. My robe was soiled by tea, so I need a change of clothes. Could you direct me to where the dancers reside? I’ll borrow a set from them,\" Dai Li said calmly.","The man’s demeanor instantly turned deferential. Dai Li’s beauty left no room for doubt. He bowed deeply. \"My apologies for the earlier offense. If you need fresh attire, why trouble yourself with the dancers? Allow me to fetch a new set from the lady of the house.\"","Though a mere concubine stood leagues below a proper wife, her connection to a man of immense power—commanding elite forces and holding a noble title—made her untouchable. Even a steward knew better than to offend a woman who could whisper in such ears.","Eager to please, he expected gratitude, but Dai Li shook her head. \"No need. You wouldn’t know His Lordship’s preferences. I’ll go myself.\"","The man paused. Her words carried an intimate undertone, hinting at a closeness outsiders couldn’t fathom.","Seeing her insistence, he relented, carefully explaining the route to the dancers’ quarters.","Dai Li’s eyes gleamed. She then asked for directions to the West Pavilion, which he provided.","With a nod of thanks, she headed west.","Compared to other courtyards, the foreign performers’ West Pavilion felt softer, flanked by two lush apple trees. Even before reaching the entrance, Dai Li caught whiffs of perfumed powder and occasional laughter.","Stepping inside, her gaze quickly settled on two young foreign dancers in their early twenties. She introduced herself as a dancer from the East Pavilion, sent to borrow a robe.","The two women didn’t question her. For one, they were new to the estate and still guileless; for another, their clothes were provided by the household—lending a set was no great matter.","\"Do you have a color preference?\" one asked.","Dai Li initially wanted to shake her head and say no, but the words caught in her throat before she swallowed them back. \"May I go in with you? I’d also like to change out of these clothes while I’m there.\"","The young Hu girl nodded.","\"What’s your name? I don’t recall seeing you before,\" someone suddenly spoke from inside the room.","Dai Li turned toward the voice and saw a beautiful Hu woman, around thirty years old, leaning against the window frame, eyeing her suspiciously. Judging by the woman’s tone, Dai Li suspected she had visited the eastern quarters where the dancers resided and had met many of them before.","\"I’m a qin player...\" Dai Li noticed the woman’s lingering doubt and added, \"—a friend. My name is Songlan. I only arrived at the estate the day before yesterday, so it’s no surprise you haven’t seen me before.\"","The Hu woman pressed further, \"Where are you originally from? How did you end up as a dancer?\"","Whether in the eastern or western quarters, the women who lived there were all entertainers of little importance—the governor’s personal concubines did not reside here.","Following the young Hu girl inside, Dai Li answered smoothly as they walked, \"I’m from the south. I traveled north with my husband for trade, but we were ambushed by bandits along the way. Everyone in my family was killed except for me. Later, I was rescued by a group of escorts and, after many twists and turns, ended up here. The governor hasn’t arranged for me to move yet, so I suppose he has other plans for me.\"","The inner room held several clothing chests. After looking through them, Dai Li finally chose a gray-blue dress.","\"Are you sure about this one? Isn’t it too plain?\" the young Hu girl muttered.","\"It’s fine. I don’t care for flashy colors,\" Dai Li replied with a smile.","Once she had picked the dress, Dai Li also asked for a pair of round-toe silk shoes and changed into them on the spot. She wrapped her modern clothes and sandals in the wide-sleeved robe she had been wearing, tying the sleeves into a bundle.","\"What’s your name?\" Dai Li asked the Hu girl who had lent her the clothes.","The girl’s eyes brightened, and she eagerly answered, \"Mijia. My name is Mijia. Don’t... forget me in the future.\"","Dai Li caught the underlying meaning in her words. \"Of course. Mijia, do you have rice powder here?\"","She had initially wanted to ask for lead powder but remembered that in this era, lead-based makeup was expensive—only noblewomen could afford it, so it wouldn’t be found in a dancer’s quarters. Without lead powder, she had to settle for the cheaper alternative: rice powder, though its effect wasn’t as good.","Mijia nodded and said she had some. She assumed Dai Li intended to apply makeup, but after handing over the powder box, she was surprised when Dai Li didn’t use it immediately. Instead, she wrapped a small amount in a handkerchief.","\"Thank you. If I get the chance, I’ll repay you,\" Dai Li said with a smile.","Mijia was overjoyed, instantly forgetting the slight suspicion she had harbored.","Dai Li glanced around and lowered her voice. \"Mijia, do you know if there are any young servants, around nine years old, working odd jobs in the estate? Where do they usually stay?\"","The abrupt change in topic caught Mijia off guard. After a pause, she shook her head. \"I haven’t been here long, so there’s still much I don’t know.\"","No unexpected luck came her way. Dai Li nodded calmly. \"The steward is waiting for me. I should head back now.\"","After leaving the western quarters, Dai Li made her way to the rear garden. Once she confirmed no one was around, she tossed the cumbersome bundle behind a large potted plant before turning away as if nothing had happened and heading toward the eastern quarters where the dancers lived.","The main hall of the estate.","The golden sun dipped westward, its fading brilliance slanting into the hall, casting a warm glow over the meticulously decorated space and the lively scene of toasting guests.","At an ordinary banquet, the host would naturally occupy the seat of honor. But today was an exception—two long tables were placed side by side at the head of the hall, one on the left and one on the right. In this era, the left side held greater prestige, yet the person seated there was not the estate’s master.","A tall, imposing man held a wine cup in his right hand as he spoke with the round-faced estate master beside him.","Jiang Chonghai nodded repeatedly. \"That Salt Smuggler Li is ruthless and has trampled on innocent lives for far too long. The people near Ying County have suffered greatly under his cruelty. For you, my lord, to travel all this way to rid them of such a scourge is an act of profound benevolence and compassion. I am truly in awe.\"","Qin Shaozong’s gaze swept casually over Jiang Chonghai. He noticed the man’s free hand—his index finger nervously picking at the skin around his thumbnail. Whether from excessive force or prolonged habit, the edges of his nail had turned faintly red.","Jiang Chonghai noticed and instinctively tucked his hand into his wide sleeve. When he looked up again, intending to brush it off with a lighthearted remark, he found Qin Shaozong’s attention already elsewhere, as if that earlier glance had been nothing more than a passing distraction.","The ever-smiling Jiang Chonghai paused briefly before resuming his jovial expression, though a trace of scrutiny flickered in his eyes.","Qin Shaozong continued their conversation. After several rounds of drinks, the man suddenly set his cup down on the table. \"Governor Jiang, there’s something I’d like to discuss with you.\"","Jiang Chonghai straightened. \"Please speak freely, my lord.\"","Qin Shaozong said, \"Among the dancers in your rear quarters, there’s one named Feng Chun. She has caught my eye. Would you be willing to part with her?\""]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4","paragraphs":["Jiang Chonghai froze for a moment, his heart initially settling—so it was just a dancing girl he fancied? He had thought it was something far more serious. But then doubt crept in.","Qin Shaozong had held sway over the northern territories for years, surrounded by beauties as countless as fish in a river. Could there truly be a dancing girl in his own household who had caught the man’s attention?","Feng Chun? He didn’t recall any outstanding dancer by that name.","Though puzzled, Jiang Chonghai didn’t hesitate. “A trivial matter. For her to earn your favor is the greatest honor of her life. Consider her yours, my lord.”","Qin Shaozong raised his cup with a smile.","As the golden sun vanished, the banquet drew to a close. Once the wine and feasting ended, Qin Shaozong departed with his retinue.","Walking alone down a secluded corridor, Yan San spoke up. “At tonight’s banquet, I observed two or three of Jiang Chonghai’s subordinates—their words were hesitant, their expressions evasive, especially when I probed further. My lord, it seems the Prefect of Nankang has no intention of fully aiding us in suppressing the bandits.”","Qin Shaozong’s lips curled lazily. “Not just unwilling to help—he’s likely plotting mischief behind our backs. Li Zan, that salt smuggler who rose from peddling contraband—where do you think he got his initial stock? From colluding with corrupt officials, of course.”","“But Nankang and Li Zan’s stronghold in Ying County aren’t even neighboring territories! They’re practically at opposite ends, separated by several counties. Could Jiang Chonghai’s reach truly stretch that far, crossing multiple borders?” Mo Yanyun questioned.","Yan San countered, “You’ve got it backward. It’s not Jiang Chonghai with the long reach—it’s Li Zan.”","Qin Shaozong added, “Li Zan now styles himself ‘Grand Marshal of All Under Heaven,’ boasting a force of a hundred thousand elite soldiers. A towering tree doesn’t grow without deep, tangled roots.”","Mo Yanyun still didn’t grasp it. “My lord, just because his subordinates seemed evasive, can we conclude he’s colluding with Li Zan?”","Qin Shaozong chuckled darkly. “Of course not. But he’s guilty of something. Find an opportunity to search his residence discreetly. I suspect we’ll uncover something interesting.”","Mo Yanyun didn’t understand where this “guilt” came from, but seeing the smirk on Qin Shaozong’s face, he found it odd.","Jiang Chonghai conspiring with the salt smuggler Li Zan—wasn’t that bad news for them? So why did the lord seem almost... pleased?","He didn’t know, and he didn’t dare ask.","The journey wasn’t long, and soon they arrived at their temporary quarters. The courtyard was brightly lit, and a soft glow spilled from the rooms—courtesy of the night pearls within.","“Unless it’s urgent, do not disturb me tonight.” With that, Qin Shaozong strode toward the central chamber.","Mo Yanyun and Yan San exchanged glances, both recalling the beautiful woman who had emerged from the side room that afternoon.","The door creaked open.","Light from within spilled over the threshold, pooling around the man’s black boots before scattering underfoot.","At first, Qin Shaozong assumed Dai Li was in the inner chamber, merely too shy to greet him immediately. But soon, he realized something was amiss.","The room was too quiet—unnervingly devoid of another presence.","He strode into the inner chamber, his brown eyes sweeping the space. Empty. No trace of that graceful figure.","She hadn’t returned.","Had she encountered trouble on the way? Or was it...","The latter thought flickered briefly before he dismissed it.","His title alone hinted at his status, and he’d promised her she needn’t return to Jiang’s household. He’d even asked for her name—she couldn’t have missed the implication that she might escape that life.","On one side: crowded quarters with countless dancing girls, performing endlessly for faceless patrons. On the other: silks and delicacies, serving only him.","Even a fool would know which to choose.","Qin Shaozong turned and walked out.","Mo Yanyun had been badgering Yan San with questions, neither having yet retired. Seeing Qin Shaozong return so soon startled them—had he forgotten some urgent matter?","There was indeed a matter, though not the kind they’d assumed.","“Mo—” Qin Shaozong abruptly changed his mind. “Yan San, go to the dancers’ quarters and bring Feng Chun back.”","The two men blinked.","So, not urgent business after all.","Feng Chun—that must be the beauty’s name.","“At once.” Yan San clasped his hands and left.","Qin Shaozong returned to his chambers, leaving Mo Yanyun standing alone in the courtyard.","The burly man with thick black brows muttered to the wind, “Seems this woman’s no ordinary figure, to make the lord seek her out personally at such a time... Wait, did he originally mean to send me?”","Mo Yanyun scratched his head.","The last sliver of daylight vanished, the sky drowned in ink. No moon, no stars—just an oppressive black veil stretched over the heavens.","Dai Li stood in a shadowed corner of another courtyard, watching a distant building with pursed lips.","This was one of the servant quarters she’d learned of. But her earlier search had yielded nothing.","Her child wasn’t here.","Was he simply not in this building... or not in this estate at all? She dared not entertain the latter possibility.","“Who was that woman earlier? I’ve never seen her before—so strikingly beautiful. A new stewardess?” A hushed voice drifted from inside.","“Always said you were naive. With looks like that, how could she be just a stewardess? Probably another concubine for the prefect. Everyone knows his weakness for beauties—constantly adding new faces to the household. The prettiest become concubines, the middling ones dancers, the plainest maids. That woman just now? I’d say she outshines even Lady Bin, the current favorite. The winds are shifting again.”","“What are you two whispering about? Who’s prettier than Lady Bin? I didn’t see anyone.”","“She was only here a moment. Gone now—missed your chance.”","...","After eavesdropping fruitlessly, Dai Li turned toward another servants’ compound.","Best to act while the trail was warm. If her son wasn’t there either, she’d need to plan an escape from this estate.","Yan San was efficient, but this errand took longer than expected.","Two quarters of an hour later, he returned.","Mo Yanyun, who’d been idly waiting for the moon in the courtyard, turned eagerly—only to see Yan San alone.","Where was she?","Yan San approached the main chamber but didn’t knock. Instead, he reported from outside: “My lord, the steward surnamed Sun from the rear courtyard informed me—there is no dancer named ‘Feng Chun’ among their ranks.”","Mo Yanyun’s ears perked up in shock.","No Feng Chun?","Then who was that woman they’d seen that afternoon? Appearing from thin air, now vanished without trace—some peony spirit in human guise?","The door creaked open.","Qin Shaozong stood framed in the doorway, backlit by the room’s glow. His face remained shadowed, unreadable—but the weight of his presence pressed down like a gathering storm.","Yan San continued, \"According to Steward Sun, there are twenty-six dancers in Jiang Chonghai's residence, including seven Hu dancers recently brought back from the Northern Prefecture's governor. Among these twenty-six, only three are over twenty-five years old—one Hu dancer and two Han women. However, none of these three have a vermilion mole on their forehead...\"","Mo Yanyun couldn't help but ask, \"Could it be that she isn’t a dancer?\"","A beautiful woman appearing in the inner courtyard—if she wasn’t a dancer, then the only other identity she could have was Jiang Chonghai’s concubine.","As soon as these words left his mouth, Mo Yanyun saw Yan San shake his head. \"No. I also ran into a minor steward surnamed Lin. Coincidentally, Steward Lin mentioned seeing the woman near the long corridor around the end of the Hour of the Goat. He didn’t recognize her and asked who she was. She replied that she was the Marquis’s concubine, and because her clothes had been accidentally stained by tea, she needed to change. She also asked him where the dancers of the residence stayed. At the time, Steward Lin didn’t suspect anything and truthfully told her.\"","Yan San added, \"I went with Steward Lin to the eastern courtyard where the Han dancers reside. At the time, apart from two dancers who had gone out for a walk and hadn’t returned yet, everyone else was present. But I didn’t see 'Feng Chun' there. When I asked the other dancers, none of them knew anything about her. They all claimed they hadn’t seen any strangers recently, let alone a beautiful woman with a vermilion mole on her forehead.\"","Mo Yanyun was dumbfounded, growing more and more confused the longer he listened.","If the woman was from the residence and as stunning as she was—standing out like a bright pearl wherever she went—how could the stewards not recognize her?","She claimed to be the Marquis’s concubine... That might be true, but why would she ask about the dancers’ quarters? The dancers’ residence wasn’t a secret; anyone who had spent some time in the residence and bothered to ask would know.","Could it be that she wasn’t from the residence at all?","But that didn’t make sense either. Earlier, when the Marquis had asked Jiang Chonghai for someone, he specifically named \"Feng Chun,\" and Jiang had agreed without hesitation, showing no signs of confusion.","Yet, among the Han dancers, there was no trace of her—no one even knew of her existence. Had she simply appeared out of thin air?","\"Have you checked the western courtyard?\" Mo Yanyun thought of another possibility. If she wasn’t in the eastern courtyard, perhaps she was in the western one. Otherwise, why would she ask the steward about the dancers’ quarters?","Yan San nodded. He had always been thorough and had indeed gone to investigate the western courtyard later. \"Yes. Someone there saw her at the beginning of the Hour of the Monkey. One of the Hu dancers said the woman introduced herself as a friend of Qin Ji from the eastern courtyard and gave her name as Songlan...\"","Mo Yanyun was stunned.","Songlan? Hadn’t she said her name was Feng Chun? How could she change her name in less than two hours?","But what shocked him even more was what Yan San said next: \"According to 'Songlan,' she was originally from the south. While traveling north with her husband for business, they were ambushed by bandits. After some twists and turns, she recently arrived at Jiang’s residence. Since she hadn’t been assigned a role yet, she was temporarily staying in the eastern courtyard. The Hu dancers in Jiang’s residence were all new and unfamiliar with the household, so no one questioned her. She borrowed a gray-blue dress and some rice powder from the western courtyard and left shortly after.\"","Mo Yanyun felt as though he had fallen into a thick fog.","Her name was fake, and her story kept changing. Who was she really? What was her goal?","\"She’s got quite the nerve,\" Qin Shaozong said with a cold laugh, his anger barely contained.","Mo Yanyun shuddered, his thoughts suddenly racing in another direction:","No matter who this woman was or why she acted so strangely, the fact remained—she had made a fool of the Marquis!","Who was their Marquis?","The only man in the court who had earned the highest noble rank through military achievements, standing shoulder-to-shoulder with the Three Excellencies. The man who had beaten the wolves of the northern tribes into submission, turning them into tail-wagging dogs.","After all these years, what kind of schemes hadn’t he seen? What kind of hidden daggers hadn’t he dodged?","Mo Yanyun could swear on his life that the last person who dared to play their Marquis for a fool had been chopped into pieces and reincarnated in a dog’s belly.","Admittedly, compared to the grand schemes they’d faced before, this little trick was nothing. But being outwitted by a woman? That was a first.","\"My Lord, perhaps it’s best not to pursue this matter for now,\" Mo Yanyun said quietly.","They had other business in Jiang’s residence, and given Jiang Chonghai’s hidden motives, they couldn’t afford to let a woman disrupt their plans.","Perhaps she had also assumed that, as guests, they wouldn’t make a scene in their host’s home—which was why she had dared to borrow the Marquis’s name for her own purposes.","Qin Shaozong let out a derisive chuckle. \"Afraid? If something this trivial is enough to make you tremble, we might as well abandon the hunt for the salt smuggler Li Zan and return home. You can hide under your blankets and save everyone the embarrassment of seeing you quake at the slightest challenge.\"","Mo Yanyun froze.","Was the Marquis... actually planning to settle this score with her?"]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5","paragraphs":["“What did you say? Qin Shaozong really said that? Are you sure you didn’t mishear?” Jiang Chonghai kept asking the man in front of him.","If Dai Li were here, she would definitely recognize the man being questioned—he was Steward Lin, someone she had met before.","Steward Lin nodded repeatedly. “No mistake. Lord Qin Shaozong did say that his beloved concubine went missing inside the mansion and that he wanted to search for her within the estate. He also asked you, Master Jiang, to be understanding.”","Jiang Chonghai’s younger brother, Jiang Chongjiang, frowned deeply. “A beloved concubine gone missing? When Qin Shaozong came, I accompanied them the entire way into the inner chambers. I clearly remember it was all men—where would a concubine come from?”","Steward Lin lowered his voice. “She must have been hiding in the carriage earlier, unseen. I later saw her myself. That lady is a beauty, with delicate features—clearly someone who’s been carefully groomed. And...”","Here, Steward Lin hesitated slightly, a flicker of uncertainty crossing his face.","Jiang Chongjiang’s curiosity was piqued by the pause. “And? If you have something to say, say it. Don’t beat around the bush.”","“If I’m not mistaken, she was wearing a pair of leather shoes made from cattle hide.” This observation was a coincidence; at the time, he was only trying to observe what kind of provisions Lord Qin Shaozong gave his beloved concubine.","A cow—a great beast. Farmers never kill oxen used for plowing. Usually, a cow would only be slaughtered when it fell ill or became too old to work the fields. Only then would its meat, hide, and tendons be harvested.","Of course, Jiang Chonghai knew full well that many rules meant nothing to the powerful and influential, especially someone as mighty as Qin Shaozong. If he wanted cowhide, even the strongest bull could fall ill on the spot.","If that woman truly wore a pair of cowhide shoes, she was undoubtedly Qin Shaozong’s favored concubine. After all, only a man of great means could afford to have his concubine wear such fine leather shoes.","“Send Steward Lin outside to wait,” Jiang Chongjiang ordered, waving him away.","Once the door was closed again, Jiang Chongjiang spoke. “Though we don’t know why a concubine suddenly appeared out of nowhere, it’s true that Qin Shaozong is searching for someone. Brother, at such a critical moment, could this be a deliberate act by Qin Shaozong? Might he have learned something and is now testing us?”","Jiang Chonghai stroked his chin with his thick, stubby fingers. “What you say is quite possible. Qin Shaozong is cunning and treacherous, full of schemes. When he took over Rong Bingzhou, he used a terrifying spy tactic. Who would have thought that Kuang Ye, who served under him for seven years, fighting and dying for him, was actually a planted mole?”","Speaking of the shocking defeat of Rong Bingzhou a year ago, Jiang Chonghai still felt a chill.","To follow someone loyally for years, shielding them from open and hidden attacks, even risking death for them, only to suddenly betray them—first eliminating their other trusted aides, then poisoning the lord, and finally seizing control and opening the city gates to the enemy forces...","If this happened to any other mighty lord, ask yourself—would they not be terrified?","The answer is, of course, yes.","After the news of Rong Bingzhou's fall spread, the various warlords were struck with deep psychological shadows. It was no exaggeration to say that during that period, paranoia was rampant—everyone lived in constant fear, and even the regional governors would occasionally cast suspicious glances at their own trusted aides.","Qin Shaozong had managed to embed a long-term mole right beside Rong Bingzhou, a spy who had quietly infiltrated the very core for seven years. Who could say he wouldn’t use such a ruthless, undermining trick again?","Who would be the next Rong Bingzhou? No one wanted to become the next Rong Gong.","Jiang Chonghai felt a chill run down his spine.","Jiang Chongjiang hesitated and said, “Brother, more than twenty people followed Qin Shaozong into the mansion. Now that he’s looking for someone, who knows if he’ll mobilize all of them? If we let them roam freely, won’t things spiral out of control?”","“It won’t,” Jiang Chonghai replied. “The only critical areas in the mansion are the study and the secret vault. We just need to reinforce the guards there. The rest of the place doesn’t matter.” He paced back and forth inside the room. “If they want to search, let them search. Don’t stop them. If they want the mansion’s soldiers and servants to cooperate, just have our people put on a show—no need to really exert themselves. We’ll keep things steady and see what kind of trick Qin Shaozong is really playing.”","Jiang Chongjiang smiled broadly. “Brother, you really have a way with these matters.”","*","Dai Li stood beside a small pavilion, hidden in the darkness of the night. She stared blankly in one direction, her eyes unfocused. Rather than watching, it was more like she was lost in thought.","In truth, Dai Li’s mind was in turmoil.","Just now, she had tried the same tactic—snatching a lone little servant girl for questioning. She had come with hope, hoping someone here would tell her—","Yes, not long ago, a strangely speaking little servant, about nine years old and roughly that height, had come here. He kept saying he wasn’t originally from this place...","But there was nothing.","This second servant’s quarters held no sign of the person she was searching for.","Her son wasn’t here. Could he be somewhere else in the mansion? Or was he not even in this residence at all—perhaps not even in this era?","At that last thought, Dai Li’s temple throbbed fiercely. She gazed out into the boundless night, overwhelmed by confusion and despair.","“No, Zhou Zhou can’t not be here. The school bus and surveillance on the road all showed that no one got off before the bus plunged into the river. None of the windows were broken on a large scale. The driver was there, the teachers were there, the other children were there—only Zhou Zhou was missing. He must be here. He has to be here...” Tears welled up in Dai Li’s eyes.","The news had reported that thirty-nine people died in the Red Sun Bilingual Elementary School bus accident—one driver, two teachers, and thirty-six students—based on the number of bodies found inside the bus.","Yet almost no one knew that the bus had not carried thirty-nine passengers that day, but forty.","Dai Li never saw her son on that bus when it went into the river. He was gone—entered the water with the bus, the windows intact, but mysteriously absent from inside.","No sign of life, no sign of a body.","At first, Dai Li held onto a desperate hope—that her son had somehow gotten off alone midway, or that after the bus plunged into the river, he was swept out and rescued by someone kind on the riverbank.","Yet, no matter how many times the surveillance footage was reviewed, no matter how many times the riverbank was searched, even after hiring a costly rescue team to patrol, she waited day after day, and the strange dreams haunted her night after night. But half a year passed, and Dai Li neither found a body nor witnessed a miracle.","“If he’s not inside the mansion, then I’ll search outside,” Dai Li said, her chin lifting slightly as the glistening tears in her eyes quickly vanished.","She had an inexplicable intuition—her little one was definitely somewhere in this unfamiliar era.","But...","Not far off, a commotion was stirring. It seemed a crowd had gathered, and faint voices drifted over.","“Some of us will go this way, the rest that way.”","“Alright, we regroup and exchange information in half an hour.”","Dai Li’s heart surged as she looked toward the noisy gathering, then swiftly turned and headed in another direction.","Normally, the mansion would never be so raucous when honored guests arrived—unless all of this was at the guests’ behest.","He had discovered it.","To expose her lie, someone must have already searched the courtyards where the dancing girls lived. Those two courtyards had already undergone one round of questioning; a second round so soon was unlikely.","The West Garden sat at the edge of the estate. She remembered two thriving nai trees there—perhaps she could hide in their branches to evade the remaining searchers, and then, just before dawn when the sky was darkest and the guards most weary, she might try to scale the wall and slip out.","That was her only option, for Dai Li had no map of the mansion. Every step she’d taken so far had been by asking directions.","Other places—the warehouse, the quarters of the lord’s concubines, the kitchen—she had no knowledge of any of them.","*","“Lord Junhou, we found a hidden package in the rear garden,” Mo Yanyun reported, carrying the parcel back.","The package’s color was familiar—an inky black under the lamplight, with a loose sleeve dangling from one side.","Mo Yanyun unwrapped it, revealing a long purple skirt, a black upper garment, and a pair of shoes.","“Lord Junhou, could these be the clothes the young lady wore earlier?” Mo Yanyun asked. Dai Li had disguised herself in men’s clothing at the time, so he hadn’t seen what she wore underneath.","Qin Shaozong lifted one of the sandals by its strap, an inscrutable look on his face. “Cowhide?”","Mo Yanyun blinked, pressing the sole with his fingers, astonished. “Lord Junhou, this cowhide is incredibly soft and smooth—a top-quality material. Jiang Chonghai is too extravagant, using such fine leather for a concubine’s shoes to tread underfoot!”","Not all cowhide is equal; even if it starts from the same premium piece, differences in tanning methods and materials can create worlds apart in quality.","“This has nothing to do with Jiang Chonghai,” Qin Shaozong said, loosening the sandal strap and turning to touch the purple skirt. The fabric was soft and supple, like a clear spring flowing through his palm.","The skirt was scented; he caught that faint, elegant fragrance again—not overpowering or sharp, but gentle and pleasing. Qin Shaozong’s lips curled into a smile. “Such fabric—Jiang Chonghai himself probably never had the luxury to wear this.”","When the request was made back then, Jiang Chonghai had indeed been taken aback for a moment.","Looking back now, that moment of stunned silence wasn’t born of reluctance, but confusion. It was simply that he had no memory whatsoever of the name “Feng Chun.”","Mo Yanyun grew increasingly perplexed. It had nothing to do with Jiang Chonghai? But if it wasn’t related to anyone named Jiang, then how did she end up inside the Jiang residence? She couldn’t have just appeared out of thin air, could she? “But Junhou, she’s here in the residence.”","Qin Shaozong didn’t respond to this. The man gazed into the distance, the lamplight gathering into a tiny point in his light brown eyes—sharp as a gleaming blade’s tip, like the fierce gaze of a tiger locking onto its prey. “At midnight, send out search parties to the rear garden and the East and West courtyards. There might be something to find.”","Mo Yanyun’s face was clouded with doubt. He instinctively glanced sideways, habitually seeking help from Yan San, but then remembered Yan San had gone to assist elsewhere. Left to his own devices, he furrowed his thick brows deeply, forming a large “eight” shape.","Qin Shaozong ignored his subordinate’s eager curiosity and turned back to his chambers.","Mo Yanyun stood in the courtyard, muttering to himself, “I understand the midnight operation—deep into the night, when everything’s quiet, it helps rule out many irrelevant people. But why the rear garden and the East and West courtyards? Haven’t those places already been searched before...?”","Mo Yanyun had a habit: when he couldn’t figure something out, he would start from the beginning and try to find a new thread to pull.","What was it at the very start?","Ah, yes. After investigation, there was no “Feng Chun” in the residence. Then Yan San mentioned encountering a minor steward surnamed Lin, who claimed that the beautiful woman had asked him for directions...","Mo Yanyun suddenly shivered, as if a light bulb had flicked on above his head.","She asked for directions, which meant she was unfamiliar with the layout of the residence. Now, with the search parties mobilized in full force, anyone unfamiliar with the environment would instinctively choose the place they felt safest—the place they knew best.","For example, she hid her parcel in the rear garden.","The East and West courtyards had already been searched earlier. Logically, it wouldn’t make sense to launch a second round of searches so soon, especially since those courtyards were filled with beautiful women, some of whom were newcomers. If she were hiding among them, it would be far more discreet than in any other location.","Mo Yanyun suddenly understood everything and eagerly hoped time would pass quickly.","Once they caught that beautiful woman, all doubts would be resolved.","Midnight was approaching."]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6","paragraphs":["West Garden.","\"Mi Jia, why aren't you asleep yet? You might have to perform for the distinguished guests tomorrow—you should rest early.\"","\"Did you hear any movement outside just now? A rustling sound, like leaves swaying in the wind or a cat slipping through the grass.\"","\"I think there was a little, but why worry about it? You said yourself it was just the wind or a cat, not some ghost. If it weren’t for the unrest outside tonight, I’d go out and check for you.\"","\"Never mind, let’s sleep. It seems quiet now.\"","......","The branches of the apple tree stopped trembling, revealing a faint shadow beneath it. Dai Li suppressed the discomfort in her left ankle and limped forward, muttering to herself, \"Climbing up is easy, but climbing down is hard\"—how true those words were. The ascent had gone smoothly, but she had twisted her foot on the way down.","The West Garden was silent, a stillness that stretched all the way to the courtyard entrance and the outer walkway. In the thick darkness of the night, it carried an eerie, unsettling quality. Yet, the tension in Dai Li’s chest eased slightly.","No one was around—good. That meant she could move to a new hiding place.","Yes, Dai Li intended to relocate.","The thought had struck her while she was still in the tree, perched high enough and settled in, ready to spend the night there.","But then, a cold breeze swept past, sending a shiver down her spine. In that moment, it was as if her soul had floated out of her body, rising to a higher vantage point where she could see everything from a detached, third-person perspective.","The obstructing leaves no longer blinded her—she saw possibilities she hadn’t before.","If she had thought to hide in the West Garden, would he—who already knew \"Feng Chun\" didn’t exist—have considered it too?","If he had met with the steward, he would know she had asked for directions, making it easy to deduce she wasn’t familiar with the mansion’s layout. By combining factors like unfamiliarity with the terrain, places suitable for a woman to hide, and spots convenient for escaping, he could easily narrow down the search.","The Thirty-Six Stratagems and The Art of War were testaments to the wisdom of the ancients, especially the aristocratic families and nobility who monopolized knowledge.","Of course, whether he had actually met the steward was mere speculation—she had no way of knowing. But the sword of Damocles now hung over her fragile nerves, compelling her to take the risk and move again.","The night was pitch black. Just as Dai Li stepped out of the West Garden and was about to enter a long corridor, she suddenly heard footsteps behind her.","From the sound, there was more than one or two people approaching.","Her breath hitched, but she didn’t dare look back. Instead, she quickened her pace into the corridor. Earlier, after borrowing the identity of the \"Marquis’s concubine\" to leave his courtyard, she hadn’t retraced her steps but had taken the opposite path. Now, she knew very well that the neighboring courtyard was reserved for distinguished guests—likely housing his subordinates.","Below the two courtyards lay a small, inverted \"品\"-shaped space used for parking carriages and horses. Dai Li remembered passing by earlier—only the inner archway had occasional foot traffic, while the outer area was unguarded.","This wasn’t surprising. Once the carriages were unloaded, they stood empty, and the horses were led to the feeding troughs up front. From the inner archway, one could see the horses without needing to step outside.","Dai Li planned to take shelter in that small area—the only place she knew of that might still conceal her.","Who would expect a delicate woman like her to dare venture into the lion’s den, hiding right under their noses?","No sooner had Dai Li left than Mo Yanyun arrived at the West Garden with his men. His entrance was nothing like her stealthy departure—he simply waved a hand, and the soldiers accompanying him flooded into the courtyard like a tide.","\"Light the lamps. Everyone, dress and gather in the courtyard.\"","\"What... what’s happening?\" a Hu girl asked timidly.","\"Enough questions. Just follow orders and be quick about it.\"","Soon, all the Hu girls emerged from their rooms, huddling together like drenched sparrows, trembling as they watched the men stride inside.","The West Garden had two buildings, each two stories high, housing only the Hu girls. But with all the women outside, the soldiers combed through every nook and cranny of both buildings—yet found nothing.","Mo Yanyun’s thick brows furrowed. He turned his gaze to the gathered Hu girls, holding up a lantern to inspect each one.","The differences between Hu girls and Han women were stark—no simple disguise could bridge them. After a single sweep, Mo Yanyun was certain \"Feng Chun\" wasn’t among them.","Strange. If she wasn’t in the buildings or among the girls, where was she hiding?","\"Check the trees too,\" Mo Yanyun ordered, pointing at the two apple trees.","Immediately, agile soldiers scaled the trees, climbing swiftly to the higher branches. They descended just as fast—empty-handed.","Mo Yanyun muttered to himself: The Marquis ordered us to search the rear garden and the East and West Gardens. Since she’s not in the West Garden, could she be hiding in the rear garden or the East Garden?","With that thought, he casually pointed at two men. \"You two stay here until the end of mao hour. The rest, follow me.\"","Just as he was about to leave the West Garden, Mo Yanyun remembered something and turned back to address the Hu girls. \"If that 'Song Lan' sneaks back tonight, report it immediately to the guards. Anyone who knows and doesn’t speak up will face the consequences.\"","The Hu girls nodded fearfully in unison.","Dai Li moved with trepidation, silently praying she wouldn’t run into anyone—praying her path would remain as smooth as when she had returned to the West Garden earlier.","Perhaps luck was on her side, or perhaps the late hour worked in her favor—for now, she was alone.","She exhaled softly, but her relief was premature. The moment she relaxed, a warm glow suddenly appeared to her side, accompanied by two petite figures.","She stood at the left intersection of an \"H\"-shaped path, while they were on the right, barely a few meters apart. The lantern light spilled onto Dai Li’s round-toe silk shoes, and the sudden encounter left both parties momentarily stunned.","Dai Li reacted first, stepping back twice to vanish into the shadows again. Even though these were only maids and not guards, her tension didn’t ease in the slightest.","With the Marquis’s search sweeping through the entire mansion, anyone spotting her walking alone at this hour would find it highly suspicious.","\"Are you that—\" The taller maid didn’t finish before her companion yanked her sleeve sharply. The two turned away, pretending to be busy with their lanterns as they hurried off.","Watching their retreating figures, Dai Li fell into thought. Something flickered in her mind—too fleeting to grasp.","The rest of the journey passed without incident. Dai Li deliberately took a detour, entering the \"parking area\" from the rear. As she had guessed, the place was unguarded. The carriages stood in a neat row against the wall, while the horses had been led away to their troughs.","The courtyard was hushed, the insects silent, with only the occasional flick of a horse’s tail or a soft snort breaking the stillness.","Dai Li let out a long breath and limped along the wall, finally settling down between the carriages, her back against the cool stone.","Tonight, I might be able to evade them, but what about tomorrow...","\"Lord, I’ve searched the rear garden, the East and West Pavilions, but found no trace of Feng Chun.\" Mo Yanyun was puzzled. It was rare for the lord to miscalculate. Well, though this wasn’t exactly a major matter.","Qin Shaozong raised an eyebrow. \"Nowhere?\"","Mo Yanyun nodded. \"My men combed through every inch of those three places, leaving no chest or hidden compartment unchecked. But she truly wasn’t there.\"","After a pause, Mo Yanyun ventured a guess. \"Could she be hiding among the concubines’ quarters?\"","He still believed the beautiful woman was connected to Jiang Chonghai—otherwise, how could she be in Jiang Mansion? If they were acquainted, she could be hiding anywhere.","Just as Qin Shaozong was about to speak, footsteps approached from outside. Yan San had returned.","The soldiers accompanying Yan San halted at the courtyard gate, while Yan San stepped inside and lowered his voice. \"Lord, Jiang Mansion’s hidden treasury is shockingly well-stocked. A governor’s salary is two thousand dan, with a monthly stipend of one hundred twenty hu. Yet, a mere corner of Jiang Chonghai’s private vault holds wealth far surpassing what twenty governors could save in ten years, even if they starved themselves.\"","Mo Yanyun gaped. \"That much?\"","\"The vault is heavily guarded, with shifts changing every two hours. Clearly, Jiang Chonghai knows it’s not something to flaunt.\" Yan San’s tone was indifferent, as if infiltrating the treasury had been effortless.","\"Gorged himself to the point of bursting,\" Qin Shaozong remarked dryly.","Mo Yanyun frowned. \"Judging by the treasures in that vault, the relationship between Li and Jiang must be unusually close. Lord, our military movements haven’t been concealed. If Li and Jiang are colluding, Jiang Chonghai will surely scheme behind our backs.\"","\"That’s exactly what I want—for him to scheme. I’d be more worried if he cowered like a quail, too afraid to move.\" Qin Shaozong glanced at the sky. The dark clouds still hadn’t dispersed. Tonight, there would be no moon. A perfect night for hiding.","Mo Yanyun’s brow smoothed. The lord already had a plan, so there was no need for concern.","Qin Shaozong turned to Yan San, shifting the topic. \"Did you find any sign of Feng Chun near the treasury?\"","Yan San shook his head.","With an inscrutable smile, Qin Shaozong said, \"She’s good at hiding. No matter. Tonight ends here. She may evade us today, but not forever.\"","With the search called off, the men were free to do as they pleased—rest or attend to other matters.","Mo Yanyun chose the latter. Instead of heading straight to his quarters, he walked toward the rear, intending to pass through the stable courtyard to the adjacent pavilion. The guest quarters were well-equipped, but they lacked something important to him.","His nightly ritual involved flipping through a book of beauties, which was still packed in his luggage. No trouble—just a short walk to retrieve it.","Dai Li sat with her back against the wall, curling into herself. Earlier, her focus had been solely on fleeing, but now that she’d stopped, the pain in her left ankle flared sharply.","She touched her swollen ankle, wincing. Would it heal by tomorrow? Just as the worry set in, footsteps approached.","Someone had entered the neighboring pavilion. Muffled voices rose and fell, too indistinct to decipher.","Dai Li had expected visitors nearby and wasn’t alarmed. Surely, they’d finish their conversation and retire for the night.","As predicted, the voices soon faded. But contrary to her expectations, someone stepped through the small arched gate into her hiding spot.","Holding her breath, Dai Li clenched her fingers, listening to the footsteps.","The two pavilions’ arched gates faced each other. Under normal circumstances, no one would notice her concealed behind the carriage.","Please, no mishaps...","\"Neigh!\"","A sturdy, crimson-maned horse in the stable suddenly whinnied.","Mo Yanyun turned, amused. \"The stable’s a bit cramped, I know. Bear with it, Red Dragon.\"","He continued forward, passing through the opposite gate. Moments later, he returned with a book in hand.","\"Neigh!\"","The horse called out again.","Mo Yanyun chuckled. \"Red Dragon, no use complaining. Your master says we stay, so we stay. Don’t worry—you’ll get the finest fodder... Lord?\"","Spotting Qin Shaozong’s tall figure crossing the gate, Mo Yanyun explained without being asked, \"Red Dragon’s unhappy with the tight quarters.\"","Horses were rare treasures these days. Even an average steed could cost a commoner twenty years’ wages.","When Jiang Mansion was built, Jiang Chonghai never imagined hosting so many cavalry. Now, two courtyards shared one stable.","Qin Shaozong acknowledged with a hum. His gaze swept past the opposite gate, where soldiers bustled about, tending to their duties after the search.","Everything was in order.","He strode over, smoothing Red Dragon’s mane and patting its neck in reassurance before turning to leave.","Just as he reached the gate, the wind shifted—from north to northwest.","And on that cool breeze, Qin Shaozong caught a faint, elusive fragrance. He halted abruptly, his sharp brown eyes narrowing."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: The Seventh Image","paragraphs":["But upon sniffing more carefully, that faint trace of fragrance was now nowhere to be found, as if the fleeting moment earlier had been nothing but his imagination. Yet Qin Shaozong never doubted his sense of smell.","In his youth, the imperial court had repeatedly sent assassins to target the Qin Clan’s descendants, employing methods ranging from ambushes and poisonings to internal betrayals and surprise attacks.","By his teenage years, Qin Shaozong had encountered poisoning attempts no fewer than ten times, yet he had never once fallen victim to such underhanded tactics.","Whether it was tainted soup, spiked wine, or even bitter medicinal brews, he could always detect the slightest hint of something amiss.","Qin Shaozong swept his gaze across the small courtyard. The space was modest—to the south stood a horse trough and stable, where an unusually tall crimson steed snorted and stamped its hooves. The western side connected to the neighboring courtyard through a small arched gate, offering an unobstructed view. Opposite the stable, to the north, was a small door used by servants to clean the stables without passing through the two pavilions housing distinguished guests.","In the northwest corner, a row of unhitched carriages stood neatly against the wall, silent and still. The courtyard was unlit, and the line of carriages, shrouded in darkness, resembled large black-shrouded chests.","\"Will you come out on your own, or shall I drag you out?\" The man’s voice was deep and resonant, laced with a faint amusement, as if offering a final courtesy before drawing his blade.","Only he and Qin Shaozong were present. At first, Mo Yanyun thought the lord was speaking to him and reflexively replied, \"What?\" But seeing Qin Shaozong’s unwavering gaze fixed ahead and recalling the implication of his words, Mo Yanyun suddenly realized—the words weren’t meant for him.","Could it be...?","Mo Yanyun’s face twisted in shock.","H-How was this possible?","After toying with the lord and knowing full well that the entire estate was searching for her, how could she dare return?","His eyes darted to the row of carriages. There was no sound—not even the buzz of a mosquito.","What Mo Yanyun didn’t know was that Dai Li had nearly screamed in terror moments ago. Now, a cold sweat coated her back, the night breeze raising goosebumps along her spine. The phrase \"hair-raising fear\" had never felt more apt.","The courtyard was so silent that every sound seemed amplified. Dai Li heard footsteps—measured and deliberate, yet each step felt like it pressed against her nerves, chilling her blood and stiffening her limbs.","The footsteps drew closer.","Had his earlier words not been a mere bluff?","Dai Li bit her lip, trembling as she curled tighter into herself.","\"My lord, how did you know she was hiding here?\" Mo Yanyun couldn’t resist asking.","Qin Shaozong replied simply, \"Presence or absence—we’ll see.\"","The cargo carriages, designed for easy loading, had doors at both ends. The soldiers responsible for securing them must have had a touch of obsessive compulsion, as every door had been shut.","Qin Shaozong reached out and pushed.","\"Creak—\"","The wooden axle groaned as the small front door swung open.","But inside, there was no one.","\"Creak, creak...\"","One by one, the carriage doors were pried open, each revealing nothing but empty space.","When the last door was pushed aside, Mo Yanyun gaped at the emptiness within.","Nothing?","Every compartment had been checked, yet there was no trace of her. Had the lord’s earlier words just been a spur-of-the-moment attempt to scare the audacious girl into revealing herself?","But then, Qin Shaozong turned and strode forward, squeezing into the narrow gap between the wall and the carriages.","In just a few steps, he reached the end. From this angle, the rear of every carriage was visible—and still, no one.","Qin Shaozong arched a brow in amusement, then shifted his gaze elsewhere.","From Dai Li’s hiding spot beneath a carriage, the scene unfolding before her was more terrifying than the most chilling horror story.","The creaking of doors drew nearer, and soon, two pairs of black boots stopped right in front of her. Even after all the doors had been opened, the men didn’t leave. Dai Li clutched her hands to her chest, trying to stifle the frantic pounding of her heart.","One pair of boots moved—not away, but into the narrow passage beside her.","So close. If she reached out, she could touch his leather boots.","Dai Li held her breath. The boots soon vanished from view. She knew he had circled behind her, but she didn’t dare turn or even twitch, terrified of making a sound.","\"My lord, I really don’t think that girl would dare come back—\"","\"Pull this carriage out.\"","The two voices overlapped.","Orders were orders. Without hesitation, Mo Yanyun grabbed the long shaft and yanked.","\"Rumble—\"","To Dai Li, the sound of rolling wheels was like thunder—or the last sheltering beast being driven away by a predator.","The clouds that had obscured the moon finally drifted apart, casting a pale glow over the courtyard.","In horror, Dai Li realized that every carriage cast a shadow in the moonlight—except hers.","Because her shadow was entirely swallowed by the towering, mountain-like silhouette looming behind her.","\"She really is here?!\" Mo Yanyun exclaimed.","Beyond sheer astonishment, a stray thought flickered through his mind:","The lord’s earlier words hadn’t been a bluff—he’d known she was here all along. And now, by circling behind and ordering the carriage moved, he’d trapped her between two fronts. Was this... meant to utterly crush her will to flee?","But was that necessary? Once caught, surely she’d recognize her helplessness and abandon any further schemes.","Dai Li didn’t know what Mo Yanyun was thinking. All she felt was the icy grip of terror, her breath coming in shallow gasps.","Every nerve screamed at her to flee. Instinct took over—she scrambled to her feet, but before she could take a single step, a powerful arm wrapped around her waist from behind, yanking her backward.","\"I thought I’d caught a little rabbit, but it seems I’ve got a cunning fox instead,\" he mused, amused.","Dai Li crashed into a solid chest. Despite the lingering chill of early spring, the man wore surprisingly little, radiating heat like an inescapable wildfire or a scorching cliff face. The warmth did nothing to comfort her—instead, it sent a shiver down her spine.","Qin Shaozong held her from behind, feeling as though he’d captured a wisp of soft cloud. He lowered his head, burying his face in the crook of her neck, where the elusive fragrance from earlier now bloomed richly, intoxicating his senses.","His nose brushed against the side of her neck, his scorching breath like the bared fangs of a beast. The last thread of restraint in Dai Li’s mind snapped. Instinctively, she dug her nails into the iron-like arm clamped around her waist, struggling to break free. \"Let me go!\"","The grip around her waist suddenly loosened, only for her to be spun around—from facing away to staring directly at him.","The full moon slanted behind him, casting his face in shadow, leaving only a pair of predatory brown eyes gleaming with intensity.","Suppressing her panic, Dai Li opened her mouth to speak, but in the next moment, her feet left the ground as Qin Shaozong hauled her over his shoulder in one swift motion.","Her vision flipped abruptly, sending a dizzying rush through her head. Her waist pressed against the solid plane of his shoulder blade, one arm forced to loop around his neck while her legs kicked uselessly in the air, the other arm too weak to resist.","Mo Yanyun gaped, stunned, as Qin Shaozong strode away with the struggling woman slung over his shoulder.","Having followed the lord through countless campaigns, he had never seen the marquis act with such urgency.","Was this truly fury driving him, or...?","The courtyard was mere steps from the main house, so the distance Qin Shaozong carried her was short.","\"Bang.\" The door swung open.","The man strode inside, crossing the outer chamber before passing through the inner doorway.","By the time Dai Li was deposited onto the bed, her cheeks were flushed with heat, her chest rising and falling rapidly. The spacious divan left ample room behind her, so the moment she landed, she instinctively scrambled backward.","But before she could move far, his large hand closed around her left ankle. With a flick of his long fingers, her rounded silk slipper slipped off and landed with a soft \"tap\" on the footrest below.","A sharp pain shot through her injured ankle, drawing a hiss from her lips. The pain was acute, yet it acted like a bucket of ice water dumped over her in midsummer, cooling the feverish haze in her mind.","The room was lit by lamps, their golden glow illuminating every detail. The shadows that had obscured his face earlier now receded, revealing sharp brows that arched like swords, deep-set eyes that bore into her with relentless intensity.","Now, his lips curled lazily, but his gaze never wavered—Dai Li felt as if she were staring at a vicious tiger licking its claws, ready to devour its prey.","She thought, This is a man of unyielding dominance. Dominance that came with arrogance.","Perhaps she could use that to her advantage...","The beautiful woman on the bed lowered and then lifted her thick lashes, her expression shifting into one of fearful grievance. \"It’s not that this humble one refuses to serve you, my lord, but circumstances have forced my hand. Some matters... were beyond my control.\"","Qin Shaozong suddenly raised his hand.","Dai Li’s pupils trembled, her self-control the only thing stopping her from raising her arms in defense.","His stature was imposing, his broad palm large enough to engulf her face. His calloused thumb pressed against her forehead, slowly wiping away the rice powder that had concealed the crimson beauty mark there.","Her skin was porcelain-pale, glowing like lustrous pearl under the candlelight, her hair a cascade of dark silk—a vision of breathtaking allure.","Qin Shaozong’s lips curved in satisfaction. \"Oh? Then tell me, what circumstances led you to break your word, flee like a coward, and still resist me to the end?\"","Where his fingers had traced, her skin burned as if licked by the barbed tongue of a beast, sending shivers down her spine. Dai Li’s words caught in her throat.","\"Still fabricating excuses? Then spare me the trouble.\" His hand, still dusted with rice powder, slid downward. His arm looped around her waist, pulling her close before tossing her back onto the bed.","His shadow loomed over her, and for a fleeting moment, Dai Li felt as though she had been dragged back to that stable courtyard."]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8","paragraphs":["The night was deep, and many houses had long extinguished their lights, their occupants already lost in dreams. Yet one particular courtyard stood as an exception.","The room was quiet, with only the sound of two breaths lingering in the air. Yet, Dai Li felt as though she could hear the rumble of thunder—no, not the spring thunder, but the frantic pounding of her heart, threatening to leap out of her throat.","As the man leaned in, Dai Li instinctively raised a hand to press against his chest. \"I wasn’t making up excuses. It’s just that the matter is complicated, and I was thinking of how to explain it briefly.\"","Qin Shaozong didn’t retreat, but neither did he advance further. He remained hovering above her, his gaze fixed on the woman beneath him.","Dai Li didn’t expect him to respond. She forced tears to her eyes and began spinning a tale that was half-truth, half-lie: \"I have a young son who was abducted by villains some time ago. After some investigation, I learned he might be somewhere in this estate. That’s why I sneaked in to search for him. Running into you was entirely unexpected.\"","Qin Shaozong wasn’t surprised she had a child.","In this dynasty, girls were considered marriageable at fifteen. To encourage population growth, the court had issued decrees promoting childbirth and reducing taxes, one of which stated: \"Unmarried women aged fifteen to thirty must pay five times the usual poll tax.\"","Thus, daughters from common families married early. Even noblewomen, despite delaying slightly, rarely remained unwed for more than a year or two.","\"I know you are a man of great standing, and I’m grateful for your favor. Though wealth and comfort are tempting, I am a mother. My son is the flesh of my heart. From the moment I decided to bear him, I vowed to protect and raise him. How could I bear to see him suffer alone in the world? My desperation to find him drove me to take reckless actions, even borrowing your authority. The chaos that followed was never my intention. I was terrified and ashamed to face you again, knowing I had betrayed your kindness.\"","At first, Dai Li had intended to feign hardship, but as she spoke, memories of her missing son—whose body she had never found—brought genuine tears to her eyes.","\"As for your accusation of resistance, that’s not accurate.\" Dai Li refused to admit it. \"At the time, I was exhausted, half-asleep, and the night was dark. When I first woke, I didn’t recognize you. I thought you were the villain who had taken my son and had come back for me. I beg your forgiveness.\"","Pausing, she flattered him: \"That you would still hold me in regard despite my mistakes fills me with joy. How could I push you away? Your bearing alone marks you as nobility of the highest order.\"","Her explanation neatly dismissed his earlier demand—\"Will you come out yourself, or shall I drag you out?\"—as the result of her drowsiness. As for her struggles, she insisted it was the darkness that had kept her from recognizing him.","In short, the past was the past. Now, she saw him for who he was.","When she finished, Qin Shaozong let out a low chuckle, leaving her unsure whether he believed her. Pressing her lips together, she resolved to strike harder.","No longer flustered, Dai Li curved her red lips slightly. The hand on his chest slid down his black robe, her fingertips tracing a slow, teasing path designed to provoke a shiver. \"I know little of politics and your exact status, but I’ve heard even Prefect Jiang defers to you. You must be a man of immense influence. Finding a child would surely be a trivial matter for you. Might I trouble you for this small favor?\"","Her slender, pale fingers hooked onto his belt, brushing against the ornate clasp. Just as she was about to undo it, a rough, large hand suddenly seized hers.","He forced his way into her palm, enveloping her delicate hand in his, kneading and stroking every inch—from the faintly pink fingertips to the delicate bones of her wrist, even sliding between her fingers with deliberate thoroughness.","Qin Shaozong smiled. \"Finding a child is no trouble. At dawn, I’ll have men see to it.\"","Heat seemed to crawl up her arm, sending tremors down her spine. Suppressing the urge to pull her right hand back, Dai Li lifted her left to loop around his neck. \"My son’s name is Qin Yanzhou. He stands five feet seven inches tall. Half a month ago, a Taoist advised me to cut his hair short, so he should be easy to recognize.\"","A flicker of thought passed through Qin Shaozong’s eyes. \"The surname Qin?\"","Dai Li’s heart skipped.","The name \"Qin\" wasn’t uncommon—it was among the Hundred Family Surnames. But she knew that in certain eras, certain names could dominate regions, becoming synonymous with power. The Sun Clan of Jiangdong, with its three heroes; the Lü Clan of Luoyang, with four prominent figures across three generations...","Surely \"Qin\" wasn’t one such name here?","\"Who is your husband?\" he suddenly asked.","Dai Li’s pulse quickened. So \"Qin\" was indeed a prominent name. Countless lies sprang to mind, only to burst like bubbles.","She couldn’t fabricate this.","She had no idea where or when she was, nor the broader political landscape. Inventing a noble lineage out of thin air would crumble at the slightest scrutiny.","Feigning guilt, she averted her gaze. \"H-He was just a commoner. Even if I told you his name, you wouldn’t know him. The night is fleeting—why waste it on talk? Let us retire early, so I may see my son sooner tomorrow.\"","Her left arm around his neck tensed slightly, urging him down.","Qin Shaozong’s expression was unreadable. Then, with a soft laugh, he murmured, \"‘One night of spring is worth a thousand pieces of gold.’ As you wish, madam. Let us not squander this spring night.\"","The arm that had been wrapped around her waist withdrew, only to slip beneath the gap between her robe and skirt.","Despite her earlier resolve, Dai Li stiffened. The touch against her skin wasn’t a hand but something like scalding sandpaper—rough and searing, as if a single stroke might strip her bare.","The fire traced her waist, then slithered upward like a serpent. Her lashes fluttered, delicate eyelids flushing a pale pink, like peach blossoms against snow.","The shadow above her descended at last, a towering mountain engulfing her completely. The distance between them vanished, and no one could be more acutely aware of his readiness than she was in this moment.","Her breath hitched. The scent of gunpowder and windblown sand filled her senses, the scorching air grazing her ear, leaving behind faint red marks and tremors before trailing downward.","But then—","\"Hm?\" Qin Shaozong pushed himself up slightly. The small, metallic object he had just brushed against puzzled him.","The candlelight flickered brightly. On the bed, Dai Li’s sash had loosened, her outer robe slipping open to reveal an equally disheveled undergarment—and beneath it, a breathtaking expanse of soft curves.","Snow-white skin, peaks rising proudly, a sight both delicate and striking.","Unlike most women, she wore no breastband.","No—that wasn’t quite right.","Qin Shaozong caught a glimpse of a faint lavender corner peeking from beneath her undergarments.","When he let out that questioning hum, Dai Li froze momentarily, initially unsure what had disrupted her plan—until he flipped her over.","The loosely draped outer robe and undergarments were further parted by the man, revealing her ink-black hair cascading like water over the woman’s snow-white back, an alluring sight brimming with natural grace.","Qin Shaozong brushed aside her silken locks, his gaze landing on an undergarment of peculiar design.","Most women’s belly wraps nowadays had ties at the back, fastened with one or two knots behind the waist. But this one had no such bindings. It clung seamlessly to her back like an uncut swath of fabric, though upon closer inspection, its midsection concealed a hidden mechanism.","Dai Li lay prone on the bed, acutely aware of the large hand moving over her—first skin against skin, then separated by the undergarment—until a soft snap sounded.","Her undergarment had come undone.","Back in the western pavilion when changing clothes, Dai Li had considered swapping everything down to her undergarments but ultimately refrained.","For one, unlike dresses and robes, undergarments weren’t visible to prying eyes. For another, she couldn’t bring herself to wear someone else’s intimate wear.","Yet plans never survived contact with reality. She hadn’t expected him to search the estate for her, nor that she’d fail to evade him.","In modern times, undergarment clasps were made of cheap, commonplace iron. But in this era of cold steel, iron was as precious as weaponry—a force indispensable for overthrowing regimes. Even in the Han Dynasty, after leaps in metallurgy, iron remained costly. Commoners might own iron plows or hoes, but not necessarily an iron pot.","And now, this valuable material was embedded in a woman’s intimate garment.","Dai Li remembered the clasps were the same color as the fabric, invisible to the eye. She prayed he wouldn’t recognize them.","“Iron?” Qin Shaozong pressed a finger against them.","Dai Li: “...”","“Where did you buy this belly wrap, madam?” he asked.","Dai Li rolled onto her back, arms crossed over her chest, and answered languidly, “From a merchant from the Western Regions. He boasted it was unique, swearing no other woman would own its likeness. I found it novel, so I bought it.”","Then she looped her arms around his neck. “My lord, let’s not dwell on such trifles. Seizing the moment is what matters now. I dearly wish to see my son by tomorrow.”","Qin Shaozong didn’t stop her from turning, nor did he seem to care about the iron clasps anymore. He leaned in as she pulled him closer. “Rest assured. If your son is in this estate, even if hidden in the master’s private vault, I’ll bring him to you.”","“I never doubted your capabilities,” Dai Li murmured sweetly. No longer face-to-face, she finally allowed her expression to shift.","The familiar heat of his breath trailed down her neck. As she counted silently, her hand drifted lower, fingertips brushing his waist. Though still clad in his black outer robe, she could feel the firm, heated muscle beneath.","After a pause, she reached for his belt.","Belts in this era weren’t so different from modern ones—hooks and rings alike. Just as she undid it, Dai Li twisted her left ankle sharply.","“My lord, I’m unwell. It seems... my monthly courses have come,” she said, pressing a hand to his chest to push him away.","Qin Shaozong’s face darkened instantly. His scrutinizing gaze swept over her, but she bit her reddened lip, face pale, a sheen of sweat on her brow.","Expressions could be faked, but the body’s reactions couldn’t.","With a pained whisper, Dai Li asked, “Will you still send someone to find my son tomorrow?”","The woman on the bed was nearly bare above the waist, save for the crooked undergarment. Her hair fanned out beneath her like a waterfall, her flushed skin dotted with faint red marks, like a ripe peach glistening with nectar.","A vein throbbed at Qin Shaozong’s temple. The arm braced against her waist tensed, muscles straining as if holding back a storm. He inhaled sharply, then exhaled hard before straightening to refasten his half-undone belt. “My word is my bond.”","With that, he strode out of the fragrant chamber without a backward glance.","Only when his towering figure vanished entirely did Dai Li feel the weight lift from her chest.","She’d succeeded!","Just as she’d predicted, men of this era saw menstruation as unclean, something to be avoided—hence the taboos against women entering temples or touching offerings during their courses.","And as she’d guessed, a proud, powerful man like him would never stoop to verifying her claim, no matter how desperate his desire.","She’d buy herself a few days’ reprieve, use his influence to scour the estate once more, then find her chance to escape..."]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9","paragraphs":["\"Lord?\"","Mo Yanyun was still shaken by the earlier scene of Qin Shaozong abducting someone. Seeing the moon finally emerge, he found himself too restless to sleep and decided to admire it in the courtyard.","But his moonlit reverie didn’t last long before he spotted his superior stepping out of the main house.","Mo Yanyun couldn’t hide his astonishment, mixed with a private concern he dared not voice.","After devouring such a breathtaking beauty from head to toe, savoring every last drop of her essence, there were countless things a man could do—and none of them would take so little time. Yet less than the span of a cup of tea had passed, and the lord was already leaving. Could it be...?","Qin Shaozong turned at the sound of his voice. Whether it was his imagination or not, Mo Yanyun thought his superior’s eyes gleamed with a predatory green light, just like a starving wolf that had failed its hunt on the northern grasslands.","Instinctively, Mo Yanyun’s gaze flickered downward, taking a quick, knowing glance. As a man, he could tell at once whether another had been satisfied.","Ah. So it wasn’t his imagination after all. The lord was truly left hungry—judging by the timing, he might not have even gotten a taste.","A seasoned veteran of pleasure houses, Mo Yanyun quickly ruled out other possibilities and guessed that \"Feng Chun\" was likely indisposed due to her monthly courses, making her unable to serve. He knew well how irritable men became in such situations. With so many dancers in the residence, if she couldn’t perform, why not summon another beauty to ease the lord’s frustration?","\"Shall I select a lovely dancer for you?\" he suggested.","Qin Shaozong replied, \"Fine.\"","Mo Yanyun turned to carry out the order, but after only a few steps, his superior abruptly changed his mind.","\"Never mind.\"","Mo Yanyun spun back in surprise. \"Why not?\"","Qin Shaozong’s voice was rough but noticeably calmer. \"I have a plan to expedite our current affairs, and she plays a role in it. Introducing another woman now would complicate matters.\"","\"Lord, can she truly be trusted?\" Mo Yanyun couldn’t help but doubt.","Knowing Qin Shaozong as he did, if the man said she was needed, then \"Feng Chun\" wouldn’t merely be a background figure. A stranger with unknown allegiances—one who had already deceived the lord once—how could she be relied upon?","\"She has no ties to the Jiang Mansion,\" Qin Shaozong said coolly. \"She has a young son named Qin Yanzhou—short hair, about five feet seven inches tall. He may be in the residence. Tomorrow, take men and search discreetly. Also, investigate whether any child from the northern Qin clan has gone missing, and look into the movements of the noblewomen from their households.\"","Mo Yanyun was stunned by this revelation. \"Lord, you suspect 'Feng Chun' is a noblewoman? How... how could that be possible?\"","A noblewoman’s status was derived from her husband’s prominence—his family’s prestige and his own achievements. Such powerful families always formed alliances with equals, meaning her own lineage would be no less distinguished.","In short, a noblewoman was a pampered daughter before marriage and, after, remained fortunate enough to wed into a family—and a husband—of exceptional standing.","Qin Shaozong gave him a sidelong glance, uninterested in elaborating. \"Why ask heaven, earth, and everything in between? Planning to quit as captain and become a gossipmonger in a teahouse?\"","Mo Yanyun stammered a denial.","Qin Shaozong turned his gaze back to the house behind him, his eyes dark with unspoken thoughts.","Common women toiled in fields or over washbasins, their hands inevitably calloused over time. Dancers, though entertainers, were still servants—when not attending to guests, they labored like any other. Only those waited upon by maids, indulged by wealthy husbands, could keep their hands untouched by hardship.","Her hands were soft, save for a faint callus on the inner side of her right middle finger. Her skin was smooth, her body exuding a delicate floral fragrance—proof of a life coddled in luxury.","Add to that her leather shoes and the undergarment lined with small iron plates, and it was clear her husband’s family was no ordinary one.","\"Feng Chun\" was a false name, and so was \"Song Lan,\" but Qin Shaozong sensed her desperation to find her son was genuine. Thus, \"Qin Yanzhou\" was likely real.","Her husband’s family was the Qin clan, a prominent northern lineage. Yet, to his knowledge, none of their branches boasted a noblewoman renowned for such striking beauty.","Could she be a concubine?","It wasn’t impossible.","A proper wife would never lack guards or maids at her disposal. And if a legitimate child from a branch family were kidnapped, he would have heard rumors. A matriarch wouldn’t be reduced to searching the streets alone...","With that in mind, Qin Shaozong added, \"Aside from noblewomen, look into favored concubines who have borne sons and are deeply cherished by their lords.\"","\"Understood.\"","The moon set, the sun rose, and dawn broke as promised. Military men never slept in—morning drills were routine.","When Qin Shaozong returned from training, he saw Yan San stepping out of the main house. The latter explained, \"Lord, 'Feng Chun' said she twisted her ankle and asked for medicinal oil. I just delivered it.\"","Qin Shaozong acknowledged with a hum before shifting topics. \"Pack your things and move in with Mo Yanyun. Clear the side room, and this afternoon, fetch two maidservants.\"","Yesterday, he had refused Jiang Chonghai’s servants; today, he requested his own. A clear reversal, but Yan San didn’t question it, merely clasped his hands in obedience.","After Qin Shaozong left the previous night, Dai Li hadn’t dared remain in the main house. She quickly relocated to the small side chamber adjoining it—meant for attending servants.","Cramped as it was, with a narrow bed, it was safer than the open courtyard, and she managed a decent rest.","Burdened with worries, she woke early. Instead of venturing out, she listened quietly until the men departed before asking Yan San for medicinal wine.","She hadn’t expected the lord to return just as she applied it.","This was the finest guest courtyard, its layout and furnishings impeccable. Even the side room was brighter than most, sunlight streaming through the window to outline Qin Shaozong’s towering frame. Though daylight softened his presence slightly, his oppressive aura remained.","Dai Li had just schooled her expression when he asked, \"Twisted your ankle? When did that happen?\"","She couldn’t let him suspect her injury predated her exposure—lest he realize her discomfort last night had nothing to do with her monthly courses.","\"After you left last night, I was uneasy and distracted. I stumbled over the threshold on my way back,\" she recited her prepared excuse.","Qin Shaozong’s gaze dropped. She sat cross-legged on the bed, her shoes and stockings removed, her skirt spread like petals around her. One foot remained hidden beneath the fabric, while the other—mid-calf exposed—gleamed like polished jade in the dim light. The swollen ankle, slick with oil, confirmed the injury.","His stare burned like a brand. Dai Li’s skin prickled as if scalded, and she nearly tugged her skirt down.","But she stopped herself just in time.","A woman who actively seeks the company of the powerful, eager to share intimate moments with them, would never dislike such gazes.","\"Has Your Excellency come to see me because there is news of my son?\" Dai Li's face lit up with excitement.","The medicinal wine had been uncorked, its pungent aroma filling the room like a ravenous beast devouring the delicate fragrance that clung to the woman. As a military commander who had weathered the chaos of battlefields, Qin Shaozong was intimately familiar with all kinds of medicinal brews. Yet, for the first time, he found today's medicinal scent particularly unwelcome.","Qin Shaozong: \"There is no news of your son yet.\"","Dai Li lowered her eyes, her disappointment unmistakable.","\"It's still early. We’ll see later.\" The small room meant for servants was sparsely furnished—just a table, a cabinet, and a single chair. Influenced by the cultural influx from the northern tribes, the chair was a low, foreign-style seat. Qin Shaozong picked it up with one hand, placed it before the bed, and sat astride it with an air of authority, facing Dai Li directly.","\"Your name, madam?\" he suddenly asked.","Dai Li was about to speak when he added in an unreadable tone, \"No need for false names like Feng Chun or the like.\"","\"...Dai Li. 'Dai' as in the distant mountains, 'Li' as in the dawn.\" This time, Dai Li had no intention of lying. She still needed to stay here for a few more days, and if someone called her by a false name, she might not react in time and give herself away.","Qin Shaozong studied her for a long moment before responding with a simple, \"Mm.\" Then he continued, \"Madam Qin—\"","\"I do not take my husband's surname,\" Dai Li interrupted.","A shadow flickered in Qin Shaozong's eyes.","Women who did not take their husband's surname fell into two categories: those whose maternal lineage far surpassed their husband's status, who preferred to be addressed by their own names, and those who were mere concubines or dancers, passed around like gifts. The former disdained the practice, the latter were unworthy of it—a difference as vast as heaven and earth.","The Dai family—there was no prominent \"Dai\" clan in either the northern regions or the Central Plains.","Qin Shaozong: \"You don’t seem to be from Nankang County.\"","Dai Li smiled faintly. \"Your Excellency has sharp eyes. Indeed, I am not a local. I came to Nankang only by chance.\"","He pressed further, \"Where is your hometown?\"","Dai Li inwardly cursed. Unlike the plots of many dramas, she had come directly from the modern era, leaving no trace here—effectively making her a person without records.","If she refused to answer, he would not let it go, possibly disrupting the delicate balance she had worked hard to maintain. But if she answered, what could she say?","Her thoughts tangled like yarn mauled by a cat. Her eyelid twitched, and suddenly, inspiration struck. \"Jiaozhou. I am from Cangwu County in the southern Jiaozhou region.\"","In ancient times, travel was not as convenient as in the modern era, where a journey from south to north took mere hours. Even if he were determined to dig deeper, it would take months for a message to make the round trip. By then, she would no longer be in Nankang.","\"Jiaozhou’s Cangwu County?\" Qin Shaozong arched a brow. \"Jiaozhou is at least three or four thousand li from here. Why did you leave your homeland?\"","Dai Li offered a feudal-era response: \"Naturally, one follows the fate of marriage—where the husband goes, the wife follows.\"","The man nodded, clearly approving of her answer. But his questioning did not stop there. \"Why are you searching for your son alone? Where is your husband?\"","Dai Li adopted a sorrowful expression. \"I wonder which husband Your Excellency is referring to?\"","Qin Shaozong paused. \"How many husbands have you had?\""]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10","paragraphs":["\"I have had five husbands before, just enough to count on one hand.\"","Dai Li sighed with a hint of melancholy: \"My fate has been fraught with hardship, which is why I gradually traveled north from Jiaozhou. In truth, I deceived you last night—my son’s father was no commoner. Judging by his demeanor, he likely came from a prominent clan, though I don’t know his exact identity. I only know his name was Qin Yi, styled Huali. He was elusive, his returns unpredictable, and he rarely stayed by my side or our son’s.\"","This was the new story she had concocted after tossing and turning all night.","What else could she do? She had just claimed her husband was a commoner, only to be caught with small iron pieces hidden in her undergarments. Common folk reserved every scrap of iron for blades—such extravagance was unthinkable for them.","If the \"commoner husband\" story didn’t hold, she’d fabricate a mysterious noble instead. While men in ancient times could take concubines, they weren’t without limits—the number was restricted.","For instance, the Duduan recorded: \"The Son of Heaven takes twelve women, symbolizing the twelve months—three consorts and nine concubines. Lords take nine women, symbolizing the nine provinces—one wife and eight concubines. High ministers take one wife and two concubines. Scholars take one wife and one concubine.\"","In short, these were the official limits. What if one still craved more?","Then they kept women outside the household—hence the existence of unofficial concubines.","After much deliberation, Dai Li decided to reinvent herself as someone whose background would be difficult to verify, yet just plausible enough to pass scrutiny.","After all, she was accustomed to switching husbands. Her current one was often absent, and she felt no deep attachment to him. Naturally, when a higher branch appeared, she wouldn’t hesitate to climb it—especially when he’d promised to help find her son.","Qin Shaozong twisted the ring on his finger.","Qin Yi, Qin Huali.","No such name existed among the outstanding scions of the Qin family’s main or collateral branches. Was this Qin Yi simply too obscure to be known, or was the name itself false?","If the latter, was it because \"Qin Yi\" wished to conceal his identity, or...?","Qin Shaozong fixed his gaze on the woman before him. His light brown eyes, illuminated by the growing daylight, gleamed like a razor-sharp blade capable of slicing through all pretenses.","Dai Li’s heart raced uncontrollably. Unable to bear his scrutiny, she lowered her lashes to avoid his piercing stare.","He asked, \"Where is your home?\"","Dai Li heard her own heartbeat quicken. \"My husband dislikes me appearing in public or interacting with outsiders, so our humble abode lies in an inconspicuous woodland about ten miles west of Nankang Commandery. By the way, I overheard your household referring to you as 'Lord Marquis.' Might I ask which region you govern?\"","The last question was posed with an air of naivety—fitting for a woman with no grasp of politics.","A governor’s title included the name of his jurisdiction, so \"Lord Marquis\" likely followed the same pattern, didn’t it?","Qin Shaozong chuckled. \"The court has not granted me both a fief and a marquisate.\"","As soon as the words left his lips, he noticed the faint crease between her brows—a flicker of worry, or perhaps regret. Worry over a bad bargain, regret for following him too hastily.","A moment ago, he had found her naivety amusing. Now, the smile vanished from his lips. \"Since I am helping you find your son, shouldn’t you reciprocate?\"","Dai Li wasn’t sure how the conversation had taken this turn. Had she overplayed her hand, provoking him to assert dominance elsewhere?","Her scalp prickled with unease. \"Of course. My son is my life. I could never forget such a lifesaving favor. If there’s any way I can be of service, I won’t refuse. Only...\"","Here, she bit her lip, feigning embarrassment. \"Only, my monthly courses make intimacy impossible at the moment. Could you... wait a few days?\"","Her heart hammered in her throat, terrified he might reply with something like, \"No matter—there are many pleasures short of the final act.\" But perhaps he wasn’t so crude, or perhaps he still remembered she was injured. Thankfully, her fears didn’t materialize.","Qin Shaozong said, \"Not intimacy. Last night, when I searched Jiang Mansion, I used the pretext of a missing concubine. Governor Jiang took an interest and may have his wife speak with you later. Do you know how to respond?\"","Though he framed it as a question about \"later,\" Dai Li understood his meaning extended far beyond the governor’s wife. She grasped the underlying message: \"Rest assured, my lord, I know what to say. But to avoid slips, could you share some details?\"","\"I lead three thousand Black Cavalry from Weizhou, en route to Ying Commandery to suppress a major salt smuggler surnamed Li. My stop in Nankang is merely incidental.\" He briefly outlined the smuggler Li Zan’s background. Since she’d be at his side, it was inevitable she’d pick up some knowledge about the man.","Dai Li’s eyelid twitched.","In ancient times, soldiers were the most critical strategic resource. Modern dramas and novels often exaggerated numbers—even the mighty Tang Dynasty’s total military strength never reached the fanciful \"million-strong armies\" depicted.","During the early Eastern Han, the entire nation’s forces numbered around three hundred thousand. A warlord commanding even ten thousand—even if half were feeble or infirm—could dominate a region. After all, Dong Zhuo once cowed the central army with just three thousand men.","The Black Cavalry—clearly an elite mounted unit.","Cavalry were the empire’s most prized military assets. And he had three thousand at his disposal? How many more remained unseen?","Dai Li inwardly gasped. Suddenly, the title \"Lord Marquis\" carried no exaggeration—this man had undoubtedly earned his rank through genuine military merit.","Qin Shaozong continued, \"My name is Qin Shaozong, styled Changgeng, of ancestral home in Youzhou’s Yuyang. A month ago, someone presented a beauty to the emperor, which led to our meeting. You and your maid fell ill on the journey. She was frail and didn’t survive, while you barely pulled through. Due to your poor condition, you remained hidden in the carriage when we arrived yesterday.\"","His eyes swept over her, amusement flickering in their depths. \"You’re simple-minded, jealous, and spoiled. You often threw tantrums over subpar meals during the trip. Last night, irritated by your antics, I deliberately asked Jiang Chonghai for a nonexistent dancer and leaked the news to you, hoping you’d behave. Instead, you flew into a rage and sneaked out. To save face, I announced my concubine had gone missing in the mansion while secretly searching for you. As for how I coaxed you back afterward—well, that’s a private matter between us.\"","Dai Li realized he wanted her to play a role in this charade. Thoughtfully, she said, \"You wish for me to relay this 'truth'—and our private reconciliation—to the governor’s wife?\"","Qin Shaozong smiled. \"You’re not as dull as you seem.\"","Dai Li pressed further, \"How spoiled should I act? Any limits?\"","\"Act as spoiled as a favored concubine would. Tearing the roof off wouldn’t be out of line,\" he replied.","Dai Li felt goosebumps rise on her back as he spoke in that half-amused, half-mocking tone. At that moment, it was as if she were deep in a jungle, surrounded by dense foliage, with a vicious tiger lurking beside her—its fur blending seamlessly into the environment, its predatory gaze fixed on the outside world.","Only now did Dai Li finally understand the unease she had felt the night before when she encountered two maidservants, one of whom clearly recognized her but deliberately pretended not to.","He and that Lord Jiang were nothing more than cordial on the surface, each deeply wary of the other. That was why, when he had sought her out earlier, the servants in the mansion had likely feigned compliance while secretly defying his orders under their master’s instructions.","After a moment of contemplation, Dai Li ventured cautiously, \"My Lord, the overall framework shall follow your design, but might this humble one have some freedom with the finer details?\"","Qin Shaozong agreed.","Seeing that he seemed unusually amenable, Dai Li pressed further, \"Since Your Lordship and I met a month ago, the matter of you helping me search for my son...\"","\"Naturally, it will proceed in secret,\" Qin Shaozong replied. Noting the disappointment in her downcast eyes, he added, \"If the boy isn’t found within Jiang Mansion, we’ll search outside. As long as he’s still within Nankang Commandery, even if he’s hidden in the most remote corner, we’ll dig him out.\"","\"To make the act convincing, perhaps you could order someone to create a new identity document for me,\" Dai Li suggested softly. \"That way, I can flaunt it before Lady Jiang, ensuring she believes it without doubt.\"","The identity document, or \"chuan,\" bore a person’s name and place of origin. It was both a symbol and proof of one’s status—without it, traveling far was nearly impossible for those who weren’t slaves or vagrants.","As the favored jewel of the Marquis, how could she allow herself to remain among the ranks of undocumented concubines and servants?","Qin Shaozong said simply, \"Granted.\"","Dai Li couldn’t suppress a smile and was about to thank him when he remarked, \"So pleased over a mere document?\"","Her heart skipped a beat, but she refused to admit it. \"My Lord misunderstands. This humble one rejoices because we’ve reached a full agreement, and the day I recover my son draws near. Rest assured, once I step beyond this courtyard, I shall be the spoiled concubine who flaunts your favor—leaving no room for suspicion.\"","\"Not from the moment you leave here, but from this afternoon onward. I’ll have two maidservants from Jiang Mansion sent to attend to you.\" Qin Shaozong rose from the folding chair.","Dai Li assumed he was leaving and prepared to bid him farewell, but instead of turning away, he took a step forward.","The chair had been placed barely an arm’s length from the couch, and now, with that single step, they stood so close that the slightest lift of her hand would brush against the dark fabric of his robe.","The man leaned down, one arm encircling her waist while the other slid beneath her knees, lifting her effortlessly into his embrace.","Dai Li gasped, instinctively clutching the wrinkled fabric of his belt sash. His body radiated heat like a furnace—her shoulder, pressed against his chest, and the bend of her legs, cradled in his arms, grew uncomfortably warm. \"...My Lord?\"","\"I’ve had them prepare a side chamber for you. You’ll move there.\" Qin Shaozong carried her out of the small room.","Dai Li lowered her eyes. It made sense—what kind of outrageously spoiled concubine would live in a servant’s cramped quarters?","As they stepped outside, they encountered Yan San, who was moving his belongings to the adjacent room, and Mo Yanyun, who had just returned from outside. Both men froze at the sight.","\"Fetch the mansion physician,\" Qin Shaozong ordered before carrying Dai Li into Yan San’s former room.","Mo Yanyun turned to Yan San. \"Last night, His Lordship told me he had a plan to achieve twice the result with half the effort, and that ‘Fengchun’ would play a part. Has the scheme already begun? Since when does His Lordship stoop to such condescension?\"","Yan San turned on his heel without a word and strode away.","\"Hey, where are you going? I’m talking to you!\" Mo Yanyun called after him, annoyed.","Without looking back, Yan San replied, \"Fetching the physician.\""]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11","paragraphs":["In the main chamber of Jiang Mansion.","\"Is there a dancer or concubine in my rear courtyard named Fengchun?\" Jiang Chonghai asked his wife, Yun Rong.","Yun Rong thought for a moment. \"No, there isn't. Why do you ask?\"","\"Yesterday, Qin Shaozong suddenly asked me for this dancer during the banquet, but then never mentioned it again. It’s quite strange.\" Jiang Chonghai stroked the thin mustache on his upper lip and instructed his wife, \"They took two maidservants, didn’t they? Find an opportunity to question them thoroughly. Make them report every detail about the situation in that lady’s chambers.\"","Yun Rong covered her lips with a light laugh. \"Such a trivial matter hardly needs your reminder. I’ve already arranged it—Tao Xiang came by earlier. According to her, that Lady Dai Li is breathtakingly beautiful, with skin like snow and cheeks like peach blossoms, as if she stepped out of a painting. With such a peerless beauty by his side, even if Lord Qin is momentarily intrigued by wildflowers outside, he’ll likely forget them the moment he returns to her.\"","\"Is his favored concubine truly that stunning?\" Jiang Chonghai’s tone was unreadable.","Yun Rong paused. Though she knew her husband had always been fond of beauty—hence the mansion full of dancers—she couldn’t help but feel irked that his focus lingered there. Her voice cooled slightly. \"Well, Tao Xiang was practically spellbound, so I suppose it must be true. After all, Lord Qin holds high rank and has campaigned across the land for years. His tastes must be far more refined than ours, confined to this small province. What kind of beauty hasn’t he seen? For him to be so protective, Lady Dai must be extraordinary.\"","\"Protective? Why protective?\" Jiang Chonghai snapped back to attention.","Yun Rong recounted how Dai Li had twisted her ankle and how Qin Shaozong had urgently summoned the mansion physician. She added, \"...Though Tao Xiang mentioned she’s uneducated, spoiled, and rather difficult to serve.\"","Jiang Chonghai saw no issue with this. A great beauty was entitled to her temper. \"Did Qin Shaozong bring only this one favored concubine on this trip?\"","Yun Rong nodded, saying it was likely so.","Jiang Chonghai paced the room. \"This afternoon, personally deliver a gift to visit Lady Dai. Accommodate any other requests she might have.\"","Yun Rong remained silent.","Noticing her reluctance, Jiang Chonghai scolded, \"Just go. Is this the time to stand on ceremony? So what if she’s a concubine and not the principal wife? Qin Shaozong’s three thousand troops are still camped outside the province. If you befriend her, perhaps she can whisper in his ear and hasten his departure.\"","Yun Rong had no choice but to agree.","The afternoon was clear and bright, with a gentle breeze carrying the scent of flowers through the carved wooden lattice window. The gauzy curtains, embroidered with peony motifs, fluttered dreamily in the wind, creating an ethereal beauty.","Yet even more captivating than this scene was the woman reclining on the cushioned chair by the window. Sunlight bathed her, accentuating her crimson lips and snow-white skin, as if the essence of spring itself brimmed within her. She resembled a peony nourished by the sun, moon, and dew—even the slightest lift of her eyelids carried a mesmerizing, languid grace.","Yun Rong froze in place.","But the woman in the room merely glanced past her indifferently, as if Yun Rong were nothing more than an inconsequential ornament or a new servant unworthy of her attention.","Yun Rong snapped back to reality, her expression darkening.","As the wife of the provincial governor, she had long since outlived her mother-in-law’s reign and hadn’t endured another woman’s disdain in years. Every lady in the province treated her with deference and flattery.","Yet today, she was slighted by a mere concubine!","Drawing on her years of experience, Yun Rong forced a smile. \"I heard you twisted your ankle, madam. Ah, it’s my fault—I should have added more lamps when arranging these quarters. I deeply apologize for the inconvenience.\"","Most people, upon hearing this and noting her attire, would deduce her status as the lady of the mansion. Combined with her humble apology, they would at least exchange pleasantries.","The woman on the chair did look at her again, but things didn’t proceed as Yun Rong expected.","\"Are you the steward’s wife?\" she asked.","Yun Rong nearly saw black. Her smile faltered once more. Was Lady Dai truly this empty-headed, or was this a deliberate power play?","Dai Li lazily straightened, seemingly convinced of her own assumption, and launched into a rapid-fire critique: \"The arrangements here are indeed lacking. Not only are the decorations sparse, but what even are these? The vases aren’t gilded—they look downright cheap. Spring is when peach blossoms bloom, so why aren’t there any in the room? The peony embroidery on the curtains is passable, but the color is too plain, almost inauspicious. And this table—\"","With every word, Yun Rong’s head throbbed. Then, to her disbelief, Dai Li added, \"It really is your oversight for not placing enough lamps, which caused me to trip. You should report back and accept your punishment.\"","When Yun Rong stood motionless, stunned, Dai Li waved her off. \"Did you memorize everything I said? Go handle it.\"","Yun Rong’s face turned ashen. Finally, her maidservant seized the chance to interject: \"My lady’s husband is Governor Jiang.\" Not some lowly steward.","Dai Li feigned surprise.","Just as Yun Rong was about to exhale in relief, Dai Li clicked her tongue and chided, \"Why didn’t you say so earlier?\"","Yun Rong: \"...\"","She suddenly recalled Tao Xiang’s description of Lady Dai as spoiled. In her opinion, this woman wasn’t just spoiled—she was outrageously arrogant and shockingly devoid of social graces.","\"Tao Xiang, serve tea to the governor’s wife.\" Still not rising from her chair, Dai Li gestured for Yun Rong to take a seat opposite her.","Yun Rong stood rooted for several breaths, swallowing her indignation before complying.","\"You came to chat, yet you brought gifts?\" Dai Li eyed the brocade box in the maidservant’s hands.","\"My husband insisted I bring you presents after hearing of your mishap. Do see if you like them. If not, I’ll replace them,\" Yun Rong replied, adjusting her approach.","Dealing with someone this shallow required bluntness. Subtlety would be lost on her walnut-sized brain. Best to be direct.","Her instincts proved correct—Lady Dai’s expression finally softened slightly.","Dai Li opened the box, revealing an assortment of jewelry: a gold hairpin adorned with a ruby, a honey-colored crystal hairpin, twisted-gold peony hairpins, and a pair of decent-quality bangle bracelets.","Picking up one bangle with slender fingers, Dai Li tossed it back after a glance. \"Too big. Not my size.\"","Yun Rong’s temple twitched.","Gift boxes like these were usually regifted as-is or replenished after selecting preferred pieces—never had she seen someone so brazenly nitpick.","Taking a deep breath, Yun Rong silently reminded herself not to argue with a foolish woman—someone with such a temperament would be far easier to manipulate than a composed one. She warmly reached out, \"Let me see what size bracelet would suit you.\"","Dai Li didn’t pull away.","Seizing the opportunity, Yun Rong lavished praise on Dai Li’s beauty, and the latter smiled as if pleased, gradually opening up the conversation.","During their chat, Yun Rong learned that aside from her sprained ankle, Dai Li was also feeling unwell. Alarmed, Yun Rong pressed for details and immediately sent a maid to summon the mansion’s physician.","\"It’s nothing, just my monthly courses. My body isn’t at its best,\" Dai Li waved it off.","Yun Rong froze.","She recalled her husband mentioning at noon that Lord Qin had asked him for a dancer named Fengchun during the banquet. So, was the reason Lord Qin wanted someone because Lady Dai couldn’t serve him?","Connecting this to last night, when Lord Qin had searched the entire mansion for someone, Yun Rong felt she’d stumbled upon a private matter. She comforted, \"Lady Dai’s grace is unparalleled—how could ordinary beauties compare? Even if those dancers caught Lord Qin’s eye, it would only be a fleeting fancy. With the moon shining so brightly, how dare the stars compete?\"","Yun Rong was certain her words would soothe, and indeed, the woman across from her smiled—just...","A little too brightly. It didn’t seem like she’d been comforted, but rather as if she was laughing at Yun Rong’s mistake.","Confused, Yun Rong hesitated.","\"Who told you a dancer caught Lord Qin’s attention?\" Dai Li picked up a small bamboo token from the table, twirling it playfully. \"I dare you to check the rear courtyard. I guarantee you won’t find anyone named Fengchun, even if you turn the entire Jiang Mansion upside down.\"","Yun Rong was stunned.","What did she mean?","Lord Qin had explicitly asked for someone by name at the banquet—how could she be so certain there was no such person?","Leaning forward, Yun Rong asked, \"Why do you say that?\"","Dai Li grinned. \"Because there is no Fengchun. Lord Qin made her up to mess with me—he was annoyed I’d been giving him attitude on the way here and wanted to teach me a lesson. But I’m not falling for it. After all, he’s hopelessly devoted to me and even swore a blood oath to the heavens. Last night, I grilled him, and sure enough, it was all nonsense. This ‘Fengchun’ was just a ruse to scare me. But don’t spread this around, or Qin Changgeng will be furious.\"","Yun Rong gaped.","Earlier, her husband had described Lord Qin as shrewd and cunning. Was his reputation exaggerated? Were his so-called brilliance and intimidation all just a facade to make others cower?","Otherwise, how could such a formidable man swear a blood oath for the sake of a vapid beauty like this? Blood oaths weren’t to be taken lightly—anger the heavens, and the consequences ranged from bad luck to being struck by lightning!","Or was this just how men were? Willing to say anything for a moment of pleasure in bed.","When no flattering response came, Dai Li frowned. \"Why that look? Don’t you believe me?\"","Yun Rong forced a stiff smile. \"O-of course I do.\"","Dai Li lovingly stroked the bamboo token before flipping it to show off. \"See? This is Lord Qin’s and my token of love.\"","Yun Rong took a closer look and recognized it—","A household register.","All citizens, except slaves and vagrants, possessed one.","It dawned on Yun Rong then—the reason Dai Li was so smug was likely because she’d once been a servant, without a registered identity. Lord Qin must have arranged this for her, hence the \"token of love.\"","After offering some obligatory praise, Yun Rong casually remarked, \"Such a precious thing should be kept safe.\"","\"I carry it with me—it won’t get lost,\" Dai Li cheerfully tied the token to her waistband.","Yun Rong cautiously steered the conversation toward Qin Shaozong. Dai Li answered with smug smiles, holding nothing back.","An hour later, Yun Rong stepped out of the room in a daze, nearly tripping over the threshold on her way out.","\"Tao Xiang, go pick fresh flowers from the garden and replace these wilted ones. Ding Xiang, fetch that vase Lady Dai mentioned from the storeroom,\" Dai Li ordered her maids.","Once they left, she exhaled deeply, rubbing her temples wearily.","Playing the fool was exhausting. Who knew even being a simple-minded beauty would be such hard work?","Her gaze fell on the bamboo token at her waist, and her eyes darkened.","If Zhouzhou wasn’t in Nankang County, she’d head south to check near her hometown. As for that salt-smuggler-infested Ying County? Someone else could deal with it—it had nothing to do with her.","The excuse of her monthly courses wouldn’t last much longer. Time was running out."]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12","paragraphs":["Dai Li's foot was only slightly sprained, not serious, and after resting in the mansion for two days, she could walk again. During these two days, Yun Rong came to keep her company every day, chatting about everything under the sun, doing her utmost to amuse Dai Li and cheer her up. Since Yun Rong never arrived empty-handed—each time bringing gifts better than the last—the two became as close as sisters in just two days.","\"Sister Yun, I’ve been in Nankang County for some time but haven’t left the mansion yet. Now that I can walk, why don’t we go out and explore the market?\" Dai Li asked for her opinion, though she had already beckoned a maid to help her change.","Yun Rong hesitated. \"Little sister, as they say, 'a torn ligament takes a hundred days to heal.' Shouldn’t you rest a bit longer in the mansion?\" If anything happened outside, she wouldn’t be able to explain it to Marquis Qin.","Dai Li waved it off. \"It’s just a minor sprain—my foot isn’t broken. Besides, we’ll take the carriage and won’t have to walk much.\"","Yun Rong tried again. \"My husband is hosting a banquet this evening, and the Marquis will surely bring you along. If we return late...\"","\"It’s still early!\" Dai Li cut her off. \"If Sister Yun doesn’t want to accompany me, just say so. I’ll go out on my own.\"","With things put so bluntly, Yun Rong could hardly refuse. She had no choice but to order the carriage prepared and accompany this demanding lady out.","Only then did Dai Li smile in satisfaction.","Her smile was genuine. Over the past two days, her people had secretly combed through Jiang Mansion without finding any trace of Zhou Zhou. It seemed her son truly wasn’t there.","If he wasn’t in the mansion, she would have to look outside.","The carriage wheels rumbled over the stone-paved road, heading toward the bustling market. Once outside the mansion, the quiet gave way to clamor, and the lively scent of everyday life seeped through the lowered curtains.","Dai Li lifted a corner of the carriage curtain, letting in the warm sunlight as she caught sight of the lively streets. Vendors crowded shoulder to shoulder, their stalls packed with an array of goods, a dazzling spectacle.","Her brows relaxed slightly.","The dancers’ indifference to the corpse had led her to believe they were numb to death, and with salt smugglers running rampant, she had assumed the world had already descended into chaos.","Yet the bustling city brought her a sense of reassurance. Perhaps the times were troubled, or perhaps the world was on the brink of upheaval, but everything happened gradually—chaos didn’t arrive overnight.","Take the late Eastern Han Dynasty, for example. Thirty-six years passed between the Yellow Turban Rebellion and Emperor Xian’s abdication. For someone short-lived, that could be an entire lifetime.","Dai Li fervently hoped this \"unrest\" was merely a budding sign, not yet at its worst.","Their first stop was a silk shop, a favorite among ladies. As a local, Yun Rong naturally took on the role of guide, selecting Ruixiang Silk Shop. The shop was spacious, its entrance spotless, with a few donkey carts and a carriage parked outside. Neatly dressed attendants carried out bundles of wrapped fabric.","Clearly, this shop catered to high-end clientele.","The moment their carriage stopped, a sharp-eyed attendant rushed over with a small stool in hand. He placed it by the carriage door, and if not for the guards blocking him, he would have opened the door himself.","After all, carriages were rare in Nankang County—only a handful of households owned one.","When he recognized Yun Rong stepping out, his smile turned obsequious. \"No wonder the magpies were singing on the branches today—it’s because the Prefect’s Lady has graced us with her presence! Please, come inside.\"","But then Yun Rong turned back, eagerly speaking to the lady still inside the carriage. Soon, a second woman descended, bringing with her a wave of exquisite fragrance.","The attendant froze, only snapping out of it after the two had already entered the shop.","It was nearly noon, the busiest time of day. Inside, Dai Li saw young ladies shopping together for clothes, as well as women with their hair tied in simple buns.","With so many people, the noise was inevitable—some chatting idly, others discussing fabrics, and attendants bustling about.","Amid the din, Dai Li faintly overheard someone say:","\"I’ve heard there’s been an increase in refugees lately. That ruined temple outside the eastern suburbs has practically become their battleground.\"","\"My son told me he passed by that temple yesterday while out for a stroll. He saw about a dozen people inside—some old, some young, all dressed in rags.\"","\"With so many refugees appearing suddenly, there must have been a disaster somewhere, and disasters always bring more suffering. Heaven knows how many more will lose their homes.\"","\"Exactly. My son mentioned seeing a child there, about eight or nine years old, fair-skinned and dressed a little better than the others, with short hair. Who knows if he was kidnapped and had his hair cut by traffickers.\"","\"It must be traffickers—they’re experts at disguising their victims...\"","Dai Li didn’t catch the rest. Those key words—eight or nine years old, fair-skinned, short hair—swelled in her mind like a sponge soaking up water, consuming her thoughts entirely.","Could it be Zhou Zhou?","\"Ah—sister, where are you going? Didn’t we agree to look at clothes?\" Yun Rong reached out instinctively as Dai Li suddenly turned to leave.","Dai Li’s arm was caught, and with it, her scattered thoughts snapped back. She stood still for a moment, listening expressionlessly as Yun Rong called her name several times.","\"Sister, what’s wrong?\" Yun Rong felt a flicker of unease.","Finally, Dai Li turned to her, the corners of her eyes faintly red. \"Sister Yun, I just overheard them talking about refugees outside the city—there are even children among them. They must be starving and barely clothed. It’s heartbreaking. Why don’t we bring them some food at the temple outside the city?\"","Though phrased as a question, she was already pulling Yun Rong toward the exit.","Yun Rong was stunned. Over the past two days, she had come to realize that this favored consort of the Marquis was a spoiled, naive woman—as if heaven had poured all its blessings into her beauty, leaving none for her brains.","But she never expected Dai Li to be so sentimental on top of being empty-headed.","Disasters and suffering were hardly rare these days. There were too many pitiable souls in the world—uttering a word or two of sympathy was kindness enough. Who had the time to help every single one?","Yet Dai Li was already dragging her into the carriage, ordering Yan San to buy flatbread along the way.","The carriage, which had been parked outside Ruixiang Silk Shop, now headed out of the county. The sturdy horses moved swiftly, and before long, Dai Li caught sight of a temple.","The place truly lived up to its description as \"ruined.\" The lacquer on the signboard had peeled away, the wood riddled with worm-eaten holes. Broken walls, crumbling pillars, and drafty windows—it was impossible to tell how many years it had been abandoned.","An old saying warned, \"Never enter a temple alone,\" as these deserted places often harbored bandits evading the authorities.","But Dai Li, accompanied by guards, paid no heed. The moment the carriage stopped, she leaped out eagerly.","The dilapidated temple was small but unusually filthy, the moment they stepped inside, a wave of rancid stench assaulted their senses. A few heads peeked out at the sound, initially thinking their own comrades had returned or some fool had come to challenge their territory—only to be met with the sight of a stunningly beautiful woman.","Some faces immediately twisted with greed, but then they noticed the man following close behind her, a short knife hanging at his waist. His gaze was sharp as a blade, making them instinctively shrink back.","Armed, physically imposing, and not alone.","These were no ordinary visitors.","Dai Li paid no mind to the onlookers’ thoughts and cut straight to the point: \"Is there a nine-year-old child with short hair here? Where is he now?\"","The vagrants exchanged uneasy glances.","Yun Rong, recalling fragments of gossip she’d overheard at the silk shop, couldn’t help but give Dai Li a thoughtful look.","\"Lady Dai once had a nephew who was abducted. She and her brother were deeply attached, so she’s been distraught over it. The Prefect’s wife understands,\" Yan San explained briefly.","Yun Rong suddenly grasped the situation.","With this context, she wasn’t surprised when Dai Li began searching every corner of the temple.","Dai Li combed through the place with desperate hope, spotting several children along the way—including the fair-skinned, short-haired boy others had mentioned.","But alas, it wasn’t her little one.","Watching the child devour a flatbread with ravenous hunger, Dai Li’s heart ached with a cold, piercing pain.","\"Everyone has their own fate. We’ve done all we can—some things simply can’t be forced, sister. Let’s go back,\" Yun Rong said, covering her nose with a perfumed handkerchief, unable to bear another moment in the foul-smelling ruin. Assuming Dai Li was hesitating out of misplaced sympathy, she added firmly, \"We’ve already distributed all our supplies. Standing around won’t help. We should return to the mansion and send more food later.\"","Dai Li seemed to think of something, then suddenly glanced down, her eyes glinting with something unreadable. \"As you say, sister,\" she replied.","Yun Rong wasted no time heading out.","Noticing no one was paying attention, Dai Li quickly untied the small bamboo token hanging at her waist and slipped it into her sleeve, using the wide fabric to conceal the now-empty spot at her hip.","The two women left the temple and boarded their carriage.","By the time they returned to Nankang County and entered the bustling streets, Dai Li gasped softly, \"Where’s my token?!\"","Yun Rong immediately looked at her waist—the small wooden plaque that usually hung there was indeed missing. Her first thought was that someone in the temple had sticky fingers, stealing it when they got too close.","\"I told you that place was crawling with thieves!\" Yun Rong fumed. \"Turn the carriage around—we’re going back.\"","\"No!\" Dai Li stopped her urgently. Meeting Yun Rong’s puzzled gaze, she lowered her voice. \"Some of the guards accompanying us today are Marquis Qin’s men. If we turn back now, he’ll know I lost the token—our keepsake.\"","Yun Rong scoffed, \"So what? Given how much he dotes on you, he’d just make you another.\"","Dai Li laughed awkwardly. \"True, but... I’ve already lost it four times before.\"","Yun Rong: \"...\"","No wonder—if she flaunted it every day, losing it was inevitable.","\"Besides, I’ve been quarreling with him lately. I can’t let him catch me at a disadvantage now. He mustn’t find out,\" Dai Li pleaded, clutching Yun Rong’s sleeve. \"Dearest sister, could you do me a favor...?\"","That evening, a banquet was held—once again in honor of Qin Shaozong. But unlike before, Dai Li’s recovery meant female guests could now attend.","When the two women arrived at the main hall, Qin Shaozong and Jiang Chonghai were already there, seated at the head of the table, drinking competitively.","A slender silhouette stretched into the hall with the setting sun, a delicate fragrance drifting in on the breeze. The man at the head of the table relaxed his brows, casually setting down his wine cup as he stood.","Qin Shaozong was tall—descending from the dais seemed to take only a few strides.","This was Dai Li’s first time performing this act in front of the Jiang couple. She was still gauging how far to take it when a strong arm suddenly wrapped around her waist, pulling her into an embrace.","The man held her close, his lips curving as he looked down. \"Back from your outing, my lady? No trouble, I hope?\"","Dai Li’s heart skipped a beat."]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13","paragraphs":["If you don’t want others to know, don’t do it in the first place. For a moment, Dai Li thought Qin Shaozong had discovered what she had done, but she quickly realized it was impossible—he couldn’t possibly know.","Yan San entered the main hall with her, and even if he had seen through her plan, he wouldn’t have had time to report it to Qin Shaozong. So the man must have spoken offhandedly.","No, not entirely offhanded. Given her current persona, it was perfectly reasonable for her to stir up minor trouble now and then.","Out of the corner of her eye, she noticed Yun Rong watching her, her expression tense. Dai Li knew what she was worried about.","Their secret collaboration had already been established, and Yun Rong was afraid she might use this opportunity to reconcile with Qin Shaozong. If they made up, Yun Rong’s position as the official wife would be meaningless.","This was her chance to whisper in his ear.","Dai Li raised a hand to press against Qin Shaozong’s chest, stopping him from coming closer. \"What kind of nonsense is that? In your eyes, am I really the type to cause trouble the moment you take your eyes off me?\"","After saying this, she suddenly changed her gesture from pressing to gripping, seizing his collar as she stood on tiptoe, frowning and sniffing. \"The banquet hasn’t even started, and you’re already reeking of alcohol. How much have you drunk? You should drink less—drinking on an empty stomach will make you drunk and harm your health. If you’re wasted tonight, don’t expect me to take care of you.\"","Qin Shaozong chuckled, clearly enjoying being scolded by his concubine in public. \"As my lady commands.\"","Yun Rong exchanged a glance with Jiang Chonghai at the head of the table, giving a slight nod. Realizing they had finally found the opportunity to influence Qin Shaozong, Jiang Chonghai brightened and ordered servants to bring out several more jars of wine.","With all the distinguished guests present, the evening banquet began.","Qin Shaozong and Jiang Chonghai sat at the head of the table, while Dai Li and Yun Rong took the first seats on either side below them.","The banquet table was laden with delicacies—steamed lamb tripe, roasted deer tail, braised crucian carp, chestnut chicken, and cold dishes like wild garlic and asparagus salad. There were also thinly sliced, translucent raw fish, accompanied by sweet soup and honey-glazed pastries. It was a feast fit for royalty.","Of course, aside from the lavish spread, the banquet also featured towering stacks of wine jars.","The women chatted and laughed, while the men engaged in drinking contests.","Dai Li noticed one detail—they drank fiercely and barely touched the food. Every time Qin Shaozong picked up his chopsticks to take a bite, three out of five times, he was interrupted and ended up drinking instead.","She nibbled on a piece of chestnut chicken, guessing that Jiang Chonghai was trying to get Qin Shaozong drunk.","Many military men loved wine, and countless had suffered for it. In the past, Dian Wei had been robbed of his weapons while drunk and died in battle, and Zhang Yide lost Xuzhou due to his indulgence in drink. A little wine was fine, but excess led to disaster.","For now, she and Qin Shaozong were bound by shared interests. The search for her son in Nankang County wasn’t complete yet, and she couldn’t afford for him to falter at this critical moment.","Thud!","Dai Li suddenly slammed her chopsticks on the table.","She timed it perfectly—right in a lull between conversations—so everyone heard.","All eyes turned to her, but she stared straight at the man at the head of the table, her tone petulant. \"Qin Changgeng, the smell of alcohol is making me sick.\"","The hall fell silent.","Jiang Chonghai was so shocked he spilled his wine.","She dared to call Qin Shaozong by his full name in public and speak to him so insolently? It was just as his wife had said—this Lady Dai was spoiled and lacked propriety.","Yet the man in question showed no anger, only a tipsy laugh. \"If my lady dislikes it, then I shall stop. It wouldn’t do to anger her and be barred from her chambers tonight. Servants, remove these wine jars.\"","Jiang Chonghai’s brow twitched, stunned by Qin Shaozong’s submission. He was frantic—the whole point of this banquet was to get him drunk and test certain crucial information.","For the past few days, Yun Rong had been visiting Dai Li, not just to build rapport but also to uncover an unexpected lead.","According to Dai Li, Qin Shaozong had recently taken in an eccentric strategist. This man was brilliant but loathed attention, preferring to lurk in the shadows like a damp mushroom. He rarely appeared in public yet held immense influence over Qin Shaozong.","For instance, the infamous spy scheme that had shaken the world was actually his idea. This time, when Qin Shaozong set out to suppress the salt smugglers, the \"Mushroom Scholar\" had been summoned to accompany him. But halfway through the journey, he fell ill and had to be left behind to recuperate.","That was why there were no strategists among the entourage—not because none had come, but because one had been left behind.","These details hadn’t been revealed all at once. Yun Rong had carefully extracted them from Dai Li, piecing together the fragments of information.","Jiang Chonghai’s paranoia made him suspect a trap, but he couldn’t shake the possibility that this \"Mushroom Scholar\" truly existed.","Noble families amassed wealth and, in turbulent times, raised private armies to carve out their own domains. The scions of these families became warlords, recruiting strategists for wisdom and generals for strength.","As the chessmaster, a warlord only needed to be good at accepting counsel and displaying some decisiveness to thrive. His political background and military resources gave him an inherent advantage far beyond ordinary men.","True geniuses who combined intellect and martial prowess were as rare as phoenix feathers. Qin Shaozong had been born into privilege and possessed extraordinary combat skills—how could he possibly have everything?","Rumors spread like wildfire. Perhaps Qin Shaozong’s fearsome reputation was just a carefully crafted illusion. Jiang Chonghai speculated maliciously.","After much deliberation, he had arranged this banquet to probe the truth. Now, with his plan on the verge of collapse, he couldn’t let it end like this. He shot Yun Rong a meaningful glance.","Dai Li had initially worried that Qin Shaozong’s drunkenness might ruin things, but hearing his words, she relaxed.","Oh, he’s still so clear-headed? His alcohol tolerance must be excellent. Then we can proceed as planned.","\"Sister, I’m feeling a bit stifled too. Why don’t we take a stroll together?\" Yun Rong ventured nervously.","She had no confidence—this woman was notoriously self-centered and heedless of others’ feelings. Yet, surprisingly, it worked.","\"Fine. I’ve eaten my fill anyway. A walk would do me good.\" Dai Li set down her chopsticks and stood, then added to Qin Shaozong, \"You reek of alcohol. Sleep alone tonight.\"","After the two women left the hall, Jiang Chonghai sighed. \"Lady Dai is like a peony in moonlight when silent, but once she opens her mouth, she turns into wild ginger—spicy indeed.\"","\"I like that about her. Ordinary women lack flavor,\" Qin Shaozong replied with a laugh.","Jiang Chonghai tried to coax him. \"Since Lady Dai has left, shall we continue?\"","Qin Shaozong remained silent.","Jiang Chonghai sighed again. \"Ah, my wife probably won’t let me back into our chambers tonight either. When drinking companions meet, they should drink their fill. The night is long—why not drown in wine? Do you dare accept the challenge?\"","\"What’s there to fear?\"","After leaving the main hall, Dai Li and Yun Rong wandered aimlessly through the estate.","The prefect's residence was built extravagantly, with pavilions scattered throughout and winding corridors. Along the main path, exquisitely carved white jade lantern covers stood every ten paces or so. A single candle placed inside would cast a soft, glowing circle of light.","As the sun dipped below the horizon and the last traces of daylight faded, night fell. Dai Li watched the maids deftly light the lanterns and thought to herself how lavish this prefect's estate was—even candles were lit outdoors.","\"Sister Yun, about the matter I asked you to help with this afternoon... could you have it settled by tomorrow?\" Dai Li murmured.","For commoners, replacing a lost identity document was a tedious process. One had to report the loss to the authorities, submit proof and application forms, and wait for approval before receiving a new one.","But for the powerful, especially someone like Prefect Jiang Chonghai—the highest authority in Nankang Prefecture—reissuing a document was effortless. A single word from him would send his subordinates scrambling to get it done, even if it meant working overtime.","Yun Rong's eyes flickered. \"Why the urgency, little sister? Is Lord Qin about to leave Nankang soon?\"","\"Of course I'm anxious! If he finds out I've lost my identity document again, he’ll have another excuse to control me,\" Dai Li sighed. \"As for when he’ll leave, he hasn’t told me. He only mentioned taking me to see the peach blossoms. I’ve never seen endless stretches of peach trees before—I’ll have to take a good look when the time comes.\"","Yun Rong froze.","Peach blossom groves?","Lord Qin’s mission was clear: he was here to eradicate the salt smugglers. Nankang Prefecture lay directly west of Ying Prefecture, and there were three possible routes to get there.","The first was to march northeast first, then turn southeast—a detour from above. This was the upper path.","The second was to head straight west without changing direction, directly into Ying Prefecture. This was the middle path.","The third was to march southeast first, then turn northeast—a detour from below. This was the lower path.","Of these three, only the upper path passed by a mountain covered in peach trees. Locals called it Peach Blossom Peak, and in spring, the slopes were blanketed in blossoms—a breathtaking sight.","\"Sister Yun, will you promise me this?\"","Yun Rong’s mind was entirely occupied with Qin Shaozong’s marching route. She had no attention to spare for anything else and only nodded hastily.","Dai Li smiled in satisfaction.","After another stroll, Yun Rong spoke up. \"Little sister, let’s head back. Even though the wine was eventually taken away, men are fickle creatures—they can’t resist the lure of alcohol. Who knows if a casual remark might stir their cravings again? It’s safer to return and keep an eye on things.\"","\"Lord Qin has a decent tolerance. He’s unlikely to cause a drunken scene,\" Dai Li said, her objective achieved. She had no desire to stay outside feeding mosquitoes any longer.","They had left midway through the banquet, and by the time they returned to the main hall, the evening feast was winding down.","The opulent hall was thick with the lingering scent of alcohol. One didn’t even need to see the countless wine jars littering the tables and floor—the heavy aroma alone was proof they had indulged again.","A piercing gaze locked onto her. Dai Li looked up and met the eyes of Qin Shaozong, seated at the head of the room.","His complexion wasn’t fair, so only a faint flush tinted his cheeks, making it hard to gauge how drunk he was. But his eyes held a dark, smoldering intensity—something between desire and something else entirely, enough to make one’s heart race.","In full view of everyone, he beckoned to her.","\"Come here, my lady.\""]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14","paragraphs":["All eyes converged upon her, the scent of alcohol in the air thickening into a tangible haze. The surrounding gazes gleamed like eerie green wolf eyes—faceless, countless—fixated on her without blinking, as if a single misstep would send them lunging to tear her apart.","Dai Li felt goosebumps rise along her back.","She remained motionless for a long moment until the man at the head of the table called out again, \"My lady...\"","\"It seems you’ve grown deaf tonight, Qin Changgeng. Very well, have it your way.\" With those words, Dai Li turned and strode away under the stunned gazes of the crowd.","Even Yun Rong, who was well-acquainted with her willful nature, couldn’t help but pale.","This wasn’t some private quarrel behind closed doors—they were guests at a banquet! Throwing a tantrum like this was nothing short of trampling Marquis Qin’s dignity underfoot. Yun Rong imagined the roles reversed and concluded that if she had dared such behavior, she’d likely be handed a letter of divorce.","\"My lord, this...\" Jiang Chonghai was equally taken aback.","Qin Shaozong, however, showed no anger. He merely sighed with a faint smile. \"I provoked her first. I’ll make amends later.\"","A glint of something unreadable flashed in Jiang Chonghai’s eyes. For a man of his stature to openly admit he’d apologize to a mere concubine—clearly, the drink had gone to his head.","Elsewhere.","Dai Li returned to her chambers. After her maidservants attended to her washing, she dismissed them under the pretense of retiring for the night.","Closing the door, extinguishing the lamp, and slipping into bed—she moved in one fluid motion.","Lying beneath the covers, her heart raced wildly.","She and Yun Rong had left the estate at noon, then excused themselves midway through the evening banquet. There was too much to explain about what had transpired in between, and she couldn’t rule out the possibility of him coming to her quarters afterward.","She had to fall asleep quickly. Hopefully, the sight of a darkened room would deter him, and whatever needed saying could wait till morning.","A man dead drunk was harmless—incapable of rising in every sense. But one merely tipsy or halfway there? That was far more dangerous.","Dai Li usually slept soundly, but whether it was the night’s tension or something else, she tossed and turned, unable to drift off. Each time she shifted, it felt as though the sword of Damocles hung precariously above her.","The banquet in the main hall was already winding down when Dai Li left. Shortly after her departure, it disbanded entirely.","Most guests were thoroughly drunk, Jiang Chonghai among them—so much so that he needed two servants to support him as he staggered back to his quarters after bidding farewell to Qin Shaozong.","Yun Rong had long since instructed the maids to prepare hangover-relieving kudzu root soup. As soon as he sat, she brought him a bowl. \"Husband, drink this quickly, or you’ll suffer tomorrow.\"","Jiang Chonghai had spent the entire evening drinking, and the mere sight of liquid now turned his stomach. What rotten luck, he thought.","Tonight’s banquet had been held in Qin Shaozong’s honor. They’d started drinking long before the wives returned, and though he’d eaten beforehand to cushion his stomach, everyone else had pretended to drink on an empty stomach, keeping up the charade throughout the feast.","Yet despite drinking nonstop, they’d failed to reduce Qin Shaozong to a drunken mess. The man’s tolerance was inhuman—how infuriating.","\"Leave us,\" Jiang Chonghai dismissed the servants. Once the door shut, he turned to Yun Rong. \"Where did you and Lady Dai go when you left the estate at noon? What did she say? And why did you both leave the banquet early? Tell me everything—no detail is too small.\"","Yun Rong began with their noon excursion—first the silk shop, then Dai Li’s sudden detour to a ruined temple outside the city. She emphasized how Dai Li had lost her identity pass and sought her help to discreetly replace it, as well as the revelation during the banquet that Marquis Qin planned to take her to see the peach groves.","Jiang Chonghai’s expression shifted repeatedly. \"You’re certain she said ‘endless peach groves’?\"","Yun Rong huffed. \"Husband, you’ve stressed this matter’s importance a thousand times. How could I dare be careless? Every word is exact—that’s precisely what she said.\"","A cold laugh escaped Jiang Chonghai. \"Well played, Qin Shaozong. You dared deceive me.\"","After the women left, he’d seized the drunken moment to press Qin Shaozong about his plans to suppress Li Zan—asking about routes, tactics, and whether he could assist.","Qin Shaozong had paused briefly before launching into an elaborate explanation: a divided-force strategy, two units advancing via central and lower routes to simultaneously capture Ying Province.","A lie!","Had he not planted ears near Dai Li, he’d have been thoroughly fooled.","Clearly, Qin Shaozong’s tolerance wasn’t his only formidable trait. Perhaps he’d been slightly drunk, but not enough to forget his priorities. Of course—a man who’d held power for years might dote on Dai Li, but he’d never reveal his hand entirely to the Governor of Nankang Province, a man he barely knew. Such caution was only natural.","\"...Husband, should we arrange those two replacement passes for Lady Dai?\" Yun Rong asked.","\"Why would she need two? Isn’t one enough?\" Jiang Chonghai frowned.","Yun Rong scoffed. \"She’s hopelessly scatterbrained—why else would she have lost four passes before this? And now, after just one trip to the eastern city, she’s misplaced another. Wanting two this time is probably just her way of keeping a spare without having to confess to Marquis Qin. So, do we help her or not?\"","\"Two passes are nothing. Of course we’ll arrange them! She’ll be useful later—we can’t afford to alienate her now. Tell me everything you remember from the pass you saw.\" Jiang Chonghai, bloated from years of indulgence, slumped deeper into his seat, unwilling to move. \"Later, summon my brother. I have urgent matters to discuss with him. You’ll sleep in the adjacent room tonight.\"","After Yun Rong finished recounting the pass details, she reminded him, \"Don’t forget the kudzu soup, husband. I’ll take my leave.\"","Jiang Chonghai closed his eyes, offering no reply.","Roughly half an hour later, Jiang Chongjiang pushed the door open.","\"Brother, what’s so urgent?\" he grumbled. \"Dawn’s a few hours away. Couldn’t this wait till morning? One night won’t change anything.\"","He’d also attended the banquet and drunk heavily; all he wanted now was to collapse into bed.","\"If I called you, it’s urgent. Shut the door properly.\" Jiang Chonghai held the soup bowl. \"Go to Old Zhuo’s place yourself. Tell him to work through the night forging two passes. They must be delivered to my estate by noon tomorrow. If he’s late, he’ll never eat another bite from me.\"","Jiang Chongjiang froze, his expression gradually hardening. \"Brother, what’s the rush?\"","Since his brother needed to relay the pass details personally, Jiang Chonghai saw no point in hiding it. \"Lady Dai lost her pass and doesn’t want Qin Shaozong to know, so she asked your sister-in-law to arrange two new ones.\"","Jiang Chongjiang shrugged. \"It’s just a pass. Why hide it from Qin Shaozong? The man spoils her rotten—he didn’t even react when she humiliated him publicly tonight. Ten passes wouldn’t faze him.\"","Jiang Chonghai couldn’t be bothered to explain the intricacies. \"Never mind her reasons. Just get it done. Lady Dai’s value is immense—that’s why I’m sending you out in the dead of night.\"","The curfew was now in effect, and ordinary citizens were forbidden from going out. Anyone caught wandering outside would face imprisonment at best or be beaten to death at worst. His younger brother’s face served as a pass, ensuring smooth passage, and even the cunning Zhuo Bing would recognize the gravity of the situation and not dare to delay.","Jiang Chongjiang knew the banquet was a trap, but since he was already there, he decided to ask outright, \"Elder brother, do you think Qin Shaozong’s proposed military route is credible? Should we send word to Ying County?\"","Jiang Chonghai slowly closed his eyes, his mind replaying his wife’s earlier words, before finally uttering four words: \"Not entirely trustworthy.\"","Compared to when he had first returned to his chambers, Jiang Chonghai was now much calmer. Qin Shaozong had suggested advancing troops through the central and lower routes, but that couldn’t be trusted—after all, the man hadn’t seemed drunk enough to speak recklessly.","But what about Dai Li? Could she be entirely trusted? Was it possible that she was part of a trap set by Qin Shaozong, waiting for him to walk right into it?","The ever-suspicious Jiang Chonghai couldn’t stop turning it over in his mind.","\"Elder brother, what about Ying County...?\" Jiang Chongjiang hesitated.","Jiang Chonghai opened his eyes. \"Tonight, I will send a letter to Brother Li Zan, informing him of the general situation and asking him to await my second message.\"","Dark clouds obscured the full moon, and under the cover of the pitch-black night, a side gate of the governor’s mansion silently opened, allowing two figures to slip out.","In the dead of night, neither rode a horse. One headed south toward the city, while the other went east. The former knocked on the door of a residence in the southern district and, ignoring the occupant’s stunned expression, strode confidently inside. Soon, the house was brightly lit. The latter continued eastward, using a token to open the city gate and mounting a fast horse provided by the guards. With the rhythmic clatter of hooves, the lone rider vanished into the vast darkness along the eastern highway.","Meanwhile, beside the road leading to Ying County, long after the sound of hoofbeats had faded, the dense grass rustled suddenly. A figure emerged, brushing off stray blades as they stood.","\"Two days of waiting, and finally this bastard passes by. At last, I can report back to Marquis Qin.\"","Time flowed slowly. Dai Li tossed and turned, unable to sleep no matter how many times she shifted.","Just as she turned once more, she suddenly heard footsteps and voices outside her room. Her breath hitched, and she instinctively pulled the blanket up to cover the lower half of her face, leaving only her eyes exposed.","\"My lord, shall I have someone fetch you a bowl of kudzu root soup from the kitchen?\"","\"No need. All of you, retire for the night.\"","Perhaps it was the silence of the night, or perhaps it was her imagination, but Dai Li felt the footsteps grow louder, as if someone was approaching her room.","A few moments later, her door gave a soft thud—not loud, but unmistakably the sound of someone trying to push it open, only to find it locked.","\"Madam, open the door.\"","Dai Li’s heart sank.","He had actually come for her!","Just then, movement came from the small adjoining chamber. The maidservant, whose very bones were steeped in servitude, hurriedly rose and slipped through the connecting door into the main bedroom before swiftly unlocking the door for the man outside.","Before Dai Li could react, she heard the creak of the door opening.","\"No need for any of you to attend to me tonight. Leave.\" The man’s voice was deep and commanding, like the roaring waves of a storm-tossed sea, carrying an undeniable authority."]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15","paragraphs":["The two maidservants dared not delay and quickly left the room.","With a creak, the door closed. Dai Li, lying on the bed, stiffened. The darkness before her eyes gradually dissipated after a few breaths, and through the thin peony-patterned bed curtain, she caught sight of a faint candlelight flickering.","The glow illuminated a tall, imposing figure beside her. His shadow stretched long under the lamplight, merging seamlessly into the surrounding darkness as if transforming into a towering, oppressive mountain.","At this point, pretending to sleep was futile—remaining on the bed would only invite greater danger. Dai Li sat up.","She had slept in her clothes, so rising was quick. Her delicate fingers lifted a corner of the bed curtain, hooking it onto the jade fastener. Turning properly, she swung her legs onto the footstool beside the bed, intending to step down—only to glance down and see a pair of black boots at the very edge of her vision.","Her gaze traveled upward: first, the silver-edged wide sleeves hanging at his sides, then the dark blue sash at his waist.","Dai Li paused. He stood less than half a step from the footstool. If she continued rising, she would practically be throwing herself into his arms.","Advancing was impossible; retreating...","Qin Shaozong stood before the bed, his gaze descending upon her. She wore a peach-red round-collared dress, her fair skin and crimson robes illuminated by the dim lamplight, accentuating the striking beauty of her features. In the silence of the night, she resembled a midnight epiphyllum in full bloom.","She had removed her embroidered socks before sleeping, leaving her slender ankles and delicate feet bare, the nails painted with rouge. Even in the dim light, the skin of her feet gleamed with a pearl-like luster, standing out starkly against the dark footstool.","Suddenly, those bare feet slipped like fish back beneath her skirt. When she looked up again, she had already shifted to sit cross-legged at the edge of the bed, leaving a space beside her.","Dai Li feigned nonchalance, patting the empty spot. \"Come, sit. Let me tell you about my outing today with Lady Yun Rong.\"","Whether it was the sluggishness of a drunken mind or his thoughts being elsewhere, he did not move immediately after she spoke.","Dai Li’s heart trembled. \"Are you unwell from the wine? Should I have Tao Xiang prepare a kudzu root soup for you?\"","As she spoke, she quickly stood, intending to slip past him—only for his hand to suddenly seize her arm.","\"No need.\" His voice was as deep and heavy as ever.","Qin Shaozong pulled her back onto the bed, pressing her down to sit before taking the spot beside her. \"Speak. What happened between you and her today? And after you left the banquet?\"","He still hadn’t released her, merely shifting his grip from her arm to slide downward, finally settling over her wrist.","His palm felt like scorching sandpaper against her skin—searing hot and rough, sending her heart racing. She pressed her lips together tightly before beginning to recount the day’s events.","Dai Li knew Yan San had accompanied her outside the manor today and would likely report everything to Qin Shaozong. Thus, her account had to match his word for word.","She spoke truthfully of the day’s affairs, carefully omitting any mention of the message exchanged in the carriage.","After laying out everything she \"knew,\" she cautiously added, \"On our way back today, Yun Rong and I agreed to go out again tomorrow. Given how unpleasant things were between us at the banquet tonight, it would be entirely in character for someone as willful as me to take my anger out on your soldiers. Could you instruct them not to accompany me tomorrow?\"","The air grew still. Dai Li felt sweat gathering in her palms. What she planned to do could not afford witnesses—especially not his men. With his shrewd mind, he would quickly deduce she had ulterior motives.","The large hand over her wrist suddenly turned, his fingers sliding beneath her palm as if to lift and toy with it. But halfway through the motion, Qin Shaozong paused, his tone unreadable. \"Why so nervous?\"","Dai Li had always known his sharp perception was why she’d been discovered hiding behind the carriage that day. Yet she hadn’t expected even alcohol to dull it. For a moment, she was at a loss for words.","The atmosphere grew heavy.","\"Seems you truly are nervous. Something you can’t tell me? Planning to go somewhere tomorrow? Or secretly discuss something with Yun Rong? I’d wager the former—after all, Yun Rong has been visiting you often lately. If you wanted to speak privately, you could do so within the manor.\" Qin Shaozong turned her hand over, exposing her palm to the candlelight.","The two sat side by side on the bed, the unhindered glow casting a faint sheen over Dai Li’s palm.","Unmistakably, a thin layer of sweat had gathered there.","Qin Shaozong slowly dragged his thumb across her palm, wiping away the nearly imperceptible moisture. \"What is my lady hesitating over?\"","\"My lord sees all. Truly, nothing escapes you.\" Dai Li lowered her eyes, her thick lashes casting shadows over her cheeks. \"Our visit to the ruined temple in the eastern city today reminded me of my son, still missing. I thought to seek out a broker tomorrow to inquire if there’s any news of him.\"","Brokers—middlemen who dealt in livestock and servants.","She stole a glance at him, continuing only when she saw no anger on his face. \"You once promised to help me find him, and by rights, I shouldn’t act on my own. But the thought of him wandering alone out there is like a knife to my heart. I can’t eat or sleep unless I do something to ease this torment.\"","What kind of lie was hardest to detect?","One woven with truth.","Her desperation to find her son was real. Her intention to visit a broker tomorrow was real. These could not be faked.","As for the rest... that was another matter.","Dai Li sighed softly. \"I didn’t tell you because I feared displeasing you.\"","He had promised to help, and she had previously acted as though she trusted him completely. For her to now seek answers on her own could only be interpreted as distrust—hence her secrecy.","Then Qin Shaozong dropped a bombshell. \"This afternoon, my men reported no boy matching your son’s description in the local markets.\"","Dai Li froze.","\"Y-you’re certain?\" Her voice trembled when she finally spoke.","Qin Shaozong pinched her delicate fingertips. \"Every boy of similar age and height was questioned. None had lost their memories to illness or injury. If your son was taken nearby, he can’t have gone far. We’ll expand the search from Nan’an Commandery outward, investigate every trafficker in the surrounding regions. Once we find a lead, tracking him down will be a matter of time.\"","Dai Li barely heard the rest. Her mind was consumed by one thought: Zhou Zhou wasn’t in Nan’an Commandery.","Did that mean he wasn’t even in the same region as her? If he wasn’t in Nan’an, she needed to return home.","To Hangzhou.","She had to go back to Hangzhou!","A firm rub against her wrist snapped her back to the present. Dai Li instinctively looked up, meeting the man’s gaze.","Perhaps due to the dim light, his brown eyes appeared darker than usual—nearly black, like an unfathomable sea. Ripples stirred across its surface as a colossal beast emerged from the depths: first the towering fin, then the gaping maw lined with fangs, ready to swallow her whole.","Time seemed to snap backward abruptly, as if pulled by an invisible hand, and Dai Li felt herself transported back to the banquet from not long ago.","She had stood at the lower end of the hall, while he sat at the head. Back then, he had looked at her with the same undisguised intensity—only now, it was even more brazen than before.","Dai Li instinctively shifted slightly to the side, trying to put distance between them.","Yet that small movement shattered an already precarious balance. The man’s large hand, which had been gripping her wrist, suddenly released—but not entirely. Instead, it slid around her waist, pulling her flush against him before securing her firmly at the small of her back. With just the strength of his arm, he hauled her onto his lap.","To Dai Li, the scene unfolded absurdly fast—a mere two breaths’ time.","The solid heat beneath her was impossible to ignore, especially as the prominent swell of his body pressed snugly between her thighs. The thin fabric of their clothing did little to conceal the growing tension, the heat between them spreading silently, intertwining until it sparked an uncontrollable tremor.","\"Today is the fourth day,\" he murmured, his fingers trailing forward to toy with the sash at her waist, tugging it lightly.","\"It’s only the third full day,\" Dai Li corrected softly, making no move to stop his hand. Instead, she asked in a gentle tone, \"My lord, do you know how long a woman’s monthly courses typically last?\"","His movements froze.","The man’s expression was unreadable, most of his face cast in shadow, but his dark brown eyes grew heavy.","For the first time, Dai Li didn’t find him intimidating.","He truly didn’t know!","Seizing the opportunity, Dai Li lied without hesitation. \"Seven days. Any healthy woman’s courses last a full seven days.\"","The moment the number left her lips, she caught the faint twitch of a vein at his temple. A rare bloom of satisfaction unfurled in her chest.","But the next instant, her heart lurched as she felt his arm tighten around her, pressing her even closer against him.","Dai Li was no naive maiden—she knew well that pleasure could be found without crossing the final line. Quickly, she lifted a hand to brace against his chest and whispered, \"We can’t be certain the maids outside have truly left. At the banquet, I treated you with cold indifference, yet here I am, welcoming you into my chambers and enduring my discomfort to indulge in such acts—hardly fitting for a woman of my notoriously willful temperament. My lord, patience is the companion of wisdom.\"","She remained composed, certain of her victory.","These past days had taught her one thing clearly: he was a man ruled by reason, not desire.","Just as she predicted, the leviathan of his hunger sank back into the depths. He inhaled deeply before slowly releasing her. \"A few more days... I can wait.\"","In his low, rough voice, Dai Li heard the promise of a storm four days from now. She lowered her lashes, veiling the calculations swirling behind her eyes.","The warm afternoon sunlight filtered through the trees, casting dappled patterns of gold on the ground.","Dai Li strolled through the rear garden, admiring the blossoms. The vibrant hues of flowers and willows stretched before her, a sight that lifted her spirits—and her mood soared even higher when Yun Rong arrived.","With no outsiders present and only Jiang Mansion’s maids trailing behind, Yun Rong saw no need for discretion. \"Little sister, I’ve brought what you asked for. It wasn’t easy—Zhuo Jili worked through the night to finish it. But since it was my husband’s direct order, he’d have burned the midnight oil to the last drop if that’s what it took to deliver perfection.\"","Then, remembering Dai Li’s blunt nature, she hastily added, \"You must remember this favor, sister. If I ever need your help in the future, don’t turn me away.\"","Dai Li accepted the two small bamboo tokens, running her fingers over them lovingly. The engraved details matched the hidden pass she possessed—down to the official seal.","These were government-issued identity permits, granting unimpeded travel.","\"If you ever face difficulties, Sister Yun, come to me. And if I can’t help, I’ll make Qin Changgeng handle it for you,\" Dai Li promised, feeding her empty assurances.","Yun Rong beamed with delight.","Laughter and cheer flowed between them—a mutually satisfying exchange."]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16","paragraphs":["Dai Li asked, \"Sister Yun, I plan to leave the estate at the Hour of the Goat. Will you accompany me?\"","\"Again? Didn’t we just go out yesterday?\" Yun Rong hesitated. She was over a decade older than Dai Li and had borne four sons in her youth. Combined with her worry over her drunken husband last night, she had tossed and turned, leaving her exhausted today.","Dai Li ignored her weariness, complaining petulantly, \"Yesterday was just a short outing—we didn’t even explore all of Nankang Commandery. If I don’t take the chance to enjoy myself now, once the march begins, I’ll be stuck in a carriage day after day, bored out of my mind.\"","At first, Yun Rong was reluctant, but then she reconsidered. Yesterday, while strolling through the market together, Dai Li had mentioned wanting to visit a dilapidated temple in the eastern part of the city. Yun Rong had been unwilling to go to such a filthy place, but as the saying goes, a loss may turn out to be a gain—it was precisely because of that detour that she had lost her jade pendant, and Dai Li had later returned it, earning her favor.","Fine, she might as well go out again. Who knew? Another opportunity might present itself.","The side gate of the commandery office opened once more, and the carriage rolled out slowly.","This time, Yan San was not among the escorting guards, and only one of Qin Shaozong’s personal soldiers remained. When Yun Rong casually inquired about the reason, Dai Li simply said that her lingering anger from last night made her irritable at the sight of the marquis’s men, so she refused to let so many of them follow.","The wheels turned, and the carriage bearing the wooden plaque of the \"Jiang\" estate slowly entered the bustling marketplace. Commoners instinctively made way as it passed.","\"Sister Yun, we didn’t get a proper look at Ruixiang Silk Emporium yesterday. Why don’t we visit again today?\" Dai Li began making demands once more.","What could Yun Rong do but agree?","Most fabric shops and silk emporiums in the market only sold materials, displaying bolts of cloth in various patterns on their shelves for wholesale purchase. They didn’t include tailoring—that was the work of seamstresses.","High-end silk emporiums were the exception. These establishments, catering to the nobility, had no shortage of funds. They invested heavily in hiring skilled seamstresses to create sample garments. These samples allowed customers to try them on—regardless of fit—primarily to experience the fabric’s comfort and the richness of its patterns.","Ruixiang Silk Emporium was the best of its kind.","The journey there was uneventful, and Dai Li didn’t get sidetracked by gossip this time.","However, Yun Rong hadn’t expected the marquis’s favorite concubine to be so easily dazzled. Watching Dai Li try on one outfit after another, her face alight with greed and novelty, Yun Rong couldn’t help but roll her eyes in secret.","Tch. She really hadn’t been by Marquis Qin’s side for long. The luxury she’d seen was still limited, leaving her without the poise of a woman accustomed to finery.","At first, Yun Rong had the patience to wait, but as Dai Li took longer with each fitting and Yun Rong herself was exhausted, she eventually retreated to a secluded resting area in the corner.","There were plush chairs, round tables, maids fanning her and serving tea, and even snacks provided by the emporium. As the wife of a prefectural governor, why should she stand idly outside the fitting room when she could sit comfortably?","Creak.","The fitting room door opened again.","Dai Li stepped out, tossing the dress in her hands to an attendant maid. Her eyes flicked toward the resting area. \"Tao Xiang, Ding Xiang, go attend to Sister Yun. I have enough help here—you two are just in the way.\"","The two maids exchanged glances. Given past experiences, they silently obeyed.","Once they left, Dai Li selected one of the emporium’s maids to follow her inside, leaving the other outside.","Creak.","The wooden door closed again.","Dai Li turned to the maid and whispered, \"I have a business proposition for you. This must remain confidential. If you succeed, I’ll pay you three taels of silver.\"","At present, an ox cost four thousand coins—equivalent to two taels of silver. This wasn’t a small sum, considering an adult laborer’s daily wage was only about twenty coins.","For an ordinary person, this was a fortune.","The maid froze in surprise.","\"The reason I’m asking you and not my own maids is that I’ve only recently been taken in as a favored concubine and don’t yet have trustworthy people around me. You’re unconnected to me and inconspicuous,\" Dai Li explained calmly.","Seeing the maid’s hesitation, she added, \"It’s nothing complicated. Just buy a few things and make two deliveries to different inns. No shady business involved.\"","The maid’s doubts vanished. A simple errand for three taels of silver? This was a windfall. \"Please, go on!\"","Dai Li listed the inns she had passed yesterday. \"You know Moonlight Lodge and Orchid Pavilion, correct?\"","The maid nodded. Of course she did—they were among the finest inns in Nankang Commandery, far beyond the means of commoners.","\"Prepare a bundle. At the end of the Hour of the Monkey today, take it to Moonlight Lodge and give it to the manager. Tell him it’s something Madam Dai has left here and will retrieve no later than the day she checks out. He must keep it safe. Tomorrow, do the same—same time, same bundle—but deliver it to Orchid Pavilion and repeat the message.\"","Dai Li took out some silver from her small purse and handed it over. \"This is the deposit. You’ll get the rest when the job is done.\"","The maid eagerly accepted it, her eyes glued to the money. Dai Li asked, \"Repeat what I just told you.\"","With silver at stake, the maid had listened carefully and now recited the instructions flawlessly.","Dai Li nodded. \"Moonlight Lodge first, then Orchid Pavilion—the order must not be reversed. The delivery must be at the end of the Hour of the Monkey, not a moment earlier. As for the bundle’s contents: two sets of plain black-gray women’s robes, a small jar of rice powder, charcoal pieces, black dye...\"","After listing everything, Dai Li added, \"Wear a veil when delivering the bundle. If you can’t leave it at Orchid Pavilion tomorrow, don’t force it—just take it away. I’ll return to Ruixiang Silk Emporium tomorrow afternoon. If today’s task is done, just nod to me from a distance. No need to approach.\"","...","Creak.","The fitting room door opened.","Dai Li stepped out as if nothing had happened and selected another outfit to try on. After two more changes, she finally finished and walked over to the resting area.","\"Sister Yun, I’m done. I’ll take all the fabrics I tried earlier.\" The marquis’s favored concubine was extravagant, spending money like water.","Yun Rong wasn’t surprised in the least.","Whether a man truly cared for a woman was most plainly seen in his willingness to spend on her.","Given how much Marquis Qin doted on Madam Dai, buying a few bolts of fine fabric was nothing. Even if she wanted to purchase the entire Ruixiang Silk Emporium, he likely wouldn’t bat an eye.","Dai Li glanced down at the small purse tied at her waist, flicking it lightly with her fingers. Feeling its weight, she smiled in satisfaction.","Whether it was the deposit for the maid or the payment for the luxurious fabrics, all the silver came from Qin Shaozong—the only difference was whether she handed it over herself or had a servant settle the bill.","Dai Li not only spent money without a shred of guilt but even stashed away a portion as funds for her eventual journey south. After all, she was now an actress playing a role, laboring both mentally and physically—wasn’t she entitled to some compensation? She felt no psychological burden whatsoever.","After leaving the silk shop, the two continued their shopping spree, visiting a teahouse, a rouge shop, and the jewelry store Jin Shi Zhai. By the time they exited Jin Shi Zhai, Dai Li was so energized that she dragged Yun Rong along on foot, forgoing the carriage entirely.","Yun Rong was exhausted to the point of dizziness, her face pale with a faint greenish tinge. Several times, she nearly blurted out a demand to return home, but she held back each time.","She was here as an escort—how could she speak up when her guest hadn’t had her fill? Besides, this particular guest was notoriously capricious. Ruining her fun now might undo all the rapport they’d painstakingly built. Fine, she told herself, she’d endure a little longer.","Just as Yun Rong managed to console herself, she suddenly heard the voice beside her say, \"Sister Yun, I’m a bit tired. Why don’t we rest at this Ming Yue Ju? The place looks clean, and the attendants are well-dressed. It seems like a decent spot.\"","Without exaggeration, Yun Rong felt as if the clouds had parted and sunlight burst through the gloom overhead.","The diva was finally tired!","Forget Ming Yue Ju—why not just head straight home?","Yun Rong hurriedly said, \"Little sister, we’ve already visited quite a few places today. Surely we’ve shopped enough. How about we—\"","\"Who said we’ve shopped enough?\" Dai Li cut her off.","As if oblivious to Yun Rong’s stunned expression, Dai Li continued, \"We still have to go to the West Market later. Back at Jin Shi Zhai, I overheard someone say that merchants from the Western Regions are selling exotic cats there—long, dense fur, big fluffy tails, completely different from our local ones. I want to see them.\"","Yun Rong’s vision darkened. The half-dispersed clouds above her seemed to knit back together.","\"Come on, let’s take a short break at Ming Yue Ju, have some snacks, and set out again soon,\" Dai Li said, pulling her inside.","Inns like Ming Yue Ju not only provided lodging but also served meals to guests.","High-end establishments of this caliber naturally offered food far superior to ordinary inns—even surpassing many dedicated restaurants. However, such elite inns had their own rules: meals were not sold separately.","If you were staying the night, they’d prepare food for you. But if you just wanted to eat without lodging? Sorry, the inn wouldn’t accommodate you.","This policy won the favor of many nobles and wealthy merchants. After all, everyone preferred a quieter environment where their lodgings weren’t turned into a noisy, open-to-all dining hall.","Dai Li first booked a room for the night to secure dining privileges, then ordered food. After a few bites, she was so impressed that she waved her hand and—to Yun Rong’s astonishment—splurged on extending their stay by several more days.","Yun Rong: \"...\"","Her face turned frosty. She wasn’t focused on Dai Li’s gluttony but was instead consumed by one terrifying thought:","Several more days?","Did this mean she’d have to endure more shopping excursions tomorrow and the day after?!"]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17","paragraphs":["Along the way, Dai Li told Yun Rong she needed to relieve herself. Yun Rong’s mind was still buzzing, and at first, she didn’t respond. Only when Dai Li stood up did she hurriedly signal Tao Xiang to follow and attend to her.","Dai Li paused but didn’t object.","The two went to the eastern privy in the backyard.","Shortly after the wooden door closed, Dai Li called out to Tao Xiang outside, \"I need to change into a fresh menstrual belt. Go fetch one from the carriage for me.\"","\"My lady, I have it with me.\" Tao Xiang didn’t leave but instead pulled a small cloth pouch from her sleeve. She had risen above the other maids precisely because of her meticulousness.","Knowing how exacting Dai Li could be in certain matters—such as never reusing the expensive silk menstrual belts, instead burning each after a single use—Tao Xiang dared not be careless. When traveling, she carried Dai Li’s menstrual belt in a small pouch, ready for use at any moment.","Behind the door, Dai Li furrowed her delicate brows. After a brief pause, she opened the door and took the menstrual belt from Tao Xiang. Once the door closed again, she glanced down, then suddenly let go.","The menstrual belt fell to the ground.","\"Tao Xiang, I dropped it just now—I didn’t hold it properly,\" Dai Li said, her voice laced with irritation.","Unlike modern sanitary pads, which are thin and flat, a menstrual belt had multiple straps for wrapping around the waist, making it thick when folded. Tao Xiang’s pouch only held one, and now, staring at the empty bag, she was at a loss.","\"Is there another menstrual belt in the carriage? If so, go fetch it,\" Dai Li instructed.","The traveling carriage had two small chests for storing spare clothes and small items for emergencies. Tao Xiang quickly replied, \"There’s another belt in the carriage, my lady. Please wait a moment—I’ll fetch it right away.\"","Dai Li agreed and waited inside until Tao Xiang’s footsteps faded into the distance. Then she swiftly opened the door.","\"My lady, what do you require?\" asked the young attendant she summoned, bowing respectfully.","Dai Li handed him a handful of coins. \"Deliver a message to your manager for me...\"","The afternoon sun was waning, its golden rays softening as dusk approached, painting the sky like a master’s oil painting. In the Moonlight Residence, a servant walking through the backyard paused to admire the sunset, oblivious to the hushed conversation near the eastern privy.","Dai Li pressed the coins into his hand. \"Handle this discreetly, and this is your reward.\"","The attendant bowed even deeper, eager to comply.","Dai Li then turned back to the privy, barely shutting the door behind her before Tao Xiang returned in a fluster with the fresh menstrual belt.","Once finished, mistress and maid returned to the dining hall.","As Dai Li entered, she sensed a gaze from the side. Turning, she met the eyes of the Moonlight Residence’s manager. She gave him a slight nod, and he responded with a polite smile.","Though puzzled, the manager recalled the attendant’s emphasis on \"personal discretion\" and wisely kept silent.","Nobility and wealthy merchants guarded their privacy fiercely. If this lady had come with a companion yet acted covertly, she clearly didn’t want it known. The Moonlight Residence’s policy was to follow orders without unnecessary questions—never overstep.","Dai Li resumed her seat beside Yun Rong. When the meal was nearly done, she suggested, \"Come, Sister Yun, let’s visit the Western Market to see the exotic Persian cats.\"","Yun Rong’s lips trembled, her head spinning.","When exhaustion weighed heavily, rising after sitting was a struggle—and she was in precisely that state.","The air hung silent for a few breaths.","At last, the marquis’s willful concubine seemed to show a sliver of consideration. \"Sister Yun, are you tired?\"","Yun Rong nearly teared up—finally, this block of wood had learned empathy! Seizing the opportunity, she said, \"I am quite weary. Perhaps we should return to the estate?\"","\"I’m not tired and could keep exploring. But since you are, rest here awhile. I’ll go to the Western Market for half an hour and return to meet you later,\" Dai Li declared matter-of-factly.","Yun Rong stiffened. \"Sister, that’s hardly proper.\"","\"You said you were exhausted—what’s improper about it? I’ll only be gone briefly, not hours. Besides, with maids and guards accompanying me, what could go wrong?\" Dai Li rose from her seat.","Yun Rong’s resolve wavered.","Dai Li didn’t give her time to reconsider. \"It’s settled. Rest here at Moonlight Residence while I visit the market. I’ll return soon. Don’t worry, Sister Yun—given our bond, if the marquis asks tonight how my outing went, I’ll tell him you were the perfect host and I enjoyed myself immensely.\"","Yun Rong watched Dai Li’s retreating figure, mouth slightly agape, but no words came out.","Jiang Mansion, Guest Courtyard.","Mo Yanyun, having received the secret report, said excitedly, \"My lord, last night Jiang Chonghai sent a messenger to Ying County to relay the news. It seems he’s taken the bait.\"","Once Li Zan confirmed their route, he would act. This campaign involved the elite Xuanxiao Cavalry, renowned for their invincibility. In a direct clash, they’d stand no chance.","But an ambush was different.","By lying in wait at a choke point, flanking the enemy, and disrupting their formation with a small strike force, they could easily decimate the majority of their forces.","\"He may not be entirely convinced,\" Qin Shaozong mused, studying the sheepskin map spread on the table. \"Jiang Chonghai has always been suspicious. This alone isn’t enough.\"","He tapped a spot on the map—his encampment outside the city. His finger traced eastward briefly before returning, then moved southeast. \"Since I declared at the banquet that we’d take the central and lower routes, let’s make a show of it. Send troops fifty li down both paths, then pick a spot near water—but not too close—to set up camp and cook meals, pretending to be the vanguard.\"","His gaze shifted to the upper route, a faint smile in his brown eyes. \"Meanwhile, dispatch a small scout party to quietly survey the upper route. With my wife’s ‘unintentional’ slip earlier, Jiang Chonghai will surely have spies watching that path. Seeing is believing—once he confirms the central and lower routes are decoys, he’ll be eighty percent convinced.\"","The best way to deceive a paranoid man was to let him think he held all the cards.","They would indeed take the upper route—not as the cicada, but as the oriole waiting to devour the mantis.","A knock sounded at the door.","Qin Shaozong glanced at Yan San, who went to answer. After a hushed exchange, he returned, his expression grave.","Mo Yanyun frowned. \"What’s happened? Did Jiang Chonghai change plans, or is there trouble in Ying County?\"","Yan San shook his head. \"Neither. It’s about Lady Dai.\"","Mo Yanyun was about to dismiss it as trivial when Yan San added, \"My lord, the guards report that within a five-li radius west of Nankang County, they found no residence matching Lady Dai’s former home.\"","Qin Shaozong, who had been studying the sheepskin map, suddenly looked up.","Meanwhile.","After leaving the Moonlight Residence, Dai Li headed toward the West Market.","During her stroll through the markets the previous day, she had already gathered information about the different districts of Nankang County.","The East Market was mostly filled with teahouses, eateries, and inns. The North Market housed numerous fabric shops, jewelry stores, bookstores, and pawnshops. The South Market, a quieter area relatively distant from the other districts, had become a neighborhood for the wealthy and noble.","The West Market, on the other hand, sold all kinds of ingredients—rice, flour, oil, spices, and various vegetables. Occasionally, hunters who caught wild rabbits, boars, or snakes in the outskirts would bring their game here to sell. Additionally, foreign merchants from the Western Regions sometimes sold exotic goods like spices and even live animals such as civets alongside their wares.","Dai Li arrived at the West Market by carriage, and as soon as she stepped out, her pace slowed.","It was now early in the hour of Shen (around 3 PM), and with sunset just an hour away, the best cuts of meat and freshest produce had already been sold out in the morning. The West Market in the late afternoon was noticeably less bustling than it had been earlier.","The stalls in the West Market were arranged with care—grains and oils in one section, butcher shops occupying a corner, fruit and vegetable vendors grouped together, and then—","A row of elevated stalls, built with stacked bricks into small square enclosures.","The ground here was noticeably wetter than elsewhere, and scattered glimmers of light occasionally caught the eye, like tiny stars embedded in the earth.","Compared to other areas, there were far fewer vendors here. Along the row of stalls, only a handful of merchants remained, most of them already packing up.","As she approached, Dai Li caught a strong whiff of fishy brine.","\"Madam, this place sells seafood—it's dirty and smelly. Perhaps we should go elsewhere,\" Tao Xiang whispered.","Dai Li seemed lost in reminiscence. \"My hometown is in the southern waters, where the fish markets were incredibly lively, with countless varieties of seafood. After coming north, I’ve always wanted to find even a faint trace of home. But some things, no matter how much gold or silver you possess, aren’t easily obtained.\"","A fishmonger who had been packing up paused, his nose keenly catching the scent of money. \"Madam, what kind of seafood are you looking for? Fish, turtles, shrimp, crabs, or perhaps shellfish and seaweed? Ah, if you’d like some exotic marine delicacies or sea cucumbers, that can also be arranged—though the price would be considerably higher.\"","The \"exotic marine delicacies\" and \"sea cucumbers\" the fishmonger referred to were rare seafood and trepang.","Dai Li’s eyes brightened slightly. \"You can really get them? Let me be clear—I only enjoy live seafood. I have no taste for dead fish or spoiled shrimp.\"","The fishmonger grinned, flashing a row of white teeth. \"Rest assured, Madam. Though the Hutuo River’s currents are far swifter than ordinary rivers, making upstream travel much more time-consuming and laborious, if you truly wish to purchase these delicacies, I can have my men divide the cargo among smaller boats. Light vessels move faster upstream, ensuring the goods stay fresh and alive.\"","Dai Li’s heart raced uncontrollably.","The Hutuo River!","This great river, flowing west to east through Shanxi and Hebei, actually passed near Nankang County.","The \"Tuo\" in Hutuo meant \"torrential,\" a testament to the river’s fierce currents and surging waves. Traveling downstream was effortless—boats could cover hundreds of miles in a single day. No wonder the saying went, \"A thousand miles to Jiangling in just one day.\"","The Hutuo River flowed eastward. If she boarded a boat downstream, she could quickly put distance between herself and Nankang County, disembarking midway to change course and head south toward Hangzhou."]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18","paragraphs":["Dai Li couldn't help but smile. \"That sounds excellent. However, I’ve heard plenty of such promises before—flowery words that end up delivering nothing but stale fish and rotten shrimp.\"","The fishmonger wasn’t the least bit offended. Wealthy patrons always had high standards; those who complained were the real buyers. \"How about this? The day after tomorrow, at the hour of the Goat, I’ll bring a crate of seafood for inspection. Would that suit you?\"","The round trip, plus the time needed to collect goods at the docks, meant even working nonstop, the earliest he could return was the hour of the Goat the day after tomorrow.","That timing aligned perfectly with Dai Li’s plans.","\"Good.\" She paid a portion of the deposit. \"I’ll send someone to collect the goods no later than the end of the hour of the Monkey.\"","Dai Li had once told Qin Shaozong that her main purpose for leaving the estate was to inquire with a broker, hoping to find traces of her son. This was the official reason—one she had to uphold.","Brokers weren’t like fishmongers. The latter needed to sell their goods fresh and fast to fetch a good price, while the former operated more leisurely. Even as evening approached, brokers could still be found in the market.","Dai Li sought out an experienced broker and carefully described her needs, only for the man to shake his head. \"I don’t have a child like that in my hands.\"","Noticing her fine attire—gold hairpins adorning her coiled hair, a dark blue ruqun dress with subtle shimmering patterns, clearly made of high-quality fabric—he could tell she was no ordinary woman. Her fair, delicate skin only confirmed it.","\"I’ll ask my associates. Perhaps one of them has what you’re looking for.\" The old broker made a silent resolution. Even if none had such a child, it wasn’t impossible to procure one matching her description.","Dai Li stood there for a long while before turning away without a word.","The setting sun melted into gold, the evening clouds merging like jade.","As dusk fell, the Jiang family carriage rolled home under the fading light, this trip outside having been quite fruitful.","Yun Rong, upon returning, leaned on her maidservant’s arm and retreated straight to her chambers, too exhausted to move. Even her beloved grandson came seeking her, only to be gently dismissed.","Just as she was about to drift off, the door opened. Jiang Chonghai stepped inside. \"Where did you and Madam Dai go today? Did she mention anything unusual in passing?\"","The mere mention of \"Madam Dai\" made Yun Rong’s head throb. \"We covered countless places—she toured all three markets in the north, west, and east. That woman has the stamina of a soldier’s wife. I didn’t hear her say anything noteworthy, but I’ll have Tao Xiang come later to confirm.\"","Jiang Chonghai stroked his beard but said nothing.","After all, womenfolk knew little. Any useful information would be a pleasant surprise, but he wasn’t disappointed by its absence.","\"Ah, from the way she spoke, she intends to go out again the next two days. I’m utterly spent—could our daughters-in-law accompany her tomorrow?\" Yun Rong complained.","\"Nonsense! Absolutely not!\" Jiang Chonghai’s first reaction was to scold her. \"In rank, I’m beneath Qin Shaozong. Sending our daughters-in-law as escorts would be improper—as if I’m slighting him. We cannot afford missteps at this critical juncture.\"","Yun Rong felt indignant but lacked the energy to argue.","Seeing her pallor, Jiang Chonghai softened his tone. \"You’ll continue accompanying her. If you grow too weary, rest at a teahouse and let the maids keep a close eye on her afterward.\"","Yun Rong had no choice but to nod.","After parting ways with Yun Rong, Dai Li returned to her pavilion.","Today’s plans had gone smoothly, and learning that the Hutuo River was nearby felt like heaven’s favor. Barring unforeseen circumstances, she would leave Nankang Commandery the day after tomorrow.","Her good mood lasted until she pushed open her door.","The brilliant hues of sunset spilled into the room as the door swung open, casting a warm glow across the floor. But as the light stretched inward, it halted abruptly upon reaching the hem of a man’s black robes.","The man inside lifted his head. His expression was calm, but his eyes were deep—bottomless like an abyss. \"You’ve returned, my lady.\"","For some reason, Dai Li’s spine prickled with unease.","Something felt off.","She stood frozen for a breath before stepping inside as if nothing were amiss, her tone laced with sarcasm. \"Oh my, what brings such a busy man here?\"","But Qin Shaozong didn’t look at her. Instead, he addressed the two maids trailing behind her. \"Leave us. I wish to speak privately with my wife.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","The maids hesitated before retreating.","Click. The door shut softly, sealing the room in silence. The stillness felt like creeping vines, tangling around her legs and rooting her in place.","\"Sit,\" he said.","Dai Li lowered her eyes and obediently took a seat across from him. \"Does my lord have urgent matters to discuss?\"","Instead of answering, Qin Shaozong gestured to the tea set on the table. \"Can you brew tea?\"","Dai Li: \"I know the basics.\"","In this era, tea cultivation and consumption had become widespread. Tea culture was not only regarded as refined but was also praised by physicians for its medicinal benefits—\"bitter tea, long consumed, sharpens the mind.\"","From nobles to commoners, every household kept tea. The quality, quantity, and accompanying utensils, however, depended entirely on one’s wealth.","Dai Li eyed the fruit tray and teacups on the table, feeling slightly overwhelmed. Her claim of knowing \"the basics\" wasn’t modesty. Unlike the modern method of simply steeping leaves in hot water, tea in this era involved additional ingredients—dried melon, fruit pulp, mint, salt, tangerine peel, and more.","The sequence and proportions eluded her.","Under the weight of his gaze, she decided not to overthink it. The order didn’t matter—as long as it became tea. She’d already warned him.","\"Though you need not return to your former residence, your sudden disappearance would surely alarm your old servants. They might even report it to the authorities.\" Qin Shaozong’s voice was as flat as the unheated water before them.","Dai Li’s hand, scooping dried melon, froze mid-motion. A small piece slipped from the ladle and clattered onto the table.","For a moment, the table no longer felt like wood but the thin membrane of her own nerves—how could such a tiny sound nearly unseat her?","No, it wasn’t the melon. It was the danger lurking in his words.","A large, well-defined hand suddenly entered her periphery. His nails were neatly trimmed, but a pale scar ran from his knuckle to his index finger. Against his darker skin, it stood out like a wolf’s fang.","Qin Shaozong picked up the fallen melon slice. \"We cannot afford any mishaps now. To prevent your old servants from alerting officials, I’ll need you to write them a letter. I’ll have it delivered to ease their concerns.\"","Dai Li slowly raised her eyes to meet those brown orbs. \"You needn’t worry about them raising an alarm—how could a few mute women report anything to the authorities? As for written messages, those are useless too; they’re illiterate and can’t read. There were two capable, literate guards at my humble abode before, but after my son was abducted, one succumbed to a sudden illness, perhaps out of guilt, while the other left a letter saying he was going to seek reinforcements from his master.\"","Qin Shaozong merely smiled. \"No matter. We should still go. Leave a letter informing that Qin Huali of your whereabouts, so he won’t disturb you in the future.\"","If she had only been worried before, now Dai Li suspected this man had likely sent someone to the fabricated address she had once told him about—ten li west of the city.","He was suspicious.","Otherwise, he wouldn’t keep circling back to this topic.","A chill ran down Dai Li’s spine as countless thoughts flashed through her mind. Just then, Qin Shaozong set down the slice of melon and reached out as if to take her hand.","The memory of last night surfaced—this man was far too perceptive. If he noticed her palms were damp again...","Dai Li abruptly placed the small wooden spoon down and rose from her seat.","Qin Shaozong’s outstretched hand paused as he watched her step around the low table and kneel beside him.","The act of kneeling required adjusting her skirts and bracing her hands against her thighs—a movement she used to discreetly wipe away the faint sweat on her palms. \"My lord, have you been unable to locate my former residence?\"","Qin Shaozong’s gaze had been lingering on her hands—pale, slender fingers with delicate pink tips, like tender willow catkins in spring or fine mutton-fat jade carvings.","But at her words, he averted his eyes, arching a brow with amusement. \"What makes you say that, madam?\"","Dai Li adopted a serious tone. \"From my dealings with nobility, they are all cautious and meticulous, thinking three steps ahead. And men of your stature are rarely idle—you don’t strike me as someone with time to spare. You wouldn’t bring up my old home without reason. Thus, I dare to guess you sent men to search for it, but your soldiers found nothing, barred by some illusionary barrier, leaving you... perplexed.\"","As long as he still had use for her, no matter how deep his suspicions ran, he wouldn’t act rashly.","Dai Li was certain of that.","Qin Shaozong took the hand resting on her knee and enveloped it in his own, scoffing. \"An illusionary barrier?\"","Dai Li’s heart skipped a beat.","He pinched her fingertips, his tone mocking. \"Are you about to say next, madam, that some rogue Daoist from the mountains set up this ‘barrier,’ making your home impossible to find?\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","An atheist.","Why did she have to encounter such a rare breed in this era?","The light friction against the inside of her wrist sent tingles crawling along her nerves, mingling with the fading heat of the sunset outside, stirring an unbearable restlessness.","Pretending not to catch his implication, Dai Li continued, \"Huali didn’t want me interacting much with the outside world, so he built our home outside the city. But since we still needed supplies, complete seclusion wasn’t feasible, so we settled ten li beyond the prefecture. For the first two years, hunters often came knocking. After too many visits, Huali grew weary of it and invited a certain Zhengyangzi—who claimed to have received teachings from the Donghua Emperor—to our home.\"","She stole a glance but saw no skepticism, curiosity, or even reverence for Daoists on his face. His attention remained fixed on her hand, as though it fascinated him more than her tale.","She pressed on, \"Strangely enough, after Zhengyangzi placed a few stones around the house and the southeastern corner, everything changed. Unless guided by someone familiar, ordinary people couldn’t find the path to our home. From then on, we were left undisturbed. Had my son not been abducted during an outing, I might never have left those woods...\"","When he still showed no reaction, Dai Li played her final card. \"If you’re truly curious, perhaps I could personally take you there another day.\"","At last, the man beside her lifted his gaze. The last rays of sunlight from the window gilded his sharp features, casting a brilliant glow over his deep-set eyes. The unconnected tail of his left brow resembled an unsheathed blade, exuding an oppressive weight. \"Tomorrow, I’ll have Yan San accompany you.\"","He had agreed to the visit—but he wouldn’t be going himself.","Dai Li frowned delicately. \"Tomorrow won’t do. I’ve made plans with the prefect’s wife for the next two days—we’re visiting several places, and I’ve already shown great enthusiasm for it. How about the day after? I haven’t finalized my schedule with her then.\"","Qin Shaozong neither agreed nor refused. Instead, he asked abruptly, \"You had no identity pass before. How did you enter the city?\"","The pass was essential for entry and exit through the gates.","Dai Li lowered her voice. \"I paid a traveling vendor I often worked with to arrange for me to join a merchant group, posing as a servant to enter the city.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"What’s the vendor’s name? Where does he live?\"","Dai Li shook her head. \"I only know his surname is Wang. The rest, I’m unaware of. The guards handled all dealings with vendors before.\"","\"And if you couldn’t find your son after entering the city, how did you plan to leave?\" Qin Shaozong pressed.","Dai Li peeked at him again. \"If I couldn’t find him, I didn’t intend to leave. I’d find a well-off household to stay with temporarily.\"","Qin Shaozong’s fingers stilled around hers. Seeing her cautious expression and the way she kept stealing glances, he let out a soft scoff. \"Quite the scheme, madam. Serving one master is as good as another—so long as they’re valuable, correct?\"","\"You asked, so I answered truthfully, without a shred of deceit. But that was all in the past. Now that I have a noble lord like you, why would I settle for less?\" Yet his expression remained cold and unreadable.","Dai Li untied the small bamboo token at her waist and placed it in Qin Shaozong’s palm. \"Those who’ve been servants understand the importance of an identity pass. I admit my motives weren’t pure before, but what’s done is done—let the past scatter like sand in the wind. Since this token has been shown to the prefect’s wife often, it’s likely no longer needed. Could you spare a moment to safeguard it for me?\"","As she spoke, her gaze lingered on the token, her reluctance plain.","His large, well-defined hand slowly closed over it, the engraved details vanishing beneath his grip like ink dissolving in dark water.","\"That night, you already searched me and know this is the only pass I have. You must keep it safe,\" Dai Li murmured wistfully.","Qin Shaozong only said, \"Rest assured. It won’t be lost.\"","\"My lord, there’s another matter I must report.\" Dai Li straightened. \"Today, while out, I visited Ruixiang Silk Shop, a teahouse, the Moonlight Residence, and other places—spending quite a sum.\"","Qin Shaozong once again noticed that furtive gaze observing him and couldn’t help but chuckle. \"If the money’s spent, then it’s spent. Is it really worth worrying over, my dear wife? Or was that Qin Huali of yours such a miserly old goat that he’d only rattle his coin pouch just to tease your ears with the jingling sound?\"","Dai Li’s lips twitched.","This man really..."]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19","paragraphs":["The cycle of day and night continues endlessly. The slumbering town awoke to the sunlight, as empty stalls welcomed their owners, and the streets gradually filled with the clamor of voices.","After breakfast, Dai Li once again pulled Yun Rong into the carriage to leave the estate.","For someone who rarely exercised, an abrupt change in routine would inevitably lead to sore muscles by nightfall—a discomfort that couldn’t be dispelled overnight, leaving one’s legs as weak as noodles the next day.","Yun Rong sat stiffly in the carriage, her body moving with the vehicle, but her spirit seemed to linger behind at the estate.","Dai Li knew she was reluctant but pretended not to notice.","“Sister, where is your pendant? I don’t see it on you today,” Yun Rong suddenly remarked, snapping out of her daze as she noticed Dai Li’s empty waistband.","Had she lost it again?","Losing it wouldn’t be so bad—it would give Dai Li another chance to owe her a favor. But if she recalled correctly, Dai Li had still been wearing the pendant when she returned to the estate yesterday...","Dai Li paused briefly before sighing. “After returning to my room yesterday, I noticed the cord holding the pendant had loosened—it was barely hanging on. Qin Changgeng happened to be there and saw it. Naturally, he scolded me a little. Since I’d kept it from him that I’d lost it once before, I felt guilty, so I agreed to put it away for now. That’s why I’m not wearing it today.”","Yun Rong had only asked out of curiosity, and after hearing the explanation, she let the matter drop.","Today, the two first visited a bookshop, where Dai Li waved her hand and purchased numerous scrolls and paintings, all claimed to be the final masterpieces of a renowned artist—much to the shopkeeper’s barely concealed delight.","After leaving the bookshop, they strolled through the entire North Market. Along the way, they passed Ruixiang Silk Emporium, which they had visited the day before, and Dai Li pulled Yun Rong inside once more.","Yun Rong was baffled. “Didn’t we come here yesterday? Why return today?”","Dai Li replied, “I might have misheard, but I thought someone mentioned new stock arriving today. Let’s take a look.”","Yun Rong racked her brain.","New stock? Had anyone said that?","When they left yesterday, she hadn’t heard a word about fresh fabrics arriving today.","Lost in thought, Yun Rong failed to notice Dai Li slipping away to speak with a maid. Meanwhile, just five steps away, another person locked eyes with Dai Li and gave a slight nod.","Soon after, Dai Li returned. “Sister Yun, I must have misheard—Ruixiang isn’t getting new stock today. But since there’s nothing here, let’s try another silk emporium.”","Though they had only visited two places, Yun Rong’s legs were already aching terribly. Her frustration and impatience bubbled up like swamp gas, impossible to suppress.","What was the point of all this? These fabric shops were all the same. If she truly fancied a particular material, she could simply notify the shopkeeper, who would deliver it to the estate as soon as it arrived. Why bother going in person?","Or was this just the way of a spoiled concubine—neither dignified nor refined, but as narrow-minded as a frog in a well?","“Sister Yun, are you tired again?” Dai Li suddenly asked.","Caught off guard, Yun Rong stiffened before forcing a smile. “Indeed, I am a little weary. How about we rest at a teahouse for a while?”","Dai Li walked out with her, but as they boarded the carriage, she said, “The food at Moonlight Residence is quite good. Since you’ve lived in Nankang County for years and have seen much of the world, are there any other high-class inns like Moonlight Residence here?”","Rarely praised by Dai Li, Yun Rong was happy to offer advice. “There are two others—Breeze Pavilion and Orchid Retreat. Both are excellent.”","“Orchid Retreat—what a lovely name. Let’s go there instead. It must be more refined than an ordinary teahouse.” Dai Li ordered the coachman to change course.","Moonlight Residence and Orchid Retreat were both located in the East Market, though they stood at opposite ends, facing each other across the street.","Yun Rong and Dai Li entered Orchid Retreat and, just like the day before, booked a private room to enjoy some sweets. And once again, pleased by the delicacies, Dai Li extended their stay with a generous tip.","A quarter of an hour later, Dai Li left Orchid Retreat with her maids and guards, while Yun Rong remained behind to rest.","But shortly after stepping outside, Dai Li halted. She turned to a square-jawed guard among her retinue and said, “Return to Orchid Retreat and switch places with the guard serving Sister Yun—the one with the black mole on his jaw. You needn’t follow me.”","“But the lord instructed—”","“Last night, Qin Changgeng told me that when we’re out in the city, I make the decisions. Did he not inform you?” Dai Li’s expression darkened.","Whether it was the weight of Qin Changgeng’s name from Dai Li’s lips or the guard’s own awareness of certain matters, he hesitated before bowing and turning back.","Once the only soldier belonging to Qin Shaozong had been dismissed, Dai Li turned and headed back to the North Market.","On the way, she casually instructed Ding Xiang, “Go back and inform Sister Yun that if she wishes to find me after resting, she should go to Prosperous Silk Emporium before the hour of the Monkey, and to the slave market afterward. I’ll definitely be at one of those two places. After delivering the message, bring me some honey cakes from Orchid Retreat—and be careful not to break them.”","The carriage was fast, and they had already entered the North Market. Ding Xiang would have to walk back, ensuring she wouldn’t return to Dai Li’s side anytime soon.","Bound by her mistress’s orders, Ding Xiang had no choice but to comply.","With three guards and two maids in tow—now reduced to just Tao Xiang after Ding Xiang’s departure—Dai Li arrived at the silk emporium.","In a place frequented by ladies, it was improper for the guards to follow too closely, so they were ordered to wait at the bookshop.","Dai Li began trying on garments. After the first set, she turned to Tao Xiang. “Go to the bookshop next door and check if the three of them have been driven out. If the shopkeeper dislikes their presence, take them to the bookshop where I bought the paintings earlier. Since you accompanied me then, the shopkeeper will recognize you. He won’t refuse—not after the business we did.”","Tao Xiang couldn’t help but feel puzzled.","Since when did the capricious Madam Dai care about her servants’ comfort?","Just as the thought arose, Dai Li added, “If people see my guards being chased out and standing around like wooden posts in the street, where would that leave my dignity?”","Tao Xiang: “...”","Her doubts instantly vanished. Clearly, she had overthought things—this mistress would never empathize with others.","“But Madam, if I leave, you’ll be alone here. That’s hardly proper,” Tao Xiang murmured.","Dai Li scoffed. “What’s improper about it? I’ll stay inside the emporium—where else would I go? If you can’t find me outside, I’ll be trying on clothes. Don’t disturb me; just wait. I’m not a fool—why would I abandon the comfort of being waited on to wander off alone?”","Tao Xiang supposed that made sense. This mistress was far too pampered to lift a finger herself. Still, she hurried off, eager to return quickly.","As Tao Xiang’s figure receded, the mockery and impatience on Dai Li’s face faded like ink dissolving in water, leaving only stillness behind.","The fable of \"The Boy Who Cried Wolf\" is well-known to later generations. The first time an incident occurs, it is usually treated with great caution. But if it turns out to be nothing serious afterward, then the second time it happens, people become far less wary and vigilant.","Just like yesterday, when she parted ways with Yun Rong at Moonlight Residence, the latter had been hesitant and full of worry. Today, when the same scenario played out again, Yun Rong agreed much more readily than before.","The maids and guards who were sent away today were understandably on edge—after all, this was the first time the \"wolf\" had appeared.","Logically, she should have staged a few more \"wolf\" incidents to desensitize Tao Xiang and the others, but she didn’t have the time.","Tomorrow would be the last day of her \"monthly courses.\" She had to leave Nankang County by then. If she didn’t leave tomorrow, then the day after...","Selecting a dress, Dai Li took a clever-looking maid from the silk shop into the fitting room with her.","Once the door was closed, Dai Li pulled out some silver coins from a small pouch and weighed them in front of the maid. \"Answer a few questions truthfully, and all this will be yours.\"","\"Please speak, madam,\" the maid immediately straightened up. Earning silver just for answering questions? Such an opportunity couldn’t be missed.","Dai Li: \"How many ports are there around Nankang County, and where are they located?\"","The maid: \"There’s only one port, four li east of the city, called White Horse Crossing.\"","Dai Li fell into thought.","A single port meant there was only one major river nearby. It seemed that in this era, the Hutuo River had no other significant tributaries.","Four li—roughly half an hour’s walk, or two ke. In peaceful times, walking half an hour outside the city wouldn’t be an issue. But this port was in the east, where a ruined temple served as a gathering place for refugees. Walking alone outside the city walls as dusk approached was far from wise.","Better safe than sorry.","But before that...","\"Does White Horse Crossing have daily departures to other places?\" Dai Li clenched her fist, her palm damp with sweat, fearing the maid would shake her head and say no.","The maid nodded. \"Yes. Nankang County has a large population, so ferrymen and fish vendors find it profitable to operate there, rain or shine.\"","The weight in Dai Li’s chest lifted instantly. \"Do the long-distance voyages depart in the evening?\"","The maid nodded again. \"Indeed. The ferrymen usually set sail at the end of the Shen hour. Any later, and the city gates would be closed, preventing passengers from leaving. Besides, long-distance ships benefit from evening departures—passengers can sleep and wake up at their destination.\"","Ferrymen operated for profit, after all, so they naturally tried to attract as many passengers as possible.","Dai Li tossed the silver coins to the maid, and as the latter beamed with delight, she pulled out another handful. \"I have a simple business proposition for you. If you agree, I’ll reward you handsomely—enough to keep you well-fed and clothed for years.\"","The maid’s heart raced at the sight of the coins. \"Please speak, madam. If it’s within my power, I won’t refuse.\"","Dai Li: \"A distant relative of mine will depart for White Horse Crossing tomorrow after the Shen hour. I need you to arrange a donkey cart for her—whether it’s a merchant’s cart or a security escort’s, as long as it’s reliable. The cart must wait at the eastern end of Harmony Street between the start of the Shen hour and the second ke. Once it picks her up, it must leave immediately.\"","A small pouch was tossed over, and the maid caught it eagerly with both hands.","Dai Li: \"This is the deposit. After deducting the cart fare, there’ll still be plenty left. Once the job is done, I’ll give you three times this amount.\"","The maid clutched the pouch and nodded repeatedly, now fully invested. \"One of the silk shop’s delivery workers is a distant cousin of mine. I’ll make sure the trip to White Horse Crossing is arranged perfectly. But... what does your relative look like?\"","\"She has dark skin and many moles on her face, often wearing a veil to hide them. She won’t be hard to recognize.\" Dai Li handed her a small bamboo slip with half of a black character for \"cart\" carved on it. \"This is the token. Give it to the driver. My relative will bring the other half to match it as proof.\"","The maid accepted the slip solemnly.","Creak. The fitting room door opened.","Not long after, Tao Xiang returned. Dai Li tried on two more dresses and ordered several bolts of fine fabric before leaving.","At the second ke of the Shen hour, Dai Li returned to Orchid Pavilion with her guards and maids, rejoining Yun Rong, who had napped and now looked refreshed, before heading back to the estate.","Over an hour after their departure, a veiled woman carrying a bundle appeared in Orchid Pavilion.","\"Shopkeeper, Madam Dai has a package she’d like to store...\"","Having already dined out, Dai Li went straight to her chambers upon returning and instructed Tao Xiang and Ding Xiang to prepare bathwater. She needed to relax—tomorrow would be a tough battle, and a good night’s rest was essential.","\"Madam, the bath is ready,\" Tao Xiang announced.","Dai Li untied her belt and began undressing when Tao Xiang spoke again. \"Madam, has your monthly course ended? Should I prepare the sanitary cloth?\"","Creak. The wooden hinge of the outer door turned.","Ding Xiang had just stepped out to fetch fruit, so Tao Xiang hadn’t locked the door yet. Now, it swung open with a light push.","Dai Li’s heart skipped a beat.","Ding Xiang had only just left—she shouldn’t be back so soon. Could it be...?"]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20","paragraphs":["A towering black shadow stretched across the carved wooden screen, its silhouette cast by the lamplight. The screen was adorned with delicate paintings of flowers and birds, yet under the shadow's oppressive presence, those elegant motifs seemed to sprout menacing fangs and claws, making it difficult to meet their intimidating gaze.","In the side chamber, Dai Li heard Tao Xiang's greeting from outside, followed by a deep, resonant voice dismissing her with a curt, \"You may leave.\"","Dai Li immediately looked down at herself, attempting to straighten her disheveled robes. Unlike modern attire, ancient garments were far from simple—layers of undergarments, sashes, and outer robes tangled together, each fastened with ties that easily slipped out of place.","The side chamber lacked shadowless lamps, and as footsteps drew nearer, a faint, elongated silhouette entered her line of sight like a prowling tiger leisurely stalking through the woods.","Her long lashes fluttered slightly. Instead of fumbling with the ties as before, Dai Li slowly lifted her gaze to the man standing just a few steps away.","Now that they were alone, he no longer restrained the commanding aura he had honed through blood and battle. The oppressive weight of his presence, that of a high-ranking figure accustomed to dominance, made him seem unapproachable.","\"It seems my timing is unfortunate, interrupting my lady’s bath,\" he remarked, though his tone carried not a shred of apology.","Dai Li wore a stone-blue deep robe with cloud-patterned lapels, its sash untied and collar loosened, revealing more of her décolletage than usual—a glimpse of snow-white skin half-concealed, half-exposed.","He advanced step by step until he stood before her, his shadow enveloping her. Qin Shaozong reached for her sash, his long fingers winding around it twice. A single tug would undo the already loose belt entirely. \"I heard my lady dismissed her guards today. May I ask why?\"","The side chamber held far fewer lamps than the outer rooms. The flickering bean-sized flame in the humid air cast an uncertain glow, weaving an unspoken tension between them—like two towering trees whose roots had entwined over time, inseparable.","\"Might the guards my lord speaks of be the one with the...\" Dai Li gestured a square shape over her face, \"whom I sent back to the lady of the mansion?\"","Qin Shaozong watched her movement, a hint of amusement flickering in his eyes, though he countered with a question of his own. \"What does my lady think?\"","\"I suppose so.\" Dai Li lowered her gaze, using both hands to gently pry his fingers from her sash, slowly unwinding the silk from his grasp.","\"However, when we first arrived at the mansion, we quarreled—so fiercely that I stormed off in anger, and you didn’t assign me maids until noon the next day. Such a rift isn’t trivial. A proud and willful heart holds grudges easily. It’s only natural that I wouldn’t want to see your soldiers while strolling outside.\"","\"Today marks the seventh day. Any quarrel between us should have faded by now.\" His fingers suddenly tightened around the sash.","With that motion, the half-undone belt was pulled taut in his grip.","Yet, strangely, Dai Li’s heart steadied.","His questioning wasn’t about reprimand or punishment—it was a warning. Like many in power, he despised subordinates who twisted his authority to issue false commands.","\"Indeed, it’s nearly settled. Tomorrow, I’ll venture out again, indulging in lavish purchases of jewelry and fabrics, all while leaving your captain of guards waiting. Consider it my way of venting. I hope my lord won’t take offense.\"","Her soft fingers brushed lightly over the scar on his hand before attempting to loosen his grip.","She barely exerted any force—just a teasing scratch—yet his ironclad hold slackened. Dai Li retrieved her sash with a deft hook of her fingers. \"By tomorrow night, it will have been exactly seven days since my monthly courses began. By then, my body will be... suitable again. We can reconcile in bed, letting all grievances dissolve as nature takes its course.\"","Qin Shaozong stood nearly a head taller, his gaze descending upon her.","The woman before him had cheeks tinged pink, ink-dark hair, brows like distant mountains, and a vermilion mark between her brows as vivid as spilled blood—radiant beyond compare.","Her robes were in disarray, the overlapping collars loose enough to reveal a tantalizing expanse of milky skin, glowing like moonlit cream or the most fragrant magnolia in spring. With each breath, the snowy curves trembled faintly.","One of the bean-sized lamps flickered out, and Qin Shaozong’s eyes darkened further.","Yet even in the dimming light, her striking allure remained undiminished, now tinged with a lazy sensuality that invited wild imaginings.","Dai Li waited, but when no words came, she glanced up—only to nearly gasp at the look in his eyes.","His brown irises had darkened to near-black, smoldering with a hunger so fierce it seemed ready to leap out and devour her. For a moment, she felt like prey beneath the gaze of a starving tiger sharpening its fangs.","Instinctively, she lowered her head—only to catch sight of the pronounced tenting of his black robes.","A shiver ran down her spine.","Perhaps she had pushed a little too far...","\"My lord should leave now, lest the maids grow suspicious,\" she urged softly.","When he remained unmoving, as if deaf to her words, Dai Li took his arm and guided him toward the door. \"I shall await my lord’s esteemed presence tomorrow night in my chambers.\"","As they stepped out of the side chamber and reached the main hall’s entrance, a low, husky reply came: \"Agreed.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","The door opened and closed swiftly behind him.","Finally alone, Dai Li exhaled in relief, her spirits lifting at the certainty he wouldn’t return tonight.","After a soothing bath, she curled beneath the blankets and drifted into a deep, dreamless slumber.","The sun rose, painting the eastern sky in pale gold.","Spring rain was as precious as oil, yet the past few days had been cloudless, the heavens a crystal blue promising fair weather.","Citing the fine day as perfect for an outing, Dai Li once again left the mansion early with Yun Rong in tow.","They began their excursion in the bustling East Market, sampling delicacies as they wandered, then made their way westward in search of a Western Regions merchant selling exotic cats. Luck, however, was not on their side—after scouring the entire street, they found none.","Yun Rong, having spent years serving her in-laws, bearing four children, and managing a sprawling household, had long since exhausted her vitality.","Now, after hours of walking, her face took on a sickly pallor. Exhausted, she finally called for a halt. \"Sister, I’m weary. Didn’t you reserve a room at the Orchid Pavilion yesterday? Why not rest there as before?\"","Dai Li, sensing the moment was right, countered, \"Sister Yun, didn’t you mention another inn called Breeze Tower? Having tried the other two, we can’t let this one slip by. Let’s rest there instead.\"","Yun Rong’s mind clung only to the word \"rest.\" Where mattered little—if Dai Li suggested Breeze Tower, so be it.","The group changed their route and returned to the East Market, this time heading to Qingfeng Tower located on another street within the market.","The two main streets of the East Market formed a cross, with Qingfeng Tower situated at the southern end of the vertical line. Mingyue Residence and Youlan Court were both on the horizontal line—Mingyue Residence to the east and Youlan Court to the west, the former closer to the eastern city gate.","After securing rooms at Qingfeng Tower and enjoying some refreshments, Dai Li glanced at the square-faced captain of the guards and said dismissively, \"You don’t need to follow me today. Stay by the Prefect’s Lady’s side. I have no use for you.\"","Yun Rong couldn’t help but laugh. \"Still upset with Lord Qin, are you?\"","Dai Li turned away, muttering under her breath, \"Who told him to ignore me when I warned him not to drink? If I don’t make my displeasure clear, he’ll think he can fool me so easily.\"","Yun Rong’s lips twitched, torn between disdain and an inexplicable flicker of envy.","Among the lords of the present era, most had risen through the ranks as civil officials—only Qin Shaozong hailed from the vast borderlands. Though younger than her own husband, his status was already beyond reach.","Born into a prestigious family, possessing the physique of a warrior, and ruling over the entire northern territories, he was at the peak of a man’s power. And yet, this Dai Li, with nothing but a pretty face, had somehow bewitched Lord Qin into doting on her. Worse, she had the audacity to act spoiled and capricious—utterly unaware of her own insignificance.","A mere favored concubine, destined to be cast aside sooner or later...","Dai Li paid no mind to Yun Rong’s thoughts. She left Qingfeng Tower with the same attendants as the day before.","The day wore on as Dai Li visited numerous places. The sun slowly dipped westward, its light softening as the hour approached Shen (3–5 PM).","\"Oh! I nearly forgot—two days ago, I placed an order with a fishmonger in the West Market for seafood and sea cucumbers. The three of you, hurry to the West Market and fetch the goods back to the mansion,\" Dai Li suddenly exclaimed.","These three were not Qin Shaozong’s soldiers, just ordinary guards who carried little more than spare coins. Dai Li had only paid a deposit, and the remaining balance still needed to be settled.","The guards hesitated.","They had no silver on them, and Dai Li hadn’t provided any funds...","Tao Xiang, having served in Jiang Mansion for years, was familiar with its retainers. Seeing their dilemma, she offered, \"Madam, shall I lend them my silver to cover the payment?\"","It was both a reminder and an out.","Dai Li took the cue, glancing at Ding Xiang and signaling her to hand over the money pouch.","The guards accepted the coins but remained uneasy. If they all left, who would ensure the safety of Lord Qin’s favored concubine? Yet sending only one or two might not suffice—after all, the noble’s carriage could hardly be used to transport seafood.","Dai Li waved them off impatiently. \"Go quickly. I’ll wait for you in the Xinglong area. If you’re late and the fishmonger sells my order to someone else, ruining my plans, I’ll have Lord Qin punish you for negligence!\"","Exchanging glances, the guards recalled how she had lingered safely in the bookstore the day before. Surely a brief absence wouldn’t matter.","Besides, even if all three left, Ding Xiang and Tao Xiang remained. It should be fine...","With that, they bowed and departed.","Once they were gone, Dai Li led her attendants to Jin Yu Zhai, an upscale jewelry shop, where she splurged on the most expensive items, emptying Tao Xiang’s money pouch.","\"Tao Xiang, we’re running low on silver. Return to the mansion and fetch more,\" Dai Li ordered, not waiting for a reply before adding, \"Ding Xiang and I will wait at Xinglong Silk Emporium. Be quick—I don’t want to be left without funds later.\"","Without another word, she strode off, indifferent to Tao Xiang’s hesitation. After a moment, Tao Xiang complied.","At the silk emporium, after trying on two outfits, Dai Li fished a few coins from her small embroidered purse. \"Ding Xiang, go to the old man with the goat beard at the end of Pinghe Street and buy me two sesame cakes. I had his cakes yesterday—they’re better than most, and I’ve been craving them. If I’m still trying on clothes when you return, don’t rush me. I’ll come out when I’m ready.\"","Ding Xiang clutched the coins. \"Madam...\"","Dai Li clicked her tongue. \"The shop attendants here can assist me for now. Must you all dawdle and ignore your mistress’s orders? Disgraceful. Perhaps later I’ll complain to Lady Yun about how impossible it is to command her household’s servants—might as well not send any at all!\"","Ding Xiang shuddered and hurried off without another word.","Watching her go, Dai Li exhaled in relief.","Finally, it was done!","Moments after Ding Xiang left, Dai Li slipped out of the emporium.","Silk and fabric shops were in the North Market, while inns were in the East Market. Leaving Xinglong behind, Dai Li hastened toward the East Market.","Her heart pounded the entire way. Though Yun Rong and her entourage were resting at Qingfeng Tower, and the guards and maids had been dismissed, there was no telling if misfortune might strike.","If some Jiang Mansion servant spotted her before she changed clothes, escape would be impossible.","Mingyue Residence lay at the easternmost end of the cross-shaped street, but to reach it, she had to pass Youlan Court on the western side.","Dai Li ducked straight into Youlan Court.","A quarter-hour later, a figure in a wide-brimmed hat emerged, clad in plain, grayish robes—utterly unremarkable.","This figure continued eastward, crossed the intersection, and entered Mingyue Residence, soon exiting with a bundle.","As arranged, a carriage would wait for her at the corner of Donghe Street from Shen Zheng (4 PM) until Shen Er Ke (4:30 PM).","It was now Shen Zheng Yi Ke (4:15 PM).","Donghe Street, a smaller lane branching off the main crossroad in the East Market, was far humbler than the bustling thoroughfare.","Rounding the corner, Dai Li spotted a donkey cart laden with goods, attended by two men in brown tunics—one young, barely twenty, the other middle-aged.","Approaching, she held up half of a \"carriage\" token. \"Is this the cart to Baima Ford?\"","\"So it’s you? Right on time. Get on.\"","The cart’s wheels rumbled over the stone-paved street, heading for the eastern gate. At the checkpoint, their papers were inspected without issue, and soon they passed beyond the city walls.","Seated on the cart, Dai Li felt an overwhelming lightness as the wheels rolled past the gate, as if a great weight had lifted from her shoulders. She turned for one last look at the city behind her—its ancient, solemn silhouette stood silent under the sun, a witness to the passage of time.","Farewell, Nankang Commandery!"]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21","paragraphs":["Qingfeng Tower.","Yun Rong had just woken from a nap, feeling much refreshed. She glanced at the sky, satisfied. It was already nearing the end of the Shen hour, with dusk approaching. As usual, Dai Li should have come looking for her by now to return to the manor together.","Honestly, these past few days of wandering outside had left her with little appetite for dinner. Tomorrow, no matter what that troublemaker said, she absolutely wouldn’t leave the manor with her again.","No—not just tomorrow, but for the next few days as well...","\"Madam! Madam of the Manor!!\"","Just as Yun Rong was lost in thought, a panicked shout snapped her back to attention. She turned and saw Ding Xiang, and her irritation flared.","\"Why are you so frantic? You’ll scare away all the good fortune—\"","\"Madam of the Manor, Lady Dai is missing!\"","Their voices overlapped.","The surroundings fell silent in an instant.","Yun Rong’s eyes widened, wondering if she was still dreaming. Otherwise, how could she be hearing such absurd news?","Yun Rong stood frozen, while the square-faced guard captain beside her, who had been forcibly left behind by Dai Li’s orders, turned pale with alarm.","He immediately demanded, \"How did Lady Dai disappear? Where did it happen? When? Speak quickly!\"","Ding Xiang had run all the way to Qingfeng Tower and was still gasping for breath. Her explanation came in broken fragments, making Yun Rong even more anxious, her own breath nearly catching in her throat.","Once the details were finally pieced together, Yun Rong sucked in a sharp breath. \"That troublemaker is the most willful person, always doing as she pleases without a care for others. Could it be that she quarreled with Lord Qin again last night, leading to this unnecessary drama today?\"","After all, this favored concubine had a history of such behavior. Once, she had vanished from her pavilion without a word, throwing the entire manor into chaos.","Yun Rong hastily ordered, \"Send people to search immediately—the jewelry shops, fabric stores, and silk shops in the North Market, the Moonlight Pavilion and Orchid House in the East Market, and check the West Market too. Oh, and we must return to the manor—she might have gone back ahead of us.\"","The servants quickly dispersed, rushing out of Qingfeng Tower in a flurry.","After some thought, Yun Rong decided Dai Li might still come to Qingfeng Tower, so she left Ding Xiang behind while she returned to the manor with the square-faced guard captain and another Jiang Manor attendant.","Jiang Manor.","Yun Rong entered through the side gate and asked the guards if Dai Li had returned. When they said no, her heart sank, but she still clung to hope as she stepped inside.","The manor had more than one gate—what if that troublemaker had come back through another entrance?","She headed toward the guest pavilion but happened to run into Qin Shaozong, who was just leaving the main house.","The setting sun cast a golden hue over the tall, imposing man, bathing his black robes in a soft, honeyed glow. Yet the warmth did nothing to soften his demeanor. The general, whose family had guarded the borders for generations, remained stern and distant, exuding an unshakable air of authority.","This was the first time Yun Rong had faced Qin Shaozong without her husband present, but she had no time for fear now. She cut straight to the point. \"Lord Qin, has Xiao Li returned to see you?\"","Qin Shaozong replied, \"No. Why do you ask, Madam of the Manor?\"","Yun Rong hesitated for a few breaths, torn between telling the truth outright or waiting to see if Dai Li would return first. In the end, she chose the former and tentatively shifted the blame.","\"Xiao Li sent her maid away to buy snacks and then disappeared from Xinglong Silk Shop without a word. No one knows where she went. When she left the manor today, she seemed upset and even complained about you once or twice along the way. Did you two quarrel last night?\"","The casual expression on Qin Shaozong’s face slowly faded, like a tide receding. \"We had no quarrel. She dismissed one maid to buy snacks—what about the others? Don’t tell me only a single maid was with her the entire time?\"","Yan San and Mo Yanyun, hearing the commotion, stepped out from the side room. Seeing the Madam of the Manor there, they curiously asked what had happened.","Yun Rong grew uneasy, stammering as she explained that she had grown tired and parted ways with Dai Li—she had gone to rest at an inn while Dai Li continued shopping. She emphasized that Dai Li had left with three guards and two maids.","The unspoken implication was clear: It wasn’t that she hadn’t arranged for attendants—Dai Li had dismissed them all herself.","Under their scrutinizing gazes, Yun Rong didn’t dare leave anything out. She swallowed hard and continued recounting what she had learned from Ding Xiang, her voice growing quieter.","When she mentioned that Dai Li had ordered seafood and sea cucumbers from a fishmonger in the West Market two days prior, scheduling pickup for today—hence why three guards had been sent there—Mo Yanyun froze.","But that wasn’t all. Yun Rong added that Dai Li had claimed she was short on silver and sent one maid back to the manor to fetch more. Then, not long after in the silk shop, she had dismissed the last maid to buy flatbreads.","Even the usually reserved Yan San couldn’t hide his shock.","What was Lady Dai doing?","Had Lord Qin discussed a new plan with her last night? But this didn’t seem like it...","Qin Shaozong stood motionless for several breaths before finally speaking, his voice devoid of emotion. \"I understand. Thank you for informing me, Madam of the Manor. You may go now. I will handle the rest.\"","Yun Rong’s heart pounded with unease. The moment Qin Shaozong gave her leave, she wasted no time in departing.","Once she was gone, Mo Yanyun frowned and asked in a low voice, \"My lord, could this be the work of Li Zan’s faction? They might have infiltrated Nankang County in secret, learned of Lady Dai’s recent favor, and orchestrated this.\"","Yan San, however, countered, \"If that were the case, there’s one necessary assumption—that Lady Dai is one of Li Zan’s people.\"","\"True. And since you’ve allowed her to serve by your side, why would she risk so much for so little?\" Mo Yanyun scratched his head, utterly baffled.","Qin Shaozong took a deep breath and closed his eyes, replaying his recent interactions with Dai Li in his mind. Scenes flashed by like a reel unwinding.","\"Since you’ve been gracious enough to overlook the past and still hold me in high regard, how could I possibly push you away?\"","\"A night of spring is worth a thousand in gold—why don’t we retire early?\"","\"...Let us find joy together, resolve our disputes in bed, and let things unfold naturally. That way, we may reconcile.\"","\"I shall await your esteemed presence in my chambers tomorrow evening.\"","The lingering sweetness of her voice echoed in his ears, tender as honey, weaving an intricate web that ensnared him effortlessly.","Qin Shaozong suddenly opened his eyes and turned to Mo Yanyun, his gaze dark and unfathomable. \"Is it true that all healthy women must bleed for exactly seven days during their monthly courses?\"","Mo Yanyun, well-versed in such matters, instinctively answered, \"Who said that? Of course not.\"","The air around them seemed to grow colder, biting to the bone. Mo Yanyun unconsciously lowered his voice. \"It varies. A lover I once had in Yunzhong County was done in just three days. Why do you ask?\"","Qin Shaozong’s expression turned thunderous. The corners of his lips curled into a humorless smile.","\"She’s truly something!\""]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22","paragraphs":["Mo Yanyun stared blankly at the cold smile on Qin Shaozong's face, his mind momentarily failing to catch up.","Lady Dai... what was 'very good' about it?","Why would His Lordship say such a thing? And why had he suddenly asked about the duration of the young lady's monthly courses earlier? He had never shown any concern for such matters in the past.","\"Hu Bao, send your men into the city. Search where you must, inquire where you must,\" Qin Shaozong said, looking at the square-faced captain.","The courtyard was not a place for conversation. He turned and walked back to the main house.","Yan San immediately followed. Mo Yanyun, his soul seemingly detached from his body, drifted along behind them in a daze.","After Mo Yanyun, who was last to enter, came in, Yan San saw he was still standing there dumbfounded and turned to close the door. Just as the door shut, he heard Mo Yanyun speak: \"My Lord, this subordinate has a question. I dare to ask for your instruction.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"Speak.\"","Mo Yanyun took a deep breath. \"That night seven days ago, when you suddenly left the main house... was it because Lady Dai's monthly courses had arrived then?\"","He had previously speculated that Lady Dai had simply been unlucky with her timing, that her courses had inconveniently arrived, thus preventing her from serving. But that was merely speculation, and such a matter was awkward to state outright. Now, however, the situation was different.","His Lordship had specifically set a trap for Jiang and Li. Lady Dai was the most crucial piece in that scheme, yet such a circumstance had arisen halfway through the game. As his subordinate, some questions, no matter how awkward, had to be asked.","Qin Shaozong replied expressionlessly, \"Correct.\"","Mentioning this only made the fire in his heart burn fiercer. Whether her courses had truly arrived seven days ago was still debatable, but one thing was certain: she truly had no desire to serve him.","Her previous interactions were merely an act, all that tender affection was false compliance, meant to beguile him so she could seize an opportunity to escape.","She was utterly audacious!","Connecting the dots, Mo Yanyun had also arrived at this realization and was momentarily speechless.","How dare a mere woman like Lady Dai act in such a manner? Could... could there be some misunderstanding here?","After a long pause, Mo Yanyun finally said, \"My Lord, I feel this matter is full of doubts and strangeness. Moreover, the current situation cannot proceed without her. It might be best to first bring her back for careful questioning. Right! You previously issued her a travel pass. She must have used it to leave the city and head to her old residence in the western district! Please assign me a squad of men. I will go and bring Lady Dai back.\"","Qin Shaozong, standing by the window, offered no reply. He merely turned and walked towards a wooden box in the corner of the inner room.","Yan San suddenly uttered two words: \"The array.\"","Mo Yanyun slapped his forehead. \"Right! There's also a maze array. I almost forgot about that. The surrounding area has an array that can conceal dwellings within the wilderness. Ah, when you think about it, Lady Dai's old residence in the western district really is a perfect hiding place.\"","Creak. A layer of the wooden box was pulled open.","Mo Yanyun turned at the sound just in time to see an object flying through the air. It was caught with swift precision by Yan San, who raised his hand.","He focused his eyes. It was a small bamboo tablet, its appearance somewhat familiar. Before he could ponder further, he saw Yan San's expression suddenly change. \"My Lord, this is...\"","Mo Yanyun moved closer curiously to look and was instantly stunned.","The travel pass. It was Lady Dai's travel pass!","No wonder it looked familiar. Yan San had made it with his own hands, and Mo Yanyun, sharing a room with him, had seen it several times.","\"Does this mean she didn't leave the city? Or does she have another pass?\" Yan San said gravely.","Qin Shaozong let out a light, cold laugh. \"She's full of deceit and falsehoods. Do you truly believe that so-called old residence in the western district and its maze array even exist?\"","The ways of the Jianghu were bizarre and varied—talismans and spells, summoning spirits, exorcisms, divine possessions, prophecies, divinations, fortune-telling... all ultimately boiled down to one word: \"deception.\"","They deceived the shallow-minded, the unenlightened common folk, manipulating these fools for their own ends. Whether it was to temporarily placate them and avoid unrest, or to turn them into weapons in their own hands, it all came with ulterior motives and couldn't escape the word \"profit.\"","Those Taoist priests, he detested them deeply.","Therefore, when his men initially failed to find any dwelling at the address she provided, his first thought wasn't that he hadn't sent enough soldiers or that his subordinates had been negligent. It was... suspicion that she was lying.","But at the time, she had been calm and composed. She had even proactively set a time to personally lead people to the old residence, and later submitted the travel pass. So he had suppressed his doubts, thinking he would grant her those three days.","And as a result of waiting, he had waited until she vanished!","His first impression had been correct after all. She was no docile little rabbit, but clearly a cunning fox with more schemes than a honeycomb has holes.","\"My Lord, what should we do now?\" Mo Yanyun was at a loss. He tentatively offered a suggestion: \"Should we search the city? It's the Hour of the Rooster now. The city gates are closed. Without a pass, she cannot leave. We could catch her like a turtle in a jar. We would surely apprehend Lady Dai.\"","\"She may not be without a pass,\" Yan San suddenly interjected.","When His Lordship gifted something to the young lady, it was given and he never condescended to ask for it back. The fact that this travel pass had now returned to His Lordship's hands must mean Lady Dai had actively returned it.","She clearly knew her deception would provoke His Lordship's great wrath. She clearly knew one couldn't leave the city without a pass. Why would she actively return it?","Clearly, she had a backup plan!","Qin Shaozong said in a low voice, \"Mo Yanyun, go and summon one of Lady Yun's personal maidservants. I have questions for her.\"","Mo Yanyun bowed, accepting the order, and quickly left.","Qin Shaozong twisted the thumb ring on his finger, his gaze dark and turbulent like a black sea. Numerous conjectures flashed through his mind, only to be swiftly dismissed one by one.","Nankang Commandery, Eastern Suburbs.","The donkey cart traveled through the desolate outskirts of the city, passing the ruined temple in the eastern suburbs from a distance, and finally arrived at White Horse Ferry. As the only ferry within a ten-mile radius of Nankang Commandery, White Horse Ferry was undeniably bustling.","The crescent-shaped ferry was clearly organized. The area closer to the upstream was concentrated with cargo ships, though by now, with the sun setting in the west, there were few ships left, whether arriving or departing.","Further downstream, there were many passenger ships, large and small, new and old. One could see a continuous stream of travelers boarding the ships via long planks from the shore.","\"We're here,\" said the brawny man in short attire.","Perhaps because he had earned a particularly handsome sum for this trip, he didn't mind saying a few more words to Dai Li. \"The large passenger ships are all capable of long voyages, the furthest reaching White Wave Ferry in Haijian Kingdom. If you wish to travel far and aren't short on funds, I suggest you board a newer ship... There, that one.\"","He pointed towards a two-story passenger ship. \"The helmsman of that ship is the son of the Commandery Deputy. His family isn't lacking in silver, so he runs this ferry purely out of interest—he loves being a 'white strip in the waves' on the river. Therefore, compared to other helmsmen, he's a bit more straightforward.\"","Seeing the other party was in a talkative mood, Dai Li seized the chance to ask: \"If I want to go south to Hang... to Qiantang, which route from White Horse Ferry would get me there the fastest?\"","The ancient name for Hangzhou was Qiantang. If she said Hangzhou directly, no one would understand. Yet even so, the young man in his twenties scratched his head, puzzled. \"Where is Qiantang?\"","Dai Li was momentarily taken aback before she realized that in this era, due to inconvenient transportation, ordinary people rarely traveled far from home, except for merchants who traveled north and south for business and some wandering tourists or knights-errant. For most, visiting a few nearby commanderies was likely the limit; they would not journey to a foreign land a thousand miles away.","The older, burly man said, \"I don't know where Qiantang is either, but since you're heading south, you can take a boat to Riyue Crossing. It's less than half a day's journey from here. Once you reach Riyue Crossing, head south, and you'll soon arrive at Taiping Commandery. Continue south through Taiping Commandery, and you'll see a ferry called Zhuya Crossing. It connects to the Qi River flowing from north to south; you can change course there and head south.\"","Beneath her veil hat, Dai Li curved her lips into a smile and gave a slight bow of thanks to the two men. \"Thank you.\"","Jiang Residence, Guest Courtyard.","Mo Yanyun made a quick round trip and soon returned with a maid.","Qin Shaozong, Mo Yanyun, Yan San—each of them had fought their way through scenes of swordplay and bloodshed. They had beheaded others, built victory mounds of enemy heads, and taken countless lives.","The maid had never faced such an intimidating scene, like a tribunal. Standing before them, under the gaze of three pairs of eyes as cold as icy blades, looking at her as if she were already dead, she nearly fainted from fright.","There was no need for threats or bribes. She answered whatever Qin Shaozong asked, trembling as she confessed how Dai Li had lost her travel pass, then used Yun Rong's hand to have a replacement made—not just one, but two passes.","Qin Shaozong had long stopped twisting the jade thumb ring on his finger. As the questioning deepened, a web of fine cracks appeared on the surface of the ring.","Mo Yanyun couldn't help but rub his face.","What a masterful deception!","Good heavens, this Lady Dai truly has a heart of seven apertures and eight cavities—exceedingly clever, perhaps too clever.","Two passes. It seemed extremely likely that Lady Dai had already left the city. No, not just likely—she must have gotten out! Otherwise, staying in the city would only mean capture.","Just as they finished questioning the maid, Hu Bao came to report that some traces of Dai Li had been found.","Hu Bao: \"My Lord, we went to several major markets besides the Southern Market, visiting the jewelry shops, bookstores, fabric and silk shops, eateries, teahouses, as well as inns and courier stations that Lady Dai had frequented these past few days. The proprietors of both the Moonlight Lodge and the Orchid Court stated that Lady Dai had both deposited and retrieved packages at their establishments, though the times differed slightly.\"","Mo Yanyun exclaimed in surprise, \"When were the packages deposited? Who deposited them for her?\"","Hu Bao continued, \"The proprietor of Moonlight Lodge said a package was deposited at his shop at the end of the Shen hour the day before yesterday and retrieved at the Zheng quarter of the Shen hour today. The proprietor of Orchid Court said a package was deposited at the end of the Shen hour yesterday and retrieved at the Zheng quarter of the Shen hour today. As for the depositor...\"","The cold, piercing gaze from directly ahead remained fixed on him. Even though Hu Bao knew it wasn't directed at him, his square face paled slightly. \"Both inn proprietors said the young woman who deposited the packages wore a veil hat, so her features were unclear. However, her clothing appeared quite plain, most likely that of a servant girl.\"","Mo Yanyun blurted out, \"She had an accomplice? Could it be one of those hidden servants from the old residence in the west city?\"","\"Is that fifty-ounce lump you call a head only capable of remembering the old residence in the west city? Or is everything else just deadwood and weeds to you?\" Qin Shaozong couldn't be bothered to look at him.","Mo Yanyun choked back his words, not daring to respond.","\"If she had an accomplice, she wouldn't have needed to wait until today,\" Yan San recalled Dai Li's schedule. \"Before today, Lady Dai had left the residence for three consecutive days, each time wandering the streets and alleys. That very much seems like preparation for today. If she had help, why would she need to go through three full days of effort?\"","Qin Shaozong turned to look out the window. Through the carved wooden lattice, he could see only the faintest, almost imperceptible remnants of twilight in the sky. The golden crow had already set in the west. Dusk was nearly over, and night was about to fall.","From the moment Yun Rong returned to the residence with news of Dai Li's disappearance to the soldiers being dispatched to search and bring back messages from the inns, more than an hour had passed.","The city gates closed at the end of the Shen hour, the beginning of the You hour. That time had long since passed.","Qin Shaozong pondered for a moment, then instructed Hu Bao, \"Hu Bao, take a squad of men. Bring along her two former personal maids. Have them identify all the maids from the silk and fabric shops she had contact with in recent days, and question each one about their whereabouts at the end of the Shen hour yesterday and the day before yesterday. Anyone who can't give a proper account, bring them all before those two proprietors and have them identify each one.\"","Hu Bao cupped his hands and accepted the order.","Mo Yanyun said in a low voice, \"My Lord, Nan Kang Commandery borders Yulin to the east, Chizhou to the south, Gu Han to the west, and Tian Wu to the north. There aren't too many cities and commanderies nearby, but they're not few either. If she really has left the city, there are plenty of places she could go. The sky is vast for the bird to fly... maybe... just let it go.\"","By the last two words, his voice had dropped several more notches, barely louder than a mosquito's buzz.","\"The sky is vast for the bird to fly? Hah, I'd like to see where she can fly to.\" Dark clouds seemed to churn in Qin Shaozong's eyes.","A soft crunch sounded. Qin Shaozong's jade thumb ring completely shattered into pieces. The man opened his hand, and fragments of jade scattered down.","Mo Yanyun fell silent, not daring to respond to that.","Qin Shaozong asked, \"If you were her, how would you travel after leaving the city?\"","\"Head west to Gu Han Commandery. She mentioned her old residence was in the west city before. I always felt there might be a grain of truth in that... she might have gone west...\" Mo Yanyun muttered.","Qin Shaozong clicked his tongue lightly. \"With a brain like yours, it's no wonder you get swindled out of your silver by young women every time. You deserve it.\"","Mo Yanyun seethed inwardly but dared not speak.","Yan San said seriously, \"White Horse Crossing. If Lady Dai has truly left the city, this subordinate guesses she would head east, to White Horse Crossing. My Lord, your forces are strong, your horses sturdy, and you have countless well-fed steeds. She most likely travels by donkey cart, and a donkey cart's pace is far inferior to that of horses, let alone unharnessed warhorses. Her departure would be fully exposed within an hour and a half at the latest. If she chooses land routes, being caught up is only a matter of time. Moreover, it's unsafe for a woman to travel through the night. However, waterways are different.\"","Traveling by water means traveling by boat, and a boat has an owner.","The boat owner, having collected the passenger's fare, must protect the passenger's safety to some extent, whether for the sake of peace or to maintain his own reputation.","Mo Yanyun looked at the sky outside. \"At this hour, the boats have long since departed. Besides, there are several docks east of White Horse Crossing. We don't know at which one she might disembark.\"","Qin Shaozong thought for a moment. \"The Jiang residence maids attended to her closely. The only time they left her side these past few days was when she was trying on clothes at the fabric and silk shops. That must have been when she found an opportunity. In those fitting areas for noblewomen and ladies, male servants would absolutely not be present. As long as we find that maid, follow the trail, we can learn how she left the city, whose carriage she took, which boat she boarded at White Horse Crossing, and whether she revealed any information along the way.\"","Mo Yanyun suddenly understood.","Indeed, as long as one finds the flaw and follows these threads of clues, there will always be a lead.","Qin Shaozong turned and instructed Yan San, \"Go and notify Jiang Chonghai, have him prepare a tower ship for me.\"","Yan San did not leave. He bowed respectfully to Qin Shaozong and said, \"My Lord, please entrust the task of retrieving Lady Dai to me.\"","\"No, I will go personally,\" Qin Shaozong refused.","Mo Yanyun exclaimed in shock, \"My Lord, you must not! With the prior collusion between Jiang and Li, your going will surely prompt Jiang Chonghai to send word to Li Zan. Ying Commandery is east of Nankang Commandery, and while we don't yet know where Lady Dai has gone, venturing into enemy territory when they are prepared is truly perilous. We are men of action, perhaps... we should not bother with a mere woman.\"","Yan San also advised, \"Lady Dai's current actions show she is not the unlearned woman she initially appeared to be. Her contradictory behavior means this pawn is now useless. Retrieving her at this point would be futile; it would be better to readjust our plans. My Lord, I beg you to reconsider.\"","However, Qin Shaozong curled his thin lips into a smile. \"Do you remember when I said that using a feint to split our forces along the central and lower routes would make Jiang Chonghai about eighty percent convinced?\"","The two men nodded, saying they remembered.","The curve of Qin Shaozong's mouth deepened. \"The remaining twenty percent has now come knocking on our door of its own accord. Why should I turn it away?\"","Mo Yanyun frowned in confusion, while Yan San seemed thoughtful.","Qin Shaozong continued, \"Jiang Chonghai, using the Yun clan as his eyes and ears, certainly knows she has been my favored concubine for only a short time. Since his understanding of her is shallow, why couldn't she be a spy planted by another faction beside me? Now that the spy has succeeded, what's wrong with her retreating with secrets, mission accomplished? Moreover, at this point, her true identity is no longer the key issue. The key lies in my subsequent attitude and actions.\"","The more reckless, foolish, and besotted by beauty he appeared, the more people would believe that there truly was a deeply hidden Mr. Junzi behind him, and that the information she had initially revealed was genuine.","After all, he and this \"spy\" belonged to opposing camps; she would delight in his misfortune. And after this incident, Jiang Chonghai would likely not harbor the slightest doubt again.","\"Have Jiang Chonghai prepare a tower ship for me,\" Qin Shaozong repeated the order, then added, \"Mo Yanyun, you will accompany me. Yan San, you stay at the Jiang residence.\"","Seeing Mo Yanyun hesitate to speak, Qin Shaozong scoffed, \"Back in the northern lands, when I hunted the Wuhuan prince Langye, I took his head right from amidst twenty thousand Wuhuan jackals, was pursued for a hundred li after succeeding, and still managed to retreat unscathed. Even if Li Zan has many capable men and strategists under his command, with both wisdom and courage, could the local terrain here possibly be more treacherous than the northern lands?\"","The northern grasslands were vast, with nomadic tribes following water and grass. There were no large forests, only yellow sand or low, sparse grass. With no cover for miles, one could see far into the distance, with nowhere to hide.","But inside the Great Wall, it was different—rolling mountains and endless forests provided plenty of hiding places.","Mo Yanyun and Yan San exchanged a glance, both simultaneously recalling an old story.","Back when the Qin family was not yet so powerful, there was a prominent Wu clan in the north that rivaled the Qins. Normally, two such prominent families would end up forming a marriage alliance, creating a bond for mutual benefit.","But the Qin and Wu families were an exception due to a blood feud from their ancestors' generation.","Qin Shaozong's own paternal granduncle, the Qin heir at the time, had died indirectly because of the Wu family. The Qins naturally refused to let it go, attacking the Wus openly and covertly, not only costing the Wus their heir but also making them lose a nearly secured provincial governor position.","The Wu family hated them to the bone, wishing they could devour their flesh and crush their bones. The conflict reached the younger generation... or rather, the Wu family targeted several direct descendants of the Qin clan, aiming to uproot them completely and leave the Qins without successors.","Back then, the not-yet-crowned Lord was sent by his father on a distant mission. On the road, he was ambushed and hunted by several hundred men. The Lord immediately abandoned his horse and fled into the mountains.","After three days and two nights, all of the Wu family's hunters were dead. The Lord efficiently completed his mission and leisurely returned home, even having the leisure to pen a letter of admonishment to the Wu family, advising them to send men with better skills next time.","How the Wu family raged afterward and how they eventually fell is beside the point. The key is that once the Lord entered the mountains, it was like a fish returning to the sea or a bird soaring into the sky.","If he didn't wish to be caught, he truly couldn't be.","The two men felt their hearts settle back into place.","Qin Shaozong took the tally from Yan San's hand and, with a slight exertion, the bamboo tally cracked under the pressure. \"Nothing ventured, nothing gained. If this trip can succeed in swallowing Li Zan's main forces in one go, taking Ying Commandery afterward will be as easy as reaching into a bag. Using the letters and other evidence from Li Zan as proof, we can then use them as grounds to remove all officials, large and small, who colluded with him, and replace them with our own men.\"","Mo Yanyun and Yan San bowed respectfully and said no more.","But secretly, Mo Yanyun couldn't help but mutter to himself: Actually, an eighty percent chance seemed pretty high already. Was the Lord truly seeking absolute certainty, or was he unwilling to simply give up on Lady Dai?","Or perhaps, both?","Main Hall.","\"My Lord, these are...\"","Jiang Chonghai looked at the several individuals brought back under Hu Bao's guard and asked, though he already knew the answer. The news of Dai Li's disappearance, or rather her opportunistic departure from the city, had already reached his ears.","Upon first hearing it, Jiang Chonghai was greatly shocked. His first thought was to wonder which faction Lady Dai belonged to, that her methods could be so formidable as to thoroughly dupe Qin Shaozong.","His second reaction was to ponder whether the words spoken through Dai Li's mouth were actually true—had Qin Shaozong really said he wanted to take her to see the peach forest?","But as events unfolded, Jiang Chonghai's doubts gradually diminished. Qin Shaozong seemed unable to swallow this insult, dead set on getting to the bottom of it and recapturing her.","Qin Shaozong replied, \"Lady Dai's disappearance is related to these individuals. I hope Prefect Jiang will temporarily lend me this main hall to use as an interrogation room.\"","\"Of course, my Lord. This humble official also wishes to know who is so bold as to dare persuade your favored concubine to run away from home.\" Jiang Chonghai smiled with a kindly expression, his words making it clear he intended to stay and listen.","Hu Bao looked at Qin Shaozong, who said indifferently, \"Speak directly.\"","So Hu Bao first pointed to the young woman on the far left. \"My Lord, this person is a maidservant from the Ruixiang Silk Shop. Her whereabouts were unknown for the last two days at the end of the Shen hour (around 5 PM). Furthermore, the shopkeepers of both the Bright Moon Residence and the Hidden Orchid Courtyard identified her as the person who deposited the packages.\"","Jiang Chonghai asked curiously, \"My wife previously mentioned to me that there was only one depositor. Why have you brought back two young women and a man?\"","Hu Bao replied, \"The one in the middle is a maidservant from the Xinglong Silk Shop. This woman arranged transportation out of the city for Lady Dai.\"","This discovery was purely a pleasant surprise.","At the time, Hu Bao was leading Ding Xiang and Tao Xiang to thoroughly visit silk and cloth shops, attempting to screen out all suspicious individuals. By chance, he noticed a maidservant acting strangely. When he pulled her out, she was even more terrified out of her wits.","Upon interrogation, the woman indeed proved to be problematic.","Hu Bao then pointed to a brawny man dressed in short work clothes: \"This man has some kinship with a maid from the Xinglong Silk Shop. He was commissioned by her to escort Lady Dai out of the city to White Horse Ford.\"","The three of them trembled like chaff in a sieve, never imagining that a simple transaction would not only alarm the city guards but even bring the Prefect Lord Jiang himself to the scene.","Considering Prefect Jiang's earlier attitude, the man he addressed as \"Junhou\" (Marquis/Lord) likely held a rank no lower, if not higher.","No further interrogation was needed. The brawny man spilled everything like beans from a sack, including Lady Dai's attire at the time, how he escorted her to White Horse Ford, her inquiry about the fastest route to Qiantang by water, his own recommendation, and finally, he stammered, \"...My Lord Prefect, this commoner is truly wronged! Had I known the passenger was a nobleman's consort, I would never have dared to help her leave the city!\"","Jiang Chonghai paid no heed to the man's subsequent pleas. Stroking his chin with two thick fingers, he mused, \"Sun-Moon Ford, Taiping Commandery.\"","Then, as if recalling something, he asked Qin Shaozong, \"Junhou, I just heard Commander Yan mention that you requested a lou-chuan (tower ship). Do you intend to send someone to bring Lady Dai back?\"","Qin Shaozong: \"I will go myself.\"","Jiang Chonghai was taken aback, then exclaimed in surprise, \"You yourself?\"","Qin Shaozong nodded. \"It's the first time in my life I've been played for a fool by a woman to this extent. If I don't capture the Dai woman, I can hardly quell the fury in my heart. Moreover, Taiping Commandery does not border Ying Commandery. That salt smuggler surnamed Li likely won't know of my arrival. It will be a quick trip there and back, it shouldn't pose a major problem.\"","Jiang Chonghai secretly sneered. Truly, fame often exceeds reality. He had thought a vicious tiger had been bred in the north, but now it seemed it was no tiger, but clearly just a wildcat.","Once this Qin Shaozong left, he would immediately send word to Brother Li, ensuring this northern wildcat would never return!","Suppressing his surging thoughts, Jiang Chonghai gestured towards the three captives, his tone as casual as if commenting on weeds in a stone crack. \"Junhou, how would you like to deal with these people?\"","\"Ignorance is no crime. They are but innocent commoners. Besides, they cooperated during the questioning earlier. Release them all,\" said Qin Shaozong. He then brought up the matter of the lou-chuan again, his words implicitly urging Jiang Chonghai to prepare the ship quickly.","Jiang Chonghai smiled like the Maitreya Buddha, inwardly scoffing at his 'womanly benevolence', yet feeling considerably more at ease.","...","A heavy darkness spread across the sky. The night was deep, with chickens and dogs silent. During the thickest darkness of the Yin hour (3-5 am), the east gate of Nankang Commandery slowly opened. A contingent of men and horses slipped out under cover of night, the commotion so great it startled a dozing gate guard awake.","\"Who's making such a grand procession?\"","\"It's Lord Qin and Prefect Jiang leaving the city together. I caught a bit of it earlier; seems the latter is escorting the former to White Horse Ford.\"","\"White Horse Ford? What business is at the ferry in the middle of the night?\"","\"How would I know the affairs of nobles?\"","...","White Horse Ford.","A two-story lou-chuan was moored at the dock. Qin Shaozong dismounted. \"Prefect Jiang, you may stop here. This is far enough.\"","Jiang Chonghai also dismounted, squinting as he watched a group of soldiers board the ship first. He thought to himself that the escort was merely thirty men; this Qin Shaozong was far too arrogant and unaware of the dangers.","On the surface, however, Jiang Chonghai offered a deep bow. \"I pray Junhou takes great care. This humble official awaits good news in Nankang Commandery. May Junhou achieve all his wishes on this journey.\"","Qin Shaozong replied with a faint, ambiguous smile, \"I accept your auspicious words.\"","After Qin Mo and the last two men boarded, the gangplank connecting the ship to the shore was hauled up.","Yan San and a few soldiers stood on the shore watching until the lou-chuan completely disappeared from view. Then, he and the remaining handful of soldiers took hold of the horses.","Jiang Chonghai secretly shot a look at one of his accompanying retainers. The man understood and suddenly called out, asking if anyone needed to relieve themselves.","Several voices answered immediately, all from Jiang Chonghai's retinue. They headed together into the nearby woods. After the sound of flowing water, they returned one after another.","Yan San's gaze swept over the returning Jiang retainers. He noticed one was missing but said nothing, pretending not to know, and left White Horse Ford with Jiang Chonghai and the others.","After the hoofbeats faded into the distance, a figure furtively emerged from the grass. He walked along the dock and finally found a hidden canopy boat in a dense thicket.","A man in a rain hat and cape was inside. Without a word, the man untied the mooring rope as soon as the other boarded, then pushed off from the bank with an oar.","The canopy boat drifted leisurely from the shore, then was swiftly carried eastward by the rushing current.","The sun rose in the east. A gentle breeze skimmed the river surface, carrying a damp, watery chill towards the bustling shore. Sun-Moon Ford was undoubtedly lively in the morning, teeming with noise and clamor, occasionally punctuated by the braying of donkeys.","Fishing boats of all sizes, laden with catch, pulled up to the bank. Basket after basket of fish was loaded onto donkey carts onshore. Fishmongers haggled with the boat owners, money finally changed hands, and some headed back to the city while others prepared to depart.","In another corner of Sun-Moon Ford, passenger lou-chuan began disgorging and taking on travelers.","A tall yet utterly ordinary figure descended from a large lou-chuan. As if new to the place, she walked slowly.","Since disembarking, Dai Li's mood had improved another notch. However, being alone in a foreign place, she didn't let her guard down. There were donkey carts for hire on the shore; a few copper coins could spare her the walk.","But Dai Li did not take one. She observed covertly and noticed that those willing to pay for a ride were mostly in groups and dressed well, almost wearing the words \"financially comfortable\" on their faces.","Dai Li adjusted her veil hat and followed the crowd walking south. After the better part of an hour, an ancient-looking commandery city came into her view. She stopped to look, her brow furrowing beneath the veil.","The scale of this Taiping Commandery was noticeably smaller than that of Nankang Commandery.","Small places are prone to disorder.","But it didn't matter. It was still morning, and she had plenty of time to pass through Taiping Commandery and continue south to Red Cliff Ford. Once aboard a long-distance lou-chuan at Red Cliff Ford, safety would be less of a concern.","She didn't get carsick or seasick and had given last night's lou-chuan journey high marks.","She entered the city using her travel pass.","Once inside, Dai Li didn't head south immediately. Instead, she found a food stall, planning to appease her stomach before leaving the city.","The morning food stall was bustling. Amidst the shouts and haggling, Dai Li also listened to the chatter around her.","\"Things are chaotic out there lately. My peddler cousin told me the Governors of Qingzhou and Yanzhou seem to have had a major falling out over suppressing the Green Lotus Sect, and it ended with their armies clashing.\"","Someone sucked in a sharp breath through their teeth. \"They're fighting? But the border between Qing and Yan is quite a distance from us. The impact shouldn't be too great here.\"","\"Hah, who says the impact isn't significant? They fought fiercely. Seeing the situation turning bad, several bandit lairs on the nearby mountains all packed up and fled. My cousin said a bunch of those bandits simply headed north and put down roots near Taiping County. Haven't you heard that the barges at Zhuya Ford haven't been coming lately?\"","Daili, who was eating noodles, abruptly stopped.","Someone chimed in, \"They won't stop coming completely, I reckon they'll just lay low for a while at most. The Qi River isn't as mighty as the Hutuo River, and Zhuya Ford was always smaller in scale anyway. It's common for boatmen to lay low during times like these, biding their time and waiting for more passengers to gather. After all, people still need to travel south—they wouldn't just pass up silver, would they?\"","\"Tsk, you don't get it. Just look at what kind of places Qingzhou and Yanzhou are? Everywhere is nestled against mountains and rivers, full of waterways. The bandits from those parts are all like 'White Streaks in the Waves'—toss them into the water and it's like releasing a fish into a river, every one of them is an excellent swimmer. Sure, boatmen want to earn silver, but they value their own lives and their boats even more!\"","Daili's heart sank steadily.","These days, there might be no southbound boats at Zhuya Ford."]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23","paragraphs":["Some matters shouldn't be judged by just one side of the story. After finishing her noodles, Daili, unwilling to give up, set down her bowl and headed straight for the marketplace.","Places with many people are good for gathering information, and traveling merchants are especially well-informed. If you ask them, merchants who are eager to highlight the value of their own goods won't hold back; they'll tell you everything they know, even details you didn't ask about—","\"...Zhuya Ford? Yes, the big passenger ships haven't been coming from there recently. When did it start? About four or five days ago, I think. It began when a boatman's vessel was robbed by river pirates. Those pirates have no honor and are utterly heartless. Even though the boatman surrendered his boat, they still killed him to silence him. After word spread, many boatmen were scared out of their wits. They sailed away overnight and won't go near Zhuya Ford anymore. At least for now, there are no ships.\"","\"You ask why the authorities don't intervene? Ha, it's not my place to say clearly, but roughly speaking, among those pirates, there's a shrewd one who's very good at currying favor and building connections. He threw a huge amount of silver at... those up there.\" The peddler pointed skyward. \"Bought their protection, you see. You're asking about other quick routes south? Since you mentioned Zhuya Ford, you must know there's fighting in the south. Once war breaks out, what 'quick routes' are there to speak of? Being safe is blessing enough.\"","\"...Hmm, yes. You could travel south with armed escorts or merchant caravans. But in times like these, it's best to choose a reputable, large escort agency or a big merchant caravan. The former, we don't have here in Taiping County. The latter...\" The peddler grinned and pointed at himself. \"One just returned, fully loaded, and doesn't have plans for another long journey soon.\"","Having said that, the peddler continued enthusiastically trying to sell Daili his tea and spices.","Daili politely declined and turned to leave.","So it was confirmed: the passenger ships at Zhuya Ford had indeed stopped operating. The water route was impassable; she would have to consider traveling by land.","Perhaps because she had only been on the boat for half a day, Daili felt an inexplicable anxiety and unease.","Her escape from the city wouldn't remain secret for long. If that man investigated thoroughly, the maidservant from the silk shop would surely be found. Following that lead, the carter who took her out of the city might also be exposed.","Once the carter was found, he would undoubtedly know she was in Taiping County.","But would he really pursue the matter to the end?","A little white angel with wings said: No, he won't. Qin Shaozong is busy dealing with Prefect Jiang right now, and after Prefect Jiang, there's a major salt smuggler waiting for him. How would he have time to care about a small fry like you? Besides, Taiping County is closer to Ying County. Would he dare come alone? But if he brings troops, where would he find the ships to transport his three thousand soldiers!","A little black demon with wings said: Hah, Qin Shaozong is so proud. Counting the first time, you've tricked him twice now. Do you really think he can swallow that anger? A man with such deep cunning can change his plans as easily as drinking water. It's only half a day's journey from Nankang County. If he sets out at night, he could arrive by noon or afternoon the next day. A quick lightning strike, in and out fast—why not? Better safe than sorry!","The two little figures fought fiercely, until finally the little demon pulled out a big hammer and sent the little angel flying.","Daili looked up at the sky.","It was nearly the end of the Chen hour (around 9 AM). She still had a short period of absolute safety.","She needed to solve the problem of where to stay tonight first.","The official hostel was no longer safe.","Daili pondered for a long time. First, she went to the hostel to pay for storing her bundle. Then she sought out a medical clinic, and finally went to find a cloth merchant's shop.","After spending a little more money, she obtained information about several embroiderers from a young helper at the cloth shop.","In this era, there were no embroidery workshops. Embroiderers worked independently or were employed directly by cloth or silk shops. Whether independent or employed, they all worked from their own homes.","...","\"Knock, knock.\"","Hearing the knocking, the homeowner called out, \"Who is it?\" There was no answer from outside, only another two knocks: \"Knock, knock.\"","The homeowner had no choice but to put down her needlework and go to the door. With a creak of the wooden hinge, Lin Erniang saw a woman wearing a veil hat standing outside.","The other woman was tall and slender, her clothes worn, and she looked unfamiliar even with her face hidden.","She didn't seem to be from the nearby neighborhood.","\"Who are you?\" Lin Erniang asked warily.","She had recently lost her husband and lived alone with her son. The current dynasty encouraged widows to remarry. Not long ago, she had agreed to a marriage proposal and was preparing for her wedding at home, which would take place in a few days.","\"My surname is Rong. I'm an embroiderer from the south. I heard through inquiries that Madam Lin is a highly skilled embroiderer in this area, so I came to visit,\" Daili said softly.","Hearing she was an \"embroiderer,\" the wariness in Lin Erniang's eyes lessened somewhat. The visitor was a woman, less threatening than a large, burly man. Moreover, people always feel a sense of security around things familiar to them and within their own areas of expertise.","Even so, Lin Erniang didn't invite Daili inside, but asked at the door, \"What brings you to me?\"","Daili began her story: \"My elder brother is a traveling merchant. A while ago, I came north with him for business. After purchasing goods in the north, we headed south, but were beset by river pirates at Zhuya Ford. Although we lost all our goods, we managed to escape with our lives. Among the goods was a very important custom embroidery order. I had already finished it, but because of this misfortune, I have to start over. However, the encounter with the pirates injured my hand, and I am unable to embroider the new piece.\"","As she spoke, Daili pulled up her left sleeve a little.","Lin Erniang looked and couldn't help a small gasp.","Heavens, the hand was wrapped up like a dumpling, not a single finger visible. How severe was the injury? No wonder she had smelled medicine earlier; the source was here.","Everyone locally knew about the river pirates near Zhuya Ford, so Lin Erniang had no doubts about that. And judging by the implied meaning in this \"Madam Rong's\" later words, it was very likely she wanted to ask for help in rushing the embroidery.","This was business coming to her door.","Lin Erniang stepped aside. \"Please, come in first.\"","Daili walked in slowly.","\"There's no one else here. My son is only four. You can take off your veil hat,\" Lin Erniang said, closing the door.","\"I have a black birthmark on my face from birth, quite frightening. I hope Madam Lin won't be alarmed,\" Daili said, raising her hand to remove the hat.","Although forewarned, when Lin Erniang actually saw the fierce black birthmark covering nearly half of the woman's face, she still couldn't help but immediately look away.","The image lingered in her mind.","It stretched from the temple down to the bridge of the nose, covering the entire left eye and the jaw on the same side.","What did it resemble?","It looked like a black flame imprinted on her face. As if, when being reborn and drinking the Broth of Oblivion, the whole pot had tipped over, and the torch beneath had scorched a firebrand onto her face.","Daili put her veil hat back on. \"My apologies for startling you.\"","Lin Erniang swallowed awkwardly. \"N-no, not at all. Please, sit. Would you like some tea? I'll brew some for you.\"","Daili did not refuse.","For a moment, only the gurgling sound of boiling water remained in the room, the atmosphere somewhat awkward. Lin Erniang stole several glances at the young woman sitting opposite her, somewhat worried that she had offended the other party earlier, which might lead to her being lowballed later. She was currently preparing for her wedding, and the boys in her household had hearty appetites, leaving her finances truly tight.","Lin Erniang proactively broached a topic, \"May I ask what kind of picture the young lady wishes me to embroider?\"","Dai Li: \"A landscape of mountains and rivers.\"","Lin Erniang was stunned.","The embroidery work she usually received involved flowers, birds, fish, insects, or at most, plant patterns and characters.","How does one embroider a landscape of mountains and rivers?","Dai Li explained, \"My client was a traveler in his youth, having traversed famous mountains, beautiful waters, and vast landscapes across the land. In his old age, he wishes to reminisce about the past, hence he is searching far and wide for someone to embroider the landscapes from his memory. Having traveled north and south with my elder brother for business, I have seen countless mountains and rivers, which aligns with his requirements. That's why he initially chose me.\"","As if sensing Lin Erniang's concern, Dai Li continued, \"Don't worry. This landscape embroidery isn't difficult. I will describe it, and you will embroider. Embroider as much as you can, and I will pay you based on the progress. However, there is one point...\"","\"What is it?\" Lin Erniang hurriedly responded.","Dai Li: \"I must keep a close eye on the progress of the landscape embroidery, making timely adjustments to the details to avoid errors. I will likely need to stay at your residence.\"","This point hadn't occurred to Lin Erniang. She fell silent for a moment. Welcoming a stranger she had only met once to stay in her home felt unsettling no matter how she thought about it.","\"Tap.\" A stack of silver coins was placed on the table.","\"I won't impose on your hospitality. This is for room and board for occasional meals.\" Dai Li smiled and placed another stack of money. \"After losing my goods, I also discarded my needles and threads. If you are willing to take on this commission, please use this for the cost of embroidery materials. Also, only I will be staying at your residence. My elder brother is staying at an inn and will not come to disturb you.\"","Lin Erniang's gaze fell upon the money on the table.","\"This is my identity pass. I am a law-abiding citizen. You can set your mind at ease.\" Dai Li produced a wooden identity tablet. Her left hand was bandaged, so she used her right hand to hold the pass, pressing her index and middle fingers together against the edge of the small bamboo tablet, just covering the surname.","From Lin Erniang's angle sitting opposite, she could only see that the name field contained a single character: \"Li.\"","Dai Li merely showed it briefly without handing it over, putting the pass away after displaying it.","\"My humble abode is crude. I hope the young lady won't mind,\" Lin Erniang said somewhat stiffly.","This was her agreement to let Dai Li stay.","Dai Li's eyes curved into a smile as she pushed the two stacks of silver coins across the table. \"A pleasure doing business. I'll go to the inn to inform my brother and fetch my luggage.\"","After leaving Lin Erniang's home, the time had reached mid-morning. Dai Li pursed her lips in thought for a long moment. She went to the inn to retrieve her bundle but, carrying her belongings, left the city.","The brand-new two-story pleasure boat sailed with the wind, its bow cutting through the river surface, leaving overlapping \"八\"-shaped ripples in its wake. The warm, orange-gold glow of the setting sun spilled over it, raising a layer of brilliant, shattered gold.","After six shichen (twelve hours) of sailing, this pleasure boat departing from Nankang Commandery finally reached its destination.","The boat docked, and a long plank was laid down to connect it to the shore. A group of strong, robust guards disembarked swiftly. They were neatly dressed, their expressions cold, their eyes holding a chilling gleam like the sharp glint of concealed blades.","Those working or ferrying passengers at Riyuejin, and even anglers lurking in the shadows, couldn't help but glance over.","The bustle on the shore seemed to abruptly cool with their arrival, only reigniting after they had left.","\"Whose private troops are those? Their presence is truly intimidating. Just now, when that bushy-browed giant swept his eyes over me, it sent a chill straight to my heart.\"","\"Could they be from the Zhu family? I heard they were ambushed and suffered heavy losses by river bandits at Zhuya Ford a few days ago. Perhaps they've hired men to suppress the bandits?\"","\"Don't be foolish. Look at the sabers at their waists—all uniform in规格, and the scabbards are of excellent quality. The Zhu family lacks that kind of capability.\"","\"Best not to mind or provoke them. They're certainly not here for me.\"","...","Qin Shaozong passed through the city gates just before they closed for the night. Once inside, he didn't immediately search for anyone but first went to the prefectural office of Taiping Commandery.","The prefect of Taiping Commandery was surnamed Deng, with the given name Tuo. This man was already in his sixties.","The current dynasty had regulations stating, \"Officials retire at seventy.\" Deng Tuo still had a few years before stepping down. The older he got, the more cautious he became, and his style of governance had grown increasingly sluggish in recent years.","This evening, like many evenings before, Deng Tuo sat by the window, enjoying his evening meal while admiring the peach blossoms swaying in the breeze in the courtyard, leisurely and content.","\"Prefect, a... a distinguished guest has arrived!\" A servant hurried in at this moment.","Deng Tuo slowly swallowed the beef in his mouth. \"Why such a fluster? Who is the visitor?\"","\"Qin Shaozong. It's Marquis Qin...\"","The servant spoke softly the first time. Deng Tuo only caught the surname \"Qin.\" His gray-white eyebrows furrowed.","Qin?","There were no major households with the surname Qin in the commandery, though there were many branches of the Qin clan in Youzhou to the north and neighboring Bingzhou.","Why would someone from the Qin clan come to see him?","Could it be a passing merchant whose goods were seized by those river bandits at Zhuya Ford? That would be a troublesome matter...","\"Prefect, it is Marquis Qin visiting. That clan leader from the Qin family of the north,\" the servant raised his voice.","Clatter. Deng Tuo's jade chopsticks fell.","After a dazed pause of two breaths, Deng Tuo quickly stood up, abandoning his meal, and hurried out. \"Why would Marquis Qin come to this insignificant little place? No time to ponder that. You, quickly go to the Li residence. Tell my eldest son, who is drinking there, that Marquis Qin from the north has come to our home. He must return immediately to act as host.\"","Deng Tuo stopped abruptly before entering the main hall, straightened his attire, and took a deep breath, thinking that even though his official rank was far inferior, he must not appear too subservient. Yet, the moment he took a step into the main hall, his legs immediately felt weak.","On both sides of the reception hall stood over ten burly men each. They wore light armor, carried ring-pommeled sabers, and the muscles on their arms, clad in bracers, bulged with fluid strength. As he emerged from the side corridor, these soldiers all turned their gaze towards him.","Deng Tuo's white beard trembled slightly. He seemed to catch the scent of yellow sand and blood mingled, the smell of the battlefield.","Only one person sat in the main hall. He was a man of imposing stature, broad-shouldered and long-legged. Sitting there with an authoritative air, he seemed to bring with him an oppressive, towering mountain range, the weight of years having settled upon him with a heavy, formidable dignity.","Now, hearing the noise, he looked over. His brown eyes were stern and cold, the few fine lines at the corners of his eyes seeming to transform into blades. His aura commanded awe without anger, chilling one to the core.","All doubt vanished from Deng Tuo's mind.","It truly was Qin Shaozong!","\"Exigent circumstances compel this abrupt visit. I hope Prefect Deng does not take offense,\" Qin Shaozong said, expressing hope that the host would not mind, yet he remained seated in the chair without the slightest intention of rising.","Deng Tuo bowed deeply, his hands clasped in a formal salutation. Your Lordship possesses such a heroic bearing and extraordinary presence; your reputation precedes you like a clap of thunder. Your visit truly brings honor to my humble abode. How could I possibly take offense? I only wonder what business brings Your Lordship here. If there is anything this humble subordinate can do to assist, I would go through fire and water without a second thought.","Qin Shaozong reached out a hand to steady him, though he did not change his explanation. In recent months, I took a concubine. She was very much to my liking, and I kept her by my side day and night out of great affection. Unexpectedly, she turned out to be a spy for another party. She seized some of my secrets and fled while I was off guard.","Deng Tuo was visibly shocked, yet a sense of inexplicable unease washed over him. My Lord, could it be that this woman is currently hiding within Taiping County?","Most likely, Qin Shaozong replied, though he did not state it as an absolute certainty.","Deng Tuo hurried to reassure him. Rest easy, My Lord. Taiping County is not large; finding one person will not be difficult. Please, My Lord, provide a detailed description of her. I will immediately dispatch men to apprehend her. Once she is cast into the dungeons and subjected to all eighteen forms of torture, I guarantee she will confess everything, whether she wants to or not.","Mo Yanyun felt his eyelid twitch as he listened.","Had this Governor Deng grown so old that he no longer understood the nuances of romance? His Lordship had first said the woman was \"very much to his liking\" and then mentioned his \"great affection,\" yet the Governor dared to suggest using eighteen forms of torture on her.","Qin Shaozong first detailed the information listed on the travel permit, then added, She is approximately seven chi and three cun tall, with a well-proportioned figure, peach-blossom eyes, and a cinnabar mole on her forehead. However, as she is alone and on the run, she will certainly use a disguise. You should look among women with dark complexions or those who appear ugly and unrefined.","As he reached the end, his tone grew a fraction heavier. Once she is caught, I will interrogate her personally. You need only assist in the search, Governor Deng. You need not trouble yourself with anything else.","Realizing belatedly that he had overstepped, Deng Tuo forced an awkward smile. Your Lordship is quite right. She is, after all, your person. How she is handled is entirely up to you.","Qin Shaozong stated, Night has fallen, and we require a place to rest. Let us first head to the county’s official inns.","An order from above is like a spreading fire; those below did not dare to be idle.","If one were to look down from the sky, observing the entire county from a high vantage point, they would see several columns of men departing from the Governor’s manor under the cover of the pitch-black night, snaking through the streets toward the various inns like long serpents.","The manager of one inn watched in terror as a group of soldiers strode through his doors. What... what is the meaning of this? This humble commoner dares to ask the brave warriors—is there something wrong with my shop?","The lead soldier barked, Do not panic. It is no great matter; we are merely looking for someone. Bring out your guest registry for the past two days.","Similar scenes played out across different inns, with largely the same results, until they reached one particular establishment.","Dai Li? Yes, yes, we have her! The woman arrived this afternoon. She is upstairs, in the very last room on the left, the manager said hurriedly.","Boss, let’s go inform the Great One immediately! a young soldier said, eager to claim credit.","The captain, however, was more cautious. He asked the manager, What does she look like? How tall is she?","The manager had a vivid impression of her. She is about seven chi and three cun tall, dark-skinned, and as ugly as Wu Yan. She also carries a rancid, sour stench.","The captain felt confident. Every detail matched. It had to be her! He immediately ordered his subordinates, Guard the front and back doors. No one is allowed in or out. I am going back to inform the Noble Guest.","In less than fifteen minutes, Qin Shaozong appeared at the inn’s entrance.","The inn was surrounded so tightly that not even a drop of water could leak through. The manager and the young servants were all huddled trembling in the corner of the counter, looking like chicks plucked from their nest.","Qin Shaozong already knew Dai Li was on the second floor. After entering the inn, he didn't spare a glance for anything else and went straight upstairs.","Soldiers stood guard on the second floor, and all guests were confined to their rooms. Qin Shaozong walked all the way to the room at the very end of the corridor and pushed the door open.","With a creak, the door swung wide.","Light spilled out from within, and along with the glow came an odor far more pungent than the smell of spoiled food.","The captain who had brought the news instinctively took a step back from the stench, but he saw the tall man in front of him standing as steady as a mountain. He couldn't help but feel a surge of secret admiration.","As expected of someone who had come from battlefields strewn with corpses—he could remain unfazed even in the face of such a foul reek.","A cold sneer suddenly rang out.","The captain shuddered, a chill climbing up from the soles of his feet. For a moment, it was as if he saw a furious tiger in the jungle snapping a thick branch with a single swipe of its claws.","No... hadn't they found the person?","Why was the Noble Guest still unhappy? Could it be that this wasn't...","Inside the room, a tall woman in her forties looked at the crowd outside in terror. Who are you?","She was dressed in a greyish-black robe, and her skin was dark and wrinkled, a clear sign that she hadn't seen many good days. The suffocating stench from before came from a pile of clothes in the corner, which looked as though they had just been taken off and hadn't been washed yet.","The travel permit—who gave it to you? Qin Shaozong stood at the doorway, refusing to step inside.","Seeing that the situation was dire, the woman didn't dare to be anything but cooperative. I found it! I picked it up off the ground!","Fearing they wouldn't believe her, she hastily added, I really did just find it, in the outskirts north of the city. I was walking along when I suddenly saw a bundle. The cloth on the outside was quite old, but I thought there was no harm in looking. I thought there might be something good inside. And there really was...","Inside the bundle was a set of clothes, a travel permit, and even some silver coins. It looked exactly as if someone had been careless and lost it.","She was a displaced person with no possessions and was nearly starving to death. There was no room for the virtue of returning lost property; she had to look out for her own stomach first. So, she had immediately taken the bundle and entered the city.","My Lord, could it be that Lady Dai lost her permit? Mo Yanyun asked in disbelief.","Qin Shaozong turned to leave. She had two permits in her possession. Even if she lost a bundle, she wouldn't lose only one of them. There is no need to search the inns in the county anymore. She is definitely not there.","Mo Yanyun hurried to keep up. Then where should we look?","Qin Shaozong said in a low voice, The pleasure districts, the fabric shops, and the residences of women associated with those shops. Anywhere women frequent must be searched thoroughly.","Mo Yanyun nodded.","It made sense. If Lady Dai was alone, and she wasn't staying at an inn, she would surely hide in places where women gathered, as those places were relatively safer.","Qin Shaozong added, Furthermore, post a notice in the county tomorrow. Publicize that a female thief has entered the city and warn every household not to harbor strangers. At the same time, station men at all four city gates. Inspect every woman who tries to leave the city with the utmost scrutiny.","Run? Hide?","He wanted to see exactly where she could run, and where she could possibly hide!","Once he caught this little fox by the tail and dragged her back, he would certainly show her exactly what happened to those who crossed him."]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24","paragraphs":["Daili woke up and overheard some gossip at Lin Erniang's doorway:","Last night, there was a major search through the guesthouses of the commandery, apparently because the commandery office was looking for a fugitive.","Street rumors were plentiful as always. Some claimed with certainty that the authorities were searching for a female fugitive, a woman with dark skin and an ugly face, frightening enough to make children cry.","As for her crime, it seemed she had stolen a precious family heirloom from a noble, hence the warrant.","Daili held a bowl of porridge but had lost her appetite, her heart sinking steadily.","It sounded very much like Qin Shaozong had come looking.","Regardless, it was best not to go out these days. Fortunately, Lin Erniang, planning to focus on seclusion in the coming days, had bought three days' worth of groceries yesterday, so there was no need to venture out today.","Daili stayed indoors at Lin Erniang's house for two days, playing with Lin Erniang's four-year-old child, Shangnu.","Lin Erniang lived in a commoners' district, a place somewhat like a later-era urban village. Almost every household had a single-courtyard home, and the houses were relatively close together. Standing by the Li family's courtyard wall, one could hear the conversations of the Wang family next door.","Daili had planned to stay in on the third day as well, but after finishing breakfast and taking a stroll in the courtyard, she suddenly heard voices from the other side of the wall:","\"When I went to the East Market today, I saw the east city gate is still heavily guarded from afar. It seems that female thief hasn't been caught yet. Who knows how long this search will go on?\"","\"It should end soon. Speaking of which, about an hour ago, I saw soldiers heading toward Hemin Street with household registers. They're probably going door-to-door for verification. Once they finish that area, it'll be our turn. Screening every household like this without missing a spot, how could they not catch that female thief?\"","\"Notices are posted in the city offering rewards for any information about the female thief...\"","Daili lowered her gaze, turned, and went back inside. She said to Lin Erniang, who was engrossed in her embroidery, \"Madam Lin, I'm going out to look for my elder brother. I'll be back by dusk at the latest, no need to prepare dinner for me.\"","Shangnu also wanted to go out; he wished to find his friend Tieshuan at the end of the street to fight crickets.","Daili gently nudged the child back inside. \"Be a good boy and stay home, Shangnu. If you stay home today, Auntie will bring you a flatbread when she returns.\"","Hearing there would be food, Shangnu nodded repeatedly.","Daili put on a veil hat and went out.","Yesterday, while chatting with Lin Erniang, she had already inquired about the general layout of this area.","The streets here crisscrossed, somewhat like a zigzag shape. Lin Erniang's house was at the easternmost end, while the Hemin Street mentioned by the neighbor was on the western side.","Daili walked into an eastern alley. Just as she was about to exit the alley mouth, she suddenly spotted a group of people ahead.","Among them was actually a familiar face.","It was that square-faced soldier captain; Daili remembered his name was Hu Bao.","So it was indeed Qin Shaozong who had come!","Daili's breath hitched. She immediately pulled back, turned without hesitation, and headed into another alley. Turning left and right, she narrowly avoided another group of people and finally left the commoners' residential area.","Although the city's thief hunt was causing quite a stir, daily life for the common people was largely unaffected. Shops operated as usual, and vendors still peddled their wares by the roadside.","The streets were bustling with people. Apart from the occasional patrols of soldiers passing through, everything else seemed normal.","Daili entered an upscale teahouse, paid for a small private room on the second floor by the window.","The young attendant left after setting down a tray of dried melon slices and closing the door.","Daili took off her veil hat, opened the window just a palm's width, and then began to brew tea.","Teahouses were places for conversation and gossip; one could hear all sorts of rumors here. If one had the money for a private room, sitting idly for an entire afternoon was perfectly acceptable.","People came and went on the street. Daili had intended to observe the frequency of soldier patrols, but instead, she saw... Qin Shaozong.","Daili's hand holding the teacup shook, spilling tea onto the table.","On the street.","Qin Shaozong and Mo Yanyun were strolling through the market.","\"My Lord, it seems the conflict between Yan Province and Qing Province is fierce, and this battle won't end quickly. Otherwise, river pirates wouldn't have ventured near Zhuya Ford,\" Mo Yanyun remarked with a sigh.","Qin Shaozong said, \"The friction between them had been long-standing; an open conflict was only a matter of time. This time, using the Green Lotus Sect as a pretext, it's just the right opportunity...\"","Suddenly, he stopped walking.","Mo Yanyun asked, puzzled, \"My Lord?\"","The imposing man in black robes stood at the crossroads, his gaze sweeping from east to west—the vendor smiling behind his stall as he collected payment, the group of children playing with mud by the alley entrance, the teahouse attendant welcoming guests inside...","Each scene entered his eyes, imprinted in his mind like frozen paintings.","The bustling market had many shops. Eateries and teahouses had their doors wide open, with people coming and going. Buildings with two stories were everywhere. Some private room windows were opened wide to let in sunlight, some were tightly shut as if unused, and others were only open a crack the width of a palm.","Everything seemed normal, utterly unremarkable.","\"My Lord?\" Receiving no response, Mo Yanyun called again, \"What is it? Is something amiss?\"","Qin Shaozong turned and beckoned to the commandery office guards following at a distance. \"Search this area. Focus on eateries and teahouses. Ask the attendants if there are any private rooms used by a single person, or by two or three people.\"","The guards acknowledged the order, scattered, and quickly headed toward different shops.","\"My Lord, you think she would come out onto the streets?\" Mo Yanyun was astonished, his first reaction being it was unlikely. \"The thief hunt is all the rage in the commandery now. Not only are the common folk discussing it fervently, but patrols have also increased severalfold. Lady Dai must know you are searching for her. How would she dare show her face?\"","Qin Shaozong gave a cold laugh. \"What wouldn't she dare? Beneath that fox's skin lies the heart of a bear and the courage of a leopard. There's nothing she wouldn't dare do.\"","Mo Yanyun knew his superior was still simmering with anger. Only by apprehending the culprit could those ever-rising flames be quelled.","...","A little over a quarter of an hour later.","A soldier hurried back. \"My Lord, a private room at the Jade Bamboo Teahouse matches the description. Furthermore, an attendant in the main hall said the guest who booked the room was a woman alone, wearing a veil hat when she entered, making her features hard to distinguish.\"","As he spoke, the soldier gestured a height. \"The attendant also said she was about this tall, roughly seven chi and three cun. The height matches.\"","Qin Shaozong abruptly looked toward the building to the side.","Jade Bamboo Teahouse.","Mo Yanyun quickly asked, \"Are the front and back doors of the teahouse covered?\"","The soldier nodded immediately. \"The lady's room is on the second floor. I've already stationed two men to guard each staircase. Unless she jumps out the window or grows wings, there's absolutely no way for her to leave.\"","Qin Shaozong strode into the Jade Bamboo Teahouse. The attendants and the manager all wanted to approach, but were stopped by the soldiers. \"Just have the attendant who served her come forward.\"","The teahouse had two staircases, their entrances located on either side of the main door like two massive arms encircling the building.","Qin Shaozong casually chose one to ascend, the tea attendant following behind him, speaking as they walked. \"That female guest arrived alone roughly half an hour ago and ordered the 'Blossoming Wealth and Honor' tea set. When this humble one entered the private room a second time with the tea set, her veil hat was still on. At the time, I merely thought her character shy and retiring. How could I have guessed she might be the female thief...\"","The entire city was searching for someone. In principle, a thief should lie low, so why would one brazenly stroll the streets?","\"Creak—\"","With a push of his hand, Qin Shaozong abruptly opened the unlocked door to the private room.","It was a small room, barely five paces from the door to the window. With no screen inside, everything was visible at a glance.","A window open just a palm's width, a tea cauldron boiling water, some scattered dried melon strips, a small incense burner in the corner, and a low table with a small puddle of moisture on its surface.","Everything was there, except for a person.","Mo Yanyun was dumbfounded. He immediately turned to ask the soldier who had earlier thumped his chest guaranteeing he'd guarded the staircase, \"Where is she?\"","\"She runs faster than a rabbit.\" Qin Shaozong clicked his tongue lightly.","\"I... I really had men guard the staircases immediately,\" the soldier stammered, his face flushing red. He had secured the staircases first, then rushed back to report his success, so he hadn't had time to verify the situation upstairs.","Mo Yanyun thought to himself that these soldiers from Taiping Commandery were all useless fools, unable to handle even this small task properly, letting the Marquis get his hopes up for nothing.","Qin Shaozong suddenly furrowed his long brows. \"There's a medicinal smell?\"","Mo Yanyun was taken aback, sniffing hard, but only caught the faint fragrance drifting from the incense burner.","\"She hasn't been gone long and surely can't have gone far. Keep searching,\" Qin Shaozong ordered.","...","The moment she saw Qin Shaozong, Dai Li knew things had gone wrong.","This feeling was hard to describe precisely, like a taut string in her mind humming and vibrating, making it impossible for her to stay seated.","Her previous successful attempts at deceiving him had all relied on Qin Shaozong's belief that she would inevitably cling to his lofty branch. Under that blind assumption, many things remained unclear to him, allowing her to slip past.","But times had changed. Dai Li dared not relax for even a moment, so she swiftly left through the teahouse's back door.","This area was all shops. Dai Li walked and hid, her main strategy being to move against the expected flow. Perhaps her demeanor was too leisurely, or perhaps, like the tea attendant, many people thought a female thief would be busy hiding, not swaggering down the street.","In any case, Dai Li traversed two streets unharmed.","She went to each of the four city gates in turn, seeing from a distance that the guards at each had doubled compared to the day before yesterday when she entered the city.","There was no leaving for now.","Dai Li sighed and turned back. She had been wandering outside for two hours, and now dusk was approaching. She figured the area around Lin Erniang's place had probably been searched by now.","Returning now might be just right.","It would be false to say she wasn't worried at all, but if she didn't go back to Lin Erniang's, where else could she go?","Her travel pass bore the name \"Dai Li,\" which couldn't be changed. Using that pass at an official hostel would be no different from turning herself in.","A faint sense of regret stirred within Dai Li. Had she known it would come to this, she shouldn't have disembarked at Taiping Commandery in the first place, and she resented the infrequent ferry schedule at Riyue Crossing.","After buying a flatbread from a street stall, Dai Li entered the alleyways. Bathed in the warm, lingering glow of the setting sun, she turned left and right, making her way back to Lin Erniang's home.","When she had left earlier, she had encountered two patrols in quick succession, nearly running right into them. Yet the return journey was strangely smooth all the way.","She didn't run into a single soldier.","That was a good thing.","\"Knock, knock.\" Dai Li rapped on the door.","The door opened quickly. Lin Erniang stood behind it and smiled. \"You're back!\"","Perhaps it was because of the veil hat, or because the orientation of the house kept the evening sun from falling on Lin Erniang, but Dai Li felt the woman before her seemed somewhat unfamiliar at this moment.","Dai Li nodded and entered the house, carrying the flatbread wrapped in straw paper. \"Where's Shangnu? I promised to buy him a flatbread before I left. It's still a bit warm; he should eat it while it is.\"","\"Tieshuan from next door came by earlier looking for Shangnu, insisting they go out to play together,\" Lin Erniang explained.","Dai Li paused, handed the flatbread to Lin Erniang, and only then removed her veil hat. \"Then he can eat it when he returns.\"","She had handed over the bread, but even after removing her hat, Dai Li didn't hear Lin Erniang's footsteps retreating. She looked up, meeting the other woman's eyes directly.","When they first met, Lin Erniang had been startled by the \"black flame birthmark\" on her face. Afterward, she had largely avoided looking directly at Dai Li, even when speaking, keeping her gaze on Dai Li's collar or letting it drift elsewhere.","This was the first time the other woman was staring at her so intently.","Feeling somewhat strange inside, Dai Li showed nothing on her face, merely returning the look with a smile. \"What is it?\"","\"It's nothing. I just wanted to ask if you'd like fish for dinner tonight? The fish in the water vat won't keep much longer,\" Lin Erniang hastily averted her eyes.","Dai Li was stunned. That sense of strangeness suddenly intensified. She had clearly told Lin Erniang before leaving not to prepare a meal for her tonight.","Why was she asking if she wanted fish for dinner...","Dai Li shifted her gaze to the courtyard. Her original intention was to look at the earthenware vat where the fish were kept, to see how they were \"not keeping well.\"","Yet, that casual glance felt like an ice-cold arrow shooting forth abruptly, piercing through her chest and pinning her rigidly in place.","Lin Erniang lived in the \"city village,\" and most who resided here were of modest means. Their homes were single-courtyard houses with plain tile roofs, only slightly better than thatched huts.","Being financially strained, money was naturally spent on essentials. Therefore, many households, including Lin Erniang's, had courtyards without paved bricks.","The ground was simply packed earth, which would become muddy and difficult after rain. If the weather stayed clear, it wasn't too unsightly.","But regardless, anyone walking on it would leave footprints, deep or shallow.","And now, a series of footprints appeared in the courtyard.","There were only two women and one young boy in the house. None of the three of them could have made such broad, long footprints, let alone the fact that these prints were chaotic and dense, impossible for a single person to leave.","Dai Li felt her muscles trembling and spasming, her skin becoming hypersensitive. A mere cool breeze brushing past made her heart pound with fright.","She whirled around and strode rapidly towards the outside without a word.","\"Creak—\"","She pulled open the two wooden leaves of the door. From the moment the crack appeared, the first thing revealed was a swath of black.","At this moment, the scene seemed to slow down immeasurably. A cool wind lifted the hem of the towering man's black robe outside the door, like a vicious tiger raising its sharp claws, or a warrior's prelude to drawing his blade.","The sky seemed to suddenly darken, then was torn asunder by a claw-like flash of white lightning. Dai Li's pupils trembled with the crash of thunder, the color draining completely from her face."]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25","paragraphs":["The sun dipped westward once more, its light dimming another shade.","Qin Shaozong stood outside the simple hut. The warm orange light of the setting sun slanted across, falling on his sharply defined face. His high-bridged nose served as a dividing line, casting one side in light and the other in shadow. Even his brown eyes seemed altered—one turned as dark as ink, while the other remained the tawny hue of a large feline's iris.","Daili instinctively stepped back. Yet, she had barely taken a single step when a powerful hand shot out, gripping her upper arm tightly.","\"Still thinking of running?\" Qin Shaozong looked at Daili's face, seeing it smeared with black, gray, and yellow pigments layered with a certain artistry, almost convincingly natural.","If one didn't look closely, she truly could have fooled anyone.","The fire in his heart flared up again, a surge of blood burning his very core with a dull ache.","Daili was by now too startled to speak, only shaking her head repeatedly. The iron-like arm encircling her pulled back, and she crashed into the solid wall of his chest.","This man always ran hot, but today he seemed even more so. Daili pressed a hand against his chest; the scorching heat penetrated his thin clothing, making her feel as if she were standing before a furnace.","Before Daili could even gather her words, he suddenly seized both her wrists. His large hand closed easily around them, binding them together in his grip. Then, producing a silk ribbon from somewhere, he wound it three times around her wrists and tied it tight.","\"Qin Shaozong, let me explain!\" Daili cried out in desperation.","Qin Shaozong gave a cold snort, offering no reply. After securing her hands, he swept her up by the waist, turned, and strode purposefully toward the mouth of the alley.","Mo Yanyun and the others quickly followed. Hearing that \"Qin Shaozong,\" their temples throbbed in unison.","Good heavens, after a few days apart, Lady Dai's ability to provoke had not diminished in the slightest. Calling the Marquis by his full name like that—she truly wasn't afraid of making him even angrier.","Lin Erniang's home was at the easternmost edge of this \"urban village,\" quite close to the alley entrance. Qin Shaozong was tall and his strides were long and fast. In what seemed like the blink of an eye, he had already emerged from the alley with Daili in his arms.","A carriage, its origins unknown, stood waiting there. The door to the rear compartment was wide open. Hu Bao sat on the driver's seat. As soon as Qin Shaozong boarded, he flicked the reins. The horses, stung, began to trot.","...","Inside the carriage.","Qin Shaozong shoved Daili into the corner of a cushioned seat and did not retreat. Instead, he pressed closer, his knee thrusting between her legs, one hand braced against the tightly shut window frame. Using the carriage wall behind him and his own formidable physique, he effectively trapped her in the small corner.","\"You said you wanted to explain. Then speak properly. Why all the lies before? What was your aim?\" His brown eyes were heavy, smoldering, almost spitting fire.","Yet, at this moment, Daili's fear was somewhat less than when she had first seen him standing outside the door.","Because she realized he didn't seem intent on killing her—at least not right now. Otherwise, the blade at his waist would have already tasted blood the moment he saw her at the hut's entrance.","Since that was the case...","Daili's eyelashes fluttered violently. She pressed her lips together and remained silent.","Qin Shaozong reached out, gripping her chin and tilting it up slightly. \"Speak! Silent when you should talk, full of lies when you shouldn't. Do you not want that mouth anymore?\"","\"There's no explanation. I was lying to you just now.\" Daili's voice was very low.","Qin Shaozong almost thought he had misheard. His anger, having reached its peak, cooled into a deadly calm. \"You were still thinking of lying just now?\"","Daili's gaze drifted lightly, cautiously, to his face, touching it briefly before skittering away. She didn't speak, but her eyes clearly carried a hint of \"You're unhappy when I tell the truth.\"","A vein throbbed on Qin Shaozong's forehead.","Fine. She was certainly something else!","And just then, the carriage stopped.","Qin Shaozong withdrew his hand, his rough palm now smeared with black and gray pigment. He paid it no mind, dug the woman out of the corner, clamped her against his chest, and carried her out of the carriage.","As her view expanded from the confined space, Daili realized with a start that the carriage had stopped before a hostel.","The hostel's facade was clean, with an elegant plaque hanging high. Vines crept beside the windows of the second-floor rooms, their intertwined stems dotted with delicate little flowers, adding a touch of bright color.","Based on Daili's street-wandering experience today, this place could be considered the equivalent of the Bright Moon Inn in Nankang Commandery. At this moment, two sturdy soldiers stood guard at the entrance. Looking inside from the doorway, the manager and servants were nowhere to be seen, as if the place had been cleared.","But Daili had no mind for any of that now.","Dusk had ended. The last vestiges of daylight had been swallowed by darkness, leaving a heavy night sky that seemed ready to collapse at any moment. Lanterns hung in the hostel's main hall and corridors, their fiery glow stretching inward like a path. The night and the lamplight mingled, blending into shadows that were startlingly intense.","Daili twisted her bound hands slightly, her heart filled with anxiety. Her earlier small test had confirmed her life was temporarily safe, but something else felt perilously precarious...","\"I'm sorry. I shouldn't have deceived you before.\"","Thud.","Qin Shaozong pushed the door open with his foot.","The two sounds collided—the former muffled and almost inaudible.","Qin Shaozong's gaze slanted downward, his face expressionless, his imposing aura heavy, still the very picture of an impending storm.","Daili had been watching him. Seeing this, she hurriedly added, \"I was wrong. I shouldn't have lied to you. You are magnanimous, a true pillar of heaven and earth, a great man. Could you please not hold it against a mere woman like me?\"","\"You certainly know how to bend with the wind,\" Qin Shaozong mocked. He set her down on a cushioned chair by a low table and untied the ribbon from her wrists. \"Wash your face.\"","The black, gray, yellow, and the patch of white revealed where he had smudged the pigments earlier—all mixed on her palm-sized face—was an eyesore.","Several pottery basins were placed on the table, with a silk cloth laid beside them. Clearly, this step had been anticipated.","Daili raised her hands. Her wide sleeves slipped down slightly, revealing the bandage wrapped around her left hand.","Qin Shaozong's gaze fell upon it. He had noticed the scent of medicine in the tea room earlier and the bandage when apprehending her. But considering past precedent, he thought it likely Lin Erniang had been deceived once again, eight or nine times out of ten.","Daili unwound the bandage from her hand layer by layer, finally revealing a perfectly smooth, uninjured left hand.","The corner of Qin Shaozong's mouth twitched almost imperceptibly.","Daili began washing her face. The water in the basin immediately turned murky as the silk cloth soaked. As she cleansed her face, Qin Shaozong sat opposite, watching her unblinkingly.","It had to be said, the scene held a certain aesthetic.","The black paste was gradually wiped away, the charcoal powder washed off by the water, the lead-based cosmetics cleansed, revealing luminous, fair skin and a vivid vermilion beauty mark. The gentle lamplight brushed her face. The faintly gathered brows and eyes held a landscape of striking beauty, like the interplay of light and shadow in an oil painting, captivating and soul-stirring.","Daili did not wash quickly, and throughout, the gaze from opposite her never wavered.","It was intensely invasive, like flames wrapped in pine resin, or like a gleaming blade reflecting cold light.","Daili showed nothing on her face, but her heart grew increasingly frantic.","She realized that, having come this far, she truly couldn't think of any reason to delay him, let alone escape.","It took four basins of water, turning clear into murky, before Daili managed to wash her face clean. Setting down the silk handkerchief, she straightened her stiff spine and said softly, \"My lord, there's an old saying: 'Don't contend with petty people, don't get entangled in trivial matters.' You hold a high position, your time is as precious as gold...\"","\"Hand over the tally.\" Qin Shaozong interrupted her coldly.","Daili paused, then obediently took the small bamboo tally from her sleeve and placed it on the low table, pushing it toward him.","Qin Shaozong picked up the small bamboo tally. On it was written \"Daili\"—the one she had originally tricked out of Madam Yun's hands.","It was also the last one.","Snap. The small bamboo tally broke in the man's hand, one becoming two, two becoming many more.","Daili's eyelids twitched slightly.","Qin Shaozong opened his hand, and bamboo fragments of various sizes clattered down from his palm. \"Next, I'll ask, you answer. If you utter even half a lie, after I finish my business tonight, I guarantee you will be broken into exactly as many pieces as this tally split into. Not a single piece less.\"","Daili: \"...\"","Though not entirely convinced, she knew the proper attitude was required. Daili promptly composed herself. \"Please ask, my lord.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"Was someone behind you, instructing you?\"","This question was easy to answer. Daili shook her head immediately. \"No. If there were, why would I have had no one to receive me?\"","Qin Shaozong gave an \"Mm\" of acknowledgment, seemingly neither surprised nor suspicious. \"Qin Yi, Qin Huali. Does this person exist?\"","Daili: \"...He does not exist.\"","Qin Shaozong continued, \"So from the very beginning, you were not from Jiaozhou, nor did you wander north from the south. The so-called five former husbands and the old residence in the west of the city were all your fabrications, is that not so?\"","Daili lowered her eyes submissively. \"Yes.\"","Although he had long anticipated that her lies might be rotten to the core, hearing her admit it with her own mouth still caused Qin Shaozong's anger to churn.","He would settle accounts with her later; there would be plenty of time for her to suffer. Qin Shaozong suppressed the fire in his heart. \"Where is your ancestral home?\"","Daili: \"Qiantang.\"","Qin Shaozong tapped his long fingers lightly on the low table twice.","This matched what the carriage driver had said. Ancestral home Qiantang, she wanted to go to Qiantang—it seemed she wanted to return to her native place. He pressed on, \"Why did you appear in the Jiang residence? What was your intention?\"","This time, Daili fell silent, her delicate brows knitted in prolonged contemplation, so long that Qin Shaozong curled his knuckles and rapped heavily on the low table as a warning.","\"Speak.\"","Daili spoke softly, her tone helpless: \"If I tell the truth, you will only find it utterly absurd and certainly won't believe it. Yet if I weave another lie to deceive you, you will hold me accountable. Neither choice seems right. I am truly caught between a rock and a hard place.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"Just tell the truth.\"","Daili pondered for a long moment, carefully choosing her words. \"Let me tell you a story. There is a place called the Peach Blossom Spring. It is cut off from the world. Everyone can read, every household has surplus grain, and the elderly and children alike are content and happy. A woman lived there with her young son, but one day, the child suddenly vanished. The woman searched as she traveled, and unexpectedly fell into a river. When she awoke again, she had arrived at a completely new place. The master of that place... was surnamed Jiang.\"","Qin Shaozong stared fixedly at the person before him, not missing the slightest change in her expression.","Daili knew he didn't believe her. Changing someone's beliefs was extremely difficult. Just as it was nearly impossible to make a devout Christian, convinced of entering heaven and being with God after death, renounce their faith with a few words.","Similarly, it was equally impossible to make an atheist believe in a paradise existing separately from the world, or that someone could simply fall into a river and appear elsewhere.","\"You initially knew I was in the side room because you heard the sound of water, right? It was because my shoes were wet that I was exposed.\" Daili left it at that.","Whether he believed it or not, she had told the truth.","In reality, given the current situation, it seemed she couldn't extricate herself for now. If she fabricated another story now, it would be easily exposed and would further enrage this already furious tiger.","She was different from a young girl just come of age. She no longer felt much shyness about sex, nor would she make a life-or-death fuss over such matters.","Now there were only two choices left: be bitten by the dog once, or be bitten by the dog once and then have him help her find her son.","Since arriving here, she had never again had those bizarre, fantastical dreams. Zhou Zhou must be here. She had to survive, survive to find Zhou Zhou!","Silence spread through the room. No one spoke.","The candle flame, teased by the night wind slipping through the window, flickered slightly, causing the boundary between light and shadow to sway. A small moth fluttered its wings and crashed into the wick. With a soft sizzle, only a speck of ash remained by the lamp.","Watching that falling speck of ash, Daili's heartbeat uncontrollably quickened.","She had said all there was to say. If he still didn't believe her, if he thought she was weaving lies to deceive him again, and pressed her for the \"truth\"...","Daili suddenly felt a headache coming on.","Suddenly, the lamplight on the low table swayed violently, and the shadow cast on the floor from the side rose and lengthened like a mountain.","Qin Shaozong had risen from his seat.","Regarding Daili's earlier account, he offered no comment, leaving it unclear whether he believed it or not. The man walked around the low table, reached out a long arm, scooped the woman from the soft chair into his embrace, and carried her toward the bed.","Daili's hands rested on his shoulders, unconsciously crumpling the fabric over his shoulder blades.","She knew what he intended to do.","When placed on the bed, Daili did not shrink back nor avoid his intensely predatory gaze. Matters having come to this, she decided to negotiate terms with him. \"My lord, I must find my son.\"","Fearing he wouldn't take it seriously, as he leaned closer, Daili raised a hand to press against his chest, looked directly into his eyes, and repeated, \"You must help me find my son. You must find him!\"","The fire within Qin Shaozong was burning fiercely. It hadn't diminished since the day she fled, and as the days of searching passed, the already impure anger had increasingly transformed into something else.","He watched her lips part. This mouth was truly beautiful—naturally red lips, a rich color like the vibrant crimson at the heart of a red peony, full lip peaks, with corners slightly upturned. It was just that the words it spoke were never pleasant.","Qin Shaozong raised his hand, reached around Daili's neck, and placed his large palm on the back of her neck. Like a tiger seizing its prey, his long fingers spread, holding the woman before him in an absolute posture of control.","Daili was thoroughly startled by this move.","She had previously thought he wouldn't kill her. Could those two slightly commanding sentences have angered him?","Her breath hitched. The large palm on her nape was scorching and rough, like a red-hot iron clamp holding her, making it impossible for Daili to turn her head or move. However, she quickly realized she had misjudged; this man currently had no intention of snapping her neck.","The man leaned in, and the distance between them vanished in an instant. The hand Dai Li had initially pressed against his chest ended up with its back pressed against herself.","Even with some mental preparation, when this moment arrived, a shiver still ran down Dai Li's spine.","He was too fierce, his kiss too savage, conquering and plundering as he pleased. It was as if he had brought a raging, scorching wildfire, or was dragging her down into a boiling sea.","The transition from shallow to deep preliminaries was fleeting. The rising, searing heat engulfed her. The innermost nerve was teased and toyed with relentlessly. Dai Li trembled with a muffled sob. The hand pressed against his chest slowly curled into a fist, clutching and crumpling the man's robe until the entire front was a mess of wrinkles.","Qin Shao Zong originally had one arm wrapped around her waist and the other gripping the nape of her neck. As the kiss deepened, the hand at her waist loosened, then moved to untie the sash at her waist. His large, dark hand slipped inside like a swimming fish.","Dai Li trembled even more violently, but her tongue was held captive, sucked and entangled with such force that she couldn't even turn her head away, let alone do anything else.","The grey-black sash came loose, the robe fell open, vaguely revealing the porcelain-like fairness within.","However, right at that moment...","\"Knock, knock!\" Someone was at the door.","The force was heavy, clearly from a military man's hand, and the knocker's mood seemed quite urgent.","Qin Shao Zong paused but ignored it.","The person outside, hearing no movement from within, knocked heavily again.","\"My Lord, scouts report that Li Zan's troops are approaching. They come with great force, estimated at over a thousand. We must retreat immediately.\" It was Mo Yan Yun's voice.","Qin Shao Zong's breathing was rough. The veins on the side of his neck bulged, throbbed, and subsided, repeating this several times.","Dai Li also heard the words from outside the door. She was momentarily stunned, not expecting such a sudden turn of events. Feeling Qin Shao Zong clearly release her, she turned on her side, burying her face in the quilt.","Qin Shao Zong panted heavily. He had intended to get up—leaving Taiping County was now imperative, an arrow already on the bowstring. But seeing Dai Li's little action, he halted his movement, reached out, and nudged her slightly outward.","Dai Li, caught off guard, inadvertently exposed half her face.","Thus, completely unobstructed, Qin Shao Zong saw the corner of her mouth curled upward.","Here he was, pent up and burning with frustration, while she was over there secretly delighted.","It had been a long time since Qin Shao Zong had felt such uncontrollable rage. Ever since the Qin family made him clan leader, ever since he beat the northern jackals into submission until they were as docile as puppies, if not everything went exactly as he wished, at least major matters proceeded smoothly, and he hadn't suffered any significant setbacks.","—Until now!","Dai Li was startled, her heart sinking. This was bad, trouble was coming. \"My Lord, I wasn't...\"","Before she could finish, she was flipped over, her waist gripped and lifted, until she was lying face down across his lap.","Immediately after, \"Smack—\"","Not heavy, but loud enough.","Dai Li's pupils constricted sharply. The smile that hadn't completely faded from her face froze solid.","Shock, disbelief, shame, anger, chagrin.","Each of these unmistakable emotions flashed across Dai Li's face one by one.","Watching her rapidly changing expressions, the stifling anger in Qin Shao Zong's chest inexplicably dissipated quite a bit. Not only did his hand not move away, it spread open and gripped the soft, rounded flesh, giving it a fierce squeeze. \"We will set off to leave Taiping County shortly. Behave yourself on the journey. Tuck away all that craftiness brewing in your belly. Otherwise, when we get back, I'll make sure both sides bloom red.\"","\"Creak.\" The door opened, and the two inside emerged one after the other.","Mo Yan Yun heaved a huge sigh of relief.","Good thing the Lord came out, otherwise he really would have had to commit the great disrespect of barging in.","\"My Lord, everything is ready. We can depart at any time.\" Mo Yan Yun's gaze drifted around, looking here and there, his mind buzzing with questions.","The Lord's condition clearly indicated he hadn't gotten what he wanted, yet strangely, he seemed to be in a rather decent mood. In contrast, Madame Dai behind him wore a cold expression, looking very displeased.","In the short time inside—less than half an hour—their moods seemed to have completely swapped.","What on earth had happened in that room?","Regardless, Madame Dai's skills were truly impressive. To extinguish such a raging, sky-threatening wildfire so abruptly and retreat completely unscathed.","\"Keep up.\"","The two heavy words thrown from ahead snapped Mo Yan Yun out of his thoughts.","On his very first day in Taiping County, Qin Shao Zong had demanded several dozen good horses from Prefect Deng Tuo, one for each soldier, assembling a cavalry unit.","Now, for the retreat, Qin Shao Zong decided to head south first. They would exit through Taiping County's south gate, then turn west, taking a detour back to Nankang County.","Dai Li didn't know what scheme this man was plotting. She only knew she was helped onto a horse, and then Qin Shao Zong swung up behind her.","The whip rose and fell, the steed neighed and reared before galloping off swiftly, carrying them away. Under the cover of night, the troop moved quickly south and soon exited the southern city gate.","Not long after their departure, another large force entered the city from the east. They rushed straight to Deng Tuo's prefectural office and dragged him out.","After intense questioning, learning that Qin Shao Zong had taken many horses, the leader, Feng Liang, said furiously, \"How could you give him horses?\"","Deng Tuo, his white beard trembling, dared not speak, his heart filled with bitterness, lamenting his ill fortune.","When Qin Shao Zong asked for horses, how could he refuse? How dared he refuse? He was just a minor prefect waiting to retire; how could he oppose a major warlord?","\"Commander, they went south,\" a soldier reported.","Feng Liang frowned, puzzled. \"South? Why would they go south? Exiting west would get them back to Nankang County faster. Why would Qin Shao Zong take the longer route?\"","Before he could figure it out, another soldier said, \"Commander, the city guards say they left less than half an hour ago.\"","Feng Liang's eyes immediately gleamed with ferocity. \"Never mind why. Pursue them directly! They came by boat. What good horses could a small place like Taiping County have? They can't have gotten far.\"","Dai Li had thought she'd have to spend at least the whole night on horseback. Surprisingly, only an hour after leaving the city, Qin Shao Zong reined in his horse.","\"Dismount.\"","At his command, all the soldiers swiftly dismounted.","The sturdy chest that had been pressed against Dai Li's back vanished. Sitting on the horse, she gripped the front pommel tightly, looking down and wondering how to get off.","Although he had put her up here, after what happened in the room earlier, she really didn't want to speak to him first.","Qin Shao Zong somehow produced several silk ribbons from somewhere. Standing beside the horse, he first lifted the hem of Dai Li's skirt, then tucked the legs of her trousers into her socks. Using the ribbons, he deftly tied the tops of her socks securely.","After both her legs were bound with the ribbons, he lifted her down from the horse. \"What are you staring at with those big eyes? If you don't want to be drained dry by mountain bugs, lift your arms.\""]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26","paragraphs":["Dai Li was no stranger to mountain climbing, but climbing a wild mountain in the dead of night was a first for her.","There were no steps, no signs, no proper climbing gear, and certainly no cable cars.","Everything was terrifyingly primitive.","Their small party, holding sparse torches, snaked a faint line of orange-red light. The firelight fell at their feet, illuminating dead leaves, vines, and some nocturnal insects.","Mo Yanyun walked ahead of Dai Li, with Qin Shaozong behind her. Several times, Dai Li's foot failed to find solid ground, and she slid down with a rustle, only to be caught squarely by Qin Shaozong, who steadied her by the waist before setting her back on her feet.","Halfway up the mountain path, Dai Li was genuinely tired. She was about to ask Mo Yanyun ahead how much longer it would take when a voice came from the front: \"Lord Marquis, the marked point is here.\"","Dai Li couldn't fathom what they were up to, until she saw a cave.","The cave was about half a person's height, resembling the den of a wolf or some other carnivore. Vines hung straight down over the entrance. Unless one knew it was there beforehand, it would be nearly invisible even in daylight, let alone by torchlight.","\"Keep only one torch inside the cave. Extinguish all the others,\" Qin Shaozong ordered.","With a few swift whooshes, the slender fire dragon writhed among the trees and was swallowed by the night. As the dragon vanished, only a nearly imperceptible sliver of light remained before them. Dai Li's face paled slightly.","Climbing a wild mountain at night, and he dared to extinguish the torches.","This era was not like later times, where human footprints covered the land and most beasts were confined to zoos. Here... they roamed the mountains freely, searching for food.","Remembering how bears fed, a wave of palpitations washed over Dai Li.","\"Madam, stay still for now,\" the man behind her said.","Dai Li didn't move, not entirely because she was obeying him, but partly because her own imagination had frightened her.","There was a steep slope in front of the cave. Qin Shaozong took a long stride, found a foothold, and easily ascended one level. He turned and looked down at Dai Li. \"Your hand.\"","Dai Li was a beat slow in offering her hand to him.","His rough, large palm enveloped hers. In the cool spring night, he was excessively warm, as if he had hidden the vanished fire dragon within his grasp.","In just a dazed moment, Dai Li found herself effortlessly atop the steep slope.","Mo Yanyun pushed aside the vines covering the cave entrance, allowing Qin Shaozong and Dai Li to enter. As the heavy curtain of vegetation lifted and fell, firelight spilled out, only to vanish again instantly.","Once inside the cave, Dai Li realized it was shaped like a sideways funnel, much larger than she had imagined. However, judging by the not-too-strong odor inside and the dense covering of grass and leaves on the ground, this cave had been abandoned for quite some time.","\"Stay here. Don't run off. I'll return shortly,\" Qin Shaozong said, pressing a dagger into Dai Li's hands.","Dai Li looked down at the dagger in her hand and murmured, \"I don't know the way. Where could I possibly run to?\"","Qin Shaozong laughed in exasperation.","Just listen to what she was saying. She wouldn't run because she didn't know the way. If she did know the way, that would be a different story entirely.","But now was not the time to dwell on it. He would settle this score with her later, along with the previous ones.","Qin Shaozong left one of his personal guards behind and departed with the others.","Dai Li didn't know what he intended to do. He said he would return shortly, so she could only wait. She found a corner, sat down with her back against the wall, hugged her knees, and placed the dagger beside her.","The sole remaining torch was placed in an L-shaped nook. From here, the cave entrance was out of sight, further weakening the firelight.","As for the personal guard left behind, he sat behind the thick curtain of vines at the cave entrance, his eyes keenly observing the outside through tiny gaps.","Having settled Dai Li on the mountainside, Qin Shaozong led the rest of his men upward at an accelerated pace.","Choosing to climb this mountain was not because they were fleeing helter-skelter from Li Zan's pursuing troops. Rather, a bandit stronghold was located a little further up and to the side.","A band of brigands had recently arrived at Zhuya Ford. These bandits, forced northward, had not been here long and likely weren't yet intimately familiar with the surrounding terrain. They probably hadn't even fully established their lair.","Such bandits were the easiest to eradicate.","After wiping out the mountain stronghold and crossing over this mountain, they would be able to see the Qi River. The bandits on the mountain had robbed a lou-chuan (towered ship) some days ago; it was reasonable to assume they had kept at least one for themselves.","Then, they could advance, using the terrain to ambush Li Zan's pursuing troops, or retreat, escaping on the lou-chuan.","As for Li Zan's pursuers, Qin Shaozong wasn't worried they would cling to them like hyenas catching the scent of blood.","Recently, fearful of the bandits' brutality, the common folk had unanimously avoided this area, with very few entering or exiting through the southern city gate. The roads branching south from Taiping County were numerous. He had ordered his soldiers to ride horses along them daily during daylight, ensuring fresh hoofprints marked every path.","Just figuring out which route he had taken would be a headache for the pursuers, let alone on a dark and windy night like this, when light was at its dimmest.","After scaling an extremely treacherous section, the soldiers formed a horizontal line. Upon hearing Qin Shaozong's bird-call whistle, they all scrambled upward like lightning.","...","\"Big Brother, did you hear something strange just now?\" Li Wu opened his eyes, looking around.","Li Si lazily yawned. \"What strange noise could there be in the middle of the night? Probably just some animal up the mountain getting hungry and having a midnight snack. Relax, the boss already checked. This mountain has no tigers or blind bears. Wolves seem rare too. The sound you heard was probably just a little wildcat. What's there to panic about?\"","Li Wu muttered, \"Is that so? But I can't shake this uneasy feeling. It's exactly like that time we nearly lost our lives at Misty Cliff.\"","Li Si was utterly unconcerned. Governor Deng of Taiping County was a pushover, and they had been living quite comfortably these past few days, hardly even bothering with night watches. \"Little Brother, instead of worrying about this and that, you'd be better off thinking about how to snatch a few pretty women. This fort is sorely lacking in women, it's just not...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, a spray of blood suddenly blossomed from Li Si's throat. Looking closely, an arrow had pierced straight through his windpipe.","Li Si's eyes instantly widened like bells, the whites filling with blood. Without uttering a sound, he toppled straight backward.","\"Big Brother!\" Li Wu was both shocked and furious.","He was about to grab the bronze whistle at his waist when, from the corner of his eye, he saw a flash of cold light flying toward him. Alarm bells screamed in Li Wu's mind. Forgetting the whistle, he hurriedly raised his blade to block.","Clang!","The first clash of weapons rang out clear and sharp.","But soon, as both sides exerted force in their deadly contest, an ear-piercing screech sounded. It was the mournful cry of Li Wu's aged, worn-out blade.","His opponent's blade was clearly superior.","Knowing escape was impossible, Li Wu glanced at his fallen, motionless brother. A ruthless glint flashed in his eyes. Abruptly, he stopped gripping his sword with both hands and instead freed one to grab the bronze whistle at his waist.","Just as the blade sank into his flesh, an earsplitting shriek erupted from the bronze whistle.","Qin Shaozong heard the whistle and said impatiently, \"Can't even handle a trivial matter like this. Was all the good meat and wine I fed you just thrown down the drain? You're going back to extra training. Move faster; Li Zan's lot will be following the sound soon.\"","Inside the fortress.","Meng Dahong, who was sleeping soundly, was jolted awake by his subordinates.","\"Chief, someone is attacking the fortress!\"","Meng Dahong gave a start, his sleepiness instantly replaced by a surge of rage. \"I just sent Deng Tuo a heavy gift two days ago, and today he sends people to raid my nest? That damn Deng Tuo!\"","\"Chief, those people are agile and exceptionally fierce. They don't look like those useless soldiers from Taiping County. Our brothers' gear isn't nearly as good as theirs; we won't last long before suffering heavy casualties. This is no place to linger. Please consider a retreat, Chief,\" his subordinate urged.","Meng Dahong could not hide his shock. \"Has the situation truly become this dire? Then we retreat. As long as the green hills remain, we need not worry about a lack of firewood! We'll retreat through the back mountain and take the boats.\"","Under the night sky, two riders rode side by side along the mountain path.","\"This Qin Shaozong is truly cunning. He left hoofprints on every path, and now we don't even know where to begin the search.\" The rider holding the torch controlled his horse's speed, careful not to let the wind blow out the flame.","The light could not be too dim, or it would be difficult to see certain tracks on the mountain path. This slowed them down, which was incredibly frustrating.","Suddenly, one of them reined in his horse. \"Did you hear something? It sounded like a copper whistle.\"","The other rider remembered something. \"Bandits often use whistles as signals, but they don't usually blow them unless there's a special circumstance. Could it be that Qin Shaozong entered the mountains and ran into bandits?\"","\"Then it's highly likely we're on the right path. Quick, let's check up ahead.\"","\"...A discovery! So many horses. They actually abandoned their horses to enter the mountains here. We finally found them! Go back and report to the Commander immediately!\"","Qin Shaozong flicked his ring-pommel saber, sending a thick arc of blood splattering onto the ground.","Mo Yanyun reported, \"My Lord, it has all been cleaned up. A total of seventy-three bandits were killed. There are five treasure chests in the fortress, all filled with gold and silver ornaments.\"","Qin Shaozong's gaze remained fixed ahead.","Before them were mountains and a lake. Indeed, it was a lake. The Qishui River made a turn here, forming a square-shaped body of water.","Surrounded by mountain peaks on both sides with a wide waterway in the middle, this place was a perfect natural port.","At this moment, blood meandered into small red streams in front of the port, and corpses lay scattered haphazardly across the ground. One man had fallen with his arm stretched forward, his eyes wide as he stared ahead.","He had been just a step away—just a step away from boarding the galley in front of him.","\"Beep—Beep—\"","Two long whistle blasts suddenly echoed from the mountain.","Qin Shaozong's face darkened. He knew Li Zan's men had found this place and were beginning to ascend the mountain.","\"My Lord, I will go and bring Madam Dai up,\" Mo Yanyun volunteered.","Qin Shaozong sheathed his ring-pommel saber and turned to walk away without looking back. \"I'll go get her. You take four men and stay here to handle the retreat.\"","It wasn't until that tall figure disappeared into the darkness that Mo Yanyun finally exhaled slowly, feeling the invisible pressure that had been surrounding him gradually dissipate.","It seemed the Lord was still fuming. Better to let him go and take his anger out on Li Zan's soldiers.","Dai Li had not dared to sleep. From the moment they entered the mountains, her nerves had been as taut as a bowstring; any rustle in the wind could make them vibrate with fragile tension.","When she heard the copper whistle, it was no exaggeration to say that Dai Li felt it was the herald of death.","Who would use a copper whistle as a signal during a sneak attack?","They must have been discovered by the bandits.","Perhaps the fearful cries in her heart were so loud they felt tangible, for the guard standing at the cave entrance turned around. \"Madam Dai, those petty bandits are nothing to fear.\"","Dai Li pursed her lips and said nothing.","The guard said helplessly, \"Years ago, the bandits in the Bore Mountain and Tianze Mountain range were a true plague. It was the Lord himself who led the troops to suppress them. He was invincible, and he built several trophy mounds of enemy corpses. For ten years after that, those two regions never saw banditry again. The bandits in this little ravine aren't even a tenth of what those were. Why should you worry?\"","Dai Li knew nothing of Qin Shaozong's past military achievements. Seeing the guard so confident and full of pride, she couldn't help but feel a flicker of relief, though she remained skeptical.","She hoped it was true.","If his side was wiped out, or if they suffered such a heavy blow that they had to cut their losses to survive, she would be left in the mountains with only one guard, likely ending up as food for wild beasts.","The faint sound of fighting drifted over, but it soon returned to silence. She didn't know if the battle had ended or if the distance had increased so much that the sound could no longer reach them.","Time passed slowly until she heard another sound—","The sound of hooves.","A single horse makes a limited sound, but hundreds or even thousands of horses could produce a rumbling roar, as if the earth itself were moaning.","The guard's gaze sharpened, and he quickly slipped out of the cave to investigate.","Perhaps because the night path was difficult to traverse, or perhaps because they were so numerous they had no fear, Li Zan's men had brazenly lit torches. A monstrous fire dragon coiled at the foot of the mountain, waving its four claws as if searching for the perfect angle to strike.","After two long whistle blasts sounded outside, the guard returned and said solemnly, \"Madam Dai, the pursuers have caught up. Someone will be here to meet us shortly. Please be sure to stay close to me.\"","Dai Li nodded heavily, her face pale. she took the torch from the corner and pressed it against the wall.","With a sizzle, the torch went out, and the cave was instantly plunged into darkness.","As the minutes ticked by, Dai Li moved to the cave entrance and watched nervously. She saw the fire dragon on the ground rise, the fiery light spreading upward, and she heard the distant voices becoming clearer.","They were searching the mountain with great fanfare, closing in step by step, yet the person the guard mentioned had not yet arrived.","The hanging vines were suddenly pushed aside, and a tall, dark shadow appeared at the cave entrance. Like an immovable mountain, he loomed over the entrance, which was over half a man's height.","Dai Li's heart nearly jumped out of her chest. In her daze, she thought she saw a pair of eerie green wolf eyes.","Her icy hand was grasped. The palm, which felt scalding to her, made Dai Li realize that it wasn't a giant wolf looking for prey—it was Qin Shaozong who had returned.","Dai Li heard him let out a soft chuckle.","\"You're usually bold enough to pierce the heavens, doing all sorts of mischief while hiding under a rabbit's skin, but now you've frozen into a block of ice.\" Qin Shaozong gave a slight tug and pulled her out of the cave.","Dai Li opened her mouth, but the lingering fear was still stuck in her throat, preventing her from speaking a single word.","\"Hu Bao, escort the Madam up the mountain,\" Qin Shaozong designated a man.","Hu Bao took the order. \"Madam Dai, please follow me.\"","Dai Li followed him for a few paces before coming to a halt. Glancing sideways, she saw the guard who had been in the cave with her trailing behind. Qin Shaozong remained at the cave’s mouth; he had turned around and was now facing the serpentine trail of torches winding up the mountain like a dragon of fire.","Dai Li lowered her eyes and followed Hu Bao in silence.","\"Move faster! Don't let Qin Shaozong escape. The Grand Marshal has declared that whoever takes Qin Shaozong’s head will not only be promoted directly to Governor, but will also be rewarded with ten grand estates, hundreds of servants, and a thousand taels of gold!\"","\"Those two whistles just now came from the northeast. Someone is definitely there. Hurry, move in that direction!\"","\"The city guards said Qin Shaozong took a female companion with him when he left the city. As long as he refuses to abandon that woman, she will be a burden on this mountain climb. He won't be able to run far.\"","The fire dragon stretched out in a long, horizontal line, acting like a massive, jagged-toothed sieve slowly filtering through the entire mountain.","Whoosh!","A cold arrow streaked through the air from above, riding the wind to strike a torch-bearing soldier with pinpoint accuracy. The force behind the shot was so immense that the long arrow did more than just pierce its target; it pinned him to the tree trunk behind.","The fletching of the arrow hummed with a vibrating ring, striking terror into the hearts of the searching soldiers.","\"He’s over there!\" someone was the first to shout.","\"Is it Qin Shaozong?\"","\"Who else could possess such monstrous strength?\"","\"Qin Shaozong is here!\"","The cry spread like a plague. Several more cold arrows whistled down from above, their aim impeccable. Every shot found its mark, and many men fell dead before they could even draw their own arrows to retaliate.","Torches fell to the ground one after another.","It was spring, the season of growth. Combined with the proximity to the Qi River, the soil was damp and the vegetation held high moisture. Many of the dropped torches failed to stay lit.","The fire dragon seemed to have its claws snapped up by a dark, monstrous beast. The severed talons were torn away and dropped to the ground, quickly losing their light. The broken line of fire no longer looked continuous.","\"Fire!\"","After a moment of preparation, a rain of arrows hissed into the darkness. But the forest, which had just seemed to harbor a giant beast, was now silent. There were no screams, only a terrifying stillness. To Governor Feng Liang, it seemed as if all the demons and ghosts had gone into hiding.","If the enemy hid behind tree trunks for cover or shifted positions stealthily, then firing a volley—or even emptying their quivers—wouldn't graze him in the slightest.","Feng Liang ground his teeth and snarled, \"Pass the order! Tell them to extinguish all the torches!\"","The enemy was in the dark while they were in the light; the situation was unfavorable. Since they already knew Qin Shaozong’s general location, there was no need to give him the advantage.","The military order swept through the ranks like a wind, snuffing out the flames in the soldiers' hands.","When a person moves from bright light into sudden darkness, their vision goes black for a second or two. Seizing this brief window, Qin Shaozong discarded his longbow, drew a blade the length of a forearm, and plunged into the crowd of men nearby.","He moved with the predatory grace of a tiger, closing in on the nearest soldier from the flank. His blade flashed like lightning across the man's throat—a swift thrust and pull, executed with chilling efficiency.","Blood sprayed in a gruesome arc as the man collapsed. A round object rolled from beneath Qin Shaozong’s feet toward the steep slope.","\"He’s here! Support!\" someone yelled from behind. At the same time, a saber swung toward him. Qin Shaozong swung his own blade back over his shoulder to block. With a sharp metallic clang, the enemy's blade was held firmly in place.","With a nimble pivot, Qin Shaozong delivered a powerful kick to the man's midsection. The force was so great it sent the soldier flying into a tree. The man spat out blood mixed with internal fragments, his eyes rolling back as he lost consciousness, his fate unknown.","The search line had originally been stretched thin, and gathering the troops in the dark of night would naturally take time.","After Qin Shaozong claimed five heads in quick succession, the area around him fell silent.","The man looked up at a nearby tree, his narrow eyes narrowing further. He sheathed his blade and leaped from a standstill, his long arms catching a high branch. His powerful muscles rippled as he pulled himself up with an effortless pull-up.","In the blink of an eye, the man who had been on the ground had vanished.","A few moments later, several soldiers rushed to the spot. They gasped at the sight of the mangled corpses on the ground.","\"The blood hasn't traveled far; he must have just left. Move! Search ahead!\"","\"Governor Feng said Qin Shaozong was still carrying a woman while he fled. The man certainly knows how to enjoy himself.\"","\"I imagine that woman must be a rare beauty. Once we kill Qin Shaozong, we can take advantage of the chaos and enjoy the Marquis's favorite concubine ourselves. I'll make sure she—\"","A dark shadow plummeted from the tree, landing precisely behind the two men. Even as his blade licked across the throat of the man on the left like a venomous snake, his large, calloused hand clamped onto the neck of the one on the right.","Veins bulged on the back of his dark hand—a grip like a tiger's claw—snapping the man's neck with sheer, terrifying brute force.","In an instant, both were dead.","Qin Shaozong had jumped down with his back to the tree, landing behind the group. By the time the others noticed something was wrong and turned around, their pupils reflected only a chilling glint of white light.","Splash...","Blood splattered onto the leaves, pooling along the veins before dripping down. A drop landed right on an eye frozen wide in shock and disbelief.","Qin Shaozong sheathed his blade and grabbed one of the bodies, stripping the soldier of his uniform and red cap to don them himself.","As he prepared to leave, something caught his eye. He looked down coldly at the first two men he had killed. Passing by, he kicked them into a nearby ditch.","\"Frogs and toads in a ditch,\" he muttered, \"how dare you covet the bright moon?\""]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27","paragraphs":["Having changed his attire, Qin Shaozong walked along the path leading down the mountain, stopping people along the way to ask for directions.","\"Where is Commander Feng? I have urgent military intelligence to report to him,\" Qin Shaozong said.","The night was dark and the wind high. The branches and leaves of the dense undergrowth seemed to coalesce into large patches of shadow, falling impartially on the faces and bodies of all who passed, rendering them even darker.","Of those questioned by Qin Shaozong, eight or nine out of ten would truthfully tell him, with the remaining one or two simply too busy to attend to him.","Suspicion?","None existed.","Although features were hard to distinguish in the dark night, the round, crimson headpiece just barely visible on the other man's head was enough to mark him as one of their own.","If still uneasy, one could spend a little more effort examining his military uniform—clearly identical to their own. What was there to doubt?","\"Commander Feng is this way,\" those in the know all directed this comrade from the front lines.","Qin Shaozong: \"My thanks.\"","Miserable screams echoed through the mountains, one after another. Each cry fueled Feng Liang's rage, twisting his features and making him gnash his teeth.","Despite their numbers, visibility was poor in the mountains at night, and their opponent was as slippery as a loach, disappearing into the densest thickets.","Qin Shaozong was so close, yet they couldn't lay hands on him. How could this not infuriate him!","Just as Feng Liang was considering whether to adjust tactics, a voice suddenly came from not far away: \"Commander Feng, moments ago Qin Shaozong was seriously wounded by the brothers in our squad. He fled northeastward and seemed to duck into a small cave over there.\"","From Qin Shaozong's perspective, after he shouted this, one particularly agitated figure among the group hastily pushed aside those beside him to look in his direction.","\"Who spoke just now? Come forward at once,\" Feng Liang said urgently.","Qin Shaozong stared unblinkingly at that figure, slowly curving his thin lips into a smile.","So you are Commander Feng!","A path opened ahead. Qin Shaozong strode forward, his hands empty, the ring-pommeled sword hanging properly at his waist.","\"Was it you who spoke just now?\" Feng Liang was so anxious he even took two steps forward to meet him. \"You say Qin Shaozong was seriously wounded by you and ducked into a cave to the northeast. Is this true?\"","Qin Shaozong: \"Naturally. That man, believing his innate divine strength made him invincible, grew overconfident and reckless, venturing alone into our camp. While several of our brothers worked together to pin him down, we had one man sneak up from behind and stab him in the back.\"","In the chilly depths of this spring night, a gust of wind swept through, pulling apart the thick cloud layer overhead. The moon beneath finally peeked out. Faint moonlight spilled down, seeming to brighten the mountains a fraction.","Qin Shaozong happened to be standing in an open area, with no dense thickets around him. The moonlight fell unimpeded on his profile, casting the contours of his face into sharper relief—his high nose, deep-set eyes, and long brows giving him a very imposing appearance.","Feng Liang had now come to a place about three paces from Qin Shaozong. Looking at the man wearing the round crimson headpiece, he felt a strange sense of unease well up inexplicably in his heart.","But the next moment, Feng Liang saw the man before him point toward the northeast. \"Commander Feng, follow this direction for about two hundred and fifty paces, and you'll see a steep slope. There's a cave on the slope, covered with dense vines, quite inconspicuous. I saw that Qin fellow slip inside. His injuries must be severe, forcing him to hide there and wait for his subordinates to rescue him.\"","These words were highly compelling. Not only was the location precise, but they also revealed that the target was seriously wounded and currently isolated and helpless.","Feng Liang couldn't afford to overthink; he just wanted to strike while his enemy was weak and finish him off quickly. He turned and waved his hand. \"Men, head northeast! Search every cave carefully. We must capture Qin...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, a sudden bolt of lightning seemed to flash through Feng Liang's mind. This thought came abruptly, yet it struck him like a thunderclap, making his whole body tremble and sending a chill of horror down his spine in an instant.","Qin Shaozong of the North, the Marquis of Wu'an personally enfeoffed by the court, the only nobleman guarding the border who also served as the Regional Inspector of two provinces. Rumors said this man possessed divine strength but was born with broken eyebrows, having brought misfortune upon his father and elder brother.","Broken eyebrows!","The soldier who just reported the intelligence clearly had a disconnected tail on his left eyebrow.","\"You are Qin...\"","\"Shlick.\" A long blade swept across his neck. Feng Liang's round head flew clean off.","Following Feng Liang's earlier order, the guards around him had all turned, facing northeast, ready to advance. Consequently, when this sudden change occurred, no one reacted in time, let alone rushed forward to rescue him.","Qin Shaozong shouted loudly: \"The Marquis is wounded, Feng the traitor accompanies him in death! Your commander has perished!\"","His voice, resonant as a bell, carried far, causing the surrounding soldiers who heard the news to panic.","Capture the leader first to cripple the gang. Now that the rebel leader had fallen, the army was left without a head. This force of a thousand men instantly fell into chaos.","Qin Shaozong took advantage of the confusion to slip into the jungle. As he made his way up the mountain, he dealt with any soldiers he encountered along the way.","\"Preeeet— Preeeet—\"","Several long whistles sounded. Hearing the signal, Qin Shaozong's personal guards fought a rearguard action, swiftly withdrawing upward.","With Feng Liang dead, his deputy commander gritted his teeth and struggled on, sustained solely by the phrase \"the Marquis is wounded\" as he continued to organize the fight.","Due to the withdrawal of Qin Shaozong's side, the speed of Li Zan's army's ascent also increased considerably. The deputy commander led his troops in pursuit all the way to the mountain stronghold at the peak, then chased them down the mountain, finally reaching the edge of a lake.","From a distance, the deputy commander saw two figures ahead supporting a third by the arms, helping him onto a plank connecting the shore to a tower ship.","They intended to escape by boat!","\"Hurry, stop them! Qin Shaozong is wounded; we cannot let him escape!\" the deputy commander shouted hoarsely. \"Whoever takes his head, the Grand Marshal will ensure his entire clan enjoys wealth and honor!\"","The soldiers' spirits were roused. One after another, they charged forward as if injected with adrenaline. However, it was regrettable; the distance separating them was no small matter. No matter how hard they ran until they were breathless, a large gap still remained between them and the tower ship.","Watching Qin Shaozong board the ship and his guards retract the plank, the deputy commander's eyes nearly burst from their sockets. \"Loose arrows!\"","\"Whoosh, whoosh, whoosh—\"","A rain of arrows flew forth, menacing in momentum, but ultimately fell short of their range, embedding themselves in the ground. They didn't even reach the tower ship, let alone the people on board.","By the time the deputy commander finally led his men to the lakeshore, the two tower ships had long since sailed to the center of the lake.","Arrows couldn't reach them, and there were no boats to use. Success had slipped from their grasp at the final moment.","The deputy commander vented his fury by throwing his longbow to the ground, his gaze turning venomous. \"We were so close! How utterly hateful!\"","\"Deputy Commander Chen, what should we do now?\" a soldier asked.","The deputy commander took a deep breath. \"The news of Commander Feng's death and Qin Shaozong's wounded escape must be sent to the Grand Marshal immediately. They are taking the Qi River. The Qi River runs north-south longitudinally and west-east latitudinally. They will surely head upstream—that is, toward the area closer to Nankang Commandery.\"","A nearby aide's eyes lit up. \"Ximen Commandery! The upper reaches of the Qi River connect to Ximen Commandery.\"","The deputy general gnashed his teeth in fury. \"Qin Shaozong is gravely wounded and will certainly need a physician and medicine to treat his injuries. If we rush to Ximen County immediately, we can capture him there.\"","When a general is in the field, he does not always follow his sovereign's commands.","This Deputy General Chen, eager to see his entire clan enjoy wealth and honor, had his own calculations. After hastily writing a letter and entrusting it to a subordinate to deliver, he led the remaining troops and rushed headlong towards Ximen County.","The tower ship.","When Qin Shaozong was helped aboard, appearing \"on the brink of death,\" Dai Li was surprised, yet not entirely so. She thought to herself that their course would definitely have to change now.","They would surely rush to another county to find a physician to treat Qin Shaozong in the dead of night. In the ensuing chaos, perhaps she could...","Her little scheme was only half-formed when she watched, wide-eyed, as the man who had seemed half-dead just moments before suddenly straightened up once he was helped into the cabin.","His spine was ramrod straight, his gaze sharp and bright as he looked over. That fierce, vital energy of his was strikingly conspicuous even in the night, leaving no trace of his earlier feigned weakness.","Before she could react, their eyes met.","Dai Li: \"...\"","Qin Shaozong walked straight towards her.","He advanced; she retreated until her back was against the cabin wall, with nowhere left to go.","\"What little scheme are you plotting now, my lady?\" Qin Shaozong asked with a smile that didn't reach his eyes, which held a cold sharpness.","The moment he looked up, he had seen her big eyes darting around. This little vixen was probably thinking of putting on her rabbit disguise to do something mischievous again. He really couldn't take his eyes off her for even a moment.","Dai Li, of course, denied it. \"I wasn't.\"","\"The sound of your abacus beads is ringing in my ears. How could you not be scheming? Besides, if you weren't, why are you retreating?\" Qin Shaozong continued his advance step by step.","Dai Li said softly, \"The smell of blood on you is strong. I'm not accustomed to it.\"","This wasn't a lie. The moment he returned, she had caught the thick scent of blood, which had swept through the cabin like a gust of wind.","As he drew closer, the smell grew even stronger. It was like a cloth thrown into a bucket full of blood, every fiber saturated with a heavy, metallic scent, so much so that it seemed it would still drip wetly when pulled out.","For a moment, this dense, almost viscous smell of blood gave Dai Li the illusion that what stood before her was a ferocious tiger that had just returned from the hunt, its long fangs and the crevices of its sharp claws still carrying bits of un-cleaned flesh.","\"How delicate you are,\" Qin Shaozong clicked his tongue lightly but did not press further.","Both tower ships had three decks. Originally used for passengers, they not only had many rooms but also basic amenities in each.","Seeing that they seemed to have matters to discuss, Dai Li went upstairs alone. She went to the third floor and chose the room at the end of the corridor.","Enter, lock the door, all in one smooth motion.","Only when she was alone did Dai Li take out a cloth pouch from each of her sleeves.","Her monthly cycle was approaching, so she carried menstrual cloths with her. The other pouch contained silver and some delicate, easily pawned jewelry.","That was all she had. Her bundle was left at Lin Erniang's house, and there had been no time to retrieve it when they fled.","As for the most important thing, the heirloom...","Dai Li sighed.","Downstairs, in a cabin.","Qin Shaozong sat in a chair, facing Mo Yanyun, who was writing furiously about three paces away. His hand rested on a small table beside him, his long fingers tapping idly.","He was waiting, but his thoughts were elsewhere.","While Mo Yanyun could be foolish when it came to women and sometimes slower than his comrades, he possessed a rare talent: he was exceptionally skilled at drawing maps.","Mountain paths traversed, bridges crossed, rivers forded, even maps glimpsed months ago—all these were etched in Mo Yanyun's mind. Whenever he wished, he could recall and piece them together.","\"My lord, it's done,\" Mo Yanyun said, setting down his brush.","Qin Shaozong collected his thoughts, lowered his gaze, and reached out to take the still-damp silk map.","The map depicted the mountains and rivers near Ximen County and Taiping County, with particular detail given to the flow and tributaries of the Qi River, its confluence with other rivers, and the counties it passed through.","\"At our current speed,\" Mo Yanyun said, \"we will reach Ximen County in two and a half hours at the latest. By then, it will be broad daylight, and we can enter the city without exposing our identities.\"","Qin Shaozong looked at the Qi River on the map, a glint of calculation in his eyes.","The Qi River flowed roughly from north to south, with a slight westward-to-eastward bend, resulting in a southwestern course. This southwestern waterway passed near several counties, including Taiping County, which had the Zhuya Ferry, and Ximen County, their destination.","Further upstream was the third: Guhan County.","Guhan County happened to be directly west of Nankang County. It was as if he had taken a southwestern route, making a wide detour to end up west of Nankang County. What was particularly interesting was that Guhan County was near the Hutuo River, which had a small tributary beside Peach Blossom Ridge.","\"I am 'gravely wounded,'\" Qin Shaozong said. \"This trip to Ximen County for a physician is unavoidable. They are traveling by land, and with that Commander Feng dead, I doubt they will pursue too closely. Let's lead them on a little chase first.\"","The recent battle had been in the mountains, where horses were useless, so everyone had dismounted. The difference was that his side had left directly by ship, while the enemy had to cross the mountains again to retrieve their horses. This back-and-forth meant his ship had gained a significant lead.","He continued, \"Send a message to Su Xiuzhu. Tell him he will soon receive news of my grave injury. He is to enter the Jiang residence and take Yan San and the others away. After waiting one full day, they are to seek out Li Zan to avenge me. The Dark Cavalry is to be temporarily led by Yan San. The general marching plan remains largely unchanged. However, since I am in critical condition, there is no need for excessive secrecy now. Have them march directly along the upper road. The success of this plan hinges entirely on speed. Order Yan San to advance swiftly without delay.\"","From his perspective, Jiang Chonghai's collusion with Li Zan, and Li Zan's attempt to ambush the Dark Cavalry at Peach Blossom Ridge, were now clear.","As for Li Zan, he only knew that the Dark Cavalry would take the upper road past Peach Blossom Ridge. Based on this, he would likely choose to set an ambush there.","Both sides wanted to seize this ambush point. The difference lay in one side knowing the full picture and thus rushing to gain the advantage, while the other, feeling confident of victory, might proceed more leisurely.","The Su Xiuzhu Qin Shaozong mentioned was the Dark Cavalry's quartermaster and secretary, handling provisions and documents—a civil position within the army. When they entered the city, he had remained outside the walls with the three thousand Dark Cavalry troops.","Mo Yanyun nodded and began writing furiously again.","Half an hour later, the cabin door opened. The meeting was over.","Outside, the sky showed a faint, hazy light. A sliver of white appeared on the horizon as the darkest hour before dawn quietly passed.","Soon, the sky would be fully bright.","Climbing mountains, engaging in battle, boarding the ship, discussing plans. Qin Shaozong hadn't closed his eyes all night, but it didn't stop him from being full of energy. \"Hu Bao, have the ship pull ashore for now.\"","\"Lord, why is that?\" Mo Yanyun stopped his steps on his way back to his room to catch up on sleep, thinking that this wasn't part of the plan they had just discussed.","Qin Shaozong glanced at him faintly. \"What's with the fuss? Just going down to the river to wash up. You come too. If you don't bathe soon, the dung beetles from the mountains will smell you and come to roll you away.\"","Mo Yanyun: \"...\"","Mo Yanyun was greatly shocked.","Wait, since when was he smelly?","Last night, he had been left at the stronghold to prepare for the retreat and hadn't participated in the bloody battle. Compared to the Lord, whose robes were caked with blood thick enough to form clots and who was thoroughly marinated in the scent, he had at most just sweated a little.","But fine, since his superior ordered it, he couldn't not go. Mo Yanyun simply called out, \"Come on, everyone, let's all go wash up.\"","The moon set, the sun rose, daylight returned, and a new day began.","Dai Li was awakened by the sunlight streaming through the window. She had been too exhausted after returning to her room last night and had forgotten to draw the curtains before sleeping.","Now, the sunlight outside was strong. Judging by the sun's height, Dai Li estimated the time to be around Chenshi (7-9 AM). She usually woke at this hour, but having rested late last night, she was still very tired.","Since no one had come to call her, why not draw the curtains and go back to sleep? Thinking this, Dai Li got off the bed, slipped on her wooden clogs, and went to the window to pull the curtains. But with one look, she was surprised to find the ship had docked.","It wasn't just pulled up to any random riverbank; it was moored at a ferry.","In the early morning, other ships were also at the ferry. Boats, both new and old, were moored quite orderly at the piers, disgorging and taking on passengers carrying large and small bundles.","If one looked further into the distance, one could see many covered boats gathered near the ferry, where fishermen wearing straw hats were unloading baskets of river catch.","The ferry was bustling with a constant stream of people coming and going.","Dai Li remembered the cart driver who had sent her out of the city saying the Qi River generally flowed from north to south. Since Qin Shaozong was fleeing, wouldn't he possibly choose the faster route of going downstream with the current?","If so, hadn't she gotten a step closer to Hangzhou?","Even though she knew perfectly well that Qin Shaozong wouldn't take her back to Hangzhou, Dai Li couldn't help but feel her spirits lift.","She wasn't sleepy anymore, couldn't sleep at all.","Just as she was about to push the window open wider to let the breeze in, a familiar warm surge rushed downwards. Dai Li froze, then hurried to fetch her menstrual cloth.","Her monthly courses had arrived.","Perhaps due to her constitution, Dai Li's cycle was quite regular. During her period, she only felt more easily fatigued than usual. Other negative effects, such as menstrual pain, backaches, or being prone to diarrhea, she didn't experience at all.","After changing into the menstrual cloth and washing up, Dai Li went out.","The entire third floor was quiet. Walking from one end to the other, Dai Li saw all the other guest rooms had their doors tightly shut, showing no signs of use, as if she were the only one staying on this floor.","She went downstairs.","It was livelier downstairs. Mo Yanyun and Hu Bao were talking beside the staircase.","\"Later, when you get to the clinic, put the silver on the table, then just grab the physician on duty and carry him off, to show the urgency of the situation,\" Mo Yanyun said, pounding his right fist into his left palm.","Hu Bao nodded and continued, \"And have people sweep through the medicine cabinets, take as many medicinal herbs as possible. Like locusts passing through, leaving not a blade of grass.\"","Listening to their plan, it sounded more like preparing for a raid.","\"Lady Dai?\" Mo Yanyun caught sight of Dai Li from the corner of his eye.","Dai Li descended the stairs. \"Are you planning to go into the city? Could I possibly go with you? I'd like to buy some things.\"","Upon hearing this, both Mo Yanyun and Hu Bao's pupils constricted. Then, they actually both simultaneously made a motion of turning their heads away, pretending not to have heard.","Dai Li: \"...\"","For a moment, a faint awkwardness hung in the air.","\"What are you all doing blocking the staircase?\" A tall figure emerged from a room.","Hu Bao immediately said, \"Lord, Lady Dai has something to discuss with you.\"","\"Right, she has important matters to discuss with you. She was just passing by earlier,\" Mo Yanyun secretly gave Hu Bao an approving look. Good fellow, his mind was really sharp.","The gaze that had originally held a hint of evasion now settled firmly upon her, as invasive as ever. Dai Li paused for two breaths before meeting those brown eyes. \"Yes, it's me. I have something I wish to discuss with you.\"","\"Come here.\" Qin Shaozong turned and went back into his room.","Meaning the conversation was to be held inside the room.","Dai Li followed without hesitation. If it had been half an hour ago, she would certainly have felt nervous, but not now.","The two entered the room one after the other, with Dai Li, who was behind, casually closing the door.","Seeing this, Qin Shaozong raised a brow. This little fox had grown quite a bit bolder after a night's sleep.","Dai Li walked up to him and got straight to the point. \"Lord, I just overheard Commandant Mo and the others discussing fetching a physician from the commandery. May I accompany them into the commandery to purchase some items?\"","Qin Shaozong let out a soft, derisive sound.","This wasn't just a little bolder. Clearly, her courage had grown yet again, trending towards the audacity of a leopard."]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28","paragraphs":["The room fell silent, the temperature plummeting as if the air had frozen into ice, sending a chill down one's spine.","Hearing his cold laugh, Dai Li quickly added, \"My travel permit has been confiscated by you. Without it, I cannot travel far. I truly have something I need to buy in the city this time.\"","\"If there's something you want, just tell Mo Yanyun. He can bring it back for you,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Dai Li glanced at him cautiously. \"Some things are... inconvenient.\"","\"It's just a matter of a few words. What could be inconvenient?\" Qin Shaozong retorted.","Seeing her feigning obedience, the fire that had never truly extinguished in his heart flared up again. \"Or are you planning to contact this person, bribe that one again? Let me tell you, Dai Li, forget it! Those few who took your silver and helped you escape before have all been imprisoned by me. Tell me, should I sentence them to six years of hard labor, or simply give them a hundred lashes and beat their flesh to a pulp?\"","With every word he spoke, Dai Li's lips pressed tighter together. Finally, hearing that the maidservants and the coachman had been thrown into prison, her face paled. \"My Lord... in the past, you toiled tirelessly, personally leading troops to Bolei Mountain to eradicate bandits for the people, protecting the region from bandit raids for over a decade. This shows you are a man of broad mind and compassion for the world. They were merely carrying out tasks for me, completely unaware of the circumstances. Ignorance should not be a crime. Why must you trouble yourself with mere commoners, as insignificant as grass?\"","Qin Shaozong rotated the jade thumb ring on his finger, then suddenly said, \"Didn't you claim you lived in the Peach Blossom Spring?\"","If it was truly isolated from the world, how did she know of outside affairs?","\"I heard the squad leader mention it last night in the cave,\" Dai Li murmured, lowering her eyes.","After these words, silence filled the room once more.","Hearing no sound, Dai Li slowly raised her eyes. The man before her wore a cold, displeased expression, but he seemed slightly less furious than moments before.","Qin Shaozong dropped the matter of the servants and returned to the original topic. \"What do you need to buy?\"","Dai Li no longer concealed it. \"Sanitary cloths.\"","Meeting his gaze again, she added, \"My monthly courses have come. Sanitary cloths are indispensable. It wouldn't be appropriate to have Commandant Mo bring such an item back for me.\"","The words \"monthly courses\" seemed to strike Qin Shaozong's forehead, making a vein throb twice.","Monthly courses again...","\"Didn't your monthly courses come just a few days ago?\" Qin Shaozong's tone was sharp.","Dai Li averted her eyes, phrasing it delicately, \"This time it's real.\"","Qin Shaozong's face darkened.","If this time was real, then last time was fake. Not only had she deceived him about a healthy woman's courses lasting seven days, but she hadn't even been having them at all.","\"Then earlier, on the bed, you said you were unwell?\" His tone grew even sharper.","Dai Li slowly bowed her head, silent.","Qin Shaozong's gaze was icy. \"I don't recall gagging you, my lady. Or do you have a fondness for that wretched cloth and wish to get accustomed to it early?\"","Dai Li kept her head down. \"...The discomfort was because I sprained my ankle.\"","She spoke softly, almost mumbling, but Qin Shaozong didn't miss a single word.","Crack. Something seemed to shatter.","The fire in his chest erupted violently, blazing like oil poured on flames. For a moment, Qin Shaozong felt the urge to simply deal with her right then and there. Otherwise, he might not die wrapped in a horse's hide on the battlefield, nor fall to an assassin's blade, but rather perish one day from sheer rage provoked by her—an utterly absurd end that would invite the world's ridicule.","Sensing a penetrating chill, Dai Li immediately looked up and said, \"That was in the past. I won't deceive you anymore.\"","She stood by the window, half her figure bathed in sunlight streaming through. With dark pupils, fair skin, and an enchanting grace, she wore the plainest gray-black dress and no ornaments, yet she radiated a stunning, jade-like brilliance. Like a luminous pearl temporarily resting on coarse, dark cloth, the contrast made her soft glow even more pronounced.","She watched him nervously, her peach-blossom eyes soft as water, the vermilion mark between her brows vividly alive.","Qin Shaozong was once again infuriated into a cold laugh. Now she knew how to play the obedient one—truly adaptable. \"If you remain stubborn this time, single-mindedly scheming and causing trouble, you won't need those two legs of yours anymore. And those maidservants and coachmen in the Nan-kang Commandery prison will suffer severe torture because of you. Do you understand?\"","Dai Li nodded, inwardly delighted at her success.","Ah, he agreed.","Qin Shaozong's face remained stern. \"Use your words.\"","Dai Li didn't argue at this moment. \"I understand.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"Get out. Send Mo Yanyun and Hu Bao in.\"","Dai Li didn't linger for a second longer, swiftly turning and exiting the room.","Expressionlessly, Qin Shaozong removed the jade thumb ring now crisscrossed with cracks and tossed it into a wastebasket nearby.","Outside the room.","Mo Yanyun and Hu Bao still stood where they were. Hearing the door open, they both looked over simultaneously.","They were somewhat curious, wondering if Dai Li had managed to provoke the tiger.","Dai Li smiled. \"Gentlemen, the Lord requests your presence.\"","Seeing her able to smile, Mo Yanyun's heart jolted.","Something was off. Could she have told the Lord the truth, and he actually agreed?","That shouldn't be!","Both men were bewildered. When they emerged from the room later, they looked even more dazed. Mo Yanyun nearly tripped over the threshold.","His mind was filled with those eight resounding words: If you lose sight of her, bring me your head.","Ximen Commandery was similar in size to Taiping Commandery. Dai Li, wearing a veil hat, was followed by Mo Yanyun, Hu Bao, and a group of elite soldiers.","Entering through the east gate, they split into two groups. The group led by Dai Li and Mo Yanyun headed for the west market, which sold fabrics; the other group, led by Hu Bao, went to the south market, where apothecaries were concentrated.","Ever since disembarking from the tower ship, Mo Yanyun's heart had been in a vise. He barely dared to blink, fearing Dai Li might vanish into thin air in that instant.","If Lady Dai disappeared, his life would be forfeit.","This time, however, Mo Yanyun worried unnecessarily. Dai Li had no plans to escape. She currently lacked advantageous timing, location, and support. Her goals were simply to procure some sanitary cloths and gather some information.","Dai Li lingered around the cloth shops. After spending over an hour, she left the city with her purchases, accompanied by Mo Yanyun and the others, and returned to the tower ships docked at the ferry.","Once back on board, Mo Yanyun instinctively turned his head.","Ah, his head was still attached.","\"Commandant Mo, the Lord is on the stern deck. He requests your presence,\" a soldier reported.","Mo Yanyun glanced toward the staircase. Dai Li had already gone upstairs; only the fleeting hem of a gray-black skirt remained in his sight. The burly man with thick eyebrows rubbed his nose and headed for the stern deck.","Having set out separately, Dai Li's group returned later. After they boarded, bone whistles sounded, and the two tower ships set sail from the shore one after the other.","The afternoon sunlight was exceptionally brilliant, the rippling river water shimmered with golden light—truly a scene of sparkling waves under clear skies. Countless splashing droplets refracted the sky's glow and mirrored the reflections of the pleasure boats from various angles, as if forming myriad bizarre and kaleidoscopic little worlds.","Standing on the stern deck gazing into the distance, the distant city was being gradually pushed away by an invisible hand, slowly shrinking.","Qin Shaozong heard footsteps but did not turn around. \"Any anomalies in the city?\"","Mo Yanyun replied, \"None. This time we encountered no special inspections; entering and exiting the city went smoothly. It seems Jiang Chonghai did not send word to the local governor.\"","Qin Shaozong asked, \"How is she?\"","Without naming anyone, Mo Yanyun understood perfectly. \"Lady Dai went to the cloth shop, hired a seamstress to work for her, and spent most of her time there without going elsewhere. It's just that...\"","Mo Yanyun hesitated slightly.","The report itself was ordinary, but reporting on a woman's affairs, especially in such meticulous detail, always made him feel like he was tattling, which undermined his dignity as a man of stature.","A gaze as cool and thin as water swept over from the side. Though it held no particular emotion, it made Mo Yanyun feel as if he had been doused with a bucket of ice water in the height of summer, instantly sobering him up.","He hurriedly added, \"Lady Dai did nothing else and had no contact with others. She just spoke rather more with the seamstress. She asked her which direction Ximen Commandery was from Taiping Commandery. Upon hearing it was northwest, she seemed quite disappointed.\"","Mo Yanyun recalled the coachman who had earlier said Dai Li wanted to go to Qiantang. \"My Lord, Lady Dai previously wanted to go to Qiantang. Could she still be fixated on that now?\"","\"Naturally. Her mind is single-heartedly set on burrowing her way to Qiantang,\" Qin Shaozong said, his gaze dark and inscrutable.","Mo Yanyun fell silent, not daring to utter another word.","Qin Shaozong then said, \"I recall a collateral branch of the Qin clan was skilled in commerce, led by a man named Qin Chong. Years ago, he took that branch south to Yangzhou for business. Many years have passed; the head of that collateral branch has likely changed. Send a message back to Yuyang for me. Have Yun Ce investigate who the current head of Qin Chong's branch is and exactly where they are now.\"","The Qin clan was a major northern family. With Qin Shaozong leading the main branch, which held immense influence, all collateral branches naturally took pride in this connection, eager to maintain frequent contact and intertwine themselves like vines around the main family tree.","Therefore, given the main branch's current prominence, the main family possessed comprehensive records. Which branch was where, who the current head was, who the family members were—all were meticulously documented.","Mo Yanyun's expression changed dramatically. \"My Lord, are you still thinking of searching for Lady Dai's son?\"","He was aware that Dai Li was looking for her son. He had played a part in the previous orders to search both the Jiang residence and Nankang Commandery.","Lady Dai had deceived His Lordship multiple times, even later scheming to escape, nearly ruining His Lordship's grand plans. With such a record of misconduct, how could His Lordship still want to help her find her son?","Why go to such lengths?","Qin Shaozong did not deny it. \"Finding someone is merely a matter of my saying the word. A person without a weakness will never be obedient.\"","Yet Mo Yanyun remained full of doubts. \"But Qiantang is a thousand li away from Nankang Commandery. Lady Dai's young son was abducted. She was in Nankang Commandery; there's no reason her son would be in Qiantang, a thousand li away.\"","Not one or two li, nor ten or a hundred li, but over a thousand. For an ordinary person to cover that distance would take at least several months.","Being so far apart, why was she so adamant about Qiantang? And why was she so certain her son hadn't been moved elsewhere by others during the months of his disappearance?","Qin Shaozong simply said, \"Just carry out the order.\"","\"...As you command.\"","Nankang Commandery.","A fast horse galloped from the east, pounding through the night to knock at the eastern city gate, then raced straight to the largest and most luxurious mansion in the southern market.","\"Who comes visiting in the dead of night?\" The gatekeeper, full of resentment, felt no goodwill toward this late-night visitor.","The person outside announced himself.","The gatekeeper's face paled, and he promptly opened the door. \"So it's the Captain. My apologies, my apologies. Please, come in quickly.\"","The man paid him no mind, striding urgently inside toward the main hall. Soon, the main hall of the Jiang residence was ablaze with light, bright as day.","Jiang Chonghai, roused in the middle of the night, was uncharacteristically free of anger or weariness. His eyes shone with an alarming intensity. \"...Is it truly so? Qin Shaozong was seriously wounded in the mountain ambush?\"","The messenger nodded. \"I heard Qin Shaozong was supported by his men as they retreated, suggesting the injury was critical. Moreover, when they passed through Ximen Commandery, his subordinates took all the resident physicians from three clinics in one go and cleared out most of the medicinal supplies.\"","Jiang Chonghai paced back and forth in the room, murmuring, \"A leaderless dragon—a heaven-sent opportunity! Have him march his troops here directly? No, that's not suitable...\"","Although the head of the Xuanxiao Cavalry was lost, they were still elite armored troops. Clashing head-on with them would surely cost Brother Li some losses.","Perhaps send word to the Xuanxiao Cavalry outside the city, letting them know Qin Shaozong's life hangs by a thread, to throw them into disarray? That seems possible, but it must be done cautiously, or it could backfire.","\"I am aware. You may go and rest,\" Jiang Chonghai said to his confidant.","Before Jiang Chonghai could decide how to proceed, as if someone offered a pillow just as he was dozing off, a Xuanxiao Cavalry officer came to his residence the very next day.","The visitor introduced himself as Su Xiuzhu, a marching instructor of the Xuanxiao Cavalry, and said he had come to the Jiang residence to find Yan San.","Accompanying him were several strong soldiers in light armor, all imposing in stature, clearly tempered repeatedly on battlefields shrouded in the smoke of war.","The household servants dared not slight them and hurriedly led them to the guest courtyard.","What transpired within the courtyard remained unknown to outsiders. Jiang Chonghai only knew that Su Xiuzhu and his party came and went in haste. They did not even wait to see him, the master of the house, before leaving swiftly with Yan San and the other soldiers stationed there.","The quarters were emptied, the stables cleared out—truly swept clean.","\"Elder Brother, they are far too disrespectful. Eating and drinking for free is one thing, but now leaving without even bidding you farewell. They truly are crude northerners, arrogant and ill-mannered, lacking in propriety,\" Jiang Chongjiang complained.","He expected his elder brother to agree, but instead, Jiang Chonghai smiled meaningfully. \"It's understandable. After all, with a fire at their heels, how would they have time for other matters?\"","\"What fire at their heels?\" Jiang Chongjiang was puzzled.","Jiang Chonghai offered no explanation but turned and went to his study. He needed to write another letter to Brother Li, informing him that the time was ripe and urging him to come quickly to set an ambush at Peach Blossom Ridge.","Speaking of which, Peach Blossom Ridge was a marvelous place. Not only did it have endless stretches of peach blossoms, but the road was also wide, flanked by dense forests, with high terrain on both sides like sloping ladders.","Such a beautiful place would not be an unworthy burial ground for the Xuanxiao Cavalry.","A fast horse set out from the Governor's residence, speeding toward the eastern city gate.","The man did not notice that amidst the bustling crowd at Baima Ford, a fishmonger kept glancing frequently in a certain direction. After he watched a man board a dedicated boat and sail away, the fishmonger immediately broke into a beaming smile and even gave away the unsold fish in his hands to the buyer before him.","\"Alright, time to call it a day!\"","East of the city, at the Dark Cavalry camp.","\"Finally back.\" Su Xiuzhu welcomed the returning scout. \"How did it go? Smoothly?\"","The burly man nodded. \"Everything went smoothly. Confirmed it was that bastard. I've seen him before, couldn't possibly mistake him.\"","Su Xiuzhu said, \"Jiang Chonghai has sent a letter to Ying Commandery. The Lord's letter says we are to wait one full day before setting out.\"","Yan San pondered for a moment. \"That's indeed prudent. With no one currently in command at the camp, even though we are eager to avenge the Lord, we need time to decide on a temporary leader and also allow time for the messenger to travel far and deliver the report.\"","The location of Peach Blossom Ridge was actually quite strategic; it was closer to Ying Commandery. In other words, setting out from Ying Commandery to reach this place would be much, much faster than starting from Nankang Commandery.","Waiting one full day in the eastern outskirts also meant they would have to force-march at night to make up for the lost daylight.","Yan San ordered, \"Pass the command: let the soldiers rest more. Starting from tonight at Xu hour (7-9 PM), we will begin a high-intensity march, day and night without rest.\"","Time flashed by. The sunlight gradually faded, the sky dyed with brilliant sunset hues before slowly being shrouded in a layer of dark gray.","Night fell.","The Dark Cavalry in the east of the city quickly struck camp. The thunderous rumble of hooves echoed like distant thunder as they galloped straight onto the main road.","Traveling by starlight and moonlight without rest, after days of marching, the Dark Cavalry, temporarily led by Yan San, arrived near Peach Blossom Ridge.","Yan San did not immediately lead the main force into Peach Blossom Ridge. Instead, he cautiously dispatched two teams of scouts, splitting them to ascend along the ridge from two different paths to survey the situation within the hills.","A little over two shichen (over four hours) later, the scouts returned, reporting no ambush in the mountains.","Upon hearing this, Su Xiuzhu couldn't help but smile. True to his name, he possessed an elegant and handsome appearance, a kind of clean-cut, refreshing handsomeness. \"This so-called Grand Marshal of All Under Heaven is truly arrogant and overconfident. He really took it for granted that we would arrive late.\"","Yan San reminded him, \"Not late. He simply assumed we would travel at a normal pace.\"","For the forced march, the Dark Cavalry had split into two parts.","One part was the vanguard forced-march unit. Each man in this group had a fast horse, carrying only dried rations, water skins, and the like, spending most of the subsequent days on horseback.","The other part was the logistics corps responsible for supplies. They followed behind, bringing pots, pans, bowls, and ladles, herding the army's livestock, grain, and fodder.","The vanguard unit, by force-marching, arrived at Peach Blossom Ridge a full three days ahead of the estimated time.","Yan San began assigning tasks. \"The North and South units will enter the mountains from both sides to lie in ambush. The East and West units will position themselves at the eastern and western ends of Peach Blossom Ridge respectively. The East unit will guard the eastern pass. When Li Zan's troops scatter and flee in defeat, you will charge out and cut off their retreat. During this time, be careful to avoid enemy scouts; they might send troops to reconnoiter and probe.\"","The Dark Cavalry quickly divided into four units, each led by its commander to carry out the orders.","After a brief period of clamor, Peach Blossom Ridge returned to silence once more. A breeze swept through, causing the peach blossoms on the ridge to rustle and sway, like a silent welcome from the buds and fallen petals.","The sun rose and set. In the blink of an eye, two days passed, and the tranquil Peach Blossom Ridge welcomed another large group of guests.","These past few days, Li Zan had been in high spirits. First, he learned from his sworn brother Jiang that Qin Shaozong's reputation did not match reality. Then, Qin Shaozong, having lost his head, actually chased after a fleeing concubine with only a handful of men to Taiping Commandery, followed later by news of him sustaining serious injuries.","With Qin Shaozong severely wounded ahead and his knowledge of the Dark Cavalry's marching route behind, what worry was there about burying this famously formidable cavalry right here?","Li Zan felt victory was firmly within his grasp and, wanting to witness this moment in history, personally led his troops to Peach Blossom Ridge this time.","Simultaneously, neither Yan San nor Li Zan were aware—","Two tower ships that had earlier turned out from the main river channel had sailed along a minor waterway until they ran aground. Everyone on the tower ships disembarked and proceeded on foot towards the rear of Peach Blossom Ridge.","And there, was precisely where the Dark Cavalry's logistics corps was stationed.","Daili walked beside Qin Shaozong, with Mo Yan, Yunhu Bao, and others behind them. After walking a stretch, she slowed her pace, slipping back from Qin Shaozong's side.","Qin Shaozong tilted his head slightly, his peripheral glance sweeping over Daili who was now walking beside Yunhu Bao. He said nothing.","After another stretch of road, it so happened that Mo Yan started chatting idly about anything and everything. As Qin Shaozong responded, his gaze inadvertently swept past them again, only to see that the spot beside Yunhu Bao was now empty.","Looking further back, well, she had drifted further and further back as she walked, all the way to the tail end of the group. Given a little more time, she might just vanish into the forest altogether.","\"My Lord?\" Mo Yan noticed Qin Shaozong suddenly turning back.","Qin Shaozong simply said, \"You lead the group forward for now. I'm going to check on the rear.\""]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29","paragraphs":["The mountain path was treacherous, and Daili walked at a sluggish pace.","From the front of the line, to the middle, and then slowly slipping all the way to the rear. Daili knew she was walking very slowly; in a little while, she might fall behind.","But she believed she had done well enough. As for that spirit of gritting one's teeth and never giving up until the last breath...","Forget it, it wasn't for her.","Daili stopped and looked around.","\"Has my lady found a suitable location?\" A deep male voice came from ahead.","Daili turned her head at the sound and saw that the man who had been at the front of the line had somehow come over. The ground was thick with grass and foliage; large, connected leaves could hide the rugged, uneven terrain beneath. A moment of inattention, and one could easily step wrong and twist an ankle.","But Qin Shaozong moved as if walking on level ground. In fact, in the brief moment Daili hesitated and felt a pang of envy, he had already walked from the distance right up to her.","Perhaps because she hadn't answered, the corners of his eyes lifted with a sharp edge. \"You used to spin lies effortlessly. Has your tongue stopped working now?\"","For a moment, Daili completely understood why Li Zan had sent men to hunt him across the mountains. This man was just that arrogant, that infuriating.","But under another's roof, one must bow their head. Daili could only say, \"What location?\"","\"Walking so slowly, weren't you trying to find a place to retire to the mountains? To live among the birds and beasts.\" Qin Shaozong said, raising a hand to point at a ravine they had just crossed. \"In my opinion, that spot isn't bad. There's a snake den there. Red chain snakes, non-venomous, only about as thick as a child's wrist. A bite wouldn't be life-threatening, and my lady certainly wouldn't be bothered by mosquitoes at night.\"","Daili: \"...\"","Even though she knew he was trying to scare her, Daili was inherently afraid of those cold-blooded, crawling creatures. Just the thought that she might have actually stepped over a snake den made goosebumps break out all over her back.","Daili quickly walked forward.","Qin Shaozong followed, a smirk playing on his lips.","It didn't last long, however. Qin Shaozong watched as she began to veer off course, finally walking to a large tree and picking up a straight branch about as thick as a chicken egg.","Daili wanted to find a branch to use as a hiking pole, to make walking the mountain path less strenuous. But after testing it, she found the branch she had picked was a bit too long.","The length of a hiking pole relates to the user's height. For someone of her stature, around 1.2 meters would suffice.","This branch was about 1.45 meters.","Daili stepped on the lower end of the branch, trying to use her weight to snap off the extra twenty-some centimeters.","Unfortunately, perhaps because the branch was relatively thick, or perhaps because the section she wanted to break off was too short and too close to the ground to apply force properly, she stomped several times without breaking it.","A gaze brimming with amusement had been watching her from the side. \"Is my lady picking out a snake-driving stick in advance?\"","Daili corrected him, \"It's a hiking pole. Using this as an aid makes walking mountain paths much less tiring.\"","Qin Shaozong didn't quite understand why this \"hiking pole\" needed a specific length, but seeing her futile attempts, he reminded, \"Use a knife.\"","Daili paused, suddenly remembering she had a tool on her.","The night they hid in the cave, he had given her a dagger. He hadn't asked for it back, so she had kept it, feeling somewhat more secure with the blade by her side.","Daili took out the short knife and, under Qin Shaozong's complicated gaze, crouched down. Holding the knife in her right hand and pressing down on the branch with her left, she began to saw slowly.","\"Scratch, scratch...\"","The dagger left a few shallow scratches on the branch's surface.","Qin Shaozong's mouth twitched. \"By the time you finish sawing through that branch, the sapling next to it will be tall enough to block out the sun. Give it here.\"","Daili looked at the knife marks, thinking to herself that she only needed to cut partway in, then she could step on it from the opposite direction to snap it off. It couldn't be as exaggerated as he said.","But she stood up anyway and handed him the branch.","Qin Shaozong took the branch. Before Daili could even hand over the dagger from her other hand, she saw a flash of white light before her eyes, followed immediately by a soft snap as something fell to the ground.","Daili looked down. It was a small section of branch, about twenty-some centimeters long, precisely the part she had wanted to cut off. The cut followed exactly along her shallow scratches, not a hair off.","Daili: \"...\"","Qin Shaozong casually scraped off the excess twigs from both sides of the branch, sheathed the short knife, and said, \"Take it. Keep up.\"","Daili silently put away her dagger, took the hiking pole, and continued on her way.","About halfway, Daili suddenly heard a cacophony of battle cries. War drums thundered, shouts and the clamor of combat rose in waves, like a depth charge exploding and sending towering waves skyward.","Daili's heart leaped, and she instinctively looked around.","Her surroundings were normal. No cold arrows flew from the forest, no armored soldiers charged with drawn blades. There was only the mountain wind, carrying the sounds of slaughter as it brushed past her face.","Whether it was Daili's imagination or not, she thought she caught a faint scent of blood on the wind.","The sounds of battle seemed to materialize into invisible lions and tigers before her eyes, locked in combat with fangs and claws, churning up dust and splattering flesh and blood.","\"It seems the hunt has begun.\" Qin Shaozong's lips curved into a smile.","Mo Yanyun, Hu Bao, and the others were extremely excited. They had prepared for a long time, eagerly anticipating this hunt that could crush Li Zan's main forces in one fell swoop.","\"The Xuanxiao Cavalry has surrounded them from all sides, taking full advantage of the terrain. This battle should be over quickly,\" Mo Yanyun said, excited yet with a touch of regret that he couldn't be on the field himself.","As he spoke, he suddenly remembered something. \"My lord, I heard Li Zan has a fierce general under him named Wang Qinglie. This man possesses extraordinary martial skill, Herculean strength, and wields a three-pointed double-edged blade with god-like prowess. In the past, when Li Zan's power wasn't as great and he suffered several encirclements by the Jizhou troops, it was this Wang Qinglie who repeatedly saved him from peril.\"","\"The tide has turned, and morale is shattered. How can the mere bravery of one man salvage that?\" Hu Bao said quietly.","Mo Yanyun thought for a moment and agreed.","Taking a step back, even if Wang Qinglie managed to extract Li Zan from this encirclement, saving him from death, it still wouldn't change the fate of the army Li Zan brought to Peach Blossom Ridge being annihilated.","With the main force gone, only the old, weak, sick, and injured would remain. Dealing with them would be as easy as slicing vegetables.","Amidst the continuous sounds of slaughter, Qin Shaozong and the others arrived at the rear of Peach Blossom Ridge, the encampment of the Xuanxiao Cavalry's commissariat.","The dark \"Qin\" banner fluttered in the wind. Its edges were not straight but cut into flame-like points. As it rippled in the wind, the edges seemed to form a row of sharp tiger teeth, exuding formidable intimidation.","The guards at the camp saw a group approaching from afar. Once they recognized who it was, their hearts surged with excitement and immense joy.","\"The Lord Marquis returns—!\"","A long horn blast swept through the entire camp like a gale. More and more soldiers came forward to welcome them, and the previously solemn camp instantly became bustling with noise and excitement.","This was Dai Li's first time encountering an ancient military camp. It was largely as she had imagined; this temporary encampment was much more rudimentary than a permanent garrison.","There was no dedicated armory, no formal training grounds. The soldiers lived in separate camps with their weapons, prioritizing ease of departure.","A multitude of gazes turned her way—admiration, shock, curiosity, confusion, bewilderment...","They came in all varieties, akin to a pack of wolves suddenly discovering a lamb, utterly out of place, nestled in their den.","Dai Li pondered. The look in their eyes suggested the army was exclusively male, with no camp followers kept.","This was a good sign. It indicated that the commanding officer held his soldiers to high standards, wanting their strength focused solely on slaughtering enemies on the battlefield, not on women.","The leader sets the example and should act accordingly.","Based on her understanding of him over these past days, that man would not compromise his authority for the sake of a woman. Even if she followed him into the camp, she would likely have her own tent.","At most, one more day and her monthly courses would be over. It was fortunate they had come to the camp. If they had stayed on the tower ship, he would certainly have...","Thinking this, Dai Li suddenly found the intense stares around her somewhat endearing.","Qin Shaozong suddenly turned his head to glance at Dai Li. Sensing his gaze, she quickly composed her expression, instantly becoming elegant and dignified, as if the flicker of cunning he had just seen was merely his imagination.","The muscles along Qin Shaozong's jaw tightened. He unconsciously ran his tongue over a canine tooth, trying to wipe away that thoughtful itch upon it.","However, very soon, whether it was Dai Li, Qin Shaozong, or any soldier in the army, all their attention was captured by another matter.","\"Clatter, clatter, clatter—\"","A fast horse galloped in from the direction of the battlefield, its hooves pounding, kicking up a cloud of dust. Upon closer look, one could see this horse was somewhat unusual.","An ordinary cavalryman rode one horse, but two people were hunched over this steed.","A voice, clear as a booming bell, shouted from the distance, so urgent its tail end even cracked, \"Doctor Ding! Doctor Ding Lianxi! Come quickly, save a life!!\"","The Dark Cavalry were all equipped with sturdy, well-fed steeds, their speed unmatched by ordinary horses. In mere moments, the distant rider charged into the camp.","A gust of wind swept past, carrying a thick, heavy scent of blood.","\"Doctor Ding!\"","The entire camp was calling for Doctor Ding. Dai Li guessed this Doctor Ding was likely a military physician, and probably the most skilled one in the army.","She saw Qin Shaozong's face darken as he strode quickly towards the newcomers. After a moment's thought, Dai Li followed.","Hearing the shouts outside, Ding Lianxi hurried out of his tent. He was around forty, with a broad forehead, fair complexion, and a light beard, appearing to have a very gentle disposition.","But at this moment, the chief physician of the Dark Cavalry wore a look of shock, drawing a sharp breath. \"How could Commander Qiao be injured so grievously? He's nearly bled dry.\"","This was no exaggeration. The man called \"Commander Qiao\" was critically wounded. The breastplate on his torso had been torn open by a weapon with brute force, the armor breached and the flesh beneath injured. As far as the eye could see, everything was stained a blinding red.","And still, blood continued to gush relentlessly from his body. In stark contrast to the vast, glaring red was his face, growing paler by the second.","Anyone could see his life force was fading.","The man who had brought Qiao Wangfei back said with fury, \"The encirclement strategy was going perfectly. We had wiped out countless enemy troops and were on the verge of taking the salt smuggler leader's head when that Wang Qinglie suddenly appeared. The man was nearly ten feet tall, massive as a mountain, incredibly strong. He wielded a three-pointed blade with masterful skill, killing many of our soldiers to cover Li Zan's retreat. Seeing this, Commander Qiao, Commander Feng, and Commandant Yan joined forces to fight him. After a long, bitter struggle, at the cost of Commander Qiao's severe injuries and Commander Feng and Commandant Yan's lighter wounds, they finally managed to behead him.\"","Those around listened, both shocked and enraged.","Every soldier in their Dark Cavalry was the elite of the elite. One could say that within the regions of You and Bing, under Qin Shaozong's control, the very best of all troops were selected for the Dark Cavalry.","They ate good meat at least every other day, with meat and rice in ample supply. Combined with training intensity far exceeding that of ordinary soldiers, over time, every Dark Cavalryman developed a robust physique.","Yet this was merely the foundation. This cavalry unit, built with heavy investment, eliminated a portion of its men every season.","Those who failed the assessments were sent away. Then the staggeringly high allowances were gone, the fine food they could eat to their heart's content was gone, and the honor envied by others was gone.","Under such stimuli, every soldier was trained to be agile and skilled. If ordinary soldiers were like this, how much more so the commanders?","The three thousand Dark Cavalry were divided into four companies: East, South, West, and North. Each company had only one head commander. This head commander led over seven hundred men. He might not be the absolute best fighter, but his martial prowess was certainly among the top ranks.","Even so, with three of them joining forces, Qiao Wangfei was still gravely injured to this extent. How could they not be shocked?","While the man was speaking, Ding Lianxi had already given Qiao Wangfei a preliminary examination. The more he checked, the grimmer his expression became. Finally, he shook his head helplessly at Qin Shaozong. \"My lord, the wound is too large. The bleeding simply cannot be stopped. I beg your pardon, but I am powerless.\"","Silence fell all around at his words.","Some gritted their teeth, their eyes reddening uncontrollably. Others clenched their fists, glaring towards the battlefield with murderous intent.","Qin Shaozong closed his eyes. \"Take Qiao Wangfei...\"","\"Do you have any cattle in the camp? Perhaps try slaughtering a healthy ox, then place him inside the ox's belly. He might not have to die.\" A gentle voice came through, like a spring breeze sweeping across the boundless, sandy wilderness.","Qin Shaozong whirled his head around.","Everyone's gaze shifted in unison, focusing on the woman standing just two steps outside the circle surrounding Qiao Wangfei.","She wore dull, grayish garments, yet her skin was like snow, her hair like satin, her eyes limpid as water. Her entire person seemed to glow with a gentle, pearlescent light, making it hard to look away.","Dai Li met those deep brown eyes, unafraid. \"He's already in this state. The worst that can happen is death. Why not try this folk remedy? Treat a dead horse as if it were still alive.\"","\"My lord, I have never heard of such an absurd thing,\" Ding Lianxi frowned.","Placing a dying man inside an ox's belly to save him? In his decades of medical practice, he had never heard of such a thing. This was sheer nonsense! Not only might the man still be lost, but a sturdy ox would be wasted too.","But Qin Shaozong said, \"Bring an ox here.\"","A soldier immediately went to carry out the order. The logistics corps had ample supplies, with no shortage of oxen and horses for transport. Soon, an ox was led over.","Qin Shaozong drew the ring-pommeled sword from his waist and personally sliced open the cow's belly. With a wet, sloshing sound, bright red blood immediately flowed out. Hu Bao swiftly cleared the cow's entrails, making space within the abdominal cavity.","When it was about ready, Mo Yanyun and another man lifted Qiao Wangfei together and placed him inside the cow's belly, leaving only his head exposed to breathe.","Ding Lianxi crouched beside the cow, his fingers pressed against Qiao Wangfei's neck, checking his pulse.","Everyone watched nervously, no one speaking, as if afraid that the sound of their voices might flatten out the faint beat of Commander Qiao's pulse.","Time flowed slowly by. No one left.","\"Huh?\" A high-pitched sound of confusion startled them all.","Their nerves felt plucked by an invisible hand. Before their hearts could fully leap into their throats, they heard Ding Lianxi exclaim in astonishment, \"C-Commander Qiao's pulse... it's stabilizing!\"","Normally, after losing so much blood, Qiao Wangfei should have already breathed his last. Yet now, a pulse remained. True, it was weak, but it was definitely palpable and gradually becoming steadier.","A miraculous cure, truly unbelievable!","Doctor Ding's exclamation was like a boulder dropped into a lake, immediately stirring up a wave of astonished murmurs around him.","\"Is it really true?\"","\"Heaven has eyes! This is wonderful, Commander Qiao can be saved!\"","...","Dai Li noticed the man beside her looking at her. She also turned her head and said seriously to Qin Shaozong, \"It's still too early to say he's out of danger. We must wait and see what happens next.\"","This dose of cold water was necessary because this \"abdominal packing therapy\" was something she had only read about in books.","It was said that Genghis Khan, the legendary conqueror, once had a beloved general who was gravely wounded and on the brink of death during a campaign against the Khitans. The Great Khan immediately ordered a live cow to be cut open, and the general was placed inside its belly, thereby evading the summons of the King of Hell.","This therapy was later recorded by Li Shizhen in the Compendium of Materia Medica: \"For the severely wounded, place them inside a freshly opened ox's belly; after some time, they will revive.\" 1","Reportedly, the principle was twofold. First, the freshly opened cow's belly was warm, and its abdominal cavity was largely a sterile environment.","Excessive blood loss causes a sharp drop in body temperature. At such a time, what is critically needed is a clean, warm furnace close to human body temperature to stabilize the wounded person's core temperature, preventing their body from consuming fat reserves on futile heat production.","Second, ox spine could be used medicinally; even applied externally, it was said to have the ability to staunch bleeding swiftly.","However, the above were merely cold words on a page. Whether it would actually work in practice, Dai Li had absolutely no certainty.","It truly was a case of treating a dead horse as if it were still alive.","Saving him would mean gaining a life. But if the treatment failed, it could only be considered a return to his destined fate.","Ding Lianxi looked at Dai Li, both excited and remorseful. \"This lady is...\"","He didn't know how to address her.","Dai Li introduced herself, \"Dai Li. 'Dai' as in the color of distant mountains, 'Li' as in dawn. You can just call me Dai Li.\"","Qin Shaozong's eyebrow twitched.","Feeling his superior's gaze sweep over, Ding Lianxi quickly lowered his eyes, avoiding looking directly at Dai Li. He bowed deeply to the woman before him. \"My ancestors practiced medicine for generations, and I myself have been a physician for thirty-five years. Yet today, I have learned that there is always someone greater, and skies beyond our own sky. I was disrespectful earlier. I beg Lady Dai not to hold it against me.\"","Dai Li hadn't expected such a formal gesture. She paused, then returned a slight curtsey. \"I merely happened to know some folk remedies. I hardly deserve the phrase 'skies beyond our sky'.\""]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30","paragraphs":["\"Thud-thud-thud—\"","The heavy sound of horse hooves piled upon one another, the kicked-up dust seeming to carry the momentum of a thousand troops.","The first batch of the Dark Cavalry had returned. This group consisted mainly of the wounded, rushing back to camp for urgent treatment after the battle. The remaining soldiers, with minor injuries or none at all, stayed behind to clear the battlefield.","Weapons were to be confiscated, horses to be rounded up, and as for the prisoners...","Those who surrendered would not be killed.","In ancient times, human labor was an extremely valuable resource. Prisoners could repair city walls, serve as beasts of burden plowing fields and growing grain, or, after being disciplined, be integrated into one's own army to bolster its strength.","Therefore, the victorious side generally did not execute surrendered soldiers.","Moreover, Li Zan was merely a salt smuggler who rose to power through wealth, having enjoyed only a few years of prestige without any true military spirit to speak of.","\"This battle annihilated over three thousand enemies, captured nearly five thousand prisoners—a great and complete victory!\" Feng Feng, commander of the Northern Garrison, returned with the first batch of soldiers and immediately proclaimed the battle achievements.","After announcing that, he urgently asked, \"Where's Old Qiao? Where is Old Qiao?!\"","Feng Feng had been one of the three who fought fiercely against Wang Qinglie, so he knew all too well the peril of that earlier clash. Had it not been for Old Qiao using himself as bait and feigning an opening, the outcome of the battle would have been uncertain.","They had all underestimated Wang Qinglie. His three-pointed glaive came with overwhelming force, not only breaking Old Qiao's blade but also cleaving downward through his armor. Fortunately, Yan San was quick-eyed and swift-handed, otherwise Old Qiao might have died on the spot.","Thinking of his friend's injuries, Feng Feng couldn't help but feel dejected. Even now, it seemed the situation wasn't much better...","\"Commander Feng, Commander Qiao is with Master Ding and Lady Dai,\" a soldier said.","Feng Feng, who had been about to go look for him, stopped. He was both puzzled and instinctively wary of this breach of protocol. \"Lady Dai? How can there be a woman in the army? Why is she here?\"","The soldier hurriedly explained, \"She was brought back by the Marquis. Just now, when Commander Qiao was sent back, Master Ding examined him and shook his head, saying it was beyond hope. It was Lady Dai who thought of a method to keep Commander Qiao's life hanging on.\"","The soldier's eyes shone with fervor.","Commander Qiao had one foot in the underworld, even Master Ding was helpless, yet Lady Dai had forcefully pulled him back. One must understand, what she saved was not just one life, but countless future \"Qiao Wangfeis.\"","If possible, who would want to see a comrade they were just chatting with yesterday die before their eyes?","Feng Feng stood there dumbfounded for a long moment, as if unable to comprehend the words, before finally sprinting off in a certain direction.","Never mind why she appeared in the army; being able to save Old Qiao was the absolute best news!","Feng Feng ran like the wind to the infirmary tent but was barred from entering, stopped by the reason that \"the tent needs to maintain clean air; idlers keep out.\"","Also waiting outside were Mo Yanyun and a few others.","Since he couldn't go in, he inquired from those outside. Feng Feng asked Mo Yanyun, \"Old Mo, where did the Marquis find this divine female physician? Her medical skills are actually this superb.\"","Who knew that upon hearing this, Mo Yanyun turned with a complicated expression.","\"What's with that look? Is the matter of the divine female physician not to be spoken of?\" Feng Feng was confused.","\"...That's not it.\" Mo Yanyun suddenly asked, \"Didn't Yan San tell you?\"","Feng Feng reflexively countered, \"Tell me what?\"","Mo Yanyun muttered, \"Right, Yan San has always been a man of few words and never gossips. It's normal he didn't tell you.\"","Feng Feng grew anxious, scratching his head and ears. \"Then hurry up and give me the details. Where exactly did this divine female physician come from? I need to find a way to get on good terms with her. She might save my life someday.\"","\"She's the one the Marquis captured from Taiping County,\" Mo Yanyun said in a low voice.","Feng Feng froze, feeling as if his brain had been struck by a heavy hammer, as though something had been overturned.","Yan San indeed disliked gossip, but those who stayed behind at the Jiang residence weren't just him; there were a few other Dark Cavalry soldiers.","Feng Feng vaguely knew the Marquis's trip to Taiping County was ostensibly because of a young woman, though the specifics were unknown to him. He couldn't connect a seductive concubine who served with her looks to the divine female physician who saved his friend from mortal peril.","Mo Yanyun patted his shoulder, his expression still complex. \"This Lady Dai is no ordinary person. Privately, I believe she has extraordinary abilities. You'll understand later.\"","Being able to \"extinguish the fire\" of the enraged Marquis—wasn't that an extraordinary ability? At the very least, in all these years, he had never seen anyone who could stroke the tiger's whiskers, even slip away from the Marquis a few times, and still remain completely unharmed.","Inside the medical tent.","Originally sealed up like a cocoon, the medical tent now had windows opened as per Dai Li's request, maintaining air circulation as much as possible.","The cow wrapped around Qiao Wangfei had been moved here. Dai Li and Ding Lianxi were discussing the matter of suturing.","Surgical procedures had already appeared in this era. The Book of the Later Han: Biography of Hua Tuo records: \"If an illness arises and knots within, where needles and medicine cannot reach, then first have the patient drink the Mafeisan powder with wine. Once intoxicated and unconscious, cut open the abdomen or back, and remove the accumulated mass.\"","This means when acupuncture and medicine are ineffective, one must anesthetize, then open the abdomen or back, and excise the tumor.","But surgery rests on three cornerstones: antisepsis, anesthesia, and hemostasis.","Antisepsis means sterility. One must ensure a clean environment, preventing the weakened patient with an open wound from getting infected. This single requirement alone is extremely difficult to fulfill. Fumigating the room with mugwort, clove, and other plants is possible, but how can one guarantee complete sterilization?","Ancient times lacked antibiotics. Post-operative infection mortality rates were extremely high, essentially like sending your name ahead to the underworld, just waiting for the person to arrive.","Therefore, surgical procedures in this era were undoubtedly rare, a type even the most elite masters at the pyramid's peak would not lightly attempt.","Ding Lianxi was a military physician, so his chances of performing surgery were far higher than others in the medical field. Yet now, facing the severely injured Qiao Wangfei, he had no confidence at all.","Earlier, he had roughly examined him. Qiao Wangfei's wound was massive, almost cleaving him open from the collarbone down to the middle of his abdomen.","\"We need to clean the wound and then suture it closed,\" Dai Li said, standing at the tent entrance, not getting too close to Qiao Wangfei.","How dirty blades were—covered in mud, stained with others' blood, perhaps even crawled over by insects. If debridement wasn't done, even if Qiao Wangfei's life was hanging on now, he would definitely die from infection.","Ding Lianxi instinctively frowned, thinking it dangerous to reopen the wound now that the bleeding had finally stopped. Nevertheless, he said, \"Then let's wash the wound. Xiao Li, go fetch charcoal to boil water.\"","\"We also need salt. Go get some salt from the kitchen troops on the way, and bring another cow,\" Dai Li added.","Ding Lianxi was surprised. \"Why do we need salt?\"","Dai Li fell silent.","How to explain that she wanted to make saline solution? Normal saline has a concentration similar to human extracellular fluid, making it perfectly suitable for wound cleaning.","In this era, distillation technology had not yet emerged, so there was no purified water, and strictly speaking, it was impossible to prepare a proper saline solution. Using salt water with impurities to clean wounds carried certain safety risks.","But as the saying goes, desperate times call for desperate measures. Qiao Wangfei was at death's door anyway; he couldn't be worse off, so it was worth a try.","\"It's another folk remedy,\" a deep male voice remarked. It was Qin Shaozong, who had been standing at the entrance of the military tent with Dai Li and had remained silent until now.","Ding Lianxi's lips moved, but in the end, he asked no further questions.","While the soldier was off boiling water and fetching salt, Ding Lianxi prepared the items needed for \"suturing the abdominal wound with medicinal paste\": silk thread and medicinal ointment. The former was for stitching the wound, the latter for accelerating its healing.","Dai Li picked up the silk thread, hesitating to speak.","Ding Lianxi was now paying extra attention to Lady Dai's every move. Seeing her expression, he promptly asked, \"Lady Dai, is there something unsuitable about this silk thread?\"","Two pairs of eyes fell upon her. One was eager, thirsting for knowledge; the other was obscure and unfathomable, like a vast sea on an overcast day, holding an impenetrable darkness.","Dai Li turned her head, meeting those brown eyes directly without flinching.","If before her monthly courses had arrived, she had been apprehensive of this man, thinking Qin Shaozong was a man-eating tiger that left no bones behind, and that she might be devoured by him if she let her guard down for a moment...","During the days of her courses, she had stayed within the temporary enclosure. Outside, that very tiger had paced back and forth, watching her with a covetous gaze.","And now, as the fence was about to be dismantled, she felt not a trace of panic. Because she believed she might have found a muzzle, something that could keep this greedy tiger from opening its jaws at her.","A smile curled on Dai Li's red lips. Although her words were for Ding Lianxi, she didn't look at him. \"Master Ding, have you ever considered using mulberry bark thread instead of silk thread?\"","Ding Lianxi was stunned, murmuring, \"Mulberry bark thread?\"","Mulberry bark paper already existed in this era. This type of paper, highly absorbent and resistant to insect damage, was highly favored by calligraphers.","Dai Li continued, \"Mulberry bark has medicinal properties for clearing heat, detoxifying, and promoting wound healing. Using it to suture wounds is not only beneficial for the body, but because the mulberry bark thread can fuse with flesh and blood, there's no need for later stitch removal. It's truly achieving twice the result with half the effort.\"","When Dai Li mentioned the medicinal efficacy of mulberry bark, the corner of Ding Lianxi's mouth began to tremble uncontrollably. With each sentence she spoke, the light in his eyes grew brighter. Finally, he sighed in admiration, \"Marvelous! Lady Dai is truly knowledgeable and well-traveled. I am filled with admiration. This mulberry bark thread should indeed replace silk thread!\"","Dai Li smiled without replying.","Just as Shennong, the legendary founder of herbal medicine, once identified herbs by tasting hundreds of plants, leading to the discovery of various medicinal herbs, every profession develops through a process of exploration. She was merely standing at the later end of the long river of history, looking back to inform her predecessors of certain outcomes.","Ding Lianxi was extremely excited, wishing he could immediately make mulberry bark thread and use it on the wounded. Immersed in his own thoughts, he failed to notice the undercurrents swirling within the tent.","Across the distance, the two of them locked eyes, neither looking away. Qin Shaozong watched the slow curl of her red lips, realizing that her deeply hidden defiance was surfacing again.","Well, this cunning fox was up to her tricks again.","The soldier was quick, soon returning with the required items.","After Dai Li estimated the proportions and prepared the salt water, she handed everything over to Ding Lianxi. She was merely an armchair strategist; the actual cleaning of the wound was something she couldn't do at all.","Moreover, Master Ding probably hadn't realized that from the very beginning until now, she had never taken a close look at Qiao Wangfei's injury. It was too bloody, the wound too large; she couldn't quite bear to see it.","After a great deal of busy work, and later changing the dressing for Qiao Wangfei, everything was finally finished. Ding Lianxi let out a long breath and looked at Dai Li again. \"Lady Dai, what should be done next?\"","Dai Li thought for a moment. \"Keep the area ventilated. The clove and mugwort incense must burn without interruption. If Battalion Commander Qiao wakes up and says he's thirsty, don't let him drink too much water. At most, just moisten his lips.\"","Someone who has just suffered major blood loss should not consume large amounts of water. Excessive fluid intake can lead to a drop in blood volume and, if one is not careful, cause heart failure.","The admiration in Ding Lianxi's eyes grew even stronger.","Regarding not immediately replenishing fluids after major blood loss, he actually knew this point.","How did he know?","Learned through the tragic cost of soldiers' lives.","Without having treated large numbers of wounded soldiers, for her to know this point likely meant only one thing—","Knowledge passed down through generations.","It seemed this Lady Dai was likely like him, coming from a family with generations of medical practice. However, unlike the widespread fame of his Ding family, her family practiced medicine to aid the world without seeking reputation, possessing true integrity.","Ding Lianxi felt a desire to exchange knowledge with a fellow practitioner. \"Lady Dai, I wonder when you might have time. I would like to—\"","\"She has no free time recently,\" someone interjected abruptly.","\"My lord,\" Ding Lianxi called out disapprovingly.","Qin Shaozong looked at Dai Li and simply led her away. \"My lady, there is no further use for you here in the tent. Come with me.\"","This Ding Lianxi was already becoming dim-sighted at such an early age, actually mistaking her for a physician. Pray tell, where in this world is there a healer who dares not even look directly at a soldier's wound?","Indeed, there was no use for her here. She couldn't help with anything else, and staying would only be in the way. Dai Li followed Qin Shaozong out.","All the Xuanxiao Cavalry had returned to the camp. Today was a day of triumphant return, and the atmosphere in the camp was fervent and jubilant. The army cooks, having received military orders, were enthusiastically sharpening their knives, generously slaughtering sheep and boiling meat to celebrate the great victory.","The news that Qiao Wangfei, hanging by a thread between life and death, had been pulled back from the gates of the underworld also spread through the entire camp like a whirlwind. From battalion commanders to common soldiers, everyone knew that a miraculous female physician had arrived in their army.","As the sun set in the west, the aroma of meat and dishes gradually wafted through the camp. Dai Li and Qin Shaozong walked side by side through the camp, their shadows stretched long by the orange-yellow sunset, one tall, one shorter, not far apart, like two trees standing close together.","At first, neither spoke, until Qin Shaozong broke the silence.","\"What are you plotting?\" His voice was very calm, betraying no emotional fluctuation.","Hearing this, Dai Li paused, turning to look at him. Those captivating, watery eyes curved slightly, their long, straight lashes catching the brilliant, shattered gold of the sunset, like a beautiful little fan.","Alright then. Since he had taken the initiative to broach the subject, she would seize the opportunity to speak.","\"If that Battalion Commander Qiao survives, would it count as me saving his life?\" Dai Li asked softly.","\"Yes.\" His answer held no hesitation.","Dai Li asked again, her tone light and cheerful, \"The Marquis's army must have regulations for rewarding merit, right?\"","They both knew perfectly well this was a completely superfluous question. Qin Shaozong glanced at her sideways. The half of his face not touched by the sunset appeared exceptionally stern and imposing. \"Without rules, nothing can be accomplished. Where there are laws to reduce crimes, naturally there are also rewards for merit.\"","\"The Marquis speaks most wisely.\" The smile in Dai Li's eyes deepened a little. \"I hope Battalion Commander Qiao can overcome this danger. That way, I can claim a reward from you for this along with submitting the folk remedy.\"","Now that they were alone, Qin Shaozong had no need for pretense. \"Was it truly a folk remedy?\"","\"Actually, not entirely. This method was recorded in an ancient text from my family's collection. As for its authenticity...\" Dai Li answered honestly, \"Just as I said at the time, Commander Qiao's condition couldn't be worse, facing certain death. It was worth trying, a case of treating a dead horse as if it were still alive.\"","Unconsciously, Dai Li followed him to the front of the main tent.","The main tent was distinctly different from the other military tents in scale. It was larger and more towering, standing firmly in the Xuanxiao Cavalry camp like an immovable pillar. The small flag atop its peak and the army's main standard were both whipped into sharp arcs by the wind.","In front of the main tent, low tables were arranged in opposing rows. In the center stood a large cauldron and a wooden-frame fire pit, over which half a sheep, impaled by an iron halberd, was roasting.","The sheep had clearly been cooking for some time, its surface already a mouth-watering golden brown. Hot fat dripped from within, gathering and falling into the flames below. The fire's tongues licked it up and, as if crying out in pleasure, flared up with a satisfying sizzle.","Such fire pits roasting sheep were not few. From where Dai Li stood, she could see at least two sheep-roasting fires in front of each tent.","Judging by the setup, a victory feast was about to begin.","The sun had completely sunk below the horizon, leaving only a barely perceptible pale light in the sky. Night surged in like a tide, bringing deep, silent darkness. Yet here, in a certain part of Peach Blossom Ridge beneath the vast sky, patches of firelight connected, creating a scene of extraordinary bustle and continuous laughter and chatter.","For ease of transport, the army mostly used long, narrow tables. Two or even three people shared one, crowding together for meals.","Dai Li sat beside Qin Shaozong, sharing his long table. As the commander's table, their fare was undeniably sumptuous—fine dishes and good meat. Dai Li even spotted a small plate of wild berries.","During forced marches, they typically ate dry, hardened rations that required no heating, just hard chewing, for convenience. But during ordinary marches, the frequency of eating such rations wasn't particularly high. The army usually ate rice porridge, wheat grain meals, and occasionally flour paste mixed with various wild vegetables.","Like now, a bowl of wheat grain meal sat before Dai Li. In this era, wheat meal was made from steamed, unhusked wheat grains. As for the texture...","Dai Li, eating it for the first time, chewed thoughtfully. Well, it wasn't especially unpleasant; it felt rather novel.","The sheep was ready. The military officers, with their rough and unrestrained style, directly cut off large chunks of mutton with their short knives, each piece larger than a palm. With a thud, they were tossed onto the tables lined with broad leaves, to be eaten by hand.","The mutton was shared, everyone receiving a portion. Dai Li also got a piece.","Her table was occupied by high-ranking officers. The one who had just distributed the meat was Feng Feng. Whether he was specially thanking her for saving his long-time friend or trying to build good relations with Dai Li, Feng Feng's goodwill at this moment was particularly obvious. This was specifically demonstrated by the piece of mutton he gave Dai Li, which was twice the size of her face.","Dai Li: \"...\"","\"Lady Dai, eat your fill. If it's not enough, just say the word, and I'll cut you more.\" Feng Feng grinned, showing a row of white teeth.","Dai Li: \"...Thank you, but that likely won't be necessary.\"","Marching and fighting were physically demanding work. The officers devoured their meat ravenously. Though Dai Li hadn't been on the battlefield, she had walked many mountain paths today and was now quite hungry.","The whole piece of mutton was too large. She took out her short dagger, carefully wiped it first, then held the knife in one hand while using the other to roll up a corner of the broad leaf, wrapping it back over the mutton to press it down without dirtying her hands, before she began to cut.","The polished surface of the dagger reflected the firelight, appearing brilliantly bright from a certain angle. Dai Li was wholly focused on cutting the meat and didn't notice the man beside her glancing at her several times.","That glint of light kept catching the corner of his eye, flickering back and forth, irritating Qin Shaozong.","Such a small piece of meat, and she could fuss over it for so long. Anyone else would have finished eating, woken from a nap, and started on a second meal before she was done with that wretched piece.","\"Bring it here.\"","Dai Li didn't initially realize Qin Shaozong was speaking to her, until he called again, \"Lady.\"","Dai Li turned to look at him, her eyes carrying a hint of confusion. But after meeting his gaze and seeing it shift downward to glance at the mutton in her hands, she recalled his earlier words and suddenly understood his meaning.","Pinching a corner of the broad leaf, Dai Li pulled the \"tray,\" moving the mutton in front of Qin Shaozong.","Qin Shaozong picked up his knife, ready to cut, when he suddenly heard a soft, feminine voice drift over. \"Could you... perhaps use my knife to cut it?\"","Immediately after, as if presenting an offering, a short dagger, handle-first, tentatively and slowly intruded into the edge of his vision from the side.","Qin Shaozong paused, his expression darkening slightly.","Did she think his knife wasn't clean enough? She might as well be spoiled to death."]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31","paragraphs":["After changing knives, Qin Shaozong remained in a low mood throughout, and Daili didn't dare provoke him further.","Once he had deftly finished cutting the meat, Daili smiled and offered a flattering remark, \"How impressive, my lord,\" before once again pinching the edge of the \"tray\" and pulling the meat back in front of herself.","Qin Shaozong lowered his gaze, watching that piece of mutton slink away, before finally turning his head to speak with the other military officers.","The original piece of mutton, twice the size of Daili's face, had been sliced into strips about two fingers thick. Qin Shaozong's knife skills and eye were excellent; each strip was almost exactly the same width, a sight that would soothe any perfectionist.","Daili picked up a strip with her wooden chopsticks, took a bite, and then paused.","The roasted mutton smelled wonderful, its aroma insistently drilling into her nostrils. But when she actually tasted it, she found she couldn't ignore the gamey flavor.","Perhaps there weren't enough seasonings, or perhaps it was roasted directly without prior marination. In any case, it was quite different from the completely gameless mutton she'd eaten in restaurants in the past.","But she had already taken this first bite; she couldn't just throw it away. Military rations were precious, and meat was especially hard to come by. It was only for celebrating a victory that they were roasting a lamb now. Under normal circumstances, that single bite of hers would be the stuff of many soldiers' dreams.","The guilt of wasting food weighed on her like a mountain. Staring at the two-finger-thick strip of meat, Daili began to coax herself.","It's pure, natural mutton, slaughtered and roasted fresh, with no chemical additives. It's free, doesn't cost me any silver. Meat is precious in this era, who knows when the next chance to eat it will be. Eat more, it'll give you more strength for the next escape attempt!","Yuck...","She took a small bite of mutton, ate two wild berries, followed with two mouthfuls of wheat rice, a sip of rice porridge, and then circled back to take another bite of mutton.","When that strip of meat was finally finished, Daili let out a long sigh, feeling as if she'd just survived a minor ordeal.","Looking at the remaining large plate of mutton, Daili felt a headache coming on. One strip was bad enough; there was no way she could finish the rest.","What should she do?","Daili first frowned, then her gaze gradually drifted to the side.","At that moment, Qin Shaozong was speaking with Feng Feng and a few others.","\"What a triumph! After this battle, in a few days when we march on Ying County, breaching its gates and capturing Li Zan alive will be as easy as picking something up.\"","\"Li Zan's power is broken. Would he abandon Ying County and flee? But even if he escapes, it's fine as long as he leaves all his family wealth behind.\"","\"Ha! He might want to take it, but could he?\"","\"True. Even with three heads and six arms, he'd have no hope of taking those things with him.\"","Everyone was in high spirits. What this great victory meant was clear to all the military officers present.","Li Zan's main force had been eliminated, along with Wang Qinglie, who had protected him since the very beginning of his rise. It could be said that Li Zan had now lost both his elite troops and his top generals.","The Ying County he occupied had become a hollow shell. Not just their own Xuanxiao Cavalry, but even if the Marquis sent other armies under his command, they could easily smash open Ying County's gates.","With Li Zan dead, his salt stores and the large salt lake near Ying County would belong to them.","Yes, the reason the Marquis had decided to personally lead the army to suppress this salt smuggler wasn't just because Li Zan was a scourge harming the people, and eliminating him would bring prestige. Nor was it solely because the other's growing power posed some threat.","What their Marquis had his eye on was the salt itself.","Yes, the salt itself, not the silver to be made from selling it.","Ever since pacifying the northern territories, they had acquired large numbers of high-quality Mongolian horses from the region. Mongolian horses were muscular, had excellent endurance, and could withstand both heat and hunger.","They were fine horses, but raising them was exceedingly expensive. Fodder was a major cost, and so was salt.","Each fine steed needed to eat over half a sheng of salt daily. Salt wasn't cheap to begin with, and their needs were vast. If they had to purchase it all from others, it would be another staggering expense.","Don't be fooled by their Marquis's current position, holding the northern territories, being immensely influential, practically the uncrowned king of the north. If you looked closely, every single internal expense was shockingly large.","Soldier (and fallen soldier) stipends, battlefield and siege rewards, provisions (for both soldiers and warhorses), weapon depreciation, city repairs...","The provisions category alone was calculated as a daily expenditure.","Well, no wonder that miser Jin Duole was always crying poor.","\"But speaking of which,\" Feng Feng said, finishing a piece of mutton and reaching for another, \"if Li Zan does run, it's hard to say if he'll find shelter anywhere. We've just made a big show of crushing him. If he runs to someone else's doorstep, who would dare take him in?\"","\"Perhaps someone would.\"","These three words caused a momentary silence around them. Everyone looked at Qin Shaozong.","Qin Shaozong continued, \"Fan Tianshi, Fan of Yanzhou, has always had an ambiguous relationship with the White Lotus Sect. The speed of Li Zan's rise these past few years is somewhat unusual. Perhaps there's more to it.\"","A private salt smuggler, amassing a claimed army of a hundred thousand in just a few short years, and corrupting officials in the surrounding commanderies with himself at the center—that certainly suggested some capability.","Many of those around him voiced agreement.","Just as Qin Shaozong was about to say more, the corner of his eye caught a dark mass slowly inching closer, with the same sneaky demeanor as its owner earlier.","He turned his head and, sure enough, saw her holding a plate of mutton with both hands. The firelight from the bonfire reflected in her eyes, casting fine, sparkling lights in those clear peach-blossom eyes, like scattered stars from the sky.","She looked much more obedient now than before.","Qin Shaozong asked, \"What is it?\"","His gaze swept downward. Although the meat had been rearranged, judging by its outline, he could still tell one piece was missing.","The piece from the very center, the most tenderly roasted one.","Daili said with a serious expression, \"Leading an army strains both mind and body. You've been rushing about all day today, so you should eat more meat. Battalion Commander Feng's roasting skills are unparalleled. After tasting it, the flavor lingers, and I noticed your plate was empty. So I thought to offer you this portion first, to save you the trip of getting up.\"","Seeing the surrounding officers wolfing down their food, looking as if they wished they could chew and swallow the very bones, Daili felt her line about \"unparalleled roasting skills\" should be quite credible.","Qin Shaozong raised a long eyebrow. \"Why is my lady being so unusually attentive tonight?\"","Daili pressed her lips together in an ingratiating smile. \"Military discipline is strict. I imagine I'll mostly be staying alone somewhere tonight. I'm just borrowing flowers to offer to Buddha, trying to curry favor so you might assign me a slightly better tent.\"","Qin Shaozong's eyes slid downward again.","Although a piece was missing, the meat was arranged neatly. In the corner, she had even placed two wild berries for a pop of color, making the presentation brighter and more appealing than before.","She had put in some effort.","The corner of Qin Shaozong's mouth lifted. \"Fine. Put it down.\"","Daili's heart leapt with joy. She hurriedly placed the mutton before him. Worried he might forget about it while talking, she specifically positioned it directly in front of him, ensuring it would be within his line of sight at all times.","With this major concern off her mind, Daili went back to eating her wild berries.","The wild strawberries of this era were no different from those of later times—small, bright red, spherical fruits. A single bite released a sweet and sour juice, quite effective at cutting through greasiness.","Unconsciously, all the wild strawberries on the long table had found their way into her stomach, except for...","the two used to garnish the mutton.","Daili's gaze drifted over. She noticed that while she had been busy eating the strawberries, the mutton that had given her such a headache had been nearly finished by him. Looking around at the group of military officers, each had also polished off at least two or three large pieces of meat.","Daili: \"...\"","Just then, someone asked, \"My Lord, would you care for more meat?\"","\"Cut another piece.\" Qin Shaozong paused, glanced sideways at Daili beside him, and amended his order, \"Make it two pieces.\"","Daili had just finished her meal and was listening to their conversation, so she naturally didn't miss any movement beside her.","When the gaze from the person next to her swept over, internal alarm bells immediately started ringing. The shadow cast by that earlier piece of mutton was so large that Daili instinctively said, \"Not for me, I'm full.\"","Qin Shaozong, who had been about to look away, stopped.","His amber eyes appeared even lighter in the firelight, increasingly resembling those of a large carnivorous feline. His expressionless stare carried a heavy, oppressive weight that made one's courage falter.","Daili was already feeling guilty inside. She couldn't hold this gaze and involuntarily averted her eyes.","He was all too familiar with this little mannerism of hers; it was a sure sign she had done something mischievous. Qin Shaozong narrowed his long, narrow eyes slightly, his gaze shifting from Daili to the low table before him.","The wheat paste seemed untouched, but the millet rice and wild strawberries were completely gone.","The memory of the earlier scene resurfaced.","Her smiling face as she offered the mutton; the long table before her laden with many bowls; the now-empty bowl that had held the millet rice; the small pottery jar still full of paste; the soup bowl with slightly less rice porridge; the plate piled high with wild strawberries.","And now, aside from the small plate for the strawberries being empty, everything else perfectly matched his memory.","Well, well. So this little fox had already been full earlier. She couldn't finish the rest and had thus found a way to pawn it off on him. All that talk about how he, having taxed his mind and spirit, ought to eat more meat—it sounded better than a song.","Qin Shaozong let out a cold chuckle.","Daili kept her eyes downcast, feigning deep contemplation of her own nose and heart.","\"My Lord?\" Feng Feng hesitated.","So, was it one piece of meat or two?","\"One piece is sufficient,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Daili breathed a sigh of relief.","Qin Shaozong teased, \"If you don't eat now, don't go crying about being hungry in the middle of the night. You could shout yourself hoarse and no one will pay you any mind.\"","Doesn't care for meat, just loves to snack on useless wild fruits. Put a house cat on the table and it would probably eat more than her.","Daili certainly wasn't hungry. A bowl of millet rice, half a bowl of rice porridge, a substantial piece of mutton, plus a good number of wild strawberries were more than enough to fill her.","After the bonfire feast, Daili was allotted a small tent. Military tents were divided into small and medium sizes. The former slept a few people and were usually for high-ranking officers; the latter could accommodate dozens and mostly housed common soldiers.","As the only woman in the army, Daili naturally got a small tent to herself. The small tent was pitched, its flap rolled up for ventilation, and some mugwort and cloves were burned to mask the odors.","Once these tasks were done, Daili hugged her quilt, climbed onto the soft couch, and blissfully drifted into dreamland.","The deep night was silent, all things hushed. This newly pitched small military tent, situated next to the commander's tent, bore witness to the moon's rise and fall upon the vast earth.","After resting and reorganizing the army for a night at Peach Blossom Ridge, the Xuanxiao Cavalry set out again the next morning, continuing eastward towards the location of Ying Commandery.","Compared to before, the presence of wounded and prisoners slowed the Xuanxiao Cavalry's pace somewhat. However, Peach Blossom Ridge was already quite close to Ying Commandery, so merely two days later, the army arrived in the vicinity.","When they were still about seven li from Ying Commandery, Qin Shaozong ordered the establishment of a camp and dispatched a squad of scouts.","The swift scouts rode off like shooting stars, heading straight for Ying Commandery.","A distance of only seven li meant the scouts went and returned quickly, bringing back heartening news.","It seemed Li Zan had abandoned the city and fled.","Normally, armies wouldn't be stationed inside a city or commandery. Firstly, there weren't enough houses to accommodate these outsiders; secondly, it was difficult for unified management and military orders to be effectively conveyed.","Therefore, military camps were mostly set up in the outskirts beside cities. During non-combat periods, many powerful lords would have their soldiers turn into farmer-soldiers, reclaiming land and growing grain to reduce provisions expenditure—this was the famous Tuntian system (garrison farming).","Logically, since they had already killed their way to the gates of Ying Commandery, just shy of battering down the city gates, the opposing side should be sharpening their weapons and preparing for battle.","But in fact, the opposite was true. The scouts reported seeing scattered soldiers deserting from the military camp, some alone, some in groups, some carrying large and small bundles on their backs.","Deserters!","Deserters had appeared in the enemy army.","\"Hahaha, excellent, excellent! Well done deserting! Their morale declines before the battle even begins; they are surely doomed to defeat. It seems that salt-smuggler surnamed Li was scared out of his wits last time at Peach Blossom Ridge.\"","\"Escaping the tiger's jaws, only to have his left and right arms bitten off—is it any wonder he's scared stiff? Probably as soon as he returned to Ying Commandery, this Li Zan packed his bags, gathered his wife and children, and chose flight as the best strategy.\"","\"My Lord, I request permission to lead the attack on the city!\"","\"My Lord, I also...\"","While the commander's tent was abuzz like a roaring fire, at the other end of the camp, inside the medical tent, spirits were also high.","Whether it was Qiao Wangfei's exceptionally strong will to live or thanks to his robust physique honed through daily training, after a little over two days of care, this Xuanxiao Cavalry platoon leader who had been cut open had narrowly and perilously passed the most dangerous period, snatching his life back from the jaws of death.","During her daily visit, Daili saw Qiao Wangfei sitting on a straw mat spread on the ground, eating meat paste.","\"Madam Daili.\" Upon seeing Daili, Qiao Wangfei instinctively tried to stand up.","Daili was startled and quickly said, \"Stay seated, don't move recklessly. You mustn't tear your wound open.\"","Qiao Wangfei regained consciousness yesterday. After learning from the medics how he had miraculously survived, he expressed profuse gratitude to Daili during her visit. Earlier, when he knew his situation was dire, he had even entrusted the care of his children to a friend. He had never expected to encounter a noble person who would help him turn danger into safety.","He figured his ancestors in the underworld must have kowtowed one by one to invite a great immortal down to save him.","Qiao Wangfei held a touch of awe for Daili that others couldn't match.","\"How are you feeling today, Platoon Leader Qiao?\" Daili asked.","Qiao Wangfei: \"Much better.\"","Daili carefully observed his complexion. His face was still as pale as gold paper, but he looked more spirited than yesterday.","Able to eat, drink, and sleep, Qiao Wangfei was indeed gradually improving.","Daili felt genuinely happy, not only because a life had been saved, but also because a living Qiao Wangfei represented \"merit.\" She needed to use this merit to seek a reward from a certain someone.","\"Woo—— Woo——\" The ox horn horns sounded their mournful blasts, spreading to every corner of the camp.","Qiao Wangfei knew immediately what it meant upon hearing it. \"The assembly horn is sounding. They're setting out for battle.\"","He pondered briefly, then laughed. \"With morale at its peak, how can we not hold the winning ticket!\"","Daili had no experience in warfare, but even she felt that Ying County could be taken quickly. By pressing the advantage and striking while the iron was hot, they could secure a great chance of victory.","Just as the two of them had guessed, the expedition led personally by Qin Shaozong soon returned triumphant. Moreover, the speed at which Ying County was captured was much faster than Daili had imagined.","He had led the troops out at mid-morning, and by noon, a swift rider from the Black Cavalry had returned with news for the logistics troops to break camp and advance. It was said that Ying County had been taken, and they now needed to set up camp in a new location.","Morale in the army was high. With a great bustle, they packed their belongings, struck camp, and set off.","Daili sat in an open-top carriage, watching the distant city walls draw nearer.","The ancient city was bathed in sunlight, appearing remote and weathered. Carrion birds circled ceaselessly in the sky beside it, yet the plants and trees along the official road flourished, creating a fractured yet eerily harmonious scene.","The soldiers guarding Ying County's walls had long been replaced by the Black Cavalry. After the military camp was set up outside the suburbs, Daili entered the city by carriage along with Qiao Wangfei, Su Xiuzhu, and others.","Ying County had no governor, or rather, it once did. Since Li Zan occupied this place, officials had been killed, surrendered, or some had resigned and left.","Thus, over the years, the civilian officials in Ying County had largely overlapped with the military officers in Li Zan's army. Now that Li Zan had been defeated and fled with his remaining forces, Ying County's officials were almost entirely swept away with him, even their mansions vacated.","Daili's open carriage drove into the former residence of the former governor, the former residence of the Grand Marshal of All Under Heaven.","Within the mansion, halls were resplendent, towers and pavilions were scattered throughout. There were grotesque rocks arranged as ornamental hills, and square springs channeled to form ponds. A nine-bend corridor arched over a pond, its carved pillars made of white marble. The opulence within was beyond description.","Daili's carriage proceeded unimpeded all the way to the main courtyard of the central residence. The main courtyard had clearly been cleaned up; not a single person from the former household remained, not even any maidservants.","\"Lady Dai, a group of maidservants will be sent later. Please select a couple who are to your liking,\" said Hu Bao.","Daili's first reaction was to refuse. \"I don't need maidservants. I've always been self-reliant in the past and am long accustomed to it. I don't require anyone to serve me.\"","Staying with Qin Shaozong was merely a temporary arrangement; she was certain she would leave eventually. If she grew attached to a maidservant, should she take the girl with her when she left or not?","Taking her might cause inconvenience for Daili herself; but if she didn't, given Qin Shaozong's domineering nature, it would likely cost the girl her life.","Hu Bao said solemnly, \"This is the Lord Marquis's order.\"","Daili also said sternly, \"I don't care, I—\"","\"What does my lady not care about?\"","Daili paused and turned to look towards the arched gate connecting the courtyard to the outside. There, having changed out of his armor and back into his black robes, Qin Shaozong entered from outside.","He was truly tall. Passing through the gate, there was little space left above his head. His entrance seemed to shrink the courtyard itself, his authority felt even without a display of anger.","\"Lady Dai, you may discuss this with the Lord Marquis,\" Hu Bao said, cupping his hands and quickly taking his leave.","Daili: \"...\"","Fine, discussing it with him it is. Might as well bring up my reward at the same time.","Daili turned to meet those amber eyes. Though the sunlight was bright at this moment, she seemed to see within them a deep, dark sea—not calm, but churning with a desire that grew deeper by the day.","The battle had reached a pause; the army's prohibition on women was no longer in effect."]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32","paragraphs":["After Hu Bao left, the courtyard fell quiet.","A phoenix tree grew in the yard. A breeze passed by, gently swaying its branches and leaves, making the dappled shadows cast on the ground dance along. The sky was clear, the air fresh, and the sun bright—today was a pleasant, heart-easing day.","Dai Li steadied her nerves and decided to lay some groundwork. \"Congratulations, my lord, on another great victory and capturing Ying County.\"","Qin Shaozong strode towards the house. \"Around the hour of Shen, a group of maidservants will be delivered. Pick two to keep by your side.\"","Dai Li followed him. \"My lord, regarding the maidservants, I thank you, but I do not need anyone to attend to me.\"","\"Why not?\" Qin Shaozong sat down by the low table after entering the room, struck a flint to light the charcoal, and began to boil water.","Dai Li took a seat opposite him. \"I'm not accustomed to it. In my past life at home, I did not have maidservants waiting on me.\"","She had bought various machines to do the work instead. A dishwasher, a dryer, a robot vacuum, and a smart home assistant... hiring a cleaning lady every weekend on top of that. It was a different kind of liberation for one's hands.","\"If you weren't accustomed to it before, then learn to be accustomed now,\" Qin Shaozong raised his eyes, their depths dark and inscrutable. \"Or is it that my lady feels having two extra pairs of eyes on you would make certain... little maneuvers inconvenient?\"","Dai Li's hands on her knees involuntarily curled. This man was always so sharp. Of course, she couldn't admit to what Qin Shaozong implied. \"My lord wrongs me greatly. I harbor no such thoughts. You previously said merits would be rewarded. Now that Commander Qiao is out of danger, I am eager to claim my reward. Why would I stir up other troubles?\"","This was the second time she had brought up claiming a reward. Unlike the last time's glancing mention, Dai Li was determined to make it concrete this time.","The groundwork had been laid, the stage set, and Qiao Wangfei's condition had indeed stabilized. This was the perfect moment. If she didn't bring it up now, it would only become harder later.","A corner of Qin Shaozong's mouth suddenly hooked up. \"Very well, then let's reward merit. My lady has rendered service in saving a life. Your reward: ten warhorses, five treasure chests, two maidservants, and three prosperous shopfronts. The deeds for the shops will be given to you after we return to Fuyang.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","He didn't ask what she wanted but gave directly. This was something Dai Li hadn't anticipated, but upon reflection, it fit his style perfectly.","He had likely guessed.","Dai Li decided to be direct. \"I do not want those four things you mentioned. I want something else. What I seek requires no expense from you. Considering that Commander Qiao has rushed about on your orders and risked life and limb for you, would you, my lord, permit me to exchange this merit for what I desire?\"","First, state that what she wants is of little value—equivalent to trading a high price for a low one, which benefits the other party. Then, invoke the life-saving favor for Qiao Wangfei to apply moral pressure.","See, I saved a subordinate who goes through fire and water for you, a subordinate who was indispensable in slaying Wang Qinglie in the last campaign. For his sake, you should agree to my not-too-excessive little request, right?","Qin Shaozong watched her, her eyes sparkling with a hint of a smile, as if he could see a fluffy big tail wagging behind her.","Hah, she's starting to brew mischief again.","Qin Shaozong didn't address her statement. Instead, he said with a faint, ambiguous smile, \"My lady might care to guess: how tall is the grass on the graves of those who previously deceived me?\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","He actually chose this critical moment to bring up old grievances.","Seeing her silence, Qin Shaozong began counting them off for her, one by one. \"Your background and history are fabricated, your menstrual cycle was a fabrication, the timing of your sprained ankle was not truthful, and you privately attempted to escape, nearly ruining my grand plan. You have deceived me time and again. Tell me, how many times should I have your head chopped off?\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","Qin Shaozong smiled. \"Where there is rewarding merit, naturally there is also atoning for crimes with merit. My lady, you tell me: how many lives can saving Commander Qiao and presenting the 'ox belly wound therapy' buy back for you?\"","The water in the small earthen pot boiled, bubbling with a gurgling sound. Steam wafted from the spout, drifting leisurely between them, forming a thin, misty layer that seemed to conceal all the undercurrents beneath.","Dai Li pressed her lips together, knowing some matters must be laid to rest, or there would be no end to it. \"It's not just Commander Qiao. The abdominal poultice therapy may save many soldiers in the future. Let merits offset faults, and let this matter be written off entirely—including your promise not to vent anger on those maidservants and the cart driver from Nankang County. What does my lord think?\"","\"Agreed.\" This time, he agreed swiftly.","Dai Li sat up straight, striving to appear both sincere and solemn. She looked directly into those imposing brown eyes, not flinching, and spoke word by word: \"My lord, your prestige is known across the land. Willing young ladies to serve you are as numerous as fish in the river. I believe that compared to a dispensable concubine, an advisor beneficial to your army would surely bring you greater satisfaction.\"","This completely lifted the thin veil that both of them understood. She was not willing to serve him, did not wish to be his woman.","Qin Shaozong averted his gaze and began leisurely placing dried melon strips, tangerine peel, and other items into a cup.","Tap, tap.","The firm dried melon strips fell into the cup, producing crisp, clinking sounds.","\"The advisors in my army either knew me from humble beginnings and helped me rise, or are renowned scholars of established reputation and truly exceptional talent who sought me out later. None of them are women,\" Qin Shaozong stated flatly.","He picked up the nearby water pot and poured hot water into the tea cup. \"Under my command, past or future, there will be no female advisors. Women should stay in the residence, admiring flowers, feeding fish. Dealing with schemes, intrigues, and bloody storms is the duty and mission of men. There's no need for women to trouble themselves with it.\"","The hot water entered the cup, and the steam grew even thicker, almost obscuring the other's face.","Dai Li gritted her teeth inwardly. What kind of feudal patriarch speech was this? So utterly chauvinistic. She hadn't even finished her proposal, and he had already flatly declared there could be no female advisors under his command.","Dai Li took a breath, suppressing the surging irritation. \"My lord, everything has a process of starting from nothing. If you grant me this, I will write down the detailed method for making mulberry bark suture later and give it to Master Ding.\"","Qin Shaozong placed the tea cup in front of Dai Li and suddenly chuckled. \"Ding Lianxi is quite flexible in medical matters, adept at drawing inferences. Since my lady has already informed him that mulberry bark thread can replace silk thread, it's likely that mulberry bark thread will be developed soon enough.\"","The subtext was: Your detailed notes are unnecessary; Ding Lianxi will figure it out on his own sooner or later.","Having this item or not amounts to the same thing.","Dai Li understood but didn't mind, as she could simply offer something else. \"Sow in spring, harvest in autumn. Spring is the season of cultivation when all things revive. Has my lord ever considered trying to grow more grain?\"","The topic shift was abrupt, but Qin Shaozong seemed rather interested. \"The amount of fertile land remains unchanged, and the number of farmers remains unchanged. How can one grow more grain?\"","\"Has my lord heard of the dragon bone water pump?\" Dai Li countered with a question instead of answering.","Qin Shaozong did not speak.","Observing his expression, Dai Li had her answer. He had not heard of it.","Since arriving in this era, Dai Li had been gathering information. This dynasty was called \"Yan,\" and the current emperor's surname was \"Han,\" known as Emperor Han. Chinese history had seen a \"Yan State,\" but never a \"Yan Dynasty.\"","This was an unfamiliar, historically unprecedented ancient dynasty. Based on the clothing and daily items of the people in this era, Dai Li privately believed the current Yan Dynasty closely resembled the Han Dynasty.","But there was an Eastern Han and a Western Han, the two Han dynasties spanning over four hundred years. Which specific period of the Han Dynasty was she in? Was this unfamiliar Yan Dynasty following the historical trajectory she was familiar with?","Dai Li couldn't say for sure herself.","No, actually, it wasn't that she couldn't say. It was because she discovered that the stirrup, which should have appeared much later, had already emerged prematurely.","The history was broadly similar, yet not entirely identical.","A moment later, Qin Shaozong finally asked, \"What is a dragon bone waterwheel?\"","Dai Li felt completely reassured. She picked up the teacup in front of her and took a sip. \"A dragon bone waterwheel is an irrigation tool. You can think of it as an upgraded version of the well sweep and the bucket scoop. It draws water by hand-cranking or foot-pedaling, saving more time and effort and being more efficient than the well sweep and bucket scoop. This way, land that was previously water-deficient or required strenuous irrigation can easily become fertile fields.\"","The well sweep was essentially a lever, with a counterweight on one end and a bucket suspended on the other, using the principle of leverage to lift water from a low place to a high place or divert it elsewhere. The bucket scoop was woven from bamboo strips and rattan, shaped like a dipper, hence its name.","Whether it was the bucket scoop or the small bucket tied to the well sweep, the amount of water they could hold was limited, in no way comparable to a continuous flow of water.","\"How is the dragon bone waterwheel made?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","A rich smile appeared in Dai Li's eyes. \"So, does that mean you acknowledge me as your advisor?\"","Qin Shaozong saw her smiling, her eyes curved into two little crescents, like a cunning little fox crouching by a trap, wagging its tail, waiting for dinner. He felt both annoyed and amused.","All her little schemes were used on him.","Qin Shaozong wasn't in a hurry to agree. He also picked up his teacup and took a sip. \"In earlier years, a branch of the Qin clan went south for business, to the Yangzhou region. A few days ago, I sent a message back to Yuyang, asking someone to investigate the movements of this branch. I expect to receive a reply in at most another day. The Qiantang you've been thinking about is in Yangzhou. When the time comes, I'll have them go to Qiantang to see if they can find your son.\"","Clatter.","\"Are you serious?!\" Dai Li was so excited she accidentally knocked over the teacup beside her hand.","Tea was only filled to seventy percent, and since Dai Li had already drunk some, even if all the tea spilled out, it wasn't a complete disaster.","Dai Li's hand was scalded by the hot tea, and only then did she belatedly realize she had knocked over the cup. A cloth napkin was placed beside the ceramic pot, meant for the person holding the pot to insulate against heat, though Qin Shaozong hadn't needed it earlier; he had picked it up barehanded.","Dai Li's fingertips touched the napkin, and she picked it up. Just as she was about to withdraw her hand, a large, dark hand reached over and covered hers.","The man was long-limbed, and his palm was also two sizes larger than Dai Li's. Covering her hand, only a hint of the paleness beneath was faintly visible.","Dai Li's pupils trembled slightly.","Qin Shaozong moved his hand sideways against the back of hers. His four fingers slid underneath, lifting her palm along with the napkin, and wrapped it within his own grasp.","Their palms pressed together through the not-too-thick napkin. Dai Li felt a continuous flow of warmth, as if she had touched the small ceramic pot that had just boiled nearby.","His long fingers, calloused, stroked the delicate skin on the inside of her wrist, then slipped into the gap at the top of the napkin, completely pushing aside the bothersome cloth before gathering her hand into his palm once more.","Without the barrier, she felt every subtle movement of his with increasing clarity.","The man's gaze was deep and profound. His brown eyes were like a tiger lurking in the shadows, claws retracted, patiently waiting for its prey to approach. \"Of course it's true. I have never once deceived you, Madam.\"","Dai Li slowly lowered her eyes. When she looked up again, she had already adjusted her emotions, returning to her previous composure.","She withdrew her hand, not forgetting to take that napkin with her. \"Thank you, Lord Marquis, for keeping my son in mind. If there is indeed news of him, I will naturally thank you. The gift of gratitude is guaranteed to satisfy you.\"","She didn't specify what the gift was. At first glance, these words sounded very much like an offer of herself. But Dai Li's tone was too composed. Even though her voice was still that captivating, gentle tone, it contained no hint of provocative flirtation.","Qin Shaozong raised a long eyebrow. For the moment, he truly couldn't figure out what scheme she was hiding.","Dai Li used the napkin to soak up the water, then righted the overturned teacup. \"Might I borrow the study in your residence? I will draw the diagram of the dragon bone waterwheel for you later.\"","The study shared the same decorative style as the rest of the residence—extremely luxurious. Even the floor here was paved with Han jade, the lamps were made of crystal and jade, and the hanging curtains were woven with lustrous pearls.","Dai Li's first impression was that this place didn't resemble a solemn council chamber, but rather a relaxation area.","That salt smuggler surnamed Li certainly knew how to enjoy himself.","On one side of the low table lay silk, mulberry-bark paper, and blank bamboo slips. On the other side were a carving knife, a wolf-hair brush, and pine-soot ink.","The Four Treasures of the Study were all present and ready for use.","Yet Dai Li hesitated.","Although both were paper, the paper of this era was far inferior to modern paper in terms of smoothness and fineness. Moreover, she had never learned calligraphy and didn't know how to use a brush.","Combined, even before putting brush to paper, Dai Li could foresee a monstrous drawing about to be born.","Dai Li: \"...\"","\"Madam?\" Qin Shaozong noticed her prolonged stillness.","Dai Li turned to look at him, her tone somewhat unsteady. \"If I said I'm not accustomed to using a brush and therefore find it difficult to draw, would you think I'm deceiving you?\"","Qin Shaozong said meaningfully, \"What do you think?\"","The atmosphere froze. Neither spoke. Dai Li couldn't hold out and was the first to look away.","Steeling herself, she stepped forward and spread out the mulberry-bark paper. The paper was rough and uneven; even running her hand over it, she could feel a distinct fibrous texture.","Then she took out the pine-soot ink and the wolf-hair brush, ground the ink, dipped the brush, and held the upper part of the brush handle with a modern pen-holding posture before attempting to draw.","Qin Shaozong's gaze fixed on her brush-holding technique, the corner of his eye lifting slightly.","On her hands, only the inner side of the middle finger of her right hand had a thin callus. If one used this brush-holding posture over a long period, the callus that should have grown on the ring finger would indeed form on the inner side of the middle finger.","A young lady who could read, write, and even paint. Qin Shaozong had only met three other young ladies with such capabilities before.","Even among noblewomen, at most they only learned some arithmetic for managing household accounts. Beyond that, it was generally not pursued, as it was deemed unnecessary. Furthermore, no academy would accept female students. Without a teacher willing to instruct, how could one even begin to learn?","Unaware of the man's thoughts beside her, Dai Li was currently trying to tame the wolf-hair brush in her hand.","The idea was beautiful, but...","She failed.","The paper was uneven, the tip of the writing brush was far too soft, and there was a considerable distance between where one held it and the brush tip below.","All these factors combined meant that what Daili envisioned and what she drew were two completely different things—a failed attempt at taming the tool.","Setting the brush down on the desk, Daili turned her head to see Qin Shaozong watching her, his expression thoughtful.","Daili didn't pay it much mind. She knew he was deep and calculating, and understood that this type of cautious person harbored a certain degree of suspicion. From the moment she told him she came from \"Peach Blossom Spring,\" she was destined to be regarded with doubt by him.","\"My Lord, let's go to the courtyard,\" Daili decided to try a different approach.","Qin Shaozong said nothing and followed her out.","The courtyard outside the study was also beautifully landscaped. A pebble pathway, branching out like leaf veins, meandered to various areas, cutting the once whole courtyard into fragmented sections.","Although the courtyard itself wasn't usable, Daili spotted a branch of suitable thickness. After cutting it off with a knife, she suggested to Qin Shaozong that they go look elsewhere.","Qin Shaozong likely understood her intention and thus followed her lead.","As the two walked out of the study's courtyard, they ran into Su Xiuzhu and Mo Yanyun coming their way together.","\"My Lord,\" the two men bowed with clasped hands; they had both come to report on their duties.","With Ying County newly captured, there was no shortage of matters to handle. These didn't require the superior's personal involvement, but he needed to be kept informed of all progress.","It made no difference where he heard the reports. \"Accompany us,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Su Xiuzhu and Mo Yanyun exchanged a glance, both puzzled. This confusion only grew as they followed Daili through three courtyards, reaching its peak.","What was Lady Dai trying to do? Merely stroll around the estate?","Even if she was strolling, why was the Lord indulging her? Ying County had been hollowed out like a sieve by Li Zan and was in dire need of rebuilding. There simply wasn't this much time to waste on a leisurely tour.","Just as Mo Yanyun was about to speak up and remind them, he heard Daili say, \"This place will do. Right here.\"","Qin Shaozong looked at his two subordinates. \"Report your matters. Speak.\"","Mo Yanyun glanced at Daili, who was bending over with the branch in hand, hesitated, and finally whispered, \"My Lord...\" Not only was this a remote courtyard, but Lady Dai was also present.","\"Speak plainly,\" Qin Shaozong insisted.","The branch was stiff and much easier to handle. Once Daili entered her working state, she automatically tuned out external sounds. While the report was being given, it went in one ear and out the other, completely failing to distract her.","The dragon bone waterwheel could be roughly divided into two parts. One was the lower section: the dragon bone embedded within a long trough. The other was the upper section: a giant bearing fitted with a rotating axle and gear, connected to foot pedals.","Drawing the entire structure was difficult, so Daili used a split-diagram method. She first drew a long dragon bone trough, then used a small arrow to point to the side where she enlarged and detailed a section showing the two chain boards connected by the dragon bone inside the wheel.","Qin Shaozong divided his attention, his ears listening to the two men's report, his eyes watching Daili and the gradually forming diagrams beneath her branch.","\"Go to the study. Fetch several sheets of mulberry bark paper and a brush,\" Qin Shaozong suddenly said to Mo Yanyun, who was taken aback.","Qin Shaozong: \"Quickly.\"","This time, Mo Yanyun didn't dare delay. He hurried back to the study. On the way, he ran into Yan San and Feng Feng and couldn't help but mutter a few words as he walked. So, when he returned to the small courtyard with the supplies, he found Yan San and Feng Feng were also there.","The two men stood beside Su Xiuzhu, making the only civil official present seem rather slight by comparison.","Su Xiuzhu's report had stopped at some point. Now, all three of them, along with Qin Shaozong, were watching Daili in front of them.","Baffled, Mo Yanyun shot a questioning, startled look at his comrades. Yan San noticed but expressionlessly looked away, having no intention of responding.","The corner of Mo Yanyun's mouth twitched. He decided to look at the more cheerful Feng Feng, but unfortunately, Feng Feng for some reason was entirely focused on watching Lady Dai and didn't notice him at all.","Feeling aggrieved, Mo Yanyun grumbled under his breath as he walked forward from the front, completely oblivious to what was at his feet.","\"Stop!\"","\"Don't step there!\"","\"You fool!\"","Several voices crashed down on him at once, leaving Mo Yanyun utterly bewildered.","Wh-what was happening?","Why were they looking at him like that? Had he committed some cardinal sin?"]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33","paragraphs":["It wasn't until he was roughly jerked aside that Mo Yanyun looked down, belatedly realizing why he had just been shouted at.","A diagram was drawn on the ground right where he had been standing. Looking further out, Mo Yanyun now saw that the courtyard floor was covered in numerous drawings. Some were long, some were wide, and some looked like small wooden boards.","A dragon bone waterwheel was not difficult to draw; the main thing was to explain the principles clearly and leave the rest to the craftsmen. Even with just a few words and a rough sketch, a skilled carpenter could bring it to life.","Thus, after finishing the upper bearing, Dai Li stopped. Turning around, she found several pairs of bright, focused eyes fixed upon her.","Dai Li paused for a moment, still holding a twig in her hand. She looked at Qin Shaozong. My Lord, if you are busy...","I am not busy. You may tell me about this dragon bone waterwheel now, Madam. Qin Shaozong then called Su Xiuzhu by his courtesy name, instructing, Qingluo, make a copy of the diagrams on the ground.","Dai Li used the twig in her hand as a pointer. This type of dragon bone waterwheel is usually ten to twenty feet long. The lower end of the chain is submerged in the river, and as the chain wheel is driven from the upper end, the connected paddles inside the trough are pulled forward one by one, thereby pushing the water upward against the current.","The twig pointed to each corresponding component in the diagram as Dai Li continued.","It can be driven by hand cranks, foot pedals, or even donkeys and oxen. If driven by human power for a full day, it can irrigate about five mu of land. If replaced by ox power, that capacity can more than double.","Under their burning gazes, Dai Li stepped out from the edge of the drawings. The reason some places struggle to become farmland, or why their grain yields are so meager, is entirely due to the difficulty of drawing water. If this problem is solved, there is no need to worry about the amount of fertile land not increasing.","My Lord, this method has immense potential! Feng Feng exclaimed excitedly.","Unlike Yan San and Mo Yanyun, who were backed by clans subordinate to the Qin family, Feng Feng had no background to speak of. His father had been a tenant farmer working for a powerful local landlord.","Tenant farmers owned no land of their own; they survived by renting land from the wealthy to cultivate, handing over a portion of their harvest and rent every year. When the weather was favorable and the heavens were kind, life was slightly more bearable for them. However, if a drought struck, it became a matter of life and death. The landlords cared nothing for the whims of the heavens; they only cared about collecting their rent.","If one could not produce the money, they would first be forced into a loan with compound interest. Those with daughters sold them; those without daughters or money were reduced to serfs. Unlike the contractual relationship of a tenant farmer, a serf was a slave. Even if the master beat, scolded, or even killed them, there was essentially nowhere to seek justice.","Feng Feng’s parents had died during a year of famine. As a half-grown youth, he had become a displaced refugee. When the northern barbarians invaded and Youzhou began recruiting soldiers, he had no choice but to enlist.","Since then, he had lived with his head on the line. Relying on a physique and wit far exceeding that of ordinary soldiers, along with a bit of indescribable luck, he had fought his way through countless trials over the years. Not only had he broken into the ranks of the Xuanxiao Cavalry, but he had also successfully become a Squadron Leader.","Though the days of tilling the soil were years behind him, they had never faded from his memory. Feng Feng could fully imagine how many farmers would benefit if this dragon bone waterwheel could spread like the wind into thousands of households.","Dai Li chuckled. It certainly has potential. Dragon bone waterwheels can be linked together with small ponds acting as bridges in between. Chain after chain, even highlands over thirty feet high can be irrigated without worry.","Lady Dai, who came up with this dragon bone waterwheel? Feng Feng asked urgently.","Waterwheels existed currently, but they were only used to draw water to sprinkle on the roads to prevent dust from rising and harming health; they had never appeared in the field of agriculture.","Dai Li replied, An inventor named Ma Jun.","Ma Jun? Why have I never heard of this person's name? Mo Yanyun frowned.","Feng Feng quickly asked, Lady Dai, where is this person's ancestral home? Where are they now? If such a brilliant mind could come to serve My Lord, our Northern Lands would surely be like a tiger with wings.","Dai Li turned her gaze. After finishing the model of the waterwheel, she met that exceptionally strong gaze for the first time. She saw the darkness and glimmer in his eyes, as if she were glimpsing a great tiger in the forest, muscles tensed, ready to leap and bite.","But she knew that no matter how fierce and greedy this tiger appeared, it was merely an intimidating surface.","Her red lips curved as Dai Li smiled at him. This gentleman is no longer with us. There are other scholars, however, though I suspect your Lord would not like her to serve him.","How could that be?","My Lord has always been respectful to the wise and thirsty for talent. If such a talent could be brought under his command, My Lord would be more than happy. Why would he dislike it?","Exactly.","The four of them spoke one after another, none of them noticing that Qin Shaozong had not spoken for a long time.","Qin Shaozong watched the woman a short distance away without blinking. She stood in the sunlight, her eyelashes appearing as if coated in a thick golden glow. Those dark eyes were as bright as mirrors, reflecting the silhouettes of clouds in the sky and the beauty of the flower buds in the courtyard. Every blade of grass and every tree was contained within them, as if they held the entirety of a brilliant spring.","Her happiness and slight smugness were unconcealed, as if she were saying: Look, even your subordinates think you are being ridiculous.","That thread of rich, dark fragrance seemed to float in the air again, refreshing and incredibly enticing.","For the first time, Qin Shaozong felt a different kind of challenge.","It was not the life-and-death slaughter of the battlefield, nor the bloodless deception of the political arena, but a completely new sensation. It was a bit like the surge of excitement felt when taming a wild horse, yet not entirely the same, for at this moment, his thoughts were racing far more than when he had first tamed his steed, Red Flood Dragon.","Su Xiuzhu remembered something. Mr. Nalan should be arriving in Ying County soon. We can show this dragon bone waterwheel to him then. By the way, Lady Dai, you can tell Mr. Nalan about those 'other scholars' you mentioned. He is widely experienced and has friends among the talented across the world; perhaps he will know their names. If Mr. Nalan acts as an intermediary to persuade them, the chances of them joining My Lord's service will be much higher.","He unconsciously used a respectful title for Dai Li.","Dai Li smiled but said nothing.","It was true that Ying County was in a state of neglect, but the core team of the Xuanxiao Cavalry, having followed Qin Shaozong through years of southern and northern campaigns, was already capable of handling matters of all sizes quickly and steadily.","In just one afternoon, proclamations were issued to reassure the people, city defenses were taken over, and vacancies in the county’s official positions were filled. Everything was arranged in an orderly fashion.","As night fell, the lights within the manor shone brightly, as clear as day. Su Xiuzhu, in his capacity as the military instructor, organized a grand banquet.","Dai Li attended by invitation. She was purely there for the food. Now that they had finally entered a county city, there was no need to compromise on her diet.","The discipline of the Xuanxiao Cavalry was very strict; during wartime, there were explicit bans on sex and alcohol. At the previous bonfire feast, Dai Li had not seen a single wine jar.","But today was different. Jars of brewed wine were carried into the main hall, soon stacked behind the head table and the two rows of long tables below, appearing at first glance like walls built of wine jars.","Daili was only there to scrounge a meal. As an outsider with no official rank, she saw no reason to take a prominent seat at such a grand banquet, so she quietly settled herself at the very back.","The seats ahead of her were mostly occupied by military officers. They were a phalanx of brawny men, all dressed in a uniform palette of dirt-resistant blacks and grays—much like the outfit Daili was wearing herself. Thus, when she kept her head down and blended in with the crowd, her presence was truly inconspicuous.","Since it was an internal celebration, there wasn't much tedious formality. Once Qin Shaozong took his seat, he gave a brief speech and raised his cup.","The company drank in unison to celebrate the great victory.","Then, the feast began. Everyone ate and drank their fill, and the hall instantly became a scene of bustling excitement.","While this meal didn't quite match the scale of the previous banquet at the Jiang estate, it offered a fine spread of both hot and cold dishes. To Daili’s delight, there was even a dish of steamed Mandarin fish on the table.","There was an old saying: \"When the fields are deep, the rabbits grow fat; when the frost falls, the sea bass is at its best.\" Autumn was indeed the season for plump sea bass, but spring had its own seasonal delicacies. The Mandarin fish of spring was renowned for its tender flesh and delicate texture—a true gourmet treat.","Daili loved fish, whether steamed or grilled. After having survived on \"authentic\" roasted mutton for so long, the plate of Mandarin fish before her was so delicious that she didn't even look up from her plate.","Until—","Daili heard the crisp chime of silver bells.","Her eyelashes fluttered upward as flashes of vivid silk caught her eye. Into the hall, which had been thick with the scent of wine, a metaphorical spring breeze seemed to blow, bringing with it the alluring fragrance of rouge and powder.","Upon the jade-inlaid walls, the light caught the flickering shadows of dancers moving with ethereal grace. The veiled dancing girls wore short tops and long skirts; as they turned and tossed their sleeves, their daringly short bodices rode up even further, revealing glimpses of slender, snow-white waists.","Daili had seen plenty of live performances in her time. She vividly remembered when her college roommate had been cheated on; in a fit of rage, the girl had treated their entire dorm to a trip to Pattaya to party with male models.","In terms of \"boldness,\" she had to admit that those shows had been far more provocative than this midriff-baring dance.","Still, Daili watched with an appreciative eye. Setting aside the skimpy costumes, this was, after all, authentic classical dance.","After several rounds of wine, many of the generals left their seats. No longer content to sit still, some roamed the hall with a wine jar in one hand and a cup in the other, seeking out their comrades for drinking matches.","With so many people moving about, Mo Yanyun was no exception. He went a step further in his boldness, plopping himself down right on the steps leading up to the head of the hall. Holding both a jar and a cup, he drank while chatting with Qin Shaozong.","Or rather, he had been rambling to himself for quite some time.","\"My Lord, I never realized that while Li Zhan’s competence left much to be desired, his taste in women was actually quite excellent.\" Mo Yanyun’s eyes were practically glued to the dancers below.","These dancers had originally been kept in the estate. Li Zhan had even been expanding the side courtyards to house more concubines and entertainers, but he had been forced to pack his bags and flee before the construction was finished.","There was no response from the high seat. Mo Yanyun continued, \"My Lord, what do you think of the lead girl? Her skin is like jade, her fingers are slender, and her figure is exquisite. Though her face is partially hidden, she’s the lead dancer, so she must have some extraordinary charms.\"","Still no answer.","Mo Yanyun didn't mind and kept talking. \"That girl with the little fish-shaped floral mark on her forehead is also quite something. She has a peach blossom tucked behind her ear and a pair of 'peach blossom' eyes—so radiant and full of life. They complement the flower in her hair perfectly.\"","He expected his words to sink into silence once more, but this time, he actually got a response.","\"Mediocre.\"","Mo Yanyun instinctively turned his head. Seeing his superior’s cold expression and a hint of disdain, he was momentarily stunned. Emboldened by the wine, he couldn't help but shoot back, \"Even that is considered mediocre? Then, in your eyes, what counts as truly beautiful?\"","Qin Shaozong didn't answer him directly, but in his mind, he was judging what he had just seen.","The red floral mark on the dancer's brow was meant to be striking, but where others might look elegant and noble, here it looked forced and tacky. And all that spinning—the peach blossom behind her ear looked like it was about to fall off at any moment. Where was the beauty in that?","As for those \"peach blossom\" eyes, they were too small, the whites were slightly cloudy, and the shape wasn't refined enough. None of it deserved to be called \"radiant.\"","What counted as beautiful?","\"A face like polished jade, with natural beauty that requires no adornment.\" Only that could be called peerless elegance.","Qin Shaozong’s gaze shifted back toward the right rear of the hall. He saw the woman who had been buried in her fish earlier. At some point, she had stopped eating and was now watching the performance in the hall.","Judging by the slight curve of her lips, she seemed quite satisfied with what she was seeing.","She was watching with such gusto from the very back; if she were moved to the head of the hall, she probably wouldn't even need the fish—she could fill up just by watching the dancers.","Daili suddenly sensed a familiar gaze coming from above. It was intense, impossible to ignore, and just as overbearing as the man himself. She turned her head and, instead of looking away, she picked up her wine cup and gave him a smiling toast.","Regardless of everything else, this was a victory banquet. She was eating the host's food, and since they had locked eyes, she felt she should show some congratulatory intent.","Daili was genuinely happy at that moment. There were plenty of beautiful dancers in the estate, and surely many would be willing to serve him. This man really didn't need to keep his eyes fixed on her anymore.","From his high seat, Qin Shaozong watched as she raised her cup with a smile. Her eyes were bright and expressive, and the natural flush of her lips was stunningly vivid. Even though she was dressed in drab, dusty clothes, she seemed to glow with a soft, pearly luster—beautiful, lush, and mature, like a precious peony in full bloom.","The man’s calloused thumb brushed against the winged cup in his hand. The long-necked, wide-mouthed vessel spun in his grip before being suddenly clamped tight by his large hand, rendered immobile.","A drop or two of wine splashed out, landing on the dark skin of Qin Shaozong’s hand, but he didn't seem to notice.","It would be impolite to raise a cup and not drink. Daili happened to be a bit thirsty, so she took the opportunity to drain the cup.","This was her first time tasting the liquor of this era. As soon as it hit her tongue, she recognized it.","It was yellow rice wine, made from broomcorn millet.","Because millet yields were relatively high, it was very popular among the common people, making yellow rice wine the most prevalent drink. It was known to aid digestion and nourish the liver and kidneys; a small amount was actually good for one's health.","Taking a sip, Daili pursed her lips to savor the flavor. It was quite pleasant, so she took another sip.","Before she knew it, the cup was empty. There was a small wine pot nearby that a servant had brought out with the meal, which Daili hadn't touched until now. Since her cup was dry, she picked up the pot to refill it.","The pale yellow liquid flowed from the spout, catching the light from the pearls on the wall. It shimmered with a jewel-like clarity, looking like a ribbon made of liquid crystal.","Using the digestive yellow rice wine to wash it down, Daili finished every last bit of the Mandarin fish. In a particularly good mood, she used her jade chopsticks to nudge the fish head, lining it up with the perfectly picked-clean skeleton.","The wine pot was empty, the bowl of rice was gone, and the fish was finished. Having had her fill of food and drink, Daili set down her chopsticks and stood up to leave the increasingly rowdy main hall.","\"My Lord, which one catches your eye? The one in red, or does the one in pale yellow suit your fancy? You pick one, and leave the rest to me.\" Mo Yanyun looked back and forth, privately thinking that the dancers in the red and pale yellow dresses were the most dazzling in the room.","Ever since they left Yuyang and embarked on the campaign to crusade against the salt warlords, they hadn't touched a woman. There had been an opportunity earlier at Jiang Chonghai's manor, but the Marquis had devised a sudden plan, and naturally, the greater mission took precedence over everything else.","Now that Ying Commandery had been conquered, they could finally relax, and of course, they had to seize the moment.","Besides, the hall was full of dancers who were anything but eyesores; on the contrary, he felt several of them were quite striking, like beauties stepped right out of a painting.","Having asked his question, Mo Yanyun craned his neck, eagerly awaiting his superior's reply, when he heard a sharp clack.","The wine cup was set down upon the low table. Under Mo Yanyun's stunned gaze, Qin Shaozong rose from the seat of honor, left a single phrase—\"Suit yourself\"—and strode into the side corridor.","He was a man of tall stature, and in just a few moments, he had disappeared from sight.","Mo Yanyun was flabbergasted.","Suit himself?","Did... did that mean he was giving them all to him? Was there really such good fortune? Was this for real?","Truly unable to decide what to make of it, Mo Yanyun hugged his wine jar and walked over to Yan San, whispering, \"Brother, let me ask you something. Analyze this for me...\"","Then, like spilling beans from a sack, he recounted everything that had just happened.","With Ying Commandery taken, Yan San was in a good mood and spoke a few more words than usual. \"It means exactly what it sounds like. Do as you please.\"","Mo Yanyun muttered, \"Exactly what it sounds like? But that's not right. Earlier, I saw the Marquis looking like he was about to burst with pent-up fire, his eyes practically glowing green. There's no reason he wouldn't want one!\"","Hearing this, Yan San stood up, took two steps back, and turned his head to the left. He was seated in the right row of the lower positions, the same column as Lady Dai, but separated by many people. If he merely turned his head while seated, he wouldn't be able to see the back of the row along the same line.","\"Lady Dai has left the banquet,\" Yan San said.","Mo Yanyun didn't understand. \"What does that have to do with Lady Dai?\"","Lady Dai held a rather unique status in their army at the moment. You could call her the Marquis's concubine, yet nothing had truly happened between her and the Marquis. Moreover, given her great contributions regarding Old Qiao and the dragon-bone waterwheel, she was distinct from ordinary women.","If you were to call her a strategist, that wasn't right either. Their Xuanxiao Cavalry had never had female staff, and given the Marquis's attitude of being determined to possess her, she could absolutely never just be a strategist.","Lady Dai couldn't be touched for the time being, but other women could be. There were so many dancers in the hall, each as lovely as a flower; why would the Marquis deny himself?","Yan San looked away, too lazy to explain it to this rake. \"Anyway, just do as you please.\"","\"Yan San, explain it to me again. I'm racking my brains and I still don't get it.\" Mo Yanyun simply sat down beside him.","Yan San said coldly, \"Your brain is useless anyway, so let it break.\"","\"Hey, why do you always copy the way the Marquis talks?\"","*","After Lady Dai left the banquet, she had originally intended to return to her room to rest, but she accidentally took a wrong turn along the way. By the time she realized something was amiss, she had already turned left and right several times and now had no idea where she was.","Just as she was thinking of finding someone to ask for directions, Lady Dai suddenly saw a black shadow rise from beside her feet. It surged upward like a rising mountain, far broader and thicker than her own shadow, carrying a terrifyingly oppressive aura.","In the blink of an eye, the black shadow had crept up to the waist of her own shadow.","Lady Dai's pupils trembled slightly, and she spun around quickly to look.","The long corridor was opulent, with floor-standing carved candelabras set at regular intervals. Tonight, as the residence was hosting a welcoming banquet, the candelabras were in rare use.","In this moonless night, all illumination came from the not-so-bright candlelight flickering within two carved stands not far away.","And at this moment, between those two candelabras, on the path she had just walked, a tall, imposing figure was approaching step by step.","The night breeze brushed past, and Lady Dai smelled a strong scent of alcohol. perhaps it was because there was no one else around, or perhaps the night was too dark, or due to some other indescribable feeling—whatever the reason, in this moment, Lady Dai felt a sudden, inexplicable sense of trepidation."]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34","paragraphs":["That shadowy figure rose like the tide beneath a moonlit night, gradually submerging Dai Li. In a fleeting moment, as if awakening from a dream, she hastily retreated two steps, moving herself out of the shadow's enveloping reach.","\"How did you come to be here?\" Dai Li initiated the conversation.","Her voice was soft and calm, the momentary panic that had flashed across her face now nowhere to be seen.","Dai Li had assumed Qin Shaozong would say something about the room being stuffy, prompting him to stroll outside, or perhaps that he had stepped out to relieve himself—safe topics that wouldn't disrupt the delicate balance.","But just as she had never imagined he would pursue her all the way to Taiping County back then, she now equally failed to anticipate...","\"I came for you, my lady,\" the man's voice was low, carrying a hint of huskiness from the wine.","He didn't bother with trivialities, instead pinning the topic squarely on her. In the darkness, Qin Shaozong's brown eyes were far deeper than usual, like a vortex in the deep sea capable of swallowing a person whole.","Dai Li's breath hitched slightly, her sensitive nerves humming a warning, as if even the night breeze brushing her face had turned several degrees sharper. \"I... I have eaten my fill and wish to return to rest. The banquet is not yet over; your subordinates must be waiting for you to preside. You should hurry back.\"","With that, Dai Li turned to leave.","As her sleeves fluttered, poised to slip away like a darting fish, a large, calloused hand reached out and precisely grasped her fair, soft hand hidden beneath her sleeve.","His fingers splayed, making his palm seem even broader, almost completely enveloping hers.","Qin Shaozong retracted his arm, easily pulling her into his embrace. The hand that had been holding hers loosened, only to circle her slender waist instead. \"In all the land, those whose status surpasses mine can be counted on one hand. Why, my lady, do you resist me so?\"","The world bustles, all for profit; the world hustles, all for gain. Qin Shaozong had always been acutely aware that many fawned over and attached themselves to him precisely because he was the head of the Qin clan, the Marquis of Wu'an enfeoffed by the imperial court, the man with the greatest influence in the northern territories—because the power in his hands could bring them benefits.","There was no reason to be annoyed by this, nor any need to take it to heart. After all, he likewise used and directed these followers, making them run his errands to seek even greater gains for himself.","In essence, it was a transaction.","He considered himself a man who never mistreated women. So why did she reject him time and again?","Dai Li was forced to turn, now facing Qin Shaozong. They stood extremely close, near enough for her to clearly smell the strong scent of wine on him.","He had drunk quite a lot at the banquet. He might not be as clear-headed as usual, or perhaps—","He was intentionally or unintentionally indulging his own actions.","The latter was more dangerous, for it meant he was fully aware of what he was doing from start to finish.","Dai Li raised a hand to press against his robust chest, preventing him from drawing closer. \"Everyone has their own preferences. Some favor fine swords and despise paintings and calligraphy, while others are the exact opposite.\"","Qin Shaozong fell silent for a moment, then suddenly remarked, \"Was your former husband, then, a scholar too weak to truss a chicken?\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","There was no moon tonight. Dai Li was enveloped within his shadow, the surroundings dim, but it didn't hinder Qin Shaozong from seeing her expression clearly.","He chuckled abruptly, sounding rather pleased. \"When you were in Taiping County, you told me you lived there with your young son. Your words made no mention of a husband. I surmise he is most likely no longer among the living.\"","As a man, if one possessed a great beauty of such breathtaking loveliness, one would never let her have the chance to leave.","Dai Li's pupils contracted slightly. She knew he was sharp, but this kind of insight—piecing together a rough picture from just a few careless words of others—was truly terrifying.","\"He has not passed away. The reason I didn't mention him before was solely because we had a quarrel. My anger hadn't subsided, so I didn't speak of him at the time,\" Dai Li insisted, refusing to admit it.","Qin Shaozong offered no comment on this, leaving it unclear whether he believed her or not. He took the delicate hand pressed against his chest, his thumb rubbing heavily against the fine skin on the inside of her wrist. \"My lady wishes to find your son. I can undertake that task. Back then, on the bed, you told me I must help you find him. If it was possible then, why is it not possible now?\"","Dai Li couldn't help but regret uttering those few hasty words at the time. She tried to pull her hand free but couldn't, and anxiety began to rise.","Initially, she had thought that forging the dragon-bone waterwheel into a muzzle and fitting it onto this vicious tiger, then dangling a piece of rich meat before him, would be akin to dangling a carrot before a donkey—making him work for her.","But the plan had deviated somewhat from reality.","A vicious tiger, after all, is a vicious tiger. He was cunning and unpredictable, with a profound, scheming mind, worlds apart from a docile donkey.","Perhaps it was because women of this era generally lacked access to education, and because he had personally heard her say the creator of the square-pallet chain pump was named Ma Jun, not Dai Li herself. Thus, even though she promised a reward and specifically guided the description of that reward towards something beneficial to his regime, he still remained somewhat unconvinced.","It was like hiking in the modern wilderness when suddenly a stranger appears, telling you there are ten tons of gold hidden in a cave on the mountain ahead, urging you to hurry and bring it home to make your fortune. He shows you a gold ring as proof.","Do you believe it, or not?","Most likely, you don't.","In a socialist environment, not only are all mineral resources state-owned, but even if there were a gold deposit, it couldn't possibly exist in a place that isn't truly remote—as if the prospectors were incompetent.","Yet Dai Li understood perfectly well that she absolutely must not, due to his suspicion, blurt out everything she knew at once. The situation awaiting her then would be nothing short of a nightmare.","Dai Li's heart gradually tightened. \"My lord, when I said earlier that if you had news of my son, I would surely repay you handsomely, those words were no empty promise. Countless young ladies in this land admire you. Among the dancers at the banquet just now, which one would not be willing to offer you pleasure and charm if it pleased you? Why must you endure the cold shoulder from another?\"","With one of his arms circling her waist and the other gripping her wrist, Dai Li's only free limb was her left hand. But she dared not struggle forcefully now, fearing it might provoke the ferocious nature of this tiger.","Qin Shaozong gave a slight smile and was about to speak when he suddenly heard voices in the distance.","\"Where has the lord gone?\"","\"Seems to be near the gardens. What do you need him for?\"","\"An urgent letter from Yuyang has arrived. I must present it to him immediately.\"","...","The smile in Qin Shaozong's eyes deepened. He looked down at the woman in his arms. \"My lady, a letter has come from Yuyang.\"","Dai Li didn't possess his keen hearing. From the distant voices, she only caught fragments—\"the lord,\" \"gardens,\" \"present it\"—but couldn't make out the specifics.","Now, hearing him mention Yuyang, Dai Li was stunned.","She remembered him saying his ancestral home was in Yuyang, and remembered even more clearly that today he had mentioned a branch of the Qin family that had moved to Yangzhou years ago. He had already sent a message back to Yuyang to have that branch's movements investigated, and said they would receive a reply in at most another day.","Had the reply... arrived already?!","\"Quick, go and get it.\" In her excitement, Daili completely forgot all else. She used her left hand to push aside his large palm, then grabbed the area near the girdle at his waist, trying to make him turn around.","Qin Shaozong raised a brow slightly, turning with her motion and taking two steps forward under her pushing force. \"Why is my lady in such a hurry? That letter won't grow legs and run away.\"","Daili retorted, \"The letter won't run, but the soldier carrying it might. Please hurry.\"","She told him to hurry, yet he seemed to do the opposite, slowing down deliberately, moving lazily, taking only one step for each of her pushes.","Daili gritted her teeth secretly, thinking this man was utterly detestable.","However, the delay wasn't long, as Qin Shaozong soon returned to normal because the soldier carrying the letter found them.","\"My Lord, a letter from Yuyang.\" The soldier presented the letter with both hands.","Qin Shaozong took it.","The soldier's eyes flickered quickly to the side, catching a glimpse of the person beside him, then wisely took his leave.","After the soldier departed, the surroundings returned to silence. The earlier undercurrent that had been so unnerving seemed to swell again with the departure of the third party.","Both now faced the carved standing candlestick. Daili clearly saw the wax seal on the letter and also a small moth fluttering its wings, flying towards the candle flame in the distance.","The moth flew into the flame. With a faint, almost imperceptible sizzle, only a speck of ash remained in the carved candlestick.","Daili stood frozen in place.","Qin Shaozong raised his hand to wrap around her shoulder, drawing her into his embrace. She had also drunk wine at the banquet—a whole pot, which was rather much for a lady.","Although the wine she drank was the same as his, both millet wine, Qin Shaozong detected a different scent. The aroma of wine was blended with several strands of an elegant fragrance. The two scents intertwined like vines, making her distinct from anyone else.","Life on campaign was austere. The vast majority of people were dusty and grimy. Even those who loved cleanliness couldn't bathe daily. For the rougher sort, going days without water was common, and the less fastidious might go even longer...","One only had to see how some large camps reeked to the heavens—enough to make dogs vomit, horses bolt upon passing, and even mosquitoes and flies steer clear in disgust.","But Qin Shaozong had always felt she carried a very special fragrance, like flowers, or like the rich aroma of ripe fruit. It seemed to seep from her very skin and flesh, present as long as she herself was present.","And now, the source of that fragrance was in his arms. Qin Shaozong felt himself drawn to bend slightly, his chin brushing against her cloud-like hair. He asked a question he already knew the answer to, his tone carrying a hint of coaxing. \"Does my lady wish to see this letter?\"","The stubble on his jaw wasn't completely shaven. Daili felt as if her temple had been lightly scraped by sandpaper. She snapped back to her senses instantly, her previously agitated and swollen head cooling rapidly.","Daili didn't hurry to move. Instead, she said, \"Naturally, I wish to see it. However, letters are important items. It's best to be prudent. Why don't we go to the study? What does my lord think?\"","The surroundings were dim, the light from the carved standing candlestick too faint. The atmosphere here was disadvantageous for her.","Footsteps of a patrol team sounded in the distance, growing from soft to heavy, from far to near. They were approaching this area.","Qin Shaozong straightened up and released her. \"Very well.\"","Inside the study.","Breaking the wax seal, the mulberry paper was spread out on the low table.","The letter was a scroll bundled into a cylinder. Upon unrolling it, Daili saw two letters. Before she could examine them closely, the top one was taken by Qin Shaozong.","With the upper layer removed, the one beneath was revealed.","Having been rolled up for too long, it tried to curl back upon itself after being spread out, but was pressed flat by a delicate hand. Daili smoothed it out again and used the tiger-head paperweight on the table to hold it down.","The writing on the letter was in Zhangcao script.","Zhangcao script evolved from the cursive clerical script of the Qin Dynasty and was also the precursor to Xiaocao (modern cursive). Traditional characters combined with Zhangcao script, the two layers stacked together, made Daili's head ache slightly.","So, by the time Qin Shaozong finished reading that not-so-brief report and pondered how to reply, he looked up to see Daili frowning delicately, still utterly focused on the mulberry paper before her.","His gaze lowered, sweeping over the letter. He raised his brow in some surprise.","Just three lines, and she had been looking at them for half the night. And judging by her expression, she truly hadn't finished reading. Could it be she needed to recognize each character one by one?","Qin Shaozong placed the letter in his hand casually to the side. \"Has my lady understood? If there are characters you don't recognize, you may ask me.\"","Daili didn't lift her head. \"Thank you, but your esteemed assistance is not required.\"","Qin Shaozong chuckled softly, letting her struggle with the few characters on her own. He took a fresh sheet of paper from beside him, ground the ink, lifted the brush, and wrote his reply in one smooth flow.","In mere moments, a letter destined for Yuyang was complete.","Qin Shaozong set down his brush and looked up; he happened to catch sight of Daili smoothing his brow, wearing an expression as if he had solved a great dilemma.","Placing the wolf-hair brush on the brush rest, the man turned the jade thumb ring on his finger, then suddenly leaned back against the chair behind him, returning to his earlier languid demeanor.","When Daili looked up, Qin Shaozong pointed to the paper and brush beside him. \"Paper and brush are here, the ink is ground for you. My lady, please proceed at your convenience.\"","Daili: \"...\"","Their eyes met. In this stare-down where neither looked away, Daili clearly saw the corner of his mouth slowly curve upwards.","This fellow was doing it on purpose. He clearly knew during the day that she couldn't use a brush pen.","Qin Shaozong smiled. \"If my lady requires a scribe, I am willing to serve. However, even Confucian scholars in the marketplace can earn a few copper coins. I, a Marquis officially enfeoffed by the court, surely cannot work for free. Wouldn't you agree, my lady?\"","Daili stared at him for two beats, then suddenly snatched up the mulberry paper containing the information about the Qin family in Yangzhou. Without a word, she turned and walked out.","If he wouldn't help her write it, she would find someone else. There was more than just Qin Shaozong in this residence who knew how to write.","Yet she had only taken two steps when the man behind her spoke again. His tone was as lazy as he himself appeared at the moment, without much pressure. \"You may certainly try to find someone else. See if they will write it for you, and see if this letter penned by another's hand can ultimately leave Ying Commandery.\"","But just that one sentence made Daili stop dead in her tracks.","Only a small panel of the window in the room was open. The wine fumes that had permeated the room hadn't dissipated much; instead, they seemed to grow heavier as time passed.","Daili took a deep breath, then turned around, her tone displeased. \"What do you want?\"","\"My lady, come here.\" He beckoned to her.","Daili pressed her lips together but ultimately went back, though she stopped on the other side of the long table, facing him.","Qin Shaozong said nothing, but his gaze clearly lowered, resting on the mulberry paper in her hand for a moment, before he beckoned again.","Not close enough.","He wanted her to come closer.","Daili averted her gaze, no longer looking into those brown eyes, and slowly circled around the long desk. Behind the desk, the man sat with an imposing, domineering posture. From her lowered, narrowed field of vision, she could only see the edge of his black robe.","A deep, dark black, a heavy color, as inscrutable as the man himself, and carrying the same oppressive weight.","Her wrist was suddenly seized, her vision swaying violently for an instant. By the time Daili regained her senses, she had gone from standing to sitting. She was sitting sideways on his lap, her back supported only by the long arm encircling her waist.","Qin Shaozong wrapped one arm around her waist, his large hand first settling firmly at the small of her back. Once she was seated steadily, that hand slid along the curve of her waist to the front.","The moment the pressure was applied to that sensitive spot at the small of her back, Daili shivered reflexively. She instinctively tried to twist away in the opposite direction, only to collide with his solid chest.","All of Daili's thoughts of standing up or breaking free ceased with the words he spoke next:","\"What would Madam like to instruct them to do in the letter? All the collateral branches of the Qin clan follow my lead without question. They will execute the orders in this handwritten letter meticulously.\"","Daili's eyelashes fluttered rapidly several times. A scale was tilting back and forth in her heart.","On one side was offering something like the \"heavy bombshell\" of the dragon-bone water wheel, using it as a bargaining chip to secure his help and escape her current predicament.","On the other side was enduring for now, not revealing another chip. After all, things were far from reaching the point of sharing a bed, and that Master Nalan, said to hold high prestige in the military, had not yet arrived in Ying County.","She needed someone else to help her check Qin Shaozong's power. Clearly, this potential ally had not yet arrived.","He had drunk a great deal at the banquet, and after the confrontation in the corridor, she realized this man did not play by conventional rules at all.","After the scale wavered left and right several times, the left side finally shot up high, while the right side sank down.","\"Have them go to Qiantang to find a nine-year-old boy named 'Qin Yanzhou.' He...\" Daili's voice trembled slightly.","The hand resting on her lap was taken by the large hand that had been circling her waist. The rough, thick calluses were overwhelmingly present, scorching hot and possessive as they encircled her wrist.","The dark hand moved up against the skin of her wrist, first hooking her index finger. A long finger slid into the space between her two fingers, slowly stroking the soft flesh on the inner side of her finger.","Daili instinctively wanted to make a fist, but the spaces between her fingers were successively filled by his.","With his right hand, Qin Shaozong picked up the wolf-hair brush from the desk. With swift, flowing strokes on the spread mulberry paper, he neatly wrote down the description of the boy's appearance Daili had just given.","\"What else, besides your son's appearance? What else does Madam wish to say?\" The tip of the brush, dipped in black ink, lifted and returned to the brush rest.","Qin Shaozong turned his head. The long arm holding Daili tightened, forcing the person in his embrace to lean closer.","Sitting on his lap, Daili was, for once, slightly taller than him. Now, pressed forward by the hand on her lower back, she had to raise a hand to brace against his solid shoulder blade.","\"How about ordering them to search all of Qiantang and the smaller cities and counties within a hundred miles around it within a month? Have them comb through all the human markets and investigate every trafficker in Qiantang.\" With each sentence Qin Shaozong uttered, the resisting pressure against his shoulder blade diminished a fraction.","The slender, pale neck before him resembled the elegant neck of a white bird. Qin Shaozong pressed his lips against it, clearly feeling the slight tremor of her throat bone beneath his touch.","That unique, refined fragrance seemed to intensify in that moment. Qin Shaozong leaned in even closer, pressing the bridge of his nose against the expanse of skin before him, so fair and tender it seemed one could squeeze water from it.","He traced a path upward bit by bit, following the woman's involuntary tilt of her head, finally placing a kiss just below her lips. \"What does Madam think of my suggestion?\"","Daili's breathing grew somewhat heavy. \"Setting out from Ying County, traveling day and night with fast horses to Yangzhou, one can definitely arrive within half a month. A month for the round trip. Within two months, I must know the results of the search.\"","Qin Shaozong chuckled softly. \"Naturally. If they can't even handle such a small matter properly, it would truly disgrace the Qin name.\"","\"Hurry up and write,\" Daili urged him to pick up the brush again.","Qin Shaozong did not take the brush. Instead, he leaned in once more and kissed her. Different from the last kiss placed on the tip of her chin, this time his lips met her crimson ones."]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35","paragraphs":["The thick layers of clouds in the sky were blown away by the night wind, and the bright moon slowly emerged from behind them. A faint, silvery moonlight showered down upon thousands of households, some landing on upturned eaves and corners, others slipping quietly through open windows into the study.","The room was silent, yet not entirely devoid of sound; occasionally, faint, wet sounds intertwined with soft whimpers.","This was not the first time Dai Li had kissed Qin Shaozong, but whether it was the last time or this one, her heart raced with trepidation. In this regard, he was truly consistent with his outward persona—dominant and utterly uncompromising.","The back of her neck was fixed in place by his large, tiger-paw-like palm, her waist tightly encircled. Trapped within the cage of his arms, Dai Li was like a white crane that had fallen into a swamp, entangled by vines, unable to break free in the slightest.","His advance was fierce, overwhelming in its force.","He was like an arrogant general who had breached the enemy city gates, determined to patrol every corner of the city, leaving no place for the foe to hide.","Her sensitive palate was repeatedly attended to, a terrifying tingling sensation exploding from her neurons, rushing like wildfire to the crown of her head before madly spreading down her spine and meridians, finally reaching her limbs.","Her fingertips trembled uncontrollably, and her back began to shiver with unbearable tension.","The iron arm trapping her moved around her waist, a long, dark finger marked with scars hooked the corner of her garment's sash and gently loosened it.","Today, Dai Li wore a top and skirt, different from the one-piece deep robe. With this two-piece attire, once the sash was undone, there were many opportunities to exploit.","A sea beast covered in rugged scales invaded the territory. It greedily circled the moist, lustrous white jade, occasionally measuring it with its long tail. The rough scales slid against the white jade, leaving faint red marks.","After circling several times, the insatiable sea beast flicked its tail and swam downward along the white jade.","Dai Li's breath hitched. She immediately pushed against him with all her strength, yet he remained unmoved, continuing to trap her against the hard stone wall. Just as she was about to push again, her pupils constricted sharply. A weak nasal sound escaped her, and her entire body trembled violently, her spine almost curling inward.","Forgetting to push him away, Dai Li hurriedly reached a hand downward.","The black-hearted sea beast was stirring up trouble. It had discovered a precious pearl, adored it exceedingly, teased it with its fins, coiled it with its long tail, now closing it within its twin fins, and mischievously grinding its rough scales harshly against it.","Just then, a delicate, pale net descended from the sky, enveloping the malicious sea beast and attempting to drag it away. However, the latter, relying on its massive size, continued to act as it pleased.","Seeing she couldn't pull him away, Dai Li simply clenched her pearly teeth and bit down hard.","Qin Shaozong didn't utter a sound, only pausing for two breaths before, mingled with the taste of blood, launching an even more ferocious assault.","A short, choked whimper escaped Dai Li's throat. As she prepared to bite him again, he seemed to sense it and finally withdrew his hand, pressing the base of his thumb against her jaw. His broad palm completely enveloped her entire jawline, his index finger and thumb gently pressing between her upper and lower teeth through her skin, blocking her second attempt.","He did not separate from her immediately. Deliberately, he sucked and nibbled at that peach-pink, soft tongue, making wet, noisy sounds before Qin Shaozong finally drew back slightly. A smear of blood-red stained his thin lips, which under the lamplight did not appear weak in the slightest, but rather like a tiger that had just finished a meal.","Dai Li's chest heaved violently. \"My son has not yet been found...\"","The base of his thumb was still pressed against her jaw, now rubbing forcefully, with an indescribable greed, until the porcelain-white skin flushed a brilliant crimson.","\"Finding your son is merely a matter of time. Moreover, since messages have been sent to search for him, naturally there will be arrangements for his safe return.\" His eyes burned like blazing stars, intensely scorching. \"Back at the Jiang residence in Nankang Commandery, Madam repeatedly invited me. I have not forgotten a single word of what you said.\"","Dai Li furrowed her delicate brows and pushed against him again, but this time she still couldn't get up. \"Regarding the previous deception, didn't we agree to let bygones be bygones?\"","Qin Shaozong held the woman in his arms tightly, pinning her on his lap. \"Settling this debt by debt is too tedious. Has Madam ever considered a permanent solution?\"","Dai Li knew exactly what this \"permanent solution\" referred to. He still brooded over her rejection and had not given up his desire to draw her into his inner courtyard.","\"I am a rather peculiar person; I actually prefer complications. Besides, even blood brothers must settle accounts clearly. Some things are better kept distinct.\" Dai Li turned her head away.","Her words were resolute, but inwardly, Dai Li had no confidence at all, for at this moment, no one understood better than she how stirred he was. So she hurriedly added, \"My Lord, you are a pillar of the community, a true gentleman of high principles, who treats his subordinates as brothers. Surely you would not force a mere woman who saved the life of your trusted aide.\"","Since he had just mentioned never forgetting her words, it was only polite to return the favor. She could also bring up the \"debt of life.\"","Qin Shaozong did not respond to that line. His kisses fell on the side of her face and her glistening, pale ear. \"Spend this night with me, Madam, and I promise that no matter how distant or perilous the journey, as long as your son is alive, he will return safely to your side. Furthermore, when he comes of age, I will grant him a sinecure, bestow upon him a grand residence and servants, ensuring his wealth and honor for decades to come...\"","The deep, male voice wormed its way into her ear, easily plucking at the strings of Dai Li's heart.","In that moment, he became like the venomous serpent in the Garden of Eden, flicking its crimson forked tongue, cunning beyond measure, each word dripping with immense temptation.","The dark, long finger hooked the sash once more. Just as the loosened garment was about to fall open completely, a soft, pale hand pressed down on the parting robes.","Dai Li whispered, \"What you promise, My Lord, seems too distant to me. Zhou Zhou is only nine this year; it will be eleven years before he comes of age. Many vows between lovers prove unreliable, let alone promises between two people who merely chanced upon each other like drifting duckweed. Who can say what will happen eleven years from now?\"","A vein throbbed on Qin Shaozong's forehead.","Not to mention after he became the head of the Qin clan and took charge of the family, even in his youth before coming of age, no one had ever dared to question him so repeatedly.","Greed and fury intertwined, like adding oil to a raging fire. Just as this inferno was about to set the entire sky ablaze—","A finger, pink like a flower bud, touched his chest, like a cloud bringing rain from the heavens. \"However, the first part of what you said, I find impossible to ignore. Perhaps... I could assist My Lord this once, as full payment for my son's safe return journey.\"","Dai Li drank an entire pot of millet wine during the evening banquet and later caught the wind in the long corridor. Yet, at this moment, she felt not the slightest hint of drunkenness, but was instead exceptionally clear-headed. She realized it was absolutely impossible for her to retreat tonight without being touched at all.","Whether it was his forceful attitude or the conditions he laid out, she could not avoid them.","Choosing the lesser of two evils, Dai Li decided to help him with her hand, just to get it over with.","Her fingers lightly touched his lapel. Through the fabric, she could feel the firm, lean muscles beneath, now heaving intensely with her movements. \"However, I'm in charge this time. You must not move. Can you promise me that, Lord Marquis?\"","The clouds in the sky began to rain, quenching the towering flames of anger. Qin Shaozong's Adam's apple bobbed up and down.","He stared at her without speaking, as if weighing his options, or perhaps considering where to start.","Dai Li feigned displeasure. \"You can't even grant me such a small request? Fine, if that's the case...\"","\"My hands and feet will not move. Proceed, my lady.\" Qin Shaozong cut her off, simultaneously pressing the person who was about to rise back onto himself.","Dai Li secretly frowned.","Hands and feet not moving? What about the rest?","The two, so close they could touch, locked eyes. He understood her doubt, and she saw his unyielding resolve.","This was the furthest he could concede. He could not, and would not, give any more ground.","Dai Li lowered her gaze, her voice soft. \"A gentleman's word is as good as gold.\"","Her jade-white fingertips touched the beast-headed leather belt at his waist. Looking at the tiger's head hidden in shadow, feeling his increasingly heavy breathing, for some reason, she was inexplicably reminded of Pu Songling's tale, \"Three Stories of Wolves: The Wolf.\"","\"A butcher returns home late, his load of meat gone, only bones remain. On the road, two wolves follow him a great distance. The butcher, afraid, throws them a bone. One wolf stops for the bone, the other still follows. He throws another bone. The following wolf stops, but the first wolf catches up again. The bones are all gone...\"1","\"My lady,\" he urged.","Dai Li's spine stiffened, snapping back from her thoughts. \"What's the hurry?\"","The room, with only a small casement window open, was hazy with the scent of alcohol. The few remaining honey candles slowly burned down. One honey candle spent, its small flame flickered twice before suddenly extinguishing.","A corner of the study instantly darkened. In the tide of encroaching gloom, the sound of breathing grew more pronounced. Heavy, urgent, like a gale whipping up towering waves, containing astonishing force.","Amidst the interwoven sounds of light and heavy breaths, an unusual noise occasionally surfaced. A wet, sucking sound, like a newborn tiger cub licking or suckling something.","The moon tilted westward, its silvery light crawling further into the room. In the dim interior, two figures could vaguely be seen on the chair behind the long desk.","Mostly a deep black, but with a small part that was a startling white, as if the layer of grey gauze used to veil a bright pearl was no longer tightly secured.","Dai Li had long since shifted from sitting sideways to sitting upright. Her back pressed against the beechwood desk, her legs parted and tightly flanking his long legs. The loosely tied sash from earlier was now completely undone, parting her upper and lower garments to reveal a sliver of flesh, a moist, translucent white like a ripe lychee, faintly visible as if veiled by a layer of holy moonlight.","That sea creature, clad in jagged scales, tried once more to swim through the layered obstructions toward the deeper, luminous white sea wall. But just as it flicked its tail, about to burrow inward, its fish tail was suddenly slapped with a smack.","\"Don't move!\" Dai Li's breathing was very heavy.","She had withdrawn. The sudden arrival of the cold, empty air became inexplicably unbearable. The veins on the side of Qin Shaozong's neck bulged and then receded. \"My lady...\"","\"A lord's promise is worth a thousand pieces of gold. You agreed to it yourself moments ago.\" Dai Li's retreating hand immediately returned to its original position. She secretly shook her sore, stiff fingers.","Qin Shaozong's long arm encircling her waist tightened, pressing her against him. He buried his face once more into that milky-cake-like, dazzling white.","Dai Li's back stiffened. The prickly stubble on his jaw made her instinctively lean back, only to be blocked by the iron-like arm around her waist.","A night breeze drifted in from the window, causing the flame on the candlestick to dance. The shallow firelight flickered, faintly illuminating the man's canine teeth gleaming in the dark.","The canine teeth caught a thin strap of her undergarment. As he turned his head, the knot on the strap gradually loosened.","Dai Li gasped in surprise, hurriedly reaching out to grab the precarious knot, taking hold of the thin strap and pulling it back. Quickly retying it, she stacked two simple knots and then directly tied a dead knot over them.","A fierce light flared in Qin Shaozong's eyes. But before he could voice his displeasure, her hand returned to its position, retaliating by giving a hard squeeze.","A muscle on the side of his jaw twitched twice. The fierce light in his eyes dimmed for an instant before suddenly blazing up again, fiercer than before. He abruptly lowered his head, causing havoc wantonly through that obstructive undergarment.","Dai Li's cheeks flushed crimson, a fine sheen of sweat breaking out on her forehead.","After who knows how long, a peculiar scent suddenly spread through the room. It had nothing to do with freshness; instead, it somewhat resembled the April-blooming flowers of the Photinia shrub.","The sky was just beginning to lighten. Right at the moment the city gates opened, five fast horses set out from the Grand Marshal's residence in Ying Prefecture, heading straight for the southern gate. Once outside the city, they continued southward, towards Yangzhou.","A military officer's morning training must not be neglected. Even though last night had been utterly debauched, Mo Yanyun still rose early today, arriving punctually at the temporary training ground set up in the residence.","It was early by common standards, but among the military officers, he was relatively late. By the time he arrived, many were already there, some even nearing the end of their morning drills.","\"Mo Yanyun, spar with me.\"","Suddenly being called out, and by his superior at that, Mo Yanyun's burly frame shuddered, his legs inexplicably going a bit weak.","He initially stood frozen in place, then was called again.","\"Come.\" Qin Shaozong had already walked onto the pre-arranged training ground.","A weapon rack stood to the side of the ground. Qin Shaozong didn't choose a blade, casually picking up a long staff instead. Mo Yanyun hesitated, finally selecting a wooden hook.","The two men stepped onto the platform.","Mo Yanyun swallowed. \"Lord Marquis, I beg you to go easy on me.\"","\"On the battlefield, will those charging at you with blades, aiming for your head, listen to your plea of 'go easy on me'?\" Qin Shaozong mocked.","Mo Yanyun immediately fell silent.","Qin Shaozong advanced first, wielding the long staff.","Below the platform.","Feng Feng, the Southern Garrison Commander Bai Jianping, and Yan San, among others, stood watching. The first two chatted in low voices as they observed.","\"His Lordship seems to be in a good mood today.\"","\"I don't think so. If His Lordship were truly pleased, he wouldn't be fighting like this. Ah, Old Mo seems a bit weak. Looks like he overindulged in pleasure last night.\"","\"You still don't know him. He loves nothing but beauties. This mansion is filled with pretty dancers, and he's like a rat falling into a grain barn—utterly in his element. The Lord surely knows of his dissolute ways and is probably reprimanding him right now. Otherwise, why would the Lord be all smiles with us today, yet only have a sour look for Old Mo?\"","\"You make a good point. Old Mo definitely deserves a scolding. Speaking of which, if nothing unexpected happens, Master Nalan should arrive in Ying County this afternoon.\"","\"By the way, yesterday the Lord urgently summoned over a dozen carpenters from the county, ordering them to work overtime to build a dragon-bone waterwheel according to the drawings. With everyone's combined effort, it should be finished around noon. Wouldn't that mean Master Nalan can see that irrigation marvel as soon as he arrives at the mansion?\"","\"That would be excellent.\"","...","\"Clang—\"","Following the wooden hook being knocked from his hand and clattering to the ground, Mo Yanyun himself was thrown heavily onto the floor. This fall was hard, making him grimace in pain as he hurriedly begged for mercy, \"My Lord, I yield. No more.\"","Qin Shaozong finished with a flourish of his staff. His breathing was steady, though his whole body steamed with the heat of exertion. \"Though there has been no recent battle, training must not slacken.\"","Mo Yanyun nodded repeatedly, though inwardly he was puzzled.","He hadn't slacked off in his training—hadn't he come for morning practice today? At most, he'd only relaxed last night. Could it be the Lord's anger hasn't subsided yet, and he can't stand to see him so carefree?","Mo Yanyun didn't know, and he didn't dare ask.","When Daili woke up, it was bright outside. Perhaps because half the matter was resolved and it seemed there wouldn't be major obstacles ahead, she had slept exceptionally well last night.","Daili vaguely remembered having a pleasant dream. In the dream, her little one was found. During her absence, Zhou Zhou had been adopted by a kind family. Although their food, clothing, and shelter couldn't compare to before, and the little one had gotten much tanner, he was still as lively and cheerful as ever.","After getting up and washing, Daili had just opened her door when she saw two people standing outside.","Two young women, at most in their early twenties. One tall, one short. The taller one had a small black mole on the tip of her nose. The slightly shorter one had round, cat-like eyes that lent her a somewhat adorable appearance.","Both were dressed simply. Behind them were stacked three identical wooden boxes, their style resembling clothing trunks.","Upon seeing Daili, the two women curtsied and spoke in unison, \"Madam, we are here to serve you, as instructed by the noble lord.\"","Daili didn't need to ask who this \"noble lord\" was. She frowned. \"I have no need for servants. You may return.\"","The two women looked troubled. The round-eyed maid's eyes even welled up with tears as she immediately knelt down. \"Madam, please, have mercy and take us in. If we leave your side, Bipo and I will be sent back to the slave market. That place is a mixed bag, all sorts of people are there. Some masters buy slaves purely to keep them as outlets for their anger... it's a living death...\"","The taller Bipo also knelt, even kowtowing. \"We beg for your grace, Madam, to take in Nianxia and me. We can do any hard work, and we promise to obey your every word, serving you faithfully to repay your kindness.\"","Previously, Daili had been determined not to take on maids. She didn't want to form other connections. But seeing the two young women trembling as they knelt before her, she couldn't help but recall last night's beautiful dream.","In the dream, her Zhou Zhou had been adopted by kind people. In reality, if she didn't keep these two, would she become one of those indifferent faces watching her own little one wander helplessly...","\"Alright, get up,\" Daili sighed.","Their faces instantly brightened with smiles. They rose, reported their names, and asked if Daili wished to rename them.","Daili naturally shook her head, telling them to keep their own names.","\"These clothing trunks were sent by the noble lord. There are also some jewelry and other items to follow. Madam, Bipo and I will first move these into the room,\" Nianxia said with a smile.","The clothes Daili was wearing were still the drab, gray dress she had prepared for her escape—the most ordinary color and fabric, with just two sets to alternate between.","She thought it was fine, but last night in the study, someone had been quite disdainful of it.","Bipo and Nianxia were quick and efficient. They moved what needed moving, organized what needed organizing, even meticulously wiped down all the furnishings in the room, and then lit incense in the censer.","In just two short quarters of an hour, the already not-old room seemed to sparkle like new.","\"Nianxia, please go to the study and fetch a set of calligraphy tools and a book for me. Any book will do. If anyone asks, say I wish to practice my handwriting,\" Daili said when Nianxia came to ask for instructions once more.","It's better to rely on oneself than others. She needed to learn brush calligraphy and cursive script. If she ever needed to write a letter one day, she'd have to do it herself.","Nianxia accepted the order and left, returning soon after with the requested items.","Mulberry-bark paper was spread out on the desk, pine-soot ink was ground to a dark hue on the inkstone, and the wolf-hair brush was placed on the rest.","Daili picked up the brush, trying to adjust her grip based on memories of the proper posture. But after holding it a couple of times, it just felt wrong everywhere. She couldn't help but furrow her delicate brows.","The brush felt wrong. Her hand felt wrong.","The former was a matter of sensation; the latter, a matter of state.","In frustration, Daili threw the brush down."]},{"number":36,"title":"Chapter 36","paragraphs":["As the sun climbed to the zenith of the firmament and began its descent toward the west, a convoy of carriages escorted by cavalry entered Ying Commandery through the northern gate.","Amidst the rhythmic clatter of hooves, a carriage with an unassuming exterior traveled smoothly through the streets, finally coming to a halt before a lavish residence with its main gates thrown wide open.","The carriage door opened, and a figure clad in long green robes stepped out. Mo Yanyun, Feng Feng, and the others waiting by the entrance broke into smiles.","\"It has been over a month since we parted. Nalan Zhi, your complexion is much improved; it seems you have fully recovered.\"","\"A cause for celebration indeed.\"","The figure in green looked up, revealing a man of about fifty years. He had a pale complexion, long ears, and a long beard, exuding the air of a scholar. However, starkly at odds with his gentle temperament was a black mark upon his right cheek.","It was not a birthmark, but a black brand with sharp edges and a distinct pattern within.","This was a man who had once suffered the punishment of facial branding.","Nalan Zhi smiled and replied, \"I would not say fully recovered, but I am barely fit enough for long journeys. However, when news of the Lord's encirclement strategy reached me, my spirits were greatly lifted. It was enough to instantly cure seven parts of a nine-part illness.\"","Feng Feng laughed heartily. \"Then, when you see the Dragon Bone Waterwheel later, surely the remaining two parts of your ailment will vanish like mist in the wind?\"","\"What is this Dragon Bone Waterwheel? To make a knowledgeable Xuanxiao Cavalry Captain like yourself so excited, it must be something extraordinary,\" Nalan Zhi asked curiously.","The Dragon Bone Waterwheel—the name was certainly ingenious.","Feng Feng gestured with his hand, inviting Nalan Zhi to enter the mansion first. The latter smiled, stroked his long beard, and walked in alongside him.","As they walked, the two men vividly recounted the events of the previous day to Nalan Zhi.","Mo Yanyun began with his initial report, describing how Dai Li had used a tree branch as a brush to draw in the courtyard, and how Qin Shaozong had ordered a dozen carpenters to work through the night to build the waterwheel.","Feng Feng picked up the thread, \"The Dragon Bone Waterwheel was moved to the rear garden just a short while ago. The Marquis is there now. Would Nalan Zhi care to go take a look?\"","Nalan Zhi naturally nodded in agreement.","Having just arrived, propriety dictated he pay his respects to his Lord first. Moreover, unless he saw this invention with his own eyes, his curiosity would remain unbearably unquenched.","The afternoon sun was pleasant. The mansion's rear garden was built on a grand scale, landscaped with rockeries and strange stones, with pavilions and waterside terraces rising from the ground.","A breeze swept past, carrying the elegant fragrance of flowers throughout the garden. Amidst the fresh, pleasant scent, the sound of water was distinct. It was not the gentle gurgle of a spring-fed stream, but a loud, rushing sound, like floodgates opening.","Mo Yanyun, caught off guard, accidentally stepped into a puddle. \"Strange. Why is there water here? Did the pond leak?\"","\"You blockhead, the Marquis must be testing the Dragon Bone Waterwheel,\" Feng Feng retorted grumpily.","Nalan Zhi quickened his pace, following the sound. After rounding a rockery adorned with flowering vines, his view suddenly opened up.","The pond, vast as a lake, was exceptionally broad. A pavilion stood upon the water, connected to the shore by a winding walkway, and snow-white cranes could be seen flapping their wings by the water's edge. Yet, none of these sights could hold Nalan Zhi's gaze.","He stared unblinkingly at the wooden dragon by the pond.","The wooden dragon was about twenty feet long, its tail dipped into the pond, with a body made of linked wooden planks winding upward. As a burly man at the top turned the 'dragon horn' at the dragon's head, the mouth spewed a continuous stream of water.","That powerful rushing sound from earlier originated right here.","A piercing light appeared in Nalan Zhi's eyes, like a meteor streaking across the night sky. He did not even pause to exchange pleasantries with Qin Shaozong, whom he hadn't seen in over a month. Instead, after a quick bow, he asked, \"My Lord, where is the creator of this Dragon Bone Waterwheel? May I meet her?\"","Even though Mo and Feng had not explained the waterwheel's capacity or that animal power could replace human labor, Nalan Zhi saw through its potential at a glance.","He saw even further—","More water meant more arable land, which meant increased grain production. It meant grain reserves for the North, surplus food in the homes of the Northern people, and a massive surge in his Lord's prestige.","Extending beyond that, it meant benefits for all the people under heaven.","This was absolutely an object destined to leave its mark on history, and correspondingly, history would reserve a place for its inventor.","\"When the waterwheel arrived, I sent someone to inform the Madam. She will be here shortly,\" Qin Shaozong said with a smile, addressing Nalan Zhi by his courtesy name. \"Wugong, you just need to wait.\"","*","After throwing down her brush, Dai Li stared at the books on her desk for a long while. Thinking of the events of the previous night, she finally took a deep breath and picked up the wolf-hair brush once more.","She had barely finished copying a single character when Bipo entered the room from outside. \"Madam, a soldier has come to the courtyard. He says the Dragon Bone Waterwheel has been delivered to the rear garden, and the Marquis invites you to go take a look.\"","Dai Li's eyes widened involuntarily. \"So fast?\"","She had only drawn the design yesterday at noon. In just one short day—a mere twenty-four hours—the physical object had been built?","How many artisans had he put to work simultaneously?","\"Alright, I'll go over there now.\" Dai Li set down the wolf-hair brush, which was starting to feel heavy in her hand.","\"Madam...\"","Dai Li turned to look at Nianxia. \"What is it?\"","Nianxia whispered, \"Many beautiful clothes were delivered just now. Would you like this servant to help you change into them?\"","Dai Li was currently wearing her simplest grey dress. Judging by this outfit alone, eight out of ten common women in the marketplace dressed exactly the same.","It would not matter in an ordinary household, but within these high gates—especially in the premier mansion of Ying Commandery—even the lowest-ranking dancer would likely be dressed far better than her.","Nianxia knew well that, aside from the official wife, all the women in the backyard relied on the master's favor to survive. She had seen concubines in wealthy households lose favor and fall from the clouds—from cherished flowers held by all, to mud scattered on the ground.","With favor came power and influence; without it came decay.","She was now Madam Dai's servant. When the master prospers, the servant glories. She sincerely hoped this mistress would remain in favor for a long time.","But Dai Li said, \"No need. This will do.\"","Nianxia and Bipo wanted to persuade her further, but Dai Li had already stepped out the door.","Taking the shortcut, the journey wasn't far.","When she reached the moon gate connecting to the rear garden, Dai Li heard the sound of Qin Shaozong speaking with someone else.","The voice was unfamiliar; she hadn't heard it before. However, judging by the way Qin Shaozong spoke as if chatting with a close friend, she deduced that this person must be a key official under his command.","Dai Li thought of that Nalan Zhi. It seemed this heavyweight strategist had finally arrived.","She curled her lips into a smile, her steps instantly becoming lighter.","...","Nalan Zhi learned from his Lord that Madam Dai was merely the messenger. She claimed the inventor of the Dragon Bone Waterwheel was someone else, and the Lord asked him if he knew of a man named Ma Jun.","But he searched through every famous scholar, great and small, stored in his memory, yet he could not find this \"Ma Jun\" in any corner of his mind.","There was no such person. No, rather, he should say he was unaware of such a figure.","Thus, this Lady Dai became the key.","Aside from the moment he entered the manor, Nalan Zhi had heard no further news of Dai Li. In his imagination, this Lady Dai ought to be a simple, rustic peasant woman.","He imagined she might be forty or fifty years old, her skin darkened by years of labor, living in the secluded village where the hermit Ma Jun had hidden away from the world. One day, the great hermit invented this world-shocking device, but as he was unable to leave due to other matters, he entrusted this Lady Dai to carry the blueprints out of the village and deliver them to the Lord, who happened to be nearby.","However, when that figure clad in grey-black entered his field of vision, Nalan Zhi was stunned into a rare, prolonged silence.","There are some whose beauty cannot be concealed by attire. Even dressed in old, plain clothing, a halo of temperament seemed to shine from her, illuminating features that were already transcendent.","The vibrant spring colors filling the garden seemed to dim significantly with her arrival.","Dai Li saw the ink brand on Nalan Zhi's face. The mark was hideous, looking at first glance like a black centipede coiled upon his skin.","Leaving aside the myriad strange tattoos of the modern world, compared to which this was mere child's play, she could not afford to show even a hint of rejection or disdain, simply because she would need this Mr. Nalan to counterbalance Qin Shaozong in the future.","Dai Li offered a polite smile, as if the ink brand did not exist. \"Earlier, I heard Commander Mo and the others chatting, saying that a scholar of unparalleled talent, well-versed in both the past and present, would be arriving at the manor today. I assume that must be you. Mr. Nalan, I have long looked forward to meeting you.\"","From the moment Dai Li stepped into the rear garden, Qin Shaozong's gaze had been fixed upon her.","He watched her sweep a breezy glance over everyone else, himself included, the corners of her lips tilting up slightly in what passed for a greeting, before she went straight to speaking with Nalan Zhi.","Starting right off with a heap of flattery, and claiming she had 'long looked forward' to meeting him? If she hadn't previously confessed to living in a secluded utopia cut off from the world, she would have sounded quite convincing.","Heh, she was definitely harboring ulterior motives again.","Qin Shaozong twirled his jade thumb ring, watching coldly as Dai Li exchanged pleasantries with Nalan Zhi, his gaze dark and inscrutable.","In the eyes of Nianxia and Bipo, the scene was utterly inconceivable. It was as if a thousand-foot wave had risen in a vast ocean, crashing fiercely against the shore and shattering everything they had ever known.","In their limited experience, even the official wife of a bureaucrat was required to show respect to her husband's direct subordinates and officials.","If an official wife must behave so, how much more so for concubines and mistresses...","Yet now, they stared dumbfounded as Dai Li, dressed in old clothes, conversed with the green-robed gentleman as if no one else were present.","Everyone in the rear garden was watching them. Whether it was the Lord Marquis who was said to control the entire North, or the commanders, captains, and soldiers standing by, not a single person spoke up to interrupt. The vast garden seemed to center around the two of them, while everyone else waited in silence.","She wore no fine silks or golden hairpins, yet she glowed like a luminous pearl, shockingly brilliant.","Nianxia felt a bit dazed, thinking she might still be dreaming; otherwise, how could she be witnessing such a surreal scene?","Establishing an instant rapport with someone like Nalan Zhi was, in Dai Li's view, not actually difficult.","For a famous scholar capable of serving as a strategist under a powerful noble and holding a significant position, profound knowledge was merely the baseline. Following that were traits like decisiveness in planning and an insight into the human heart.","Combining Qin Shaozong's high standards with the respectful attitude of those around him, Dai Li surmised that this Mr. Nalan, in addition to the aforementioned qualities, likely possessed unbending pride and compassion. He was likely someone who cared for the common people and took the peace of the realm as his personal duty.","As someone standing at the vantage point of the future—specifically one who had worked in a state-owned publishing house editing and reviewing books mostly related to history and agriculture—Dai Li found it perfectly within her wheelhouse to impress a scholar from a thousand years ago.","After all, the information gap lay squarely between them.","Feng Feng stood beside Qin Shaozong. As time slowly passed, he felt an inexplicable chill, though he didn't know if it was an illusion.","He looked around. The tested keel waterwheel had stopped working, and the wind that had risen earlier had stilled. There was no breeze blowing water vapor their way, and the golden sun in the sky was shining fine, unblocked by clouds.","Feng Feng had climbed from a destitute refugee to his current position thanks in no small part to a mind more flexible and acute than the average person. He scanned the area, finally keeping his head still while his eyes darted quickly to the side to look at his superior, then followed his superior's gaze to the woman not far away.","Suddenly, it dawned on Feng Feng what was happening.","Dai Li used the keel waterwheel as a starting point to discuss crops with Nalan Zhi.","The crops of this era were primarily \"millet.\" Because of its short growing season and tolerance for poor soil and drought, millet had always occupied a core position, despite its relatively low yield. One could simply plant it in newly reclaimed wasteland, and it would survive.","Later, following the rise of large-scale water conservancy projects across the land, wheat—which had a high demand for water—gradually covered the North. Winter wheat was planted in autumn and harvested in summer, allowing for rotation with other crops, and compared to millet, the yield of wheat was significantly higher.","Dai Li paced the conversation carefully, not talking with Nalan Zhi for too long. Just when his interest was clearly piqued, she seemed to suddenly realize that she and Nalan Zhi were not the only ones in the garden. She hurriedly turned her head toward Qin Shaozong, who was a few steps away. \"My Lord...\"","The words that followed stuck in her throat. His expression—an enigmatic half-smile that seemed to see through everything—made Dai Li suspect that this man knew her plan.","He had likely guessed that she wanted to use Nalan Zhi to counterbalance him.","\"If I recall correctly, the last time Madam was this enthusiastic and hit it off so well with someone, it wasn't long before she schemed against that 'old friend,' nearly costing him everything,\" Qin Shaozong said with profound meaning.","Dai Li: \"...\"","He was a perfectly fine man, so why did he have to have a mouth like that?","It seemed he really had guessed it.","But it didn't matter. Even if he guessed it, she could use it as an overt stratagem. In any case, this was something she absolutely had to do!","Nalan Zhi looked surprised, his gaze shuttling between the two of them thoughtfully.","\"Mr. Nalan has only just arrived at the manor today; I imagine the Lord has many important matters to discuss with you, so I will not disturb you further.\" Dai Li decided to retreat for now, avoiding the brunt of the confrontation and waiting for a more suitable opportunity to strike.","She looked at Nalan Zhi, smiling as politely as before. \"Mr. Nalan, until we meet again.\"","After Dai Li left, the garden fell silent for a moment. The atmosphere was indescribably strange. Finally, Nalan Zhi gave a light cough. \"My Lord, this keel waterwheel is truly superior to the swape and the scoop by an unknown measure. Now is the season for spring plowing; it would be best to gather the carpenters and have them produce a small batch first. Then, distribute these keel waterwheels to the various commanderies of the North, and post notices in the cities to widely publicize the method of their construction. I imagine that within a year, this device will spread throughout the entire North.\"","Recalling the wheat Dai Li had just mentioned, Nalan Zhi stroked his long beard. \"If fetching water becomes significantly easier, the wheat yields will increase, sweeping through thousands of households like a spring breeze.\"","If the common people lived well and had ample surplus grain at home, collecting grain taxes from them would also be convenient.","Qin Shaozong nodded. \"That is exactly my intention as well.\"","The implementation of the keel water wheel was imperative. The money and manpower consumed in the initial stage, whether great or small, would pale into insignificance compared to the future results.","Nalan Zhi couldn't help but ask, \"My Lord, this Lady Dai is extraordinary. Where exactly is she from?\"","Qin Shaozong let out a light chuckle. \"She escaped from a fox's den.\"","Nalan Zhi’s hand trembled, nearly plucking out a hair from his beard. Even knowing that his Lord could be sharp-tongued at times, he was still astonished at this moment.","The Lord rarely commented on young women in the past. Such unusual and subjective wording was, to his knowledge, a first.","His gaze shifted toward Mo Yanyun, whose expression was complicated. Judging by his look, Lady Dai's background and deeds were not something that could be explained in a few words.","*","Dai Li returned to her room, planning to take a nap before going to \"accidentally\" meet Nalan Zhi. Presumably, they would have finished discussing important matters by then, and Mr. Nalan would be free.","However, as she turned to sit on the couch, Dai Li looked up to meet two pairs of eyes. One pair was round like a cat's, the other slightly narrower. The shapes were different, but the gazes were identical in their fervor.","Dai Li was startled. \"What's wrong with you two?\"","\"Madam, you...\" Nianxia's face turned red from holding back, and finally, she only managed to squeeze out, \"You're so amazing!\"","Beside her, Bipo nodded repeatedly as well. \"I have never seen anyone as imposing as you before.\"","Although they were vague, Dai Li understood. They had never seen a maverick woman like her, so they found it extremely novel.","Dai Li sighed and said something they didn't quite understand. \"In the future, the distant future, everything will get better.\"","In the final analysis, it was the limitation of the era. This man-eating feudal era had cut off their path to reading and becoming officials, binding thousands upon thousands of women, trapping them in backyards where they could only live at the mercy of others.","If only it were possible...","A certain thought flickered for a moment, only to be dismissed by Dai Li.","Impossible. It was impractical.","When the dust of an era settles on a single person, it weighs as heavy as a mountain. How could she fight against the entire era with her strength alone? She was currently a clay idol crossing a river—hardly able to save herself, let alone possessing the ability to save others.","Nianxia and Bipo truly didn't understand, but that didn't stop them from nodding at whatever Dai Li said now. \"Madam is right.\"","\"I'm going to take a nap. Please wake me in an hour.\" Dai Li lay on the couch and pulled the quilt over herself.","The two maids agreed.","Listening to the chirping of insects outside the window, her mind slowly calmed down, and Dai Li soon fell into a deep sleep.","When she said an hour, Nianxia timed it precisely, not missing by even a moment. An hour later, Dai Li was awakened. After a short nap, her spirits were higher, and she decided to go out and run into Nalan Zhi.","Perhaps her luck was good today; not long after walking out of the main courtyard, Dai Li saw people going in and out of a courtyard pavilion not far away. Her intuition told her someone might have moved in.","Walking over to take a look, she hadn't guessed wrong. Not only was she right, but she had also found her target.","Dai Li's eyes curved into a smile, and she immediately invited herself in.","The idle people in the courtyard had mostly retreated, leaving only a young man in his early twenties, dressed as a servant, organizing boxes.","Hearing footsteps, he turned his head. After a moment of stunned silence, his face flushed red. \"Who... who are you?\"","\"Is Mr. Nalan here? I have business with him,\" Dai Li said.","Inside, Nalan Zhi heard the voice and came out, personally inviting Dai Li in. \"Lady Dai, please come inside to talk. Musen, stop organizing for now. Go boil some water and serve tea to the Lady.\"","Dai Li followed him into the room.","Nalan Zhi's room had excellent lighting. The furnishings inside did not appear rich or extravagant; instead, they were quiet and elegant, showing that care had been put into the arrangement.","After taking a seat, Dai Li didn't beat around the bush and got straight to the point. \"Mr. Nalan, I wish to ask you to act as a persuader. I want you to convince the Lord to allow me to join his council of advisors.\""]},{"number":37,"title":"Chapter 37","paragraphs":["The doors within the room were wide open, and outside the windows lay a small, serene bamboo grove. In this leisurely afternoon, the intermittent chirping of insects drifted in from outside, becoming the only sound in the room now.","When he first heard Daili say, \"Master Nalan, until we meet again,\" Nalan Zhi had a faint premonition in his heart.","\"Until we meet again\"—they would indeed meet later.","At the time, he simply felt that they really should meet again. They still had much to discuss, and he himself was not yet satisfied—how could they meet only once?","But later, after Mo Yanyun privately told him about the origins of this Lady Daili, Nalan Zhi thought to himself that she was not merely \"extraordinary.\" Such boldness in action was perhaps one in ten thousand.","However, shock aside, Nalan Zhi still greatly admired Daili. Now, hearing her express a desire to join the strategist group, his face showed only surprise, without any trace of scorn or arrogance.","After a moment of silence, Nalan Zhi spoke, \"Lady Dai, we share similar interests, so I will be frank with you. Unlike many powerful lords who keep thousands of retainers and advisors, our lord has rather strict requirements. In the early years, those scholars who came to seek patronage, once he deemed them merely mediocre, would not be employed at all. Later, he even established rigorous examinations, turning away many who did not meet his standards, showing a clear preference for quality over quantity.\"","Daili smiled gently. \"Master Nalan treats me with sincerity, so I will also be honest with you. In fact, I already mentioned this to the Marquis yesterday. The most important reason he gave for refusing me then was that I am a woman. He said women are only suited to admiring flowers within the manor, and that dealing with schemes and intrigues is men's business.\"","As she spoke to the end, Daili lowered her eyelids, for she was truly furious, and looking directly at Nalan Zhi would too easily betray her feelings.","Daili's tone gradually became flat. \"I privately believe the Marquis is mistaken in saying so. As the saying goes, whether a cat is black or white, if it catches mice, it's a good cat. If someone can bring a continuous stream of financial revenue to the Xuanxiao Cavalry, and indeed to the entire Northern region, why can't she become the precedent?\"","Nalan Zhi was stunned.","Bring financial revenue to the Xuanxiao Cavalry, and the entire Northern region?","What an audacious and proud statement!","If Nalan Zhi had merely been helpless a moment ago, now his doubt was evident. \"Might I ask where the continuous financial revenue Lady Dai speaks of would come from?\"","Daili said only two words: \"Refined salt.\"","This era had no refined salt, because in the not-too-distant pre-Qin period, the utilization of salt was still in a relatively primitive stage.","The Qin and Han dynasties saw its beginnings, and only when time entered the \"Tang\" period did the salt industry reach a completely new stage.","Daili was well aware that she was now walking a tightrope over a cliff; a single misstep could lead to utter ruin.","Salt taxes had existed since the Zhou dynasty. During the Spring and Autumn period, the state of Qi, under Guan Zhong's guidance, reorganized the salt industry, creating enormous profits through a system of \"official procurement and official sale.\"","Whether it was the emperors of the Five Dynasties and Ten Kingdoms period, or later Huang Chao, the Yellow King who directly captured Chang'an, or even Li Zan, who previously occupied Ying Commandery and posed a threat and unease to Qin Shaozong, the ruler of the North—they all started by selling illegal salt.","Those in power were deeply aware of the profits from \"salt,\" so they kept a very tight rein on this area, often resorting to the elimination of entire clans.","This matter absolutely could not be discussed directly with Qin Shaozong. Judging by the man's methods in dealing with Jiang Chonghai and Li Zan, he was undoubtedly a formidable figure.","To say such a man's rules and morals were flexible would be an overstatement.","Nalan Zhi's expression changed dramatically. \"Refined salt?\"","That single word \"refined\" was enough to shatter Nalan Zhi's composure. He had not considered the possibility that Daili might be speaking nonsense, but that thought lasted only a moment before he dismissed it.","There was no need.","Matters concerning salt were no trivial affair. Throughout history, countless people had lost their heads over it. She had no reason to make such a potentially life-threatening joke.","\"Lady Dai, do you understand what those two words of yours represent?\" Nalan Zhi asked her.","Daili looked at the fair-skinned man with a long beard before her. He was over fifty, the marks of time and hardship on his face heavier than on most, his hair mostly grayed—likely his earlier years had been very difficult. That ink-black mark clung to his face like a stubborn insect; timid children might burst into tears at the sight.","But Nalan Zhi's eyes were clear. Even though the lines of time surrounded them, and his face bore the mark of a convict, he remained gentle, like the clear stream in a mountain creek, or the spring breeze brushing over the open scrolls on the desk.","He did not exclaim in shock, nor did he sternly reprimand her for being absurd, nor did he call guards to subject her to harsh interrogation to see how much could be extracted.","He was confirming her earlier words, giving her a well-intentioned reminder. A reminder that some words should not be spoken carelessly. If she denied it now, he would not speak of it to others and could pretend it never happened.","Daili thought to herself that while Qin Shaozong might not be much of a man, his judgment of people was indeed impeccable.","\"I understand.\" Daili knew very well what she was doing. Some things, however dangerous, were necessary paths.","\"Currently, salt largely comes from three sources: boiling seawater, excavating salt wells, and mining rock salt from mountains. The first method often results in disappointing purity due to impurities like silt and shells mixed in the water. The latter two are difficult to extract and limited in quantity, hence the saying, 'Boiling the sea is easy, boiling the well is hard.'\"","At this point, Daili smiled. \"Natural salt springs and salt wells are mostly located in the southwest. I imagine there are almost none in this region that the Marquis could utilize.\"","With each sentence she spoke, Nalan Zhi grew more solemn. By now, he was sitting upright with grave attention. \"It is indeed 'Boiling the sea is easy, boiling the well is hard.' Then, in your view, Lady, how can today's salt be transformed into the refined salt you speak of?\"","If Qin Shaozong had asked this, Daili would definitely have been evasive.","She and Qin Shaozong were almost like parties in a clear-cut transaction. She exchanged the dragon-bone water pump for information on the Qin clan's collateral branch, and then, with certain undisclosed bargaining chips, secured his order for that branch to search for her son and return him safely to her side.","She would not release the hawk without seeing the hare. If the person sitting across from her were Qin Shaozong, not to mention the follow-up, she wouldn't even have mentioned the two words \"refined salt.\"","Just then, the attendant Musen entered with boiled water. Seeing a tea set and cups on the table, Daili simply took over the task of preparing tea, letting Musen return to tidying the previously unpacked chests.","Only after the other had left did Daili speak: \"There are many methods. One method involves constructing high embankments on land where the tidal waves do not reach, making the land suitable for salt cultivation. Salt-growing households each have their own demarcated plots, not encroaching on each other's boundaries. If one anticipates no rain the next morning, then that day, one broadly spreads rice or wheat straw ash, or reed and rush ash, about an inch thick over the ground, pressing it flat and even. By dawn the next day, when the dew-laden air rises, salt efflorescence will emerge beneath. At midday, if it clears, the ash and salt are swept up together for leaching and boiling.\"","...","Nianxia and Bipo came with Daili but did not enter the room with her. The two women, knowing this courtyard housed an honored guest, dared not intrude. So, after Daili went inside, they merely waited outside the main gate of the courtyard.","Initially, they thought Lady Dai's visit wouldn't last long, but an hour passed with no sign of her emerging. After much more time, when the golden sun had nearly sunk to the horizon and their feet had grown numb from standing, the lady still hadn't come out.","Finally unable to stand any longer, the two maids sat down leaning against the wall.","So when Qin Shaozong returned from his study, he saw from a distance what looked like two short posts by the gate of Nalan Zhi's courtyard.","He had seen these two maids in the rear garden earlier and knew they were Lady Dai's personal attendants. Seeing them now outside Nalan Zhi's courtyard, and in such a seated state...","He couldn't help but suspect that a certain fox had been burrowing into that particular courtyard for over an hour. Such a long time—had she perhaps dug herself a fox den inside?","\"Lord.\"","\"Lord.\"","Upon seeing Qin Shaozong approach, the two women hurriedly stood and bowed.","Qin Shaozong didn't even bother asking if Lady Dai was inside, going straight to the point: \"How long has the lady been here?\"","Nianxia: \"The lady arrived around the Hour of the Goat.\"","Qin Shaozong calculated in his mind.","Well then, she'd been inside for nearly two hours. Likely she'd managed to dig several fox holes by now.","Qin Shaozong stepped inside. Before even entering the main room, he could see from a distance the two of them chatting merrily, with Nalan Zhi smiling as he refilled the teacup for the lady opposite him.","If their encounter in the rear garden had seemed like they'd become fast friends, judging by the current scene, they had progressed to becoming close confidants despite the age difference.","Striding into the room, Qin Shaozong raised an eyebrow, his tone laced with meaning. \"Wugong, what interesting matters are you discussing with the lady? Don't be stingy, share them with me as well.\"","Dai Li was slightly startled, turning her head at the sound of his voice.","Unnoticed, dusk had fallen.","The orange-gold sunlight dyed large swathes of the sky in brilliant hues, also draping a layer of golden gauze over the man in the courtyard. Yet this man's aura was truly formidable; even wrapped in the warmth of the setting sun, he still carried a sharp, dangerous edge, like a blade about to be drawn.","The curve at the corner of Dai Li's lips faded slightly. But recalling her conversation with Nalan Zhi, she raised her smile again. \"Of course we can tell you, my lord. I only fear some of the talk might displease you.\"","She and Nalan Zhi sat facing each other at either end of a square table. Qin Shaozong took a seat to their side.","Without waiting for anyone to serve him, he reached over to the wooden box beside him, took out a cup, and said leisurely, \"Have I not heard enough of the lady's disagreeable words?\"","Dai Li looked at Nalan Zhi opposite her. He gave her an inquiring look. She smiled and nodded slightly, her left hand resting on her knee slowly curling into a fist.","There's no day like today. No need to wait any longer. She would muster her courage and fit the muzzle onto this fierce tiger in one go.","The corner of Qin Shaozong's eye seemed to sweep past them inadvertently, taking in their expressions. The man's narrow eyes narrowed further, a pool of darkness settling in their depths.","\"For those in high positions, recognizing and promoting exceptional talent should not be hindered by lowly origins. For those below, recommending the worthy should not avoid one's own kin or enemies. My lord, today I wish to recommend an exceptional talent to you.\" Nalan Zhi stood up and bowed respectfully to Qin Shaozong.","Qin Shaozong didn't speak immediately. Instead, he turned to look at Dai Li. They sat side by side, merely an arm's length apart, close enough to touch each other with a reach. He clearly saw her eyes crinkle into a smile after Nalan Zhi stood up, her long, straight lashes lifting like tiny fans.","Well then. In just a short afternoon, she had truly managed to dig herself a fox den.","The stage was set. Qin Shaozong could only gesture for Nalan Zhi to rise. \"Wugong, there's no need for such formality. Please, tell me, what remarkable person is worthy of you holding them in such esteem?\"","Nalan Zhi straightened up, speaking solemnly. \"It is Lady Dai. Many praise me as outstanding among my peers, saying I am learned and extraordinary. But today, I feel deeply ashamed. The phrase 'learned' is something I dare not claim in Lady Dai's presence.\"","Qin Shaozong had guessed Nalan Zhi would recommend Dai Li, but he hadn't expected him to humble himself to this extent.","Nalan Zhi had never been one to flatter and fawn. If in his early years in Chang'an he had been willing to bow and scrape before the powerful, the reforms he proposed back then would not have been entirely rejected. The Nalan family would not have been framed by treacherous individuals, causing him to suffer the indelible punishment of facial tattooing and his entire family to be exiled a thousand miles to Youzhou.","All these years, his original aspirations remained unchanged, his unyielding integrity unbroken.","Such a man would absolutely not use himself as a stepping stone for others to climb upon, whether out of pity or any other reason.","\"Why is Wugong being so modest?\" Qin Shaozong asked, puzzled.","Nalan Zhi shook his head with a smile. \"My lord, it is not modesty, but facing facts. To be perfectly honest, even if I lived another sixty years, or even longer, I could not devise a method to perfectly purify the salt we have today.\"","Those brown pupils constricted sharply. Qin Shaozong instinctively turned to look at Dai Li beside him. She merely smiled politely, showing little surprise on her face, as if all his reactions were within her expectations.","\"Purify salt? How?\" Qin Shaozong pressed.","Dai Li did not answer his question. Instead, she picked up the earthenware pot on the table and poured water for him, tentatively asking, \"My lord, may I now address you as 'my lord' in the manner of a retainer?\"","Qin Shaozong's temple twitched.","The air seemed to solidify. Steam rose from the hot water in the cup, blurring Qin Shaozong's inscrutable, shadowed expression.","Nalan Zhi spoke up at the opportune moment. \"My lord, in ancient times, there was the story of buying a horse bone for a thousand gold to show sincerity, and building a golden platform to widely recruit talents from across the land. In the past, you did not look down upon me, a convicted man bearing the mark of punishment. Today, why should you turn Lady Dai away from your door simply because she is a woman?\"","That cup filled with tea sat beside Qin Shaozong's hand. The veins on the back of his hand stood out. The tip of his index finger subconsciously lifted towards the cup before being forced back down.","He stared at the steaming cup before him, his gaze fierce. It wasn't as if he was looking at an ordinary vessel, but rather a piece of fragrant meat dangled before his mouth that he simply couldn't bite.","\"I beg you, my lord, to consider the greater picture,\" Nalan Zhi spoke again.","That large, dark hand finally moved. It shifted forward a foot, grasping the teacup. Qin Shaozong turned to look at Dai Li, a terrifying darkness settled in his eyes. His smile didn't reach them as he said, \"The lady has remarkable skills. Regarding the matter of salt purification, I await with great interest. I hope the lady does not disappoint me.\"","Dai Li could hardly miss his anger. His gaze was still ferociously intense, as if he wished to tear her apart and devour her.","But now that she had been promoted to advisor, with a figurative \"pardon token\" added to her person, Dai Li wasn't the least bit flustered. On the contrary, she deliberately addressed him once more as \"my lord,\" then said, \"You shall see.\"","Crick. A faint sound.","A small crack appeared in the ceramic teacup in Qin Shaozong's hand, tiny beads of water slowly seeping out from within.","Yangzhou.","The Qin clan's rising heat in the northern lands sent shockwaves rippling a thousand miles away, its terrifying aftershocks still felt.","This branch of the Qin clan, rooted in Fanhua County of Yangzhou, often had a bustling gate with constant streams of visitors and carriages. Today the Wang family paid a visit, tomorrow the Zhang family arrived with gifts, the day after they received a warm invitation from the Zhao family.","Prospering daily, surrounded by splendor, it truly lived up to the name of its county, Fanhua—\"Flourishing Flowers.\"","The current head of the Yangzhou Qin family is Qin Ran, who has just reached the age of forty. His father, named Qin Chong, was the one who made the decision years ago to move the entire family south.","The main gate of a wealthy household is usually kept closed, unless distinguished guests are visiting or the family is hosting a major banquet. Only on such occasions would the main gate be opened in advance to show respect.","The side gate, however, is always open, guarded by a gatekeeper.","The gatekeeper had long grown accustomed to visitors arriving every few days, so when someone came to the door today, he wasn't the least bit surprised. His eyes swept over the group, and his demeanor grew even more casual.","They were all dressed in black, with no valuable ornaments at their waists, to the point of being called plain.","Servants represent the face of their master. If the servants sent to deliver a visiting card were dressed so shabbily, how distinguished could their master possibly be?","Yet the next moment, the gatekeeper heard the visitor announce himself: \"I am from the Northern Xuanxiao Cavalry. On this trip, I am following the Marquis's orders to pay a visit to Qin Ran. I hope you can announce us.\"","The Northern Xuanxiao Cavalry, that elite force which once helped Qin Shaozong subdue the northern barbarians, was renowned far and wide. Not just in Yangzhou, even in the southernmost Jiaozhou, their thunderous reputation was known.","The Northern Xuanxiao Cavalry... the Marquis...","They were from that person!","The gatekeeper gave a start. Stunned to the extreme, he couldn't utter a single word, only flushed red, hurriedly opened the gate wide, and bowed deeply to invite them in.","The men quickly entered.","Qin Ran had just finished dressing properly and was about to leave the residence to attend a banquet. The Governor of Fanhua County was hosting a hundred-day celebration for his eldest grandson today, having invited a wide circle of friends and relatives.","His second son held a sinecure in the official administration. Officials and merchants were like one family, so it was only proper, both in sentiment and reason, for him to attend this banquet hosted by Prefect Song.","His attire was in order, and the gift was prepared.","Just as Qin Ran, accompanied by his sons, was about to board the carriage to depart, a servant came running in a panic.","The servant said urgently, \"Master, the Northern Xuanxiao Cavalry has come. They say they are following the Marquis's orders to pay you a visit.\"","Qin Ran was stunned, then drew a sharp breath. \"How many have come? Have they been properly received?\"","Following the Marquis's orders? There was only one Marquis in the north—he was both the Marquis of Wu'an and the clan leader of the Qin family.","And they had actually sent the Xuanxiao Cavalry. This matter was absolutely no trivial affair.","The servant replied, \"Five in total. They are all in the main hall and have been served good tea.\"","Qin Ran turned to his two sons beside him and said, \"I will not be attending Prefect Song's banquet. The two of you can go. If Prefect Song asks why I am absent, tell him I caught a slight chill last night. Children are delicate, and it's not suitable to pass on any illness.\"","The two sons acknowledged his instructions.","After giving his sons their orders, Qin Ran hurried to the main hall.","As the servant had said, there were five visitors. Qin Ran discreetly sized them up. They were uniformly dressed in black, each man robust and powerfully built—exceptionally skilled individuals.","Just by their sharp, blade-like aura, they indeed lived up to the formidable reputation of the Xuanxiao Cavalry.","The leader, Hu Bao, was also observing Qin Ran. Seeing him in fine robes, with features and age matching the description, he knew this was undoubtedly the head of the Yangzhou Qin family."]},{"number":38,"title":"Chapter 38","paragraphs":["Qin Ran looked at the seal on the mulberry paper in his hand, confirming once more. Both the official seal and the private letter were present, there was no mistake.","But...","Go to Qiantang to find a nine-year-old child? And to send the Black Cavalry to deliver the message? Why would that lord attach such importance to this? What is so special about that child?","The surname is Qin. Could it be that the child is the lord's illegitimate son, lost to the outside world? But in his memory, the lord had not been to Qiantang ten years ago!","Or perhaps, a favored concubine went to Qiantang, and the lord only recently found out...","Qiantang is not a small place, and no one knows if the child has been moved elsewhere. A time limit of one month is quite tight.","This matter carries a certain degree of difficulty.","Myriad thoughts swirled in his mind, but one thing Qin Ran was absolutely certain of: this matter was an opportunity. It was a chance for his branch of the family, which had been distant from the main Qin clan of the north for many years, to finally distinguish itself!","Qin Shaozong's power and influence had grown increasingly formidable in recent years. Others worried about lacking a ladder, having no path to climb. Now, this ladder to the clouds had been delivered to his doorstep—how could he not seize it firmly?","Hu Bao and his men arrived at the Qin residence near the end of the Chen hour. Qin Ran did not delay for long. After issuing a few instructions, he personally led a group of his retainers and departed with Hu Bao and the others from Fanhua County for Qiantang.","As for whether news of his departure would leak and be reported to Prefect Song, Qin Ran paid it no mind.","So what if Prefect Song is displeased? The lord's matter takes precedence.","Fanhua County and Qiantang were not far apart. Qin Ran rode hard and fast, arriving at his destination the very next day.","The Qin family's shops were spread all over Yangzhou, and Qiantang was naturally no exception. Qin Ran used one of his mansions in Yangzhou as a base. Once settled, he immediately dispatched all the retainers who had come with him.","They were sent to the human markets to find brokers. Regardless of gender or age, anyone engaged in this trade was to be lured back with silver.","Hu Bao and his five men split up, each joining a team of retainers. The human market in Qiantang was not large, with roughly forty brokers. With all retainers deployed, in less than three hours, the main hall of the Qin mansion was packed with people.","Those in this trade were familiar faces to each other, having some degree of acquaintance. Now gathered in the hall, they whispered among themselves.","\"Why is the Qin family so urgently seeking us out?\"","\"Whatever their purpose, we'll get silver for it, that's what matters.\"","\"You always say I have shallow vision, but look—we haven't even done anything yet, just coming here earns us payment. If we help the Qin family succeed in their task, perhaps we won't need to work for several years and still live comfortably.\"","Others hearing this found it reasonable and grew even more eager for the master of the house to appear.","Upon hearing that everyone had basically arrived, Qin Ran finally emerged from the side corridor and made his appearance.","The present day was vastly different from the early years of the dynasty's founding. Back then, emphasizing agriculture and suppressing commerce was severe. Merchants could not register in the market census, were forbidden from riding in carriages or wearing silk garments, and their descendants were barred from entering official service.","But as time passed, especially with the highly developed trade with the Western Regions and northern states, the economy received an undeniable boost, and the government's attitude towards \"commerce\" gradually became more tolerant.","Not to mention the current turbulent times, where collusion between officials and merchants was commonplace. Many merchants no longer bowed and scraped as they had centuries before.","Qin Ran wore a deep blue robe with a round collar and wide sleeves, a headscarf, and an exquisite piece of jade of exceptional quality hung from his waist, exuding an aura of wealth and authority.","The crowd in the hall fell silent, their gazes fixed eagerly on him.","Qin Ran declared in a clear voice, \"I have invited you all here today to entrust you with a matter. The Qin family has lost a young boy in Qiantang, named Qin Yanzhou. He is nine years old, about five chi and seven cun tall, fair-skinned, with peach-blossom eyes, and a light brown, teardrop-shaped birthmark on his back near the shoulder. He is handsome, with short hair, the longest strands reaching his shoulders.\"","His eyes swept over the people in the hall. \"The misfortune has already occurred; dwelling on its causes is pointless. Better to do a good deed and accumulate merit. To anyone who can find our young boy, the Qin family will offer a reward of one hundred taels of silver, five prosperous shops, one residential property, and five mu of fertile land.\"","The hall erupted in an uproar.","So the meaning was not only a heavy reward, but also that they would not investigate how the boy was lost.","A significant number of these brokers had vested interests tied to human traffickers; where there was profit, there were dealings. Now that the Qin family had clearly stated they would not investigate, it seemed they were truly desperate to find the person.","After Qin Ran finished speaking, he gave a servant a look. The servant understood and began distributing silver coins—the previously promised payment for simply coming to the Qin mansion, now settled on the spot.","Someone then asked, \"May I ask, sir, how long has the boy been missing?\"","Qin Ran recalled what the letter said. \"Six months.\"","With the information obtained and the silver in hand, the brokers quickly dispersed.","After they left, Qin Ran looked at Hu Bao. \"Captain, the matter in Qiantang has been set in motion. Shall we go to the neighboring county tomorrow?\"","The letter said one month, but Qin Ran naturally wanted to finish as quickly as possible. Moreover, the boy had been missing for half a year; it was possible he had been sold elsewhere. They absolutely could not focus the search solely on Qiantang, or the chances would be vanishingly small.","Hu Bao naturally nodded in agreement.","For over half a month straight, Qin Ran traveled with Hu Bao and the others between Qiantang and the various counties surrounding it.","They visited every human market, large and small, in each county. Countless brokers learned of the silver offered and the reward, and even some traffickers proactively joined the search.","During this time, there were those with agile minds who quietly investigated and learned that Qin Ran's own household was complete, guessing he was helping someone else find a child. They then brought children to his door to claim the reward.","Hair, height, birthmark, general appearance—at first glance, many seemed to match. Qin Ran initially thought they had succeeded, but Hu Bao would take one look and shake his head in denial.","The child bore no resemblance to Lady Dai whatsoever, let alone showing no reaction upon hearing the name \"Dai Li.\"","It was not the right person.","After such impostors were exposed several times, everyone came to understand:","Ah, even if the child is not a close junior relative of Qin Ran's, there is someone who recognizes him. This matter cannot be faked.","After several such incidents, attempts at fraudulent claims gradually ceased.","The days passed one by one, and the search area continued to expand. Qin Ran went from his initial ambitious determination to complete the task ahead of schedule to growing increasingly bewildered.","They actually couldn't find him?","Not even a single trace of a clue. It was as if no matter how large a stone was thrown into the sea, it could not stir even the faintest ripple on this strangely placid surface.","Qin Ran sat alone in his study all night, and finally made a decision.","The mobility within the broker trade wasn't enormous, but it wasn't small either. Some people found better opportunities and put down their burdens, retiring from the business. Since the current batch had no news to report, perhaps they should ask those who had already washed their hands of the trade.","It was worth a try. After all, there were no better options left.","Ying County, Prefect's Residence.","Dai Li was having her morning meal, eating a boiled wheat dish known in this era as \"soup cakes,\" resembling palm-sized pieces of dough, served with fish balls made from mandarin fish meat and shrimp, garnished with some scallions. The color combination was quite appetizing.","\"Madam, are you going to the salt ponds again today?\" Nianxia stood before the clothing chest.","Daili swallowed the fish ball in her mouth. \"Yes, I'm going again today.\"","The matter of refined salt had long been scheduled. Qin Shaozong had many capable people under his command. Strictly speaking, she didn't need to go to the site personally; she could enjoy the flowers, feed the fish in the mansion, and simply send out instructions.","But Daili had a clear understanding of her current position. The project of purifying crude salt was initiated by her. The more military officers knew she was a strategist, the safer she was.","Upon hearing this, Nianxia took out a set of deep cyan riding attire from the clothing chest. The deep cyan color was dark, making stains less noticeable, perfectly suitable for wearing to such a place. Then she fetched two hair ribbons and a peachwood hairpin, waiting to help Daili change after she finished her breakfast.","Looking at the rows of clothing chests and the several five-tiered dressing cases placed before the cloud-patterned bronze mirror, Nianxia felt it was such a pity. Even though the carved dressing case inlaid with jade beads wasn't open at the moment, she knew what treasures were hidden inside.","Gold filigree hairpins with bees and butterflies chasing flowers, gold hair ornaments inlaid with gemstone flower heads, gold sideburns covers inlaid with jade beads, pearl ear pendants, tinkling jade bracelets...","Just one category of jewelry could fill several layers of a dressing case. When Nianxia had moved the items back upon orders, she once suspected that the finest pieces from the young lady's ornament allowance in the storeroom were all here.","Unfortunately, for the past half month, the lady had often gone to the salt lake. Describing that place as merely unclean was an understatement; sometimes one even stepped into pits.","Nianxia felt both heartache over Daili's endless toils and regret that the beautiful clothes and jewelry filling the room never had a chance to be worn.","After breakfast, Daili changed into the riding attire and went out. She didn't know how to ride a horse, so she traveled by carriage.","The carriage stopped at the entrance of the main courtyard. When Daili came out from her side chamber, she saw Qin Shaozong was already beside the carriage.","For the past half month, both she and he had been frequenting the salt lake. \"Refined salt\" was like a giant bomb dropped into the sea, its countdown already ticking, waiting only for a deafening explosion to set off a towering, earth-shattering wave starting from the northern lands.","\"It seems you rested well last night, Madam,\" Qin Shaozong said, looking at Daili as she walked towards him.","Her complexion was excellent indeed. Her already delicate, snow-white skin glowed with a healthy pink hue. Her eyes were dark and bright, sparkling with vitality. The vermilion mole on her forehead looked vivid and lively. Her whole person carried the vigorous, thriving energy of plants striving upward in spring.","When did it start?","Ah, yes. Since over half a month ago, when she used Wugong's help to dig a fox's den among the strategists under his command. From that day on, she had visibly grown more pleased with herself day by day.","Swishing her fluffy fox tail arrogantly before him, occasionally scratching him with a paw without restraint—truly audacious.","Daili smiled and nodded. \"Thanks to the Marquis's fortune, I did indeed rest well. After the efforts of the previous days, the various tiers of ponds by the salt lake are now completed, and plant ash has all been collected. The preparatory work is completely finished. I believe refined salt will see the light of day in at most two more days.\"","The \"Kěnqí Jiāoshài\" (reclaimed-plot irrigation and sun-drying) method of salt production, also called the \"five-step salt-making method.\"","When she first explained the steps to Nalan Zhi, she only covered the initial stage of brine collection and evaporation. The subsequent steps—sifting, brine storage, crystallization, and shoveling out—were still to come.","With flawless preparatory work and clear weather, the operational cycle of the irrigation-and-sun-drying method for reclaimed ridges was five to seven days.","The weather had been excellent lately. When Daili said \"two more days,\" it was the maximum estimate; the actual time would likely be less.","Avoiding that large, dark hand meant to assist her onto the carriage, Daili got on by herself. \"Thank you. But I need everyone to know that the strategists under the Marquis's command are not only resourceful but also physically robust. Merely boarding a carriage requires no assistance from the Marquis.\"","As she spoke, Daili grabbed the wooden beam for leverage and entered the carriage.","Qin Shaozong only caught a whiff of fragrant breeze, and in the blink of an eye, she had disappeared from before him. The faint, elusive scent still lingered at the tip of his nose, but she herself, like the fragrance, was untouchable and ungraspable.","Listen to what she just said—her fox tail was proudly raised again.","Qin Shaozong stood still outside the carriage for two breaths, then stepped into the compartment with a calm expression.","Once that child is found, there will be a time when she begs him.","The carriage left the mansion, passed through the bustling streets filled with traffic, and headed towards the south city gate.","As distance from the marketplace increased, the clamor gradually faded, and quietness gradually settled around them. All the fine details, like planks swept into the depths by a torrent, resurfaced after the noise receded, leaving nowhere to hide.","The gaze from across had been on her the entire time, its presence intense, its aggression unconcealed. Whenever she lifted her eyes or turned her head, she would meet those large, feline-like brown pupils.","Daili cast a casual glance, pretending not to see.","The carriage exited the city through the south gate.","On the way to the salt lake, they would first pass by a stretch of farmland. Daili lifted the side curtain and looked out.","\"Plant one seed in spring, reap ten thousand grains in autumn.\" Spring was the sowing season. The previously captured male prisoners of war had now all been put to work plowing the fields.","By the fields, Daili saw the silhouette of a dragon-bone waterwheel. A man in short clothes turned the front wheel, and water immediately gushed from the dragon's head with a splash. The burly man was elated, and the other farmers, lined up nearby—most of them waiting to \"borrow the wheel\"—also watched with expressions of admiration.","The spring breeze carried snippets of conversation.","\"It's truly like the Dragon King from the waters, flying from the rivers into our fields, bestowing favor upon us nameless commoners.\"","\"Exactly. Actually, farming is good. I never liked all that fighting and killing. A single misstep and you report to the King of Hell. I haven't lived enough yet.\"","\"If we plant more wheat as instructed by the authorities, with this divine tool, the wheat is sure to grow splendidly. Once we deliver the required amount of grain, that lord said he would release us from prisoner-of-war status and let us become commoners again.\"","\"Then we must work harder. Speaking of which, we're truly grateful to that Lady Dai for bringing this divine tool to Ying County...\"","...","Daili was stunned. Before she could listen more carefully, the carriage had already moved away from them.","For the past half month, she had been running back and forth between two points and had not gone anywhere else. It was only today that she learned the Dragon Bone Waterwheel's promotion seemed somewhat different from what she had imagined.","Daili turned to look at the man opposite, meeting those brown eyes. She asked, \"When you promoted the dragon bone waterwheel, did you tell the commoners about my involvement?\"","\"Stealing another's wealth is called theft; how much more blameworthy is it to claim as one's own the credit that belongs to Heaven?\" Qin Shaozong smiled. \"The dragon-bone waterwheel came to my attention precisely because of you, Madam. What harm is there in privately informing them of that?\"","The public notice did not mention Daili; it only summoned the city's carpenters to rush the production of dragon-bone waterwheels. The news was spread separately by privately sending people to teahouses and eateries.","The rumor circulating among the people was: The dragon bone waterwheel was invented by a recluse surnamed Ma. However, the recluse, overworked, fell gravely ill. On his deathbed, he entrusted a lady surnamed Dai to take this object to the authorities, to use the government's power to promote it.","Seeing Daili staring at him blankly, Qin Shaozong raised his long eyebrows slightly. \"What are you looking at me with those big eyes for? A true man stands firm between heaven and earth—how could he covet a woman's achievements? My lady deserves to leave her name in the annals of history.\"","Of course, what he didn't say was that apart from disdaining to steal credit, he had other plans in mind.","When one lacked the power to protect oneself, a prominent reputation was anything but a good thing. With her intelligence, she would sooner or later realize that rashly leaving his side would only lead to a dead end.","Daili hadn't yet thought that deeply. Hearing his words, she smiled and flattered him, \"The Marquis is wise. Serving under you is truly a stroke of fortune.\"","Qin Shaozong smiled without speaking.","The carriage rumbled along the official road, soon arriving at the salt lake.","Due to differences in ion composition and various physical factors, salt lakes display a vast array of colors—blue, green, brown, pink... every hue imaginable.","The salt lake before Daili was a cyan-green, a very beautiful shade reminiscent of a washed-clean sky or a captivating expanse of emerald waves. The lake's surface was smooth as a mirror, occasionally rippling under the caress of the wind.","The salt crystals formed naturally around the lake were large-grained and whiter than the salt produced by boiling seawater or sun-drying.","However, whether it was the salt from this place or other crude salts of the time, the taste was actually quite bitter and astringent, no different from the strongest bitterness of seawater.","Refined salt is sodium chloride. Crude salt, besides sodium chloride, contains many impurities, among which magnesium chloride tastes particularly bitter. The purification process from crude to refined salt is, in essence, a matter of removing impurities.","Seeing the familiar carriage stop, Feng Feng and Bai Jianping, the chief of Nantun, who had been working at the salt lake for over half a month, quickly hurried forward to greet it.","Both men wore expressions of excitement, nearly dancing with joy. \"Marquis, Lady Dai, we've succeeded!\"","As they spoke, they held out cloth bags in their hands, the openings wide to reveal a crystalline, snow-like purity within.","Unlike the salt from the lake, the contents of these small bags were visibly purer and finer.","Daili hadn't expected it to be ready even earlier than planned and couldn't help but smile. \"That's excellent.\"","Qin Shaozong reached into a bag, hooked a bit of the white substance with his long finger, and brought it to his lips for a taste.","A pure saltiness, incomparable to anything from the past, exploded on his taste buds. With that single taste, Qin Shaozong knew the value of this small bag of salt in Feng and Bai's hands surpassed even that of gold.","What the nobles of Chang'an lacked was never silver, but the ultimate luxury of possessing what others did not, or having what was superior to all others.","Daili did not taste it, as no one knew better than her how salty refined salt was. Perhaps the wind by the lake was strong, but she suddenly felt inexplicably cold, a chill rising from her back that made her shiver.","She instinctively turned to look behind her. There stood the carriage, the tall horses hitched beside it snorting and whinnying. Casting her gaze further back, she saw a sky as blue as crystal and mountains stretching into the distance like an unbroken jade belt.","This era was free of pollution; everything was beautifully unreal, like a painting.","Just as Daili was about to turn back, a small patch of black shadow suddenly intruded into the corner of her vision.","It was a corner of the black robe worn by the man beside her, lifted by the wind. This small touch of black became the only shadow in the otherwise idyllic scene, like the glimpse of a black claw tip revealed by a tiger lurking in the forest.","Daili froze. In that moment of clarity, she seemed to understand where the chill had come from."]},{"number":39,"title":"Chapter 39","paragraphs":["Daili followed Qin Shaozong to the salt-shoveling area by the salt lake.","The final step of the five-step salt production method was shoveling. Compared to the other steps, this one was purely manual labor, requiring only that the crystallized salt be piled onto salt mounds to await subsequent transport.","Looking out, one mound after another of snow-white \"ice cream cone\" peaks stood upon the ground. The pure white was a pleasing sight, utterly captivating.","After tasting the refined salt, everyone—whether it was Qin Shaozong or the Xuanxiao Cavalry he had transferred for salt production—was exceedingly happy.","Anyone could see this was a colossal fortune.","The world would be shaken by this refined salt. The nobility of Chang'an would become infatuated with it. Even foreign tribes from the Western Regions and the northern kingdoms would offer beautiful gems, precious furs, and fine warhorses, begging to trade for it.","Waves of scorching gazes fell upon her. Daili's footsteps subconsciously paused, and it was only then she realized that perhaps, just like with the dragon-bone waterwheel, he had not concealed the fact that the refined salt came from her hand.","While everyone was discussing the refined salt, he suddenly asked, \"Is the Peach Blossom Spring you mentioned, madam, near Nankang Commandery or Qiantang?\"","His tone was very ordinary, as if casually chatting with a friend. But Daili knew it wasn't like that. After the refined salt came into the world, he had developed an unusually strong interest in the \"Peach Blossom Spring\" she spoke of.","First the dragon-bone waterwheel, now refined salt... why couldn't there be other things?","What he was asking about was perhaps not just the Peach Blossom Spring at all.","Daili replied in a flat tone, \"My lord, I too would like to know the answer to that question.\"","Just as she thought he would press for a couple more details, or simply tear away that thin veil of concealment to ask her what other things not yet present in this world existed within the Peach Blossom Spring besides refined salt...","He said this instead: \"Not being able to find the way is no matter. After all, once you are reunited with your son, madam, is anywhere not a place to live?\"","Qin Shaozong automatically ignored the \"husband\" in her words—the one she said she had a conflict with and did not mention.","Never mind that she couldn't find the Peach Blossom Spring for now and couldn't see old acquaintances. Even if an old acquaintance came looking for her, he could ensure they would not return.","\"Madam, what price do you think is suitable for selling the refined salt to other regions?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","Daili glanced at him, not believing he had no opinion on this himself. \"Initially, the more expensive the better. After all, the salt field is too large, requiring many people to work together. This method won't be easy to keep secret.\"","Unlike a tightly closed-door, precise research project, the salt field's vast area lay open, accessible from all directions. Once refined salt appeared, various forces would inevitably trace its origins. Daili privately believed the production method for refined salt couldn't be kept secret for very long.","After a pause, Daili expressed deep suspicion, \"But are you sure you can sell it? Selling private salt is illegal. Be careful the local nobility there confiscates your entire operation.\"","Qin Shaozong merely smiled and said, \"I have my own methods.\"","There was a small salt pit ahead, not large, but two palms deep. Seeing she was about to step into it, Qin Shaozong reached out and pulled her back.","He did it naturally, but Daili was startled by him. By the time she reacted, the familiar feeling of restraint around her waist had already vanished. Looking at the man beside her, his expression was normal, as if he had merely lent her a hand.","Daili: \"...\"","The successful production of refined salt meant all previous processes were without issue. Therefore, the two of them spent much less time at the salt field today than before.","When leaving, Qin Shaozong also took a bag of refined salt back to his residence to improve meals. Daili thought he had finally done a decent thing.","Yangzhou, Congnan County.","A county was much smaller than a commandery, and this Congnan County was among the lower tier even among counties. Its already sparse population had been reduced by nearly a third due to a minor plague that occurred three years ago.","\"Creak.\" A dilapidated wooden door opened, and a limping, elderly figure hobbled into the thatched cottage.","\"Old Sun, see who's come?\" His wife's voice inside the house was high-pitched and enthusiastic, greeting Old Man Sun as he entered.","Old Man Sun looked up.","Well, his married daughter had returned with her husband.","Old Man Sun grinned. Clearly happy, he insisted on speaking a couple of contrary, angry words, \"Haven't seen you for two years, thought you'd died out there. What wind blows you back today?\"","He turned and instructed his wife, Mrs. Wang, \"Two more mouths to feed at home today. Go buy two more hu cakes from Old Li at the end of the street.\"","\"No need for the trouble, I brought wine and meat.\" Sun Niangzi stopped her mother, then gave her husband a look. He understood and opened the hemp bag he was carrying.","Sure enough, inside was a small pot of millet wine and a roast duck.","The elderly couple was overjoyed at the sight.","The family sat around the table and began their midday meal.","After Sun Niangzi saw her husband and Old Man Sun drink two rounds, she finally said, \"Father, I want to ask you something. Back in the days when you worked as a broker in Qiantang, did you ever see a fair-skinned, nine-year-old boy with short hair?\"","Sun Niangzi's husband, Li Aniu, added, \"The boy had peach blossom eyes and a light brown, teardrop-shaped birthmark on his back shoulder.\"","At this moment, Sun Niangzi held little hope.","Returning to her parents' home with her husband was because Aniu remembered her father had once been a broker in Qiantang and wanted to ask for information. She thought about how long it had been since she last visited her parents, leading to their mutual agreement to come.","She was aware of the Qin family in Qiantang searching everywhere for someone. She knew her husband coveted that astonishing reward. After all, not only was there a heavy reward for finding the person, but one could also receive a sum of money for providing a verified, important lead.","Privately, Sun Niangzi didn't believe this trip would yield any results.","Her father hadn't worked as a broker for many years and had left Qiantang long ago. The boy the Qin family was looking for had only been missing for half a year. How could the timelines match?","Brokers going to the Qin family had almost worn out their doorstep, yet all returned empty-handed, even the most well-connected Zhao Tietou was no exception. In her view, that boy had most likely quietly died somewhere else. With wind and rain, the corpse would be beyond recognition, and might even have been carried off by wolves outside the city.","Her husband was money-mad, confused, now turning to her father in a desperate search for a cure. But she genuinely wanted to return to her parents' home, so naturally she wouldn't foolishly stop him.","After Li Aniu finished speaking, he looked anxiously at Old Man Sun.","Old Man Sun held a ceramic cup in his left hand and wooden chopsticks in his right, his eyes fixed unblinkingly on the roast duck before him, as if contemplating which piece of meat to pick next.","The wait was so long Li Aniu was beginning to despair. He averted his gaze, intending to take a sip of millet wine to drown his sorrows, when he suddenly heard—","\"I've seen him.\"","Li Aniu's body jolted. He fired off questions in succession, \"Uncle Sun, are you sure the boy you saw is the one I just described? When did you see him? Where did you see him? What was the boy's condition then? Where did he go afterwards?\"","Sun Niangzi was also stunned, \"Father, didn't you stop being a broker seven years ago?\"","Old Man Sun didn't look at anyone, as if lost in his own memories. \"That was many years ago. Eight years, nine years, or ten years ago, I can't remember exactly. I came across that child by the river outside the city. He was all wet, his hair was very short, about this length...\" Old Man Sun put down his wooden chopsticks and gestured with his hand near his head, his palm less than half a foot from his scalp.","\"I had never seen a child with hair that short before, and the child was dressed very strangely, in short clothes and shorts, dressed like a farmer working in the fields. But his skin was delicate and fair, very clean. At the time, I saw he was all alone, and the wind was strong by the river. Worried he might catch a chill, and as I happened to have a flint on me, I told him to take off his clothes first so I could dry them for him.\"","\"What happened then? What happened after?\" Li Aniu pressed. \"Did he have a light brown, teardrop-shaped birthmark? Oh, and it must be on his right shoulder.\"","Old Man Sun raised his cup and took a sip of wine. He didn't answer Li Aniu's question immediately, but continued with his memory. \"He called me uncle, asked me to take him to some... bureau or office. He also said something in his hand was broken, he couldn't contact his mama, and he wanted to borrow something from me. The little fellow even proactively recited a long string of numbers and a name. I guess that name was the 'mama' he mentioned.\"","Sun Niangzi listened, utterly confused.","What on earth was her father talking about? What bureau? What broken thing in his hand...","What kind of address was 'mama'? Did it mean mother?","Could it be that because the other person was talking nonsense, her father remembered it all these years?","\"The child was about this tall.\" Old Man Sun raised his hand and gestured to a height beside him. \"Not big. He seemed quite clever, well-mannered, but his speech was baffling. Yet he wasn't a simpleton. At the time, I guessed he was the son of some wealthy family. Helping him dry his clothes was just so I could get a reward for sending him home.\"","Li Aniu jumped up from his chair in shock. Just now, neither Sun Niangzi nor he had mentioned the detail \"five chi and seven cun\" (approx. 5.7 ft).","But Old Man Sun's casual gesture just now indicated precisely that height.","Sun Niangzi was dumbfounded. It took her a moment to repeat her husband's earlier question. \"Th-then, did he have a teardrop birthmark on his right shoulder?\"","Old Man Sun nodded, then shook his head. \"It seems there was a birthmark, but then again, maybe not. How could I remember clearly now?\"","\"I've lost my appetite.\" Li Aniu threw down his chopsticks, in no mood to eat at all. \"Uncle Sun, come with us to Qiantang quickly! Let's go claim the reward! A large estate, prosperous shops, fertile land, and over a hundred taels of silver—they'll all be ours!\"","Old Man Sun had downed several cups of wine. Whether he was somewhat drunk or still lost in his memories, he didn't move.","He didn't react, but his wife, Mrs. Wang, heard this and her eyes lit up. \"Old Sun, go to Qiantang and claim the reward. Over a hundred taels! And shops that can keep making money. Even if your other leg breaks, you won't have to worry for the rest of your life. How much good wine couldn't you buy then?\"","Old Man Sun gave a start and hurriedly stood up as well. \"Let's go, let's go to Qiantang. We'll go right now.\"","The whole family was excited, except for Sun Niangzi. She hadn't spoken again, a small frown knotting her brow.","The \"sighting\" her father spoke of was at least seven years ago. The noble family's child had only been missing for half a year. This just didn't match up, no matter how you looked at it.","Qiantang, Qin Residence.","Ever since receiving Qin Shaozong's letter over half a month ago, Qin Ran had not returned to Fanhua County. Using Qiantang as a base, he had traveled to various counties, later mainly staying in Qiantang.","With less than seven days left until the one-month deadline, Qin Ran was so anxious that several blisters had broken out on his lips.","\"What if we still can't find the person after these seven days? How do we explain it to that lord?\" He paced in the room. Beside him was his eldest son, Qin Yishang, who had been ordered to come to Qiantang to help search.","Qin Yishang felt his father was overly anxious. \"If we can't find him, we can't find him. We did our best and can report truthfully. The Marquis is magnanimous; surely he won't blame us.\"","Qin Ran said with frustration, \"It has been exactly thirty-five years since your grandfather moved our branch of the family from the north to Yangzhou.\"","Outsiders saw the Qin clan as united. When Prefect Song of Fanhua County had tea with him, they often talked about that Marquis Wu'an from the north, and Qin Ran would put on a proud expression. But deep down, Qin Ran knew well that their branch in Yangzhou had had very little connection with the main family over these thirty-plus years.","Apart from sending someone north with New Year's gifts once a year, there was virtually no other communication.","Now that an opportunity had finally presented itself, this feeling of helplessness was truly galling.","Just then, a servant came to report. \"Master, there's an old broker at the door. He says he has important information to provide.\"","At the beginning of the search, Qin Ran had heard this until his ears calloused. People came every day, each claiming to have important information, all with their eyes fixed on the reward money in his pocket. He didn't care about the silver, but he was annoyed that these people tried to deceive him with lies, unnecessarily hindering the search.","Later, it was that Captain Hu who came up with an idea, which finally stopped the endless stream of trouble.","\"Father, the last person who said he had important information exhausted me terribly,\" Qin Yishang said, still feeling the strain when he remembered. He had traveled day and night through several counties, even running a horse to death, only to find it was all fabricated. His fury and rage at the time were entirely justified.","Qin Ran pinched the bridge of his nose. \"Fewer people have been coming lately. Regardless, we must see this old broker.\"","When the Qin father and son entered the main hall, Hu Bao happened to be leading someone back from outside. Seeing people approaching from both sides, Old Man Sun's family immediately became very nervous. Especially Sun Niangzi, who couldn't help but tug at her husband's sleeve.","She still felt this matter was somewhat unreliable.","No matter how many other details matched, the timeline didn't align! Not by a month or two, but by several years—enough for a nine-year-old child to grow into a youth.","No matter how confused the noble family was, they couldn't mistake losing a young boy for losing a youth...","Hu Bao's gaze swept over them, taking in Sun Niangzi's small gesture, but he didn't say anything for now.","Qin Ran looked down at Old Man Sun. \"So you have important information? Keep it brief. If the information is true, the reward will be yours. But if I find you're full of lies and only came here to swindle the reward, don't blame me for having the captain throw you in jail.\"","The hall was brightly lit, furnished with exquisite ornaments that were clearly valuable. The two men at the head of the hall were dressed richly, with jade pendants hanging from their belts. Behind them stood several tall, burly men, all dressed in black, with what hung at their waists...","Were those swords.","Old Man Sun gradually trembled like a sieve. The journey from Nanjun to Qiantang had taken quite a while, and his drunkenness had long since worn off. Now standing in the main hall, his heart was filled with trepidation: \"Your Honor, I will only speak of what I know. You judge if it's credible. If you don't believe me, can we just pretend this never happened and give me a few coppers for my journey home?\"","Qin Yishang's anger flared.","He had merely been given a slight warning and was already showing fear. This man was most likely another swindler after reward money. According to him, why even receive an audience? They should just throw him out.","The corner of Qin Ran's mouth twitched, and similar doubts rose in his heart. But since he was already here, he might as well hear the so-called lead. \"Speak.\"","Old Man Sun was initially somewhat stammering, keeping his head down and not daring to look at anyone. But as he spoke, he became immersed in his memories.","He gave a specific location, described how he had chanced upon the other person, and detailed the child's clothing, appearance, a birthmark on the body, and the child's strange words.","\"...His parents must have been people of exceptionally outstanding appearance. In all my years, I've never seen such a handsome little boy. It's just that his mind wasn't clear, always talking nonsense,\" Old Man Sun said.","The Qin father and son initially held little hope, but as they listened, they exchanged a glance, inexplicably feeling a flicker of anticipation.","It sounded without major holes. Moreover, unlike other swindlers who desperately tried to tailor their stories to fit known information, this old man still hadn't uttered the child's name.","Old Man Sun, perhaps having forgotten, or perhaps subconsciously finding it absurd himself, didn't immediately mention the time this time.","Until later...","\"When did you see that child?\" Qin Ran asked.","The hall immediately fell silent. Old Man Sun, who had been looking up, lowered his head. This silence was like a bucket of cold water, drenching the Qin father and son.","Something was wrong.","Had they been mistaken earlier?","\"Ten years ago,\" someone said softly.","Not only the Qin father and son, but even Hu Bao standing nearby had a drastic change in expression.","\"Ten years ago?!\"","\"Do you know what you're saying? Even the most absurd claim must have its limits! You dare to spout such lies here, attempting to deceive and swindle? Do you believe I'll have the guards throw you into prison this instant?\"","At the mention of \"prison,\" Old Man Sun, who had been somewhat timid just moments before, now seemed to throw caution to the wind, words pouring out in a torrent: \"I truly am not lying. I really did meet that child ten years ago. His height, hair, and appearance all matched. He even told me his... possibly his mother's name. His relative was called, called...\"","Old Man Sun choked up, sweating profusely in his anxiety.","A decade had passed. The only reason he still remembered this incident was because that child had been so peculiar back then. But some of the terms the child used then, including that string of numbers and the name that followed, had long been cast into the river of time by the years, leaving not a trace.","\"Father, don't listen to his nonsense anymore. Hurry and chase him out, lest we waste more time,\" Qin Ran's eldest son, Qin Yishang, said indignantly.","Qin Ran was of the same mind. \"You may lea...\"","\"You said the child was by the river, his clothes completely soaked at the time?\" Hu Bao, who had been silent until now, suddenly spoke.","Seeing someone was still asking him for details, Old Man Sun felt like a drowning man clutching a lifeline. \"Yes, yes, yes! As if he had swum a lap in the river, completely drenched.\"","Hu Bao fell into thought.","Mo Yanyun had a loose tongue, especially after drinking, with no filter on what he might let slip.","He had once heard him say that the reason Lady Dai was discovered by the Lord back then was because the Lord heard movement in the side room in the courtyard and went in to investigate. The two were in the room for less than half the time it takes to drink a cup of tea before Lady Dai emerged, draped in a man's long robe.","Why was Lady Dai wearing a man's long robe at that time?","Why couldn't she appear in women's attire? Could it be that there was a problem with her own clothes?","Hu Bao hadn't been present. He had no answer.","But faintly, he felt a subtle, indescribable connection between these two events, like spider silk wrapping around his nerves, tugging at them again and again.","\"Think carefully! What did the child say his mother's name was?\" Hu Bao pressed sternly.","Old Man Sun was sweating profusely, trembling, yet unable to utter a word.","Qin Yishang was about to speak but was stopped by a look from his father, who shook his head slightly, signaling him not to interfere.","Time flowed slowly, the atmosphere in the hall growing increasingly tense. Old Man Sun and his family began to think of retreat.","Old Man Sun still couldn't say anything. Hu Bao sighed. \"Forget it. You may lea...\"","That word \"lea\" drifted into Old Man Sun's ears like an invisible heavy hammer striking his temple, shaking off all the dust-covered, rust-stained grime accumulated over the years.","Thus, a tide rose in the long river of time, swelling and then receding. And as the water receded, the discarded past on the riverbed reappeared.","\"Li... Li Dai, or Dai Li...\" Old Man Sun only remembered two characters. \"Just these two characters. As for the order, I've forgotten.\"","Hu Bao's pupils contracted to pinpoints, a tidal wave surging in his heart. Not only him, but the other four Xuanxiao Cavalrymen also looked utterly shocked.","This old man had actually uttered Lady Dai's name.","Could it be that the strange child he spoke of was truly Lady Dai's son?","But...","But the old man said this happened ten years ago!","Lady Dai was desperately searching for her son. The time of her son's disappearance was such a crucial detail; she absolutely could not have misremembered it.","Just where... had things gone wrong?"]},{"number":40,"title":"Chapter 40","paragraphs":["Chang'an.","The city bustled with noise and activity, a tapestry of splendor stretching far and wide. By day, Chang'an's streets were a continuous flow of carriages and horses, throngs of people coming and going, truly living up to the phrase \"fragrant carriages and jeweled canopies cram the thoroughfares.\" With the majestic imperial palace at its center, bookshops, wine houses, inns, and jade shops spread out like an unrolled scroll. The closer one got to the districts of the high officials and nobility, the more exorbitant the prices, drawing a stark line between poverty and wealth here.","Recently, a wind from distant lands had stirred undercurrents beneath Chang'an's seemingly peaceful and prosperous surface. These undercurrents converged into turbulent waves, sweeping through the mansions of various high-ranking officials and the many inns and eateries in succession, until at last the boundary between rich and poor was eroded and blurred. Even the common folk in the streets and alleys knew that something new had appeared in Chang'an.","\"Hey, have you heard about the 'xian shi' (salty stone)?\"","\"How could I not? The caravan from the north the other day made no attempt to hide their movements; the commotion was so great it could wake hibernating snakes. Speaking of which, I find their story about 'buying the xian shi from Western Region merchants' a bit fishy. Do the Western Regions really have such a good thing?\"","\"Regardless of its truth, the fact is that eateries using this xian shi make food that tastes better than before. Now the price of xian shi is sky-high, with demand far outstripping supply.\"","\"It's not just about supply and demand. I heard Chancellor Dong had the northern merchant caravan selling xian shi arrested.\"","\"Oh? I hadn't heard that. Why were they arrested?\"","\"Accused of selling private salt. But they were released not long after. I've picked up some unverified rumors: first, that caravan had no more xian shi left; second, they disclosed the specific Western Region merchant they bought it from; and third, that caravan has powerful backing, making it troublesome to mess with. As for how powerful, it seems to have intricate connections with that Lord guarding the northern border.\"","\"Well, well! When gods fight, it seems even the Buddha's face must be considered! But what does xian shi have to do with private salt? Surely they can't just claim xian shi is salt simply because it's purer and lacks the bitterness? We've all eaten salt for decades; can't we tell the difference?\"","\"The 'official' character has two mouths. Whether it is or isn't isn't for us to decide. That caravan's xian shi was long since sold out. Probably the entire city of Chang'an has none left for sale now. To buy xian shi, one would have to go north to find those Western Region merchants...\"","...","Chang'an, Liang Residence.","As the maternal family of Chancellor Dong Zhou's wife, the Liang family had grown increasingly powerful in recent years under his patronage, serving openly as the Dong family's vanguard, working tirelessly and handling all matters inconvenient for the Dongs themselves.","\"Father, please entrust the mission to go north and find the Western Region merchants to me. I will surely follow the trail, get to the bottom of this xian shi matter, and return fully laden,\" the eldest Liang son said solemnly.","Liang Tai, Dong Zhou's maternal uncle, stroked his beard. \"Chancellor Dong places great importance on this xian shi matter. Although it's called 'salty stone,' anyone with eyes can see it's more precious and pure than current salt. If we can locate its source, it would be like sitting on an endless gold mountain.\"","He patted his eldest son's shoulder. \"The north is restless. For this journey, besides taking enough guards, bring ample silver. If we cannot find the source, at least bring back a good quantity of the goods. Go now, be quick, and try to return with your report within three months.\"","The eldest Liang son bowed with clasped hands. \"I accept the command.\"","A scene similar yet not identical to Chang'an's played out in the bustling markets of the various commanderies in Qingzhou.","Qingzhou, Qianfeng Commandery, Governor's Residence.","\"Father, you've been away from home for many days and surely don't know about the new thing appearing in the commandery. Look at this...\" Hearing of her father's return, Nangong Zijin hurried excitedly to the main hall and placed a small open bag on the table. \"This is xian shi. Everyone says it's even better than salt.\"","Nangong Xiong, Governor of Qingzhou, had been swamped with worries for the past few months.","The reason was simple. He and Fan Tianshi, Governor of Yanzhou, had agreed to set aside past grievances and jointly crusade against the Qinglian Sect. Initially, all went smoothly. But one day, a high-ranking officer in Fan Tianshi's army was found dead in his quarters. Several in the Yanzhou army claimed the deceased had had a dispute with a Qingzhou officer, suggesting someone from Qingzhou, bearing a grudge, had committed the murder.","He tried to prove Qingzhou was not behind the killing. With the alliance against the Qinglian Sect imminent, such a mishap seemed clearly the sect's doing to sow discord.","But that fool Fan Tianshi only listened to his subordinates' one-sided account, causing relations between Qing and Yan to deteriorate sharply. It was utterly infuriating.","However, facing his beloved daughter from his later years, Nangong Xiong suppressed his anger and said, \"My dear, your marriage arrangement with Governor Fan of Yanzhou's son will likely not proceed.\"","His daughter was now sixteen, betrothed to Fan Tianshi's son a year ago. But with relations between the two provinces so hostile now, this marriage was probably off.","Nangong Zijin didn't seem to mind at all. \"Off is off, then. I've heard none of the Fan family's young masters are any good. Leaving aside the married ones, of the unmarried, Fan Wu is mediocre, and Fan Liu has enough concubines to fill several courtyards. Managing his household would be exhausting. Oh, Governor Fan also has two adopted sons. I hear their conduct is somewhat better; one has a handsome face, the other is quite ugly... but I, a legitimate daughter, could hardly marry a mere adopted son?\"","Nangong Xiong chuckled. \"It seems this marriage has displeased you for quite some time.\"","\"I was indeed unhappy. But if you were determined to have me marry him, I wouldn't have said 'no',\" Nangong Zijin pouted.","Nangong Xiong teased her, \"Would you even marry an adopted son?\"","Adopting sons was not uncommon nowadays. Some powerful lords selected young orphans with promising physiques, raised them for several years to build strong bodies and loyalty, then used them as their own.","Of course, some lords unwilling to spend years on food would adopt boys of twelve or thirteen, raising them from halfway. While their loyalty might not match those raised from childhood, they were still somewhat usable.","Besides these, there were also warriors who had gained some reputation, eager for achievement, who would pledge themselves alone to a lord's banner and become adopted sons.","Regardless of the type, those who became adopted sons for others were undoubtedly of humble, lowly origins. Otherwise, why would they bow and scrape, acknowledging another as father?","If he remembered correctly, both of Fan Tianshi's adopted sons were raised from the age of twelve or thirteen. Hah, that man was truly stingy.","Nangong Zijin pressed her lips together, her eyes reddening.","Nangong Xiong quickly said, \"I was only joking with you, my dear. Even if you wanted to, I wouldn't allow such lowly individuals to disgrace you. The daughter of Nangong Xiong is not someone mere frogs and toads can aspire to!\"","Afraid his daughter would question his earlier inappropriate remark, Nangong Xiong looked at the open bag on the table. \"So this is the xian shi that's better than salt? Hmm, white and fine. Just by appearance, it does seem superior to salt.\"","Nangong Zijin urged, \"Father, please taste it. It truly is better than salt.\"","Unable to withstand his youngest daughter's insistence, Nangong Xiong dipped a finger in and tasted a small amount. With that one taste, his eyes widened in astonishment, and he rarely showed such a changed expression in front of his daughter.","\"Sweetheart, where did this 'salty stone' come from?\" Nangong Xiong asked urgently.","Nangong Zijin replied truthfully, \"I bought it at the market. A merchant caravan from the north was selling it. They said they acquired it from the Western Regions' Hu people and are now reselling it. Although it's expensive, many restaurant managers were willing to pay a high price for this salty stone after sampling it. Oh, and not just restaurants, even the prominent families within the commandery are exceptionally keen on it. Everyone who has tried it says it's better than salt.\"","After speaking, Nangong Zijin saw her father staring silently at the table and couldn't quite grasp his thoughts.","\"Father, what are you...\"","\"Sweetheart, I have matters to attend to in the study.\" Nangong Xiong rose from his seat, taking the small bag with him. \"Lend this to your father.\"","With that, Nangong Xiong raised his voice to summon a guard and gave him an order.","...","Zhang Mingdian had been accompanying his lord east and west these past days due to the campaign against the Qinglian Sect. Now, with the alliance with Yanzhou at a stalemate and even showing signs of breaking, he had returned with his lord to Qianfeng Commandery.","However, before he could even warm his seat at home, a guard from the Governor's mansion arrived with a message: The lord requests your presence, sir, please come quickly.","Zhang Mingdian had no choice but to make the best of it, comforting himself that at least he didn't need to bother changing clothes. When he arrived at the study in the Governor's mansion, he found the door wide open, and his lord standing behind the desk, intently gazing at an object on it.","\"My lord, what urgent matter requires my presence?\" Zhang Mingdian, having just returned with Nangong Xiong, was also unaware of the recent events in the commandery.","\"Quanshu, you're here. Come quickly and take a look at this salty stone.\" Nangong Xiong called him by his courtesy name, beckoning him over, and recounted the information he had just gathered from his daughter and the mansion guards. \"...This salty stone is very peculiar. It's like salt, yet superior to salt. It's unclear where those Hu merchants obtained this treasure. This thing has great profit potential.\"","After tasting it, Zhang Mingdian's expression changed dramatically, just like every first-time taster. He lowered his eyes, the withered lines on his eyelids layered like heavy vines hanging before a cave entrance.","In an instant, he lifted his gaze. His pupils were dark, his eyes sharp as blades, as if the vines had been parted to reveal a blazing torch within. \"My lord, I recall something. Last month, Qin Shaozong decisively defeated the Li salt smuggler entrenched in Ying Commandery. While occupying Ying Commandery, he also took control of the nearby salt lakes. The merchant caravan selling the salty stone comes from the north. Why not apprehend and interrogate them to see if they have any connection to Qin Shaozong?\"","Nangong Xiong frowned. \"Quanshu, do you suspect the salty stone originates from Qin Shaozong?\"","Zhang Mingdian nodded. \"I personally believe the two must be related. When I was young I traveled to the Western Regions. That place has plenty of agate, crystallized sugar, various spices, and fine horses, but I've never heard of anything called 'salty stone.' Besides, the timing of its appearance is too coincidental. Why not earlier? Why not many years later? It just so happens to appear after Qin Shaozong occupied Ying Commandery. Isn't there something mysterious about that? Could it be that the Li salt smuggler had just developed a new method and hadn't yet had time to make it public before being swallowed up by Qin Shaozong?\"","Hearing this series of questions, Nangong Xiong fell into deep thought.","Zhang Mingdian continued, \"Whether it is or isn't, we can find out by apprehending that merchant caravan for questioning. If that caravan has him as a backer, then this matter is fifty or sixty percent likely to be linked to Qin Shaozong.\"","Nangong Xiong agreed and swiftly dispatched men.","The Governor's mansion guards acted quickly: apprehending the men, bringing them to the official compound, and interrogating them.","This entire process took only half a day. By the time the trusted subordinate returned with information to the Governor's mansion, Nangong and Zhang had already rested and were currently having their evening meal.","This meal used salty stone in place of ordinary salt. Anyone with a discerning palate could taste that the bitterness was completely gone.","\"Governor Nangong, they have confessed. This merchant caravan does indeed have some connection to the Qin clan. The leading merchant said they are distant relatives of Mo Zhiyuan,\" the guard reported.","Zhang Mingdian murmured, \"The Mo family...\"","Powerful clans of equal strength often intermarry. Strong clans also choose to support some weaker families, making them their instruments, their claws.","The Mo and Yan clans are both vassals of the Qin family. However, the former began serving the Qin family from the generation of Qin Shaozong's grandfather, while the Yan clan was personally raised by Qin Shaozong after he came of age.","The Mo clan has deeper roots than the Yan clan; but in terms of trust, the Yan clan surpasses the Mo clan and is more heavily relied upon by Qin Shaozong.","\"Mo Zhiyuan... that name sounds somewhat familiar. I remember Qin Shaozong has a Mo Yanyun under his command. It seems this person is either a cousin or an uncle-nephew relation to Mo Yanyun,\" Nangong Xiong clicked his tongue twice. \"It seems Quanshu's guess was correct. The salty stone likely has Qin Shaozong behind it.\"","After saying this, Nangong Xiong couldn't help but feel covetous.","He understood perfectly well, even from this initial contact, the immense value of the salty stone. It was a mountain of gold and silver, an endless stream of funds for provisions and supplies.","Zhang Mingdian suddenly spoke up, \"How much salty stone does that caravan still have in hand?\"","The trusted subordinate answered, \"None. They sold every last bit and made quite a sum of silver. Governor Nangong, should we...\"","He made a gesture suggesting killing them and taking the goods.","\"Nonsense! Absolutely not!\" Zhang Mingdian slammed the table and sternly rebuked.","His reaction was so strong it even toppled a wine cup on the table, making the subordinate shrink his neck in fright. Even Nangong Xiong was surprised. \"Quanshu, what is this...\"","Zhang Mingdian said gravely, \"My lord, currently our relations with Yanzhou are deteriorating, and on the side there's still the Qinglian Sect causing trouble in the shadows. Why would we provoke Qin Shaozong at such a time? Do we not have enough enemies? Do we truly want to find ourselves surrounded on all sides?\"","Nangong Xiong heard this and realized it made sense, immediately saying, \"Do not harm that caravan in the slightest.\"","Zhang Mingdian righted the wine cup. \"The salty stone has already been sold out within Qianfeng Commandery. Its fame is far greater than before. Qin Shaozong's move is likely casting bait to attract the fish. He surely knows himself how coveted this salty stone is. Selling such an item in foreign territories would be like a child carrying a gold brick through the market—doomed to lose both goods and wealth.\"","He continued solemnly, \"However, using Hu merchants as a front, the act of selling private salt can somewhat be justified, since the salty stone is indeed quite different from current salt. Merchants chase profit and will flock to it. Luring merchants to the north, having them come to his doorstep to collect the goods—this way, it's foolproof.\"","The north is Qin Shaozong's territory. Others coming from afar, even if they bring soldiers and retainers, will inevitably be weary after a long journey, and their numbers certainly cannot match the Qin clan's.","At that point, forget about making waves, they might not even manage to stir up a ripple.","Qin Shaozong truly had a clever scheme.","Following his strategist's words, Nangong Xiong seemed to see a mountain of gold, fenced in and sealed tight without a single gap.","He couldn't help but burn with jealousy, finding even the dishes on the table, seasoned with expensive salt stones, bland and tasteless.","\"My lord, I have a plan,\" Zhang Mingdian suddenly said.","Nangong Xiong was still mired in the anguish of that mountain of gold and silver not belonging to him. Hearing Zhang Mingdian's words, he didn't react much, only subconsciously replying, \"Let's hear it, Quanshu.\"","Zhang Mingdian took the wine goblet from in front of Nangong Xiong and placed it opposite himself. Then he took a handled cup and placed it right next to Nangong Xiong's goblet. \"After leaving Guoyun County, I have been pondering. With the alliance between our two provinces to jointly crusade against the White Lotus Sect imminent, such an assassination attempt suddenly occurs. Did Fan of Yanzhou truly not consider that the White Lotus Sect might be behind it? Could he not figure it out, or is he feigning ignorance while knowing the truth?\"","Nangong Xiong was stunned.","\"If it is the latter, your current situation, my lord, is quite precarious. An ally on the surface has become a dagger planted by the enemy. Who knows when this dagger will strike?\" Zhang Mingdian reached out again, this time taking a wine pot from further away.","Thud. The wine pot landed beside his own goblet, also placed close.","The wine goblet and the handled cup, the wine goblet and the wine pot.","The two pairs faced each other, creating a confrontational stance.","\"Drive the tiger to devour the wolf,\" Zhang Mingdian's eyes gleamed with cunning. \"My lord, why not invite Qin Shaozong here to discuss the crusade against the White Lotus Sect. If I am overthinking, and Fan Tianshi has no collusion with the sect, Qin Shaozong's arrival will only better maintain the alliance. If I am not overthinking...\"","Before he could finish, Nangong Xiong was already clapping and laughing heartily, \"Excellent! With Quanshu by my side, what worries could I possibly have?\"","After a moment of silence, Zhang Mingdian added, \"However, my lord, this strategy has a flaw.\"","\"What is it?\" Nangong Xiong asked.","Zhang Mingdian picked up the wine pot from the table and shook it. They had just begun their meal, so not much wine had been drunk, and the pot was still heavy. \"This ferocious tiger we invite to devour the wolf—how should we deal with it afterward? What if it refuses to return to the mountains? How then do we drive it away?\"","Three years ago, the previous emperor, obsessed with seeking immortality, passed away. The young emperor, now eleven years old, succeeded to the throne. Court affairs were jointly controlled by Chancellor Dong Zhou and the Empress Dowager Wang, who relied on the Wang family's backing and governed from behind the curtain, barely forming a precarious stalemate.","Since the previous emperor's death, provincial governors across the land had become tigers breaking free from their chains, frequently making moves, no longer as restrained as before.","It became commonplace for neighboring provinces to clash in armed conflict one day, or for a governor to lead troops beyond his borders the next. Anyone with clear sight could see that the situation of rival warlords carving up the realm was imminent.","Nangong Xiong gritted his teeth. \"Guoyun County lies on the border between Qing and Yan Provinces. Even if Qin Shaozong wants to seize it, he can't take much territory from my Qing Province. Never mind, let's deal with the immediate problem first. We can always handle later matters the old-fashioned way if needed.\"","Ying County, Governor's Mansion.","Dai Li was eating grilled fish in the courtyard.","It was a beautiful, clear day. The refined salt matter was, for her, temporarily concluded. She paid no mind to the remaining tasks of transportation and distribution, leaving them entirely to Qin Shaozong and his subordinates to manage, while she began her vacation.","Dai Li had the kitchen prepare mandarin fish and snakehead fish. After cleaning, the fish were all sliced thinly. She also skewered many river shrimp onto sharpened wooden sticks. Setting up a small brazier in the courtyard, she placed the fish slices, coated with refined salt, onto it.","Because the slices were cut so thin, they cooked quickly with just a little grilling. She used ingredients generously, and soon a rich, enticing aroma wafted from the brazier.","Dai Li flipped the skewers, turning the side already golden brown to the top. The brazier was small, only holding a few fish slices and two shrimp skewers. Seeing they were done, she separated the shrimp skewers, giving one each to Nianxia and Bipo. The two maids initially refused, not daring to accept.","Dai Li said helplessly, \"There are plenty of shrimp, it's not just these two skewers. I have grilled fish to eat, I'm not lacking a bite just now. You both helped move the brazier earlier, how can you not eat a few skewers of shrimp?\"","Unable to refuse further, the two women accepted the grilled shrimp nervously and cautiously.","At first, they remained tense, carefully observing Dai Li's expression. But seeing that she had given them freely and then went back to eating her fish, Bipo and Nianxia gradually relaxed.","Bringing out the custom-made lounge chair from inside, enjoying the scenery, eating grilled fish and shrimp, feeling the spring breeze, Dai Li, sitting in the lounge chair, thought about the two-month deadline approaching and began to imagine the future.","Once she finds Zhou Zhou, she'll need to properly tend to the little one's mental well-being. After everything is settled, she'll arrange for him to attend school.","Nine years old, only third grade. Even in a different era, he'd still have to keep studying. Dai Li thought to herself at that moment."]},{"number":41,"title":"Chapter 41","paragraphs":["Qin Shaozong caught the aroma of grilled fish from afar. At first, he thought it was some military officer in the residence sneaking a private meal, but then he remembered he had recently dispatched almost everyone, all kept busy and on their feet over the refined salt matter. No one could possibly be slacking off now.","Perhaps it was the dancing girls from the rear courtyard. With nowhere else to go, they still resided in their original quarters.","Qin Shaozong initially paid it no mind; such trivial matters weren't worth his time. He was heading towards the main courtyard. As he drew closer, the fragrance grew richer.","The man's long eyebrows lifted.","This scale... it didn't seem like the work of dancing girls. Rather, it seemed like...","He took a few more steps forward, reaching the moon gate of the main courtyard. His gaze pierced through the opening to see a small table laid out in the yard and her, sitting leisurely on a reclining chair.","On the table were dishes—fish and shrimp—while beside it stood a small brazier with more fish and shrimp grilling on it, tended by two maidservants.","Perhaps because she no longer needed to go to the salt lake, she wore a light cloud-colored deep robe with a crossed collar today. Her hair was styled high by a maid, revealing her slender, fair neck. A gold-inlaid jade and kingfisher-feather butterfly-patterned hairpin was tucked horizontally into her coiffure.","Hearing footsteps, she gracefully lifted her head, her long, fan-like eyelashes rising with the motion. A ray of sunlight reflected in her pitch-black pupils, like two translucent black agates immersed in a cold spring. As those peach-blossom eyes curved into a smile, his figure became even more vivid within the gentle, shimmering ripples of light.","\"My Lord has returned.\" A soft voice, like a spring breeze, reached him.","Qin Shaozong's Adam's apple bobbed.","He stood still for two breaths before stepping inside. \"It seems my Lady is in good spirits today.\"","For quite some time previously, Qin Shaozong hadn't returned at this hour. Dai Li had assumed he was still swamped with work, which was why she decided to grill fish in the courtyard today. She had planned to finish eating and clean up long before he returned from his duties. But as they say, man proposes, God disposes—he didn't have to work late today.","In her good mood, Dai Li nodded along with his words. \"Things have been going smoothly lately, nothing to worry about.\"","As she spoke, she asked out of courtesy, \"Would you care for some grilled fish, my Lord?\"","She expected him to decline. He was always busy—either in meetings with advisors, visiting the military camp outside the city, or making trips to the government offices in Ying County.","It was common for him to be away from the residence for two or three days. Sometimes, Dai Li would only faintly hear the commotion of his return from outside after she had eaten her fill, bathed, and was ready for bed. By the next morning when she awoke, he was already gone. According to the maids, he rose at dawn for his morning exercises.","Dai Li was utterly amazed.","Others needed five shichen of sleep just to gather some energy. But him? He slept for two shichen, maybe even less, and could be lively and energetic all day.","\"Since my Lady extends such a warm invitation, it would be impolite of me to refuse,\" he said instead.","Dai Li's eyelid twitched, but there was nothing for it. She instructed Nianxia to fetch another chair from the room.","Qin Shaozong took his seat.","The atmosphere grew a bit strange. The gaze from beside her was obscure yet carried an undeniable heat, like an active volcano with magma surging deep beneath the ocean. But Dai Li was used to it.","Let him look. That's all he could do anyway.","Dai Li calmly turned the fish slices on the grill.","She was actually almost full. She had intended to let Nianxia and Bipo clean up the remaining fish and shrimp, but with Qin Shaozong here now, he would have to finish them.","\"My skills are not as good as Chief Feng's. I hope you can make do, my Lord,\" Dai Li said, handing him a skewer of grilled fish.","After skewering the fish, the wooden stick had limited length. Dai Li held the top end, leaving the lower section exposed for Qin Shaozong to take.","That large, dark hand reached over. He did take the lower part, but his grasp enveloped her fair hand at the top as well.","Dai Li glanced sideways, her tone remarkably calm. \"A gentleman guides others with words and restrains them with actions, selecting the good to follow, acting steadily to go far. My Lord should be cautious in word and deed, lest you chill the hearts of your many advisors.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"...\"","His large hand shifted backward, now holding the rear portion of the wooden skewer much more properly.","Watching the silent Qin Shaozong, Dai Li felt instantly pleased and couldn't help but smile. \"I am glad you can accept advice with an open mind.\"","Snap. The sound of a wooden skewer breaking rang out.","Dai Li pretended not to hear.","Qin Shaozong finished that skewer of grilled fish with an impassive face. Just as he tossed the broken stick into a small bamboo basket nearby, hurried footsteps suddenly sounded from outside.","\"My Lord, a messenger from Qingzhou requests an audience. He says he has urgent correspondence for you,\" a guard reported.","During these \"holiday\" days in the residence, besides practicing calligraphy, Dai Li would occasionally seek out Nalan Zhi for games of chess.","Relationships are built through interaction. She currently relied on this Master Nalan to keep Qin Shaozong in check and could not afford to become distant from him.","What surprised Dai Li more, however, was that Nalan Zhi would proactively discuss the current situation with her, truly treating her as a comrade-in-arms.","Through this, Dai Li had gained a general understanding of the outside world.","Several years ago, Governor Nangong of Qingzhou and Fan of Yanzhou had a falling out due to perceived court favoritism. Later, when the Blue Lotus Sect rebelled, the two regions decided to repair relations through a marriage alliance a year ago.","After the Qing-Yan alliance, whether due to someone stirring trouble or because the marriage contract was signed but the wedding not yet performed, all sorts of problems kept arising, leaving the alliance between the two regions precarious.","Based on the information available, Dai Li found this Blue Lotus Sect rather unusual.","Many uprisings were inseparable from mysticism. Examples from the past included \"Great Chu shall rise, with Chen Sheng as king,\" the \"Son of the Red Emperor\" slaying a white serpent to start an uprising, and \"Five horses crossing the river, one horse transforms into a dragon.\" These prophecies had strong specificity, directly pointing to individuals like Chen Sheng, Liu Bang, and the Sima family...","But the Blue Lotus Sect was different. The \"true words\" it disseminated contained no clear leader. It only claimed the sect possessed secret methods to deliver worldly men and women. All who converted to the Blue Lotus Sect would return to the heavenly realm in the future, spared from calamities, with the most devout believers even attaining eternal life there.","Such \"true words\" held immense allure for the common people at the bottom. Moreover, it was said the Blue Lotus Sect had a history of over a hundred years since its founding, existing since the earliest signs of the Yan Dynasty's decay.","Over this long period, the Blue Lotus Sect had grown into a colossal entity, not only boasting numerous followers but also maintaining excellent order, even to the point of being strictly hierarchical.","Now, with a messenger from Qingzhou arriving, Dai Li guessed it was likely related to this Blue Lotus Sect.","Normally, when a messenger from another region came, even if Qin Shaozong didn't receive them personally, he would send a high-ranking military officer to meet them.","\"He has traveled a long distance and must be quite weary. Escort him to rest and bring the letter to me,\" Qin Shaozong said. This meant he wouldn't receive the messenger personally, nor even send a trusted subordinate to meet with him.","The guard acknowledged the order.","Daili gave him another glance. Qin Shaozong smiled and asked, \"Does my lady find it inappropriate?\"","Daili replied honestly, \"I don't understand these matters well and cannot offer you any advice.\"","Soon, a guard returned with a letter.","Qin Shaozong broke the wax seal, his eyes scanning the lines rapidly, a slow smile curving his lips. \"This Governor Nangong is not a fool after all.\"","Although Daili had repeatedly requested to join his council of strategists, she had always been clear about her own objective. She was purely seeking shelter, a way to make herself untouchable to him, not truly intending to exhaust herself in his service.","Now, with this letter from Qingzhou, she paid it no mind and asked no questions, keeping her eyes downcast as if completely unaware—in modern terms, she was slacking off.","Qin Shaozong glanced at her sidelong, knowing she preferred to stay uninvolved, but he was determined to thwart her wishes. \"Since you are now under my command, my lady, you might as well take a look at this letter from Qingzhou. As an advisor, if you cannot offer even a sliver of insight, you risk being removed from the council.\"","Daili immediately reached out, and he handed her the letter.","Daili had been diligently studying the cursive script these past days. Although she still couldn't write it fluently, she could now read it almost as quickly as she used to.","It was an invitation letter. While termed an invitation, given the current political climate, Daili felt it read more like a plea for help.","Having resolved to idle away her time under his command, after finishing the letter, Daili promptly gave him a paraphrased summary. \"This Governor Nangong is a clever man.\"","Qin Shaozong laughed in exasperation. Her slippery, evasive nature really asked for a lesson.","He would deal with her thoroughly sooner or later.","Being stared at by those large, feline-like brown eyes was indeed pressure-inducing, especially when their owner seemed intent on finding fault with her. Daili gave a light cough, adding a supplement to her statement. \"I suggest you march your army to Qingzhou. Although the court's control over the provinces is waning day by day, rashly entering another province's territory could easily provide grounds for criticism. Now that Governor Nangong extends such a warm invitation, what reason is there to refuse?\"","Qin Shaozong gave a soft, amused snort. \"My lady speaks wisely.\"","He was about to say more when footsteps sounded from outside again. Unlike before, this time the approach was exceptionally hurried—not a brisk walk but more like a run.","Daili's brow twitched slightly.","An urgent matter?","Lately, there hadn't been many things that could be called \"urgent.\" Could it be that the merchant teams sent to sell refined salt in various provinces had returned?","Not all of them, but those sent to provinces not bordering the northern territories were likely to have their entire salt stock confiscated. However, you couldn't catch a wolf without sacrificing some bait; Qin Shaozong's men should have been prepared for such losses.","Or perhaps there was news from Yangzhou?","Daili's heart began to pound. When the figure finally appeared at the moon gate in the distance, she couldn't hold back a gasp.","It was Hu Bao! Hu Bao had returned!","Later, Daili would learn that Qin Shaozong had sent Hu Bao to the Qin family in Yangzhou. If he was back, did that mean...","Unable to sit still any longer, Daili quickly rose and hurried forward, her gaze darting to Hu Bao's side, hoping to see that familiar little figure behind him.","But there was none. Even as he entered the courtyard and stood before her, no one else followed.","Daili stopped abruptly, her muscles stiffening to the point of aching. Though the sky was clear and bright, in her vision, a heavy, sky-blotting mass of dark clouds drifted in, covering every bit of the azure blue.","\"Captain Hu, is there still no news of my son?\" Daili's eyes involuntarily reddened.","If even a powerful local clan with extensive connections couldn't find her little one, where could she, alone, possibly begin to search?","Seeing Daili on the verge of tears, Hu Bao's expression grew exceedingly complex. He had pondered it all the way back from Yangzhou, yet he still couldn't make sense of it. It was as if an impenetrable fog lay before him, concealing everything.","\"That's not it,\" Hu Bao averted his eyes, speaking softly. \"There is news of your son.\"","Daili's pupils contracted sharply. Seeing his evasiveness, she reached out to grasp Hu Bao's arm. \"News of Zhouzhou? How is he? Where is he? Why didn't he return to Yingjun with you? Has something happened?\"","There was news, but the boy hadn't returned. Could it be that Zhouzhou was already...","Suddenly, lightning flashed within the clouds shrouding the clear sky, thunder rumbled, and a torrential downpour began, drenching Daili and chilling her to the bone, freezing her fingertips.","Her legs gave way, and she began to collapse. Two arms reached out simultaneously from in front and behind, though the one in front only lifted slightly before returning to its original position.","Qin Shaozong caught her from behind, providing support so she could remain standing. \"My lady, calm yourself. It may not be bad news. Hu Bao is here now. Let him tell you everything in detail.\"","He then turned to Hu Bao. \"Report immediately what transpired in Yangzhou.\"","Hu Bao began, \"Qin Ran followed your orders and went to Qiantang. He gathered the local brokers. At first, the search yielded nothing, so he expanded the scope, searching in neighboring commanderies and offering rewards to veteran brokers and traffickers. Later, one day, a family brought their uncle to his door, claiming the uncle, an old man named Sun, had crucial information.\"","Hu Bao's voice dropped a notch. \"That Old Sun used to be a broker, but after injuring his leg and becoming unable to walk well, he left the trade. He said he once saw a drenched, solitary little boy by a river. The age, height, appearance, and short hair all matched. The boy, upon meeting him, asked him to take him to some sort of 'ju,' and said an object on his wrist was broken. He wanted to borrow something from the old man to contact his mom, for which he recited a string of numbers and a name...\"","Daili's breathing grew increasingly ragged.","River, police station, smartwatch, her phone number, Mom.","Without needing to ask more, Daili was absolutely certain it was Zhouzhou! Those bizarre dreams were actually true. Zhouzhou was really in this unfamiliar era.","The thought of her little boy standing alone by the river, with no one to turn to and everything around him utterly strange, made Daili's heart feel as if it were being twisted. \"And then? Where did he take Zhouzhou?\"","\"That Old Sun, observing your son's demeanor, thought he was a child from a noble family. At first, he helped him dry his clothes, thinking he would take him into the city to return him home and claim a reward. But then a troop came along the official road. This Old Sun had recently had dealings with traffickers. He felt guilty, and moreover, he thought it was your son's family coming to find him, so...\"","Hu Bao averted his eyes again. \"He left your son there alone and departed by himself.\"","This was something even Hu Bao hadn't anticipated at the time, but upon reflection, it made a certain sense.","A handler of dubious origins, mistakenly believing the child's family had come looking and knowing his hopes for a reward were dashed, could very well have left. After all, he had only dried the boy's clothes for him—a negligible sunk cost, nothing he would be reluctant to part with.","Daili felt as if struck by lightning, her limbs trembling uncontrollably. \"He... he left? What happened next? Since this old handler encountered Zhouzhou, what about that other passing group later? They must have seen him too, right? Where did my son go afterward?\"","\"Madam Daili.\" Hu Bao's voice was very low, carrying a trace of confusion and pity upon closer listening. \"That chance encounter the old handler spoke of, with your son, happened ten years ago.\"","Daili's pupils contracted to pinpoints, the color draining from her face inch by inch. \"No, how can that be... how can it be ten years ago...\"","Darkness swam before her eyes, and Daili went limp.","Qin Shaozong, who had been supporting her from behind, swiftly caught her. Seeing she had fainted, he simply picked her up, turned, and carried her towards the house.","The courtyard was only a few steps from the side room. Qin Shaozong carried her back to her room and pointed at the taller maid, Bipo. \"You, go quickly and fetch Ding Lianxi.\"","Bipo hurried out.","Qin Shaozong stood silently by the bedside for a moment, his gaze deep as a pool. He said to the remaining maid, Nianxia, \"Watch over Madam for now. Inform me when she wakes.\"","Hu Bao stopped at the doorway of the side room and did not follow Qin Shaozong into Daili's chamber. Seeing his superior emerge, he called out softly, \"My Lord.\"","\"Are you certain it was ten years ago?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","\"Absolutely certain,\" Hu Bao replied in a hushed tone. \"My Lord, how could Madam Daili mistake the time her son went missing? Could the shock of the event have been so great it caused a lapse in her memory?\"","\"Perhaps,\" Qin Shaozong said.","While verbally agreeing with his subordinate, Qin Shaozong privately thought otherwise.","She had said she accidentally fell into a river in Taohuayuan and woke up already in the Jiang residence. When they first met, the leather shoes on her feet were indeed soaked. Now, according to the old handler's account from ten years ago, a young boy, also drenched, appeared by a riverside.","Qin Shaozong did not believe in ghosts or gods. In fact, born with broken eyebrows, he was once prophesied by a high monk to be estranged from all kin, destined to bring misfortune to father, mother, and elder brother. Hence, he held a deep aversion to prophecies and so-called high monks.","But at this moment, he inexplicably believed in the events that had happened to her and her son—events that defied common explanation.","Finding her son was of utmost importance to her. Someone as intelligent as her could not possibly mistake the time. Furthermore, if that salt purification method had existed long ago, it could not possibly have remained obscure until now.","Ding Lianxi soon arrived with his medicine chest. After taking Daili's pulse, he frowned. \"The pulse is rapid. Madam Daili suffers from an excess of internal heat, with fiery pathogenic factors trapped within. I will prescribe several doses of medicine for her to take upon waking. This internal heat must be dispersed quickly, or it may lead to illness later.\"","\"Thank you for preparing the medicine, Congjian,\" Qin Shaozong addressed Ding Lianxi by his courtesy name.","The prescription was written, and the two maids swiftly went to prepare it. An hour later, Daili slowly regained consciousness.","Nianxia, who had been keeping vigil by the bed, noticed immediately and was overjoyed. \"Madam, you're finally awake! You've been unconscious for over an hour. Are you feeling unwell anywhere now?\"","Daili's eyes were vacant, staring blankly at the canopy above, saying nothing.","Growing increasingly anxious, Nianxia repeated her last question. At first, Daili still showed no reaction. Just as Nianxia was about to fetch Ding Lianxi again, she finally saw the woman on the bed shake her head slowly.","Nianxia breathed a sigh of relief and tucked the quilt around Daili. \"Madam, Master Ding said you have an excess of internal heat. He prescribed medicine for you. Bipo is watching over it in the small kitchen. I'll go fetch it.\"","Daili gave no response.","After Nianxia left, Daili curled up under the quilt and turned over, putting her back to the room and facing the wall. It might have been just a moment, or perhaps a long while—Daili couldn't tell—but she eventually heard footsteps.","Not the light steps of Nianxia or Bipo. These footsteps were steady and firm. The only person in the entire estate who could enter her room so openly was him.","Daili did not turn around, maintaining her curled-up posture, motionless.","\"Madam,\" Qin Shaozong stopped beside the bed.","No answer came.","From Qin Shaozong's perspective, the lady on the bed lay on her side. Her ink-black hair, freed from its updo, cascaded like water over her shoulders and back, lending her an inexplicably fragile air.","He sat down beside the bed. \"Finding someone after ten years is indeed difficult, but it is not entirely impossible.\""]},{"number":42,"title":"Chapter 42","paragraphs":["After a few breaths, the woman on the bed sat up, clutching the quilt. Daili did not turn to look at the man beside her. She kept her eyes downcast, fixed on the brocade patterns on the quilt cover, her voice as light as the wind. \"Is it really possible to find him?\"","It wasn't one or two years, nor three or four, but a full ten years.","As an adult with some knowledge of ancient times due to her work, she was barely managing here. How much more difficult would it be for a child not yet ten years old?","In the third grade, he hadn't yet begun the science subjects introduced later in middle school. Zhou Zhou knew nothing. How could he survive in this cannibalistic feudal era?","Moreover, a few days ago during a casual chat with Nalan Zhi, Daili had inadvertently learned that nine years ago, a great famine had swept through various regions.","Unlike modern agriculture, which had long entered the era of industrial development, ancient times had no machinery, no chemically synthesized compound fertilizers. Grain yields were inherently very limited.","Back then, they had not only encountered a once-in-a-century drought but also a plague of locusts. The impact was immense, affecting not just the northern regions but even areas like Yangzhou in the southeast.","The land was littered with corpses of the starved; cries of hunger and cold filled the air. Bandits ran rampant everywhere, and a peck of grain cost a thousand coins. Commoners could only swallow tree bark and eat grass. Children were exchanged to be eaten; families were torn apart, scattered like stars.","When Daili had once sorted through books and read \"Lament for the Vegetable People\" with its lines like \"First, the two arms are severed and hung at the butcher's shop, then the thigh meat is slowly cut to make soup,\" she had felt the phrase \"Great famine, men ate each other\" was a curse. But after all, that was history, a flat description in black and white, a tragedy that would absolutely never repeat in modern times. So, apart from discomfort, she hadn't felt anything particularly strong at the time.","Now, however, the thought that her little boy might have been weeping, carved up, and cooked for meat during that famine made a chill rise from the depths of her heart. Her heart ached in spasms, the pain so intense she unconsciously curled up, shrinking into a ball.","She couldn't help but imagine it: amidst the child's desperate cries, his screams for his mother begging for help, that gleaming knife comes slashing down.","Then skin and flesh are split open, bright red blood gushes out like a spring, and white bones are exposed.","Pieces of tender flesh fall into the pot. A crowd of faceless diners around it cheer incessantly, each holding bowls and spoons, scrambling to get a share of that steaming pot of human flesh stew.","What Hu Bao brought back wasn't just news, but also a snake made of ice. The snake burrowed deep into Daili's heart, gnawing at her flesh and blood with its sharp, serrated teeth.","A cold air surged from the bottom of her heart, and Daili began to tremble uncontrollably.","Suddenly, the brocade quilt beside her was swept up, unfurled, and draped over her shoulders, wrapping her securely from the neck down.","Through the quilt, a large, dark hand covered her own, which rested on her knees. \"As long as you don't lose heart, there is always hope.\"","Spring was already at its end, summer was approaching, and the quilt wasn't as thick as before. The warmth from his palm transmitted steadily through the thin layers.","Daili still hung her head, like a porcelain doll drained of all spirit. She didn't respond, showed no reaction.","At that moment, Nianxia and Bipo returned.","Nianxia showed no surprise at Qin Shaozong's presence in the room. The two maids curtsied. \"Madam,\" Nianxia said respectfully, \"the medicine is ready. Please drink it while it's hot.\"","Daili, wrapped in the quilt, didn't move.","\"Give it to me,\" Qin Shaozong said, reaching out toward Nianxia.","Just as the medicine bowl was about to be handed to him, Daili whispered, \"I'll drink it myself.\"","Qin Shaozong's movement paused slightly, but he still took it from Nianxia's hands. Brewing medicine took time; it had just finished. Considering it shouldn't be too hot to drink, Bipo had thoughtfully cooled it with warm water earlier. Now it was at a suitable temperature.","Taking the bowl, he confirmed the temperature was right. \"Don't leave any,\" he said.","Daili extended a hand from her cocoon-like quilt bundle and, under the gaze of the three, silently drank the medicine slowly until it was all gone.","She couldn't taste any flavor; all the bitterness had gathered in her heart, leaving no room to distinguish anything else.","After finishing the medicine, Daili handed back the bowl but still avoided looking at anyone. Keeping her head bowed, she said in a muffled voice, \"I want to rest.\"","Sitting to the side, Qin Shaozong could only see her ink-black hair hanging down, covering half of her profile. The rouge at the corners of her eyes was much deeper than usual, and a faint, unshed glimmer of tears was visible in her eyes.","After speaking, Daili simply lay down wrapped in the quilt, curled on her side with her back to them.","After watching her quietly for a moment, Qin Shaozong stood up and instructed the two maids, \"Take good care of your mistress.\"","The medicine probably contained sedative herbs. Not long after lying down, Daili's mind began to drift. She faintly heard Qin Shaozong's voice and the maids' responses.","After that, she fell into a dream.","A dream, an endless nightmare, a nightmare without memory or any logic.","In the dream, there were nine suns in the sky. The sunlight, like raging flames, scorched the earth. The surface temperature was so high the air density changed abruptly, distorting the view. The road ahead seemed to pitch and roll with the undulating layers of heat waves.","The land gradually dried up; rivers broke off in the heat. Crops in the fertile fields all withered and died; even the hardiest weeds by the roadside were stained a lifeless, waxy yellow. Daili didn't know where this was. In the dream, enduring the baking of the fierce sun, she pushed forward with a single-minded desire to find the village school where her son studied.","Suddenly, a small village appeared ahead, with triangular thatched huts standing in clusters. Beside one hut grew a crooked-neck tree. Daili felt a surge of joy, thinking she had finally found some shade. She would rest there and, once recovered, ask someone for directions to the school to pick up her son after class.","The crooked-neck tree stood directly in front of the thatched hut. When Daili reached the tree, she saw the hut's door was wide open, and as far as her eyes could see, there wasn't a single person inside.","What family could be so careless, going out and forgetting to lock the door?","Daili helped them close the door, but upon turning around, she saw the other huts nearby were also quietly standing with their doors open. Drawn to them, she went closer for a look. This hut was identical to the previous one—similarly empty.","Suspicion rose in Daili. She looked around at the rows of thatched huts and went to check each one.","Out of ten huts, nine were completely empty.","A hot wind blew, sweeping yellow dust from the ground and dried leaves onto her clothes and shoes. But at that moment, Daili had no mind to brush the leaves from her skirt, for in the wind, she finally heard a sound.","This deathly silent village had a human voice other than her own.","The sun in the sky grew even fiercer, as if determined to evaporate every last drop of moisture from the earth. Daili followed the sound, walking across the cracked, parched yellow soil. After a very long walk, until her throat felt parched and burning, she finally saw a figure.","It was a plainly dressed woman. She was side-on to Daili, walking slowly toward a hut ahead of her.","The hot wind was still blowing, lifting a long, tubular piece of cloth. On the cloth were large patches of red, as if a mischievous child had accidentally overturned a palette.","\"Eldest son, I'm back,\" the woman said.","A gaunt man walked out of the house and asked the woman, \"Well? How much did you get?\"","\"A full three thousand coppers.\" The woman raised one arm, revealing an old red-and-white patchwork cloth bag in her hand, its surface faintly showing the outlines of coins. \"The butcher saw I sold a whole one and said it was a new customer discount, so he gave me a small piece of meat. I heard it was a child who got separated from his mother by accident, with tender skin and fine flesh, the smoothest with little goosebumps. Eldest Brother, let's go inside and eat.\"","Daili couldn't understand what they were saying.","Why were they talking about the butcher giving a small piece of meat one moment, and then suddenly mentioning a child separated from his mother?","\"Younger Sister, what brings you here?\" The woman suddenly turned her head.","Daili clearly didn't know her, yet when the other woman looked at her, she inexplicably felt she should play along. \"I was just passing by...\"","Her words cut off abruptly.","She stared in horror at the woman's left sleeve. The sleeve there was completely empty. A warm breeze swept by, lifting it effortlessly. Unstoppable blood was still spreading from the area near her shoulder blade, staining a large, glaring patch of red.","Yet the woman seemed to feel no pain at all. With a face as pale as gold paper, she stepped forward. A smile cracked open on her parched, earth-like skin. \"Younger Sister, you've come at the right time. We just happen to have meat today. Come, come be our guest. I'll treat you to good dishes and good meat.\"","Just as Daili was about to politely refuse, the woman grabbed her wrist.","The woman's grip was astonishingly strong, nothing like an injured person. Daili couldn't break free and was pulled into the thatched hut.","The cottage was old and worn. The floor was covered with a layer of yellowish dust. A table with a missing leg was propped up with rubble. The man took the cloth bag and went to the kitchen in the back, leaving only the two of them in the narrow main room.","The woman opposite didn't make small talk, only kept smiling at her. The smile was exactly the same, unchanging, like a preset program, making Daili's scalp crawl. She was just thinking of an excuse to leave when the man who had just gone to the kitchen returned.","He held a chipped ceramic plate in each hand. \"Younger Sister, come have lunch.\"","The plates were placed on the table. One held a few pieces of tree bark, the other contained a pallid piece of meat, its edges marked with an incomplete brownish pattern.","\"Come, Younger Sister, try it quickly. It's from the freshest little one, taken while he was still alive.\" The woman, as if her program had been activated, began speaking, eagerly urging Daili to eat.","Daili didn't move. She stared fixedly at the pattern on the meat that looked very much like a birthmark.","Though incomplete, it felt strangely familiar to her.","The stuck gears in her mind began to turn slowly with the woman's words.","A child accidentally separated from his mother... the freshest little one... taking meat... Zhou Zhou...","\"That was a very lively child. He could still cry for his mama after being chopped several times, even said he'd report us to the authorities. Hahaha, how laughable! Who would come to save him? No one can save him!\"","The pallid meat suddenly oozed thick blood. A continuous stream of blood flowed across the slightly slanted table towards Daili, forming a mirror of blood on its surface. In the mirror, a familiar small figure was being held down by two burly men. One of them held a butcher's knife.","The knife fell. Blood spattered.","Tears of blood streamed from the crying child's eyes.","\"No, Zhou Zhou!!\"","A golden sun fell from the sky, and a prairie fire ignited. The crooked-neck tree was burned to ashes, thatched huts were set ablaze one by one. Flames surrounded Daili, fierce fire serpents leaped onto her body, voraciously devouring her flesh and blood.","Qin Shaozong was awakened by the commotion outside—first low murmurs, then the sound of footsteps running out.","The man on the bed opened his eyes. In just a few moments, his brown pupils were as clear and alert as usual. As if remembering something, Qin Shaozong got up from the bed, threw on his robe, and went out.","The main room and the side room were in the same courtyard, its layout largely similar to the guest courtyard of the Jiang residence back then. After leaving the main room, Qin Shaozong walked a short distance and arrived at the side room where Daili stayed.","In the deep silence that should have enveloped the night, this side room was brightly lit.","Qin Shaozong strode inside, passed through the hanging strings of round beads, and saw the short maidservant kneeling on the footstool before the bed.","\"Bipo, you're finally...\"","Nianxia thought it was Bipo returning, but when she turned and saw who it was, her face changed dramatically with shock. \"My Lord, did I... did I disturb you?\"","Qin Shaozong didn't answer her. He walked straight forward. As he approached, he could see the condition of the woman on the bed.","She lay curled on her side, her cheeks flushed a burning red, even her fair earlobes were crimson. But this unnatural hue did not reach her lips. Her usually bright red lips were now covered with a lifeless pallor.","A grayish-white, parched pallor, like peony petals long deprived of water, on the verge of withering.","\"The Lady has a high fever and is trapped in a nightmare, unable to wake. I just sent Bipo to fetch Doctor Ding,\" said Nianxia, holding a damp silk handkerchief.","\"No, Zhou Zhou...\" Daili's heart-wrenching cries in the dream were, in reality, only low murmurs now.","But in the deep silence of the night, both people by the bed heard them.","Qin Shaozong said, \"Give me the handkerchief.\"","Nianxia hurriedly handed over the freshly changed handkerchief with both hands and stepped back from the footstool by the bed.","Qin Shaozong sat by the bedside, folded the handkerchief, and placed it on Daili's forehead. When his fingertips touched her skin, an almost scalding heat transmitted instantly.","The man's long eyebrows furrowed. He checked the pulse at the side of her neck. That skin was also feverishly hot, as if a burning furnace lay beneath. And as he leaned closer, Qin Shaozong realized Daili was constantly shivering.","A high fever with chills—this symptom was often accompanied by cold hands and feet. Qin Shaozong lifted the quilt slightly and reached inside, grasping the pale hand that was clenched tightly into a fist.","It was indeed very cold, like a lump of ice.","She was gripping with immense force. Blue-green veins, like jadeite, stood out on the back of her hand, and her knuckles were white from the strain.","Qin Shaozong's long fingers slipped underneath, forcefully wedging into her palm and prying it open. As expected, her palm bore a row of deep crescent-moon indentations, red as if about to bleed.","Unable to claw at her own palm, Daili's nails dug into the back of Qin Shaozong's fingers, with equally great force, leaving another set of crescent marks.","\"Don't grab him, don't cut his flesh...\" Her eyelashes trembled violently. Moisture spilled from between them, wetting them into even more distinct clumps, then falling rapidly like broken strings of pearls.","Tears fell onto the silk pillow, blossoming into tiny splashes.","Insignificant damp spots, nothing compared to a downpour, let alone the spray of river waves, yet Qin Shaozong gazed at them for a long time. He raised his other hand and brushed over the reddened corner of her eye, wiping away the escaping tear. \"Dreams aren't real. No one dares to grab him.\"","Trapped in a nightmare, the woman was unaware, still lost in her own world. She had been crying too hard, her eye rims red, the tip of her nose red too. As she sobbed, her neck instinctively curved inward, that stretch of pale neck like a fragile bow, seeming as if it might snap if pulled just a little tighter.","The silk cloth resting on Daili's forehead slipped off.","Qin Shaozong picked up the cloth and found its inner layer already warmed by her fever, making the outer side no longer cool.","\"Change it.\"","Nianxia, who had been standing by, quickly handed over another cloth.","Freshly soaked in water, the new cloth was very cool. The moment it touched her feverish forehead, Daili shuddered violently. Ice clashed with fire once more, and the already cracked dream shattered completely. She finally broke free from the hopeless nightmare.","Just awakened, dream and reality still seemed fused, making it hard to distinguish false from true, illusion from substance. Daili stared blankly at the man before her, giving no reaction.","A teardrop hung from her long lashes, poised to fall. As she emerged from the dream and grew still, the tear also hung motionless. Candlelight caught within it, making it seem like a delicate mirror, clearly reflecting his figure inside.","The long finger that had earlier wiped her tears slowly curled. The rough, calloused fingertip was hidden within his palm, while the relatively smoother back of his finger lightly touched her long lashes, catching that glistening tear.","Feeling an unexpected sensation on her eye, Daili instinctively blinked. Her damp lashes swept down, brushing fleetingly against his dark-toned skin.","Qin Shaozong withdrew his hand. A terrifying depth pooled in his eyes, yet his voice was steady and reassuring. \"The name 'Qin Yanzhou' will spread throughout every region. As long as your son is alive, he will surely learn that you are searching for him.\""]},{"number":43,"title":"Chapter 43","paragraphs":["Ding Lianxi was awakened by a maid and learned that Daili had developed a high fever. It was both expected and unexpected; just yesterday he had predicted that persistent internal heat could lead to illness. It seemed Lady Dai had not escaped it after all.","This matter could not be delayed. Ding Lianxi slung his medicine chest over his shoulder and hurriedly followed Bipo to the side chamber.","In the desolate night, the side chamber was lit bright as day.","The fundamentals of diagnosis: observation, listening, inquiry, and pulse-taking. Ding Lianxi skipped the third step, \"inquiry.\" With a fever this severe, a mere glance told him it was serious. After taking her pulse, he once again wrote a prescription for Daili.","The two maids swiftly went to prepare the medicine.","\"My lord, may I have a word in private?\" Ding Lianxi looked at Qin Shaozong, his voice lowered.","Without a word, Qin Shaozong stepped out with him from the inner room, passing through the beaded curtain to the outer area.","Ding Lianxi said solemnly, \"My lord, Lady Dai's high fever is caused by emotional distress. Whether it's herbal decoctions or bloodletting treatments, these only address the symptoms, not the root cause. As the saying goes, a heart's ailment requires a heart's remedy. The root of everything lies in her emotional knot. If Lady Dai's distress persists for too long...\"","He did not explicitly state the outcome, only shook his head gravely.","Qin Shaozong lowered his gaze, rotating the jade thumb ring on his finger. Without a word, he turned and went back into the inner room.","Nianxia and Bipo had both gone to prepare the medicine, leaving only Daili inside. She was terribly cold, huddled under the new quilts the maids had added for her before they left.","High fever sometimes brings tinnitus. Amidst the growing cacophony in her ears, Daili heard footsteps.","The man who had just left had returned.","Qin Shaozong sat by the bedside as before. He placed a hand on her shoulder blade and turned the young woman, who had been facing inward with her back to him, around.","\"Do you not trust what I said earlier?\" he asked.","Daili's damp, long eyelashes fluttered. She did not answer.","She had sunk into utter despondency.","The world was vast, the population immense, and travel was highly inconvenient nowadays. Even traveling day and night from south to north took at least several months. Qin Shaozong's influence was confined to the northern territories; beyond that were others' domains. How could word spread through every province?","Moreover, many feared his power, and even more bore grudges against him. If others learned he was conducting a high-profile search, her Zhouzhou would surely become a target.","Not to mention, a full decade had passed, and there had been a great famine nine years ago. Whether Zhouzhou was even still...","Daili felt the icy venomous serpent in her heart begin to writhe again. Its maw gaped wide, greedily biting off and swallowing a mouthful of flesh and blood. She curled tighter, burying her face deeper into the quilt.","Qin Shaozong tugged the quilt down, revealing her face. \"The news of the Qin family's extensive search has likely already spread in Yangzhou and may reach other provinces later. Even if someone notices a young man sharing the same name and matching certain characteristics with the person the Qins are seeking, it won't matter. After all, we are searching for a nine-year-old boy, not a nineteen-year-old youth.\"","Having been dug out, Daili, who had intended to bury her face again, stilled.","Qin Shaozong tucked a stray lock of hair that had slipped from her temple onto her cheek behind her ear. \"Furthermore, I believe it's highly likely your son is no longer living under his original name. This would help him avoid malicious individuals who would rather wrongly capture one than let a single possibility slip by.\"","Actually, it wasn't \"would not,\" but \"could not.\"","If he were still alive, given his state back then—utterly alone, without household registration or travel documents—even if kindly taken in as a servant, his name would certainly have been changed.","Daili understood the unspoken implication in his words. Tears she had just managed to stop once again flowed from the corners of her eyes.","\"News about the refined salt has been released across the provinces. In the future, merchants from all regions coming to the north for goods will be countless. Once this group tastes the profits, they will inevitably be driven by gain to return a second time. Entrusting them to carry messages won't be difficult. If you worry they might feign compliance while acting otherwise, I can also establish a special inspection team that travels between provinces and grant you full authority over its management.\" His hand, which had smoothed her hair, moved down, still resting over the brocade quilt upon her hand.","\"You need not worry that I will break my promise, abandon the effort midway, or handle it perfunctorily. After all, from beginning to end, you understand best what I desire.\" He gazed deeply at her. The hidden undercurrents and desire within him, in that moment, leaped forth like a tiger from the forest, laid utterly bare before her.","In the current world, ordinary people who follow rules and possess kind hearts might, with luck, die peacefully in old age. But within powerful families and political struggles, such people are often devoured, leaving not even bones behind.","Qin Shaozong was not the eldest legitimate son; he was the second-born. He had once distanced himself from power struggles with an air of nonchalance, amusedly watching others fight to the death, before later plunging into the fray himself and navigating countless scenes of clashing blades and intricate deceit.","Beneath his feet lay piles of bleached bones; beside him stood rows of severed heads and rivers formed from blood.","He had never been a good man.","He watched for opportunities and struck when weakness appeared, never letting slip any chance he could seize. What wasn't his, if he coveted it, he would devise ways to make it his own.","Qin Shaozong never saw anything wrong with this. If not for this domineering nature, the north would not bear the surname \"Qin,\" he would not possess all he had today, and he might have long since perished in a rival's plot...","Daili bit her lip. She knew his meaning.","Searching for someone who appeared a decade ago and might no longer exist, versus finding a child seen half a year prior—the manpower, resources, and difficulty required were entirely different leagues.","Amidst the tinnitus, the familiar sound of a child's crying seemed to return—mournful, despairing, like a sharp long saw cutting again and again against her nerves, stretched to their limit and fragile to the extreme, making her heavy head grow increasingly muddled.","Beneath the quilt, Daili's pale hand slowly clenched. She grasped the brocade quilt beneath her, yet it seemed she sought not just the fabric, but as if trying to grasp the hem of her son's garment. \"One year. I will serve you for one year. After one year, I return to my original position.\"","Returning to her original position meant resuming her role as an advisor, ending their intimate relationship.","She thought one year should be enough.","A man of his high status and power never lacked for women. Many beautiful young ladies would vie for his favor and charm him. His attention surely wouldn't linger on her for long; growing weary of her was inevitable.","One year was also sufficient for her to establish her own foundation and connections within the merchant caravans and the traveling inspection teams. Later, even after returning to her advisory position, she could still remotely direct them.","Previously, she hadn't gone to bed with him simply because, in her view, things hadn't reached that stage yet. But now, she saw the determination and dominance in his eyes.","Dai Li knew she had no retreat left.","With less than an arm's length between them, she and he stared at each other. Finally, those light brown eyes lowered slightly. \"Fine.\"","Dai Li let out a sigh of relief.","The maid returned with the medicine. After drinking it, Dai Li wrapped herself in the quilt and lay down, her eyes still open, devoid of any sleepiness.","Qin Shaozong reached over to tuck the quilt around her. \"Rest early, Madam. That inspection team to tour the provinces will begin formation once your illness has fully passed.\"","Dai Li's pupils trembled slightly, and she slowly closed her eyes. This time, she did not deliberately turn her back to the outside of the bed as she had before.","Whether it was the medicine taking effect or the promise she had secured, the invisible clash of ice and fire within her gradually receded, and she soon fell asleep.","Qin Shaozong did not leave immediately. He remained seated by the bed, watching the woman on the couch.","The green bed curtain on one side had been let down, blocking most of the light. She lay with her head on the brocade pillow, her face, flushed with fever, gradually paling in the dim shadowy light. A once vibrant peony now seemed veiled in sickness, even the vermilion mark on her forehead appeared faded.","Her brows unconsciously knitted together. Her breathing was heavy, sometimes fast, sometimes slow. Clearly, she had fallen into another unpleasant dream, though she no longer murmured aloud as before.","The candle on the nearby stand burned out, the small flame vanishing abruptly, allowing darkness to surge in like a tide.","Qin Shaozong rose from the bedside, personally lowered the other green curtain, then glanced at the maids waiting nearby. He didn't speak, but with just one look, the two women nodded repeatedly.","The soft sound of bead curtains being pushed aside echoed, soon followed by a return to deep silence.","Qin Shaozong stepped out of the side chamber.","There was a moon tonight, a bright full moon hanging high in the sky, glowing with silvery light. After walking out from under the eaves, moonlight spilled down. Qin Shaozong raised his hand, and a shaft of moonlight fell into his palm.","There is a saying: someone who rarely falls ill, once they do, is hit hard and recovers with great difficulty.","Dai Li had been confined to her sickbed for several days, drinking bowl after bowl of medicine, until the entire side chamber was filled with the scent of herbs.","She had been recuperating all these days, never once leaving the main courtyard, unaware that Qin Shaozong had already completed the army's reorganization, and that even the troops from Yuyang had arrived in Ying County. They awaited only his order to march south.","In the study.","A brief meeting had just concluded. Normally, whether military officers or strategists, all would leave at this point.","Nalan Zhi stepped out. Just as he was about to cross the threshold, he noticed the group of military officers had not departed. He paused slightly, a vague thought occurring to him. Stroking his long beard, he left with a smile.","If Dai Li were here, she would notice two new faces in the study compared to days before.","One was a man with a scholarly, almost civil official appearance and shrewd, narrow eyes. His name was Jin Duole. Like Su Xiuzhu, he was also a Military Instructor. However, the latter was exclusive to the Black Cavalry, while the former oversaw the entire Northern Army. In terms of hierarchy, Jin Duole was Su Xiuzhu's superior.","The other had the build of a military officer, standing eight feet tall, with a simple, honest-looking face and a pair of puppy-dog eyes that conveyed a gentle, kind-hearted demeanor. His name was Kuang Ye. But anyone who trusted this honest exterior would be in for a rude awakening.","The worst possible outcome could be referenced by the late Rong Bingzhou, who had already reported to the King of Hell.","After nurturing him under his wing for seven years, a man who had gone through fire and water for him, believed to be a trusted right-hand man, only to turn out to be a spy planted by the neighbor next door. In the end, Rong Bingzhou not only lost his life but his entire province was swallowed up.","After Nalan Zhi left, Kuang Ye looked at Mo Yanyun and blinked his gentle, puppy-dog eyes.","Feng Feng, standing next to Mo Yanyun, rolled his eyes and, under the guise of clasping his hands behind his back, nudged the person beside him with his elbow.","Let Old Mo ask.","This guy has been dying of curiosity lately; let him ask. Ahem, anyway, the Lord knows he's always been rash. Plus, with him being from the Mo family, the Lord definitely won't blame him.","Burdened with the high hopes of his brothers, Mo Yanyun felt his spine straighten by three degrees.","Fine, he'd do it!","So, after Qin Shaozong said, \"Why are you all standing there like wooden posts?\", he was the first to speak: \"My Lord, when are we leaving Ying County?\"","Mo Yanyun clenched his fist excitedly. \"Qingzhou has sent word; they eagerly invite us. Striking while the iron is hot is best now. If we delay further, what if the conflict between Qing and Yan provinces is resolved, or the Green Lotus Sect flees? That would be disadvantageous for us later...\"","The meetings held over the past few days had covered many topics: protecting the salt lake, subsequent sales of refined salt, meetings with merchants from various regions, and the later matter of marching the army south, among others.","There was much to handle, and arrangements for each matter were settled. It could be said that everything was ready, waiting only for the east wind—the departure date was the only thing left.","But precisely that, the Lord had not said when they would set out.","Qin Shaozong first looked at Mo Yanyun, then swept his gaze over everyone in the study. Some lowered their heads, some scratched their ears and cheeks, and one innocently blinked his puppy-dog eyes.","\"What's the rush? We'll depart when it's time. Right now, they're the ones begging for our help. Taking our time is fine,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Seeing Mo Yanyun about to speak again, he simply rose from his seat and walked out, clearly intending to say no more.","After Qin Shaozong left, the military officers looked at each other.","\"Wait, what does the Lord mean? Just a specific date, can't he say it?\" This was the greatly astonished Mo Yanyun.","\"Perhaps he fears unforeseen changes,\" speculated Yan San after some thought.","\"By the way, have any of you seen Madam Dai lately? I haven't run into her these past few days,\" asked Qiao Wangfei, who was gradually recovering from serious injuries.","\"Why are you asking about Madam Dai? Let me tell you, Madam Dai is no ordinary woman. Don't harbor thoughts you shouldn't,\" cautioned Bai Jianping, Commander of the Southern Garrison, reminding his friend.","Qiao Wangfei said unhappily, \"I'm not like that fellow Old Mo, who gets his soul snatched by every beautiful woman he sees.\"","Mo Yanyun: \"...\"","Neither Kuang Ye nor Jin Duole had met Dai Li, but though they hadn't seen her in person, her formidable reputation preceded her.","Kuang Ye stroked his chin, thoughtful. \"How about we pay a visit to Mr. Ding later?\"","\"Why go find Mr. Ding? Are you feeling unwell?\" Mo Yanyun didn't understand.","Yan San was taken aback, then caught on. \"I'll go with you.\"","The two were in immediate agreement. Without waiting for the others, they left the study right after Qin Shaozong.","Jin Duole watched their departing backs, drew in a sharp breath through his teeth, and began counting on his fingers. \"If there really is a situation with Mr. Ding, there might be a major expenditure in the near future.\"","\"What major expenditure?\" Mo Yanyun asked, puzzled.","Jin Duole muttered to himself as he calculated, \"The Marquis's estate in Yuyang needs refurbishing, and the garden will surely require repairs as well... No, no, that shouldn't be necessary. Why would it come to that?\"","\"What's wrong with that miser?\"","\"Who knows? He's often like this.\"","The main courtyard.","Having been confined to her room for several days in a row, Daili grew restless. Feeling much better today, she put on warm clothes and went for a walk in the courtyard.","\"Nianxia, go and find out where Squad Leader Hu is. I have a matter and wish to request his presence,\" Daili said to Nianxia, who, upon receiving the order, hurried off.","Since Hu Bao's return from Yangzhou, she had only seen him once—during his initial report. Later, she fell ill and had not seen him since.","Even though she had heard those words before, and even though they had been haunting her like a curse these past few days, Daili, in a self-punishing manner, still wanted to hear them again from the person involved.","When Qin Shaozong returned, he happened upon Nianxia in the corridor outside the main courtyard. Seeing her hurried pace, he didn't wait for her formal greeting and asked proactively, \"Going to find Ding Lianxi?\"","Nianxia replied, \"My lord, no, not to find Master Ding. This servant is following the lady's order to summon Squad Leader Hu.\"","Qin Shaozong said, \"There's no need. Hu Bao has already returned to Yangzhou.\"","Nianxia was very surprised, thinking to herself, Squad Leader Hu went back to Yangzhou? When did he leave? But she knew these were not questions she should ask, so she simply followed Qin Shaozong back the way she came.","Daili walked slowly in the courtyard, trying to regain some of the strength dissipated from days in bed. Out of the corner of her eye, she saw a dark figure turn into the moon gate and instinctively looked over.","It was him returning, with Nianxia following behind.","Daili pressed her lips together.","\"The wind has been strong lately. My lady should not stay in the courtyard catching a chill. Return to your room.\" His tone brooked no refusal.","After saying this, Qin Shaozong saw she hadn't moved. He stepped forward, his long arm reaching out to draw her in, holding her as they walked together towards the room.","Daili only stiffened for an instant at first, then allowed him to lead her inside.","Upon entering the room, the scent of medicine rushed forth like a ravenous beast, devouring all other odors completely. Qin Shaozong's brow furrowed almost imperceptibly. \"I've sent Hu Bao to Yangzhou. If my lady has anything she wishes to know, you may ask me directly.\"","Daili was slightly taken aback. \"He's gone to Yangzhou?\"","Qin Shaozong explained, \"After that interrogation in the hall, we didn't silence Old Man Sun's family afterwards, nor did we give Qin Ran any instructions. This trip is for him to go back and tie up loose ends.\"","Back then, after Hu Bao obtained the lead, he rushed back to Yingjun without stopping, leaving matters in Yangzhou completely unattended. Since the subsequent plan involves searching extensively across various prefectures for a nine-year-old boy, the information about the \"ten years\" must be kept absolutely secret.","Qin Shaozong guided her to the long chaise lounge and sat down with her. After settling her, he turned her to face him for a careful look. \"My lady's condition seems better today than yesterday.\"","Daili turned her head away. \"I can't have drunk Master Ding's medicine for nothing.\"","Then she asked him, \"That old man surnamed Sun... he truly didn't see afterwards whether my son made contact with that convoy?\"","\"No. He fled upon hearing the commotion, feeling guilty over the past incident,\" Qin Shaozong's voice was calm.","Daili lowered her gaze.","\"In a few days, my lady will accompany me south to Qingzhou,\" Qin Shaozong brought up another matter.","Daili was not at all surprised he was heading south.","Governor Nangong had extended a ladder; this man would certainly take hold of it. Going south... going south is actually good too. Heading south brings one closer to Qiantang...","\"My lord, when may I meet the leader of that inspection team?\" Daili asked eagerly.","Qin Shaozong took one of her hands. His calloused thumb stroked over her soft palm, tracing the fine lines upwards, finally rubbing the tender flesh on the inner side of her fingers. \"As I said before, my lady, that inspection team will be assembled whenever you have fully recovered.\"","A tingling sensation rose from her fingers. Daili instinctively tried to withdraw her hand, but her slender wrist was captured by a large, darker hand, allowing no escape.","Daili paused before saying, \"My fever broke completely today. I feel I have recovered.\"","As if eager to prove her restored health, Daili reached out and touched the leather belt at his waist."]},{"number":44,"title":"Chapter 44","paragraphs":["A dark, large hand reached over, enveloping the slender hand resting on the beast-head buckle of his girdle. He neither tugged at the waistband following her motion, nor did he pull her hand away.","It stayed right there.","His long fingers slid between hers, parting her digits, finally giving a gentle squeeze to those bamboo-shoot-like fingertips. \"I wish to take my lady south, yet my lady seems intent on staying in Ying County.\"","Daili didn't catch his meaning at first.","Who said she wanted to stay in Ying County?","She had no desire to remain here any longer. She wanted to go south, preferably to visit that old man Sun in Qiantang herself.","They sat on a soft couch by the window. The sunlight was strong, making his amber eyes appear even lighter in hue. Qin Shaozong made no attempt to conceal the desire in his gaze now; all the scorching, heavy greed was laid completely bare.","A vicious tiger emerged from the jungle, fully prepared—claws sharpened, fangs cleaned exceptionally well, waiting only to feast and sate its hunger. But the little fox freshly dug out from its den had fallen ill, not as plump or lively as before. So the tiger thought for a moment, chose to lie down, encircling it with its paws, occasionally giving it a lick to curb its craving.","Under his stare, Daili's brow twitched twice.","This man wasn't just thinking of a vigorous, full-scale engagement; he also believed that if they were to indulge recklessly for a night now, her body might not withstand it. She could fall ill again, forcing them to stay in Ying County.","\"Couldn't the Marquis settle for just a taste?\" Daili tried to negotiate.","Qin Shaozong gave a soft chuckle. Just as Daili thought there might be hope, he uttered two decisive words: \"Not possible.\"","Daili gritted her teeth inwardly. This man could be truly, excessively wicked at times.","The sun rose and set, tides ebbed and flowed, and in the blink of an eye, Daili had endured two more days of medicine.","Early this morning, Ding Lianxi came to check her pulse. A look of relief crossed his face. \"Lady Dai's illness has receded by ninety percent. However, this high fever came fiercely and lasted a considerable time, somewhat injuring your foundational vitality. For the next few days, my lady must avoid overexertion. Only then can you fully recuperate from the depletion.\"","While Ding Lianxi was taking her pulse, Qin Shaozong listened nearby. The man rotated the jade ring on his thumb, his expression inscrutable. \"Congjian, prepare several doses of tonic medicine to consolidate her foundation for the lady.\"","Daili had already taken medicine for many consecutive days. It had left her tongue numb and her head dizzy. Hearing she needed more, she immediately frowned delicately. \"No need, I'll just rest—\"","\"Prepare it.\" His tone brooked no argument.","Qin Shaozong looked at her, his amber eyes calm and unrippled, holding only one meaning: Does my lady still want that inspection team?","Daili fell silent.","Qin Shaozong then turned to Ding Lianxi. \"Congjian, we will break camp and depart Ying County at noon sharp. Instruct the servants to purchase more medicinal herbs in the county.\"","After waiting for several days, the order to depart had finally come. The military officers collectively breathed a sigh of relief, all sharing a single thought:","Lady Dai's illness has finally recovered.","Military orders are urgent. In less than half an hour, everything was packed, items to be left behind were settled, and everyone in the residence had efficiently prepared.","Not everyone was accompanying Qin Shaozong south; Yan San was left behind in Ying County.","The Yan family was a collateral branch personally raised up by Qin Shaozong. After Yan Da and Yan Er successively died in the war against the northern kingdom, Yan San, who had always been the most outstanding among the Yan descendants, received even greater responsibility.","Ying County was no ordinary county now. With the advent of refined salt, it also represented the money purse of the northern territories. Yan San's task was to guard this purse well, a testament to the importance of his assignment.","Daili shared a carriage with Nianxia and Bipo.","Listening to the rumble of wheels on the official road and the fading clamor of the city, Daili slowly lowered her gaze.","For the first time, she felt no unease about leaving a city behind.","She was heading south, closer to Qiantang, and perhaps also closer to Zhou Zhou...","Gaoling County, Yanzhou.","The Fan clan of Yanzhou was a prominent local family. Tracing its roots, one could go back two hundred years to a period of internal strife involving imperial in-laws. The Fan family contributed to quelling the rebellion and was thus rewarded.","Of course, it wasn't a monumental feat. Otherwise, they would have put down roots in Chang'an back then, not moved to Yanzhou.","However, the founding ancestor of the Fan family was a clever man. Not only did he start from nothing, but he also excellently nurtured the next two generations of heirs. Leveraging the prestige from their merit, the Fan family widely associated with the powerful and noble, gradually growing in strength within Yanzhou until they became a leading family.","But not every clan head was astute. The Fan family later suffered a lack of capable successors, declining to the point of withdrawing from Yanzhou's elite circles. The turning point came with Fan Tianshi's father. He was a man of considerable wisdom and resourcefulness, pulling the family back from the brink. Unfortunately, heaven envied his talent. Just as he had rescued the family from decline and was rolling up his sleeves for greater endeavors, he was taken by a sudden illness.","Fan Tianshi was not as outstanding as his father, but he was certainly far more capable than the average person—better than most, if not the very best.","Supported by the family's earlier wealth, the Fan residence was enormous. The main reception hall, the principal bedchamber, the rear gardens, the guest courtyards—each was at least three times the size of those in a typical wealthy household. The estate even housed a menagerie where wolves were kept.","There were many courtyards within the residence. Some housed retainers, others advisors, and still others sheltered adopted orphans and sworn sons.","Whether it was an oversight or a touch of a 'survival of the fittest' mentality, all the orphan boys shared one courtyard. Next door to this courtyard, Fan Tianshi's two sworn sons were no exception; they also shared living quarters here.","\"Well, look who's back, the busy one! Often nowhere to be seen. Have you been seducing someone else again? Not satisfied with enticing the Eighth Miss, you still have eyes for others? Truly, the appetite grows with eating. Let me offer you some friendly advice: you'd better tread carefully. Don't capsize in a ditch. Being kicked out of the Fan residence would be the least of your worries.\"","After this torrent of sarcasm from Pingwei, the newcomer continued walking without pause, as if he hadn't heard. This ignited Pingwei's anger. \"Quanjie! I'm talking to you!\"","The figure stopped and turned around.","A black ghost-patterned mask reflected cold glints of sunlight, its ferocious designs seeming to writhe to life, utterly repulsive.","He stood around eight feet tall, wearing a simple black-grey curved-hem robe tied with a plain belt, without any adornments. Perhaps still growing, his frame lacked the solidness of a mature man, appearing somewhat slender and lean.","\"My interactions with the Eighth Miss are merely passing acquaintances. If you continue speaking so recklessly, I will not cover for you when our sworn father holds you accountable.\" Quanjie's voice was unpleasant, carrying an ineradicable hoarseness, as if his throat were damaged.","Hearing this, Pingwei's face contorted, its handsomeness instantly diminished by half. \"Passing acquaintances? How can you have the nerve to say that? If it's just passing acquaintances, why does the Eighth Miss come here every few days? Why does she ask every time if you're here? And why does she send you gifts!\"","Quanjie merely stood his ground, the mask making his expression unreadable.","Pingwei was consumed with jealousy.","That was the Eighth Miss, the most beloved legitimate daughter of his sworn father, Fan of Yanzhou. To gain her favor could mean transforming from a sworn son into a son-in-law.","That Eighth Miss, for some unknown reason, had previously looked down upon Quanjie, avoiding him like the plague, but a few days ago her attitude suddenly changed drastically. The difference was like night and day, as if she had been put under a spell.","The jealousy in Pingwei's heart had been simmered into a thick, poisonous brew, making every part of his body ache with discomfort. He couldn't control himself and began to speak of the past. \"Seven years ago, you dragged your broken leg and knelt before the manor gate, kowtowing and begging to be taken in. Our foster father saw you wagging your tail and begging for pity, and his heart softened. That's why he led you into the manor and gave you a bite to eat. Taking you in as a foster son later was merely showing you favor. Do you really think you're someone now? You're just a house dog. How dare a beast aspire to climb so high?!\"","\"We are both foster sons. If I am a house dog, then so are you,\" Quanjie said calmly.","Pingwei was furious. Once he stepped out of this courtyard, he would have to put on his refined and gentle mask—respectful to his superiors, courteous to those below. No one knew the resentment and frustration simmering inside him. Only when facing Quanjie, another foster son, could he fully vent the poisonous fire in his heart. \"Enough. I'm not like you. I've recently contacted a distant uncle of mine. He's now a county magistrate. He unexpectedly lost his son last year and now wants to adopt me. I'll have a family soon. And you? You'll remain a lonely ghost. If you die out there one day, no one will shed a single tear for you!\"","\"Then go and tell our foster father. Tell him you don't want to be his foster son anymore,\" Quanjie remained unperturbed, like a stagnant pool of dead water. Whether the wind blew or stones were thrown in, it could not stir the slightest ripple.","Having said that, Quanjie turned his head away, stepped past him, and headed towards the side room.","Pingwei choked for a moment. Realizing he had been countered, his anger surged even more. \"We're both orphans. What are you so smug about? I was kidnapped and sold by traffickers, that's why I drifted from place to place. And you? Your birth parents abandoned you, didn't they? No, perhaps you brought misfortune upon them, causing them to die untimely deaths, each meeting a bad end...\"","The word \"end\" remained stuck in his throat, unable to be uttered.","It wasn't that Pingwei didn't want to say it, but he couldn't speak at that moment. A pale hand was gripping his neck. As that scar-covered hand tightened, Pingwei's face rapidly turned crimson, his eyes beginning to bulge.","Both his hands instinctively grabbed the other's arm, trying to free his pitiful neck, but he was shocked to discover the other's strength was astonishingly great.","Quanjie turned his head back. The ghost mask on his face was still eerily cold, but what frightened Pingwei more now were the eyes behind the mask.","Cold, chillingly sinister, enough to make one's hair stand on end, like terrifying waves capable of swallowing a person rising on a dead sea.","He wanted to kill him.","A massive shockwave hit Pingwei's heart. He tried to roar that he was also the foster father's son, and if he died, Quanjie would certainly face severe consequences.","The hand on his neck suddenly loosened. Pingwei immediately bent over, gasping for air.","A few words drifted down from above. \"Don't be so noisy next time.\"","Flat and bland. He had turned back into a pool of dead water, as if that dead sea had never stirred any waves.","Ignoring Pingwei, who was still coughing violently, Quanjie turned and returned to his room.","The room was extremely simple, with no decorations inside. The table and chair were the most ordinary kind. The room contained nothing more than a table, a chair, a bed, and a few wooden cabinets.","What seemed utterly out of place in this room was an ornately packaged brocade box placed on the table. The outer layer of the box was wrapped in silk, and a faint fragrance wafted from it. It was clear at a glance that the item inside was of considerable value.","Quanjie did not touch the box. He walked directly to the window on the west side of the room and pushed open the tightly shut window. The wind blew in, carrying away the scent left by the brocade box.","Quanjie was about to turn around when his gaze swept past a red kite caught in a tree not far away, and he suddenly froze.","That large tree was not within the courtyard where he lived, nor was it even within the Fan Manor. However, because it grew exceptionally tall, it could be seen even from inside the Fan Manor. A bright red kite was tangled in the high branches, very much like a child's kite accidentally caught there while flying.","Quanjie stared at the red kite for a moment, then left his room again.","Pingwei was still in the courtyard. Seeing him come out of the room, he instinctively wanted to sneer a word or two, but as soon as he opened his mouth, his throat burned with pain, silencing him.","Watching that departing figure, Pingwei gritted his teeth. That scoundrel Quanjie must be going to seduce Eighth Miss again. No, he couldn't just sit idly by and do nothing.","...","Quanjie did not leave the Fan Manor. Instead, he went to the servants' quarters in the west. This was a common dormitory housing many household servants, including gatekeepers.","Compared to other servants, gatekeepers were among those who left the manor relatively more often, so maids and attendants would occasionally ask them to buy things.","On the way, he encountered others. An old gatekeeper said with a smile, \"Quanjie, here to see Old Zhang for your goods again?\"","Quanjie nodded silently and walked past him into the room where Old Zhang stayed.","Faint whispers drifted from behind.","\"I've been in the manor for over three years. Quanjie is still as strange as ever. It seems besides being somewhat familiar with Old Zhang, he has no connections with anyone else.\"","\"I've been here for over five years, and he's always been like this. Some people at least answer when asked a question. He doesn't speak even when others ask, like a mute, with a wooden personality. A real oddball.\"","\"Shh, not so loud. He hasn't gone far yet. In the past, it was different. Everyone knew the master raised his foster sons like dogs, and more than a dozen have died that way. But times have changed. I heard Eighth Miss has somehow suddenly taken a fancy to him. Who knows, he might fly up the branch and become a phoenix.\"","\"It's not that easy. Eighth Miss is the master's most beloved legitimate daughter. Do you think Quanjie is the son of a provincial governor? He's just a lowly servant, with no father, no mother, and no power. Even if Eighth Miss doesn't mind his filth and ugliness, the master would never allow it.\"","...","Quanjie entered the small room, leaving the voices behind completely. At the moment, there were only two people in the room: Old Zhang, the gatekeeper he was looking for, and a retainer who had worked the night shift yesterday and was now resting.","\"You're here,\" Old Zhang said, lifting his eyes at the sound of footsteps, appearing honest and slow. He took out a small paper packet from a cabinet. \"Here, this is what you asked me to buy before. Recently, that shop has been short on supplies, business is tough, and the prices are going up...\"","He lifted his eyes. His somewhat dull gaze suddenly changed—sharp, shrewd, like a snake awakening from hibernation. \"But the shopkeeper said you're an old customer, and every transaction has been very smooth. So, if you pay for the next two batches upfront, not only will he not raise your price, he'll even give you a discount.\"","Old Zhang lived in the common dormitory. The sleeping retainer was not far away. There was no door separating them; one could see the other's every move just by turning their head.","The retainer turned over, mumbled something, scratched his arm, and continued sleeping.","The awakened serpent has returned to hibernation. The sharpness in Old Zhang's eyes faded, and he reverted to being that taciturn gatekeeper. Quanjie placed the paper packet inside his robe, then returned to his own room without a word.","Once the door was securely closed, he took out the packet, set aside a portion of fish maw contained within, and retrieved a folded sheet of mulberry bark paper.","The paper was covered with writing, densely packed, appearing to be several utterly unremarkable nursery rhymes. Quanjie studied it for a moment, extracted the hidden information, then fetched a flint to light the candle on the table and promptly burned the mulberry bark paper.","The flame had just died when a knock came at the door.","\"Quanjie, the Benefactor summons you. Go to the study at once.\" It was a servant delivering the message.","Quanjie acknowledged, tidied everything, and left his quarters.","The Prefectural Governor's study was located in a heavily guarded area of the estate. Upon entering this zone, one frequently encountered patrolling guards, while an intangible aura of opulence pressed upon the senses.","Soaring eaves and upturned corners, carved beams and painted rafters—each detail exuded solemnity and grandeur. The summer breeze stirred, causing the exotic planted shrubs to sway, their blossoms sending forth faint traces of fragrance.","The study door was shut tight. Quanjie knocked.","\"Enter.\" A deep voice sounded from within.","He pushed the door open and entered. The moment he turned around after closing the door, two heavy words struck him.","\"Kneel.\"","Quanjie lowered his gaze and silently sank to his knees.","A dark shadow suddenly lashed out, its speed so great it even whipped up a whooshing sound, followed immediately by—","Crack!","A long whip struck fiercely across his arm and shoulder blade. Quanjie's figure swayed slightly, but he did not utter a sound.","Fan Tianshi was past forty, with a broad forehead, pale complexion, and a light beard. He usually wore a smile, easily giving the impression of an amiable, approachable man. But at this moment, his smile was gone, his face inexplicably appearing sinister and cold to the extreme. \"Do you know your fault?\"","Quanjie kept his head bowed. \"I beg my foster father to instruct me.\"","\"A fine 'instruct me.' If you cannot remember, I don't mind giving you another reminder,\" Fan Tianshi said with a cold laugh.","The whip swept through the air, landing two more cracks on his body. Quanjie remained kneeling where he was. Apart from the initial slight sway, he afterward stood as immovable as a stone statue, enduring the blows.","Fan Tianshi was not a military man; after three lashes he was somewhat tired.","Placing the long whip on the desk, he suddenly softened his tone. \"Quanjie, do not blame your father for being harsh with you. Seven years ago, the moment I saw you before the estate gates, I knew that young boy—who didn't wail in agony like an ordinary person even with a broken leg—possessed an inherently resilient nature. You could endure more hardship than others, bear what they could not. You might achieve great things in the future. That is why I permitted you to enter the estate and even sought out Xinglin for you.\"","\"Quanjie dares not forget the great kindness of my foster father,\" Quanjie replied, still with bowed head, submissive and obedient.","Fan Tianshi gave a slight smile. \"You are meticulous, more steady than Pingwei. You are the foster son I hold in highest regard. All you have done for the Fan family these years, I have seen. My heart is a clear mirror, I understand perfectly well. Your father places high hopes in you...\"","His smile suddenly vanished, revealing a trace of malice. \"But you have your own path. A man with bloodstained hands should not taint pure white. There are some people you should not even touch, let alone dare to yearn for. Do not let greed destroy you.\"","\"Quanjie would not dare. Quanjie's heart is solely devoted to serving my foster father, to repay his life-saving grace. I have no other thoughts,\" said the man kneeling on the ground.","Fan Tianshi's tone softened completely as he moved on to other matters. \"A merchant caravan from the north has arrived selling 'saltpeter.' This substance is rather suspicious; I suspect it is related to Qin Shaozong. Go and interrogate that caravan. Also, I have received word that a shipment of tribute goods from Ganxu Province is to be transported to Chang'an, taking the route through Heng Hui and the Fei River. It will arrive in Xinzhou in a few days. Take some men and handle it. Follow the usual method. Do it cleanly. Leave no trace behind.\"","Quanjie: \"As you command.\"","Fan Tianshi rose from his seat, walked around the long desk, and helped Quanjie to his feet. He personally straightened Quanjie's lapels. \"Go. Your father awaits good news.\"","The sun moved, the stars shifted. Amidst the tightly coordinated military advance, the northern army led by Qin Shaozong finally reached Guoyun County.","Guoyun County—this was the border area between Yan Province and Qing Province. To be more precise, Guoyun County belonged to Qing Province.","After setting up camp outside Guoyun County, Qin Shaozong once again received a warm invitation from Nangong Xiong.","\"Madam, accompany me into the city.\""]},{"number":45,"title":"Chapter 45","paragraphs":["As the governor of a province, even though Guoyun County lacked a proper governor's mansion, Nangong Xiong could arrange two residences with just a few words.","Two large mansions were built next to each other. They had been vacant because the merchant who owned them had gone to another region for business and were listed with a property agent, waiting for a destined buyer.","A destined buyer never came, but a powerful overlord did. Nangong Xiong commandeered the two mansions and dispatched servants to clean them. They were scrubbed from top to bottom, the overgrown weeds in the courtyards were all pulled out and replaced with pleasing greenery, striving to make the residences look brand new.","In the main hall of the southern mansion.","As the host who issued the invitation, Nangong Xiong paced back and forth in the hall, his steps faintly betraying a trace of anxiety.","\"Governor Nangong, he's here, Marquis Qin is here,\" a guard hurried in to report.","Nangong Xiong's spirits lifted, thinking he had finally arrived. He was about to go out to welcome him when he heard the guard had more to say:","\"This subordinate saw several young women in Marquis Qin's entourage. He took them and went to the northern mansion first.\"","Generally speaking, for such an important meeting, to show respect, the leader should proceed directly to the other party's residence. As for luggage and other matters, they could be left to subordinates to sort out. It wasn't as if there was no one available, so why bother doing it personally?","Moreover, with the two mansions being adjacent, this act of \"passing by the door without entering\" seemed somewhat arrogant no matter how one looked at it.","Nangong Xiong was astonished. \"Young women? When did Qin Shaozong ever bring women on campaign?\"","It wasn't unheard of for powerful lords to bring female companions on campaigns; many armies even kept prostitutes. But as far as he knew, the Northern Army was very strict about such matters, and Qin Shaozong had never been known to bring women on past expeditions.","And now he brings several at once?","Where there's an anomaly, there must be a trick. Something was off.","\"Are you sure you didn't mistake them?\" Nangong Xiong asked.","The guard nodded. \"Three young women shared a carriage, though two of them seemed like maidservants.\"","Nangong Xiong looked at Zhang Mingdian beside him. \"What do you think, Quanshu?\"","Zhang Mingdian said, \"Let's set aside the matter of the women for now. As long as the alliance is solid, even if he brought a hundred women, it would be acceptable.\"","After waiting another two quarters of an hour, Nangong Xiong finally saw the man.","To tell the truth, the two had met years ago, back when Qin Shaozong was not yet capped, merely a youth of sixteen or seventeen who didn't have to bear the family responsibilities.","He had left the north with a few attendants to travel through various provinces and encountered Nangong Xiong in Qingzhou. One was young and vigorous, proud to the bone; the other had just recently come of age, having smoothly secured his position as heir, and was brimming with ambition.","When the two clashed, minor incidents could escalate into major friction. After Qin Shaozong's attendants were beaten, he retaliated by setting fire to Nangong Xiong's private residence and then made a quick escape with his people.","Years had passed, and what was once a major clash had long since become an insignificant trifle.","But upon seeing this old acquaintance, Nangong Xiong's back teeth still itched a little. Pleasantries were still necessary, though. Considering this man had first slighted his messenger and now arrived late, the greetings that left his mouth inevitably carried a hint of sarcasm. \"It's been many years. Marquis Qin's heroic bearing surpasses even before. It seems the north suits you better than Qingzhou.\"","Zhang Mingdian's brow twitched.","A faint smile touched Qin Shaozong's eyes. \"The scenery in the north is indeed fine. Otherwise, merchants from Qingzhou wouldn't swarm there in droves.\"","Nangong Xiong's face darkened slightly. He was about to retort when he caught his strategist frantically signaling him with his eyes. He paused, then cleared his throat. \"It's getting late. Perhaps we should start the banquet.\"","It was both dinner time and easier to discuss matters over food and wine.","The banquet began.","Two tables were placed side by side at the head of the hall. Below, generals and advisors from both sides were seated to the left and right. Fine wine and dishes were served in abundance, wine jars piled up like clouds, as they ate and talked.","After three rounds of drinks, Nangong Xiong said, \"Those monsters of the Green Lotus Sect have been making frequent small moves lately, which is utterly annoying. I'll be frank with you. Earlier, I formed an alliance with Fan of Yanzhou, intending to eradicate the Green Lotus Army entrenched in Huaian County. But just as we were about to launch the campaign, a general died within the Yanzhou army.\"","Qin Shaozong twirled the wine cup in his hand.","Currently, message delivery was often inconvenient, and this matter had been deliberately suppressed, so he truly hadn't known about it.","However, it wasn't surprising.","Nangong Xiong angrily slapped the table. \"That fellow Fan Tianshi actually concluded that my side killed his man! Preposterous! Why would I kill someone in his army at such a critical juncture? If I really disliked him, I could simply deal with him after the fact.\"","Below, Zhang Mingdian coughed heavily twice. \"What my lord means is, he would teach him a lesson afterward.\"","Mo Yanyun laughed. \"Ha! You scholars always talk in circles. If he's unprofitable, eliminate him. What's wrong with that?\"","Nangong Xiong also laughed. \"Qin Changgeng, I never thought you had such a straightforward person under your command. Rare, truly rare.\"","Zhang Mingdian: \"...\"","The corner of Qin Shaozong's mouth twitched. He decided to skip this topic. \"So now, you and Fan of Yanzhou have completely fallen out?\"","\"Not entirely,\" Nangong Xiong stated frankly. \"But it's close. In any case, he's now more concerned with finding out who killed his general than with suppressing the Green Lotus Sect.\"","Taking a sip of wine, Nangong Xiong sighed again. \"Although Fan Tianshi is foolish, the foundation his father left him is substantial enough for him to squander. And this man...\"","\"What about him?\" Seeing his complicated expression, Qin Shaozong casually prompted, \"Is he perhaps fortunate?\"","\"You said it. He does have good luck.\" Nangong Xiong said in a low voice, \"Fan Tianshi picked up many orphaned boys in his early years, didn't he? It's said he specifically chose those with exceptional bone structure, filling several courtyard compounds. Among these hundred or so, some died, some were crippled, but a few truly stood out.\"","Qin Shaozong pondered.","He had eyes and ears in every province, though their numbers varied. He had heard about Fan Tianshi adopting sworn sons, but that was the extent of it.","Some liked to keep dancers, some liked to raise fierce beasts, and naturally, some liked to play father to others everywhere.","But 'stood out'?","No name had yet reached his ears.","\"Quanjie,\" Nangong Xiong offered a name. \"But because he often wears a ghost mask, many call him Ghost Face. This man has done many dirty deeds for Fan Tianshi, including eliminating old ministers who traded on seniority and spies from other provinces. I once suspected that the tribute my Qingzhou delivered to the imperial court last year was hijacked by this bastard.\"","Qin Shaozong drained his cup in one gulp. \"Quanjie—a house dog, also a worthless weed. Expecting the horse to run fast without feeding it grass—how can such a good thing exist under heaven? This Quanjie won't stay under Fan Tianshi's command for long.\"","As if finally catching Qin Shaozong's weak point, Nangong Xiong mocked, \"Break away? How could it be so easy? As I know, this Ghost Face Quanjie entered the Fan residence at the age of twelve, and it's been a full seven years now. In those seven years, he's done a basketful of dirty deeds, already making enemies everywhere. Not to mention that scoundrel Fan Tianshi won't let him go; even if he did escape, with no one to protect him then, the Fan family's pursuit plus his enemies coming for him, that kid would die even faster.\"","Qin Shaozong was utterly indifferent, simply pouring himself a cup of wine. \"That's true.\"","\"If he wants to escape this situation, there are only two paths. First, slit his own throat, die early and be reborn early, hoping for more luck in the next life, not having to be someone's house dog. The second...\" Nangong Xiong suddenly chuckled, \"...is to find a father more powerful and influential than Fan Tianshi, have this father handle both Fan Tianshi and all the enemies he's offended, that way he might be kept safe. But if it's not his own flesh and blood, with no kinship or ties, what great leader would be such a fool, putting in great effort for no reward, purely looking for trouble, unless his brain's been kicked by a donkey? Even if it were a real son, not everyone would be willing to go to such great lengths.\"","With many concubines, offspring are plentiful too.","Fan Tianshi is a prime example, with concubines filling several rooms, not counting those who died young, he has over fifteen or sixteen living offspring. If that scoundrel really had such an unlucky son, he'd most likely let him fend for himself, acting as if he was never born.","\"So the first option is still better, a clean slash across the throat, a neat death. Remember to pray to gods and buddhas before your next reincarnation, begging for a better birth.\" Nangong Xiong said.","Just an insignificant person, Qin Shaozong's tone was indifferent, \"Indeed, death would be more merciful.\"","Ghost Face Quanjie was merely a minor topic over wine; Nangong Xiong mentioned it casually, Qin Shaozong listened casually, neither paid it any mind.","Afterwards, they returned to discussing the alliance, including how to deal with Yanzhou later.","When major matters were almost settled, Nangong Xiong said to Qin Shaozong in a low voice, \"The young ladies of my Qingzhou are gentle and charming, delicate and moving. Would Marquis Qin like to experience their grace?\"","\"Thank you. But Governor Nangong should keep them for your own enjoyment.\" Qin Shaozong put down his wine cup.","Hearing his flat tone, Nangong Xiong immediately felt somewhat displeased. His Qingzhou ladies are beautiful as flowers, what did this man mean by that tone, looking down on them?","\"I heard Marquis Qin brought a female companion along. Could it be you've hidden a heavenly beauty in the neighboring residence?\" Nangong Xiong couldn't help but ask.","Qin Shaozong turned his head. He had drunk quite a lot tonight, several wine jars already piled around them, but those brown pupils showed no haze. Instead, they were like knife blades reflecting cold light. \"I came south this time to campaign against the Green Lotus Sect. I hope Governor Nangong can focus on this matter.\"","The implied meaning: Don't meddle in what you shouldn't, and don't be curious about what you shouldn't.","Nangong Xiong gave a cold laugh. \"Offering hospitality out of goodwill, fine if you don't accept it. The beauties of my Qingzhou surpass celestial beings, more enchanting than those from your northern lands.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"The journey here was exhausting, I am quite fatigued. Now that matters are settled, there's little else to discuss. Perhaps we should disperse to rest and recuperate. What does Governor Nangong think?\"","Nangong Xiong's face darkened slightly.","Guoyun County is, after all, part of Qingzhou territory. He is the host; the words to end the meeting should rightfully come from him. Over twenty years have passed, and this Qin Shaozong still hasn't changed his stubborn ways...","\"Then let's end here for today.\" Nangong Xiong said with a forced smile.","Daili finished her evening meal, took another stroll around the residence, and finally returned to her room for a bath.","Compared to Ying County, Qingzhou has a much more developed water system, making water relatively easier to obtain.","This residence had been meticulously prepared before their arrival, with all supplies available, from furniture and decorations down to clothing and horse fodder, even petals to scent the bathing tub.","The preparer could indeed be described as meticulous and thorough.","It was already summer, so the bathwater only needed to be warm.","Nianxia and Bipo prepared a tub of water and thoughtfully placed a basin filled with hot water nearby, allowing Daili to add water as needed and prolong her bath.","After a comfortable bath, Daili dressed and returned to the inner chamber. She took out a mulberry bark paper notebook and a small charcoal pencil from a box and began writing and sketching.","This was a roster, recording the names of each member of the inspection team, as well as basic information about the merchants who had already gone north to purchase refined salt, including which caravan came from where and which state they were headed to.","Besides that, there was also a condensed map she had asked Mo Yanyun to draw.","\"They need to go further south to have a look.\" Daili murmured.","The candle stand beside her burned quietly. Unnoticed, the candle had already shortened by a section. Daili closed the notebook containing her plans and placed it under her pillow. Just as she was about to get into bed, a commotion arose outside.","Daili guessed it must be Qin Shaozong returning.","As before, their rooms were adjacent, so hearing movement now was nothing strange.","Daili let down the plain bed curtain on one side of the bed, then moved to the other side, intending to lower the other one as well to block the increasingly numerous summer mosquitoes.","\"Creeeak.\" The door was pushed open.","Daili's fingers twitched. The other bed curtain slipped from her grasp, and the two curtains closed together.","The bamboo curtain over the inner chamber archway was pushed aside. The bamboo strips clacked against each other, a sound exceptionally clear in the quiet night. Daili's heartbeat gradually quickened along with this soft noise.","Through a layer of indistinct, hazy plain curtain, she saw a tall figure approaching from afar.","Daili caught a strong whiff of alcohol. Her heart skipped a beat. \"How much did the Marquis drink at the banquet?\"","Dark, long fingers parted one side of the bed curtain. The haze between them was pushed aside, and their eyes finally met without obstruction.","The woman on the bed wore apricot-colored inner garments, with large embroidered peonies climbing from her waist and abdomen up to her shoulders. Approaching bedtime, her black hair was unbound, flowing over her shoulders like water.","Black hair, fair skin, red lips—the clash of colors was strikingly vivid. Black like ink, white like jade, red like rouge, the vermilion dot on her forehead serving as the finishing touch. She was truly the soul of snow, the spirit of a flower, making it impossible to look away.","\"Drank not too much, enough to ensure I won't disappoint you by failing halfway tonight.\" His Adam's apple bobbed.","In his eyes, Daili saw a darkness like the deep sea, turbulent and unstoppable.","His hand rested on his belt, his long fingers about to undo its hidden clasp, when he suddenly heard:","\"Wait...\"","Qin Shaozong's face was expressionless. \"Madam.\"","The two words were heavy, carrying a hint of displeasure.","Under that obscure, unfathomable gaze, Daili mustered her courage and continued, \"The Marquis has been traveling and toiling today. Perhaps you should take a hot bath to relieve your fatigue. Also, the smell of alcohol is quite strong; it's making me feel a bit dizzy.\"","The smell of alcohol was actually secondary; the main point was that today, after riding on the march, this man on horseback had surely collected who knows how much dust along the way. She felt that if he had been wearing a white robe today, it probably could have been dyed black.","\"My lady's delicate nature truly cannot be changed one bit.\" The man standing before the plain bed curtain clicked his tongue lightly and turned to walk out.","Daili let out a sigh of relief.","Once the person had completely left, she lifted the brocade pillow, took out that small mulberry-bark paper notebook, and carefully flipped through it once more, gently stroking the rough paper.","The notebook was already quite filled, the earlier pages packed full of writing. She truly hoped to receive good news before it was completely filled.","Just as she turned to the last recorded page, Daili actually heard footsteps.","Not the light steps of Nianxia or Bipo, but rather...","Clatter. A small bamboo strip swayed and made a soft sound.","Daili looked up in disbelief, and indeed, that familiar, towering figure appeared before her eyes once again.","For a moment, she couldn't tell if she had been too absorbed in reading the little booklet, or if he had simply changed his clothes, for why else would he have returned so quickly.","He stepped forward, one pace after another. His shadow seemed to grow wings, swiftly extending from his feet, rushing ahead, arriving first beside the daybed, and then climbing onto it ahead of him, enveloping her slender, pale fingers."]},{"number":46,"title":"Chapter 46","paragraphs":["The night was deep and still. Thousands of households in the commandery had long extinguished their lamps and fallen asleep. Yet, in a side room of a certain grand residence, candlelight flickered, casting a dim, hazy glow that filled the chamber.","Qin Shaozong walked to the bedside and picked up the small mulberry-bark paper booklet resting there. Seeing his movement, Dai Li snapped back to attention. She instinctively reached out to take it back, but her hand stopped halfway and withdrew.","It was unnecessary.","There was no need to hide or conceal it. She was simply burning with anxiety, wishing she could find Zhouzhou tomorrow. Perhaps it was for the best that Qin Shaozong knew now. Maybe he also felt the investigation team was understaffed and would assign more people to her...","However, Dai Li didn't expect that after flipping through a couple of pages, he remarked, \"Madam's handwriting is quite distinctive.\"","Dai Li was stunned, belatedly realizing she had written in the booklet using simplified characters.","He had seen them.","Qin Shaozong flipped through the remaining pages. From beginning to end, it was all written in a strange script he had never seen before, though he could occasionally make out one or two characters.","If it were just a few scattered odd characters, one could explain it away as a personal creation for encryption. But several full pages like this... it seemed less like an invention and more like a script that already existed...","Many things were already beyond clear explanation. Dai Li simply stated, \"These are simplified characters. Everyone where I come from uses them.\"","\"Simplified characters.\" He repeated the three words, then suddenly chuckled softly. \"Rather interesting.\"","Dai Li's eyes shifted craftily. \"If my lord wishes to learn, perhaps I could—\"","Thud. The booklet was tossed onto the small cabinet.","\"We can discuss that later. Right now, there are more important matters.\" With a casual tug, the loosely tied belt at his waist came undone.","The body of a general in his prime was tall, robust, and powerfully built. The lines and contours of his chest and back were solid and flowing. The lamplight from the side spilled over him, giving his deep-toned skin a hue like molten amber or golden honey. An intensely aggressive wildness emanated from him, the potent aura of his hormones seeming to boil the very air around them.","Then, like a fierce tiger breaking free from its cage, a vast shadow engulfed her.","Lips and teeth met. At first, it could still be considered a contest. Dai Li attempted to use softness to overcome strength, to make the man who now had her cornered against the headboard of the bed slow his pace.","But she soon found it utterly useless. He was uncontrollable, acting entirely according to his own whims, running wild.","Learning from past experience, Qin Shaozong initially cupped Dai Li's jaw with his palm, his long fingers pressing lightly against her snow-white skin, just outside her teeth.","He invaded and plundered wantonly, like a starved and savage tiger who, after a long and perilous journey, had finally arrived at a sumptuous feast meant for him alone.","Their breaths, one urgent, one deep, mingled together. The scorching heat seemed to fill her entire mouth, choking Dai Li until her eyes glistened with unshed tears and the tip of her chin began to tremble uncontrollably.","It was as if tiny sparks had been lit within the very marrow of her bones. As his assault grew fiercer, the flames traveled through her bloodstream, setting her entire body ablaze. Her apricot-colored belt was hooked and pulled loose; the embroidered belly-wrap adorned with peonies of the same color came undone as well.","A rough, grating sensation traveled up her waist, following the curve of her side like a wind carrying embers, igniting a prairie fire wherever it passed. When it reached the summit, his hand opened wide, then closed tight again.","A muffled moan escaped Dai Li's nose.","He was far from docile; in fact, he was creating havoc—alternating between tightening and loosening his grip, and at times, with deliberate mischief, using the thick calluses on his fingers to tease, twist, and pluck.","A wave of electric sensation crashed over her. Moaning, Dai Li tried to curl into herself, but with him in front and the solid bedboard behind, the space left for her was pitifully small.","Her fair fingers, clutching at his shoulder blades, tightened incessantly. Her neatly trimmed, rounded nails left several faint red trails on his taut shoulders. The slight sting only fueled his excitement further, causing the thick, dark muscles of his shoulders and back to ripple slightly.","Soft flesh, like the ripe fullness of a lychee, spilled from between his long fingers—a translucent, gleaming white so bright it dazzled the eyes, like luminous pearls glowing in the faint candlelight.","At that moment, a small bird with folded wings alighted on the windowsill. It blinked its beady black eyes, peering curiously into the room.","Strange noises drifted out from within, sounding like a tiger in the jungle crouched by a pond, lapping up water with its tongue. The little bird hopped a couple of steps closer, but was suddenly startled by a sharp, muffled sob that arose. It hurriedly flapped its tiny wings and flew away.","Inside the dim bed curtains.","As if satisfied she wouldn't try her old trick again, Qin Shaozong released his grip on her jaw. Then he pressed down on her and kissed her fiercely once more, not pulling back slightly until whimpering sounds of surrender rose from her throat.","Qin Shaozong gazed at the woman lying on the brocade quilt. Her full, lovely lips and cheeks were now flushed a deep rouge. Her eyes shimmered with watery light, holding a pool of captivating, dazed confusion that could drown a man.","Threads of a subtle, dark fragrance drifted within the curtain, brushing past his nose, skimming over his intensely excited, humming nerves. It was like pouring honeyed oil onto a raging fire, igniting a shocking greed.","He leaned down again, this time finding her plump earlobe. Nuzzling against that delicate skin, he deliberately let his hot breath wash into her ear canal.","\"Qin Changgeng, you can't do this...\"","Dai Li shuddered violently from his touch, desperately trying to turn away, but he pursued her until she was trapped once more in the corner of the bed. Even curled into a ball, she was forcefully unfolded, left to his mercies.","The window in the room wasn't shut completely. A breeze slipped in, causing the candle flames inside to flicker several times.","The light cast on the floor by the candles also wavered uncertainly between brightness and shadow. A stream of apricot-colored silk suddenly slipped from the bed, landing on the footstool beside it.","The wind died down, and the candlelight steadied. The apricot-colored trousers lay quietly on the footstool, forgotten.","Yanzhou, Gaoling Commandery, the Fan Residence.","In the deep of night, when most were already asleep, the study of the Fan Mansion remained brightly lit.","Fan Tianshi, along with his legitimate eldest and second sons, were gathered in the room, the three of them standing around a long table.","\"Father, I never imagined Ganzhou and Xuzhou had such substantial resources!\" Fan Tianshi's second son, Fan Zhongmin, exclaimed repeatedly while holding the gift list.","Not long before, a shipment of tribute from Xuzhou had been transported into Gaoling Commandery under cover of night and silently delivered to the Governor's mansion.","Currently, the Emperor of Great Yan was young and essentially a figurehead, having lost control over the various provinces. However, the provincial governors were not stingy with maintaining appearances.","Each year, they still presented gifts to the imperial court and delivered grain taxes, though exactly how much was skimmed off and how much ended up in their own pockets, only they themselves knew.","The route the tribute took to the capital wasn't hard to trace, as there were only so many official roads. And with the world growing increasingly chaotic and banditry rampant, whether these gifts successfully reached the capital depended entirely on one's own capability.","The eldest son, Fan Boliang, said, \"That Quanjie is reliable in his work; his operations mostly succeed. By the way, Father, how many men did we lose this time?\"","Fan Tianshi: \"Three returned. One is basically useless now.\"","Fan Zhongmin clicked his tongue twice, his tone devoid of any pity. \"Almost a complete wipeout. This Quanjie's life is uncommonly tough. I recall the last shipment from Qingzhou was also brought back by him. I just wonder how the subsequent cleanup went?\"","\"He has always been meticulous; it shouldn't be a problem,\" his elder brother, Fan Boliang, said calmly.","Their Fan family had deep roots; it wasn't that they lacked the silver, but they cared more about the significance represented by those goods. It was both to make that other prefecture appear more arrogant and overbearing before the imperial court and to conveniently frame another party.","When the east household's goods are lost, leave clues pointing to the west household as the thief, let the two families fight, and they would reap the benefits from the sidelines.","\"Father, Quanjie is indeed a useful blade, but I always have an indescribable worry,\" Fan Boliang frowned. \"Over these years, many matters have passed through his hands. He knows too much. If one day he betrays our Fan family, while it might not necessarily splash mud on us, it would still be considerable trouble.\"","Fan Zhongmin, seemingly reminded of something, also nodded angrily. \"Father, this Quanjie is dishonest! Who knows what trick he used, he actually has Xiao Ba chasing after him. Could it be he's no longer satisfied with being a foster son and wants to become your son-in-law? Truly wishful thinking. A lowly slave with neither father nor mother, he should take a piss and look at his own reflection to see what he really is.\"","The Eighth Young Lady was their full-blooded sister, their only younger sister, and the two brothers had always been extremely protective of her.","\"Father, have you considered changing to a different blade?\" Fan Boliang whispered.","Fan Tianshi took the long gift list from his second son's hand, his eyes filled with deep reluctance and doubt. \"Among the new orphans taken in these past few years, none have been particularly outstanding. Without Quanjie, no one can fill his position. Regarding Xiao Ba's matter, I have already warned him. I believe he feels ashamed of his own inadequacy and will act with more discretion in the future.\"","The two brothers wanted to say more, but Fan Tianshi changed the subject. \"Qin Shaozong has come south. That fellow Nangong Xiong is truly reckless, actually inviting him here. It's easier to invite a god than to send him away. Hah, I'd like to see how Nangong Qingzhou will manage to conclude this in the end.\"","The name \"Qin Shaozong\" was like a massive rock thrown into a lake, stunning the Fan brothers for a moment.","Both knew that the Youzhou region originally had extremely poor terrain. In previous years, the northern kingdom repeatedly invaded, coupled with unrest in the southern prefectures, it could be said they were beset by enemies on all sides.","Yet, such a barren land had actually been revitalized. First, they absorbed fine horse breeds from the northern kingdom, then annexed territory from Bingzhou, and subsequently took control of Ying County nearby, which had salt lakes.","The former frontier marquis's capabilities were no longer limited to just guarding the borders...","\"Father, just as you predicted, that northern merchant group selling saltpeter in the commandery is connected to the Qin clan,\" Fan Boliang said in a low voice.","\"This Qin Shaozong is truly capable, actually managing to get such good things from the Hu merchants,\" Fan Zhongmin said, full of envy.","Fan Tianshi: \"Not necessarily from the Hu merchants.\"","\"Father?\" Fan Zhongmin was surprised and doubtful.","But Fan Tianshi changed the topic again: \"I recall Qin Shaozong has two sons and one daughter. Both sons are unmarried, their ages roughly matching Xiao Ba's.\"","\"Father, are you thinking of marrying our sister to one of Qin Shaozong's sons?\" Fan Zhongmin immediately looked conflicted. \"But I remember the first two aren't his biological sons. The last biological one...\"","Fan Zhongmin's expression was complicated. \"He's the youngest, not the eldest. I've heard Qin Shaozong doesn't pay him much mind. Even if our sister married him as the principal wife, I still feel it's somewhat of a disadvantage.\"","Fan Boliang's face showed agreement. Their own full sister was, of course, the best in their eyes no matter what.","Fan Tianshi said coolly, \"If the Fan and Qin families could form a marriage alliance, the Qin family would be a rather good destination for Xiao Ba.\"","The night was extremely deep, the moon having passed its zenith and now slowly slanting westward.","In this hour when the vast majority of commoners were already meeting the Duke of Zhou in their dreams, a certain residence in Guoyun Commandery remained very lively. More accurately, the activity in a small chamber remained undiminished, as both its occupants had yet to rest.","The candle had long since burned down and extinguished itself. All light within the room came from the moonlight slipping in through the window lattice.","Looking from outside the bed towards the inside, one could see a burly figure with its back turned outward, seemingly blocking something into a corner. A long, pale leg extended from the man's side, its pink-tinted heel trembling unsteadily as it rubbed against the brocade coverlet below, as if trying to borrow leverage to retreat.","But behind the corner were two tightly joined walls—no retreat possible; ahead were jagged, rock-like protrusions—advance even less possible.","Who knows what was touched, but the muscles along that pale leg suddenly tensed sharply, even the rounded toes curling tightly. After about two breaths, they abruptly went limp again.","A low chuckle sounded.","A large, dark hand grasped that section of pale leg, lifted it slightly, and hooked it over the crook of his own arm, then continued the vigorous, sweeping motions of the unfinished business from before.","\"Qin Changgeng, change places, not the wall...\"","Her voice seemed to carry a pool of water, the tail end trembling with an indescribable allure, making the prominent Adam's apple of the man before her slide up and down once more.","\"Just now you clearly said you didn't like lying down, and now you change your mind. Not this, not that. My lady is truly terribly spoiled, so difficult to serve,\" Qin Shaozong laughed as he withdrew some distance.","His withdrawal was slow, every minute movement excruciatingly clear.","Dai Li humphed, instinctively tilting her head back to draw a breath, trembling too much to speak. But before she could adjust her breathing, her waist suddenly tightened. She was dug out from the corner, flipped over, and placed face down.","A colleague of Dai Li's from before kept a cat at home and often shared daily photos, including ones of the cat stretching after a nap.","She had always found that posture adorable—a furry ball curving into a slope, cute enough to melt one's heart, making anyone who saw it want to reach out and rub that furry bundle.","However, when she herself became the cat, with the small of her back firmly gripped and unable to break free, Dai Li found everything had taken a turn for the worse.","This man on the bed favored broad, sweeping motions; the phrase \"gentle and refined\" had absolutely no connection to him. Dominant, allowing no resistance, and with some less-than-proper minor proclivities not spoken of to outsiders.","The piled brocade coverlet before her eyes kept swaying, almost occupying her entire field of vision.","When that unbearable sensation surged up from below once more, rising to her throat, Dai Li felt as if her throat bone were being brushed by a feather tip, producing a fine, dense tingling that nearly made her cry out. Unable to help herself, she crawled forward on her knees a step, biting down on the swaying corner of the coverlet, just barely stifling the sound rising in her throat.","Dai Li was covered in a fine sheen of sweat, as if she had been steamed in a sauna. She glistened with perspiration, like she was draped in a layer of shattered starlight.","Summer is also a season of harvest, with ripe, luscious peaches displaying a moving, vivid pink on their surface.","A breeze passed, causing the heavy fruit to sway and tremble. With the occasional soft sound of a palm meeting flesh, that vivid pink deepened, as if the overripe fruit on the branch were about to burst forth with sweet juice.","Dai Li deeply felt that whether in ancient times or modern, perhaps all those in leadership positions have mastered the art of making empty promises. Whenever she felt she couldn't hold on any longer, this man would dangle a carrot before her.","\"Just endure a little longer, my lady. Once we find your son, I shall treat him as a true son of the Qin family. How does that sound?\"","\"...Really?\"","\"Naturally.\"","Dai Li, sobbing and utterly disoriented, had the illusion that she had transformed into a fallen leaf, swept away by a violent storm.","She drifted ethereally in the wind and rain, utterly at its mercy, unable to control being lifted high, suspended mid-air only to plummet suddenly. It was as if she had just touched the ground one moment, and the next was carried onto a tightrope over a ten-thousand-foot cliff.","After being tossed about like this for what felt like an eternity, she was then swept to a mountain spring's surge point. The torrential waters rushed and churned, battering her until she felt completely shattered.","As her consciousness gradually faded into a haze, only one thought remained in Dai Li's mind: The promises he makes in bed had better be as binding as his word given in daylight!","As dawn broke, many in the estate were already awake, with the military officers beginning their unwavering morning drills.","This residence was originally an old merchant's home, so naturally it lacked a proper training ground. But it was no matter; the officers had brought their own weapons and could simply find any open space to practice martial arts.","Banquets were the best places for exchanging information. After a few rounds of drinks, those with loose tongues generally became very talkative, answering whatever was asked.","Kuang Ye was sharing with several others the information he had gathered yesterday after getting chummy and brotherly with the Qingzhou officers.","\"Qingzhou suspects that the batch of tribute goods they previously sent to Chang'an was intercepted by people from Yanzhou. Because of this, there was previously some friction between their troops and Yanzhou's side.\"","\"I also overheard a bit last night. They suspect it was a foster son of Fan Yanzhou, one called Ghost Face, who robbed the goods.\"","Mo Yan Yun scoffed disdainfully, \"Ghost Face? Tch, what an ill-omened name. If that fellow dares to set his crooked schemes on us, I'll wring his head off and use it as a wine cup!\""]},{"number":47,"title":"Chapter 47","paragraphs":["Daili woke the next day, looking at the marks all over her body, feeling as if she had misstepped and accidentally fallen into a vat of paint.","Or perhaps, been chewed on by a dog.","The bed was a complete mess. The brocade quilt had been soaked and then dried, leaving that patch stiff and hard, completely different from the other soft areas.","And such out-of-place spots were everywhere, from the head to the foot of the bed.","Daili's face darkened. That man really did just pull up his pants and leave, not caring at all afterwards.","Well, not entirely uncaring—he had wanted another round this morning. Daili vaguely remembered that in her bleary-eyed state, she had finally lost patience and elbowed him.","She got up and slowly put on her trousers and undergarment. Just as Daili was pondering how to deal with this bed, there was a knock at the door outside.","A light knock, then the door was pushed open.","It was Nianxia and Bipo.","\"Madam, why are you up by yourself?\" Nianxia hurried forward.","Looking at the two maids, Daili froze completely, the tips of her ears quickly flushing red. She belatedly realized that something extremely awkward had happened last night.","This side chamber was connected on one side to an antechamber and a small side room for servants, with a small door on each side. But those small doors were just thin layers, only serving to block the view and doing nothing to block sound.","After all, the original purpose of setting up the small side room was so that the master of the house could summon the servants inside with just a call when getting up at night.","Daili couldn't help but quickly recall last night.","Qin Shaozong had come before she fell asleep, then went to bathe and came back. Had Nianxia and Bipo left the small side room during that time?","It seemed they had not.","If they left here, they had nowhere else to stay.","Daili felt like smoke was about to rise from the top of her head.","She could accept sleeping with Qin Shaozong—they were both adults, no need to be shy or embarrassed about such matters. But as a modern person, Daili completely couldn't, like ancient ladies, treat maids as mere tools, being heard without any reservation, or even watched.","What had Qin Shaozong said last night?","That was far too much. He had been very excited, speaking without restraint, all sorts of lewd talk.","And what had she herself said last night? It seemed she had been forced to respond quite a bit as well.","Daili: \"...\"","\"Madam?\" Nianxia blinked her round eyes, not understanding.","The two pairs of eyes before her were filled with nothing but confusion, without any trace of embarrassment. Daili pinched the bridge of her nose, feeling helpless once again at the differences between past and present. \"Leave the bed for now. Nianxia, please prepare a tub of water for me, I want to bathe. Bipo, could you please go into the commandery town for me and buy some things.\"","Bipo: \"What would you like to buy, Madam?\"","Daili said seriously, \"Go to the pharmacy and buy five doses of contraceptive medicine for me.\"","Daili knew that Ding Lianxi had many medicinal ingredients prepared. If she sent someone to fetch them, she could probably get them. But as long as she still wanted to return to the advisors' circle later, this sort of matter shouldn't go through the other party's hands.","Bipo was slightly taken aback, but then said nothing, only obediently nodded, took the silver, and went to handle it.","The water was quickly heated. Daili sat in the wooden tub, the hot water soaking her skin, soothing her nerves. The tense string in her mind gradually relaxed.","The alliance between the Northern Territories and Qingzhou was already formed. Qin Shaozong wouldn't stay in Guoyun Commandery for too long. Once he set out on campaign again, he would have to abide by the rules he himself had set until the battle was over.","After bathing carefully and coming out, Daili found the bed had already been tidied up by Nianxia.","The brocade quilt had been replaced with a new one, the pillowcase on the brocade pillow had been removed, and her upper garment and skirt, which had been scattered on the floor earlier, were placed in a small bamboo basket. It could be said everything was handled very properly.","Daili: \"...\"","Nianxia's expression was normal. \"Madam, the kitchen has prepared breakfast. Shall I bring it over for you?\"","\"Thank you.\" Daili sighed. What's done is done. Time for breakfast first.","Yanzhou, Gaoling Commandery, Fan Residence.","\"Pingwei, is Quanjie here?\" A pretty young lady dressed in a water-green flying bird patterned silk gown stood at the entrance of the small courtyard, peering inside.","She was not tall, but had a lovely figure, with long eyebrows and phoenix eyes. The slightly upturned outer corners of her eyes gave her a somewhat sharp look. The sunlight fell, refracting a dazzling, opulent glow from the gold hairpins covering her head, making it clear at a glance that this was a young lady raised on gold and jade.","Pingwei in the courtyard stiffened his smile for a moment, then quickly regained his previous cultured demeanor. \"What matter brings Eighth Young Lady to seek Quanjie?\"","Fan Muqi frowned delicately, continuing to peer inside. With this movement, the plump pearl earrings on her ears caught the eye, clearly extraordinary items. \"I just have a matter. Just tell me if Quanjie is here or not.\"","After saying this, she murmured to herself, \"Quanjie probably isn't here. If he were, he would have heard the noise and come out by now. Pingwei, do you know where Quanjie went?\"","Pingwei did not know.","People like them would occasionally receive tasks from their adoptive father. Tasks were completed independently, some even requiring secrecy. Besides, his relationship with Quanjie was already bad—how could they possibly exchange information?","Seeing Fan Muqi get no answer and about to turn and leave, Pingwei grew anxious in his heart and couldn't help blurting out, \"Eighth Young Lady, you are a precious branch of gold, noble and priceless. Why must you lower yourself to such an extent? That fellow Quanjie doesn't know what's good for him. All those things you sent before, he hasn't touched a single one. He just put them all in a corner, acting as if they don't exist.\"","Fan Muqi's face flushed red instantly—the anger of having her warm advances met with cold rejection exposed by an outsider. \"This is between me and Quanjie! It's none of your business!\"","Pingwei was stung by these words, feeling even more wretched.","Not to mention that Eighth Young Lady's father was Fan of Yanzhou, a powerful and influential figure, even Eighth Young Lady's own appearance was something he greatly admired.","How could she, how could she be so blind as to take a liking to Quanjie?","The venomous fire in his heart churned. Pingwei began speaking recklessly. \"Eighth Young Lady, not to mention that Quanjie's status is as low as dirt, unworthy of your deep affection, just the fact that he has another sweetheart outside is enough...\"","\"What did you say?\" Fan Muqi was shocked, her voice rising sharply. \"He has another sweetheart outside? Since when?\"","Pingwei avoided her gaze. \"I haven't seen his sweetheart, but I suspect she must be a young lady in the medical field. Because that day Quanjie came back with medicine, and besides the smell of medicine, I also caught a faint scent of a young lady's perfume on him.\"","Fan Muqi glared fiercely at Pingwei, but couldn't stop her eyes from reddening.","One of her personal maidservants comforted her, \"Pingwei is right, Young Lady. You are noble and priceless. Why must you lower yourself to such an extent? The weather is fine today. How about Young Lady goes for an outing outside the city?\"","Another personal maidservant quickly added, \"Or go find the Li family's young lady and fly kites with her...\"","The words \"fly kites\" had barely left her mouth when her companion tugged her sleeve. The maidservant belatedly realized her slip.","The young lady had previously ordered Quanjie to make a kite for her. Going to fly kites now would only make her think of him upon seeing the object.","Fan Muqi glared at the maid and turned to leave. However, at that moment, a tall figure emerged from around the corner at the other end.","\"Quanjie!\" Fan Muqi's eyes instantly lit up. Originally intending to head east, she immediately changed direction and went west, heading straight for him.","Pingwei nearly ground her silver teeth to dust.","Quanjie's steps halted for a moment before he continued forward.","Fan Muqi arrived at his side, matching his pace as she walked alongside him. \"Quanjie, where did you go just now?\"","Quanjie replied, \"Busy.\"","Fan Muqi chided him with a pout, \"You're such a man of few words. Would saying a few more make you lose a piece of flesh?\"","Quanjie remained silent.","The initial excitement of seeing him faded from Fan Muqi as she remembered another matter. \"Quanjie, do you have a sweetheart outside?\"","Quanjie continued walking forward in silence, not answering the question. His lack of response infuriated Fan Muqi.","The pretty young lady immediately furrowed her brows in anger, grabbing the sleeve of the person beside her. \"You really have a sweetheart? I forbid it! You are a servant of my Fan family. I won't allow you to be with anyone else, do you hear me?!\"","For ease of labor, those of lower status did not wear wide sleeves. Typically, they wore gouyi to tie up their sleeves, with the gouyi reaching to the forearm. The part of the sleeve above the forearm was slightly billowy, and this was precisely where Fan Muqi grabbed.","As soon as she grabbed him, Quanjie froze in place. His arm was bent at the elbow and held out to the side, trying his best to prevent Fan Muqi from touching near his waist or abdomen.","He turned his head to look at this young lady adorned with gold hairpins. \"Quanjie is merely a lowly servant, not worthy of the Eighth Young Lady's concern or effort.\"","\"I want to, and that's none of your business. I'm asking you, do you have a sweetheart outside?\" Fan Muqi, worried he wouldn't speak, lowered her voice. \"If you answer me honestly, I can continue to keep your secret for you.\"","The ghost mask refracted a cold light under the sun, and the eyes behind it held no emotion whatsoever.","Only calmness, a stillness like death.","\"No,\" he said, just the one word.","Fan Muqi was instantly delighted. To Pingwei's astonishment, she laughed and said, \"Good, I believe you. Oh, Quanjie, make me another paper kite, will you? The one you made last time got slightly torn by that clumsy Li San.\"","Quanjie raised his arm, breaking free from her grip on his sleeve, and continued walking forward. \"Eighth Young Lady, send a servant at shenzheng to fetch the kite.\"","\"No, I have time today. I want to watch you make it.\" Fan Muqi followed closely step-by-step.","The attendants serving Fan Muqi closely followed her as they filed into the simple courtyard.","\"Quanjie, why aren't you using the things I gave you?\"","\"The place you live is so shabby, Quanjie. How about I speak to Father and have him arrange a different place for you?\"","\"Unnecessary. This place is fine.\"","...","After working for the better part of an hour, the new paper kite was finished. Holding the kite, Fan Muqi left reluctantly.","Once the group of young ladies departed, the courtyard instantly fell silent. Were it not for the faint scent of powder lingering in the air, this humble little yard seemed as if no young lady had ever visited.","Ignoring Pingwei's venomous glare, Quanjie turned and went back to his room.","Time flowed slowly. The sunset arrived and departed. As the last glimmer of daylight vanished, the earth was enveloped in a heavy darkness.","When the hour of youshi arrived, Quanjie went out again, this time not merely wandering within the estate. He left the Fan residence and, timing it just before the curfew, arrived at a certain hostel in the commandery, where he rented a room.","After night had fully fallen, Quanjie removed the ghost mask from his face and then climbed out over the hostel's inner wall. After curfew, patrols roamed the commandery, and anyone caught still wandering outside would be thrown into jail.","A tall figure nimbly avoided all patrols, heading south until he stopped before a certain residence. Beyond the wall where he stood was a tree. In summer, trees are lush and verdant, with dense branches and leaves, and the tree in this compound was no exception.","The young man listened quietly for a moment. After confirming, he took two steps back, then lunged forward in a sudden dash.","He jumped, his black boot pushing off the wall for momentum while his hand simultaneously grasped the top of the wall. Using the strength of his arms, he pulled himself up and flipped over.","Upon landing, Quanjie immediately and swiftly climbed the tree without pause.","The master of this mansion was surnamed Fang, his public identity a wealthy merchant. Behind the scenes, however, he was a secret agent for the Dong family of Yongzhou.","Relying on a map provided by others, Quanjie successfully located the servants' quarters. A quarter of an hour later, a young servant dressed in Fang residence attire emerged from within.","A few days prior, the Fang couple had quarreled over an outside mistress. The wife, in a fit of anger, had taken their young son and returned to her maiden home. Currently, the only master in the residence was Merchant Fang himself. It was said he had gone drinking with friends today and returned home heavily intoxicated.","At this hour, the master bedroom was still lit, clearly indicating its occupant had not yet retired.","Quanjie paused for a moment, then finally pushed the main bedroom door open a crack.","A strong smell of alcohol instantly wafted out.","The room was utterly silent, without any movement. Remembering the servant carrying a water basin he had avoided on his way here, Quanjie understood the situation. He quickly pushed the door open and entered.","The smell of alcohol was even stronger inside. Turning into the inner chamber, Quanjie saw a corpulent body lying on the bed. Merchant Fang had already been changed into clean inner garments. His shoulder blades and the side of his neck showed damp marks from being wiped, and a teacup had thoughtfully been placed on the small cabinet beside the bed.","If there was any imperfection, it was probably the small puddle of vomit beside the bed.","Merchant Fang had vomited after getting drunk.","The servant who had just left had likely gone to fetch cleaning tools.","Expressionless, Quanjie drew his blade. The gleaming tip of the knife aimed at the other's heart, then plunged down fiercely.","A streak of crimson splashed, \"splattering\" onto the bed curtains. Quanjie casually flicked the blade, about to sheathe it and leave, when he suddenly heard footsteps.","\"When you see your father later, Zhouzhou, you should just... Who are you?!\"","Quanjie's wandering thoughts snapped back instantly, but it was already too late.","The woman had seen the blood-stained, still-unsheathed knife in Quanjie's hand, and she had also seen the large pool of blood flowing from the bed behind him.","The woman at the arched doorway instantly went weak in the legs, nearly collapsing to the ground. She stared fixedly at the figure not far away, one hand constantly pushing her young son, who hadn't yet entered the doorway. \"Zhouzhou, run! Don't worry about Mother, run!!\"","The woman had already prepared herself for death. Having stumbled upon a murder scene, with the perpetrator's blade still stained with blood, another swift raise and fall of the knife would be an easy matter, wouldn't it?","Yet, strangely, she saw that face, uneven as if covered in hypertrophic scars, reveal an expression of utmost sorrow.","The woman focused her gaze to look again, only to see the other had already lowered his head, sheathed his knife, and leaped out through a window on the other side.","\"Mother, what's wrong?\"","...","The hostel.","A figure stepped on the moonlight, deftly scaling the outer wall to get inside. Upon returning to his room, however, Quanjie did not change clothes or prepare for bed. He stood by the window, tilting his head up to gaze quietly at the full moon in the sky.","Only when a dark cloud drifted over, obscuring the full moon from view, did Quanjie turn and go back inside. His eyes, along with his face, were submerged in the darkness, and everything returned to stillness.","Whether rivers ran dry or the seas turned to dust, nothing could stop the sun from rising again in the east the next day.","Quanjie had just returned to the Fan residence when a guard summoned him to the study.","\"What of that man named Fang?\" Fan Tianshi asked, sitting by the window at a small table as he brewed tea.","Quanjie: \"I have dealt with the matter thoroughly, Father.\"","Fan Tianshi smiled. \"I have full confidence in your work. Sit.\"","Quanjie walked over and sat down opposite him.","Fan Tianshi personally poured tea for him. \"Qin Shaozong has arrived in Guoyun County at Nangong Xiong's invitation. This man is no pushover. We cannot allow an alliance between Qin and Nangong. Quanjie, there are some things you can handle cleanly the first time, and surely you can do it a second time. Am I right?\"","The room fell silent, save for the gurgling of boiling water.","\"Father suspects I killed Captain Lu?\" Quanjie spoke, his hoarse voice betraying little emotion.","Captain Lu was the military officer who had died in the army camp not long after the alliance between Yanzhou and Qingzhou was formed. Afterwards, the Yanzhou side claimed Qingzhou was responsible for the killing. Qingzhou denied it, causing a stalemate that rapidly deteriorated relations between the two provinces.","Fan Tianshi stared fixedly at the man before him, trying to find some trace of evidence through those calm, dark eyes.","But there was none. Those eyes were too still, gazing into them felt like looking into a lifeless void.","Quanjie continued, \"You gave no such order, and killing Captain Lu held no benefit for me. I beg Father to investigate clearly.\"","Fan Tianshi looked away, the disgust in his heart growing stronger. Simultaneously, the seed planted by his son during their conversation in the study that night swiftly took root and sprouted. He instead put on a kindly smile. \"Someone came to me with an accusation, claiming Captain Lu's death was connected to you. However, your father knows your loyal character. I did not believe a single word of those baseless claims.\"","Quanjie: \"Thank you for your trust, Father.\"","\"But...\" Fan Tianshi's tone shifted, \"the method of framing and shifting blame is indeed ingenious, perfectly suited for sabotaging an alliance between two parties. Quanjie, your martial skills are exceptional. I will assign some men to accompany you. This mission requires you to eliminate a high-ranking officer in Qin Shaozong's army and frame Qingzhou for it. You must ensure the alliance between the Northern Territories and Qingzhou is broken.\"","Quanjie rose from his seat and bowed with clasped hands. \"Quanjie accepts the command.\"","Fan Tianshi revealed a smile. \"This matter is of great importance. If the mission fails, you must on no account reveal any connection to Yanzhou. Simply claim you are from Qingzhou. In that case, even if Qin Shaozong wants you dead, Nangong Xiong, in order to prove his own innocence, absolutely cannot allow you to be executed. You can then seize an opportunity to escape. Do you understand what your father is saying?\"","Quanjie nodded. \"Quanjie understands.\"","\"Quick to grasp the point, you truly are clever. Very good, your father did not misjudge you.\" Fan Tianshi lowered his gaze to refill his own teacup, hiding the ruthlessness in his eyes.","If it succeeded, causing the alliance between the Northern Territories and Qingzhou to break, that would be excellent. If it failed...","His son's words also held some truth. This blade had been used for too long, long enough to gather filth. If this matter failed, then it would be the perfect opportunity to discard it."]},{"number":48,"title":"Chapter 48","paragraphs":["Guoyun County.","Daili stared at the small booklet spread open before her, but her thoughts drifted far away.","On the morning after that night, Qin Shaozong and a group of military officers went to the barracks outside the city and stayed there for the next two consecutive days without returning.","She slept alone at night, with no one disturbing her early in the morning. But Daili knew this was only temporary. A one-year deadline had been set; he couldn't possibly be satisfied with just that one time.","Drinking contraceptive medicine would only make her suffer. Rather than suffering herself, it was better to make Qin Shaozong suffer—she needed to get some condoms made.","Condoms already existed during the Tang dynasty. Back then, they were generally made from cleaned and dried fish bladders, softened in warm water before use—hence the later term \"sneaking some fish\" for infidelity.","Besides fish bladders, highly elastic sheep intestines and pig bladders could also be used. However, considering which was easiest to process, fish bladders were still the first choice.","Daili had made up her mind. \"Nianxia, Bipo, come with me. We're going out.\"","The two maidservants didn't know her purpose, but they still quickly prepared to leave the residence. However...","At the side gate of the residence, Daili was stopped.","\"Madam Dai, you wish to go out to the market?\" The guard looked somewhat nervous.","Daili, wearing a veiled hat, nodded. \"Yes, I should be back in about an hour.\"","The guard thought for a moment. \"Please wait a moment, I'll make arrangements.\"","Daili didn't ask what arrangements he meant, standing inside the side gate as she watched him hurry off. Not long after, Qiao Wangfei led several soldiers over in haste.","A bone injury takes a hundred days to heal. It had been nearly three months since Qiao Wangfei's serious injury, and he was now in the final stage of recovery. To avoid leaving any hidden ailments, Ding Lianxi had repeatedly warned him not to overexert himself, which Qin Shaozong also agreed with.","So, while the other officers had been busy at the barracks these past few days, Qiao Wangfei became the one left behind to mind the house.","As for why he wasn't left in Ying County, it was entirely because he was the head of the Eastern Garrison of the Xuanxiao Cavalry. If the Eastern Garrison lacked its leader, it would be inconvenient for them in upcoming battles. Qin Shaozong simply brought him along on the journey to recuperate.","Qiao Wangfei said respectfully, \"Madam Dai, I will accompany you out of the residence.\"","Daili didn't mind. \"My apologies for the trouble.\"","\"No trouble at all,\" Qiao Wangfei hurriedly replied. \"I've been cooped up in the residence for days as well; it'll be good to take a walk outside.\"","Guoyun County bore the title \"County,\" so its scale was naturally not small. Its several markets were clearly distinguished by what they sold, orderly and well-organized.","Daili headed straight for her target: the fish market. Under Qiao Wangfei's puzzled gaze, she bought many fish and specifically asked the fishmonger if he sold fish bladders separately.","Unfortunately, he did not.","In this era, common folk couldn't bear to waste the slightest bit, let alone fish bladders, which could be made into zhuyi, a particularly appetizing delicacy.","\"Then I'll take both these baskets,\" Daili said, buying an extra basket of fish. There was no fear of having too much food. Those military officers in the residence were all gluttons; throwing these few baskets of fish into their stomachs probably wouldn't even make a sound.","The fishmonger beamed with joy.","\"Madam Dai, is there something special about these fish bladders?\" Qiao Wangfei couldn't help but ask.","He was someone Daili had personally saved. Later, he had also been involved in the refined salt matter, and now he revered her like a deity. Seeing her particular interest in fish bladders, he couldn't help but start to imagine.","It was probably similar to the Midas touch—wherever Madam Dai pointed, it could turn to gold. Most likely, these fish bladders, after processing, could also fetch a good price!","Daili: \"...\"","There was something special about them, but they couldn't be sold, nor was it appropriate to publicize their use everywhere.","Daili decided to change the subject, casually saying, \"There are quite a few baskets of fish here. Perhaps we should find someone to send them back first.\"","To her surprise, upon hearing this, Qiao Wangfei's expression changed dramatically, and he spoke almost pleadingly, \"Madam Dai, the Marquis truly treats you exceptionally well. Back after taking Ying County, all the finest women's ornaments from Li Zan's treasury were sent to your rooms. And when you fell ill previously, Master Ding said you needed quiet rest to restore your vitality. The Marquis held back the army from marching, only setting out south after you recovered...\"","Daili was taken aback, then suddenly understood. It turned out that her method of sending fish to distract the guards back in Nankang County had now made Qiao Wangfei a nervous wreck.","\"I haven't found my son yet; I have no plans to do anything else,\" Daili said helplessly.","The tense string loosened. Qiao Wangfei let out a sigh of relief. \"It's good that you have no other ideas.\"","Mention of her son reminded Daili of another matter. Guoyun County was sizable. Given Qin Shaozong's promotion of refined salt and the profit-seeking nature of merchants, it was very likely someone here was selling salt stones.","She immediately asked the fishmonger.","The fishmonger actually knew. \"...You're asking about the salt stone merchant? Yes, there is a merchant in the county selling salt stones. His surname is Gao. I heard he returned from the north a few days ago, bringing many expensive salt stones specifically for large eateries and the county's nobility. Madam, if you want to buy salt stones, remember to bring plenty of silver. He really doesn't sell them cheaply.\"","After thanking the fishmonger, Daili followed the direction he indicated.","Merchant Gao's shop wasn't hard to find.","He had previously been a traveling merchant in the sauce business, with his own shop. The signboard \"Gao's Sauces\" hung high, but he found that insufficient. He had made a \"Salt Stones\" flag himself and planted it high up, letting it flutter in the wind.","\"Welcome! What would you like to buy?\" Merchant Gao's shrewd eyes swept over Daili's clothing, and his smile immediately widened by eight degrees. \"Esteemed guest, I have salt stones procured from the north. They are white, fine, and even purer than salt. I heard from those foreign merchants that regularly consuming more salt stones helps expel troublesome and stagnant impurities from the body, thereby achieving the effect of prolonging life.\"","\"Many nobles in the county are fond of them. Noble guest, would you like to buy some?\" Merchant Gao rubbed his hands together.","Daili was astounded.","Prolonging life? Selling something that isn't a health supplement as if it were one—if this were modern times, a consumer complaint for false advertising would be filed immediately.","However, Daili's purpose here wasn't the salt stones. She looked around the shop. \"I heard that people in the north are looking for a child named 'Qin Yanzhou,' and have entrusted many traveling merchants to inquire. Do you know about this?\"","Merchant Gao hesitated, then nodded. \"I know about it. To be frank, when I first returned from the north, I visited the county's human market and asked several brokers, but none of them knew of that child. Later, I realized that reward money was like a flower in a mirror, the moon in the water—not something I could obtain.\"","He had gone to the brokers, completely hooked by the reward offered from the north.","However, after asking several brokers and finding none who knew, the merchant's agile mind made him realize—","This matter was extremely difficult.","The north only said to find a child, giving a name, approximate age, and general appearance. Nothing else was said. His status, whether alive or dead, his whereabouts—all unknown. This was no different from finding a needle in a haystack. How could one search?","It simply couldn't be found!","Rather than wasting time on that illusory reward, it would be better to put in more effort selling saltpeter. The latter brings solid silver coins into one's pocket.","Daili observed Merchant Gao's demeanor and understood his unspoken words, falling into silence. When she first followed Qin Shaozong south, she had worried things might develop in this direction.","And now it had indeed come to pass.","Profit-driven merchants were gradually losing interest in the moon-in-the-water reward.","\"Noble lady, why do you mention this?\" Merchant Gao asked, puzzled. His gaze shifted backward, landing on Qiao Wangfei.","One look was enough to startle him—this man actually had a sword at his waist! Looking further outside, the several men guarding in front of his shop were all tall and burly, not looking like ordinary retainers of a wealthy family at all!","Could she be a female relative of Prefect Feng's household? Or from the Zhang family...","Wait, I've heard Governor Nangong has been settled in the commandery for some time. Could she be one of Governor Nangong's people?","Just as he was secretly speculating, he heard the young lady before him speak.","\"How about I give you an idea? Write a notice, paste it outside your door with glue, just omitting the specific detail about the birthmark. Then sit back and wait for the brokers to bring children to your door. If there really is a match, you'll exert the least effort for the greatest share of the reward. What do you think?\"","\"Excellent, excellent, you speak wisely,\" Merchant Gao nodded repeatedly.","Not only did this noble guest's words make sense and seem to consider his interests at every turn, but given her elusive and prestigious status, even if she were talking nonsense, he would have to nod along right now.","To show he wasn't just being perfunctory, Merchant Gao immediately fetched a large sheet of mulberry bark paper, swiftly wrote a missing person notice, and with a \"smack,\" pasted it outside his shop.","Daili didn't let him work for nothing. Later, she made a point of buying some seasonings from his store.","Having obtained what she needed to buy and with matters weighing on her mind, Daili didn't linger outside. She returned to the residence with Qiao Wangfei.","As luck would have it, upon her return, she ran into Qin Shaozong at the gate, who had been staying at the military camp outside the city for two consecutive days.","\"Where has my lady been?\"","The burly man sat astride a tall horse, blocking a large swath of sunlight before Daili. The golden taotie-patterned helmet cast a shadow on his face as he lowered his head.","His brown eyes were hidden within the shadow, making them hard to see clearly, yet one could vaguely sense a smoldering heat deep within.","Daili averted her gaze and simultaneously took a step to the side, putting distance between herself and the overly perceptive chestnut horse. \"I went to the market to buy a few baskets of fish. Tonight, I'll have the kitchen prepare a full fish banquet for you all.\"","Qin Shaozong dismounted. \"My lady craves fish? You don't care much for heavy meats, always preferring these river delicacies that don't have much substance.\"","Daili couldn't help muttering softly, \"How is there no substance? It's just that your own appetite is large.\"","The seasonings of this era were far inferior to later times. There were no chili peppers, let alone white sugar or industrial flavorings. Steamed fish was convenient—simply add a couple of ginger slices to remove the fishy smell, and you'd have a dish of fresh fish.","Qin Shaozong said meaningfully, \"Alright, it's true my appetite is large. My lady knows that well from experience.\"","Daili: \"...\"","He'd better be talking about the same thing.","Ignoring him, Daili had the guards deliver the baskets of fish to the kitchen, then instructed the army cooks to separately save the fish bladders in a small basin.","Wash, cut, sort, and finally lay them out on winnowing baskets to dry.","After all this busywork, it was mealtime—time for the evening meal.","Tonight's full fish banquet was set with individual low tables in the main hall. Daili mingled among the military officers, eating while listening to their casual conversation.","\"Once Old Mo returns with the topographic maps of the area around Huai'an Commandery, we'll be almost ready to move.\"","\"Ah, if the terrain around Huai'an Commandery weren't so complex, we wouldn't need to go through all this trouble. The waiting is truly grating.\"","I've heard the Green Lotus Sect is just a ragtag bunch, not many regular soldiers. It should be an easy fight. I plan to earn the honor of being the first on the walls.","\"Mr. Nalan says it might rain in the coming days. Let's hope it doesn't rain on the day of the big battle, or it would be troublesome.\"","Indeed. Since it's not a surprise attack, we don't need to muffle the sound of hooves. Heavy rain greatly reduces the range and accuracy of arrows, and scaling the siege ladders would also be difficult.","\"Wait until after the rain then?\"","\"We'll see how the Marquis decides when the time comes.\"","...","While eating fish, Daili silently calculated the time in her mind.","They had arrived in Guoyun Commandery the day before yesterday. Commander Mo was sent out that same day, so he had been gone for three days now. She didn't know exactly where the Huai'an Commandery they mentioned was located, nor how far it was from Guoyun Commandery.","It probably wasn't too far. Too great a distance would exhaust both men and horses. Calculating this way, Commander Mo should be able to return soon...","Hopefully, he'd arrive before bedtime tonight. If so, Qin Shaozong would surely have to go to the study.","After the meal, Daili left the main hall and strolled around the residence to aid digestion. Night had fallen. Only a handful of places in the residence were lit; the vast majority of courtyards and buildings were shrouded in darkness.","There was neither moon nor stars tonight. The sky was dark and heavy, as if it might come crashing down at any moment.","\"Whoosh—\"","The wind picked up.","The lantern in Nianxia's hand swayed violently from side to side, the light inside flickering wildly.","\"My lady, it seems like it's going to rain. Perhaps we should head back,\" Nianxia whispered softly.","As if agreeing with her words, a dull rumble of thunder suddenly rolled across the sky, booming loudly.","\"My lady, let's return. Summer rains, once they start, can be torrential. Coupled with the wind, you might catch a chill,\" Bipo also urged.","Daili looked up at the sky. For now, there was only the sound of thunder, no lightning dragons yet wreaking havoc within the clouds.","For some reason, even though the sky was as dark as yesterday—so dark the storm clouds were invisible—she felt an inexplicable heaviness in her heart.","She had a feeling something would happen tonight...","\"Let's go back.\"","Back in the main chamber, Daili spread open her little mulberry bark paper booklet and began writing down improvement items.","Merely entrusting messages to merchant caravans wasn't enough. They needed to post notices, preferably on shop doors or conspicuous shelves.","The purchased cloth garments would spread the word from ten to a hundred...","\"What is my lady writing again?\" A deep male voice sounded close to her ear.","Daili was greatly startled, her whole body jolting violently.","A large, tanned hand first landed on her shoulder, then slid down, gently patting her back as if smoothing ruffled feathers. Qin Shaozong laughed, \"Before, you were capable of anything, full of audacity from head to toe. Why so timid today?\"","This man scared her and then had the nerve to blame her. Daili was impressed. \"It's clearly because you walk without a sound.\"","\"How could there be no sound? Those two maidservants just now paid their respects.\" Qin Shaozong's long arm suddenly tightened around her waist, and with Daili's gasp of surprise, he lifted her from the chair.","\"Clatter.\" A small charcoal pencil fell to the ground, rolling away alone and forlorn.","In the blink of an eye, Daili found herself sitting on his lap instead of the soft chair. He ran extremely hot, his body as warm as a stove. On that chilly spring night, he could wear nothing but a thin robe. Now, before the heavy rain, the summer night was stiflingly stuffy. Trapped in his embrace, Daili felt as if she was caught in a searing net.","\"I'm hot,\" Daili tried to get up.","The long arm that had wrapped around her waist tightened slightly. At the same time, his large hand with distinct knuckles spread out and grasped her waist. He knew that this part of her body was particularly sensitive. As long as he held it, she would lose most of her strength immediately.","Sure enough, the woman in his arms went limp right away.","Qin Shaozong looked at the tips of her ears tinged with a blush and couldn't help letting out a soft laugh. He rubbed the side of her fair neck with his nose, and his thin lips landed on her beautiful collarbone from time to time. \"My lady, Mo Yanyun will be back soon.\"","Daili naturally understood what he meant.","Mo Yanyun's return meant that everything was ready and they would enter the war zone immediately.","During the war, women were forbidden in the military camp.","The two of them were pressed closely against each other, and his physical reaction was obvious. Enveloped by the net of heat, Daili also became a bit restless.","She tried to pry the big hand off her waist, but those long fingers were as if made of iron, still tightly holding on to her. As if displeased with her actions, the thumb rubbing on her waist pressed a little harder.","The tingling sensation that rose from the base of her spine became even stronger. Daili couldn't help trembling slightly, and even the end of her voice quivered. \"Did you drink at the dinner?\"","\"Just a little,\" Qin Shaozong replied. Before the war, how could there be no wine at a group dinner?","As if thinking of something, he asked, \"Are you dizzy again?\"","He remembered that she said a few days ago that the smell of alcohol made her dizzy.","Daili nodded immediately, and the speed of her nodding was unusually fast, so fast that Qin Shaozong squinted his eyes slightly. He said in an unclear tone, \"Is my lady really dizzy or just pretending?\"","The oppression around him was already strong, and it became even more intense when he deliberately let it out. That sharp gaze seemed to cut her open and see what was hidden inside.","Daili couldn't stand it and kept turning her head to the side.","The next moment, a rough big hand half - wrapped around her chin and turned her back.","Those brown eyes were right in front of her, as bright as a mirror.","\"Do you dislike me?\" These two words seemed to be forced out between his teeth.","Daili really wanted to lie and say no, but she couldn't get past her conscience. If she tried to talk about something else, his gaze was too sharp, and he would probably see through her.","Since neither of these methods worked, Daili could only keep silent and blinked her eyes at him gently.","Qin Shaozong was both amused and angry. Gritting his teeth, he said, \"The bathtub in the main room is very spacious. It's very lonely to bathe alone. How about my lady accompany me?\"","Although he was asking how, he directly picked her up forcefully.","\"I've already taken a bath!\"","\"The night is long and we have plenty of time. Please trouble my lady to take another bath.\"","*","It was already late at night, and the curfew had been imposed in Guoyun County.","In a wing - room on the first floor of a post - house in the county, there was still a faint candlelight flickering. If the young servant of the post - house were inside at this time, he would surely be greatly surprised. The guests who had checked in as merchants had now changed into black night - clothes.","Black clothes and trousers, with a handkerchief covering their faces, they looked like they were going to do some shady things.","The young man blew out the candle, pushed open the window, and nimbly climbed out.","The same scene happened simultaneously in different post - houses in the county. Seen from above, some black dots left the post - houses and rushed towards the same place, meeting there.","There was no moon tonight. The residents on both sides of the street had gone to sleep early. The darkness was like a snake waking up from hibernation, opening its huge mouth to devour all the light.","The footsteps of the patrol team were drowned out by the thunder, making it difficult to tell their exact location. However, this group of people in black could always accurately avoid them.","They walked and stopped, occasionally turning into alleys. Sometimes they dispersed and acted individually, standing close to the fronts of shops to avoid the patrollers passing by the alley entrances.","At this time, Quanjie was also leaning against the front of a shop. The shop had a plaque that read \"Gao's Sauce\", and there was a flag fluttering in the night wind on top, with the words \"Xianshi\" written on it.","The group of people they needed to be wary of gradually moved away in the distance.","Quanjie took a step forward. During this process, he heard some faint noises, as if it was the friction between clothes and paper.","The sound came from behind him.","The young man couldn't help turning sideways and looking back. Vaguely, he could see a piece of mulberry paper pasted on the shop door, which looked like a notice."]},{"number":49,"title":"Chapter 49","paragraphs":["The night was pitch black, shrouded in an impenetrable darkness where one could not see their own hand. At this moment, not only were the characters on the notice illegible, but even the larger characters on the plaques, compared to the mulberry-bark paper, were impossible to make out.","A cold gaze swept over the scene, remaining as unruffled as ever. Quanjie led his men forward once more.","Both the patrol routes and the layout of the target residence were well within Quanjie's grasp. The former could be ascertained by sending men to scout at night; as for the latter, a single visit to the property agent was sufficient.","Those two grand mansions had once been listed for sale. Even if the agent had no diagrams on hand, sketching a layout based on his verbal description was not a difficult task.","Roughly the time it takes to drink two cups of tea later, Quanjie arrived before the great mansion. Just as before, he chose a section of the outer wall near a tree, first scaling the wall to enter the estate, then nimbly climbing the tree.","He listened intently for a moment, hearing no footsteps around, yet Quanjie was in no hurry to call the others in. Like a leopard lurking in the forest, he lay perfectly still, waiting only for the most opportune moment.","One quarter of an hour passed, then two...","He didn't know how long it had been, until he had seen two teams of night watchmen pass by and move into the distance. After cautiously waiting another quarter of an hour, Quanjie finally let out a bird-call whistle.","The men outside the wall moved in unison upon hearing the signal.","...","Bai Jianping, as the Southern Tun Commander of the Xuanxiao Cavalry, naturally possessed other exceptional qualities besides his superb martial skills and talent for command.","Perhaps due to having lived deep in the mountains since childhood, he was particularly sensitive to the sounds of various animals and could roughly discern the emotions within the calls of birds and beasts.","This was Bai Jianping's own claim. Mo Yanyun and the others were all half-convinced, half-doubting, sometimes even mocking him for being a lucky blind cat stumbling upon a dead mouse. Of course, this didn't hinder his near-flawless record.","Bai Jianping had an exceptional alcohol tolerance, able to drink a thousand cups without falling over. This man didn't get drunk, but after drinking too much, he would eventually fall asleep and then wake up needing to relieve himself.","Scratching his head, he climbed out of bed, muttering complaints about how having a high alcohol tolerance could sometimes be a nuisance. As he stepped down, however, because no lamp was lit in the room, he accidentally kicked the low cabinet beside the bed.","The kick sent a sharp pain shooting through his toes.","Bai Jianping jolted awake, his drowsiness instantly scattering by nine-tenths. Before he could even clutch his throbbing toes, he suddenly heard a bird-call whistle.","Bai Jianping froze, turning his head to look out the window.","He hadn't closed the window before sleeping, and now the night wind was rushing in with a whoosh, occasionally accompanied by the rumble of distant thunder.","Rain was coming.","Birds return to their nests to shelter before rain, but he had wandered around this mansion earlier; it was tidied up everywhere, with no bird nests under the eaves or on the windowsills.","Let alone that bird-call whistle just now...","Bai Jianping frowned, immediately grabbing the sword by his pillow and walking out, weapon in hand.","The mansion was large, with many rooms. Bai Jianping, used to living alone, had taken a room for himself upon entering the estate. The outer chamber should have been empty at this hour, yet as soon as he reached the turn leading from the inner chamber outward, he unexpectedly ran into several dark figures.","Caught completely off guard, both sides were startled.","\"Who are you? Guards! Assassins!\" Bai Jianping bellowed. His voice was as loud as a great bell, exploding through the silence and carrying far.","The leader of the group said nothing, simply raising his sword and charging forward.","Seeing this, the several black-clad figures around him, with the young man at their core, flanked Bai Jianping from both sides in a pincer movement, attacking simultaneously.","In the darkness, sharp blades stirred fierce gusts, each move revealing deadly intent.","Alarm bells rang loudly in his mind. Not daring to split his focus, Bai Jianping stopped shouting and concentrated fully on dealing with the onslaught before him.","\"Clang, clang—\"","In the dark, the sound of metal clashing sent chills down one's spine.","Outnumbered in the blackness and facing opponents who cooperated with extraordinary tacit understanding and were better adapted to the darkness than he was—having only just risen from bed—Bai Jianping was at a significant disadvantage.","As a sharp pain shot through his arm repeatedly, and he distinctly felt a sticky, wet liquid trickling down his forearm, Bai Jianping cursed under his breath.","The situation was dire. If this continued, he'd be dead long before reinforcements arrived.","No good, he needed a different tactic.","The darkness enveloped everyone like a tide. As the fight pushed further into the room, and with Bai Jianping constantly dodging by sound, even trying to blend in among his attackers, the battle gradually became confused, friend and foe indistinguishable, reaching a stalemate.","Right at that moment—","\"Fzzt.\"","A flame suddenly appeared. The leader of the group had lit a candle in the room.","This flicker of light was not strong, but it was enough for the men in the room to discern their surroundings. Bai Jianping, having risen in the middle of the night, wore no outer robe, only a set of white undergarments, which stood in stark contrast to their uniform black.","The black-clad men's spirits soared, and they advanced in unison once more.","Looking at his two bloody arms, Bai Jianping sucked in a sharp breath. Without the slightest hesitation, he fought while retreating, backing up from the inner chamber doorway all the way to the bedside. Beside the bed was a low table with an open bottom shelf. Using his sword to block a blade from the side, he swiftly hooked the table with his long leg and then swept it forcefully towards his opponents.","They immediately raised their blades to hack it apart.","The long table instantly shattered into several pieces, scattering to the floor like fallen petals.","Seizing this brief opening, Bai Jianping quickly dashed to a nearby small window, braced his hands on the sill, and with a leap, flipped out through the window.","Bai Jianping ran barefoot, his hair disheveled.","Just as he was about to shout another warning, he suddenly saw a crowd of people surging through the courtyard gate. Bai Jianping let out a long sigh of relief, not forgetting to grumble, \"You lot, whose brains are addled by wine, finally show up. Any later and you might as well not bother rescuing me, just collect my corpse.\"","Feng Feng laughed instantly. \"Don't worry, the wicked live a thousand years. You won't die.\"","Seeing them about to charge into the room, Bai Jianping shouted a reminder, \"There are at least six of them. They work together seamlessly, and their skills are all exceptional. Be careful.\"","\"Got it. No need to show off here.\"","Bai Jianping's mouth twitched.","Inside the room.","The moment Bai Jianping flipped out the window, Quanjie knew the mission had failed.","As for why the target was awake and armed in the middle of the night after heavy drinking, why he had his sword at hand despite being in undergarments, why the initial assault hadn't succeeded...","None of that mattered anymore. The priority now was to retreat from this place.","\"Where do you think you're going!\"","Feng Feng and Kuang Ye rushed in just in time to see them fleeing through a window on the other side. A fierce glint flashed in Feng Feng's eyes. He immediately drew a short dagger from his waist and hurled it.","The white blade traced a streak of light through the air, plunging into the back shoulder of a black-clad figure not far away.","The man jolted in pain, his movements faltering. As he slowed, Kuang Ye's long sword instantly caught up. Amid a spray of blood, a round head was completely severed, sent flying.","A headless corpse thudded to the floor.","Two black-clad intruders remained in the room, not yet having escaped through the window. One had just reached the window and was about to leap out when a small stool flew from behind, its aim remarkably true, striking the man squarely on the head.","With a loud \"thud,\" the man was smashed dizzy.","Feng Feng darted forward from the side in a swift stride, blocking the window.","Inside the room, it was now several against two, with one of the black-clad men injured. Before long, one was cut down by Kuang Ye's blade, and the other was captured alive.","\"Chief Feng, six were killed outside, two escaped,\" a guard reported from beyond.","Feng Feng's brow twitched. \"Escaped? Two got away? Did you give chase? They must be caught!\"","\"We did,\" the guard's voice lowered a notch. \"But it started raining... they'll likely get away...\"","Boom—","With a clap of thunder, the initial light drizzle rapidly intensified, transforming into a torrential downpour in an instant.","The heavy rain could wash away and conceal many things—tracks, and even the sound of footsteps.","Feng Feng frowned in irritation. \"It's over. When the Lord learns of this, we're in for a reprimand.\" To have the manor infiltrated in the dead of night, resulting in Bai Jianping's injury and two escaping... it was a disaster.","Kuang Ye asked, \"Were the two who fled injured?\"","\"During the fight, they moved positions too quickly. With the rain washing the blood from the blades, we can only confirm at least one was injured. But...\" The guard hesitated for a moment. \"Both were highly skilled. Even if injured, it wouldn't have been a critical wound.\"","\"Truly finished. Not only did they escape, but the ones who got away are still in fighting shape.\" Feng Feng looked despondently at Kuang Ye beside him. \"They won't be foolish enough to stay together in Yun County after this; they'll be scattered. Finding them won't be easy. How do we report this to the Lord?\"","Kuang Ye immediately averted his gaze, delivering a swift kick that sent a bound man—trussed up like a zongzi—sprawling. \"Where is your hideout?!\"","The man remained silent.","\"Hey, don't kick him to death. The priority now is reporting... Ah, I see! Kuang Ye, you're doing this on purpose, aren't you? Deliberately changing the subject at a time like this! Fine, you can be the one to explain this to the Lord.\"","Main courtyard, side chamber.","The side chamber was shrouded in darkness. From a distance, it seemed the occupants had settled into peaceful slumber, but drawing closer, one could hear faint movements from within.","The two plain bed curtains inside were drawn tightly shut without a single gap. Wind seeped through the slightly ajar window, occasionally causing the curtains to ripple like waves.","Yet no matter how the wind blew, it could not part them enough to peer through.","Until...","A slender, pale leg slipped out from between the curtains. Once the knee cleared the edge of the bed, the calf, marked with faint rosy traces, bent naturally, the toes lightly tapping the footboard in a gentle rhythm.","Through the small gap opened by the leg, one could glimpse swathes of dark and white within.","The dark figure above was astride the snowy expanse below. With the slight shuddering of the bed, heavy breaths mingled with soft, muffled whimpers.","The pinkish-white toes curled slightly against the footboard. Just as a heel began to rub against the wooden surface, a large, rough hand with prominent knuckles reached out from within the curtains, firmly grasping that slender calf.","A bit of soft, pale flesh bulged between his fingers. The thumb of that large hand stroked it once before pulling the leg back inside.","Suddenly, noises came from outside, as if someone was calling out loudly.","Qin Yanzhou's movements paused briefly, then he buried his head down again as if nothing had happened.","Dai Li hadn't heard the first call, only the thunderclap and the relentless patter of rain. Perhaps it was her imagination, but she thought she heard another sound mixed with the rain... like someone calling \"My Lord\" from the adjacent room.","\"I think someone's talking outside,\" Dai Li murmured. Her voice was soft, carrying a subtle, languid huskiness, like peony leaves wrinkled by dew.","\"My Lord!\" The call came again from next door, accompanied by knocking.","Dai Li jolted, instantly snapping out of her daze.","Qin Yanzhou lifted his head from between her plump, lush thighs, the tendons in his neck bulging then subsiding. \"My lady, relax.\"","She ignored him, her gaze fixed nervously on the world beyond the curtains.","Qin Yanzhou reached out, pinched her delicate chin, and turned her face back towards him, sealing her red lips with a kiss while simultaneously intensifying his pace.","...","\"My Lord.\"","Kuang Ye stood under the eaves of the main house, raising his hand to knock once more. The pouring rain muffled all other sounds, preventing him from hearing any movement inside.","Strange, Kuang Ye thought to himself.","The Lord was not one to sleep so soundly that not even a flood could wake him. He had knocked three times and called out several times, yet there was no response.","Could it be the Lord wasn't in his room?","Just as this thought surfaced, he heard the faint creak of a door opening from the side.","Kuang Ye's first assumption was that he had inadvertently disturbed Lady Dai. He turned, ready to apologize, but instead saw a tall, imposing figure emerge from the side chamber.","It was precisely the man he sought.","Kuang Ye blinked his honest, dog-like eyes, all emotion perfectly concealed, presenting the picture of an oblivious, straightforward man.","\"My Lord, there were assassins in the manor...\"","Within Yun County City.","After shaking off their pursuers, Quanjie and his sole remaining companion did not immediately return to the inn. They stood under an eave, sheltering from the rain.","\"The mission failed. How do we explain this to our Patron?\" one asked.","Quanjie replied impassively, \"We report the truth.\"","The other man gave a cold laugh. \"Fine, you report it then. You're the Patron's adopted son, after all. Others face 'success or death,' but you get special leniency. You're the most suitable to deliver the news.\"","Quanjie's tone remained flat. \"You asked me to stay just to say this?\"","\"Is that not allowed?\" the man retorted.","Without another word, Quanjie stepped directly into the rain, his figure soon vanishing from sight.","The man left behind ground his teeth, muttering, \"What's there to be so arrogant about? Do you really think the Patron sees you as a son?\"","Quanjie returned to the inn silently. He removed his wet clothes, changed back into his daytime attire, and mechanically lay down on the bed, closing his eyes to rest.","...","The next day, the sky cleared after the rain.","The inn courtyard housed two trees. The heavy rain overnight had littered the ground with fallen leaves.","Besides the leaves, the wind had blown in various bits of debris: someone's lost trousers and undergarments, wildflower petals, and... a sheet of mulberry-bark paper that had landed on the veranda.","A young servant tidied the courtyard, muttering to himself, \"Last night's rain was immense, you'd think the sky had cracked. Now there's plenty to do. Hope I can get it all cleaned up in half an hour. Whose trousers blew in here? Tsk, and they have four big holes—how long have they been worn?\"","He chattered on as he worked, sweeping all the leaves into a bamboo basket and sorting the ragged cloth separately. Broom in hand, he finally turned, ready to finish up.","\"Huh? What's this still here?\" The servant noticed the mulberry-bark paper not far away.","Unlike the clothes fully exposed in the yard, half of this paper lay on the covered veranda, half outside.","The exposed portion was thoroughly soaked, the ink on it blurred and runny. The part sheltered by the veranda had also been dampened by blown rain, but had since dried in the wind.","Just a scrap of paper, the servant thought, about to sweep it away. But a casual glance made him pause with a soft sound of surprise.","The young servant came from a poor family and had no chance to attend school. The characters he knew were all self-taught in his spare time, and he hadn't learned many—just a scattered few.","The characters for \"reward\" and \"money\" happened to be among them.","\"Reward money? There's reward money to be had?\" The servant's eyes lit up, but looking further down, he couldn't understand the rest of the content.","The servant immediately grew anxious and hurriedly picked up the mulberry bark paper, only...","The mulberry bark paper, having been soaked in water, lay in the courtyard in two separate pieces, immobile. Only the half that had taken shelter under the eaves ended up in the servant's hands.","\"Oh dear, how did it tear?\" the servant lamented. However, after glancing at the half on the ground where the writing was now illegible, his regret faded. \"Never mind, you can't make out the words on that piece anyway.\"","He took the half-sheet of mulberry bark paper back to the main hall and called for the innkeeper, who was also his distant uncle. \"Uncle Ping, I just saw what looked like the words 'reward money' on this. Could you take a look and tell me what exactly is written on this paper?\"","Reward money—perhaps he had a chance to get it.","\"Go tell the kitchen that the guest from earlier wants an extra egg in his noodle soup,\" the innkeeper instructed as he took the paper.","The servant hurried off to deliver the message. When he returned, he saw the innkeeper's grave expression. \"Uncle Ping, what does the paper actually say?\"","The innkeeper said, \"This is a notice offering a heavy reward for finding someone. They're looking for a nine-year-old child with short hair. The child's name is Qin Yan... chuan? That doesn't seem to be the character 'chuan.' It's 'zhou.' Ah, yes, it's 'zhou.' The ink blot has run, but it's definitely 'zhou.' The child's name is Qin Yanzhou.\"","A long scraping sound, followed by a thud, rang through the hall as a chair was pushed back and fell over.","Both the innkeeper and the servant were startled and looked up simultaneously. They saw a man standing alone in the middle of the hall, staring rigidly in their direction.","Meeting that fearsome face, marred by what looked like keloid scars, the servant paled and whispered, \"Uncle Ping, that man's face is truly horrifying, and his eyes are so strange.\"","The servant had a very strong impression of this guest because his face was excessively ugly. The old, hardened scars looked like flesh worms, occupying large areas of his face.","When he had attended to this person earlier, he hadn't dared to look too closely, fearing nightmares at night. Was this demon-like man staring at him because he had overheard the comments he'd muttered under his breath earlier...?","The \"flesh worms\" twitched. The servant was terrified, but it seemed the man was unaccustomed to making large facial expressions. The initial wave of shock on his surface gradually settled back into calmness.","Those eyes remained wooden, seemingly an endless void, yet they strangely gave the feeling that something was trying to stir and emerge from within.","The servant watched as the man strode swiftly to stand before them and silently raised a hand.","He clearly intended to take the mulberry bark paper from the innkeeper's hand, but just as his fingertips were about to touch it, he jerked them back as if his hand had been sharply slapped.","Quanjie stood rooted to the spot, his gaze blank.","Is this a dream?","Would it be like the thousand other times before—all false, nothing but the delusions born from his years of struggling in the mire? A pitiful illusion, an unreachable mirage, a desperate fantasy conjured just as he was finally about to lose his mind."]},{"number":50,"title":"Chapter 50","paragraphs":["The young servant saw the man before him staring fixedly at the notice, then opening his mouth, but no sound came out.","Not only was his face ugly, but his temperament was also strange. What an odd fellow, the servant thought to himself.","The innkeeper, having seen his share of the world, asked calmly, \"Guest, do you want this?\"","Seeing the other standing woodenly before the counter, the innkeeper thought he might be illiterate and too embarrassed to speak, so he kindly read it out for him: \"The person who posted this notice is looking for a child. The child is nine years old, named 'Qin Yanzhou', with short hair, fair skin, peach blossom eyes, and about five feet seven inches tall. Hmm, the bottom half is missing. Can't see the information of the poster or the reward amount, nor do we know where this missing person notice came from.\"","A moment after the innkeeper finished speaking, the young man standing before the counter finally moved. He reached out again and took hold of the notice in his hand.","The crumpled mulberry paper turned around.","The young man lowered his head, reading the contents word by word, and used his scarred fingers to repeatedly trace over that name.","The handwriting wasn't elegant, and the ink had bled considerably.","As the mulberry paper had gotten wet and dried, the characters for \"Qin Yanzhou\" on it had also become less clear, requiring some effort to make them out, but they were indeed there.","Others had seen it, read it aloud, and he had seen it too, and could even touch it.","It wasn't a dream.","So, it really wasn't a dream!","Only one person would use this name and this description to search for him...","A small splash suddenly bloomed on the mulberry paper, a spot the size of an ink drop getting wet.","\"Ah, guest, why are you...\" the innkeeper exclaimed in surprise.","\"Where did this notice come from?\" Quanjie looked up, his gaze fixed tightly on the two of them.","His face still showed little expression—wooden, stiff, as if wearing a carved mask. If not for the redness around his eyes, one would hardly have noticed he had just shed hot tears.","The young servant was still afraid of him, but now, looking into those dark eyes again, they seemed vastly different from before.","How to describe it?","It was as if spring had returned to the earth, and sweet rain had fallen from heaven.","Thus, in the desolate wilderness, a tiny blade of grass had sprouted. The sprout was tender and fragile, easily broken, and with a little force, it could be uprooted. But it had indeed emerged, dotting that barren, lonely world.","\"I... I found it in the courtyard just now. Last night was windy and rainy, it was probably blown here from elsewhere by the storm,\" the servant said in a low voice.","Quanjie carefully rolled up the mulberry paper in his hand and, without a word, took it and walked out of the inn.","\"Ah, guest! What about your noodle soup?\"","\"Uncle Ping, since he doesn't want his noodle soup anymore, can I have it?\"","A heavy rain had washed away nearly two days of stifling gloom; the morning air had become incredibly fresh and clear.","The commandery was bustling early in the morning. The market was crowded and noisy, shops had their doors wide open, street vendors were out selling their wares, and customers streamed in and out continuously.","Quanjie walked along the noisy street. At first, he tried to unfold the mulberry paper in his hand to ask questions, but people, seeing his face, immediately avoided him as if he were the plague. Often, before he could even open his mouth, they had already hurried away.","Quanjie stood still, suddenly feeling a sense of bewilderment.","The passersby seemed to be wrapped in a layer of gray clothing, the shops were gray and black too, everything looked like an ink wash painting.","Everywhere was the same, utterly unremarkable, with no point of breakthrough.","\"Are you waiting to buy something from my shop? If not, don't stand there blocking my business.\" A vendor who was late today saw a human post standing in front of his shop and immediately waved to shoo him away.","Quanjie, as if waking from a dream, took two steps to the side.","He was still somewhat dazed, his gaze unconsciously following the vendor. He saw the man open his shop door, then pull out a piece of burlap and some paste from somewhere, and with a smack, stick the burlap onto the door plank.","On the burlap were two large, clear characters: Clearance Sale.","No one noticed that the vendor's slap had shaken not only the door plank under his palm but also the young man standing not far away.","Quanjie's pupils contracted, his mind was greatly shaken, and many forgotten images resurfaced.","The pitch-black night, the patrolling guards and night watchmen on the street, the black-clad night travelers. The place where he had stood leaning against the door that night—behind him, there seemed to have been a notice.","Following his memory, Quanjie returned to the street from last night. That street had many shops; he only remembered the general area.","Holding the notice, he first went to a rice shop.","\"This? I know about it, Old Gao next door posted it. Just yesterday. I even asked him in the afternoon why he posted this. He said he got advice from a wise man, might be able to win big with a small stake, get a mountain of gold for free. Probably the strong wind last night blew the notice away, and that's how you found it. You're asking where Old Gao's shop is? Go out, turn right, it's the next shop, Gao's Sauces. Just a few steps away,\" the rice merchant said with a laugh.","Quanjie thanked him and went out with the notice.","It was indeed just a few steps. He saw the neighboring condiment shop with its \"Salty Stone\" flag fluttering.","Merchant Gao had opened early to welcome customers. He had just seen off a few servants from wealthy families who came to buy Salty Stone and was about to take a sip of water to soothe his throat when he caught sight of someone else approaching from the corner of his eye.","He felt pleased—hey, probably another customer for Salty Stone. Ever since he started stocking Salty Stone, his business had been getting better and better.","So good, really, so good.","Merchant Gao was smiling as he prepared to greet the guest, but was caught off guard by the visitor's face. Before he could adjust his expression, he heard the guest ask:","\"Did you post this notice?\"","Merchant Gao's eyes followed the words downward and saw the familiar mulberry paper. When he opened the shop this morning and found the notice gone from the door, he had felt a bit sorry about it. He never expected it to return so soon.","\"Yes, I posted it,\" Merchant Gao said, reaching out to take it.","Quanjie didn't hand it over, only unfolded it to show him the incomplete notice, then asked, \"Who issued this notice?\"","Merchant Gao replied, \"It came from the North.\"","This answer was too vague. Quanjie unconsciously frowned.","Merchant Gao didn't forget to promote his Salty Stone. \"You know about Salty Stone, right? Top-quality goods, highly favored by the noble families in the commandery. This treasure is sourced from Ying Commandery up north. When we were getting the goods, an official from Ying Commandery—I heard them call him Colonel—that person entrusted us merchants to gather information. Said he was looking for a nine-year-old child. If we could bring him back, there's a heavy reward...\"","As for how heavy the reward was, Merchant Gao could recite it by heart.","Reciting the \"heavy reward,\" he couldn't help but feel tempted. \"Guest, could it be you have news about that child?\"","\"What is the Colonel's surname?\" Quanjie asked instead of answering.","Merchant Gao: \"I think it's Yan.\"","Quanjie calculated silently in his heart.","Setting out from here, traveling day and night without rest, with fast horses at full speed, one could reach Ying Commandery in five days at the earliest.","Seeing him persistently asking about \"Jinshan\" and only questioning without answering, as if money had fallen into his eyes, Merchant Gao sighed and said, \"I was just like you before, thinking that finding this child would allow me to become rich overnight and secure my life for years to come. For this, I even specifically went to the slave market in our commandery, but found nothing. Later, I realized it's as difficult as reaching the heavens. If it were truly easy, the Northern Lands wouldn't be offering such a heavy reward. I might as well focus on selling my saltpeter.\"","Quanjie turned to leave.","\"Hey, leave that notice with me. I only wrote it yesterday. Although it's a bit torn, if I fill out the rest, it'll still be usable,\" Merchant Gao called out.","Quanjie suddenly remembered something. He stopped, but instead of returning the notice, he asked again, \"You haven't been selling your saltpeter for just one day, so you should have returned from the Northern Lands earlier. Why did you only post the notice yesterday? Is it as the rice merchant next door said, that all this was guided by a 'mastermind'? Who is this mastermind? Do they hold an official position?\"","If the \"mastermind\" held an official position, it would mean there was someone within Guoyun Commandery who knew more about the situation. Perhaps he could inquire about his mother's recent circumstances.","A barrage of questions hit Merchant Gao, leaving him stunned. After a moment's pause, he scratched his head and said, \"What official? It was a young lady. The mastermind was a young lady, incredibly sharp-witted. I hadn't even thought of this strategy myself.\"","An indescribable feeling coiled around his heart. Quanjie unconsciously quickened his pace of speech. \"A young lady? What did she look like?\"","Merchant Gao recalled, \"She was wearing a veil hat at the time, so I couldn't see her face. But her voice was exceptionally pleasant, like a spring breeze. I remember she was wearing brocade from Yun. Just one gold hairpin on her head would cover several years of expenses for an ordinary family, not to mention she had several sword-bearing attendants. With such an entourage, she must be from a wealthy household.\"","Quanjie fell silent.","Traveling merchants are eloquent; few are introverted. With no customers in the shop at the moment, Merchant Gao decided to chat with him for a bit, hoping this person might, like the lady yesterday, buy something after their conversation.","\"I heard her attendants call her 'Madam,' so she must be married,\" Merchant Gao said, spreading one hand and counting on his fingers. \"There are only a few prominent families in the commandery: the Feng family of Prefect Feng, the Zhang family connected to Chang'an, and...\"","\"Quanjie.\"","Both men paused. Quanjie turned and saw Wang Jiang.","Wang Jiang was the companion who had infiltrated the Qin residence with him last night—his only remaining companion.","\"So it really is you. What are you doing here?\" Wang Jiang stepped forward, his gaze sweeping over Merchant Gao, a hint of scrutiny in his eyes.","Was this man some kind of contact?","Quanjie had no intention of explaining further to him and turned to walk out. Wang Jiang followed.","Seeing them leave the shop one after the other, Merchant Gao muttered, \"How strange. Why are they all so interested in that child the Northern Lands are looking for? They came in and immediately started talking about it.\"","The young man's departing footsteps hesitated slightly.","Wang Jiang said in a low voice, \"Quanjie, when are we returning to Gaoling Commandery? We failed last night. Although the commandery hasn't imposed a lockdown or search yet, there's no guarantee it won't happen soon. This place isn't safe to stay.\"","\"Not returning.\"","Almost as soon as Wang Jiang finished speaking, Quanjie threw out these two cold, hard words without hesitation.","Wang Jiang was stunned for a moment, his expression turning odd. \"Are you planning a second attempt? Don't say I didn't warn you. It's just the two of us now. After last night, their defenses will be tight for days to come. Going back rashly would just be throwing our lives away.\"","Quanjie remained silent.","Wang Jiang was angered by his attitude. \"What exactly do you want? Neither returning to Gaoling nor continuing the mission. Don't tell me you're planning to betray our patron?\"","Quanjie glanced at him coldly from the side. \"Why not?\"","Wang Jiang was taken aback by that look. In his memory, Quanjie was a cold, efficient blade, striking wherever its master pointed, more obedient than a dog. After all, dogs sometimes have stray thoughts, but Quanjie never did.","And now, this blade was developing distractions.","\"If you dare betray our patron, you'll die without a place to bury your bones!\" Wang Jiang was both shocked and furious.","If Quanjie betrayed their patron, what should he do?","As if hearing his thoughts, Quanjie said indifferently, \"Do as you wish. We go our separate ways from here.\"","Seeming to detect a trace of killing intent, Quanjie looked directly into his eyes. \"Whether you report my departure to Fan of Yanzhou is up to you. But if you think of taking my head back for a reward, you'd better weigh whether you have the skill.\"","A dark glint flashed in Wang Jiang's eyes. He suddenly smiled. \"Quanjie, you misunderstand. Leave if you want to, what's it to me? From now on, you walk your sunny path, I'll cross my single-plank bridge. Let's not meet again.\"","Quanjie offered no reply.","The two parted at the intersection ahead. Quanjie went east, Wang Jiang went west.","After a few steps, Wang Jiang looked back, a strange curve twisting his lips.","Quanjie's betrayal came at the perfect time!","Since the mission failed, there had to be a reason. Why not pin everything on Quanjie? That way, the patron's wrath would surely be directed solely at Quanjie, sparing him harsh criticism.","Indifferent to Wang Jiang's sudden change in attitude, Quanjie walked down the street, taking in the surrounding houses and mansions. Merchant Gao's earlier words still echoed in his ears.","A married young lady, her voice gentle as a spring breeze, also interested in the person the Northern Lands sought...","That indescribable feeling grew stronger, completely transforming into invisible threads that entangled his legs, making it impossible for him to leave Guoyun Commandery immediately.","Forget the commandery capital; even in a county, there aren't many families that provide sword-bearing attendants for their womenfolk. He would stay in Guoyun Commandery for two more days, investigate the prominent families here, and then go to Ying Commandery.","Qin Residence, side room in the main courtyard.","\"...You said there were assassins last night?\" Daili asked in surprise.","Nianxia nodded emphatically. \"Yes, Madam. Just now, I overheard the patrolling guards saying that several assassins in black came in the middle of the night. They sneaked into Squad Leader Bai's room, trying to kill him. Thankfully, heaven was watching over him. Last night, Squad Leader Bai happened to get up to use the privy, so the two groups ran into each other right in the room.\"","Daili asked, \"Was Squad Leader Bai injured?\"","Bipo replied, \"His life is not in danger. I heard he sustained some minor wounds. The commandery hasn't been very peaceful lately, Madam. Please don't leave the residence. If there's anything you wish to purchase, just instruct me to go buy it.\"","Daili remembered someone coming to find Qin Shaozong late last night; it must have been about the attack on the residence. But speaking of things to buy, there actually was something.","The rain last night came at a most inopportune time, thoroughly drenching all the fish bladders she had been sun-drying on the winnowing basket.","She needed to prepare new fish bladders...","\"Madam, from now on, no matter what, I should still sleep in the small side room. If we encounter villains, Nianxia and I can buy you some time,\" Bipo said earnestly.","Not only did they have enough to eat and wear with little work, but they also received a generous monthly reward. Serving such a master, their lives were more comfortable than those of many young women from ordinary families.","The noble person's advice back then was indeed correct. With just one kneel, the lady's heart softened immediately.","The maid Bipo beside her nodded, \"My lady, both Nianxia and I have previously attended to our masters during... marital intimacy. We know what should be done.\"","Daili: \"...\"","No, that was not the reason at all.","Just as the atmosphere grew somewhat tense, a tall figure walked in from outside.","As soon as Qin Shaozong arrived, Nianxia and Bipo tacitly withdrew.","\"My lord, why aren't you going to the military camp today?\" Daili looked at him. Someone had infiltrated the manor, yet he seemed completely unperturbed.","\"Not for now. Have you heard about the attack in the manor?\" Qin Shaozong sat down beside her.","\"I have,\" Daili asked him, \"How many were captured?\"","Qin Shaozong: \"One was captured alive, two escaped. After interrogation, the captive claimed to be from Qingzhou.\"","\"How could that be?!\" Daili blurted out in disbelief.","\"My lady finds it impossible?\" He gave a slight smile.","Daili: \"Naturally, it's impossible. Governor Nangong invited you here to form an alliance against the Qinglian Sect. At this critical juncture, how could he possibly turn around and attack your men? It's not as if he has secretly allied with the Qinglian Sect.\"","However, by the end, Daili sounded somewhat uncertain, \"They shouldn't have secretly colluded, should they?\"","On the surface, things were always clear-cut, black and white. But with so many versions of \"Infernal Affairs\" made, some things are truly hard to say.","A hint of a smile lifted the corner of Qin Shaozong's eyes, \"What does my lady consider 'secretly'?\"","With only the two of them in the room, Daili suddenly sensed the shift in atmosphere and became wary, looking at him. \"If they were sneaking around, they certainly wouldn't do it in broad daylight, isn't that right, my lord?\"","Qin Shaozong let out a soft chuckle.","This little fox always had eight hundred schemes up her sleeve when dealing with him.","He first said something similar to what Bipo had mentioned, \"The commandery has been unsettled lately. Two of the thieves who infiltrated the manor last night escaped. There's no guarantee they won't return. You will move in with me.\"","Daili was taken aback, her first reaction being refusal. \"They won't come back, will they? Having failed once, the manor's security will surely be heightened. Moreover, with only two of them left, their strength is weak. How could they succeed?\"","\"Assassination attempts cannot be judged by common logic. Besides, only two escaped. The total number of assassins is unknown. Who knows how many more are hidden in the commandery, yet to show themselves?\" Qin Shaozong said calmly.","It was fortunate that the black-clad men last night entered other courtyards. If they had slipped into her side chamber from the eastern window, the distance was too great, and he was already asleep by then. He truly might not have heard any commotion from there.","Daili opened her mouth to speak.","But he made the final decision, \"This matter is settled.\"","Currently, Qin Shaozong had the final say in the entire manor. At his command, Nianxia and Bipo swiftly moved Daili's belongings to the main chamber.","There wasn't much luggage, mainly a pillow and a few pieces of clothing.","Daili tried to salvage the situation: \"This isn't proper, is it? It might disturb your rest.\"","\"It's only for a few days. Once the army sets out, you'll have plenty of time to sleep alone,\" Qin Shaozong suddenly smiled. \"Besides, you sleep quite peacefully, my lady. It's no disturbance.\"","It's just that when she hasn't had enough sleep, her temper flares a bit, and she extends her little fox claws to scratch."]},{"number":51,"title":"Chapter 51","paragraphs":["Quanjie walked alone on the street, heading towards his next target.","He had just come from the Feng residence in Guoyun County.","The Feng residence was the home of Prefect Feng. As the local power in Guoyun County, Prefect Feng's family wealth naturally surpassed that of the other prominent local families. Quanjie had infiltrated it, catching a distant glimpse of Prefect Feng's principal wife, and then gone to seek out the recently favored concubine who was currently the talk of the household.","He had arrived without a sound, and left the same way.","Having found nothing at the Feng house, Quanjie changed course for the Zhang residence. For an entire day, he traversed the county, visiting several other influential and notable households.","He found nothing.","He had basically checked all those that fit the criteria, except for...","Quanjie looked towards two large neighboring mansions not far away. He had infiltrated one of them yesterday, but had not yet explored the other.","After surveying both for a moment, Quanjie fixed his gaze on the one he had not entered.","The sun dipped westward, dyeing vast stretches of the sky a brilliant orange-yellow. The evening clouds spread for miles, then gradually faded away along with the sunlight.","Night fell, and darkness reclaimed the land.","Quanjie patiently waited until deep into the quiet night before cloaking himself in the darkness and scaling the wall once more. He had studied the layout maps of both mansions. For his entry point this time, he deliberately chose the most remote courtyard within the compound.","But Quanjie hadn't expected that the moment his feet touched the ground, several sets of footsteps would sound from the direction of the courtyard entrance.","\"Ah Hu, get up for your shift!\"","After this shout, rustling noises came from inside the house.","Quanjie immediately moved to the side of the building, pressing himself flat against the wall. Moments later, he heard the door open, and several figures emerged from within.","Someone yawned, \"Shift change already? Feels like I just fell asleep.\"","\"Can't be helped. After the attack on the Qin mansion next door yesterday, our Lord Nangong Qingzhou is taking a lesson from it and increasing patrols too. I even heard one of those assassins last night was captured alive and claimed they were sent by our Qingzhou forces—what absolute nonsense!\"","\"A bunch of demons and monsters causing trouble in the shadows, utterly detestable. By the way, did those assassins who slipped in next door last night hurt anyone from the Northern Territory?\"","\"I'm not clear on that. I only heard that late last night, beyond the two walls, someone suddenly shouted 'assassins!' and then it got as lively as if thunder had struck the ground.\"","\"A night assault, and a group operation at that. If they had really managed to get inside the rooms, it would've been bad. Lord Qin even brought a woman with him on this campaign. Isn't he afraid a misstep might lead to the beauty perishing?\"","\"You're overthinking it. How could she possibly perish? I heard when they got out of the carriage, there were three young women—two were her maidservants. And after entering the city, Lord Qin dared to leave our Lord Nangong Qingzhou waiting, going to his residence first, most likely to settle the woman. With that kind of treatment, she's definitely a favored concubine. At night, she probably shares Lord Qin's quarters. If assassins made it to his room, hah, no matter how many came, it wouldn't be enough.\"","\"In the past, I never heard of Lord Qin taking a woman on campaign. Why break precedent this time? Could that woman be a stunning beauty, making him unwilling to part with her even on a military expedition?\"","\"I heard she is indeed extraordinarily beautiful, surpassing all others. But more than that, she must truly be capable. Have you heard about the dragon-bone waterwheel from the Northern Territory? I heard it was brought out by this Lady Dai from the hands of a recluse. What a marvelous thing—small landowners and tenant farmers are overjoyed.\"","\"Suddenly I feel a real itch to see this Lady Dai.\"","The soldier elbowed his comrade who was currently rubbing his chest. \"You'd better not. Remember years ago when Lord Qin went alone into a wolf pack and took the head of Langye of Wuhuan from among twenty thousand men? Wringing one more head like yours would be child's play for him.\"","\"Hey, why are you boosting their morale and dampening our own?\"","\"It's not exactly 'theirs' anymore, since our armies have formed an alliance.\"","...","The group chatted as they walked away, while another group entered the house to rest—a routine shift change.","No one noticed the figure clinging to the side of the building like a gecko.","Quanjie struggled to steady his breathing, yet the heart in his chest, dead for many years, thumped violently, each beat stronger than the last.","The information he had previously overlooked now surged into the center of his vision like startled butterflies taking flight.","Ying County. This place was originally held by a salt smuggler surnamed Li. Several months ago, Ying County was captured by the Northern Territory army, and this county bordering a salt lake changed hands once more. Since then, that entire vast stretch of the Northern Territory was finally connected end to end, all becoming part of Qin Shaozong's domain.","The salt merchant's order originated in Ying County; the one who issued the search order must belong to Qin Shaozong's forces.","Could the \"Lady Dai\" mentioned by those Qingzhou soldiers just now be...?","The soldiers finishing their night watch returned to the house and slammed the door shut. The sound of the door closing overlapped with a soft, murmured name, completely drowning it out.","Quanjie cautiously waited another half hour before leaving this remote courtyard.","He retraced his path, exiting the mansion.","The dark clouds obscuring the bright moon hadn't moved. Tonight, there was no moon or stars. Under the heavy sky, gloomy winds rose intermittently—the weather was just as bad as yesterday.","The young man looked towards the neighboring mansion. His figure light as a spirit-cat, he swiftly scaled the wall.","If Wang Jiang were here now, he would be greatly astonished, for Quanjie was scaling the wall at the exact same spot as yesterday, even choosing the same landing point.","It couldn't be described as anything less than audacious.","Bai Jianping, wounded the previous night, couldn't sleep. The pain from his injury was secondary; after all, he was used to the rough and tumble of the battlefield, and the wound wasn't serious.","The main issue was that upon hearing of his injury, that fellow Feng Feng had taken the initiative to come to his room, insisting on sharing it, saying it was to guard against another attack tonight.","The result was that the guy snored like thunder, bellowing like an ox, audible even through a wall. It was maddening.","Tossing and turning, unable to sleep, Bai Jianping finally got up and walked out, intending to kick the fellow out.","Hurry up, back to where you came from.","But as he reached the outer room, before he could even rouse the man, Bai Jianping happened to see through the unclosed door a shadowy figure flash quickly past the courtyard entrance.","Bai Jianping froze for a second, then instinctively sprinted towards the courtyard entrance, thinking in disbelief: Good heavens, surely no one could be that audacious!","By the time he reached the entrance barefoot, he just caught sight of the figure ahead turning into another corridor. Bai Jianping drew a sharp breath—he couldn't believe someone really had the gall to come again!","What, did they think that after failing with one strike yesterday, today's heightened security was just for show?","\"Assassins!\" Bai Jianping yelled at the top of his lungs.","This shout stirred up a hornet's nest. The nearby patrol guards paused briefly, then swarmed towards the area.","Quanjie successively dodged several squads. For those he couldn't avoid, he first blocked with his drawn blade, then angled it sideways. After deflecting most of their force, he kicked them away.","In the darkness, the young man's figure was as slippery as an eel. He passed several men in succession, steadily advancing towards the main courtyard, infuriating Bai Jianping and Qiao Wangfei, who were rushing over from the front and rear directions respectively.","Well, there really is someone who isn't afraid of death!","\"Get out of the way. Let me deal with him,\" Bai Jianping drew his sword and stepped forward.","Bai Jianping held a long sword in his hand, while Qiao Wangfei grasped a scimitar in each hand. The two of them launched a pincer attack on Quanjie.","The glint of knives and the shadow of the sword flashed before their eyes. Quanjie's face remained unchanged. He quickly took out another short knife from somewhere, holding the long one in his right hand and the short one in his left.","\"Clang!\"","The knives clashed violently, and the metallic sound was ear - piercing.","On the other side, the long sword collided with the short knife. As the blades slid against each other, sparks flew. After the gradually intensifying fire around, it became the only bright spot in the center.","Quanjie was caught in the pincer attack. In their first close - range encounter, after the knives and the sword clashed, both sides paused for a moment.","Taking advantage of this moment, Quanjie said, \"I've come to your mansion to look for someone, Daili.\"","At this time, the guards holding torches had rushed over. They quickly formed a circle, surrounding the three of them. The firelight illuminated Quanjie's eyebrows. Qiao Wangfei, who was about to launch a second attack, was stunned.","The young man's face was uneven, with scars like wriggling worms coiling on his cheeks. Only his pair of eyes were extremely outstanding.","The inner corners of his eyes were deep, and the outer corners were slightly curved and upturned. They were very standard peach - blossom eyes. And he had seen a similar pair of eyes just the day before.","Remembering the strange story about \"ten years\" that Hu Bao had privately told him, Qiao Wangfei took a dazed step back.","Bai Jianping, however, flew into a rage. \"Don't try to deceive me with such despicable tricks, you villain. Quickly accept your death!\"","As a result, he vigorously swung his sword, aiming straight at the opponent's vital point. From the corner of his eye, he saw Qiao Wangfei, who was holding two knives, take a step back. His body straightened from a bent - over and out - stretched position, and even the tips of the two knives slowly drooped towards the ground.","Bai Jianping couldn't believe it. \"Old Qiao, what are you doing?\"","Was Old Qiao suffering from an old injury? Well, it was understandable if that was the case.","\"Old Bai, wait,\" Qiao Wangfei shouted.","But Bai Jianping didn't hear him. All he could think about was taking the man's head in front of him. He had recognized this man now. This was the one who had lit a lamp in his room last night. He had let him escape last night, but today he would surely make him die here.","Bai Jianping used a single long sword. Seeing this, Quanjie put away the other short knife and fought with him using only one knife.","\"The villain is so arrogant!\" Bai Jianping sneered.","The blades clashed, separated, and then hacked at each other. In just a blink of an eye, there had already been several clanging sounds.","Slashing, hacking, picking, stabbing... In just a few short breaths, the two of them exchanged blows, and their moves changed in an instant. The more they fought, the more Bai Jianping's fighting spirit was aroused. He thought to himself that this young man really had some skills despite his young age.","Their fight was not limited to weapon - based combat. Occasionally, they resorted to fists and kicks, and the collisions of their bodies made dull thumping sounds.","But after a short while, Bai Jianping quickly noticed that the man in front of him gradually only defended and didn't attack.","\"Old Bai, wait!\"","The more Qiao Wangfei watched from the sidelines, the more something seemed off. He couldn't help but join the fight again. However, compared to before, this time he was more like trying to break up the fight and stop Bai Jianping from continuing to attack Quanjie.","Bai Jianping was blocked several times and got angry. \"Old Qiao, what's wrong with you? If you're not feeling well, go to the side and stay there. Don't stop me.\"","Qiao Wangfei stepped between them, with his back to Bai Jianping and facing Quanjie. \"You said you're looking for Lady Dai. What's the matter?\"","Quanjie turned his head and looked into the distance. The night was vast, and he couldn't see anything. But his eyes gradually softened, and he whispered something.","Qiao Wangfei's pupils constricted. In extreme shock, there also seemed to be a bit of \"as expected\" in his expression.","Bai Jianping was completely stunned on the spot and blurted out, \"Don't talk nonsense. How is this possible? Lady Dai's son is only nine years old!\"","Seeing their expressions, Quanjie felt relieved, knowing that he had found the right place. \"You can lock me up in a room first and report it tomorrow.\"","Qiao Wangfei stared intently.","Such a big commotion had occurred tonight. It was probably impossible to wait until tomorrow...","*","Tonight, Daili was sharing a bed with Qin Shaozong. As Mo Yanyun's return was approaching, certain things would soon be prohibited. Qin Shaozong was like a tiger preparing for winter, indulging himself to store up fat so that he wouldn't starve himself thin during the coming days.","After it was over, Daili was so tired that she just wanted to sleep, but she still didn't forget one thing.","\"Change the quilt,\" Daili pushed the man beside her.","She would rather sleep on a wooden board than continue to lie on this dirty quilt.","The satisfied man was very easy - going. Instead of calling the maids outside, he got out of bed and went to the corner cabinet to get a new set of bedding. When he returned to the bedside, he found that the woman on the bed had gotten up and was walking outside.","Qin Shaozong grabbed her arm. \"My lady?\"","\"I'm going to wash up,\" Daili slapped his hand away and continued to walk limply towards the side room.","Qin Shaozong snorted with a smile. \"Is my lady a fish in disguise?\"","Daili ignored him.","There was water prepared in the side room. Fortunately, it was summer, and the hot water still had some warmth left, so it wasn't cold to wash with. Daili quickly tidied herself up. When she came out again, she felt that she could fall asleep as soon as she closed her eyes.","But in fact, she couldn't.","Because just as she closed her eyes, there was a knock on the door.","\"My lord, there's a nocturnal visitor in the mansion,\" it was Qiao Wangfei's voice.","Qin Shaozong, who had just closed the curtain, raised his long eyebrows. \"Another one? Since he's so bold, then interrogate him properly.\"","Qiao Wangfei outside clearly hesitated. \"My lord, this man claims to have been adopted by Fan of Yanzhou many years ago and changed his name to Quanjie. But he isn't parentless. He says his mother is Daili, and his original name is... Qin Yanzhou.\"","Daili on the bed suddenly opened her eyes.","Qin Shaozong was stunned.","Daili, who was sleeping inside, had already gotten up and was in a hurry to get out of bed. The room was pitch - black. Daili was too eager, taking big steps. She only stepped on half of the footstool and accidentally slipped and fell to the ground with a loud thud.","Qin Shaozong was startled and quickly picked her up. \"The man isn't going to run away. Why are you in such a hurry, my lady? Where did you fall?\"","Daili pushed his hand away. \"It's okay. Light the lamp and help me get dressed. I'm going to take a look.\"","Qiao Wangfei was standing outside the main room. Hearing a familiar female voice coming from inside, he couldn't help showing a look of surprise on his face. But by the time the door opened and the two people inside came out, his face had returned to normal.","\"Where is he?\" Daili asked anxiously.","Qiao Wangfei replied, \"He's temporarily locked up in a pavilion courtyard. Please follow me.\"","The mansion was brightly lit. The corridor was illuminated by the firelight. Daili's gaze followed the corridor and saw a pavilion courtyard heavily guarded by soldiers.","\"Slow down. Even if he grows wings, he can't fly away,\" Qin Shaozong noticed that she was walking awkwardly and guessed that she had hurt herself in the fall.","Daili still ignored him.","When entering the pavilion courtyard, Daili paused at the door, took a deep breath, and unconsciously clenched her fists.","Qiao Wangfei stepped forward a few steps and pushed open the tightly - shut door first.","\"Creak.\" The door opened.","A figure with hands tied behind the back completely filled Dai Li's vision. The moment the other person looked up upon hearing the sound, it was as if something exploded in her mind.","It was an extremely ugly face. The scars on his cheeks sprawled across a large area, so hideous that they could give children nightmares.","However, those eyes... those eyes that looked at her were incredibly gentle, like a newly - born lamb, exactly the same as in her memory.","In Dai Li's world, a fierce wind sprang up around her. She could hear nothing and see nothing except the figure not far away. The wind was mixed with countless tiny blades, cutting her until blood gushed out and bones were exposed. Every nerve and every inch of her flesh was screaming in extreme pain.","Countless invisible saws stabbed into her heart, shredding it into pieces.","The color drained completely from her face, and Dai Li staggered unsteadily.","Qin Shaozong quickly reached out to support her waist. But the next moment, the woman in his arms stumbled forward. Even though her steps were unsteady and she seemed on the verge of collapsing to the ground at any moment, she still moved forward firmly.","Dai Li had often wondered in the past ten years that when her child grew up and she saw him again, would she be able to recognize him at a glance?","Now she had the answer. Yes, she could!","How could she not recognize her own child?","He had grown taller, and his face had changed, very different from the one in her memory. But she knew, she knew that he was a part of her flesh and blood...","\"Zhou Zhou!\" Dai Li cried out in despair.","She staggered up to him and raised her hand, wanting to touch the young man's face. But when her jade - white fingertips were less than an inch away, they twitched violently, making her afraid to move forward.","In Dai Li's eyes, the large scars gradually receded, back to the scabbed state, before the scabs formed, and then turned into wounds oozing bright red blood.","Tears welled up in Dai Li's eyes, completely blurring her vision. \"Zhou Zhou...\"","How painful those wounds must have been! Oh, her child. What kind of bullying had he endured here?","At this time, the young man lowered his head and actively pressed his face against her fair hand.","It felt as soft as in his memory, which made him so happy that he wanted to smile. However, this action was so unfamiliar to him that it was slow and stiff now, with an inharmonious and strange feeling. \"It's not real. You don't have to worry,\" he said.","Dai Li couldn't hear those words, or perhaps subconsciously she thought they were just words of comfort. The rough feeling under her fingers made her heart ache so much that she sobbed uncontrollably.","Ten years ago, he was only nine years old, at an age when he would report to her wherever he went.","Such a young child. At school, he learned about civilization, harmony, freedom, and equality. However, every corner of this era was full of exploitation and cruelty.","With his mother not by his side and everything around him being strange, how many times had he secretly cried at night to grow into what he was now?","Quanjie.","He was like a domestic dog, and also like a weed.","Anyone could bully him, and anyone could trample on her child. The sweet bean she had held in her palm had become the mud in the field that others could trample on at will!","Just thinking about it made Dai Li's heart break. \"You're not Quanjie. You're Qin Yanzhou. Zhou Zhou is Qin Yanzhou!\"","Suddenly, Qin Yanzhou felt the restraint on his hands loosen. He knew that the person behind him had untied the ropes. He raised his arms and gently hugged Dai Li back.","The pendulum of time seemed to stop at this moment. The hands of the clock quickly moved backward, spinning round and round. Those precious memories that he had relived again and again over the years now took on a tangible form, as if they were reappearing around him -","The beautiful woman sent the little boy with a schoolbag to the school bus, gently tidying his collar. \"Zhou Zhou, you must listen to Teacher Lin at school. Call Mom if there's anything. Mom will pick you up after school. Good boy, go.\"","Tears welled up in the young man's eyes and rolled down his cheeks. He forced a smile that was uglier than crying. \"Mom, I'm sorry. I can never be a good boy again.\"","His hands were stained with blood, and he could never go back to the past."]},{"number":52,"title":"Chapter 52","paragraphs":["Daili heard his apology, and tears welled up like a spring. \"It's not your fault. It's mine for not coming to find you sooner. It's all my fault, all my fault...\"","If she had come earlier, instead of delaying for a full half year, would her child have been spared from being trampled upon so casually in this unfamiliar era?","Nine years ago, during that great famine, he was only ten years old.","Back then, every household was without grain, the plants and trees withered. He was just a ten-year-old child. Strangers owed him no kinship, so who would feed him? Who would give him their own life-saving rations?","Those people whose eyes gleamed green with hunger, would they have turned their gaze upon her child?","Just like in the nightmare she once had. Several butchers pinned him down, raised their knives, and fell—perhaps offering the tender meat for silver to be given to the \"vegetable people,\" or the chunks of flesh dropping into a steaming pot, while faceless diners around cheered in a frenzy.","Anyone could have trampled upon her child...","Qin Yanzhou sighed, a sigh filled with indescribable contentment, yet also the helplessness of fighting with all one's might but still being unable to resist fate. \"It's not your fault. It's all in the past now.\"","He was already content. In the ten years since, there had never been a time that made him happier than this moment.","He had thought that until madness or death, he would drift alone here. He never expected heaven to finally show him mercy once, just as he was about to lose his grip and sink into the mire, letting him see the sunlight that could dispel the gloom.","Thus, his soul found salvation; the desolation welcomed an oasis. It was like bathing in a hot spring, so warm it brought hot tears to his eyes.","But there was also an unspeakable ache. His mother said she came to find him; he said he fell into a river to get here. Could it be that...","Qin Yanzhou opened his mouth, but lacked the courage to ask that question.","Hearing him say \"it's all in the past now,\" Daili couldn't help but bite her lip hard.","No, it's not past!","How could the suffering endured over ten years simply be past? It would be a black brand seared into the depths of his soul, a festering wound that perhaps could never heal in a lifetime.","Daili's heart felt as if it were dripping blood. In the blink of an eye, after her hot tears fell, her vision cleared somewhat. Then, she saw the two scars on the neck of the person before her.","One was right at the front, about half a finger's width, coiled like a snake around the front of his neck. It looked as if a rope had once bitten fiercely into his flesh. Only after repeated instances did it leave this scar, impossible to erase even after all these years.","The other was on the side of his neck, about two inches long, perfectly straight without any curve, most likely from a blade or sword.","Daili's pupils constricted violently, her temples feeling as if struck by a heavy hammer. Details she had overlooked earlier now rose like snakes startled from the grass, suddenly lunging up to bite her hard.","Zhouzhou's voice had been off just now—excessively hoarse, as if his throat held coarse gravel, or like a damaged, rusted, discarded gong.","She had thought it was due to choked emotion, but now it seemed that wasn't the case.","His voice was ruined.","Daili opened her mouth to speak, but no words came out. She only drew in a sharp, cold breath.","That chill was truly piercing, condensing into a prism covered in sharp spikes. It traveled down her windpipe, scraping her insides until they bled incessantly.","Daili began to tremble, as if plunged into an ice cellar. Her shaking fingertips finally touched that old, years-old scar.","Qin Yanzhou paused. The scars on his face could still be claimed as fake, but those on his neck, hands, and even his body could not be falsified.","He suddenly didn't know what to do.","Daili's emotions were fluctuating intensely. Combined with the exhaustion of the night, and being overly agitated, her vision suddenly went black.","Qin Yanzhou was just about to say something when he felt the person in his arms go limp. His eyes sharpened as he moved to support her, but a large, dark hand reached from behind her, gripping the woman's waist, holding her firmly as if to pull her back.","The young man instantly looked up. His black eyes, inherited from his mother, were as dark as ink. The earlier softness had completely vanished, replaced only by a razor-sharp edge.","Earlier, when the door opened, more than just his mother had entered. But at that time, he likewise could see nothing else, only wanting one last confirmation of whether this was an intoxicating, beautiful dream.","Now...","As their eyes met, one was steady, showing neither joy nor sorrow; the other was visibly wary and resistant.","Qin Yanzhou was not yet twenty, not as tall as the other man, nor as robust as Qin Shaozong in his prime. Surrounded now by a group of northern military officers, it did nothing to hinder the murderous aura he currently directed at the man before him.","If he were an animal, all his fur would likely be standing on end by now, his throat emitting warning growls.","Qin Yanzhou didn't ask who the other man was, because there was no need. It was said the Martial Peace Marquis of the north was born with a broken eyebrow. Today, he had infiltrated the Qin residence, and after stating his name, the person who tied his hands said he would report to \"His Lordship.\"","This man arrived later, and his distinctive features matched. He must be that Qin Shaozong, whom Fan of Yanzhou greatly feared.","Seeing this, Qin Shaozong gave a low, humorless laugh.","Well, still a little wolf cub.","He had infiltrated the manor twice in one night, daring to return alone the very next day without a break, probably having crossed swords with the patrol guards more than once, unafraid of getting his head lopped off.","Truly her offspring—this boldness was inherited, both possessing the hearts of bears and the gall of leopards.","\"Your mother is unwell. I'll take her back to rest,\" Qin Shaozong reached out again.","Qin Yanzhou said nothing, stepping back with Daili, just evading his long arm, still watching him warily.","Connecting the merchant's notices and the northern search orders, he vaguely guessed why his mother was entangled with this man.","Qin Shaozong was amused by his action. \"Thinking of leaving? Your assassination failed. Do you think Fan Tianshi will let you off easy? Not to mention taking her with you—how could you possibly ensure her safety and proper care? And how much dirty work have you done over the years? How many enemies have you made? Probably no one knows better than you. Do you believe that the moment Fan Tianshi announces your betrayal, people will be at your door seeking revenge?\"","After saying this, Qin Shaozong's own temples throbbed twice.","These past few days, while drinking with Nan Gongxiong, the latter had mentioned this \"Quanjie\" fellow trailing a pile of troubles behind him. Qin Shaozong had paid it no mind at the time.","Just a pitiful soul with a bitter fate, nothing more.","This world was inherently unjust; there were countless people with bitter fates. Some, due to bad weather and inability to pay the ever-increasing land rent, were persecuted to death by powerful landlords. Some, harmed by treacherous officials, saw their entire families exiled to the frontiers, gradually breaking apart and dying on the long journey. Others, betrayed by villains, died on the battlefield, leaving behind only a pair of orphaned children.","The unfortunate each have their own misfortune. Only by piercing the vast, sky-enveloping dark cloud overhead would dawn arrive.","So, when he heard about \"Quanjie,\" Qin Shaozong had been utterly indifferent, even agreeing with Nan Gongxiong that an early death meant an early release, hoping for a better rebirth in the next life.","But fate plays cruel tricks. This young man turned out to be the son she had been searching for all along. How in the world did he become her son? If she didn't care for him, and he kicked the boy out of the manor this very moment, she would follow without even packing a bag.","Qin Shaozong found himself with a rare headache.","The wolf cub she gave birth to was truly capable of stirring up trouble. Yet, having found him after losing him, she would absolutely never part with him again.","Fine. He had already dealt with two provincial governors before; handling one more from Yanzhou wouldn't be impossible. Besides, since allying with Nangong Xiong, he had already been at odds with Fan Tianshi...","Qin Yanzhou stiffened at his words, the bristling thorns about him wilting slightly.","Though only a little, his imposing manner was indeed less sharp than before. After a moment of silence, he asked, \"Where is my mother's room?\"","This meant he intended to escort her back.","Qin Shaozong knew this was his concession. Making allowances for their mother-son reunion, he restrained himself, merely saying in a deep voice, \"Follow me.\"","After they left the small room, the others remained somewhat dazed, with Bai Jianping being the most affected.","\"B-But Madam Dai's son... isn't he nine years old?\" Bai Jianping stammered. That young man's stature just now looked at least eighteen or nineteen.","Back then, Hu Bao had returned from Qiantang, rested only one night in Yingjun, and received orders the very next day to set out again for the Qin family in Yangzhou.","That night, before receiving the gag order, Hu Bao spoke of that strange \"ten-year\" tale to Feng Feng and Qiao Wangfei, astonishing them both. Yet, having chatted with his comrades one night, he received the gag order from his superiors the very next day.","However, Feng Feng and Qiao Wangfei were already in the know. Helpless, Hu Bao could only ask them not to spread the strange tale around.","This resulted in some under Qin Shaozong's command knowing about the ten-year gap, while others did not, still thinking they were truly searching for a nine-year-old child.","Qiao Wangfei sighed, \"It's a long story.\"","\"Then make it short,\" Bai Jianping said, itching with unbearable curiosity. \"Madam Dai looks thirty at most, and that lad around eighteen. T-There's no reason for her to have a child at eleven or twelve; she wouldn't even have come of age then.\"","Qiao Wangfei looked at Feng Feng. The other insider, wearing a grave expression, seemed lost in thought.","Bai Jianping was immediately displeased. \"Why are you looking at Old Feng? Don't tell me he knows too? You must tell me. There's no reason for me to be the only one left in the dark.\"","Qiao Wangfei let out another sigh. \"Now that he's been found, it should be alright to speak of it. Telling you all is fine. But this matter needs to start from when Hu Bao went to Qiantang...\"","While they were holding their little gathering in the small room, Qin Shaozong had already led the way back to the main courtyard.","Qin Yanzhou, having seen the estate layout plans, knew the importance of this courtyard. He now stopped at the entrance, refusing to enter.","Not hearing footsteps, Qin Shaozong looked back to see him standing motionless before the courtyard gate. \"What are you standing there for? My courtyard doesn't need a wooden post outside.\"","Qiao Wangfei's report had also awakened Nianxia and Bipo. Seeing Dai Li leave with them, the two maids simply got up to prepare, lighting lanterns in the courtyard to await their mistress's return.","Now they had waited, but...","The two maids looked at Qin Yanzhou, both inwardly startled. This man was so dreadfully ugly. How could he be so intimate with the Madam? And the Lord Marquis didn't seem to object either.","From a few steps away, Qin Yanzhou said in a low voice, \"Change courtyards.\"","Qin Shaozong's gaze turned cold. \"She lives here. There is no room for her elsewhere. Matters between elders are not for juniors to interfere in—nor should they.\"","\"This isn't a matter between elders!\" Qin Yanzhou retorted.","Qin Shaozong gave a cold laugh. \"Based on your original age, your father must be younger than I am. My surname is Qin, his surname is Qin. Sharing a surname makes us family. That father of yours, wherever he may be, would still have to call me 'elder brother' to my face, wouldn't he?\"","Qin Yanzhou stared fixedly at the man not far away, hating his own ineloquence.","Back at the Fan residence, Pingwei often mocked him coldly, but he had found it merely irritating then. Because they were all the same—disposable blades in others' hands, living day by day, with today but perhaps no tomorrow.","What was there to argue with those as good as dead? Besides, he lacked the energy to argue...","Now he wanted to argue, but years of silence left him momentarily at a loss for words.","Qin Shaozong was also seething with anger.","This kid had stirred up a heap of trouble, all of which he would have to clean up later—a complete disaster for no reason. That he could let slide; he wasn't incapable of handling it. But the infuriating part was that this kid not only showed no gratitude but also wore an expression of utmost wariness.","What was there to guard against? She had long been his woman.","This talent for provoking anger was truly carved from the same mold as his mother's.","Qin Shaozong suppressed his rage. \"The night is deep and the dew heavy. She isn't wearing much. Staying outside too long will give her a chill. If you keep dawdling, you'll not only need to treat the injury on her foot but also the cold she catches.\"","Having said that, Qin Shaozong turned and walked towards the side chamber.","\"My mother injured her foot? When did that happen?\" This time, Qin Yanzhou followed.","Qin Shaozong said leisurely, \"Not long ago, she heard news of you, hurriedly got out of bed, and accidentally fell to the ground.\"","It was already late at night when ordinary people would be long asleep. To know she fell while getting off the bed implied sharing the same room at the time.","Silence followed, unsurprisingly.","The corners of Qin Shaozong's mouth lifted slightly as he walked ahead.","The side chamber was brightly lit. Nianxia and Bipo now knew this disfigured youth was their mistress's son, and their hearts were utterly astounded.","The two maids stole glances at Qin Yanzhou, unconsciously applying an eight-hundred-fold filter in his favor.","The young master is tall, with an outstanding figure. His eyes and brows resemble the Madam's so closely! His face is more resolute than hers; his nose is very straight, and his mouth is well-shaped too. Apart from those scars, he's actually quite a handsome young man!","Qin Yanzhou placed her on the bed and then straightened up. It was only then he realized Dai Li had been tightly clutching a corner of his robe the whole time.","She held on so tightly her knuckles were white.","Qin Yanzhou paused slightly, then said softly, \"Mom, I'm back.\"","Dai Li showed no reaction, still clutching tightly.","Qin Yanzhou had no choice but to take off his outer robe. After he stepped back, Nianxia stepped forward to take off Dai Li's shoes.","Qin Shaozong instructed the other maid, \"Go to my room, find the low cabinet in the farthest corner, and bring the medicinal wine in the black bottle from the third shelf.\"","Bipo went immediately and soon returned with the item.","Qin Shaozong took the medicinal wine and began shooing people away. \"A grown daughter avoids her father, a grown son avoids his mother. There's nothing for you here. There's another side chamber next door. You, boy, go rest there yourself.\"","Qin Yanzhou stood his ground. \"No need for Your Lordship to condescend.\"","A vein throbbed on Qin Shaozong's forehead. Once again, he found the person before him an eyesore in every way, a complete source of annoyance.","At that moment, the two of them heard a soft gasp of surprise.","It was Nianxia. Upon hearing the words \"medicinal wine,\" she grew worried and had quietly lifted the hem of Daili's skirt to check the injury. One look revealed an ankle that was both red and swollen.","Qin Shaozong stood by the bedside. Glancing sideways, he saw that swollen, flushed section of ankle.","He drew in a deep breath and let it out slowly, then tossed the medicinal wine to Bipo. \"You help the mistress tend to this properly, and check if she's injured anywhere else. If she hasn't woken by nine in the morning, go and fetch Ding Lianxi.\"","Qin Shaozong turned and, passing by Qin Yanzhou, said, \"You, come out as well.\"","This time, Qin Yanzhou did not remain standing where he was."]},{"number":53,"title":"Chapter 53","paragraphs":["Daili faintly remembered having a dream, but upon waking, everything was veiled in a hazy mist, preventing her from seeing clearly the wondrous dream that had brought her such joy the night before.","Lying dazedly on the bed, Daili stared at the canopy overhead, trying to recall fragments of the dream.","Just then, the low murmur of conversation drifted in from outside.","\"I went in to check a moment ago; the Madam hasn't woken yet. It's almost si-shi (9-11 AM). In a moment, I'll go to Mr. Ding's place and invite him over.\"","\"Should we inform the Marquis?\"","\"Not yet. Let's wait until after Mr. Ding has examined her. By the way, the young master truly is the Madam's son. Between you and me, I thought last night that if it weren't for the scars on his face, the young master would surely be exceptionally handsome.\"","Daili jolted with a start, all drowsiness instantly vanishing. She immediately sat up. With her movement, something slid from the bedside onto the footstool below.","Daili turned her head and saw it was a black outer robe.","Unlike the kind Qin Shaozong wore with silver-trimmed cuffs, this robe was very ordinary, made of the most common linen. Such garments usually never appeared in her room.","It wasn't a dream. Zhouzhou had returned!","Daili hurriedly got out of bed, but her first step made her gasp sharply in pain. Losing her balance, she fell to the floor with a thud.","The conversation outside ceased, and Nianxia and Bipo hurried in at the sound.","\"Madam!\" The two quickly helped Daili up.","\"Please be careful. Your left foot is badly injured; you must take care with it these next few days.\"","Gripping their arms, Daili asked with a touch of nervous intensity, \"Has my son returned?\"","\"Of course. The young master is outside; he's been out there since early morning,\" Nianxia nodded.","Daili suddenly relaxed. \"I'd like to wash up. Thank you for your trouble.\"","\"Madam, you're always so polite with us servants,\" Bipo said with a light laugh.","Once she was properly dressed and presentable, the door opened.","Bright, warm sunlight streamed into the room, seeming to dispel all shadows.","Bathed in the sunlight, Daili saw a tall, slender figure standing as straight as a pine tree outside the door. She was about to call him in when her gaze fell upon him, and she couldn't help but pause in surprise.","The young man's face was as fair as jade, radiant and glowing. His features were particularly striking, with eyes that were the quintessential peach-blossom shape—their contours like peach petals blooming in spring, the upper lids layered, arching up slightly at the outer corners like fine brushwork in a painting, bearing the same exquisite beauty as his birth mother.","The horrifying \"fleshy worms\" were gone from his cheeks. His skin was smooth, flawless, and pale, glowing softly in the sunlight.","Qin Yanzhou had changed into a moon-white brocade robe with distinctive ink-black piping at the cuffs. Not yet of age to wear a guan cap, his jet-black hair was simply tied back at the nape of his neck with a ribbon.","Now, looking at him, he was completely different from the man of last night.","If the Qin Yanzhou of last night had been an ugly, plain-clad assassin—a cold blade casually thrust into the mud—then the present him was like jade immersed in a hot spring, the very image of a handsome, wealthy young master from a privileged family, seemingly untouched by the hardships of the world.","He seemed somewhat unused to such attire, and under Daili's unwavering gaze, he grew a little shy, murmuring softly, \"Good morning, Mother.\"","The cruel river of time began to flow backward. Daili felt as if she had returned to the beginning, before everything had happened.","Her nine-year-old child, woken by her each day, would rub his eyes and, as if about to fall back asleep at any moment, say to her, \"Good morning, Mother.\"","Years had passed. A different place, a different time, but the same—yet not entirely the same—person stood before her once more.","\"Good morning, Zhouzhou.\" A mistiness rose in Daili's eyes as she remembered the two scars on his neck.","If the ones visible were so dreadful, what of the unseen ones? How many more were there that she couldn't see? Her child had suffered untold hardships in places she could not see...","Daili lowered her head, breathing rapidly twice, yet still feeling an unbearable tightness, as if an invisible rope were tightening around her own neck.","Seeing her lower her head to wipe her eyes, Qin Yanzhou quickly took two steps forward. He wanted to say something but momentarily didn't know where to begin, leaving him somewhat flustered and at a loss.","Sensing his distress, Daili struggled to push aside the suffocating grief and looked up, beckoning him. \"Come, sit down. Have you had breakfast yet?\"","Qin Yanzhou sat down opposite her, sweeping his robe aside. \"Not yet.\"","\"Then have it here with me.\" Looking at his now-unblemished face, the sorrow in Daili's heart lightened somewhat. Yet, this relief was mingled with a thread of unease she couldn't quite name.","\"Zhouzhou, I heard you were adopted by Fan of Yanzhou many years ago. Exactly how many years ago was that?\" Daili felt inexplicably uneasy.","She had learned about Fan of Yanzhou adopting her son last night while listening to Qiao Wangfei's report. The exact words were: \"This person claims he was adopted by Fan of Yanzhou many years ago and renamed Quanjie.\"","The name \"Quanjie\" was a thorn in Daili's heart. Whoever gave her son that name was dismissive and full of malice, not regarding him as human at all.","Qin Yanzhou was silent for a moment. \"Seven years ago.\"","Daili's breath hitched slightly.","Seven years. It was actually seven years.","In that moment, Daili suddenly understood the source of that earlier thread of unease.","The timelines didn't match.","Nianxia and Bipo had gone to the kitchen to fetch breakfast, leaving only Daili and her son in the room.","Today there was no rain or gloom; the sky was clear and the air fresh. The morning summer sun was warm—a rare, fine day. Yet Daili felt inexplicably cold in her hands and feet, and the ankle she had injured last night began to throb with a needle-like pain.","\"Zhouzhou, tell Mother the truth. Before you went to the Fan residence, where else were you?\" Daili's tone was urgent.","It wasn't ten years ago.","It was seven years. Her son had only gone to Fan of Yanzhou seven years ago. This meant that before being adopted by the Fan family, he had spent three years somewhere else.","And nine years ago, this region had experienced a great famine. Its reach was vast, affecting not only the central plains and the north but also causing significant disruption in the south.","Ten years ago, Old Man Sun had seen her son standing by the riverbank in Qiantang, meaning Zhouzhou was in Qiantang at that time. Travel in ancient times was extremely difficult; a commoner might take nearly half a month to cover a hundred li.","Long journeys were nearly impossible, let alone for Zhouzhou, who at the time had no travel permits and no family by his side—he was essentially a person without status.","She suspected that when the famine struck, Zhouzhou likely hadn't managed to escape the disaster zone. In that great calamity where selling children and even exchanging children to eat were commonplace, who had taken him in?","\"By a twist of fate, I was adopted by a kind, wealthy family. They lived deep in the mountains, isolated from the world, with their own fertile land providing grain. They had substantial stored provisions, so taking in one more mouth was easily manageable,\" Qin Yanzhou said, lowering his gaze to avoid Daili's eyes.","Daili's expression softened slightly. \"The disguise on your face... was that also taught to you by that wealthy family?\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded. \"That wealthy family had two young masters around my age who were particularly fond of studying all sorts of esoteric arts and secret techniques. They said my face was too striking and would be inconvenient when traveling, so they taught me a method of disguise. After the famine passed, I posed as a servant and traveled around various regions with a branch of that wealthy family. Unfortunately, one day we encountered bandits on the road. I fell into a river and was swept away, becoming separated from them. Later, I was unexpectedly rescued by Fan of Yanzhou, who took me in as his adopted son.\"","After saying this, Qin Yanzhou added, \"I do have some scars on my body, but those were all from before that family took me in. Life wasn't so difficult after I met them.\"","Daili felt something was a bit off and was about to ask more when, after her son finished speaking, he immediately asked her, \"Mom, why are you in the northern army? What is your relationship with Qin Shaozong?\"","Daili instantly froze. \"...That's a long story, not something that can be explained clearly in a short while.\"","Qin Yanzhou sat quietly, looking all ears.","Just then, however, Nianxia and Bipo returned.","The two maids brought in the morning meal. Previously, while idle in the residence, Daili had improved the era's stone mill to satisfy her own culinary cravings.","The stone mill at this time was in the mid-stage of its development. The pattern of its grinding teeth was a radially partitioned diagonal design, which was more efficient than earlier versions but still considerably inferior to the later eight-zone diagonal design.","The improvement of the stone mill most significantly affected wheat. Because even after hulling, wheat grains remained coarse; even when cooked, they felt rough and scratchy in the throat.","This was also why soft, smooth, and exquisite-tasting millet rice was favored by noble families and the wealthy, a symbol of affluence.","Those who ate wheat meals were mostly commoners with limited means or the thousands of soldiers in the army, to keep military expenses as low as possible.","But if wheat grains were ground into fine wheat flour, its texture would improve tremendously. Furthermore, it could give rise to things like steamed buns and noodles.","What Bipo and Nianxia were serving now was noodle soup. Not the common soup with dough strips of this era, but soup noodles improved by Daili's hand, identical to those of later generations.","Thin, white noodles, topped with shredded meat and an egg, sprinkled with a small handful of chopped green onions, and floating with a couple of drops of golden oil.","A very ordinary bowl of noodles in modern times, perhaps costing less than ten dollars, found everywhere on streets and alleys, yet Qin Yanzhou gazed at it for a long time.","Some memories are like old photographs. Even if you take them out to look at again and again, over time, the corners become frayed and curled from handling, and the images grow blurry.","A small bowl of noodle soup, seen again now, felt like a lifetime apart.","After looking at the noodles, he raised his head to look at Daili across from him, as if confirming she was still there. Only then did Qin Yanzhou begin to eat.","He ate very slowly, chewing carefully, as if trying to completely recapture the feeling from ten years ago, to erase all the hardships and struggles in between.","Neither mother nor son spoke, yet the atmosphere wasn't the least bit stiff.","After the morning meal, maidservants came in to clear away the bowls and chopsticks.","The cooling-off period during breakfast had allowed Daili to figure out how to explain things to her son.","She took the initiative and began from the beginning. \"Zhouzhou, I arrived here via the river six months after the school bus fell into the water. I haven't been here long—less than four months. When I first arrived, I accidentally ran into Qin Shaozong. He hadn't taken Yingjun yet at that time and happened to need a woman to help him put on a show to deceive the salt smuggler's underlings. I wasn't affiliated with any faction, so he chose me, and I used his resources to look for you.\"","She paused, then continued, \"The 'salty stone' popular across the provinces is a formula I gave him. Qin Shaozong and I have a cooperative relationship.\"","As for the twists and turns in between—how she escaped to Taipingjun, how he caught her and brought her back, and the one-year agreement between her and Qin Shaozong—Daili felt there was absolutely no need for her son to know.","Zhouzhou had suffered enough these years; he didn't need any additional burdens.","\"Mom, do you want to leave this place? If you do, I can make arrangements for you,\" Qin Yanzhou suddenly said.","Daili's heart skipped a beat.","Arrangements?","How could Zhouzhou make arrangements? Did he have the capability to do so?"]},{"number":54,"title":"Chapter 54","paragraphs":["Perhaps one shouldn't speak of others behind their backs. No sooner had she finished speaking of Qin Shaozong than Daili heard the greeting voices of the two maidservants outside.","Daili swallowed the words that had reached her throat.","Soon, that burly figure walked in from outside, blocking a large swath of sunlight as he entered.","Qin Shaozong was not surprised to find Qin Yanzhou here. However, upon seeing the young man's face, the man raised his long brows, his gaze traveling from his temples all the way down to the tip of his chin.","His eyes and brows looked exactly like hers, but his nose, mouth, and jawline weren't very similar—probably taking after his blind, good-for-nothing biological father.","Hmph, her taste wasn't that great either. Any moderately good-looking man could have fooled her.","His gaze shifted back to the young man's eyes and brows. Qin Shaozong gave a slight nod. \"Now this looks like the son of the Lady.\"","\"What do you mean 'looks like'? He is my son,\" Daili said discontentedly, then asked him, \"Why has the Marquis come?\"","The long desk in the room was not a square table; only the two opposing long sides could be seated at. Daili and Qin Yanzhou already occupied one side each.","Without any sense of being an outsider, Qin Shaozong walked over to Daili's side, sat down next to her, close by. \"Can't I come if I have nothing else to do?\"","Daili: \"...\"","The air pressure around Qin Yanzhou dropped noticeably.","Acting as if he saw nothing of the person opposite, Qin Shaozong noticed a teapot on the desk, reached out to pour himself some tea. \"However, I do have important business for coming this time.\"","Qin Shaozong lifted his eyes to look at the young man across the desk, his tone indifferent. \"I have words to speak with your mother. You, lad, go outside and amuse yourself for now.\"","Qin Yanzhou did not move.","One breath, two breaths...","The atmosphere gradually solidified, shifting from a warm spring day to a deep autumn with chilly winds. Daili suddenly became aware of an important, weighing problem.","Although the North and Yanzhou are now implicitly opposed, with a major conflict ready to erupt at any moment, what if...?","What if Fan of Yanzhou, fearing the combined might of the two regions, turns to offer them submission? What if he pushes forward one person, claiming that this person alone spread deceitful words that ruined the peace, and then beheads that person as a public example, all to achieve the goal of sacrificing a pawn to save the king?","That series of maneuvers could very well turn conflict into harmony. The three forces could end up all friendly with each other, turn their spears around, and jointly crusade against the Qinglian Sect.","That absolutely cannot happen. She cannot accept the person who abused her son for years escaping unscathed. She wants him to pay the price, she wants him dead!","But she is weak and alone. To deal with Fan of Yanzhou, she can only borrow Qin Shaozong's hand. Before that, she cannot have a falling out with him.","On the other hand, however, Daili also understood very well that even though she had omitted much, Zhou Zhou was no longer a child. And given Qin Shaozong's domineering nature, it was entirely possible that last night, after she had fainted, that fellow had said everything he should and shouldn't have.","Her son had just been found. She didn't want him to be unhappy.","Before Daili could figure out how to balance these concerns, the young man, seeming to sense her dilemma, stood up. \"Mother, I will wait for you outside. You may call for me at any time.\"","A bitter ache welled up in Daili's heart.","Her son had become perceptive, yet she dared not think about what experiences had forced him to learn to read others' expressions.","After he left, Qin Shaozong placed the teapot on the charcoal stand. The pottery colliding with the stand made a light clink, like the toll of a bell, bringing Daili back to her senses.","A seat was now empty opposite, but Qin Shaozong showed no intention of moving. He said lazily, \"Does the Lady know of your son's experiences these past years?\"","Daili said hesitantly, \"I know little. Only that he went to Fan of Yanzhou seven years ago to eke out a living.\"","Qin Shaozong gave an acknowledging \"Hmm,\" then told her about the Fan family's background. He started from the family's rise, briefly touched upon Fan Tianshi, \"...Fan Tianshi particularly loves collecting orphans. The vast majority are taken in around eleven or twelve years old. During that time, he employs a mix of kindness and severity, training those still immature orphans into dogs who obey only him. Later, he orders them east and they go east, tells them to kill someone and they kill. If any die accidentally along the way, they're wrapped in a straw mat and tossed into a mass grave, or simply fed to the wolves in his estate.\"","They were all rootless driftwood anyway. Dead was dead. No one cared, and no one would seek justice for them.","Daili began to tremble. She clenched her hands tightly into fists, her nails digging into her soft palms, leaving deep crescent marks.","Qin Shaozong then brought up another matter. \"Two nights ago, someone attacked the estate in the middle of the night. The leader was precisely your son.\"","Daili gasped aloud, belated fear drowning her.","Zhou Zhou hadn't mentioned it earlier, and she hadn't connected the two events. Qin Shaozong was powerful; countless people wanted him dead. How could she have guessed the leader in black that night was her son?","That night, Qin Shaozong said of the attackers, one was captured alive, two escaped. He didn't say how many were killed, which meant aside from those three, all other assassins had been cut down.","Zhou Zhou was one of the two who escaped.","If that night he had been a moment slower to react, or hadn't gotten away, then today would never have happened. One could guess that her son must have only learned yesterday about the search for him in the North. Otherwise, he would have come directly to her two nights ago.","Just a little bit... just a little bit more and they would have been separated by life and death once again...","A scorching large hand reached over then, enveloping her icy, trembling one, then gently pried open her clenched fist. \"Lady, the past cannot be chased, and don't dwell on hypotheticals of what didn't happen.\"","Daili bit her lip hard. \"I know. But I can't help it.\"","She couldn't help but speculate about things that hadn't happened and things that had. Regret, heartache, hatred, self-blame—these emotions merged into a venomous snake, constantly gnawing away at her sanity.","Daili knew her mind wasn't quite right anymore.","From the moment she heard about the school bus plunging into the river, and from the moment she saw her son covered in scars, she could never go back to how she was before.","The former truly cannot be chased... but the latter...","Fan Tianshi must die. If this man doesn't die, it will be hard to dispel the hatred in her heart!","\"Fan Tianshi has adopted many sworn sons, but over the years they've died or been crippled. The only ones still in use are your son and one other.\" Objectively speaking, Qin Shaozong thought the lad's ability to endure until today truly deserved the praise of having exceptional fortitude, as well as being tough as nails.","Qin Shaozong continued unhurriedly, \"The initial training lasts at most two years. That means starting around age fourteen, your son began handling tasks for that Fan fellow. From small things like spreading rumors and petty theft, to major things like infiltrating the estate two nights ago... and killing.\"","He emphasized the last two words slightly and, as expected, saw her jolt violently, her face turning even paler.","Although she hadn't stated it explicitly, Qin Shaozong guessed from various details that \"Peach Blossom Spring\" was most likely an exceptionally peaceful place.","\"How many hands do you think it would take to count the enemies your son has made in recent years?\"","Qin Shaozong gently pinched her fingertips, then slid his long fingers between hers. \"Those enemies, some are from minor families, not worth fearing, but there are also those with great power and influence. From what I know, one is the Governor of Qingzhou. Nangong Xiong mentioned to me at a banquet that the tribute sent from Qingzhou to the imperial court was robbed. He suspects the bandit is your son. Nangong Xiong is not one to make baseless accusations. If he says so, he must have some clues or evidence.\"","Daili's pupils trembled. She opened her mouth, but her throat felt as if stuffed with straw, leaving her momentarily speechless.","It was only on the second attempt that she found her voice. \"You told me before that if my son were found, you would treat him as a true son of the Qin family.\"","\"Indeed.\" He uttered these two words without hesitation.","Daili was taken aback, unable to discern what this man was truly scheming.","\"I will clean up all the messes your son has caused. But in return, I want you, Madam, to stay by my side forever.\" He laid his cards on the table.","For some reason, at this moment, Daili felt no sense of being controlled or threatened. She inexplicably recalled a moment earlier—","Zhou Zhou had asked her if she wanted to leave. If so, he could help arrange it.","His words had shaken her heart at the time. She had immediately wanted to ask, Zhou Zhou, how could you arrange it? Do you really have that capability?","Qin Shaozong was immensely powerful, practically holding sway over the entire northern region, where no one could rival him. As for other regions where forces might contend with him, perhaps they existed, but they would never go to such lengths for a mere woman.","Furthermore, if her son possessed such ability, why hadn't he left the Fan family, instead staying there for a full seven years?","One puzzle after another enveloped Daili, leaving her mind in turmoil.","After a long silence, Qin Shaozong stroked the inside of her wrist with his thumb. \"How is Madam's consideration?\"","Having achieved his present status, Qin Shaozong was certainly not the type to give silently without expecting anything in return.","Taking on all the dirty and difficult work, only to shrink back like a turtle when it came time for rewards, not making a sound even when prodded—that was not his style.","That young man's heap of troubles was now unavoidable. Since that was the case, why not use this opportunity to advance his position with her?","After all, if that boy weren't her son, he wouldn't care if he were chased down and hacked into eight pieces or continued being a dog for Fan Tianshi.","A sudden flash of insight struck Daili. She quickly lowered her eyelids to conceal the strange glint in her eyes.","After pretending to ponder for a moment, she spoke hesitantly, \"Forever is too long. You men are notorious for growing tired of the old and favoring the new. When you no longer fancy me, wouldn't I be trapped in a tiny courtyard, with nothing to do but prune flowers and feed fish? I might even prune the branches bare and overfeed the fish to death without ever seeing you again.\"","\"Won't.\" He said only these two words.","As for what exactly \"won't\" meant, Qin Shaozong did not elaborate.","Regardless of his response, Daili followed with this line, \"Regarding this matter, I hope Your Lordship will grant me some time to consider.\"","Seeing her somewhat troubled yet submissive expression, Qin Shaozong found her demeanor vaguely familiar, as if he had seen it somewhere before.","But at this moment, his attention was captured by the half-hidden compromise in her words. \"Very well. I shall give Madam five days.\"","Daili bargained with him, \"Five days is not enough. My son has just been found. Simply recounting the events of these past years will take a long time. How about a month? I will give you my answer in a month.\"","Fearing he wouldn't agree, Daili also mentioned the impending war. \"With the battle approaching, Your Lordship must be quite busy lately. Whether it's five days or a month makes little difference to you.\"","Qin Shaozong lowered his gaze, looking into those captivating eyes. Her features were exceptionally exquisite. Now, a lingering mistiness veiled her eyes, reminiscent of wind, flowers, snow, and moon, or even more like spring waters by the riverbank, possessing an indescribable charm.","\"Agreed.\" In a moment of distraction, Qin Shaozong heard himself consent once more.","Having gained his assent, Daili immediately brought up another matter. \"When Commandant Mo returns, will Your Lordship wage war against Yanzhou?\"","The water in the small kettle beside them boiled, steam billowing from its spout, much like the seething resentment churning in Daili's chest at that moment.","Qin Shaozong picked up a teacup and took a small sip, his face betraying no emotion. \"That depends on the circumstances.\"","Daili understood his meaning.","His southward expedition was primarily to suppress the Qinglian Sect. If Yanzhou was truly entangled with the Qinglian Sect, he would deal with them as well. But if the other side showed sense and willingly submitted, the matter might be postponed.","Breaking two chopsticks one by one is easier than breaking them together.","But Daili didn't want to wait a moment longer. She fanned the flames, \"Your Lordship, Yanzhou sent assassins to infiltrate your residence and later framed Qingzhou for it. All this shows that this Fan of Yanzhou harbors wolfish ambitions and is determined to shatter the alliance between the North and Qingzhou. If we let this go unchecked, or turn a blind eye and downplay a major incident, who knows if Yanzhou might suddenly strike when our three forces jointly attack the Qinglian Sect? If trouble arises from within, and they secretly collaborate with the Qinglian Sect from inside and out, this campaign could end in complete defeat.\"","Qin Shaozong turned to look at her, his gaze amused, yet he said, \"Madam has quite a sharp tongue.\"","Neither looked away. His brown eyes were steady and inscrutable, while her black ones were resolute and growing sharper.","\"I admit I have personal motives. I can't wait to slaughter all those who abused my son.\"","Mid-sentence, Daili changed her form of address, \"But, my Lord, ultimately, I am your advisor. Do you not think what I just said is correct? If Mr. Nalan knew that Fan of Yanzhou sent men to raid the residence at night, wouldn't he advise you to deal with Yanzhou first? I believe he would.\"","She made no attempt to conceal her intent. It was unnecessary. Her conflict with Fan Tianshi was a fight to the death. Since the hatred could no longer be hidden, why add superfluous gestures?","Daili tried to pull her hand back, but the large, darker hand held it tightly; she couldn't retrieve it.","\"Your Lordship, Mr. Nalan requests your presence in the study.\" A voice came from outside.","Daili recognized it as Qiao Wangfei's voice, and she curved her lips slightly.","What had she just said? If Mr. Nalan knew about Yanzhou's night raid, he would surely come to advise. See, here he comes!","Qin Shaozong looked at her upturned lips, as if seeing her fluffy fox tail beginning to swish again.","The man chuckled softly. \"Madam's foresight is remarkable.\"","Qin Yanzhou stood several steps away from the door. Qiao Wangfei had seen him when he came to report.","At first glance, Qiao Wangfei almost didn't recognize him.","His clothes were changed, the frightening scar on his face was gone, his demeanor seemed much calmer—the man was completely transformed.","Before Qiao Wangfei could observe further, his superior emerged from the room.","Qin Yanzhou saw Qin Shaozong come out and walked straight past him into the house without a glance.","Inside, Daili, who had injured her foot, was still sitting in the same spot. When her son entered, she asked in a low voice, \"Zhou Zhou, has he left the courtyard?\"","Upon hearing this, Qin Yanzhou stepped back to the main doorway and looked towards the courtyard entrance. It was now empty; the two figures from moments ago had already departed.","He nodded to Daili.","Daili beckoned him over to sit down and, as if exchanging a secret code, lowered her voice even further: \"You asked earlier if I wanted to leave. Of course I do. But now is not the time yet. We still have to wait.\"","A hint of confusion appeared in Qin Yanzhou's eyes. \"Wait for what?\"","Daili smiled. \"Naturally, we wait for Qin Shaozong to clean up the loose ends for you. Fan Tianshi must die, and so must all the enemies you've made over these years. These matters need to be dealt with as thoroughly as possible. Once it's done, then we'll leave.\"","That one-year agreement, those promises of forever... Now that she had found her son, she was done playing the game. She was ready to flip the table."]},{"number":55,"title":"Chapter 55","paragraphs":["Yanzhou, Gaoling County, within the study of the Fan Manor.","\"...What? Quanjie has betrayed us?!\"","Fan Tianshi abruptly rose from his seat, his gaze fixed intently on Wang Jiang, who knelt before him.","The man in a blue robe sitting beside the low table frowned.","Wang Jiang kept his head bowed as he replied, \"Yes, my lord. That night, everything was proceeding smoothly at first. We had infiltrated the Qin residence and even entered one target's chamber. But just as we were about to strike, Quanjie suddenly killed two of our own men. No one anticipated he would act this way. Not only did it throw our formation into disarray, but it also woke the northern general sleeping inside.\"","\"What happened next? What was the outcome?\" the eldest son, Fan Boliang, pressed.","Wang Jiang remained with his head lowered. \"The alarm was raised, making it impossible to complete the mission. Naturally, we had to retreat immediately and wait for a better opportunity later. However, with Quanjie having just killed two men in front and northern guards swarming in from behind, escape was extremely difficult. Aside from your humble servant, none of the others managed to get out.\"","As if to prove the truth of his words, Wang Jiang removed his outer robe, revealing a bandage of coarse cloth wrapped from his left shoulder blade down his arm, already stained a deep red with blood. Judging by the area covered, the wound was not small.","Seeming to fear their disbelief, Wang Jiang then unwrapped the bandage on the spot to show them the injury beneath.","The wound was long, the flesh mangled and bloody.","Fan Boliang drew a sharp breath, unsure whether he was startled by the gruesome injury or shocked by the confirmation of Quanjie's betrayal.","Fan Tianshi's expression was grim. \"Was anyone captured alive by the northerners?\"","\"I do not know, my lord. However, if there were, they would have followed your previous instructions and pinned everything on Qingzhou,\" Wang Jiang whispered.","Fan Tianshi pinched the bridge of his nose. \"I am aware of the situation now. You may go and tend to your wound. For the time being, do not speak of Quanjie's defection. I will make the necessary arrangements.\"","Wang Jiang received the order and withdrew.","After he left, Fan Boliang looked at the two men in the room. \"Father, Mr. Shi, do you find Wang Jiang's account credible? Where could Quanjie possibly go after leaving our Fan Manor? Who would dare take in such a stray dog? Once we publicly declare that Quanjie has turned traitor, his enemies will come hunting for him within a day. Even if he had nine lives, it wouldn't be enough.\"","Fan Tianshi rotated the thumb ring on his hand, remaining silent.","Shi Wuji said, \"We have too little information. It's difficult to say at this point.\"","Fan Boliang speculated, \"Could it be that the mission failed, Quanjie also died, and Wang Jiang fabricated this story to shift the blame?\"","\"That is certainly possible. This matter requires thorough investigation,\" Fan Tianshi said, his eyes revealing a terrifying malice. \"If Quanjie has truly betrayed his master, I will make him long for death more than life.\"","...","\"Has Quanjie still not returned?\" Fan Muqi peeked into the small courtyard.","Ping Wei was so consumed by jealousy he felt sick. On the third day after Quanjie's departure, the Eighth Miss had come asking if he was back. She had asked every single day since. Sometimes she sent a maidservant, other times she came in person, even going so far as to sit for a while in Quanjie's room. It was clearly the infatuation of a young maiden, utterly besotted.","He couldn't understand it. They were all sons taken in by their foster father.","In terms of seniority, he had been with the Fan family a few months longer than Quanjie. In terms of looks, he was undoubtedly far more handsome than the disfigured Quanjie. In terms of personality, he was much more interesting than that wooden block.","Why did Quanjie get to win the Eighth Miss's favor!","\"He hasn't returned,\" Ping Wei said, trying his best to sound calm.","Fan Muqi pouted. \"Where has Quanjie gone? What is he doing now?\"","Ping Wei maintained a smile. \"My apologies, Eighth Miss. It's not that I don't wish to tell you, but the rules forbid it. Our missions are confidential. No one knows except Foster Father himself.\"","\"Then I'll go ask Father,\" Fan Muqi declared before turning and leaving without a backward glance.","The gold and jade hairpins in the young lady's hair cast scattered golden reflections on the ground, much like the brilliant, fragmented thoughts of a maiden's heart.","As the most doted-upon daughter, Fan Muqi enjoyed many privileges. For instance, while others needed repeated announcements to see Fan Tianshi, she did not. She only needed to call out from near the doorway, and as long as Fan Tianshi wasn't occupied with urgent matters, eight or nine times out of ten, she would be allowed in.","Today, after Fan Muqi called out for her father outside the door, it took much longer than usual for a response to come from within.","The news of Quanjie's betrayal had filled Fan Tianshi with fury. He had struggled for a long time to compose himself, to ensure he wouldn't meet his daughter while seething with anger. Yet, the moment his most beloved legitimate daughter entered, she asked:","\"Father, where have you sent Quanjie?\"","The question ignited the smoldering sparks of his rage, as if dousing them with a bucket of oil.","Fan Tianshi rebuked her sharply. \"Chasing after a lowly slave all day long, Little Eight, look at yourself! What kind of state are you in? Have you no dignity befitting a noble young lady? This is utterly ridiculous and brings shame upon our Fan family!\"","Fan Muqi was stunned by the scolding.","As a legitimate daughter, and the one most favored by her father, her family had always indulged her excessively, granting her every whim. If she fancied a dress or a piece of jewelry, it would be delivered to her room the very next day.","In fifteen years, this was the first time her father had ever erupted in anger at her.","It wasn't as if she wanted to marry Quanjie. She just wanted him by her side always. How could that possibly shame the Fan family?","Tears instantly welled up in Fan Muqi's eyes. The words spilled out: \"Father, I just like his appearance. I know I'll have to enter a political marriage eventually. For now, I just want to look at him a little more. Is that not allowed either?\"","Fan Tianshi narrowed his eyes. \"You like his appearance?\"","Fan Muqi belatedly realized her slip of the tongue and fell into a flustered silence.","\"What appearance could a disfigured boy possibly have that you would like?\" Fan Tianshi demanded.","Seven years ago, Quanjie had dragged his broken leg to the Fan Manor, kowtowing at the main gate, begging for mercy. Even then, large scars already marred both his cheeks.","Initially, possessing nothing, he naturally had no mask to hide his ugliness. It was only later, as he gradually distinguished himself from the crowd of orphans, rising step by step, that he earned special treatment.","He gained the privilege of living in a less crowded courtyard annex and could possess some inconsequential items, like a ghost mask.","Seeing his daughter remain silent, Fan Tianshi reprimanded her again: \"Tell me the truth! If you dare conceal even a fraction of it, you will not set foot outside your courtyard until the day you marry. And when Quanjie returns, I will have him killed immediately.\"","\"No!\" Fan Muqi reacted violently.","Fan Tianshi said no more, merely watching her with a cold gaze.","Raised in the lap of luxury and merely an unmarried young lady, Fan Muqi couldn't withstand such a stern, authoritative stare. She slowly lowered her head. \"Quanjie isn't ugly at all. No one is more handsome than him. The scars on his face... they're fake.\"","She had discovered this by accident.","That day, she had gone on a spring outing outside the city walls with a young lady from the Li family. Third Miss Li told her she had stumbled upon a treasure of a place. So, she followed her up the mountain, entered a cave, and walked through a not-so-short mountain path.","Beyond the cave was an open grassland, lush with grass and alive with birdsong, featuring a beautiful small pond at its center.","And it was there that she saw Quanjie.","The Fan Manor had many servants, so it was natural that she couldn't remember every single one. However, Quanjie's demon mask was very distinctive, and she had coincidentally seen him just the day before. Therefore, she immediately recognized the handsome young man with the demon mask hanging at his waist as her father's adopted son.","The shock and admiration she felt at the time need not be elaborated on. Afterwards, Quanjie begged her not to speak of it, and she agreed.","Later, she figured out the reason on her own: Quanjie was most likely hiding his true appearance to avoid attracting the attention of powerful nobles who had a penchant for keeping catamites.","She had once promised him to keep his secret forever. It was only now, with her father threatening his life, that she was forced to reveal the truth. Quanjie probably wouldn't blame her.","With her head bowed, Fan Muqi did not see the drastic change in her father's expression—a mix of shock and fury.","\"Outrageous! Why didn't you tell me about such an important matter sooner?\" Fan Tianshi's face darkened like a storm cloud, terrifyingly grim.","Fan Muqi was completely taken aback. She had confessed everything, yet her father was even more enraged than before.","\"Father, I...\"","Slap. He couldn't restrain himself from striking her across the face.","\"Now, get out this instant!\" Fan Tianshi was furious beyond measure; he had nothing more to say to this foolish daughter.","Fan Muqi ran off in tears.","Fan Tianshi took a deep breath and said to the servants outside, \"Go and ask the Eldest Young Master and Master Shi to come here.\"","Earlier, his eldest son had questioned whether Wang Jiang was lying. Now it seemed that was no lie at all. This Quanjie clearly had major problems.","Over the past three years, Quanjie had become the most useful blade in his arsenal. He had looked at this blade no less than a hundred, if not a thousand times, yet he had never detected the disguise on his face.","Such a masterful disguise was not something a minor family could possess. Quanjie was undoubtedly a spy!","For seven years, a major faction had planted a nail in his household. Well done! They were truly patient, ruthless, and willing to sacrifice, even going so far as to deliberately break a leg to beg at his door.","The hunter who hunts geese all day long finally gets pecked in the eye by one.","Fan Tianshi was so angry he felt dizzy, his vision darkening, and a faint chill even seemed to spread from the back of his head.","Just then, Shi Wuji and Fan Boliang arrived.","Shi Wuji bowed with clasped hands, \"My lord, for what matter have you summoned me?\"","Seeing his father's dark expression, Fan Boliang's heart sank. Sure enough, the next moment he heard him say, \"Quanjie is a spy planted in my household by another faction. What capability, to have lurked for a full seven years.\"","Fan Tianshi then told them about the disguise on Quanjie's face.","Both men were astonished.","Fan Boliang found it hard to believe: \"The scars were fake? All these years, I never noticed.\"","Shi Wuji asked, \"Do you know who is behind him?\"","\"I do not,\" Fan Tianshi took a deep breath. \"But this style seems familiar to me. Do you remember the incident in Bingzhou a year ago? That General Kuang under Rong Bingzhou was actually Qin Shaozong's man. He lurked by Lord Rong's side for seven years, going through fire and water, doing everything possible... Hah, also a spy, also seven years.\"","Shi Wuji seemed thoughtful.","Fan Boliang murmured, \"So it's Qin Shaozong? The possibility is indeed high. Such exquisite disguise techniques must come from a place with deep foundations, and the Qin family fits the bill perfectly!\"","Shi Wuji then spoke up, \"My lord, there is something odd about this. Why would he expose himself now? On the night of the assassination, Quanjie could have collaborated with the northern forces from within, capturing everyone in one fell swoop. Then he could have returned alone to continue his infiltration, waiting to turn traitor at the most critical moment.\"","\"Perhaps Wang Jiang was just lucky. Their inside-outside collaboration failed, leaving one fish that escaped the net. His early exposure now might be a last resort,\" Fan Boliang said through gritted teeth.","\"Aside from the escaped target, could Quanjie's reason for withdrawing also be...\" Shi Wuji said gravely, \"That he learned the person living in the West Tower was Li Zan, and that he discovered that matter.\"","Fan Tianshi's pupils constricted for a moment. \"Impossible! I never sent Quanjie to contact those people. He absolutely could not know.\"","His words fell, and silence flooded the study, broken only by the sound of a few rapid, uneasy breaths.","\"Regardless, we must take immediate action to minimize the fallout from Quanjie's betrayal. My lord, didn't Eighth Miss say she has seen his true face? Have her describe his appearance to a portrait artist. We should first issue public wanted posters far and wide, stating that Quanjie has betrayed his master and fled east with valuable treasures, offering a heavy reward for his head. In short, we must let the world and Quanjie's past enemies know that he is now a thorn in your side, someone you wish to eliminate at all costs,\" Shi Wuji said coldly.","\"Furthermore, order the covert agents to take the portrait to Guoyun County for investigation. There was the prior incident of infiltrating the Qin residence, and Quanjie parted ways with Wang Jiang in Guoyun County. If he truly is Qin Shaozong's man, he will most likely linger in Guoyun County for a while. Stationing people there to watch might lead us to him.\"","Without the Fan Manor's protection, with his true face widely exposed, if he is not Qin Shaozong's man, jackals will surely catch his scent and hunt him down everywhere.","Shi Wuji stroked his beard. \"Finally, I believe we now need to screen everyone in the manor, especially those close to Quanjie. I have a feeling Quanjie wouldn't be the only spy; there might be other agents hidden within the household.\"","He paused, then added a final remark. \"If Quanjie is indeed Qin Shaozong's man, the situation will develop in the worst possible direction. I believe, my lord, you should then take the initiative to contact Mr. Diting.\"","Listening to each point, Fan Tianshi's expression finally improved somewhat. \"Liuxian's words are most apt.\"","The Fan Manor launched a thunderous investigation.","And indeed, they discovered some things. For instance, a gatekeeper surnamed Zhang had left the manor this morning and never returned.","According to those below, this person was considered relatively close to Quanjie within the manor.","Qingzhou, Guoyun County.","\"...Therefore, my lord, I believe Yanzhou cannot be trusted.\" Nalan Zhi bowed to Qin Shaozong. \"One must pacify internal affairs before resisting external threats. I beg you, my lord, to first address the issue in Yanzhou.\"","\"Your advice is sound. The matter of the Green Lotus Sect can be set aside for now.\" Qin Shaozong then turned to Kuang Ye. \"Kuang Ye, you have always been meticulous. Go investigate how many enemies that lad Qin Yanzhou has made over the years.\"","Everyone in the study was shocked by these words.","He hadn't given this order privately but stated it publicly. Moreover, judging by the lord's tone, it wasn't merely an investigation.","Kuang Ye came from a scout background and was later trained as a sleeper agent, serving for seven years. No one understood the intricacies of that work better than he did.","Even for a sleeper agent retiring after success, the follow-up cleanup had to be thorough. Otherwise, even with a changed appearance, traces might be found.","\"My lord, I heard Quan... Qin Yanzhou previously always wore a mask when acting, and his face was scarred. It's likely his enemies wouldn't recognize him,\" Bai Jianping privately felt such a large-scale effort was unnecessary.","Wearing a mask, sticking fake scars on his face, and even abandoning his former name—it's like he's a completely different person.","\"That mask couldn't have been worn from his very first day entering the Fan residence,\" Qin Shaozong said calmly. \"As for the scars, they certainly make people recoil and avoid looking closely at his face, but they won't stop any determined observers in the future.\"","Bai Jianping's brow twitched.","This really is about tying up every loose end! Although it's not something the Lord couldn't accomplish, it's undoubtedly a significant undertaking, especially since it involves both Nangong Qingzhou and Fan Yanzhou.","Which one of them is an easy mark? Seems like neither is.","Thinking about it carefully, this might be the first time the Lord has brought trouble upon himself, and he's gone straight for a major one right off the bat.","Well, perhaps that's not entirely fair to say. That young man is a huge trouble, but he has a remarkably capable mother behind him. Lately, the income from the saltpeter alone has been enough to make that tight-fisted Jin Duole grin from ear to ear.","\"My Lord, Commandant Mo has returned,\" a guard announced at that moment.","Soon, the unkempt and bearded Mo Yanyun strode in. He had come straight after returning to the residence, still covered in the dust of travel and looking much more weathered, but his eyes shone like stars.","He held a scroll of mulberry-bark paper in his hand: \"My Lord, I've brought back the maps of the area near Huai'an County. When do we set out on the campaign?\"","After he finished speaking, he realized no one in the room responded.","Mo Yanyun: \"?\"","What's with their looks? Weren't we supposed to attack the White Lotus Sect?","Before he could ask, Mo Yanyun suddenly remembered something else. \"Ah, right, My Lord, just as I was returning to the residence, I saw two suspicious individuals outside the gates.\"","Without much thought, he ventured a guess: \"Could it be that the White Lotus Sect has learned we plan to attack them soon, and so they've sent spies to our door?\"","His words fell, and the room remained silent.","Mo Yanyun was baffled.","What in the world is going on? I've only been gone a few days, yet it feels like something earth-shattering must have happened within the residence."]},{"number":56,"title":"Chapter 56","paragraphs":["Inside the main residence.","In this era, meals were typically served on individual low tables. However, Dai Li found them inconvenient. After her son returned, she simply had a carpenter make a new set of small furniture.","A small round table and two wooden chairs. Dining together at the same table, no longer needing separate ones.","But the novelty lasted less than half a day. When Qin Shaozong saw this small round table, he also thought it was quite good, though a bit too small—cramped for three people.","So, with a single order from him, the carpenter set to work. Soon, the small round table in Dai Li's room had expanded by two sizes, becoming spacious enough to comfortably seat an additional grown man.","Dai Li: \"...\"","When under someone else's roof, and with the meals provided by the army cooks, she truly couldn't do anything to their commanding officer. She would just have to make do.","Today, upon hearing from Qin Shaozong about the suspected spies outside the residence, Dai Li furrowed her delicate brows. \"Why didn't Commandant Mo apprehend and question them at the time?\"","Qin Shaozong replied leisurely, \"That fellow isn't as meticulous as some. He had urgent business at hand and only wanted to return swiftly to report. Furthermore...\" He deliberately paused. As expected, she was watching him intently, her clear, jet-black eyes reflecting his own image from up close.","The man's thin lips curved into a smile. \"Guoyun County sits on the border of two provinces. This place is teeming with spies. For all we know, they've already honeycombed it behind the scenes.\"","Such border areas were the hardest to control and also the most flexible. As the superior officer to a large number of spies himself, Qin Shaozong was quite fond of such places.","Dai Li muttered, \"Could they be from Yanzhou?\"","According to what her son later said, after the assassination failed, the sole surviving companion, upon learning of his intention to defect, had returned alone to report.","Fan Yanzhou must already know the details and would certainly wonder why Zhou Zhou chose to break from the organization in Guoyun County, and whether it had any connection to the northern territories.","Although Qin Yanzhou was sitting right beside them, Qin Shaozong acted as if he weren't there, speaking directly to Dai Li. \"It could be any faction. It could also be other enemies this boy made in previous years. In any case, Madam, keep him from going out these next few days. If he goes strolling on the streets, gets a sack thrown over his head, and is beaten black and blue until even you wouldn't recognize him, don't say I didn't warn you.\"","Dai Li felt her temples throb listening to him.","Was his mouth smeared with poison? Speaking so harshly, isn't he afraid of poisoning himself?","Qin Yanzhou remained utterly unperturbed, treating it as empty noise.","Dai Li gritted her teeth slightly. \"How is the Marquis so familiar with such matters? Could it be from personal experience?\"","Qin Shaozong looked at her and suddenly chuckled. \"Madam is clever. Indeed, in my youth, I most enjoyed doing things that left others swallowing their losses with no way to complain.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","Dai Li was speechless. She simply ignored him and turned to her son. \"Zhou Zhou, stay within the residence to lay low these next few days. If you need anything purchased, just tell Nianxia or the others. They will handle it properly.\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded. \"Alright.\"","After the meal, Qin Shaozong left.","Dai Li was rather unlucky. This time, she had sprained her left foot again. Whether it was because of the previous injury or this sprain being more severe, the recovery was taking longer than last time.","Nianxia and Bipo had gone out of the residence a few times. Once, Dai Li accidentally overheard them talking.","\"Today I went to the silk merchant's shop to pick up the custom-made clothes for the young master as agreed, but they said Embroiderer Su, who was in charge, had a sudden family emergency.\"","\"Ah? So how will they handle it? It won't be delayed, will it?\"","\"A delay is certain. They've assigned a new embroiderer to take over the unfinished work. They said she would work overtime to finish within three days at most, and that the embroiderer would personally deliver the clothes to the residence as soon as they're done. Oh, and as an apology for the delay, they'll include an extra pair of black boots.\"","\"Sigh, man proposes, God disposes. Nothing to be done about that.\"","Dai Li, leaning on her crutch, paused for a moment, then called out to the two women outside.","Nianxia and Bipo entered upon hearing her.","\"Madam, did you want to fetch something?\" Seeing Dai Li standing with her crutch, they thought she wanted to get an object.","Dai Li asked, \"You just said the silk merchant changed to a new embroiderer, and that the embroiderer would personally deliver the clothes to the residence when finished?\"","The two women nodded.","Dai Li pondered for a moment. \"Nianxia, go to the silk merchant's shop again. Tell them there's no need for the embroiderer to deliver them, and no need for the extra boots either. Once the new clothes are ready, have her leave them at the shop. You can go pick them up then.\"","The usual embroiderer was replaced, the new one personally acting as a courier, and offering free boots. It was unknown if these boots were ready-made. What if the new person had doubts about the previous measurements and wanted to take them again? Wouldn't that require meeting Zhou Zhou?","Whether Dai Li was being overly cautious or not, she felt that at this critical juncture, it was better to be extra careful.","Just a pair of shoes, not something they absolutely had to have.","Although not fully understanding the reason, Nianxia always followed Dai Li's lead. Since Dai Li said not to have the embroiderer deliver the clothes, she immediately went out to the silk merchant's shop.","At dusk, just after the evening meal, a guard hurriedly came to report that Kuang Ye had urgent matters to relay.","Qin Shaozong put down his bowl and chopsticks and went to his study.","As evening deepened, the main gates opened. Qin Shaozong, on horseback, led several men to the military camp outside the city. As was usual in such cases, he would not return tonight.","Since her son's return, Dai Li had moved back to sleep in the side chamber.","Mo Yanyun had returned to the residence, and the atmosphere was visibly tense, with conflict seeming imminent. Sleeping separately was only natural. Moreover, the lead assassin had defected. Not only would he not continue any assassination attempts, but if Dai Li were threatened, he would be the first to object.","Summer nights were not very cool. Fortunately, Dai Li wasn't prone to sweating and could tolerate heat. With her son found and her heaviest burden lifted, she soon fell asleep.","Dai Li could sleep, but Bipo in the adjacent small room could not. Bipo couldn't stand the heat, suffering every summer, and was prone to heavy sweating. Sweating more naturally made her thirsty.","Usually, Bipo would keep a cup of water by her bed, taking a sip when thirsty, and would gradually fall asleep after a few times. But tonight, she had poured too little water. After drinking several times, just as she was approaching deep drowsiness, she found the cup empty.","That was unacceptable. The thirstier she thought about it, the thirstier she felt. After tossing and turning several times, Bipo was wide awake. She couldn't help but get up, intending to fetch water from outside.","There was a moon tonight, a bright wheel hanging high in the sky, shedding silvery moonlight.","The small side chamber had a window. Passing by it, Bipo glanced out unintentionally and was immediately frightened pale.","Th-there was a dark figure in the courtyard.","The Marquis was not in the residence tonight. The young master had gone to sleep early. The patrolling guards only passed by the courtyard entrance; they would never enter the courtyard itself.","There was an intruder!","Bipo instinctively dodged to the side, hiding herself completely against the adjacent wall, but the next instant, she shuddered.","No, she couldn't hide. She had to inform Madame immediately!","\"Assassins! Madame, there are assassins!\" Bipo hurriedly ran to the outer chamber.","Dai Li was jolted awake from her sleep. Her first thought was: had the assassin who went to report back returned with men to attack again?","Bipo's shout was high-pitched and sharp, causing the patrolling guards not far away to rush urgently toward the area.","Torchlight soon illuminated the courtyard. As guards encircled the outside in multiple layers, the centurion led another team straight in, heading directly for Dai Li's room.","\"Creak.\" The door opened.","The terrified Bipo appeared before the guards. Their gazes swept past her, peering inside.","The room was quiet, with no other sounds.","The guards paused, all realizing the assassin wasn't inside. After all, if an assassin had reached this place, the maid would likely already be dead.","Not here, then perhaps the adjacent room?","\"Creak.\" Another door opening sound.","The door of the front room opened, revealing a young man standing at the threshold, wearing only thin undergarments and shuffling in wooden clogs.","The guards averted their eyes. It seemed not here either. They turned their attention toward Qin Shaozong's quarters.","The Lord had gone to the military camp. Having failed in one strike, could the assassin be hiding inside?","Never mind, they should go in and check first.","Dai Li saw her son enter and looked him over carefully. He was dressed in white, visibly clean, with no glaring red stains.","Dai Li breathed a sigh of relief. Just then, the centurion who had finished checking the neighboring room returned to report:","\"Madame Dai, there are no assassins in the courtyard.\"","Just that one sentence, nothing more, but the implication was clear: it had been a false alarm.","Dai Li did not look at Bipo, only addressing the centurion: \"My apologies for making you come for nothing.\"","\"Please don't say that, Madame Dai. In such matters, we would rather run empty a thousand times than miss a single occurrence,\" the centurion said with a cupped-hand salute. \"Please rest. We shall take our leave.\"","After the centurion left, Dai Li looked at her son. \"Zhou Zhou, you should go back to sleep too.\"","\"Goodnight, Mother,\" the young man said softly.","The door closed.","Bipo fell to her knees with a thud. \"Madame, this servant truly did not missee. I really saw a dark shadow in the courtyard. I swear on everything. If I speak a single false word, may I be struck by lightning and die a horrible death.\"","Dai Li pressed her lips together.","Nianxia stood beside Bipo, anxiously nudging her secretly with a toe.","What was wrong with Bipo today? Why was she so obtuse? Madame's attitude clearly showed she wanted to let the matter drop. Why was Bipo still clinging to it?","Just as Bipo was about to speak again, she heard Dai Li sigh.","Dai Li did not say whether she believed her or not, only speaking gently, \"Regardless, no assassin was caught tonight. The matter is settled as far as the outside is concerned. Bipo, from now on, do not speak to anyone about what you saw tonight, or it will make things difficult for the guards.\"","Hearing her gentle tone, Bipo privately felt her mistress trusted her and immediately nodded repeatedly. \"This servant understands.\"","\"It's late. Go back and rest, all of you.\" Dai Li sent them away.","The two maids returned to their small side room. Dai Li sat quietly by the bed for a moment before lying down.","Inside the dark bed curtains, nothing was visible, yet Dai Li lay with her eyes open for a while blankly. When she closed her eyes again to sleep, she could not drift off as quickly as before.","The minor night alarm was like a small ripple, insignificant in the churning river of greater events, soon forgotten by everyone.","A matter of utmost importance was decided not long after:","The Northern Army led by Qin Shaozong, the Qingzhou Army led by Nan Gongxiong, and the Yanzhou Army led by Fan Tianshi decided to hold a meeting at the border of Qing and Yan provinces to jointly discuss the campaign against the Qinglian Sect.","Qin Shaozong and Nan Gongxiong had already met previously, so the Northern and Qingzhou armies traveled together, arriving first at the designated location.","The meeting point was chosen on a small plain with elegant vegetation and an open view, making any ambush obvious at a glance.","A large command tent was erected there. Flanking the tent stood two massive command banners. Looking further out on both sides were soldiers from both armies, either standing or patrolling on horseback.","Half an hour after the tent was pitched, dust rose in the west. Amidst the rumble of hooves, a large banner bearing the character \"Yan\" came into view.","Fan Tianshi, his hair tied with a golden crown, wore Tang-ni armor, carried two swords at his waist, and rode a sturdy white horse. Beside him was his eldest son, Fan Boliang, flanked by a group of Yanzhou generals, followed by a vast mass of Yanzhou troops—a truly imposing sight.","When they were still over ten meters from the large command tent, Fan Tianshi reined in his horse. He shot a glance at his deputy beside him, who understood immediately and proclaimed in a loud voice:","\"Fan, Governor of Yan, has arrived!\"","His voice, resonant as a bell, was carried by the wind into the large tent not far away.","Inside the tent.","Upon hearing this, Qin Shaozong laughed. \"That fellow really cares about face. He wants us to go out and greet him.\"","\"Fine, it's only a few steps,\" Nan Gongxiong said, rising.","Qin Shaozong, however, did not move. Unlike Nan Gongxiong, he was bound to clash openly with Fan Tianshi on this trip, so naturally, he wouldn't bother with such superfluous formalities.","\"Please relay a message to Governor Fan for me, Lord Nan of Qingzhou. Tell him I'm feeling unwell, can't walk far, and await him inside the tent,\" Qin Shaozong said, continuing to sip his tea.","Nan Gongxiong's mouth twitched. He had initially intended to persuade him further, but then it occurred to him: the worse the relationship between the North and Yanzhou, the more solid the alliance with his Qingzhou would be.","He was happy to see it happen.","He immediately agreed and left the tent with several Qingzhou deputies.","Moments later, two figures entered the tent side by side.","Hearing that Qin Shaozong was unwell, Fan Tianshi briefly wondered if the night raid had injured him somewhat. But when he saw the man not far away, his face darkened instantly.","He had never met Qin Shaozong before, but that didn't stop Fan Tianshi from recognizing him at a glance.","A few paces away, a burly man sat with an imposing air. Clad in black armor, his brown eyes were cold, his long, sweeping brows sharp as scimitars. His presence was like a mountain or sea, exuding the authority honed from commanding tens of thousands of troops.","At that moment, one hand rested casually on the table, the other held a teacup. His posture was leisurely, his complexion ruddy—there was no sign of being unwell or unable to walk far.","Their eyes met. Qin Shaozong offered Fan Tianshi a smile that had absolutely nothing to do with friendliness. \"Governor Fan, you're more refined and delicate-looking than I imagined. Don't just stand there like a post, come and sit.\"","Even if Fan Tianshi was indeed fair-skinned and his quiet demeanor somewhat gentle, in this context, no ruler would appreciate being called refined and delicate-looking by another.","Not only was it sarcastic, but the opening words also assumed the tone of a host.","Fan Tianshi's face twisted slightly. Fan Boliang, who stood a step behind him, now stepped forward. \"I just heard Marquis Qin say he was feeling unwell. One shouldn't speak such words carelessly. Speak them too often, and should one day a mishap turn them true, no amount of praying to gods or buddhas would bring back a healthy body.\"","Qin Shaozong looked at Fan Boliang with a half-smile. \"My apologies, so you are the Governor of Yan. By the way, Governor Fan, why are you standing at the back? What's the meaning of sending a subordinate to stand in the middle? Could it be you fear this is a trap, and plan to use a substitute later?\"","Not only did Fan Boliang's face turn pale then flushed, but Fan Tianshi's expression also became exceedingly grim.","Nangong Xiong was dumbfounded.","Had some unknown friction occurred between the Northern Territories and Yan Province? Why did Qin Shaozong speak with such pointed barbs the moment he saw Fan Tianshi?","Amidst his shock, Nangong Xiong felt a sliver of relief.","Ahem, it's fortunate this man with the sharp tongue is now my ally. Otherwise, these harsh words would likely be directed at me.","\"Marquis Qin is quite the wit,\" Fan Tianshi said with a forced smile. \"But sometimes, a loose tongue can inadvertently make enemies, and invite fatal disaster. That would be most unfortunate.\"","Qin Shaozong scoffed. \"Fatal disaster? Who wants to kill me? Is it you, Governor Fan?\"","His words shocked everyone present.","Nangong Xiong hadn't expected Qin Shaozong to move beyond pointed remarks this time, directly targeting the already fragile cloak of peace.","Fan Tianshi's pupils contracted, stunned that Qin Shaozong would lay everything out in the open right from the start.","No, not just laying it out, but adding fuel to the fire.","When did he ever want to kill Qin Shaozong?","\"Marquis Qin, one might eat carelessly, but one must not speak carelessly,\" Fan Tianshi said coldly.","Qin Shaozong: \"Some days ago, a group of assassins infiltrated my residence. This squad of ten failed in their mission. Two were captured alive, one escaped, and the remaining seven were cut down. Governor Fan, one of the two captives claimed you ordered the assassination.\"","\"Nonsense!\" Fan Tianshi retorted.","Qin Shaozong merely uttered three words: \"Bring him in.\"","Two men entered, dragging a formless mass between them. The scent of blood immediately began to spread through the tent.","The men from Qing and Yan Provinces stared intently, all gasping in shock. That was no 'thing'; it was clearly a person.","The man's legs had been severed below the knees, and it seemed many of his bones and tendons had been removed, leaving his body utterly limp, forced forward only by the two men gripping his wrists.","Along the path he was dragged, occasional dark blood droplets and tiny bits of flesh fell to the ground.","Although they all relied on family backing to rise to power, the lords of this era could roughly be divided into two types:","One type possessed formidable martial prowess themselves, like Qin Shaozong and Nangong Xiong. These men often led troops into battle personally. The other type were not fighters. They preferred commanding from the rear, delegating tasks to their fierce generals rather than taking the field themselves—men like Fan Tianshi.","The former were accustomed to the sight of blood. Faced with such a mutilated, barely-living wreck, they could generally remain expressionless, at most frowning slightly. The latter, however, could not.","Fan Tianshi's face changed on the spot. \"Qin Changgeng, what is the meaning of dragging this random person in here? Don't tell me you'll first claim this is one of the captured assassins, then say that under interrogation, this man implicated me. Hah, who knows where you found this wretch.\"","Qin Shaozong raised a long eyebrow. \"You truly don't recognize this man?\"","\"I do not!\" Fan Tianshi insisted firmly.","But Qin Shaozong smiled. \"Why are you in such a hurry to shut down the conversation? I haven't even had the chance to say this man was remarkably tenacious, withstanding round after round of torture, and later, taking advantage of his guard's negligence, bit off half his own tongue.\"","Fan Tianshi's nostrils flared, his fists clenched. \"If he is a tongueless man, why bring him here at all?\"","Qin Shaozong looked past him at the array of deputy generals, his meaning clear: \"Your lord's speed in discarding his pieces is truly unmatched.\"","\"Qin Changgeng!\" Fan Tianshi roared in fury.","\"He indeed said nothing. But there is one person who knows the entire story, and this is someone you, Governor Fan, must be very familiar with. After all, you spent seven years together, and later you even adopted him as your sworn son. He knows the layout of your Fan Manor, remembers every task he performed for you over those seven years, every person he killed. Governor Fan, you haven't forgotten the one called 'Quanjie', have you?\"","With each sentence Qin Shaozong uttered, Fan Tianshi's face grew darker, until finally the knuckles of his clenched fists emitted audible cracks.","\"Qin Changgeng, cease this thief crying 'stop thief' here! I already issued a notice declaring Quanjie a traitor. He is clearly your man!\" Fan Tianshi was livid with rage.","The thought that his most useful tool had actually been another's spy made his blood boil.","\"Such utter rubbish. Has Governor Fan lost his head in panic? You show no benevolence, I show no righteousness. We agreed to jointly crusade against the Green Lotus Sect, yet someone among us secretly plays foul tricks. Who knows what their true intentions are.\" Qin Shaozong rose from his seat and drew the ring-pommeled sword from his waist.","Nangong Xiong hadn't anticipated this further twist.","Quanjie was no minor figure within the Fan household. If his testimony existed, then the matter of Yan Province secretly assassinating an ally on the eve of the crusade against the Green Lotus Sect could not be denied, no matter how much Fan Tianshi protested.","This was a trap. Qin Shaozong had long been determined to tear off all pretenses with Yan Province!","But then, Nangong Xiong realized another crucial matter.","As the one who had brought Qin Shaozong from the Northern Territories as an ally, he was now forcibly drawn into this sudden, unannounced trap. He was completely aboard the Northern Territories' ship, with no possibility of disembarking anytime soon."]},{"number":57,"title":"Chapter 57","paragraphs":["The situation was changing rapidly. In the military tent where the atmosphere was already tense, as Qin Shaozong stood up and drew his sword, an invisible and extremely intense smell of gunpowder suddenly spread.","\"Qin Changgeng, don't make unfounded accusations! The campaign against the Qinglian Sect is imminent, yet you've set up this 'Feast of the Hongmen' and suddenly attacked me. In my opinion, it's clearly you who have ulterior motives. Fine, since you're unwilling to form an alliance, then let's part ways here!\" Fan Tianshi said as he retreated.","Since it was a \"Feast of the Hongmen,\" how could Qin Shaozong let him leave so easily?","\"Your people sent an assassin to kill me last night. Now you think you can just brush it off with a few words. Is Fan of Yanzhou being too naive?\" Naturally, Qin Shaozong wouldn't let him go easily.","As his voice fell, all the military generals from the Northern Region drew their swords, and those from Yanzhou also got ready for battle.","The people from Qingzhou were stunned.","But they wouldn't be in a daze for long because the fight broke out.","The sound of swords colliding rang out several times. Someone was kicked and crashed into the table, and someone slashed open the military tent with a sword, widening the exit for retreat.","Fan Tianshi was a coward who valued his life. When he came for this meeting, not only was he wearing armor, but he also brought all his fierce generals with him. Among his subordinates, there was a great general named Zang Yinghao. This man had numerous past battle achievements. In one - on - one combat, he was a rare good hand.","Zang Yinghao was eight feet tall, with a dark face and short beard, a square mouth and thick lips. He held an ancient ingot - shaped sword in his hand, the tip of which was sharp and upturned, as flamboyant as its owner.","At this moment, Zang Yinghao blocked in front of Qin Shaozong with his sword, stopping his way: \"I've long heard of your great name, Lord Qin. Let me have a match with you.\"","Qin Shaozong didn't talk much to him and stepped forward with his ring - headed sword.","There were quite a few people in the military tent, and the space was limited. It was easy to affect others during the fight. After two clangs of the swords, many people consciously stepped aside, afraid of being affected by the sharp blades of the two.","At first, Zang Yinghao could still smile, but after engaging with Qin Shaozong, his expression gradually became solemn.","Every strike from the other side was extremely powerful, as if carrying the force of thunder. Moreover, such heavy strikes were like continuous ocean waves, endless and rapid, as if each strike didn't need any energy accumulation for him.","After just a few rounds of confrontation, Zang Yinghao was greatly shocked. All the noise in his ears turned into the humming sound of the weapons vibrating, making him unable to hear the screams and the sound of weapons outside the tent.","Fine sweat oozed from Zang Yinghao's forehead, and his hand holding the sword trembled slightly. He had to change from holding the sword with one hand to using both hands.","Using the sword with two hands was not as flexible as with one hand. After another confrontation and deflecting the force, the distance between the two was closer than ever. Without any pause, Qin Shaozong bent his elbow and rammed it hard into Zang Yinghao's throat.","\"Crunch!\" The throat bone suddenly broke.","Zang Yinghao covered his throat and took two steps back, but he was no longer able to attack. His eyes were wide open, his neck was twisted into a strange shape, his breathing was extremely heavy, and the sound of inhaling and exhaling was like that of a broken old bellows.","This man had already lost half of his combat power. Qin Shaozong stepped forward again. After several consecutive strikes, he knocked the sword out of the opponent's hand. With a swift swing of the sword, an irresistible cut splashed blood, and a heavy object fell from a height.","It was Zang Yinghao's head with his eyes wide open.","Qin Shaozong kicked the head away. \"Just so - so.\"","After dealing with this obstacle, as soon as Qin Shaozong shifted his gaze, he heard someone outside shouting loudly:","\"The military tent is about to collapse!\"","After Fan Tianshi was escorted out of the military tent by his fierce generals on both sides, he was intercepted by the Northern Region's military generals outside. Seeing that there were dangers in front and behind, he simply took advantage of the fact that Qin Shaozong was still blocked inside the tent and ordered his men to cut the ropes at several fixed points of the military tent.","By then, when the tent collapsed and covered the people inside, it could at least buy him some time to evacuate.","Yes, Fan Tianshi intended to evacuate.","Don't think that he had brought many fierce generals and troops this time. But in war, it was most taboo to be unprepared, not to mention that there was also a \"Qingzhou acting as a lackey\" beside him. Therefore, as soon as Fan Tianshi knew that the alliance had fallen apart, he decided to retreat first.","When the huge military tent roof came down, Qin Shaozong was still a few steps away from the exit. He rushed forward quickly, at the same time bent his elbow and raised it high in front of him to create a little space. Then he turned his ring - headed sword over with the blade facing up and used it to lift the military tent.","The nomadic people in the Northern Region raised many cattle and sheep, and their military tents were mostly made of cowhide. The textile industry of the Han people was relatively more developed, and the materials of the military tents were mostly cloth, silk, felt, and leather. The first two were easily cut by the blade, while the latter two were stronger.","Unfortunately, this tent was made of thick double - layer cowhide to prevent rain.","Qin Shaozong finally walked out from the edge.","As soon as he came out, a cold arrow flew towards him. Qin Shaozong raised his sword to deflect it. Looking up, he saw that the surrounding area was already in chaos. The soldiers from Yanzhou were fighting two opponents with one, not only resisting the attack from the Northern Region but also dealing with the soldiers from Qingzhou.","\"Bring me my longbow,\" Qin Shaozong shouted.","His personal guard had followed him for many years and cooperated with him very well. He had already fetched a heavy bow and was waiting aside.","Qin Shaozong nocked an arrow and drew the six - shi longbow easily. The man's long and powerful fingers held the tiger - tendon string, pulling it into an almost full - moon arc.","Not far ahead, Fan Tianshi had already mounted his horse and was galloping westward whipping his horse.","Qin Shaozong aimed at him, but before he could shoot the arrow, Fan Tianshi's figure was covered by a man who was covering his retreat.","Qin Shaozong paused for a moment, then without hesitation, he deflected the arrowhead to the side and aimed at another person.","His dark - colored long fingers suddenly let go.","\"Whoosh!\"","The long arrow flew with a strong wind, turning into a stream of light and accurately hitting a person. Moreover, the force of this arrow was so great that it shot through the armor on the man's body.","Fan Boliang on the horse trembled. The huge force from behind made him lean forward. Just as he was about to straighten up again, he suddenly felt that all his strength was draining away rapidly, as if there was a big hole in his chest that couldn't be blocked.","He stiffly lowered his head and saw that half of the cold arrow was sticking out from his chest. The sharp pain came after a short delay.","He could no longer hold the reins, and Fan Boliang fell off the horse. The horse behind couldn't avoid him in time and trampled him into a bloody mess.","Hearing this, Fan Tianshi let out a scream. There was an inexplicable thud in his heart. He turned to look, and this look made his eyes bloodshot and his courage and liver split. \"My son!!\"","\"My lord, don't stop,\" the people behind him said hurriedly when they saw him trying to rein in the horse. \"The eldest young master sacrificed himself for you. You can't let down his painstaking efforts!\"","Running away also required a single - minded effort. Otherwise, if you were indecisive about whether to fight or flee, it would only result in greater losses.","Not far away, hearing the sudden commotion over there, Qin Shaozong thought that the \"little chick\" who looked three or four - tenths like Fan Tianshi was indeed his son.","He hooked his lips in satisfaction. \"Some words really shouldn't be spoken casually. Otherwise, even praying to gods and Buddhas won't save your life. Am I right?\"","The wind carried his words far away, but unfortunately, the person being questioned could no longer speak.","Nan Gongxiong had been in the inner part of the tent earlier and now emerged from the large, hooded tent. He looked at the soldiers of the three sides engaged in a fierce battle in front of him and heard Fan Tianshi's heart - wrenching cry of \"My son!\" in the distance. It felt as if an invisible rope had coiled his heart up high and then suddenly thrown it down.","So, it was shattered, and the dust settled.","Qin Shaozong had killed Fan Tianshi's son, seemingly his eldest legitimate son. Such a hatred for the killing of one's son could never be easily let go.","A broken mirror was hard to mend, and they could never go back to the way it was before.","\"How could you act like this? You're so impulsive,\" Nan Gongxiong said to Qin Shaozong with dissatisfaction, gritting his teeth in anger. \"Moreover, we are allies now. Can you inform me before making important decisions?\"","Qin Shaozong smiled and patted his shoulder in a friendly way. \"Didn't you tell me before that you were quite dissatisfied with that scoundrel Fan Tianshi? And I also had grudges with him. So, I just solved the problem all at once. No need to thank me.\"","Nan Gongxiong almost spat out a mouthful of old blood. This guy took advantage and still played innocent. \"Is this solving the problem? Killing only his son but not him is clearly asking for trouble!\"","Qin Shaozong said, \"I originally wanted to shoot him, but I was blocked, so it didn't work.\"","Nan Gongxiong didn't believe it. \"Once you, Qin Changgeng, are determined to do something, there's nothing you can't achieve. In my opinion, you thought that killing him directly here would damage your reputation. After all, the matter of Quanjie assassinating you on Fan Tianshi's order hasn't spread yet. When it comes out, people might pay more attention to you suddenly attacking Yanzhou during the alliance of the three sides and killing Fan Tianshi all at once. It would be extremely harmful to your prestige and bring no benefits at all.\"","Qin Shaozong replied, \"Really not.\"","Nan Gongxiong had a look of \"I won't believe your nonsense.\" \"Now that you've killed his eldest legitimate son, he will surely fight you to the death. Fan Tianshi is as cunning as a snake, and his subordinate Shi Wuji is full of tricks and can be called a poisonous counselor. If we let Fan Tianshi return to Yanzhou this time, it will be like setting a dragon free into the sea and a tiger back to the mountain. The future troubles will be countless.\"","Qin Shaozong smiled and asked, \"Then what should we do?\"","Nan Gongxiong gritted his teeth. There was no doubt that Qin Shaozong must have done it on purpose. \"What else? Of course, we should chase after him and kill Fan Tianshi.\"","Qin Shaozong clapped his hands and laughed. \"Great minds think alike. Governor Nangong's idea coincides with mine. It seems there's a reason why we can be allies.\"","Nan Gongxiong wanted to curse.","Suddenly, a glint of light flashed across his eyes. He grabbed Qin Shaozong who was about to turn around and mount his horse. \"My eldest daughter's marriage is completely ruined because of what you did today. You have to compensate me with a son - in - law.\"","Qin Shaozong paused and then used his own words to block him. \"If we don't chase now, it will really be like setting a dragon free into the sea and a tiger back to the mountain. The future troubles will be countless. Governor Nangong, the current important matter comes first.\"","Nan Gongxiong wouldn't let him go and grabbed the reins of Chi Jiao. \"Our armies are full of fierce generals. The pursuit of Fan Tianshi can be handed over to them.\"","While the two commanders were at a stalemate here, on the other side, as Fan Tianshi withdrew, the Yanzhou army also fought while retreating, and the soldiers from the North and Qingzhou chased after them together.","Not long after the large army left, two fast - galloping horses came back to report.","\"My lord (Governor Nangong), after the Yanzhou army withdrew from the small plain and entered the Huaxi Long Road, there were ambushes on both sides of the road to block them.\"","The Huaxi Long Road connected the small plain and Yanzhou and was one of the largest official roads leading to the west. This road was in the shape of an oblique trapezoid, with the two sides slightly higher, similar to the Taohua Ridge back then.","Nan Gongxiong clicked his tongue lightly. \"Sure enough, there's a backup plan. Most likely, it's the work of that Shi Wuji.\"","At this time, a dark cloud drifted across the sky, and the whole sky suddenly turned dark. A cold wind blew, and it seemed like it was going to rain.","\"This summer is really like a child's face, so changeable. We have neither the right time, nor the favorable location, nor the support of the people. Well, sound the gong to recall the troops,\" Qin Shaozong ordered.","Nan Gongxiong looked at the sky and also gave the order to his deputy to recall the troops.","*","Dai Li knew that Qin Shaozong had gone to have a discussion today and had taken all the high - ranking generals except Mo Yanyun with him. She knew that he wouldn't be back for a while, and there were fewer spies in the mansion than ever before.","So, she found an excuse to send Nianxia and Bipo out of the mansion and called her son over.","\"Mom, did you call me?\" Qin Yanzhou was also dressed in a white robe today.","His skin had inherited seven - tenths of his mother's fair complexion. When he wore light - colored clothes, he looked especially gentle and elegant, as if he had completely isolated all the past bloodshed and darkness.","Dai Li waved for him to sit down. \"Let's have a good talk today, just the two of us.\"","Qin Yanzhou sat down opposite her. \"What do you want to talk about?\"","Dai Li got straight to the point. \"That day, Zhou Zhou, you said that if I wanted to leave, you could arrange it for me. At that time, I didn't have time to ask because Qin Shaozong came. After he left, I suddenly realized that the timing was wrong, so I didn't mention it to you again. Now that Nianxia and the others are out and Qin Shaozong is not here, let's talk about this matter.\"","It was not only the wrong timing. At that time, she had learned from Qin Shaozong that her son had been an assassin and had almost had his head chopped off.","Hatred and resentment had occupied her whole mind. She was bent on killing Fan Tianshi and naturally didn't think about leaving.","But now that Qin Shaozong had gone on an expedition and it seemed that the rift with Yanzhou was a foregone conclusion, taking advantage of the fact that there was no one else in the mansion, she could bring up the old matter with her son again.","Qin Yanzhou was silent for a moment before saying, \"Mom, do you still remember that wealthy family who saved me at first? In the sixth year when I was in the Fan Mansion, which was last year, I accidentally ran into them. The two young masters still remembered me, and I just happened to help them out of a big trouble. So, we naturally re - established contact.\"","Dai Li naturally remembered that wealthy family.","Qin Shaozong had a deep - rooted foundation. If this wealthy family could really help, it probably wasn't an ordinary one.","\"Did you work for them in the following year?\" Dai Li couldn't help asking.","Qin Shaozong wouldn't let her go easily. Arranging for her to leave would definitely be a troublesome thing. But Zhou Zhou said he could arrange it. The only explanation was that he and that wealthy family probably had some kind of interest relationship.","Qin Yanzhou didn't deny it. \"Yes, in the following year, I sometimes helped them with some things as a way to repay them for saving my life back then. As time went by, I built up some friendship with the two young masters.\"","Suddenly, Dai Li thought of another thing and a suspicion arose in her heart. \"Zhou Zhou, since you have a friendship with them and the ability to take me away, why did you still stay in the Fan Mansion before?\"","That damned Fan Tianshi didn't treat an orphan like a human being. Zhou Zhou must have had a hard time there and often had to do dangerous jobs. Take the last assassination attempt for example. If he hadn't reacted quickly and escaped, he would definitely have lost his life.","Qin Shaozong's power was greater than Fan Tianshi's. After all, the latter was only in charge of one state, while the former controlled several connected northern states.","If the wealthy family is really capable, why don't they help Zhou Zhou get out of the Fan family?","Qin Yanzhou looked down at the teacup on the table. \"At first, I had just recognized them, so it wasn't appropriate to trouble them. Later, I did something for them. I thought it was about time. I originally planned to break away from the Fan family after going back this time. But unexpectedly, I met you here...\"","He didn't say the rest, but Dai Li knew what her son meant.","Meeting her had disrupted all his plans.","Dai Li smiled and said, \"In the end, you'll break away from the Fan family anyway. It's just different paths leading to the same destination.\"","\"By the way, there's something I need to tell you in advance.\" He hesitated a bit.","\"What?\" Dai Li asked.","There was obvious apology in Qin Yanzhou's tone. \"The dragon - bone waterwheel has not only spread in the northern region but also reached every state like the wind. Everyone knows that this thing was brought out by a Mrs. Dai from a hermit. As the saying goes, if a mound stands out from the bank, the current will rush against it. If your abilities are exposed to the public, they will surely exploit you. So after leaving, you may have to change your name and identity.\"","It's not just the dragon - bone waterwheel, but also the salt stones. He must never let them know that these were all created by his mother.","Rather than living incognito, Dai Li was more concerned about another thing. \"Zhou Zhou, you must have heard about the power of Qin Shaozong. Can we really trust this wealthy family? Will they sell us halfway?\"","What if the other party changed their mind halfway, thinking it wasn't worth offending Qin Shaozong for a friend with a bit of acquaintance and not wanting to get into trouble? Then they might sell them to the northern region as a way to atone for their sins. That would be worse than doing nothing.","\"No.\" Qin Yanzhou replied very quickly.","Dai Li asked him again, \"What's the surname of this wealthy family? Where is their ancestral home? Are they officials or in other businesses?\"","But Qin Yanzhou said, \"I'll tell you later.\"","Dai Li was puzzled. \"Can't you tell me now?\"","The young man softly called out \"Mom\", and Dai Li had no choice but to say, \"Okay, if it's later, then later.\"","Anyway, there was plenty of time. Whether it was said earlier or later, it wouldn't change the family background of that wealthy family. So she might as well follow her son's wishes.","*","Dai Li thought Qin Shaozong would be gone for a long time. But unexpectedly, just after she finished her breakfast the next day, she heard a commotion outside.","Listening intently, she clearly heard the words \"The Marquis has returned\". She couldn't help but be stunned.","Qin Shaozong was back? Was the battle over so soon? Something wasn't right...","After being in a daze for a short while, Dai Li heard the greetings of Nianxia and Bipo.","Dai Li subconsciously turned her head and saw a tall and imposing man walking straight towards her through the cave gate.","He was wearing golden armor and a helmet with a taotie pattern. The red - lined cape fluttered vigorously as he walked. His aura was as sharp as a dagger and as heavy as mountains and seas, sharp and overwhelming.","\"Why have you...?\" The words on the tip of her tongue turned into, \"Should I congratulate the Marquis on his triumphant return from the battle?\"","\"It's not inappropriate.\" Qin Shaozong took out something and threw it on the table in front of Dai Li. \"I brought something back for you. I think the lady will surely like it.\"","Dai Li looked down. It seemed to be a... cap."]},{"number":58,"title":"Chapter 58","paragraphs":["A black official's cap, smudged with dust and a bit of yellow mud, looked filthy.","Dai Li glanced at the cap, not comprehending at first. She looked up at him, puzzled.","Qin Shaozong met her gaze. Seeing her slightly dazed expression, the corner of his eye lifted slightly. \"Don't like it? That shouldn't be. Isn't my lady exceptionally hateful of Fan Tianshi, wishing you could devour his flesh?\"","Dai Li gave a sudden shudder, her voice rising noticeably. \"This is Fan Tianshi's cap?!\"","Unless one was beheaded, how could their official cap fall into another's hands.","\"It is not.\"","The joy that had exploded from Dai Li's chest and was about to spread through her meridians came to an abrupt halt with his two firm words. Joy turned into frustration, a lump of air stuck in her throat, neither rising nor falling.","Dai Li was at a loss for words. \"...If it's not, then why did my lord show it to me?\"","Qin Shaozong watched her ever-changing expressions and couldn't help but chuckle. \"Although it's not Fan Tianshi himself, it is somewhat related to him. This is the cap of his legitimate eldest son.\"","Dai Li was startled, her frustration dissipating instantly by ninety percent. \"Truly? Are you certain it's his?\"","\"I shot him dead myself. How could it be false?\" As Qin Shaozong finished speaking, he saw her eyes instantly light up, sparkling as if thousands of stars had fallen into them.","Qin Shaozong stared intently for a couple of breaths before saying, \"If my lady wishes to see the head of his eldest son, that is also not impossible.\"","\"The head is unnecessary,\" Dai Li immediately refused.","\"Usually brimming with the courage of a bear and the daring of a leopard, how come you can't bear to see this?\" Qin Shaozong's smile deepened slightly.","Initially, he had indeed considered bringing back a head to show her. But later, he thought this fox wouldn't recognize Fan Tianshi's eldest son, and when she was treating Qiao Wangfei before, she had secretly averted her eyes, likely unable to stand the sight of blood.","Fine, he took a step back and brought the cap instead.","Dai Li muttered, \"That's different. A dead person's head turns bluish, and he might have died with his eyes wide open. How frightening.\"","Not wanting to dwell on the topic of heads, Dai Li warmly invited him, \"Has my lord had breakfast yet? If not, I'll have the kitchen send it over.\"","\"That's fine,\" he said these two words and then returned to the main residence.","He removed his armor and took a simple bath.","When he came out again, he happened to meet Nianxia returning with a food box.","Nianxia was about to take the food into the main room when she heard Qin Shaozong instruct, \"Take it next door.\"","Nianxia immediately changed direction.","Dai Li had already finished her breakfast and was about to ask Bipo to fetch some atlases from the study for her to look at when she saw Nianxia enter the room with the food box, followed by a tall figure.","Although Fan Tianshi himself wasn't killed, making him lose his legitimate eldest son was quite satisfactory. In this strictly hierarchical feudal era, the legitimate eldest son was almost always the heir, cultivated with great effort from birth, probably even taught personally by Fan Tianshi.","He showed no mercy in abusing another's son; let him taste the pain of losing a child too!","Dai Li was in a good mood and had no objection to Qin Shaozong having his meal in her quarters.","Nianxia opened the food box, first taking out a porcelain bowl as large as a washbasin, then retrieving many meat buns and steamed buns from the upper layer.","After Dai Li improved the stone mill, flour-based foods became much more common: noodle soup was one, meat buns the second, and steamed buns the third.","When they first tasted the meat buns, both Qin Shaozong and the other military officers were amazed. The buns were steamed to a fluffy texture, delicate to the taste, filled with juicy and delicious mutton. One bite felt like a dance on the taste buds.","Wasn't this much better than steamed cakes?","When they first ate them, every single officer, no matter how much they usually liked to chat while eating, kept their heads down, focused solely on stuffing buns into their mouths.","Dai Li looked at the small mountain of buns and steamed buns, silently marveling at Qin Shaozong's appetite. This man's single breakfast could easily surpass her food intake for an entire day.","The rule of \"no talking during meals\" didn't exist among military officers; they weren't that particular. Qin Shaozong was the same. Before starting his meal, he pulled out a folded piece of mulberry bark paper from his robe and handed it to Dai Li. \"My lady.\"","\"What is this?\" Dai Li reached out to take it.","Qin Shaozong didn't answer. Picking up his jade chopsticks, he buried his head in eating the noodles. He was truly starving, having settled the troops today and rushed back without stopping for a rest.","Dai Li unfolded the mulberry bark paper. Upon seeing the words clearly, she couldn't help but gasp. The joy of learning about Fan Tianshi's loss of a son quickly faded.","This was a notice issued by the Fan family, or more appropriately, a wanted poster.","It stated that the Fan family's Quanjie had betrayed his master, absconding east with valuable treasures, but his specific whereabouts were unknown. A heavy reward was now offered for his head.","After briefly describing the \"heavy reward,\" there followed a detailed description of Quanjie, including approximate age, skin tone, height, and... appearance.","This wanted notice actually included a portrait.","Below was drawn a picture of her son's face without scars. Perhaps revised repeatedly for perfection, and coupled with the artist's exceptional skill, this portrait bore a seventy to eighty percent resemblance.","Dai Li clenched her teeth, gripping the mulberry bark paper tightly, hatred welling up so intensely she felt like vomiting blood.","With the Fan family's influence in Yanzhou, this wanted notice would undoubtedly spread throughout Yanzhou, even reaching other provinces.","When she and her son later left Qin Shaozong, to avoid drawing attention, wouldn't they be unable to show their true faces for years, or even longer?","Damn that Fan Tianshi, a lingering ghost!","\"This matter has likely already spread throughout Yanzhou,\" the man across from her said.","Dai Li looked up at the sound and realized that in the brief moment she was reading the wanted notice, he had already eaten more than half of his bowl of noodle soup.","Qin Shaozong continued, \"During the previous three-army talks, I told Fan Tianshi that a few days ago I caught a group of assassins in black who infiltrated my residence at night with intent to kill. I also made it clear that after interrogation, one of them confessed his identity: Quanjie, the adopted son he had raised for seven years.\"","Dai Li had guessed Qin Shaozong would break with Fan Tianshi and that he would use the assassination attempt as a starting point. But now, with the wanted notice in hand, hearing him say he used \"Quanjie\" as the entry point still made her temples throb.","There was a sequence of events. For this notice to reach Qin Shaozong's hands, it definitely wasn't newly issued today.","Dai Li's expression turned grave. \"You mentioned before that there are many spies in Yun Commandery. Now they've issued the wanted notice first, and then you revealed you've caught 'Quanjie.' Besides Fan Tianshi, other enemies will soon know my son is here.\"","Qin Shaozong said, \"Simply hiding won't work. He's not a young maiden confined to the inner chambers. It's inevitable that the boy will show his face outside sooner or later.\"","This was also why he had previously ordered Kuang Ye to clean up loose ends—because it simply couldn't be concealed. Rather than hiding, it was better to directly eliminate all those coming for revenge, then walk openly outside.","Of course, that was for the future. Before taking Yanzhou, \"Quanjie\" still couldn't show his face outside.","After all, the public reason for his falling out with Yanzhou was precisely that Fan Tianshi had sent someone to assassinate him. How could he let this \"instigator\" brazenly walk out of his residence at such a critical moment?","Daili was silent for a moment before suddenly asking, \"Then could someone infiltrate the residence at this time?\"","Qin Shaozong had just twirled a mouthful of broth noodles. Originally planning to continue slurping them down, upon hearing her words, he pulled the noodles just touching his lips slightly away. \"My lady, do you think this is a marketplace, where people can come and go as they please? Lately, the only one shuttling back and forth in my residence is that brat. Furthermore, since the first night attack, the patrols and security have been tightened and have not been relaxed. For someone to infiltrate, unless they possess heaven-defying skills, it's impossible.\"","Daili asked again, \"What constitutes 'heaven-defying skills'?\"","\"First, they would need a layout map of the residence and have figured out the patterns of the city patrols outside. Second, the residence patrols have recently been adjusted. Not only have the shifts increased, but the number of guards has too. Several squads patrol in overlapping, crisscrossing routes forming a net, not even sparing the most remote corners,\" he explained.","After all, this residence in Guoyun County was just a temporary dwelling, a mere place to stay.","Under normal circumstances, let alone adding personnel, things would proceed as usual. Even after he went on campaign, the vast majority of soldiers left behind here would be transferred away.","But now, it was not possible. She was still here.","\"My lady, why is your curiosity so heavy today? Could it be you've learned something?\" Qin Shaozong suddenly asked.","His eyes were narrow and sharp, their light amber color like amber. When he stared at someone unblinkingly, they were as sharp as a blade that could dissect one's innermost thoughts, like a great tiger crouching in the jungle.","Daili's mind went blank for an instant, unable to come up with a suitable explanation on the spot.","Unexpectedly, he then said on his own, \"I understand.\"","These four words startled Daili greatly. She subconsciously leaned forward slightly. \"Understand what?\"","\"My lady wants to talk more with me,\" Qin Shaozong said with a laugh.","Daili: \"...You are correct.\"","Fine. Him understanding it this way was better than him thinking of other possibilities.","Daili lowered her head, not looking at him.","Actually, making a public announcement wasn't entirely out of the question. On the surface, they could be labeled as part of the Northern Army. Then, when the time came for her and her son to make their escape, they could let those enemies and Qin Shaozong fight amongst themselves.","Daili did not see that the man opposite her, who had been wolfing down his food just moments before, did not immediately resume eating. Instead, he gazed steadily at her for several breaths.","Qijiang County was located at the border of Yanzhou, facing Guoyun County across the river. Both were small border counties, their geographical positions remarkably similar.","After Fan Tianshi led his army away from Gaoling County, he set up camp in the outskirts of Qijiang County. Once reorganized, he planned to lead a portion of the troops to the three-party meeting.","Now that the negotiations had broken down, Fan Tianshi retreated in defeat, slinking back to Qijiang County.","On this trip out of Gaoling County, Fan Tianshi had brought two sons. His eldest son, Fan Boliang, whom he had personally instructed, accompanied him. His second son, Fan Zhongmin, was ordered to remain stationed in Qijiang County.","Hearing of his father's return, Fan Zhongmin hurried to greet him. At the sight, he was greatly shocked. His father's armor was undamaged, but his helmet was missing. He was covered in dust, his face sorrowful, presenting a look of dejection Fan Zhongmin had never seen before.","Even after suffering a defeat, his father shouldn't be like this. Could something else have happened?","Fan Zhongmin was just thinking of seeking out his elder brother to exchange a glance, but after looking around, he couldn't find him. Suddenly, he heard someone say:","\"Lord Fan, please accept our condolences. You must not collapse at this time. Otherwise, if the Northern Army and Qingzhou Army attack simultaneously, we will be leaderless, our morale will surely collapse, causing pain to our allies and joy to our enemies.\"","Fan Zhongmin froze. The massive amount of information converged into a torrential flood. His thoughts became a lone boat upon it, first being violently pressed down into an abyss.","His brother, his own flesh and blood, had gone and not returned.","Pain and anger enveloped him.","But soon after, the wooden boat resurfaced on the water, and an irrepressible thread of secret delight crept into his heart.","His brother was gone. He, the second-born legitimate son, was now the son his father valued most.","Having lost a son in middle age, bereft of his heir, Fan Tianshi was almost supported by others as he walked. \"Where is Liuxian? Where is Liuxian? Fan Zhong, go and summon Liuxian for me.\"","The named Fan Zhongmin felt another surge of joy.","Shi Wuji had caught a slight chill the day before, hence his late arrival. Now, hearing his lord's summons, he hurried over. Upon learning of the death of the eldest young master Fan, even the usually unflappable Shi Wuji couldn't help but stagger.","Fan Tianshi dismissed the others, leaving only Shi Wuji behind. \"Liuxian, send a letter to him for me.\"","He only said this one sentence, not naming names nor saying anything else, but Shi Wuji understood.","The loss of his son was the final heavy stone, pressing down on his already wavering thoughts, causing them to tilt completely in another direction.","Shi Wuji pondered for a moment, then cupped his hands in a bow. \"I shall attend to it immediately.\"","A fast horse set out from Qijiang County, heading straight west. Traveling day and night without rest, it crossed a strategic pass and arrived at Gaoling County, where the Governor's residence was located.","A trusted aide knocked on the side gate of a residence, entered directly, and found his target in a certain pavilion.","The trusted aide first gave a military salute, then took out a letter sealed with wax and presented it with both hands. \"Marshal Li, this is a letter from Lord Fan for you.\"","The one addressed as \"Marshal Li\" was actually Li Zan, the salt smuggler who once dominated a region but was ultimately forced to flee Ying County.","Li Zan took the letter and opened it in front of the messenger. After reading it, he broke into a broad smile. \"Go and prepare a horse. I am going out.\"","The main thoroughfare of Gaoling County was bustling and lively. Shops lined both sides in neat rows, their doors wide open, with a continuous stream of pedestrians coming and going.","Li Zan went to a famous tea house in the county. As soon as he entered, a young attendant dressed in hemp cloth with a towel tied at his waist approached. \"Honored guest, will you be sitting in the main hall, or would you prefer a private room on the second or third floor?\"","Li Zan: \"I'll go to the 'Clear Mirror' private room. A pot of the new tea from the Western Regions, please. Kindly lead the way.\"","The attendant paused almost imperceptibly. \"Please follow me.\"","This tea house had the main hall on the first floor, private rooms on the second and third floors. The fourth floor was said to be the proprietor's private quarters. Now, after leading the guest to the third floor and seeing no one in the corridor, the attendant swiftly pushed open a certain wooden panel.","Behind the panel, a staircase leading upward suddenly appeared.","Li Zan ascended the steps.","Upon entering this area, the attendant's customer-service enthusiasm completely vanished from his face. He pushed open the door to the private room. \"Please wait inside quietly. I will inform the Master.\"","The formerly imposing Li Zan thanked the young attendant.","Li Zan entered alone and took a seat. Roughly half an hour later, he heard footsteps, followed by the sound of the door being pushed open.","The door swung wide, and a figure in dark jade-green robes strode confidently in.","He was an exceedingly young man, roughly in his early twenties, as elegant as an orchid or a jade tree. His pleasant, amiable face, paired with his gentle voice, gave one the feeling of a spring breeze brushing past.","\"Mr. Diting.\" Li Zan, however, started like a sparrow startled by thunder, quickly rising to his feet to bow in greeting.","Diting smiled at him. \"Marshal Li, there's no need for such formality. What brings you to seek me out today?\"","Li Zan took a letter from his bosom. \"This is a letter Governor Fan of Yanzhou entrusted me to deliver.\"","Diting took it, his eyes scanning ten lines at a glance, and the smile on his face deepened. \"Good. I am now aware of the matter. Write back to Governor Fan, saying I will make a trip to Qijiang County soon. After that, you need not stay at the Fan residence any longer. Head south; there is a new task for you.\"","A quarter of an hour later, the door to the private room opened again.","The figure in bluish-green jade color departed. He went to the rear of the teahouse and boarded a plain, unremarkable donkey cart. The driver raised a leather whip.","The little donkey clip-clopped away from the inner courtyard, following the main road to a small residence in the city. Diting went straight to the main chamber, where a long, dark underground passage beneath the bed led him to another place.","When he saw daylight again, a clear breeze carried the scent of flowers, birdsong was melodious, and all the hustle and bustle of the mortal world seemed shut out. Moreover, a faint, elusive hint of sandalwood fragrance drifted in the air.","Diting walked to a waterside pavilion. Through the curtains hanging around it, he called out \"Liudao\" to the figure inside before lifting the curtain and entering.","\"Governor Fan of Yanzhou has agreed to cooperate with us. He requests our joint effort against Marquis Wu'an. I intend to go to Qijiang County,\" Diting said.","Inside the pavilion, the man addressed as \"Liudao\" looked up from his self-played game of Go. His face bore a sixty percent resemblance to Diting's, similarly refined and gentle. However, the faint lines at the corners of his eyes revealed he was past the age of youthful vigor.","Compared to the young Diting, the warmth tempered by time seemed infused with a Buddha-like quality in the sandalwood-scented air, granting him a composure and self-restraint others lacked.","\"Marquis Wu'an killed Governor Fan's eldest legitimate son. Furthermore, he has already allied with Qingzhou. Feeling isolated and weak, Governor Fan would naturally seek our help. His second son, Fan Zhongmin, is impulsive, eager for quick success, and lacks depth. This man can be used. After you go to Qijiang County, make more contact with him,\" Liudao said.","Diting was surprised and couldn't help blurting out, \"Uncle, has news come back from over there?\" The letter had only mentioned wanting to cooperate, without stating any specific reasons.","Liudao continued on his own track. \"The Governor of Sizhou was taken by a sudden illness a few days ago. His three remaining sons are vying for power. Tell Baixiang to support the third son.\"","Diting acknowledged the order.","Liudao picked up a black stone and placed it on the northern part of the Go board. With this movement, a string of prayer beads dangled from his slender, pale wrist. \"The spy from the northern lands just returned. There's been progress on the matter of 'xianshi' (saltpeter/salty stone). This substance is a type of salt obtained through a special refining method. The process isn't overly complex, and with the salt lake being near mountains and the land vast, it wasn't too difficult to investigate. This method was provided to Marquis Wu'an by a young woman surnamed Dai.\"","Diting's brows moved slightly. \"Uncle, the dragon-bone water lift also came from this person's hand.\"","Liudao took out a white stone and placed it next to the central black one. \"I've heard this woman possesses the beauty of the moon goddess and is deeply favored by Marquis Wu'an. She must be in Guoyun County.\"","Diting understood the implication perfectly. \"Guoyun County is near the border of two provinces. That is indeed a good location.\""]},{"number":59,"title":"Chapter 59","paragraphs":["Qingzhou, Guoyunluo, the Qin Residence.","\"Achoo...\"","Daili sneezed several times in a row. She rubbed her nose, suspecting she had caught a summer cold.","\"Madam, have you caught a chill? Shall this servant go to Master Ding's place to fetch some medicine?\" Bipo asked with concern.","After rubbing her nose, Daili waited quietly for a moment before speaking. \"My throat doesn't hurt, and my nose isn't stuffy. It probably isn't a chill.\"","As for why she suddenly sneezed several times, perhaps someone was talking about her. Thinking of being talked about, she remembered that when Qin Shaozong left the residence today, he had asked if she wanted to accompany him to the military camp.","Daili had refused, citing her unhealed foot injury.","She guessed that war was truly imminent, and that man didn't want to travel back and forth, hence the suggestion.","But she wasn't willing at all. Life in this residence was perfectly good, with convenient water access, a comfortable bed to sleep on, and free use of the small kitchen in the main courtyard. Once her foot healed, she could even go out to stroll the markets. Why would she want to endure the hardships of following the army?","At the time, that man had glanced down at her foot, said nothing, and left.","\"Madam, the clothes have been fetched.\" Nianxia's voice came from outside.","Nianxia had gone out to the silk shop today to pick up the clothes custom-made for Qin Yanzhou some days ago.","Now that she had returned with the garments, and seeing Daili and Bipo gathered together, she remembered that Daili hadn't been out for several days due to her foot injury. After putting the clothes away, she told Daili an interesting piece of news from outside.","\"Madam, today in the commandery I heard of a strange occurrence.\" Seeing the two look over, Nianxia continued, \"A cook was preparing a meal when he suddenly saw a piece of mulberry-bark paper fly down from the sky. This cook picked it up intending to throw it away, but the moment it landed in his hand, he was shocked to see characters appear on the paper.\"","Bipo's curiosity was instantly piqued. \"What did it say?\"","\"'The land is fair, yet not whole; the root of calamity still comes from the north.'\" Nianxia found the phrase quite catchy.","Daili's heart skipped a beat.","\"The characters appeared out of thin air? Really?\" Bipo asked, astonished and skeptical.","\"I didn't see it myself, but they say many people witnessed this miraculous sight at the time. Later, people knelt down one after another, bowing and proclaiming it a divine revelation from heaven,\" Nianxia said.","Bipo murmured, \"For such a strange phenomenon to appear in broad daylight, could it truly be a sign from the heavens, dropping some kind of warning?\"","\"Do not speak of this matter again within the residence,\" Daili said sternly. She rarely wore such a grave expression. Seeing this, the two maids nodded repeatedly.","Still uneasy, Daili added, \"Not only must you not mention it in the residence, but you also must not join in such gossip outside. Otherwise, if someone seizes upon it as a handle endangering your lives, I won't be able to save you then.\"","The two maids were greatly alarmed and gave repeated assurances.","\"Go and call Squad Leader Hu...\" Daili started, then changed her mind. \"Never mind, don't go. You may attend to your own duties. There's no need to attend to me here.\"","After they left, Daili sat in her soft chair, lost in thought.","The land is fair, yet not whole; the root of calamity still comes from the north.","The north. Qin Shaozong.","It wasn't a particularly profound statement, but it was perfectly suited for interpretation by commoners with little education. Simple, direct, one could figure it out with a little pondering.","Once they figured it out, these \"enlightened ones\" would likely gather secretly to exchange information. If left unchecked, this shadow lurking beneath the calm would rapidly ferment.","Popular support and reputation—these two things seem incapable of being exchanged for solid silver, yet they can sometimes play a decisive role at critical moments. In years past, when Duke Mu of Qin attacked the State of Jin and was hanging by a thread, he was saved by a group of farmers. Could one say popular support didn't play a key role then?","Someone was targeting Qin Shaozong from the shadows.","Their opening move was mystical, sensational, and likely soon to be known throughout the city. Who was behind it? Had those enemies from Zhou Zhou's past come knocking?","Although Qin Shaozong wasn't in the city now, he might not be unaware of events within it. No need to rush. She would wait and see.","Daili resolved to watch quietly, but that very night something happened that gave her a terrible fright.","Assassins had broken in.","Unlike the previous false alarm, this time there were truly intruders at night. Moreover, they headed straight for the main quarters. Daili woke in the middle of the night to the sound of fierce shouts and the clashing of blades outside.","Her foot was mostly healed; she could walk, albeit slowly, without a maid's support. Daili immediately got up to go look. But just as she reached the window, an inadvertent glance outside made her face turn pale.","Her son was walking out, carrying a blade.","\"Zhou Zhou!\" Daili hurriedly called out.","The young man, who had already reached the courtyard, stopped and turned back.","\"Where are you going?\" Daili stared at the blade in his hand.","Qin Yanzhou answered truthfully, \"Assassins have entered the residence. Qin Changgeng isn't here, and most of the others are absent as well. Those assassins likely came for me or for you. I will go kill them all. Mother, you should go back to sleep.\"","These words made Daili's heart pound with fear.","The moon chose that moment to peek out from behind the clouds, casting a faint silvery light. The young man in white robes stood in the courtyard. The moonlight fell upon his handsome, delicate features but reflected no warmth whatsoever.","He resembled a cold piece of art—a blade carved from jade, perhaps, or a handful of perpetual snow atop a mountain peak.","He was undeniably calm at this moment, indifferent to the lives about to be reaped.","\"Zhou Zhou, stand right there. Don't move.\" After calling out to stop her son, Daili hurriedly made her way outside.","Under the eaves, the young man stood motionless, maintaining his previous posture, not even shifting his stance. Only when Daili reached his side did he turn left to face her.","\"If there are assassins, there are assassins. The guards outside will handle it. It's not for you to manage. Go back to bed,\" Daili said gravely.","Her son was already much taller than her. Now, bowing his head to listen to her words, which were practically an order, his eyes still held the gentleness of a lamb, without a trace of reluctance or resistance.","But he stood still.","Daili intensified her tone: \"Listen to me!\"","\"If I go back to sleep, you should rest early too. Goodnight, Mother,\" the young man nodded.","Daili said, \"Zhou Zhou, you go back first.\"","Upon hearing this, Qin Yanzhou turned and returned to his room.","Daili remained standing where she was even after the door to his room closed. Her mind was in turmoil. A realization that chilled her to the bone nailed her to the spot.","These things hadn't appeared suddenly. It was just that before, she hadn't been willing to face them squarely, deceiving herself and shutting them out. Now, they surged forth like a tidal wave, overwhelming and suffocating her.","Zhou Zhou was only nine when he came here. He has spent ten years in this era.","Nine years and ten years.","The latter span was clearly longer. Not to mention, during those first nine years, he wasn't running and jumping from the start, nor did he possess his own awareness from birth.","His worldview, not yet fully formed, had been violently erased by this ruthless era, then painstakingly reshaped with blood and wreckage.","Human life truly wasn't something of great importance in his eyes; his bones carried an indelible scent of blood.","Furthermore, after these days of living together, Dai Li had realized her son had significant problems in terms of personality and social interaction.","Under Qin Shaozong's command, there were no shortage of eloquent military officers, each curious about Zhou Zhou, with several seeking him out daily for conversation. But Zhou Zhou's state wasn't one of disliking engagement or being too lazy to respond; he was more like someone who had drawn a circle on the ground, trapping himself on a hopeless, isolated island.","Aside from speaking with her, he almost never initiated contact with anyone else. Sometimes he would sit by himself for an entire day, doing nothing, just sitting there like a wooden puppet.","While Dai Li's heart ached for his numbness, she also felt an indescribable sense of apprehension.","This couldn't go on any longer.","Dai Li stood outside for a long time, so long that Nianxia, who had gone to gather news, returned, and even Bipo couldn't help but speak up to remind her.","\"What's the situation outside?\" Dai Li asked.","Nianxia replied, \"Ten infiltrators, all have been executed.\"","\"Madam, Squad Leader Hu is guarding the courtyard gate, you needn't worry,\" Bipo thought Dai Li was frightened.","Dai Li looked in that direction and indeed saw several long shadows cast by the torchlight at the gate. She let out a soft sigh, \"You two go back and rest as well.\"","However, once she lay back down on the bed, Dai Li found herself unable to fall asleep again; she stayed awake until dawn.","The next day, after breakfast, Dai Li sent Nianxia and Bipo on an errand outside the residence. It wasn't to buy anything; the purpose was to gather information.","Dai Li instructed them to pay close attention to the happenings in the streets and alleys, preferably asking those who had witnessed the \"divine signs,\" and also to sit for a while in places like tea houses and restaurant halls, saying they might hear something different today.","The two maids accepted the order and went out.","About two hours later, they returned to the residence one after the other.","\"Madam, your foresight is divine, you are truly remarkable!\" Nianxia gazed at Dai Li with burning admiration, \"Are you perhaps a celestial maiden in disguise? How else could you have foretold this?\"","Dai Li sighed.","Looking at one spot on a leopard's skin gives an idea of the whole beast. With Nianxia holding such an attitude, it wasn't hard to guess how the common folk, who held deep reverence for gods and spirits, would react.","Uneducated, too easy to fool.","No, it wasn't just a matter of education; it was about perception.","The ancients observed the night sky, knew the twenty-eight mansions, the Four Symbols, and had partitioned the starry sky, but what lay beyond the heavens? This question that troubled people wasn't even glimpsed until the late Ming Dynasty, when the first astronomical telescope was introduced to China.","Beyond the sky is space, the solar system, the universe.","And the river of history, still flowing slowly forward at this time, clearly hadn't yet passed through that magnificent and beautiful era of exploration.","Dai Li said helplessly, \"A celestial maiden wouldn't sprain her ankle. Tell me, what happened outside?\"","Nianxia: \"I heard that yesterday and this morning, several more places witnessed divine signs, with countless eyewitnesses and no less than a hundred people prostrating themselves in worship. Madam, coincidentally, I met Mistress Su outside today—the embroiderer who used to make clothes for the young master. She was one of the witnesses to the divine sign.\"","Dai Li became interested, \"I recall you are quite familiar with her. Well, did you ask her about the divine sign matter?\"","\"Naturally, I did.\" Nianxia nodded, \"Mistress Su said that yesterday after buying groceries at the market, she suddenly felt hungry. As she happened to pass by a noodle stall, she went and ordered a bowl of soup noodles. Just as she sat down, a sudden gust of wind arose, carrying several sheets of paper and scattering them in various directions. One of them landed right on the noodle stall.\"","Dai Li asked, \"Did Mistress Su pick up the paper directly?\"","Nianxia shook her head, \"No, the paper blew towards the stove area inside the stall, some distance from Mistress Su. However, she did see with her own eyes that after the vendor picked it up, characters appeared on it—the same phrase as before.\"","Dai Li was thoughtful.","At this moment, Bipo also returned, bringing back an important piece of news: \"Madam, today outside I heard a children's rhyme.\"","Dai Li felt sure it was connected to Qin Shaozong. Sure enough, the next moment she heard Bipo say:","\"Northern tiger, fierce and greedy, swallows the salt-licking ox whole, then delves into the woods seeking the blue-robed one; The blue-robed one, dull and foolish, easy to deceive and incompetent, meets a wretched end in the finale.\"","Dai Li couldn't help but facepalm.","Anyone with a bit of understanding of the current situation could tell the insinuation was really too strong.","Children's rhymes, also called \"children's songs.\" There's a saying that because children's songs come from their innocent hearts, they are not taught by others. Many common folk also believe this to be true and place great faith in children's rhymes.","\"Madam, what's wrong?\" the two asked, puzzled.","Dai Li was about to speak when she heard a commotion outside, faintly interspersed with the words \"The Lord Marquis has returned.\"","Soon, that familiar, tall figure passed through the moon gate and strode into the main courtyard.","Dai Li had someone bring a soft chair and was sitting under the eaves to enjoy the cool. Now, as Qin Shaozong entered, their eyes met.","Without speaking immediately, Qin Shaozong looked her over from head to toe before saying, \"Madam's complexion doesn't seem too good. Were you frightened last night?\"","Dai Li hadn't slept well last night, staying awake from the latter half of the night until dawn, inevitably carrying some weariness on her face. \"Not exactly frightened, just... after being startled awake, found it hard to fall back asleep.\"","\"That means you were frightened. The residence isn't safe. Madam, come with me to the military camp.\" He stated decisively, then called for two maidservants, instructing them to pack Dai Li's belongings.","\"Why that expression? Even if you're unwilling, you must go.\" Qin Shaozong hadn't removed his armor, nor had he sat down, merely looking down at her.","Although the residence was heavily guarded and last night's assassins had all been executed, he felt uneasy not keeping this vixen within his sight.","Standing before Dai Li in full armor at this moment, Qin Shaozong's imposing figure was like a towering mountain, blocking a swath of sunlight.","Looking down from above, the sense of oppression was intense.","Dai Li was about to refuse, but then, as if thinking of something, the word \"no\" got stuck in her throat and simply wouldn't come out.","\"Those so-called divine signs and nursery rhymes outside—does the Lord Marquis know about them?\" Dai Li asked tentatively.","Qin Shaozong's gaze darkened. \"The work of petty men. Who benefits, who did it? This matter is undoubtedly connected to Yanzhou. That scoundrel Fan Tianshi bears a grudge against me for shooting his eldest son, hence these dirty tricks in the shadows.\"","But it had to be said, these underhanded methods, which left almost no evidence, were quite effective. And that children's rhyme, spreading through streets and alleys with the speed of a prairie fire, would certainly cause Nangong Xiong to waver, even if just a little, or perhaps much more.","\"How do you plan to respond?\" Dai Li asked him.","Qin Shaozong: \"Naturally, by admonishing Governor Nangong, tracing the matter to its source, and at the same time dispelling the rumors.\"","Dai Li couldn't bear keeping her neck craned up to talk to him any longer. She had Nianxia pause her task and bring over a soft chair for him. \"The first is easy, but the latter two are each more difficult than the last.\"","A soft chair was moved over, and Qin Shaozong sat down as was convenient. \"The so-called phenomenon of characters appearing on blank paper, this tale of divine guidance being spread is shrouded in mystery. I have only heard of it, never witnessed it with my own eyes. Later, I ordered someone to collect a few sheets of mulberry bark paper, but found nothing unusual about them.\"","How could Qin Shaozong not know this matter was troublesome? The other party had also chosen their timing well, specifically acting while he was away from the city.","By the time he returned, it had already stirred up a citywide uproar. When he questioned the city's military patrols, each and every one of them could give no clear explanation. Some even claimed they had personally witnessed the divine miracle, their expressions and words tinged with no small amount of awe.","This greatly annoyed Qin Shaozong, who didn't believe in fate or gods and spirits in the slightest.","Yet, raising his sword, he looked around in bewilderment, unable to find a single weak point to breach.","Daili seemed thoughtful. \"I've heard the so-called miracle is essentially papers blowing in with the wind. Do all these blown-in papers show characters?\"","\"Not all, only a portion. However, a saying has spread among the people about this, claiming that this 'wordless heavenly book' requires a predestined connection to the immortals to trigger the characters to appear.\" Qin Shaozong snorted disdainfully. \"What predestined connection? It's all just trickery and deception, nothing more than an attempt to drive a wedge between me and Governor Nangong from within.\"","\"You are right,\" Daili said, then asked him, \"My Lord, could you tell me a bit about the miracle the military patrols witnessed? I would like to know as well.\"","Qin Shaozong did not hide it, telling Daili everything the patrols had seen.","Daili's fine eyebrows raised slightly.","Qin Shaozong's narrow eyes suddenly narrowed. \"Does my lady know something?\"","Daili was once again amazed by this man's keen perception. She estimated that even without her, he would have eventually found that hidden, crucial thread. \"Indeed, I do. I know how to break this scheme. However, as payment, I would like you to agree to one thing for me.\"","Unreadable emotions shifted several times in the depths of Qin Shaozong's eyes, finally all concealed within the profound darkness. \"What matter? Please tell me, my lady.\"","\"I would like to request Mr. Nalan to tutor my son for a period of time.\" Since Qin Shaozong was, after all, Nalan Zhi's superior, Daili felt it improper to bypass him and approach Nalan Zhi directly.","It was only later that she learned the Nalan clan had originally been a prominent and influential family in the capital. Nalan Zhi had grown up in silks and satins, surrounded by a retinue of servants, but later everything changed.","The Nalan family fell victim to a villain's scheme. Nalan Zhi's grandfather died of rage on his sickbed. His parents perished en route to exile. His wife, heavily pregnant and unable to endure the rough journey, gave birth prematurely to a baby girl before dying, and the infant could not be saved either.","The first time Daili learned the details, she was stunned for a long while. If not for the ink mark on his face, she truly would have thought Nalan Zhi was no different from any ordinary strategist.","One could only say Nalan Zhi hadn't gone mad. Either his nature was transcendent, exceptionally skilled at untying knots; or he had buried all his hatred deep within to fester, waiting only for a certain day to spew out all the poison and pus.","Judging by Daili's eye for people, she believed Nalan Zhi was likely the former.","And Zhou Zhou just happened to need a psychology teacher.","Qin Shaozong was taken aback for a moment, unable to stop himself from uttering two words, \"That's it?\"","Daili hadn't initially noticed his strange expression and only turned her head upon hearing these two words. \"Yes, that's it.\"","Understanding his confusion, Daili said, \"My Lord, what people seek differs, and the value they see in things is not the same. My son was as worthless as a weed in the eyes of that man surnamed Fan, yet he is the pearl in my palm, cherished and treasured. The dragon-bone waterwheel is a treasure the tenant farmers check several times a day to ensure it remains intact; but to me, it's merely an ordinary wooden frame that draws water.\"","The nobility are obsessed with the saltpeter formula, yet it's nothing but a few sentences from me. If she could use it to exchange for her son's return, Daili wouldn't hesitate for half a moment.","Similarly, the man beside her is a rare, highly sought-after catch in the eyes of many young ladies — a lofty prize they must use every trick and skill to attain.","To her, he is merely a temporary bedfellow.","Alright, a temporary bedfellow and a hotel, a place where she and her son can temporarily hide from the bloodshed and chaos outside.","\"Regarding your son's matter, I'll speak with Wugong and do my best to get him to tell me everything he knows,\" Qin Shaozong said, his gaze intense.","\"No need for all that. I'll discuss the content of the lessons with him myself. You only need to state your position to Mr. Nalan.\" Daili waved her hand.","Qin Shaozong nodded, leaving it to her decision. \"My lady just said you could break the scheme. How should this scheme be broken?\"","Daili: \"Naturally, start from the root. As long as the so-called divine miracle is publicly exposed, the subsequent nursery rhymes can easily be attributed to troublemakers. Then issue a ban against spreading them in the city henceforth, with fines for violators.\"","Hearing her say \"publicly exposed,\" Qin Shaozong raised his long eyebrows. \"It seems my lady has completely grasped this trickery.\"","\"Would you like to see it, my Lord? If you wish, I can demonstrate it for you right now,\" Daili asked him.","It was a very simple little trick, not even requiring much preparation. Speaking of which, she had even played this kind of little experiment with Zhou Zhou before.","Qin Shaozong smiled. \"I would trouble you, my lady.\""]},{"number":60,"title":"Chapter 60","paragraphs":["Dai Li had Bi Po and Nian Xia prepare a few items.","A sheet of mulberry bark paper, a small stove, and two citrons, also known as lemons.","The bedroom already had the small stove and mulberry bark paper; they only needed to go to the kitchen to fetch the lemons.","Bi Po immediately went to the kitchen.","It was just two lemons, no need for a basket. Bi Po took them and headed back. On her return journey, she happened to meet Qin Yanzhou.","The young man was dressed in white, with the wide sleeves of his robe tied back at the arms. A long sword hung at his waist, and he was steaming with heat, having just returned from his morning exercises.","Seeing Bi Po, Qin Yanzhou initially showed no reaction, but when he noticed the lemons in her hand, his steps faltered.","\"Where are you taking those citrons?\" Qin Yanzhou asked proactively.","Bi Po was pleasantly surprised. Since the young master's return, he hardly communicated with anyone other than his mother, speaking very little ordinarily. For him to initiate conversation now was quite rare.","\"The mistress ordered me to prepare them, saying only that they are useful,\" Bi Po replied, not knowing their purpose herself.","The two walked back to the main courtyard together. As they reached the moon gate, Qin Yanzhou saw the two figures sitting side by side in the courtyard.","After Dai Li routinely exchanged a few words with her son, she heard him ask, \"Mother, what are you preparing all these things for?\"","Dai Li did not hide it from him. \"Recently, some deceptive tricks from the jianghu have appeared in the city, and many people have been misled by them. I happened to discuss this with the Marquis today, so I thought I'd explain the details of this trick to him.\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded. \"I see.\"","Dai Li had Qin Shaozong slice the lemons on the newly brought-out small table and then crush them to extract the juice. When he finished, she picked up a wolf-hair brush, dipped it in some of the juice, and wrote the character \"Qin\" on the mulberry bark paper.","She used \"ink\" that was colorless, so after Dai Li finished writing and the paper dried, it showed no abnormality, appearing as if it were still just a plain sheet of paper.","Dai Li asked Nian Xia, \"Is the stove hot?\"","It had been prepared earlier. Nian Xia nodded. \"It's already heated.\"","It was an ordinary small stove used for boiling tea. Now, only charcoal was burning inside, with no pottery kettle placed atop it. Dai Li pressed the mulberry bark paper in her hand against the side of the stove wall.","Immediately, something miraculous occurred. Amidst the exclamations of Nian Xia and Bi Po, the previously blank paper began to change.","A brownish character appeared on it, exactly matching the \"Qin\" character Dai Li had just written.","The two maids couldn't help but gasp in astonishment.","\"It's exactly as Embroiderer Su described before!\"","\"This... if I hadn't seen it with my own eyes, I truly would have thought it a divine miracle! How utterly mysterious!\"","Dai Li smiled. \"What's so mysterious about it? It's just a minor chemical reaction.\"","Lemons contain many sugar-like substances and organic acids. When heated, these substances undergo a dehydration and carbonization reaction, hence the vivid color change.","The incident began with the cook seeing writing appear on paper. The cook was preparing a meal at the time, likely near a stove or fire.","Then, Nian Xia mentioned that Embroiderer Su witnessed a \"miracle\" at a noodle stall, and she said that paper had blown near the stall's stove. Whether noodle soup is heated or not makes a world of difference in taste, and a vendor running a business would surely know this, so there was also a heat source there.","Furthermore, there was the matter Qin Shaozong had just mentioned about the military patrol. The patrol saw the \"miracle\" at a blacksmith's shop, and a blacksmith's forge also satisfies the condition of having a heat source.","Putting these incidents together, finding this common overlapping factor and then deducing the process wasn't difficult.","Dai Li privately believed that among the first group of people who encountered the \"miracle\"—the cook, the noodle stall vendor, and the blacksmith—there must have been some individuals with ulterior motives mixed in. After all, while this trick isn't overly complicated, revealing all the writing isn't entirely without its specific requirements.","She didn't mention the latter part because it was unnecessary. The man beside her was profoundly shrewd, deep as a ten-thousand-fathom ocean trench. She didn't believe he couldn't figure it out.","Qin Shaozong only glanced at the paper before shifting his gaze to Dai Li, looking at her deeply. \"My lady is erudite and talented. I am utterly impressed.\"","Those brown eyes were too deep, like an unfathomable sea, with volcanoes churning fiery magma in its abyss. Though hidden in the depths, they were strikingly conspicuous and searing, leaving one at a loss.","Dai Li averted her eyes and urged him to get back to work. \"Since you now understand the trick behind it, you should hurry and attend to your duties. Don't forget what you promised me earlier once you're done.\"","Even when silent, his presence was overwhelmingly strong. Simply sitting there, he was always difficult to ignore.","\"Accompany me outside the residence to unravel this scheme,\" Qin Shaozong said instead.","Dai Li was taken aback. \"Me too?\"","\"You proposed the strategy. What's wrong with observing it together? We'll go by carriage; you won't have to walk much,\" Qin Shaozong said.","She had been cooped up in the courtyard every day. A few more days, and this lazy fox would probably know exactly how many tiles were in the yard.","Having stayed in for several days, Dai Li did feel a stir of restlessness upon hearing this. She looked at her son beside her. \"Zhou Zhou, would you like to wear a mask and come with me?\"","Not his original ghost mask, but several masks Dai Li later had Nian Xia buy. Some covered half the face, others the full face, kept for unforeseen needs.","Since returning that day, her son hadn't left the residence. Even when traveling by carriage, he wore a mask and spent very little time on the streets. Even if enemies had tracked them to Guoyun County, they likely wouldn't have noticed.","Qin Yanzhou, however, shook his head in refusal. \"Mother, I'll wait for you in the residence.\"","Dai Li hesitated. \"Really not going?\"","Qin Yanzhou still shook his head.","Dai Li had no choice but to relent, her mind turning over what Qin Shaozong had said earlier about the residence not being entirely safe and suggesting she accompany him to the military camp. As the commander-in-chief, especially after shooting Fan Tianshi's son and with war imminent, it was impossible for him to remain in the county for long. He would likely set off for the camp immediately after dealing with the nursery rhyme matter.","That meant, at the latest by this afternoon, she would be able to see Nalan Zhi.","\"Alright then, Zhou Zhou, stay here. Mama will bring you back a souvenir,\" Dai Li said with a smile.","A carriage departed from the Qin residence, heading towards the busiest market in Guoyun County. Just then, the sound of clattering hooves approached.","Qin Shaozong, riding on horseback, turned his head at the noise. He saw a group of riders hurrying in their direction, and the one leading them was none other than Nangong Xiong.","\"Qin Changgeng, you certainly have a leisurely and refined mood,\" Nangong Xiong said, his expression grim.","Recently, nursery rhymes had been spreading throughout the county. The latter line, \"The one in green, dull and dim, easily fooled and incompetent, meets a wretched end in the finale,\" made Nangong Xiong's anger boil.","Even though he knew it was likely the work of schemers, being the esteemed Governor of Qingzhou and having people point fingers calling him stupid and foolish—how could he not be furious! What made him see red with rage was that after the nursery rhymes and \"miracles\" spread, his ally had remained completely silent, offering no response whatsoever.","What, was that scoundrel Qin Shaozong secretly gloating?","If the mountain won't come to me, I'll go to the mountain. Nangong Xiong had intended to have a good talk with his ally, preferably to find a solution. But when everything was ready, scouts reported that Qin Shaozong had returned to the city.","Nangong Xiong was so angry he overturned a table on the spot. Thanks to the strenuous persuasion of his strategist Zhang Mingdian, he managed to suppress his fury somewhat.","Fine! He was going to arrest someone in the city, and today he would surely demand an explanation from Qin Changgeng!","Now that he had rushed to the mansion, he saw Qin Changgeng on horseback, and there was also a carriage beside him that seemed to be carrying female passengers.","As for how he knew they were female passengers, Nangong Xiong had sharp eyes. When the carriage left the mansion, he caught a glimpse of the curtain inside being slightly lifted by the wind, revealing a small piece of apricot - colored clothes of the person in the carriage.","This realization was quite a shock and, like adding fuel to the fire, made Nangong Xiong extremely angry.","Good heavens! While he was getting anxious over there and considering Qin Changgeng's situation, holding back from causing trouble, who would have thought that this guy was not only not worried but also had the mood to take a beauty out for a stroll!","This made him can't help but have deep doubts. Was Qin Changgeng, this ally, really reliable?","Qin Changgeng knew why he had come. \"Nangong, don't be in a hurry. I'm going to solve the matter that concerns both of us this time.\"","Nangong Xiong was slightly stunned. His full - blown anger turned into suspicion, and his eyes wandered between Qin Changgeng and the carriage.","Solve the matter that concerns both of us?","It sounded quite reasonable, but why was there a young lady with him? Could this woman be the great beauty that Qin Changgeng had been hiding like a treasure? This made him a bit curious...","\"Really?\" Nangong Xiong asked.","Qin Changgeng said slowly, \"Seeing is believing. Whether it's true or not, come and take a look and you'll know.\"","Nangong Xiong thought that made sense, so he suppressed his anger again.","So the two teams merged into one and went towards the bustling downtown area together. The Chen hour had passed, and it was now the Si hour. People had just finished their breakfast and were going about their activities, strolling around, doing business, or having fun. It was extremely lively.","Previously, soldiers had been sent on fast horses to make arrangements at the teahouse. Now that Daili's carriage arrived, they didn't even need to ask if there was a private room upstairs. They could just go up.","Daili, wearing a veil hat, got off the carriage, and Qin Changgeng went into the teahouse with her. As soon as they entered, Daili heard someone telling a story in the teahouse.","It was a middle - aged man in a blue robe and a headscarf. He held a folding fan in his hand, and there was a tea cup, some fruits, and a few copper coins on the table in front of him.","At this moment, the man in the blue robe was telling the story with great enthusiasm. \"But on that day, the sky was clear and cloudless. It was a rare fine day. The east - side family was hosting a feast to celebrate the 100 - day birthday of their baby, and the west - side family was celebrating their new move. Just as everyone was in a happy mood, suddenly, a strong wind blew, and several pieces of paper fluttered down from the sky...\"","Qin Changgeng gave a look to Hu Bao behind him. The latter understood and fixed his eyes on the storyteller in the teahouse.","Daili went up to the pre - arranged private room on the second floor.","The private room was clean and tidy. The tables and chairs were elegant. There was a vase with delicate flowers in the corner, and there was also a carved hummingbird bronze incense burner on the small table.","The private room faced the street. Looking out of the open window, one could see the bustling and prosperous scene of carriages and people.","\"Madam, stay in the private room and watch the show. Don't run around.\" Qin Changgeng asked the tea servant to serve tea and then left a few personal guards.","Daili sat by the window. \"Okay, go ahead.\"","When Qin Changgeng came downstairs again, the storyteller was no longer in the teahouse. The man coldly averted his eyes.","Just as the water in the clay pot was boiling, Daili heard the sound of gongs \"clanging\" on the street outside the window.","Hu Bao shouted, \"Folks, there has been a so - called 'heavenly book' swindle in the city recently. The mastermind is trying to spread rumors with it. I hope you folks won't be used by those with ulterior motives and get deceived.\"","The sound of the gong was already eye - catching. Whether it was the vendors doing business or the pedestrians bargaining with the merchants, they all paid attention to it. Coupled with what Hu Bao said later, it instantly attracted the people around like a whirlpool.","So people gradually gathered there, and soon a circle was formed.","People in the circle were whispering to each other.","\"That man is equipped with a sword and there are many guards beside him. It seems that he is most likely from the government.\"","\"The matter of the 'heavenly book' has been making a lot of noise. Now the government says it's a swindle, but I don't think so. How could it be a swindle? There was no one holding a pen at that time, and the words on the paper appeared out of thin air. If it's not a 'heavenly book', what else could it be?\"","\"In my opinion, it's probably the government trying to calm things down and just finding an excuse. Anyway, I still believe it. After all, it's a 'heavenly book'. The 'heavenly book' says...\"","Qin Changgeng and Nangong Xiong were standing in the circle.","Seeing more and more people gathering, and Hu Bao still repeating what he had said before, Nangong Xiong immediately got anxious. \"Is that all? What's the use of just shouting!\"","\"Don't be impatient. Just watch.\" Qin Changgeng said with a smile, folding his arms.","After shouting three times in a row, Hu Bao then changed his words and said, \"Words alone are not enough. Now I'll reveal this swindle to you folks. Please watch carefully!\"","The whispering around suddenly died down.","There were still the simple four items: a piece of paper, a few lemons, a writing brush, and a small stove.","Hu Bao publicly dipped the writing brush in lemon juice and used it as ink to write. After the writing was dried, there was no trace on the paper. \"Just now I wrote the four characters 'Good harvest of all grains'. Now, watch carefully.\"","Not only the surrounding crowd but also Nangong Xiong couldn't help but step forward to see how the words would appear on the empty paper.","Everyone was looking at Hu Bao, except Qin Changgeng.","The man standing in the crowd looked up at this moment, facing the sunlight. He looked at the second - floor window of the teahouse beside him and accurately found the open window.","Daili had taken off her veil hat. At this time, she was looking out of the window, and her eyes met those of the man who suddenly looked up below.","She saw him curl his thin lips. His brown pupils were bathed in the bright and warm sunlight, unexpectedly showing a bit of gentleness that was out of place with his usual self. At this moment, the overbearingness on him seemed to fade a bit in the sunlight.","But when Daili regained her composure and looked again, there was no gentleness at all. His eyes were as hot as ever, as if there was a magma with astonishing heat flowing in his eyes, which could devour all of her flesh and bones.","Daili pursed her lips, suspecting that the look she had just seen was an illusion. Before she could think more, the people below suddenly let out a burst of exclamations.","\"There are words! It's 'Good harvest of all grains'. It's really 'Good harvest of all grains'!\"","\"My goodness! A miracle has descended. Kneel down quickly!\"","\"Kneel your head off! This is a swindle. The soldier just said he wrote 'Good harvest of all grains' on the paper, and now the same words have appeared. What else could it be but a swindle!\"","\"Yes, that's right. So - called 'heavenly book' is all fake. We've been deceived.\"","...","Nangong Xiong was stunned. If he didn't have to consider the face of the prefect, he would have rushed forward, grabbed Hu Bao and asked him all sorts of questions, and then asked him to demonstrate again.","Obviously, Hu Bao didn't just do it once. Later, he even asked the common people for their names and wrote them on the paper one by one.","When their names appeared exactly as they were, the common people around completely believed it.","There was no such thing as a 'heavenly book'. It was really just a swindle. How hateful! They had been deceived so badly before!","At this moment, Hu Bao took the opportunity to bring up the matter of the nursery rhyme and warned the commoners around that, just like the heavenly book, the nursery rhyme was the work of someone with ulterior motives. Children in the family were not allowed to spread it anymore.","Those who violated this rule would be fined fifty coins for the first offense, one hundred coins for the second offense. If there was a third offense, they would be imprisoned and spend a few days in jail.","The onlookers nodded repeatedly and all agreed.","After this \"performance\", Hu Bao led his men to the next bustling area and continued their tour around the county as planned.","As the crowd gradually dispersed, Daili still sat by the window, feeling the cool breeze carry the noise of the mortal world into the room.","Suddenly, that feeling of being watched returned. At first, Daili thought it was Qin Shaozong again. She looked down and saw that Qin Shaozong was talking to Nangong Xiong at the moment.","It wasn't him.","Daili looked around.","This teahouse was located beside a crossroads, with clear views in all four directions. Daili saw the restaurant across the street and the bookstore not far away.","The restaurant had three floors, and each floor had rooms with windows. Some windows were open, while others were completely closed. There were fewer open windows in the bookstore, with only two on the third floor.","On the street, the gradually dispersing pedestrians were all chatting animatedly about what had just happened, and only a very small number were looking around.","Strange. Could it have been just her imagination...","\"Madam.\"","Suddenly, a deep male voice sounded in her ear, and Daili was so startled that she jumped. Before she could jump up from the soft chair by the window, a strong arm encircled her waist.","Just as Daili turned around, she almost bumped into his arms, and her nose hit his chin.","Her eyes immediately turned red. Just as she was about to reach out to cover her nose, a large dark hand moved faster than her. The calloused fingertips touched the bridge of her nose, gently pinched it, and then rubbed the tip of her nose.","\"It's not crooked. It's still very delicate.\"","Daili angrily slapped his hand with a \"pop\". \"Qin Changgeng, can't you make some noise when you walk?\"","The slap she gave was quite loud, but it was completely painless to the thick - skinned man. He immediately laughed and said, \"How could I not make any noise? It's just that madam was too focused just now. When you're fully concentrated, you're as timid as a rabbit.\"","Just as Daili was about to speak, she saw him stretch out his long arm and close the window behind her.","Daili's eyebrows twitched.","Almost at the same moment when the window closed with a \"click\", he leaned over her.","The sudden kiss was very forceful. Daili was trapped on the soft seat. He was in front of her, and his strong arms were on both sides of her. She could only tilt her head back and bear it.","It started with the soft tongues, passionately entangled, from the outside to the inside, and then back to hook her lips and tongue.","The scorching breath swept over like a tidal wave, and the strong masculine aura engulfed her. Daili's mouth and nose were filled with his presence.","Daili was almost crazy. She didn't know what she had done to trigger his nerves. Everything was fine when they left the mansion, but now he was pinning her down in the private room and acting so aggressively.","Her whole mouth was occupied. Daili trembled constantly, and her moans were swallowed by him. This raging wildfire was getting more and more intense. A wisp of silver thread slid down from the corner of her mouth and fell, leaving an amorous spot on the man's black robe.","The long arm that had been encircling her waist slowly tightened. That large hand with distinct knuckles slid along her waistline to the back. Through the not - very - thick summer clothes, it rubbed her waist gently and then more forcefully.","Daili trembled even more. A tingling sensation spread from the base of her spine, making her waist go completely limp, and it seemed as if all her strength was being drained from her waist.","Just when Daili thought she might be taken advantage of right here, the man who was pinning her down backed away.","Qin Shaozong was breathing heavily. There was an impatient scarlet in his eyes, and his gaze was fixed on her without a blink, as if he wanted to devour her.","He raised his hand, and his rough fingertips stroked the corner of her lips, wiping away the faint amorous watermark. \"What were you looking at outside just now, madam?\"","Daili's chest was also rising and falling violently. He asked, but her head was buzzing, and she couldn't answer at all. She just stared at him blankly.","Qin Shaozong laughed. He leaned forward again. This time, he just gently touched her red lips and then backed away. \"Where did your soul go?\"","Daili reached out to push him. It took her a long time to say, \"It's nothing. Have you finished your business, my lord? I want to go shopping and buy some things.\"","\"What do you want to buy?\" he asked.","Daili said, \"I want to buy gifts.\"","In her previous job, she sometimes had to go on short business trips, which usually lasted for one or two days. Every time she went on a business trip, she would entrust her son, Zhou Zhou, to a retired couple of professors in the neighborhood to take care of him for a couple of days.","And every time she came back from a business trip, she would bring a small gift for her son. Sometimes it was a local specialty, and sometimes it was a small toy, so that he wouldn't resist her business trips so much.","Although her son had grown up and might not care about small things anymore, Daili still wanted to bring back those long - gone memories.","As she was thinking about what to buy, she didn't notice that the man in front of her was smiling more and more widely.","\"Buy gifts? That's great.\""]},{"number":61,"title":"Chapter 61","paragraphs":["Nan Gong Xiong had never been so perplexed. Qin Changgeng not going around the commandery with that low-ranking officer surnamed Hu to dispel rumors was one thing, but he was actually idling about, strolling the market with a young lady.","What puzzled Nan Gong Xiong even more was that he himself, as if guided by spirits, had also mounted his horse and followed that carriage.","Unconsciously, the carriage ahead came to a stop, halting in front of a shop selling accessories.","Dai Li had not brought any maidservants on this outing. She pushed the carriage door open herself, intending to alight, but was caught off guard to see Qin Shao Zong standing outside the door.","He extended his hand towards her.","That rough, large palm was turned upward, its lifeline clearly broken in one segment.","The main street was bustling with traffic and crowds; it seemed some people were watching, yet also seemed none were. Qin Shao Zong said nothing, merely gazing steadily at her.","The lady beneath the veil's hat showed no face, her expression unknown. After a moment's pause, she reached out her hand.","The moment her pale fingertips touched his palm, the man proactively moved forward slightly, his large hand closing to envelop her soft, slender hand within his grasp.","\"Did you bring silver?\" Qin Shao Zong asked.","Dai Li nodded, saying she had.","Ever since her biography had been destroyed by him, this man seemed confident she could no longer stir up any trouble. He placed no restrictions on her regarding money.","The doors to the storehouse were wide open, ornaments and other sundries for her to choose at will. Dai Li didn't stand on ceremony with him, nor did she feel any sense of unworthiness. If he dared to give, she dared to take.","After alighting from the carriage, Dai Li withdrew her hand from his and headed straight into the shop.","Qin Shao Zong turned his head to look at Nan Gong Xiong, who was still on horseback beside them. The latter was currently tilting his head, his gaze following that graceful figure, his eyes holding both admiration and curiosity.","Beauty does not lie solely in the face. Observing one's figure, appreciating one's bearing—sometimes a mere silhouette can be breathtakingly beautiful.","No wonder that fellow Qin Changgeng didn't want the dancing girls I prepared for him. So he's really been hiding a great beauty. It's like tasting phoenix marrow and dragon liver and then looking down on mere side dishes...","\"The matter of the children's rhymes is settled, Nan Gong. You can return to the army and prepare. Barring any unforeseen circumstances, we depart the day after tomorrow,\" Qin Shao Zong said.","But Nan Gong Xiong didn't move. \"Qin Changgeng, how did you figure out the trick behind that deception?\"","Qin Shao Zong had also ridden a horse earlier. Now holding a riding crop, upon hearing Nan Gong Xiong's words, he gave the other man a lazy smile.","Nan Gong Xiong's heart skipped a beat, an inexplicable sense of foreboding rising within him. The next moment, his premonition came true. A black riding crop cut through the air, landing a whip on the flank of his steed.","The horse, stung by the pain, immediately bolted forward.","Qin Shao Zong casually rested the whip on his shoulder. \"Nan Gong, you go ahead and get busy. Take care, I won't see you off. I'll tell you about this matter in a couple of days.\"","\"Qin Changgeng, you bastard!\"","Qin Shao Zong let the words go in one ear and out the other. Tossing the riding crop to a guard, he also entered the shop.","...","Inside the shop.","Dai Li, having removed her veil hat, was looking at jade pendants.","In this era, wealthy families, regardless of gender, mostly had the habit of wearing jade pendants. The difference lay in the shapes. Gentlemen wore pendants of green bamboo or fierce beasts, while ladies preferred flowers and birds.","Zhouzhou probably doesn't have a good jade pendant. Buying a jade ornament to bring back for him wouldn't be bad either.","\"This one is not bad, just a bit too elegant,\" someone spoke from beside her.","Dai Li didn't need to turn her head to know it was him offering unsolicited opinions. She ignored him and continued examining the jade pendant in her hand.","The patterns on the front and back were different. The front featured green bamboo, the back an orchid—both were among the Four Gentlemen.","Qin Shao Zong watched her scrutinize it intently, her expression serious and careful, seeming quite satisfied with this jade pendant.","The merchant nearby rubbed his hands together, thinking today brought esteemed guests. This noble lady had asked for the best jade pendant right away; this deal held great promise. \"Madam, this jade pendant is the treasure of our shop. Not to mention the carving, which was commissioned at great expense from the renowned master Fenghai, the seed material itself is exceptionally smooth and lustrous. It is a rare treasure.\"","Qin Shao Zong saw her looking at it again and again, his gaze drifting over once more. \"Alright then. A bit elegant is fine. Military affairs carry heavy killing aura; balancing the two might not be a bad thing.\"","Dai Li paused and turned to look at him.","Her veil hat was already off, and their gazes met without obstruction.","It was only then that Dai Li realized the man was in high spirits. Combined with his earlier comment, she felt he must have misunderstood.","Dai Li: \"...\"","As their eyes met, Dai Li could clearly see Qin Shao Zong's expression, and naturally, he could see hers too.","The curve of Qin Shao Zong's lips fell. The man's narrow eyes narrowed slightly, his gaze sharp, his tone dangerous. \"Madam, surely you aren't thinking of spending my silver, then leaving me out, buying a gift separately for someone else?\"","Those hazel eyes gradually revealed ferocity, as if daring her to nod or utter a single \"yes,\" he would immediately haul her out and head straight back home.","Dai Li: \"...No.\"","Qin Shao Zong lifted his chin slightly. \"Choose then.\"","Dai Li was still holding that piece of jade. She looked around and finally walked over to the area with the Four Treasures of the Study. Besides ink brushes, inksticks, paper, and inkstones, there were also some small ornaments, like paperweights and brush rests.","Qin Shao Zong followed Dai Li over. He saw her pick up a tiger-shaped brush rest, then look at him with a somewhat tentative gaze. \"My Lord, what do you think of this one?\"","Qin Shao Zong laughed in anger.","This brush rest wasn't even the length of a finger, tiny, and something she just picked up casually. The difference in focus compared to when she was looking at the jade was like cloud and mud.","Trying to brush him off, was she?","Seeing his displeasure and the signs of impending anger, Dai Li quickly said, \"Actually, from far away earlier, I saw this tiger-head brush rest. It's carved with such imposing majesty, just like you, My Lord. However, the item is a bit small. I wonder if you might disdain it. If you do, I'll choose something else?\"","Qin Shao Zong paused and took the tiger-shaped brush rest from her hand.","This brush rest was carved from yellow jade, and not even a piece of uniformly yellow jade at that. It had two ink-black lines diffused across it, looking at first glance very much like tiger stripes.","Qin Shao Zong turned it over.","The quality of the jade was average, but rather distinctive. The carving of the tiger head was barely acceptable. Overall, it did bear some resemblance to his own imposing manner.","Dai Li stole a glance at him, then another, surprised to find the man's anger seemed to have subsided. She lowered her head and touched the jade pendant, thinking to herself that this man was actually quite easy to fool in certain aspects.","\"This one it is.\" Qin Shao Zong felt this little trinket was ugly at first glance, but after a few more looks, it grew on him.","After purchasing the gift, the carriage turned back for the estate.","After that carriage departed, a small vendor who had been squatting by the roadside selling goods stood up, stopped selling his wares, picked up his carrying pole, and left.","The street was filled with an endless stream of pedestrians; no one noticed this insignificant scene.","The Qin Residence.","By the time Dai Li returned, Nianxia and Bipo had already packed all her luggage and loaded it onto the carriage.","\"Zhouzhou, this is a gift for you. See if you like it.\" Dai Li called her son over and gave him the brocade box.","Qin Yanzhou took the box and opened it. Inside, resting on red silk, lay a piece of Hetian jade carved with vigorous bamboo stalks. He looked at it for a moment, then, just as he did in childhood, first reached in to feel its inner texture. Only then did the corners of his mouth lift into what, for him, was a clearly perceptible smile. \"I like it. Thank you, Mother.\"","\"Don't mention it,\" Dai Li said with a wave of her hand.","She brought up another matter. To get her son to see a psychologist, besides ensuring the doctor's cooperation, the patient's own willingness was naturally essential. \"Zhouzhou,\" Dai Li said, \"how about I find you a teacher?\"","Qin Yanzhou was slightly taken aback. \"Mother, I know how to read.\"","\"No, it's not about literacy. Reading is about more than just recognizing characters; it broadens one's horizons.\" Afraid he might refuse, Dai Li lowered her voice and played her trump card. \"Learn more things. In the future, when it's just the two of us outside, we might be able to live more comfortably.\"","Sure enough, the young man before her nodded. \"Alright.\"","Dai Li felt a wave of relief.","The luggage was quickly packed. As Dai Li had anticipated, that very afternoon she boarded a carriage and left the city with Qin Shaozong.","This evacuation involved the entire force, and the retreat was executed swiftly and cleanly, not a single soldier left behind.","The convoy departed from the main residence, its wheels rolling westward under the sunlight. As the setting sun bathed the land, they arrived at the military camp outside the city.","The military tent assigned to Dai Li was already pitched. Nianxia and Bipo were busy moving the luggage inside.","Bathed in the warm, fuzzy light of the sunset, Dai Li saw military banners fluttering in the wind. Beneath them, patrols of guards moved in formation, and several familiar figures sat chatting in front of their tents.","It was nearly time for the evening meal, and with no imminent battle, everyone was quite relaxed. Likely, Nalan Zhi was in a similar state.","Dai Li glanced at the man beside her who had not yet left and hinted plainly, \"My Lord, don't you have some words you wish to share with Master Nalan?\"","Qin Shaozong gave a low chuckle. \"What's the hurry, my lady? When have I ever failed to keep a promise I made to you?\"","Despite his words, he headed towards Nalan Zhi's tent.","About a quarter of an hour later, Qin Shaozong emerged. With him came another, slender figure.","Nalan Zhi wore a gray cross-collared robe and held a feather fan. Upon seeing Dai Li, he clasped his fan in a salute. \"Lady Dai.\"","Dai Li returned the courtesy.","Although Qin Shaozong had already given him a general idea, when asking for a favor from someone, no matter what, one still needed to state it personally.","\"Master Nalan, I have a request to make of you,\" Dai Li said, her expression extremely solemn. \"I wish to ask you to instruct my son, to allow him to become your disciple.\"","In ancient times, the status of a \"teacher\" was immensely significant, hence the saying, \"A teacher for a day is a father for a lifetime.\" Particularly for renowned scholars of great prestige, accepting disciples was a very strict process. If they didn't take a liking to you, it didn't matter if you were immensely wealthy or exceptionally talented—they would not accept you.","Nalan Zhi gently waved his feather fan. \"There is one thing I do not understand. Might Lady Dai enlighten me?\"","\"Please, speak freely,\" Dai Li replied.","\"Your own talent and insight are beyond what I can match. Wouldn't your son achieve greater distinction under your personal tutelage? Why, my lady, would you seek the branch and neglect the root?\" Nalan Zhi was puzzled.","He had just heard from Qin Shaozong about the unraveling of the \"divine miracle.\" The mysteries involved were things he had never encountered before, and he once again conceded defeat. So, he couldn't comprehend her reasoning.","Dai Li glanced at Qin Shaozong beside her, reluctant for too many people to learn the details of her son's condition.","Qin Shaozong noticed her look, a vein twitching on his forehead.","He had noticed she had some rather vexing habits, like burning bridges after crossing them. Previously, in Nankang Commandery, she had used him to acquire an extra seal, only to immediately leave him with a complete mess to clean up. Now, having served as her intermediary, she instantly wanted him gone, not even allowing him to listen.","Once the battle for Yanzhou was over, he would definitely teach her a proper lesson and make her correct this infuriating bad habit.","Qin Shaozong gave a cold snort and turned to leave without another word.","Seeing this, Nalan Zhi's fan-waving paused briefly. When he looked back at Dai Li, there was a hint of increased gravity in his demeanor.","With Qin Shaozong gone, only she and Nalan Zhi remained. Dai Li got straight to the point: \"Master Nalan, to be frank with you, since learning of your experiences, I have been deeply impressed by your fortitude. Searching my heart, if I had suffered such trials, I certainly could not have achieved even a tenth of what you have. My son has had a troubled life. After enduring a great calamity, his temperament became entirely different from that of an ordinary young man. I am deeply worried yet feel powerless to change it. I couldn't help but think of your transcendent state of mind, Master, and so I boldly seek your assistance.\"","Afraid the other might find the task too burdensome, Dai Li added, \"You need not teach him astronomy or geography, nor must you impart all your knowledge like other masters. I only wish for you to guide him, to help broaden his perspective.\"","\"I have heard a little about your son's situation. Parents who love their children plan deeply for their future. Regarding guidance, I can only promise to do my best; I cannot guarantee any specific outcome,\" Nalan Zhi said with a sigh.","He had agreed.","Dai Li bowed to him. \"Your agreement alone is a great kindness. I dare not demand anything more.\"","After walking some distance, Qin Shaozong looked back. He saw the two figures standing in the sunset not far away.","At first, Nalan Zhi's feather fan still waved occasionally, but later, after she said something, the fan gradually stilled. He also saw her bow to Nalan Zhi once more.","This time, the other accepted her courtesy.","The importance placed on \"teachers\" in ancient times also meant that the ceremony of becoming a disciple was not a casual affair. The Book of Rites - Shao Yi states: \"Shu Xiu means ten strips of dried meat.\"","This refers to the tuition a student gives to the teacher: ten strips of dried meat. After the teacher accepts the Shu Xiu, the student kowtows and offers tea. The teacher then presents green onions and celery in return, symbolizing that the student should be clever and diligent. Once this process is complete, the teacher-student relationship is formally established.","Unless actively severed, this relationship would last a lifetime.","Shu Xiu: ten strips of dried meat.","Dai Li initially intended to follow the ancient custom. However, when Qin Shaozong learned what she planned to prepare, he said, \"Offering ten strips of dried meat is rather meager. My lady, simply go and tell the army cooks to pick out the ten sturdiest rams. We'll present those ten sheep as the Shu Xiu.\"","Dai Li frowned delicately. \"That doesn't seem quite right. Ten live sheep would be inconvenient to handle. They'd surely end up mixed into the general flock. Over time, who would remember that Master Nalan has ten sheep? He probably wouldn't feel comfortable bringing it up again either.\"","Qin Shaozong said, \"Then slaughter them for a mutton feast.\"","Dai Li's brow remained furrowed. \"You mentioned earlier that we depart the day after tomorrow. If we have a whole mutton feast tomorrow night, wouldn't Master Nalan's ten sheep be counted among them? The Lord orders a mutton feast, the soldiers are grateful to you, but no one knows of Master Nalan's contribution. That's not proper.\"","This whole operation would essentially be moving things from the left hand to the right. Qin Shaozong would still get to host the feast as planned, while Nalan Zhi would end up with nothing.","Forced to donate his tuition—it would all be for naught.","Qin Shaozong clicked his tongue lightly. \"This won't do, that won't do. Fine, we'll separate them. Tomorrow's army-wide mutton feast will be held in the name of Wugong. Additionally, the ten strips of dried meat will be presented separately. Does that satisfy you, my lady?\"","The dried meat is good, but is it worth her always thinking about it?","Daili smiled and said, \"My lord is wise. That is excellent.\"","...","In the blink of an eye, a day passed.","The news that Nalan Zhi was going to take a disciple, and that tonight's meat feast would be even grander because of it, spread through the entire military camp like wildfire.","\"Have you heard? Master Nalan is accepting a disciple today. Because of this, the lord ordered many more cattle and sheep to be slaughtered.\"","\"How could I not have heard? I'm looking forward to it. I'll definitely eat my fill tonight! Speaking of which, there are very few renowned scholars left who haven't taken disciples, you can count them on one hand. I previously thought Master Nalan would remain one of them forever.\"","\"Perhaps he hadn't found anyone suitable before. I heard this time the disciple is a son of the Qin family. His elders seem to have a deep connection with the lord. Come to think of it, I've seen that young gentleman before. His appearance and bearing are beyond reproach.\"","\"A son of the Qin family? What is his name?\"","\"That's not something someone like me can inquire about. Just wait, his reputation will likely spread far and wide before long.\"","...","Inside the tent.","Qin Yanzhou, dressed in white robes, first washed his hands in the basin, then straightened his attire.","Under everyone's gaze, the young man took the ceremonial gifts from Daili's hands, stepped forward, knelt on the cushion, and respectfully presented them with both hands. \"I have long admired your vast learning and profound knowledge of past and present. Your disciple, Qin Yanzhou, wishes to seek your instruction and asks to be accepted as your student. I humbly offer these gifts.\"","\"My learning is not vast. Please, do not demean yourself,\" Nalan Zhi replied as he accepted the gifts.","Qin Yanzhou kowtowed and presented the tea.","The rite completed, Nalan Zhi personally helped the young man to his feet.","With the plan progressing smoothly, Daili let out a sigh of relief and showed a satisfied smile.","Qin Shaozong glanced at her. \"When that boy comes of age for his capping ceremony, we can have Wugong perform the rite for him.\"","Having a great scholar personally perform the capping ceremony was an honor few could claim. Being capped by a renowned scholar benefited one's own prestige and would make the path ahead much smoother.","Daili slowly lowered her eyes.","Her son's capping ceremony was in half a year. Half a year...","Qin Shaozong said, \"It's settled then.\"","After the master-disciple ceremony concluded, a grand meat feast was held in the army.","Military feasts were less formal. Everyone sat around the fire, using long tables that could seat two or more people.","This time, Daili again shared a table with Qin Shaozong. Qin Yanzhou followed his master, while the other high-ranking officers grouped together in twos and threes.","The tables were arranged in a circle around a central bonfire. A split sheep was roasting over the flames, and besides the roast lamb, there were also many skewers of grilled fish. Each table was piled with steamed buns, mantou, rice porridge, and some wild berries.","Compared to the last meat feast Daili had attended, the variety of food this time was much greater.","Daili didn't care for mutton, so she took some grilled fish.","The fish, generously seasoned with fine salt, was very flavorful. Taking a bite of fish followed by a sip of rice porridge, Daili felt thoroughly content.","As this was not a victory celebration but a feast before battle, no one drank wine. Unconsciously, Daili finished her grilled fish.","It was delicious, but after eating two fish in a row, she felt a bit greasy. Daili reached for the wild berries to cut the richness.","As she ate, she listened to the conversations around her. Someone said that conquering Qijiang County wouldn't be difficult; the real challenge was White Sun City behind it, which was guarded by a strategic pass ahead.","This pass faced the Jin River to the north, was backed by a series of high mountains called the \"Red Horn\" range to the south, with only a single path wide enough for carts and horses in between.","Listening on, Daili finished her own portion of wild berries. She licked her lips, feeling a bit unsatisfied.","Suddenly, a small plate filled with wild berries was placed before her.","Daili was slightly startled. Her gaze followed the long, sun-browned fingers holding the edge of the plate upwards, meeting a pair of brown eyes reflecting the firelight.","Daili reached out to take it, but saw those long fingers retract slightly, pulling the plate back with them.","\"There's no such thing as a free meal in this world, my lady. Say something nice,\" he said.","Daili hesitated. \"...Thank you for your magnanimity.\"","His expression remained the same as before, not showing displeasure, but the plate wasn't pushed forward either. It seemed her words hadn't quite met his expectation.","Daili fell silent for a moment, then suddenly had an inspiration. \"Then I wish my lord a triumphant victory tomorrow.\"","Qin Shaozong curled the corner of his mouth into a smile and pushed the plate over. \"I accept your auspicious words.\""]},{"number":62,"title":"Chapter 62","paragraphs":["Qingzhou, Qijiang County, Fan Manor.","The door creaked open as someone entered, then cupped their hands in salute towards the young man brewing tea inside the room.","\"Sir Diting, the 'divine miracle' affair has been exposed.\" The person then recounted in full detail the incident of Hu Bao beating gongs and drums in the marketplace.","A look of surprise crossed Diting's face, his fingertips tapping rapidly on the table a few times. \"In just four days, Marquis Wu'an moves with such speed.\"","The informant continued, \"After the failed reconnaissance of the Qin residence the night before last, before we could take a second action, Marquis Wu'an returned to Guoyun County yesterday morning. That same day, he took Lady Dai out of the manor to witness the debunking of the divine miracle. The rumors are true; the woman is indeed stunningly beautiful and deeply favored by the Marquis. However, yesterday afternoon, she accompanied the Marquis to the military camp. Simultaneously, all personnel have evacuated the Qin residence.\"","Diting's eyebrows moved slightly.","With Lady Dai now inside the military camp, there would likely be no opportunity to act against her in the short term.","Diting inquired about another matter, \"The task I assigned you earlier, is it done?\"","That person took out two pieces of mulberry bark paper from his bosom and presented them with both hands. \"Please have a look, sir.\"","Diting took them and unfolded the papers.","If Nianxia and Bipo were here, they would surely be greatly alarmed, for the portraits on these two papers were unmistakably theirs.","The painter's skill was remarkable, achieving a nine-tenths likeness.","The man said, \"The maid with round eyes is slightly shorter, about six chi and seven cun tall, slim build, yellowish skin. The one with long eyes is taller, about seven chi, average build, fairer skin. The embroiderers have all seen both of them.\"","Diting set the papers down. \"Have the embroiderers personally go to Yinwan to select candidates, then help them adjust their appearances.\"","The man nodded in acknowledgment of the order.","\"With all personnel evacuated from the Qin residence, it seems he...\" Diting's words halted halfway as someone hurried in from outside.","Knowing his rules, that person stopped outside without entering. \"Sir Diting, Lord Fan requests your presence.\"","Diting rose from his seat, picked up a silver Buddhist-patterned mask nearby to cover his overly youthful face, and simultaneously said to the informant, \"Go inform the embroiderer first. That matter is not urgent; have her work meticulously, striving for perfection.\"","This indicated the orders were complete.","The informant withdrew.","Guided by guards, Diting proceeded to the study in Fan Manor.","Three people were already in the study: the Fan father and son, and Shi Wuji.","Seeing Diting, the host Fan Tianshi greeted him cordially. \"Sir Diting, have you settled in these past two days at the manor? If there are any shortages, please feel free to speak with the servants.\"","\"Everything is excellent,\" Diting replied, his tone as pleasant as a spring breeze.","Fan Tianshi got to the point. \"Previously, sir, you mentioned having a method to keep Qin Shaozong fully occupied. Now, it seems that method has failed.\"","The events in Guoyun County had not escaped Fan Tianshi's notice.","This statement carried a hint of questioning and displeasure, which Diting naturally detected. His tone remained calm. \"In a game of chess, moves are exchanged. What harm is there in conceding him one move?\"","\"Then, in your esteemed opinion, what should the next move be?\" Fan Zhongmin asked.","Diting: \"Concede another move. Withdraw from Qijiang County.\"","Fan Tianshi's gaze shifted sideways to Shi Wuji, who gave a slight nod.","Outskirts of Qijiang County.","A great wind suddenly rose this day, howling fiercely, as two different army banners snapped and fluttered violently in the gale.","Qin Shaozong wore a golden-patterned taotie helmet and golden armor, holding a three-meter-long silver Overlord's Spear. His crimson cape billowed behind him like flame, making him exceptionally conspicuous among the ten thousand troops.","Riding abreast with him was the similarly armored Nan Gongxiong. Military commanders often have burly builds, and he was no exception, currently holding a tang weapon, his presence imposing.","Not far away, the gates of Qijiang County were tightly shut. Banners fluttered atop the city walls, where a line of defending soldiers stood.","Qin Shaozong raised his head to survey the scene, his eyes sweeping across the battlements. \"Something's amiss,\" he said.","\"What's wrong?\" Nan Gongxiong hadn't given it much thought. What trouble could a mere Qijiang County possibly stir up?","Qin Shaozong called out two men. \"Feng Feng, Bai Jianping, step forward and issue the challenge.\"","Two riders detached from the ranks and advanced.","Not to be outdone, Nan Gongxiong also dispatched a commander from his side to join them.","The words of challenge were never pleasant, counting ancestors and insulting families, starting naturally with the leader, Fan Tianshi.","After a round of insults, the city gates indeed opened.","A single rider charged out from within. The man had thick eyebrows, a prominent nose, dark skin, and bore a fifty percent resemblance to Zang Yinghao, whom Qin Shaozong had slain with his blade during the previous tripartite meeting.","Zang Yingjie rode out alone, shouting fiercely, \"Where is Marquis Wu'an?!\"","Feng Feng scoffed. \"Looking for our Lord Marquis? Are you worthy, you runt? Get past your grandfather here first!\"","Shi Wei, under Nan Gongxiong's command, grew impatient. Unwilling to waste more words, he clamped his legs against his horse's flanks and charged forward, broadsword in hand.","Feng Feng and Bai Jianping knew the other side wanted to seize credit, but with Shi Wei already engaged, they had no choice but to hold back.","\"These Qingzhou men are unruly, charging ahead without even a word.\"","\"The man from Yanzhou looks quite capable. No rush, let's watch a bit longer.\"","As the two exchanged whispers, the combatants ahead had already clashed.","Shi Wei used a broadsword, while Zang Yingjie wielded a horse lance. The saying goes, 'an inch longer, an inch stronger.' On horseback, the horse lance's power was formidable. Shi Wei fought over a dozen rounds with his opponent without gaining any advantage.","\"You from Qingzhou, fall back! Let me take your place!\" Feng Feng bellowed.","Whether his shout distracted Shi Wei in the thick of battle or Shi Wei had simply reached his limit, his broadsword was sent flying from his grasp.","The long blade spun through the air before thudding into the ground.","Shi Wei hastily wheeled his horse around, urging it to flee before the lance could strike. Seeing this, Zang Yingjie laughed heartily, his morale soaring.","\"Cease your arrogance, you runt!\" Feng Feng spurred his horse forward. He used a halberd, also a long weapon. Long against long, the weapon advantage was neutralized, leaving it to personal skill.","At the front of the formation not far away, Qin Shaozong was still observing the city walls. He suddenly remarked, \"This is an abandoned city.\"","\"What?\" Nan Gongxiong responded. \"You mean Fan Tianshi is retreating without a fight? But abandoning a city and fleeing would damage morale, wouldn't it?\"","\"Look, the number of soldiers on the walls is pitifully few. If you were Fan Tianshi, knowing a combined force from two sides was coming to attack you, would you deploy so few men? Sometimes, avoiding a direct confrontation is also a strategy,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Nan Gongxiong peered at the city walls.","He hadn't noticed before, but looking carefully now, it was indeed true.","He gave a start. \"Then we must attack the city quickly, or they'll get away.\"","\"They're long gone. You think they'd wait for you to reach their doorstep before running?\" Qin Shaozong looked towards Zang Yingjie, who was locked in combat with Feng Feng.","The distance wasn't too great; he could clearly see the Yanzhou commander's features. Combined with the man's immediate demand for him upon emerging, this person was likely related to the Yanzhou commander he had slain a few days prior.","For the sake of revenge, this man had volunteered to be the sacrificial pawn.","Not far away, the battle had already been decided. Zang Yingjie's horse lance was knocked away, and Feng Feng's long halberd pierced the opponent's shoulder blade first.","Nan Gongxiong suddenly heard the person beside him give a light chuckle. He was about to get annoyed, thinking this fellow must be mocking him, but unexpectedly heard him whisper, \"She truly spoke auspicious words. A victorious start.\"","\"Qin Changgeng, what are you muttering about?\" Nan Gongxiong asked.","Qin Shaozong merely said, \"Let's begin the siege. Barring any surprises, we can take it within half an hour at most.\"","Siege ladders and battering rams were deployed, soldiers swarming like a tidal wave. Three quarters of an hour later, the gates of Seven Rivers County swung wide open.","Both armies dispatched small teams inside to clear the area.","Proclamations to reassure the people were issued, enemy remnants were cleared out, and by sunset, Seven Rivers County was fully secured.","The place where Fan Tianshi had once stayed was now empty, conveniently providing lodging for Qin Shaozong and Nan Gongxiong.","...","In the study.","A massive sheepskin map was spread out, clearly depicting the various counties and commanderies along the border of Qing and Yan provinces.","To the west of Seven Rivers County lay a strategic pass. This pass guarded the approach to White Sun City, hence it was also called White Sun Pass.","This pass faced the Jin River to the north and was backed by towering peaks to the south, effectively pinched between a river and a mountain range. The official road through the middle was extremely narrow, only allowing small groups to pass, unsuitable for large troop movements.","\"One man can hold the pass against ten thousand! Qin Changgeng, this White Sun Pass won't be easy to take.\" Nan Gongxiong's expression was grave.","Qin Shaozong's gaze shifted between the Jin River and the Red Horn Mountains. \"Tomorrow, you and I will go out.\"","Nan Gongxiong pressed, \"Go where?\"","Qin Shaozong looked out the window. The twilight was in its final moments, leaving only a faint, almost illusory glow in the sky. Anyone could tell night was about to fall.","Traveling at night inevitably required torches, which were too conspicuous and easily drew attention.","\"You'll know tomorrow,\" Qin Shaozong simply said.","Nan Gongxiong grumbled, \"So secretive.\"","The moon rose and set, and in the blink of an eye, the night passed. Nan Gongxiong, being a military man, rose early for morning drills, his timing almost coinciding with Qin Shaozong's, and they bumped into each other.","After the drills, it was time for breakfast.","Seeing the large basin of buns brought out, Nan Gongxiong asked in surprise, \"What are these?\"","They weren't like flatbreads; flatbreads weren't this plump.","\"Baozi. Someone at home came up with them. The taste is excellent. Try one,\" Qin Shaozong said with a smile.","Nan Gongxiong was half doubtful.","Excellent taste?","He, the prestigious Governor of Qing Province, what delicacies hadn't he tasted?","Yet the first bite nearly made him swallow his tongue. He immediately stopped talking and busied himself stuffing the bun into his mouth.","After the meal, Qin Shaozong called for Hu Bao. \"Hu Bao, go to the camp outside the city and relay my order. Tell Qiao Wangfei to escort the lady into the city.\"","Hu Bao was just about to clasp his hands and accept the order when he heard his superior change his mind. \"Never mind. Seven Rivers County is newly acquired. Let's discuss this again in a few days.\"","\"Qin Changgeng, is this 'lady' you speak of the one named Dai?\" Nan Gongxiong had heard the name before. Looking at the empty porcelain plate on the table, he suddenly guessed, \"Earlier you said 'someone at home,' could it also be her?\"","Qin Shaozong said yes and stood up to go to the stables.","Nan Gongxiong followed him to the stables, talking as they walked. \"I recall you've been widowed for over a decade. Are you thinking of remarrying? The surname Dai isn't a major one. I haven't heard of any prominent noble families with that surname. So she's from a humble background? Tsk, for such a one, just take her as a concubine. Don't go through the formalities of marriage.\"","Qin Shaozong's temple twitched.","Nan Gongxiong continued, \"Your late wife's maternal family, the Weis, are not to be trifled with. And if I remember correctly, the Weis made an agreement with you back then, and they were quite proud of it for a long time...\"","\"I think for the upcoming battle, we needn't mobilize the troops. We could just send you to the front of the pass and have you flood White Sun City with your saliva,\" Qin Shaozong said as he led his horse, Red Serpent, out of the stable.","\"Just reminiscing a bit about old times. Why are you getting so annoyed?\" Nan Gongxiong also went to fetch his horse. \"By the way, I forgot to ask earlier. Is Quanjie really your man?\"","Qin Shaozong: \"He is not my inside agent.\"","\"Hah, in that case, I must settle the score with that brat. Daring to touch my Qing Province tribute? I'll skin him alive and tear him bone from bone, make him regret ever being born into this world,\" Nan Gongxiong said viciously, riding out of the residence alongside him.","Qin Shaozong: \"Can you find him?\"","\"Didn't Fan Tianshi issue a wanted poster? I thought the drawing on it was quite accurate. Searching based on that should work, right?\" Nan Gongxiong said.","Qin Shaozong said calmly, \"Don't bother looking. Whatever losses your Qing Province suffered, I will compensate you threefold.\"","This statement shocked Nan Gongxiong thoroughly. He subconsciously reined in his horse, only to see Qin Shaozong continue forward. He quickly urged his horse to catch up. \"You'll compensate me? Why? That brat is no relation of yours. Why go to such lengths? Qin Changgeng, were you lying to me just now? Quanjie is clearly your inside agent.\"","\"He is or he isn't. What's the point of lying?\" Qin Shaozong kept his eyes ahead.","Nan Gongxiong changed his approach: \"He's not your inside agent, but at the very least, he has some connection to you now. That much is correct, isn't it?\"","Qin Shaozong remained silent.","Nan Gongxiong scoffed coldly. \"Fine, don't tell me. I can find out myself. It'll just take a bit more time.\"","\"That young man does indeed have some connection to me. He is a son of the Qin clan,\" Qin Shaozong said, not mentioning he was Dai Li's son.","Nan Gongxiong was puzzled. \"Quanjie is a son of the Qin clan? How do you know this? Wasn't he taken into the Fan family around age eleven or twelve?\"","\"That day he came to assassinate me. I captured him alive. When I pulled off his face covering, his features looked very familiar, reminding me of an old acquaintance. Upon careful questioning later, I learned he was abducted as a child and, after passing through several hands, was adopted by Fan Tianshi,\" Qin Shaozong glossed over the details.","Nan Gongxiong marveled at the twists and turns, then laughed. \"Earlier we said Quanjie wanting to change his fate was harder than being reborn. Who would have thought fate works in mysterious ways, and he ran into you to clean up his mess. Besides the threefold compensation, I also want ten cartloads of saltpeter, a thousand shi of grain, and three hundred fine-breed horses.\"","Qin Shaozong glanced at him. \"Once settled, the matter is closed for good?\"","Nan Gongxiong: \"Naturally.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"Done. Agreed.\"","Seeing him agree so readily, Nan Gongxiong thought to himself he should have asked for more. In these times, horses were precious, especially fine-breed ones. Three hundred were enough to form a small cavalry unit, and a thousand shi of grain could feed three hundred men for seven and a half months.","Thinking of this, Nan Gongxiong felt an itch. \"Which old acquaintance's son is Quanjie, that you're so willing to pay such a price?\"","As they spoke, they passed through the west gate, leaving the clamor behind.","Not getting an answer, Nan Gongxiong asked again.","Still no answer.","\"What's so unspeakable? Could it be that old acquaintance is a woman, and moreover, your lover?\" Nan Gongxiong deliberately provoked him.","Qin Shaozong: \"We're here. Dismount.\"","Nan Gongxiong gave a light tsk but didn't press further, nimbly swinging down from his horse.","They had headed southwest after exiting the West City Gate and had now arrived at the foot of Red Peak. After handing the horses over to their personal guards for safekeeping, Qin Shaozong led the men in beginning the ascent.","All of them were military officers, accustomed to such rugged paths, so it took them just over two hours to climb most of Red Horn Peak, though this was merely its main hump. From a prominent, jutting cliff, one could gaze out at the endless stretch of mountains, a majestic, continuous range extending far into the distance, with no city in sight for hundreds of miles.","\"Qin Changgeng, this route is impassable!\" Nangong Xiong also saw that unbroken expanse and immediately frowned.","This was completely pristine, untamed mountain terrain with no cleared paths, making it impossible for horses to travel. Without horses, supplying provisions became a major problem.","Nangong Xiong said, \"Taking the mountain paths won't work. Perhaps we should follow the Jin River upstream instead. My scouts report that about thirty li upstream, there's a relatively gentle access point. We could build boats to cross the river and land there, thus bypassing that narrow pass where ten thousand men couldn't force their way through.\"","Qin Shaozong stared ahead for a long moment before withdrawing his gaze. \"Let's go take a look at the upper reaches of the Jin River.\"","The group descended the mountain back to their starting point, mounted their horses, and rode to the Jin River. Without a moment's pause, they found a boat, boarded it, and traveled upstream.","The boat advanced against the current for about thirty li per day. After a day on the water, Qin Shaozong saw the relatively gentle access point Nangong Xiong had mentioned.","Nangong Xiong wasn't wrong. Compared to the other sheer cliffs lining the banks, this spot was indeed somewhat gentler.","But it was only somewhat.","This \"gentle\" landing was no more than ten meters wide, at best allowing two medium-small boats to dock side-by-side. Beyond the landing stretched a steep slope several dozen meters long. Looking further inland, one could see the banners planted by the Yanzhou army.","Clearly, the enemy also knew this was a vulnerable point and had stationed troops to guard it day and night.","\"Wheee—\"","Their boat had only lingered in the river near the landing area for a short while when a sharp whistle sounded from the shore.","Banners fluttered as soldiers began moving toward them.","\"The guard is quite tight. It seems they've stationed significant forces here. Let's head back for now,\" Nangong Xiong urged the soldiers to sail the boat away.","Returning from the Jin River to Qijiang County, Nangong Xiong was lost in gloomy thought, even the steamed bun he was eating seemed to have lost some of its flavor. As he ate, it belatedly occurred to him that Qin Shaozong had also been unusually quiet for a long time.","Finding some bitter comfort in having company for his worries, Nangong Xiong said, \"That battle you fought up north was brilliant. The world calls you the God of War. So, God of War, what's your brilliant idea now?\"","Nangong Xiong expected Qin Shaozong to either shake his head or retort with some sharp words—the man could be truly cutting at times. To his surprise, Qin Shaozong said, \"Nangong, I have an idea. If it succeeds, we will definitely take White Pass.\"","Nangong Xiong's burly frame jolted. \"Truly?\"","Qin Shaozong finished the last bite of his bun, then picked up the teacup beside him and drained it in one gulp. \"Come to the study after you finish your meal.\"","With that, he left the table first.","Nangong Xiong couldn't bear the suspense. He immediately grabbed his bun and followed him."]},{"number":63,"title":"Chapter 63","paragraphs":["In the study.","The large parchment map was still spread out on the desk. Nan Gongxiong couldn't wait, \"What idea do you have? Speak quickly.\"","Qin Shaozong first pointed at the city of Bairi on the map, then dragged his long finger backward, landing behind Bairi City. \"Bairi City's front is Bairi Pass, flanked by high peaks. Therefore, Fan Tianshi's grain depot must be here in the rear.\"","Both being seasoned on the battlefield, Nan Gongxiong immediately grasped his meaning upon hearing this. \"You want to launch a surprise attack on Fan Tianshi's grain depot?\"","Qin Shaozong nodded. \"Once the grain depot is burned, Yanzhou's army will surely fall into chaos. Then we can take advantage of the momentum to attack, and Bairi Pass can be breached.\"","Nan Gongxiong's brows furrowed so deeply they could crush a fly.","Burn Yanzhou's grain depot?","How could that be easy? Their depot is in the rear, but just getting past Bairi Pass is daunting enough.","Qin Shaozong first pointed at a location along the Jinshui River where the terrain was gentle. \"Dispatch a large army to build ships extensively on the opposite bank of this spot, and use iron chains to link the ships together, forming a pontoon bridge. The shipbuilding should be a grand spectacle, lasting for many days. Fan Tianshi will certainly think we've chosen that place as our breakthrough point.\"","His dark, long finger slid across the map, pointing at Chijiao Peak. Qin Shaozong said in a deep voice, \"Meanwhile, send several thousand soldiers up Chijiao Peak, travel via mountain paths to secretly circle around to their rear, and catch them by surprise.\"","\"Have you gone mad?\" Nan Gongxiong was incredulous.","His reaction was intense. \"Qin Changgeng, do you know what kind of place that is? Desolate and uninhabited, with no roads! Let me ask you, horses can't go up, so how do you handle provisions? Setting aside the rugged mountain paths, the entire mountain range stretches for hundreds of miles. Especially as the vanguard pushes deeper, can supplies be delivered relying solely on manpower? Once that supply line is cut, it's tantamount to trapping those men to die in the mountains.\"","\"Carve a path through mountains, build bridges across rivers.\" Qin Shaozong only said these eight words.","Hearing his resolve, Nan Gongxiong gritted his teeth. \"Fine, you insist on doing it this way, right? Then I'll handle the shipbuilding. The task of raiding the grain depot is yours.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"Agreed. I will personally lead the surprise attack force.\"","Although the other had agreed, Nan Gongxiong still had a thousand worries. \"Are you really going to do this? Let me tell you, a single misstep with this method could mean a one-way trip. The difficulty of traversing the mountains and the supply issues aside, wild beasts frequently appear in the mountains, and it's extremely easy to lose your way. And think about it, Qin Changgeng, even if you do manage to reach their rear, your men will be utterly exhausted by then, while Fan Tianshi's troops are well-rested and prepared. If you were captured alive...\"","If Qin Shaozong were captured alive, the Northlands would be finished.","\"Capture me alive?\" Qin Shaozong said mockingly, \"The one who can capture me alive hasn't been born yet.\"","Nan Gongxiong wore an expression of mixed exasperation. \"Don't be so arrogant. Those who love to talk like that often end up capsizing in a ditch.\"","Qin Shaozong only sneered.","\"Speaking of which, Qin Changgeng, what personal grudge do you have with this Fan Tianshi that you'd risk your life playing this game with him?\" Nan Gongxiong asked curiously.","He, Nan Gongxiong, considered himself a hero, but he truly didn't dare lead troops along that Chifeng path. He was unfamiliar with the terrain, the mountain road was long, and he had no confidence at all.","There were many ways to attack a city. The pontoon bridge Qin Changgeng mentioned earlier was also a good plan. Building a bridge across the Jinshui would allow soldiers to cross continuously. Although it would certainly be a bitter fight, it wasn't without chance of victory.","Taking a treacherous mountain path for hundreds of miles was hard enough, but then having to penetrate deep into enemy territory afterward? What was that if not playing with one's life?","Qin Shaozong paused, then scoffed. \"What personal grudge could there be? I just find him an eyesore. This matter is settled. I will allocate a portion of the Northlands army to you to assist with shipbuilding, creating the illusion that I am still here. All actions commence tomorrow.\"","Since he didn't have to take the risk himself, Nan Gongxiong was naturally happy to follow the arrangement.","Chijiao Peak.","A column of soldiers clad in black armor marched along the mountain path. At most, two could walk abreast, one following another, looking from afar like a long, winding snake moving through the mountains.","Silently, unnoticed, they blended completely into nature. Only the birds in the sky or the beasts in the forest sensed the presence of these outsiders in the mountains.","The vast majority of the column carried two packs, one on the chest and one on the back, with water skins hanging from their waists. This kind of load would likely cause an ordinary man to walk for barely an hour or two before collapsing from exhaustion, seeing black spots.","But this elite force was the Xuanxiao Cavalry, the most renowned in the Northlands. Every man was in top physical condition. Although heavily burdened, their stamina far exceeded that of ordinary men; they wouldn't be drenched in sweat after just a short walk.","At the very front of the column were soldiers serving as engineers.","They carried no provisions, only tools. Whenever they encountered difficult terrain, the engineers would carve paths through the mountains, using long knives to cut suitable-sized timber to lay on the ground, building plank roads.","Qin Shaozong was at the head of the column, watching the engineers clear the way ahead. Whenever they encountered a particularly tough spot, he would step forward personally.","The long column wound its way, leaving marks wherever it passed. At regular intervals, high-ranking officers marched with them. All four commanders of the Xuanxiao Cavalry were present, arranged in order from east, south, west, to north along the line.","The marching rations were parched grain and dried meat. When tired, they would take a sip of water and bite into the parched grain. Once slightly recovered, they pressed on without a moment's pause.","As the sun rose and set, and as the vanguard Xuanxiao Cavalry clearing the path were rotated in shifts, the packs on the soldiers' backs gradually lightened.","Hundreds of miles of mountain path, and unknowingly, a small portion was behind them.","Qin Shaozong gazed into the distance. Ahead was an endless expanse of lush green, stretching as far as the eye could see.","\"Those behind, keep up.\" The man's voice was low and firm.","North of the Jinshui River.","Nan Gongxiong led the two armies to the riverbank. They set up camp about two miles from the river, where the banners of both the Northlands and Qingzhou fluttered side by side.","Once the camp was established, Nan Gongxiong immediately mobilized the army to build ships.","With great ambition and fanfare, he paid no heed to the Yanzhou soldiers who occasionally came to scout in small boats, clearly unconcerned whether the enemy knew his strategy.","After all, it was a direct assault; knowing or not knowing made little difference.","Every day, Yanzhou soldiers on the opposite bank of the Jinshui climbed to high points to observe across the river, then relayed the intelligence back to the pass.","\"Lord Fan, it's the third day. They have been building ships continuously. Besides the ships, scouts also reported seeing them transport large quantities of iron chains and cables to the army,\" the head scout reported.","Fan Tianshi frowned. \"Iron chains and cables? What's the use for those?\"","\"My lord, could they be planning to link the ships with iron chains? Linking ships with iron chains and then laying planks on top could form a pontoon bridge,\" Shi Wuji reminded him.","\"So they are dead set on breaching the pass,\" Fan Tianshi sneered, then turned to ask Shi Wuji, \"Liuxian, do you have a countermeasure?\"","Shi Wuji stroked his beard. \"Though the allied forces of the Northern Lands and Qingzhou are fierce, there is only one pontoon bridge. As long as we destroy the bridge, unless they fill the Jin River with their own bodies, they absolutely cannot cross. As for destroying the bridge, that's not difficult either. Find a group of soldiers skilled at swimming to dive into the river, bore holes in the bottoms of their boats, and then attack with fire.\"","Fan Tianshi immediately brightened up. \"Liuxian, you are truly resourceful and wise. Good, let's do it that way!\"","\"However, my lord, it is currently summer with abundant rainfall. Moreover, their pontoon bridge does not stretch for miles, making it relatively easier to put out fires. A fire attack is not a sure thing,\" Shi Wuji added.","Fan Tianshi's smile did not diminish. \"If heavy rain falls then, it won't be a problem. Isn't there still the plan to bore holes in the boats? And heavy rain will certainly churn the river waters more fiercely. Regardless, it's a two-pronged approach. If they dare to come, we will surely make them fall head over heels and feed the fishes.\"","Setting aside boring holes and fire attacks, just that several dozen meters of steep slope alone would be enough to give them a hard time. By then, shooting arrows from above or rolling down giant boulders would certainly block their advance.","Unable to advance, and with no boats to retreat to, we will kill as many as come!","After the discussion, he gave the order, and the entire army quickly began preparing tung oil.","...","Fan Residence, Guest Courtyard.","An elegant sandalwood incense, blended to calm the mind, wafted through the refined side room. Amidst the haze of the fragrance, rhythmic knocking sounds came from within.","Listening carefully, the sound resembled several copper coins colliding with a shell.","Suddenly, the knocking stopped.","It turned out the copper coins from the tortoise shell had all fallen onto the ground.","Diting, kneeling on a prayer mat, lowered his gaze to look at the scene before him, quickly combining it with the previous five casts to form a complete six-line hexagram.","His expression gradually darkened.","Great misfortune.","As if unwilling to accept it, Diting put down this black tortoise shell, stood up, and took another tortoise shell from a chest in the room.","This time he did not shake copper coins. Instead, he took a small, red-hot iron rod and pierced it into the tortoise shell. Black fire patterns rapidly spread across the shell, branching and forking at certain nodes.","After a few breaths, the black fire patterns stopped, imprinted on the tortoise shell like a tree with only branches.","It was still great misfortune.","Diting's pupils contracted slightly. He abruptly stood up and said to the attendant outside, \"Bring me the map of the Bai Ri City area.\"","The map was quickly delivered and spread out on the table.","Diting stared at the map, his gaze moving from Bai Ri City to Bai Ri Pass, then to the Jin River, to the nearby Red Horn Peak, and finally settling on the Yanzhou army's camp.","\"Sir, is there something wrong?\" the attendant asked.","Diting pondered for a moment. \"Do you know, besides entering through Bai Ri Pass, where else the allied forces could come from?\"","The attendant had heard about Fan of Yanzhou's massive preparations of tung oil. Recalling the heavy troops stationed at the Jin River bank, he replied, \"There is one section of the Jin River with relatively gentle terrain, which could serve as an entry point. But please rest assured, sir, Lord Fan is well-prepared for this. I heard he has collected a great deal of tung oil and ordered men to quarry stones from the mountains.\"","Diting fell into thought, looking at the map again.","Both the Jin River side and the pass were heavily guarded and fully prepared. Logically, it shouldn't be like this...","Could it be that the Northern Lands and Qingzhou are not coming from these two places?","If not, that rules out the east and north, leaving the west and south. The west is Yanzhou, the rear base camp. Unless they have grown wings, it's absolutely impossible for them to attack from the west.","Then it's the south?","\"Is it possible to march through this continuous stretch of mountains?\" Diting asked.","The attendant instinctively said, \"Impossible. This area is desolate and uninhabited. It stretches for hundreds of miles, all mountains, with no paths to take.\"","But after speaking, the attendant added, \"Sir, I don't understand matters of military campaigns. I suggest you go ask Lord Fan.\"","Diting picked up the silver-white mask from the table and put it on. \"You're right.\"","...","\"Impossible!\" Fan Tianshi flatly denied.","His second son, Fan Zhongmin, was also in the room. Unlike his father's resolute tone tinged with a hint of mockery, he took the initiative to explain to Diting.","Fan Zhongmin said, \"Sir Diting, you may not know this, but Red Horn Peak is not just a single mountain peak. It stretches continuously; you could call it a mountain range. The terrain here is terrifyingly high, with rugged mountain paths and sheer cliffs—so steep even monkeys would despair at climbing them. It's extremely difficult just to travel through, let alone carrying military supplies.\"","Finally, Fan Zhongmin shook his head. \"That's why Father says it's impossible.\"","Diting: \"Better safe than sorry. Why not station a troop at the foot of the Red Horn Peak mountains to guard against any surprise troops coming through the mountain paths?\"","But Fan Tianshi said, \"The foothill line of Red Horn Peak is extremely long. Stationing troops to guard it is no easy task. If any spot is missed, it's completely the same as having no guard at all. And as my son said, this mountain area is a death zone, desolate and uninhabited. The enemy absolutely cannot come through here. Rather than wasting a large force on such a useless endeavor, it's better to use the troops to prepare incendiary materials.\"","Diting wanted to say more.","Fan Tianshi saw his intention: \"There's no need for you to worry about military matters, sir.\"","Diting sighed.","...","The dusk gradually faded, night fell, and deep black spread across the entire sky. When night first began, there was still a bright moon, but as time passed, the moon gradually hid.","In this utterly silent night, however, faint rustling sounds came from the mountains of Red Horn Peak.","Qin Shaozong pushed aside the forest leaves, looking down at the camp below with its glowing fires. The man's brown eyes now seemed tinged with a bit of that firelight, reflecting a wolf- or tiger-like dark green.","Qin Shaozong's eyesight was excellent. From a not-too-distant stretch, he could see many large ceramic vats piled up in the camp.","What were those?","\"My lord, when do we act?\" Feng Feng rubbed his hands, almost unable to wait.","Heaven knew what kind of hellish days they had lived these past few days. Feng Feng felt he himself had lost weight from the ordeal. But it was all worth it, especially now that they had crept right beside the enemy camp, and the Yanzhou army remained completely unaware.","\"Not yet. Wait until the hour of the Tiger,\" Qin Shaozong said in a low voice. \"Pass the order down. Have everyone rest where they are. Act on my command at the hour of the Tiger.\"","The guard left Qin Shaozong's side, walking down the line, soon spreading this command throughout the serpentine column.","The snake in the mountains coiled up, flicking its crimson tongue, quietly waiting for the most opportune moment.","Time passed bit by bit. The night grew deep.","...","Inside the Yanzhou army camp.","A guard yawned, unbearably drowsy. These past few days, they had been preparing tung oil non-stop, moving who-knows-how-many heavy jars.","Busy during the day, and taking turns on night watch duty—it was truly exhausting.","\"Endure it a bit longer. These hard days won't last much longer. I heard the boats from Qingzhou and the Northern Lands are almost ready.\"","\"Hah, they're planning a fight to the death. But is Bai Ri Pass so easy to attack? By then, a splash of hot oil, a roll of giant boulders, and arrows shot from above—even if they had ten lives, it wouldn't be enough to waste.\"","\"I hope I can face them when the time comes, and finally take Qin Shaozong's head. Then I won't have to worry for the rest of my life.\"","After chatting for a few more sentences, the two men began to yawn again.","Suddenly, one of them turned to look sideways, only to see the mountain range pitch black, the night merging into his eyes, making it impossible to see anything clearly. He murmured, \"I think I heard some sounds.\"","\"Probably a tiger hunting in the mountains, no need to...\"","The words that followed were left unfinished as he suddenly saw his companion's face change dramatically. The firelight illuminated his bloodless, utterly terrified face, as if a vengeful ghost had seized him by the neck.","\"Hey, what's wrong with you?\" the man asked.","His companion shouted, so frightened that his voice even cracked at the end, \"We're under attack!\"","The other man's mind jolted, and he instinctively turned his head. What met his eyes was a face with sharp, distinct features and profound depth.","Long eyebrows, deep-set eyes, a high nose, and thin lips. A small break at the end of the man's left eyebrow resembled a cold blade, fractured yet still exuding a murderous aura.","The ring-pommel sword in his hand reflected a chill colder than ice. The cold light flashed, tracing a terrifying arc of crimson.","Thud-thud-thud. Something rolled to the ground.","Qin Shaozong led the charge, spearheading the assault into the Yanzhou army camp. After killing two guards in a row, he sniffed the air and then laughed heartily, \"Well played, Fan Tianshi, thinking you're so clever, just begging for death. Feng Feng, Qiao Wangfei, take your men and go douse their army's oil stores. I'm burning this camp down.\"","\"Yes, sir!\"","The Northern Army descended like divine soldiers. Combined with the deep night, when sleep was at its heaviest, they completely stunned the Yanzhou troops.","Fan Tianshi happened to be staying in the camp that night. He was having a sweet dream where he had severed the heads of Qin Shaozong and Nan Gongxiong, bringing all the lands of the North and Qingzhou under his control. The sounds of killing drifted into his tent, piercing through his sleep like needles and jolting him awake.","The noise outside was relentless, wave upon wave growing louder. Through the gaps in the tent flap lifted by the wind, he could see the blazing light of fires.","Without even bothering to dress properly, Fan Tianshi hurried out. Before his eyes, flames shot towards the sky, and the camp was in utter chaos.","Shouts, curses, pleas for help, commands, and screams—all kinds of sounds mingled together, like a hundred demons parading through a marketplace, both cacophonous and utterly chilling.","\"How could this happen? Where did these troops come from? How is there no warning at all? Are the sentries all dead?!\" Fan Tianshi's eyes nearly burst from their sockets in rage.","A junior officer rushed over, his face covered in dust and a deep bloody gash on his right shoulder. \"Lord Fan, they didn't come through the Bai Ri Pass. They must have taken the Chijiao Peak mountain path. I... I think I just saw the Marquis of Wu'an...\"","Fan Tianshi's face turned deathly pale. \"Qin Shaozong is here? Wasn't he building ships?\"","He needed no one to answer. At this moment, Fan Tianshi finally realized he had been deceived. The shipbuilding was a feint; the real plan was to take the shortcut over Chijiao Peak!","\"Let's go! Gather the men and retreat with me!\" Fan Tianshi nearly ground his silver teeth to dust.","Crash.","A pottery vat was smashed open by the hilt of Feng Feng's blade, and tung oil inside gushed out.","The vats were too large and cumbersome to move. Feng Feng led a squad to raid the cooks' quarters, seizing a pile of pottery basins. Using basins to carry the oil was light and fast, and they could still fight if needed.","Splash—","Basin after basin of oil was splashed onto the military tents.","\"Light them up!\" Feng Feng cried excitedly.","A brazier used for illumination was kicked over in front of a tent. A serpent of fire erupted, rapidly climbing the tent and swallowing it whole.","The greedy fire serpent was not satisfied. After devouring several tents and growing into a fire dragon, it continued its rampage through the small camp.","\"The grain storehouse is on fire! Quick, put it out!\"","\"There's too much oil in the camp, we can't extinguish it. Where's Lord Fan? What are Lord Fan's orders?\"","\"Someone has already been sent to find him, but no command has come back yet.\"","Qin Shaozong killed another man with a backhanded strike and continued pressing towards the center of the camp. The commander's tent was easy to identify: the largest one in the center, with a command flag planted at its peak.","From the moment the Xuanxiao Cavalry launched their surprise attack, Qin Shaozong's goal had been singular—","Find Fan Tianshi.","Capture the ringleader, and the rest will collapse. Kill Fan Tianshi first, and the Yanzhou army would naturally crumble completely.","The burly man charged through the camp, his movements as swift and fierce as a tiger's, the sword in his hand like the claws of a ferocious beast, cutting down all who stood in his path. Overcoming every obstacle, Qin Shaozong, gripping a blood-soaked blade, arrived beside the main tent.","Just then, a figure surrounded by several others crashed into Qin Shaozong's line of sight.","The man in the middle wore plain, unremarkable clothing, even donning the most common soldier's outer garment. But Qin Shaozong, who had seen Fan Tianshi before, recognized him instantly—someone was trying to slip away unnoticed.","A fallen soldier's bow and arrows lay scattered nearby. Qin Shaozong sheathed his sword and picked up the longbow.","He drew the bowstring to its full extent, aiming at Fan Tianshi.","Just as he was about to release the arrow, as if remembering something, the man shifted his aim slightly, avoiding a vital spot, and only then let the arrow fly.","Whoosh—","The long arrow bore the force to split the wind, trailing the fire dragon's brazen arrogance, and embedded itself accurately in the figure ahead.","Amidst the exclamations of shock ahead, Qin Shaozong casually tossed the longbow aside and advanced once more, sword in hand.","Blood soaked this patch of earth. Yanzhou soldiers fell one after another until, finally, their morale shattered, and deserters began to appear.","Qin Shaozong gave his ring-pommel sword a flick. A heavy line of blood, mixed with bits of flesh, drew a long streak on the ground. He looked down at Fan Tianshi, whose face was the color of gold paper, and chuckled lowly, \"Fan of Yanzhou, we meet again.\"","Agony shot through Fan Tianshi's shoulder blade. From the corner of his eye, he saw his personal guards all fallen. Knowing escape was impossible, he simply closed his eyes. \"My defeat at your hands today is due to ill fortune. Make it quick.\"","But Qin Shaozong only laughed. \"Fan of Yanzhou, you are a grand prize. It would be a waste for you to die by my hand.\""]},{"number":64,"title":"Chapter 64","paragraphs":["\"Day five.\" Nan Gongxiong stood by the Jinshui River, looking at the rising sun in the distance with a furrowed brow. \"Is Qin Changgeng up to this? I hope he doesn't get himself killed.\"","Zhang Mingdian, the strategist from Qingzhou, stood beside him. \"My lord, you need not worry. Regardless, the current situation is advantageous and harmless to us.\"","If Qin Shaozong's surprise attack succeeded, the Bai Ridge Pass would surely fall. If executed even more cleanly, capturing and killing Fan Tianshi in one stroke, Yanzhou would become theirs for the taking.","But if Qin Shaozong died within the Red Horn Peak, it would mean the leader of the Northern Territories along with its most famed Xuanxiao Cavalry would be lost together.","The Northern Territories would be severely weakened. At that point, turning their spears around to target them was not an impossibility.","\"I still hope he succeeds. Compared to Fan Tianshi, Qin Changgeng, though his words are often sharp, acts with much more straightforwardness.\" Nan Gongxiong was still thinking about those three hundred fine-bred horses and one thousand dan of grain.","If Qin Shaozong was gone, who would he go to for those things?","Just then, a commotion suddenly arose from the opposite bank of the Jinshui. The noise was so great it cut through the roaring waves, reaching the ears of everyone on this shore with precision.","Nan Gongxiong instinctively turned his head.","That one glance happened to catch sight of a banner bearing the character \"Yan\" on the opposite bank tilting sideways as if snapped. After falling, the banner did not rise again.","Nan Gongxiong's large frame shuddered, his eyes flashing with an intense light. \"Quick, prepare the boats! We cross the river now!\"","...","Dai Li woke up and suddenly felt the atmosphere in the military camp had changed. Joy was everywhere; occasionally, she could even hear soldiers humming tunes.","Puzzled, Dai Li happened to see Mo Yanyun passing by and stopped him to ask.","Mo Yanyun's face was animated with excitement. \"The Lord Marquis's surprise attack was a success! Not only did he burn Yanzhou's grain stores, but he also routed their main forces in one fell swoop. Lady Dai, the Bai Ridge Pass has fallen!\"","Dai Li was dazed.","Fallen? In just a few days?","Driven by curiosity, she asked him, \"You said a surprise attack. How exactly was it done?\"","Mo Yanyun was one of the few officers who knew the details and remained in the camp. \"From the foot of Red Horn Peak in Guoyun County, they traveled hundreds of li westward along mountain paths, slipping behind the Yanzhou army's rear.\"","Dai Li: \"...He's quite audacious.\"","Mo Yanyun suddenly grew excited. \"Oh! The Lord Marquis is back!\"","Dai Li turned to look behind her. Several fast horses were now approaching from the direction of the Jinshui. The lead rider had a tall, imposing frame, a ring-pommeled sword hanging at his waist. Galloping towards them with the sunlight at his back, he carried an air of triumphant spirit that was hard to conceal.","Seeing the graceful figure turn around in the distance, Qin Shaozong on horseback immediately raised his riding crop once more.","The steed neighed, carrying its rider charging straight into the camp.","A gust of damp wind rushed at her face. Dai Li closed her eyes against the rush. When she opened them again, he was already before her.","The man sat astride his tall horse. That dominating aura felt even heavier from his elevated position. The corner of his mouth lifted. \"My lady rose quite early today.\"","Dai Li saw water dripping steadily from his robes. In the brief moment the horse had stopped, a small puddle had already formed on the ground, as if he had just emerged from the water.","\"Did my lord go for a swim in the river?\" Dai Li looked him up and down, her gaze lingering for an extra second on a stray lock of hair sticking up near his crown. An untimely bout of perfectionism made her fingers itch.","Qin Shaozong swung down from the horse. \"Been in the mountains for days. If I didn't wash up, you'd be finding fault again.\"","Dai Li was momentarily speechless, thinking to herself that this man really held a grudge. That one time she asked him to wash up before getting into bed, and he remembered it till now.","\"My lady, go and get ready. We'll take the water route into the city shortly.\" Qin Shaozong seemed to remember something and added, \"I brought a gift for that little rascal. I'm sure he'll like it.\"","The latter sentence piqued Dai Li's curiosity.","A gift for Zhouzhou? And he's sure he'll like it?","But before she could ask, Qin Shaozong had already hurried back to his tent to change.","With the Bai Ridge Pass fallen, the allied forces of the Northern Territories and Qingzhou began striking camp.","It was time to move.","The large herds of cattle and sheep carried by the commissariat couldn't be loaded onto boats or easily taken across the pontoon bridge. They had to turn back and take the route through the Bai Ridge Pass.","The lightly-equipped soldiers took the water route or the pontoon bridge, essentially taking a shortcut and arriving at Bai Ridge City much faster than the rear troops.","All along the way into the city, Dai Li kept thinking about that gift. The Zhouzhou of before liked many things: calligraphy, kittens and puppies, Legos and puzzles...","But now, Dai Li didn't know what her son liked anymore.","She wanted to ask, but didn't know how to start.","Whether it was his initial \"it's all in the past\" or his later \"I'll tell you someday,\" she understood it as a signal—he didn't want to recall those times.","It was actually normal. Having finally struggled free from the mire, why would he want to remember the suffocation and despair of the past?","His avoidance was too obvious. Combined with his usual wooden expression and silence far exceeding the norm, Dai Li suspected her son might be suffering from post-traumatic stress disorder.","She was terribly anxious but felt utterly helpless, only able to pin her hopes on Nalan Zhi's guidance.","If she, his own mother, couldn't figure out what her son liked, how could Qin Shaozong dare to give her such a guarantee?","It seemed utterly unreliable, yet this man had truly never lied to her.","All along the way into the city, Qin Shaozong could constantly feel a covert gaze sizing him up. It would steal a glance, look away for a moment, then return shortly after, repeating the pattern.","The man curled the corner of his mouth, continuing to control his horse's pace—neither too fast nor too slow, keeping him right beside her carriage.","The mansion previously occupied by Fan Tianshi had been cleared out. Now, its gates stood open, awaiting its new master. Knowing Qingzhou's contribution in this campaign was less than the Northern Territories', Nan Gongxiong didn't contest Qin Shaozong for this grand residence and led his Qingzhou officers elsewhere.","Dai Li's heart felt like it was being scratched by a cat. That man was utterly wicked, seemingly tossing his words aside as soon as they were spoken, acting as if nothing had happened.","Several times when their eyes met, he would pretend not to know and ask her what was wrong.","Just as Dai Li, after hesitating through lunch, finally decided to take the initiative, she turned to find Qin Shaozong gone.","\"Where is the Lord Marquis?\" Dai Li asked in surprise.","Qiao Wangfei, whom she had randomly stopped, answered, \"The Lord Marquis has gone to the Prefect's office.\"","Bai Ridge City did have a Prefect. However, after Fan Tianshi's army entered, the Prefect was naturally sidelined. Now, with the pass fallen, this Prefect still held no real power.","Seeing Dai Li's hesitant look, Qiao Wangfei offered, \"Do you need to see the Lord Marquis? Bai Ridge City was just captured; there's much to handle. The Lord Marquis likely won't be back this afternoon. Oh, Lady Dai, there's a joint banquet with Qingzhou tonight. The Lord Marquis might have some free time after that.\"","Dai Li: \"...Very well.\"","So Dai Li stopped looking and went back for a nap.","Waking from her nap, her son, who had gone to see Nalan Zhi, hadn't returned yet. Dai Li sat by the window, lost in thought.","\"My lady, if you're feeling bored, perhaps you could go for a stroll on the streets?\" Bipo suggested softly.","Nianxia frowned, \"I just heard that the Yanzhou soldiers in the city haven't been fully cleared out yet. It's not safe to go out now. Why doesn't the lady wait a few more days?\"","Daili sighed, \"Then we'll visit the market another day. For now, let's just go see the mansion's back garden.\"","To Daili's delight, however, the mansion's back garden was quite large. Leaving aside the exotic flowers and rare plants, there was also a sizable pond.","A gentle breeze stirred, leaving the water's surface unruffled. Sitting under a tall tree by the pond with a fishing rod in hand, Daili found it quite a unique pleasure.","In a teahouse within White Sun City.","Inside, tea bubbled softly on the stove, filling the air with its fragrance. Most of the windows were open, welcoming the warm, mellow sunlight into the room.","Two people were inside, one seated, one standing.","The seated man was young, with handsome features, dressed in a high-collared robe with gold-edged cloud patterns, exuding a gentle yet somewhat untamed air.","Before him was a low table. Besides the tea set and small stove, there was also a silver-white mask on the table.","\"Fan Yanzhou has been defeated. The city is being swept clean, and the Yanzhou guards on the walls are gradually being replaced by troops from both armies. Sir, when do we withdraw?\"","Diting, however, smiled. \"A perfect opportunity. Why withdraw?\"","The man paused.","\"White Sun Pass is a treacherous stronghold. Qin Shaozong broke it in just five days. If this were your achievement, wouldn't you be proud?\" Diting asked.","The man immediately nodded. \"Of course I would be proud.\"","Diting smiled. \"Since ancient times, pride has often led to defeat, and underestimating the enemy rarely brings success. Qin Shaozong is riding high on success. After clearing the city of Yanzhou troops, how could he possibly imagine there's more than one faction within these walls?\"","Their Lotus Sect had always kept a low profile, not openly participating in the conflicts between the provinces. Everyone had a legitimate surface identity; even a thorough check of household registers and backgrounds would reveal no flaws. That's because many members were already established in various professions before joining the sect.","After saying this, Diting paused briefly. \"Given the previous 'divine sign' incident, Qin Shaozong might think of us. But by then, it will already be too late.\"","\"You mean we lie in wait, quietly waiting for Lady Dai to leave the mansion?\" the man asked.","Diting smiled. \"The march has been tedious for many days. Now that we're finally in the city, it's impossible she'll stay cooped up in the mansion forever. Just wait. She will definitely leave the mansion, sooner or later.\"","The man nodded obediently, like a puppy. \"You're right.\"","\"How are the preparations going with the Seamstress?\" Diting asked about other matters.","The man replied, \"Two women with similar stature and appearance have been selected. The Seamstress is now making the final adjustments to them.\"","Diting: \"What about the city guard soldiers?\"","The man said, \"Among the few Qingzhou soldiers we've managed to contact, only two are assigned to inspection duties at the city gates, and both have been posted to the East Gate.\"","\"Only two...\" Diting poured himself a cup of tea. \"Not many, but it should be enough. What about the merchant caravan and the boatmen?\"","The man said, \"They are on standby, ready to move at any time. Now we're just waiting for the Seamstress to finish, and for Lady Dai to leave the mansion.\"","Diting picked up his teacup and took a sip. \"My uncle always said that in major undertakings, the greatest taboo is impatience. Let's just wait. We mustn't startle the snake.\"","\"Oh, and Sir, there's one more thing.\" The man looked hesitant. \"We've sent the signal several times, but Mingdeng still hasn't responded. Not even once.\"","Diting's hand, lowering the teacup, paused. He seemed thoughtful for a moment, then chuckled softly. \"No rush. He absolutely cannot do without us.\"","Qin Mansion, Back Garden.","Daili caught three fish, leisurely passing the afternoon.","As evening approached, Hu Bao came looking for her and asked, \"Lady Dai, the Lord Marquis wishes to know if you would like to attend the victory celebration banquet tonight?\"","\"I heard tonight is for you and the Qingzhou generals to celebrate together, so I won't go. Enjoy yourselves.\" Daili knew they would certainly be drinking.","A group of military men gathered for food and drink would surely be unrestrained; she wouldn't go and intrude.","Hu Bao asked again, \"And what about Young Master Qin?\"","Daili said matter-of-factly, \"Zhouzhou won't go either. Qin Changgeng mentioned before that Nangong Qingzhou suspected my son of intercepting their tribute gifts to the imperial court. My son's wanted posters were everywhere. There's no guarantee Nangong Qingzhou wouldn't recognize him.\"","Hu Bao smiled slightly. \"You needn't worry about that. The Lord Marquis has already reached an agreement with Nangong Qingzhou, who promised to let bygones be bygones.\"","Daili was slightly taken aback.","An agreement?","When did he reach an agreement with Nangong Qingzhou?","Thinking this, Daili asked Hu Bao, but he only said, \"It was settled before the Lord Marquis left for the surprise attack. As for the details, please ask the Lord Marquis yourself, Lady Dai.\"","\"Regarding the banquet, I'll ask my son first,\" Daili said hesitantly.","Although she thought her son most likely wouldn't go, the child was grown now, and parents couldn't manage everything for him.","As Daili expected, Qin Yanzhou also declined. So that evening, mother and son had a private meal in their small courtyard, eating the fish Daili had caught that afternoon.","One was steamed, one braised in soy sauce, and the other was kept in a water vat to eat tomorrow.","Summer days were long and nights short. By the time they finished their meal, the sky had finally darkened completely.","Daili had assumed that with Qin Shaozong and the Qingzhou side celebrating tonight, the banquet would run very late and he wouldn't have the time or energy to remember that \"gift.\"","However, around dusk, just after Daili had bathed and was planning to read for a while before sleeping, a guard came to find her.","The guard said, \"Lady Dai, the Lord Marquis requests that you and Young Master Qin come with him. He says he has a gift for Young Master Qin.\"","Hearing \"gift,\" Daili's curiosity perked up again. \"Did he say what the gift is?\"","The guard: \"He did not. Please come with the young master.\"","\"How mysterious,\" Daili muttered, but she dressed properly and went with her son.","The banquet had just ended over there; drunken Qingzhou generals were walking out with their arms around each other's shoulders.","Under a side corridor, Daili saw that familiar tall figure. He stood in front of a light source, his shadow stretching long ahead of him.","The man's face was shrouded in darkness, making his expression hard to discern. Only his gaze was scorching, like searing flames, or magma that could melt bone.","Daili pretended not to notice, not even exchanging pleasantries. \"The Lord Marquis mentioned a gift. Where is it?\"","Qin Yanzhou had been silent behind his mother, as he had been many times before. He showed no reaction to Qin Shaozong's presence, simply acting as if he didn't exist.","Qin Shaozong glanced at the mother and son, thinking to himself they were truly cut from the same cloth, identically dismissive of others.","Fine, he couldn't be bothered to argue with them.","\"Follow me,\" Qin Shaozong turned.","Daili thought he was taking them to the main hall, but she saw him pass by the side corridor without entering, heading instead towards the western pavilions, going further and further into a secluded area.","After walking a while longer, Daili couldn't help asking, \"Where exactly is the Lord Marquis going? There are many mosquitoes in summer, even more so at night. If it's for a garden stroll, wouldn't daytime be better?\"","\"We're here,\" Qin Shaozong said just then.","He stopped before a courtyard building. Looking in from the entrance, he could see soldiers guarding the doorway, and a lantern hanging under the eaves before the house. The lantern was small, not very bright, inexplicably emitting an air of eeriness in this pitch-black night.","\"I and your mother will not go in.\" Qin Shaozong did not enter, but kept looking at Qin Yanzhou. \"There are two people inside. Deal with them as you see fit, boy.\"","\"What people?\" Dai Li didn't understand.","She stood between the two men. Her height did not match either of theirs, and their gazes met over the top of her head.","Qin Shaozong did not speak, nor did Qin Yanzhou.","After several breaths, Qin Yanzhou nodded. \"Good. Thank you.\"","Dai Li was greatly astonished. What kind of riddle were these two playing? Why couldn't she understand?","Qin Yanzhou walked straight inside.","Dai Li kept watching his back until her son pushed the door open and entered, completely swallowed by the darkness.","A solid, long arm then wrapped around her waist, turning her around. Qin Shaozong said with a laugh, \"My wife was right earlier. There are many mosquitoes in summer, even more so at night. And that boy has many accounts to settle with them slowly. He definitely won't be out for a while. It would be better for you and me to rest elsewhere.\"","In a daze, Dai Li realized who was in the house. \"It's Fan Tianshi...\"","\"Yes, and his second son. To eradicate weeds, one must pull out the roots. Another day, we'll go to Gaoling County and arrest his other sons as well.\"","Qin Shaozong led her to walk elsewhere. Seeing Dai Li frequently looking back, he couldn't help but click his tongue lightly. \"That boy is no longer a suckling infant. There's no need for my lady to worry about him, nor to stick to his mother every moment.\"","The wave of tender emotion that had just risen in Dai Li instantly dissipated. She couldn't help but give him a shove. \"Qin Changgeng, can't you speak properly?\"","\"Honest advice is hard to take, my lady,\" he chuckled lowly."]},{"number":65,"title":"Chapter 65","paragraphs":["\"Creak.\"","The sound of the wooden door turning on its hinges was piercingly distinct in the silent night.","The two men inside the room both jolted, their eyes holding both terror and a sense of relief that an end was finally coming.","Qin Yanzhou did not enter immediately. Instead, as if remembering something, he took a step back, took the lantern hanging under the eaves, and entered, holding it aloft. The light spread from outside in, illuminating the two men inside and allowing them to see the face of the visitor.","Inside, Fan Tianshi and Fan Zhongmin had their mouths stuffed with coarse cloth to prevent them from biting their tongues, while their hands were tied tightly behind their backs.","When the two men saw Qin Yanzhou holding the lantern, they were both taken aback.","Fan Zhongmin's pupils constricted, his nostrils flared, and a heavy, muffled sound issued from his throat.","Compared to the emotionally volatile Fan Zhongmin, Fan Tianshi beside him was more composed—though this was perhaps also due to him having been seriously injured for a long time.","Qin Yanzhou casually placed the lantern on a low table, then drew a short blade from his waist and walked towards Fan Zhongmin.","Fan Zhongmin shook his head frantically. With his legs and hands bound, he wriggled on the floor like a worm, trying to get away from Qin Yanzhou.","Qin Yanzhou walked up to him, crouched down, and pulled the cloth from his mouth. \"Do you want to live?\"","Fan Zhongmin was stunned for a moment, then nodded wildly. \"Quanjie, I have no grievance with you! Let me go! I have much silver and beautiful concubines. If you are willing to spare my life, I will give you all of it.\"","Qin Yanzhou swung the blade.","Fan Zhongmin instinctively closed his eyes and screamed, but the expected pain did not come. Instead, the bindings on his hands loosened. He opened his eyes, thinking Qin Yanzhou had agreed, and a wave of wild joy surged within him. But the next moment—","\"Clatter.\" A short blade landed in front of him.","The blade bounced slightly on the wooden floor, its polished surface reflecting a cold gleam.","\"Within one quarter of an hour, cut off his right arm, and I will let you live,\" Qin Yanzhou said expressionlessly.","The joy on Fan Zhongmin's face froze. He turned stiffly to look beside him, where his father was staring at him in horror. \"I... I...\"","Qin Yanzhou silently drew another blade.","Fan Zhongmin began to tremble. Pampered since childhood, he knew he was no match for the man before him.","He shifted his gaze back to Fan Tianshi. After struggling for a long time, he gripped the blade with both hands and approached, beginning to mutter neurotically, \"Father, he's forcing me. It's all Quanjie forcing me. And Quanjie doesn't want your life, just an arm. You'll surely part with it. You've already lost one legitimate son. You wouldn't just watch your only remaining legitimate son die for nothing, would you...\"","Fan Tianshi's eyes nearly burst from their sockets, a heavy, furious sound coming from his nose.","Fan Zhongmin closed his eyes, his hands shaking as he plunged the blade in, intending to slice it off in one stroke. But he was out of shape, his strength insufficient, and his heart was filled with dread. The cut was not clean at all; it was more like he was sawing back and forth across Fan Tianshi's shoulder.","Fan Tianshi's eyes filled with blood, his teeth grinding audibly.","A long, long time later, something finally fell with a \"thud,\" blood spreading across the floor.","Fan Zhongmin, his face pale, turned around, about to force an ingratiating smile, when a short blade pierced him through. His pupils dilated. \"You... you lied to me.\"","A breeze blew in just then, causing the flame of the now-uncovered lantern to flicker violently. The wildly shifting light and shadow played across the young man's exquisite features, and as his lips curved slightly, it revealed a sick, sinister coldness. \"So what if I did? What can you do about it?\"","He pulled the blade out cleanly, kicked away Fan Zhongmin who had collapsed before him, and walked towards Fan Tianshi, blade in hand.","Wiping the blood from the blade onto Fan Tianshi's face, then tapping his cheek with the flat of the blade, Qin Yanzhou whispered, \"Even a dog can bite a man to death. Don't you agree?\"","Fan Tianshi's mouth was still stuffed, unable to utter a single word, and he could only glare at him with hatred.","Qin Yanzhou looked at his intact left arm, a flicker of excitement passing through his eyes.","The full moon hung high in the sky, shining brightly, its silvery light spilling over the earth and slipping into countless households.","At this moment, in a side room not far from the main courtyard, no lamps were lit inside. Only the moonlight slipping through the window illuminated the two figures by the window a little.","Daili sat on Qin Shaozong's lap, one hand braced against his solid chest, the other resting on the beast-head buckle of his sash, which was now exceptionally loose and served no purpose in holding his clothes together.","The night wasn't particularly sultry, but with every breath, Daili felt as if she were inhaling scorching air.","It was as if the air, still carrying his scent, entered through her mouth and nose, traveled down her windpipe, spread through her meridians, leaving behind tiny sparks of fire in her blood and bones wherever it passed.","\"...It was nothing. I just gave Nangong some horses and provisions, and made up for the things that brat looted before. He agreed to let bygones be bygones. In the future, if he sees that kid, Nangong might even exchange a few pleasantries with him. Yanzhou is already taken. Tell him he can go out boldly from now on.\"","Qin Shaozong answered her question while raising his hand first to wipe away a trace of moisture at the corner of her lips, then moving his calloused thumb a little further, brushing over her swollen lips.","\"My lord is indeed a man of his word, a true gentleman.\" As she finished speaking, the woman's soft, red tongue seemed to inadvertently peek out slightly, lightly touching his rough thumb like a dragonfly skimming water.","The corners of her eyes were flushed crimson, her red lips and the dot on her forehead the color of cinnabar. The moonlight fell on her jade-like face, adding a touch of hazy grace to her peach-blossom eyes that seemed to hold deep emotion, like a peony in full, breathtaking bloom after a misty spring rain.","It was a mature, alluring beauty that invited wild imaginings, and an enchanting charm that could drown a man.","The man's eyes darkened abruptly. The large hand resting on her spine moved back up, settling with full possessiveness on the slender, pale nape of her neck.","He pressed her to draw close to him again.","As they met once more, he first gently caught her lower lip between his teeth, nibbling and sucking, teasing her thoroughly before driving deep, capturing that soft red with an ineffable sense of possession to bully it, then sliding down to repeatedly stroke the sensitive root of her tongue.","Daili trembled violently, her dazed eyes glistening with moisture. For a moment, she didn't know whether to press down on his mischievous hand below first, or to lean back to avoid its advance.","The battle for Yanzhou was over, the war completely concluded. He came with overwhelming force, like a man finally released from restraint, ready to feast heartily, making Daili's heart quiver.","Having experienced the previous few times, she suddenly realized she couldn't let him completely control the pace. Given this man's habits, he would always make things last until very late.","Daili immediately changed her actions. She still pressed down, but this time it wasn't on his hand.","She pressed down, then began to act willfully herself, learning from him.","Qin Shaozong's pupils contracted. A low, beast-like sound of excitement rumbled in his throat, and the large hand on the back of her neck slid down once more.","The two sets of breaths in the room grew gradually heavier, the temperature seeming to climb layer by layer. After an unknowable amount of time, Daili suddenly felt the powerful body beneath her tense.","Her chest was heaving violently now, her sash completely loose, the undergarment that had been tied behind her back barely hanging on, revealing vast stretches of snowy, lush whiteness.","Moonlight fell upon it, making that expanse of fair, slightly blushed skin shimmer with a soft glow.","Qin Shaozong suddenly tightened his embrace of the woman before him, buried his head, and pressed his high-bridged nose into the soft, pearly flesh.","A moment later, Daili felt him relax. She secretly curved the corner of her lips. Unexpectedly, he chose that moment to look up, and their eyes met squarely.","Daili's heart gave a lurch, thinking to herself that she was in trouble.","\"Courtesy demands reciprocity. Let me serve my lady in return,\" he said, hooking up the corner of his mouth. Suddenly, he encircled her waist with one arm, lifting her solely by the strength of his arm, while his other hand slid down along the line of her waist and into her trousers.","By the time Daili sat down again, she was sitting entirely on his hand.","Daili was greatly startled. Before she could even speak, he leaned in again, swallowing all the words in her throat.","When Qin Yanzhou walked out of that pavilion courtyard, a night breeze happened to brush past. The wind blew against his face, cool and refreshing, like an invisible yet powerful hand lifting some of the weight of the great mountain pressing on his shoulders.","The scent of blood drifted from behind. It was distinctly unpleasant, yet the young man closed his eyes as if enjoying it, took a deep breath, and slowly exhaled, as if expelling all the depression and pain accumulated in his chest over the years.","A moment later, he finally stepped away. The area outside the courtyard was already empty.","At first, Qin Yanzhou thought Daili had returned, but when he got back to the main courtyard, he found that whether it was the side rooms or the main quarters, listening intently revealed no movement within.","\"Young master is back.\" Nianxia had been waiting in the courtyard.","Qin Yanzhou asked, \"Has my mother returned?\"","\"She did return. Madam came back to fetch something, then went out again with the lord.\" Nianxia replied thus.","Qin Yanzhou: \"What did mother take?\"","\"Fish bladder.\" Nianxia answered truthfully; she didn't understand the use of that item either.","Qin Yanzhou didn't understand either.","Nianxia remembered the lord's instruction. She hadn't intended to relay it, but who knew the young master would be so intent on getting to the bottom of it. She had no choice but to brace herself and say, \"Young master, the lord told you to go to bed early, saying that's how you can grow taller faster, and told you not to concern yourself with matters between your elders.\"","Qin Yanzhou's face instantly turned grim.","Tonight's moon was exceptionally bright and clear, without a single wisp of cloud around it. As the moon slanted westward, even larger swathes of moonlight than before slipped into the room.","The room was filled with a subtle, floating fragrance, glowing softly.","Daili no longer had the strength to hold up her spine, and could only slump limply into Qin Shaozong's embrace.","Her arms were wrapped around his neck, as if trying to leverage herself up, or perhaps seeking support. The iron-like arm tightly encircling her waist directly eliminated the first possibility.","Her fair fingers clutched tightly at the man's lapels, with such force that faint, jade-like veins appeared on the back of her hand.","She trembled violently, quivering like autumn leaves in the wind. In the end, as if finally unable to bear the rough calluses on his fingers and palm, Daili opened her mouth and bit his neck.","Attacked in such a vulnerable spot as the neck, Qin Shaozong tensed for an instant, but quickly relaxed again. Along with this relaxation came a pause in his other movements.","Daili was hanging by a thread, left suspended by him in a state of unbearable tension. She shifted restlessly on her own, only to have her rounded rear slapped by his other hand the next moment.","\"My lady has a bad habit of burning bridges after crossing the river. It's quite a nasty habit and must be changed from now on.\" Not only did he slap, but he also spread his large palm and kneaded.","Daili made no sound, continuing to bite him.","Qin Shaozong slapped again, sending a ripple through the flesh. \"Did you hear me?\"","Daili remained silent.","Qin Shaozong clicked his tongue lightly and resumed giving her what she craved. \"Speak.\"","The woman biting his neck loosened her grip slightly, letting out a sticky, indistinct sound of assent from her nose.","\"Agree or not agree?\" Qin Shaozong was not satisfied with her evasiveness.","This vixen had eight hundred tricks up her sleeve. What did \"mm\" mean? She was brushing him off again.","Daili, tormented by his teasing, saw before her his neck marked with her teeth and his prominent Adam's apple. She simply leaned closer and began tracing them with her lips.","That Adam's apple immediately bobbed violently. Qin Shaozong gritted his teeth, knowing she was playing a little trick, but the sensation came in waves, each stronger than the last, like a hurricane sweeping away his restraint.","And so, he abandoned his measured pace.","Daili's vision blurred for an instant, her heart rate skyrocketing, followed by a prolonged, melting softness.","An embroidered bird-patterned sash slipped from the side of the soft chair, followed by a light, plain silk undergarment. Layer upon layer, they spread out around the soft chair like petals.","Two breaths, one urgent, one heavy, intertwined. Suddenly—","\"Wait! Let's go inside.\" Daili whispered.","He didn't move, his voice equally hoarse. \"Earlier inside, my lady complained it was hot, and found the bed dirty, unwilling to get on it. Now you don't mind?\"","\"Someone might see here.\" It was indeed cooler by the window, but Daili, having regained some composure, was worried about being seen.","\"No one will come.\" Qin Shaozong went to kiss her plump earlobe. \"If someone comes, I will hear them.\"","\"Then let me put on some clothes.\" Daili hesitated, then said, trying to get off his lap to pick up her clothes.","Qin Shaozong reached behind himself, took hold of the black outer robe he had removed earlier, brought it back, unfurled it with a flick, and draped it over the beauty with skin like fragrant jade and fresh snow before him.","Jet black enveloped the pristine white. To one intimately close, the curves beneath the loose robe were visible. The same yet different from usual, his robe worn on her, her whole person enveloped in his scent.","Qin Shaozong was visibly more aroused. Just as he was about to move, he was pressed down by that soft hand.","\"My lady!\" A tendon pulsed and vanished on the side of his neck.","Daili hadn't forgotten the important matter. \"The fish bladder.\"","\"What use is that thing?\" Qin Shaozong was both puzzled and restless.","When she had said she was going back to fetch something, he had indulged her, only for her to bring back a fish bladder. He had asked her mid-way what use it was, but she hadn't explained, only saying he would find out later. Who knew at this critical juncture she would bring this thing up.","\"To prevent pregnancy.\" Daili was succinct.","The poor state of ancient medical conditions need not be elaborated; countless mothers had died at the ghostly gate of childbirth. But setting that aside, even if she could safely bear another child, she would not have any more.","She would only have Zhouzhou in this lifetime. All her emotions—tenderness, affection, guilt, or self-reproach—belonged solely to Zhouzhou.","She couldn't divide them, nor did she want to divide them for another child. Knowing she couldn't balance two bowls of water, it was better not to pick up a second bowl from the start.","The fish bladder had been soaking in a small bowl on the side table, within easy reach.","Qin Shaozong frowned almost imperceptibly.","Seeing he was about to speak, Daili spoke first, her tone unusually carrying an unconcealed forcefulness. \"Qin Changgeng, are you using it or not? If not, then don't do it. There's nothing else to discuss.\"","By the moonlight, Qin Shaozong saw the fish bladder clearly, then suddenly leaned back. \"I don't know how to use this. I'll trouble you, my lady, to help me.\"","Daili stared at him for two breaths, then proceeded to put it on for him.","However, the fish bladder seemed a bit too small.","She pressed her lips together and used brute force.","A vein throbbed on Qin Shaozong's forehead. \"If my lady has any grievances against me, you might as well speak plainly. There's no need to strike so directly at my vital point.\"","Daili lowered her head, striving to keep her lips pressed into a stern line.","\"What? Am I wrong about you?\" Qin Shaozong frowned.","Daili's shoulders trembled slightly, unable to hold back.","Qin Shaozong had been watching her all along; how could he not notice her odd behavior? He immediately lifted her chin, using two fingers to gently pry her jaw open from the outside.","Unable to keep her lips pressed, Daili couldn't control a soft \"Ha,\" and laughed out loud on the spot.","The main issue was that a fish bladder shrinks significantly after being dried. Even after soaking in water, it remains somewhat stiff and doesn't fully return to its original state. Moreover, she hadn't paid attention earlier; the one she picked was likely from a fish of modest size.","Qin Shaozong's face instantly darkened. \"My lady seems quite pleased. Then wouldn't it be a disservice to your current mood if we didn't... reach a higher level later?\"","Before Daili could comprehend what \"reach a higher level\" meant, she felt his hands scoop under her thighs, lifting her entire person up.","Realizing his intention, Daili instantly grew tense. \"Qin Changgeng, wait! Don't...\"","Before her words fell, he let go.","Daili's pupils constricted sharply, her unfinished words all turning into breathy gasps.","Still unsatisfied, he circled one arm around her waist, supported her leg with the other, and rose directly from the seat. And this act of rising truly, as he had said, took them to a higher level.","Daili instinctively clung to him, but being close felt wrong, and pulling away felt wrong too.","\"Have you considered what I said earlier?\" he murmured in a low voice.","Daili's mind was gradually turning into mush. \"Said what?\"","Qin Shaozong: \"That my lady stays by my side forever.\"","Daili mumbled incoherently. And so, she rode the human-powered carriage all night."]},{"number":66,"title":"Chapter 66","paragraphs":["After staying cooped up in the mansion for several days, Daili couldn't stand it any longer. Her son had been attending classes at Nalan Zhi's place recently, while she went to the small lake in the back garden every day for a stroll. She had already fished up two buckets of fish and was thoroughly tired of it.","With nothing to do and her foot injury fully healed, Daili thought of going out to the market.","\"Madam wishes to leave the mansion? This servant will help you dress and do your hair right now.\" Nianxia perked up.","Madam was usually very casual inside the mansion, sometimes not even bothering to put up her hair, and she absolutely refused to wear makeup. She said the lead-based powder was poisonous and prolonged exposure was bad for the skin.","Well, although Nianxia didn't understand why the expensive lead powder favored by noblewomen was toxic, Madam must have her reasons. She only lamented that her own eighteen skills in hairstyling and makeup had no place to shine.","While Nianxia was putting up her hair, Daili looked at Bipo beside her. \"Bipo, go and inform the mansion guards and the kitchen. Tell them I'm going out to the market and they needn't prepare lunch for me.\"","Bipo accepted the order and left.","...","In the study.","Upon hearing from the guard that Daili wanted to leave the mansion, Qin Shaozong smiled. \"Let her go. She's been cooped up for days, long enough. She truly can't stay still the moment her legs are better.\"","The Yanzhou soldiers in the city had now been completely cleared out, with soldiers from the Northern Territories and Qingzhou taking over all city defense and patrol duties. In a sense, Baizhou City had completed a preliminary transfer of power.","The guard was about to leave to relay the order when he heard Qin Shaozong add, \"Take a message to the Madam for me. Tell her to return to the mansion before sunset, and not to have her evening meal outside either.\"","A whole day out wandering was plenty. It wouldn't do for her to not be home by dark.","Jin Duole, standing to the side, secretly lowered his eyes, inwardly drawing a sharp breath. He thought to himself that the Lord Marquis seemed to be getting serious. It looked like the funds earmarked for renovating the Marquis's residence would have to be spent after all.","...","By the time Bipo returned, Daili was properly dressed.","The carriage was waiting at the moon gate of the main courtyard. As Daili boarded, she saw Hu Bao and several guards, knowing they were to accompany her.","The carriage left the mansion, first heading to the food market in the southern district where Daili had lunch, then proceeding to the northern market.","The northern market sold fabrics and jewelry.","Daili actually loved collecting jewelry. In her previous life, her home had a walk-in closet with two whole walls and several cabinets dedicated solely to her accessories.","She didn't necessarily have to wear everything, but if she saw something she liked, she wanted to own it. Just looking at them made her happy.","After arriving in this era, Daili's interest in jewelry hadn't diminished. Back in Nankang Prefecture, when she went on that massive shopping spree, eighty percent was an act, but twenty percent was her genuinely wanting to indulge.","Later, when Qin Shaozong sent jewelry to her rooms, she didn't refuse. On one hand, collecting jewelry that could be easily converted to silver was practical; on the other hand, she genuinely liked it.","Everyone has hobbies. What's wrong with women loving jewelry? Men like drinking wine!","Moreover, the craftsmanship of this ancient era was astonishing. Despite being entirely handmade, they could still produce all sorts of exquisite accessories. Like filigree gold hairpins, twisted gold wire hair clasps, and spiral-patterned earrings—they looked particularly interesting.","Daili only visited jewelry shops with clean storefronts and a large scale that suggested they were well-established.","The mistress and her two maids alighted together.","Hu Bao had several guards stay at the shop entrance while he followed Daili inside.","This jewelry shop had two floors. The prices on the second floor were far higher than the first, specifically catering to wealthy guests from affluent families. Daili didn't go directly upstairs but browsed slowly from the first floor up.","The accessories on the first floor were mostly made of silver, bronze, and various woods. Among them, a pair of earrings adorned with colorful bird feathers caught Daili's eye. She bought them without hesitation.","After browsing the first floor, Daili went up to the second.","Hu Bao also wanted to follow, but was stopped by a young shop attendant.","The attendant looked apologetic, extremely humble. \"Honored Sir, there are some young, unmarried ladies upstairs. The young ladies are shy and do not like to meet unfamiliar gentlemen. Might I trouble you to remain here?\"","Hu Bao looked at Daili.","Daili said, \"Captain Hu, wait on the first floor.\"","Daili didn't think it was a big deal. The first and second floors were only separated by a staircase. If one spoke slightly louder upstairs, it could be heard downstairs.","Hu Bao thus remained on the first floor.","Daili and the two maids ascended the stairs.","Upon reaching the second floor, it was indeed as the attendant said—there were other customers looking at jewelry, all of them women. Two of them were very young, their faces tender and fresh, reminding Daili of flower buds just beginning to bloom on a branch, probably only fourteen or fifteen.","The layout of the second floor was no different from other jewelry shops: everything was categorized, with one area for earrings, another for hair clasps, another for hairpins, and necklaces elsewhere.","From a macro perspective, the entire second floor was somewhat like a library, except the wooden shelves held jewelry instead of books.","Moreover, the design of these shelves was clever. They were latticed, but due to the angle of the latticework, they were somewhat like modern blinds. From inside, one couldn't see outside, but the reverse was possible.","The northern corner of the second floor had a curtained resting area. If one was tired and didn't want to be disturbed by others' gazes, one could draw the curtains on both sides to form a semi-transparent private space.","The western side had a row of bronze mirrors, each as tall as a woman, for customers to use.","The jewelry on the second floor was much more exquisite than on the first.","While Daili was halfway through looking, a maid carrying a tray approached. \"Madam, this is honey tea provided free by the shop. It is not only sweet in taste but also has beautifying and skin-nourishing effects. Please try it. If you find it good, you can purchase it at the South Bamboo Tea House in the eastern part of the city.\"","Hearing her spiel, for a moment Daili felt like she was facing a modern salesperson. So this was a cross-promotion!","The exquisite wooden tray held three small teacups, just enough for the mistress and her two maids.","As the maid approached with the tray, Daili noticed several other maids also carrying tea trays, heading towards the young ladies further inside.","It seemed everyone got a share.","Both Nianxia and Bipo seemed tempted upon hearing this, but if Daili didn't take one, how could they, as maids, reach out? So they both looked at her eagerly.","Daili smiled, first taking a teacup and taking a small sip, just wetting her lips.","With her leading the way, Nianxia and Bipo also reached out. Compared to Daili's sip, the two maids drank their honey tea clean.","The tray-carrying maid collected the teacups and withdrew.","A moment later, another maid came up with a tray of snacks, extremely enthusiastic.","Daili saw the two young ladies not far away receiving the same treatment. The two of them had smiles on their faces, their mood visibly cheerful.","And after having the snacks, the young ladies picked out several pieces of jewelry, clearly having been put in a good mood.","\"I'm not hungry, you two have them,\" Daili said before continuing to look at the jewelry.","Following the earlier precedent, Nianxia and Bipo were no longer reserved and each took snacks to eat.","Daili took a fancy to a bracelet. It was gold, with a circle of differently colored teardrop-shaped tourmalines hanging from the edge. The tourmalines were small, each one very clear and clean.","Daili held it up to the sunlight; the tourmalines refracted a clear, brilliant light.","So pretty. She'd take it.","\"Madam...\"","Daili turned at the sound of the voice and saw Nianxia looking awkward. \"Madam, I have an urgent need to use the privy.\"","Daili: \"Mm, go ahead.\"","Nianxia found a shop attendant to ask, who said the privy was on the first floor and gave detailed directions.","Nianxia hurried downstairs.","Hu Bao, who was downstairs, saw her come down and asked where she was going and if she needed any help. Nianxia told him truthfully.","Hu Bao understood and watched her head towards the privy.","...","Upstairs.","The young ladies from the two families who had arrived earlier had already selected their jewelry and, followed by their maids, went downstairs to settle the bill. They clattered down the stairs, and the second floor instantly became emptier with the departure of that group of mistresses and servants.","Hu Bao, standing by the stairwell, watched the crowd leave and looked up. He happened to catch a glimpse of a woman's dress hem — a delicate pale yellow, a color much favored by young women.","Hu Bao averted his gaze and continued guarding the stairwell without going up.","Not long after, a figure in cyan/green came up the stairs.","\"Bipo, come here for a moment.\" It was Nianxia's voice.","Bipo, who had been following Daili all along, turned her head, but the latticed wooden shutter blocked her view, so she couldn't see the other person. \"What is Nianxia up to, acting so mysterious?\"","Despite saying this, Bipo still walked out, passing through the layers of display shelves.","Daili didn't pay much attention at first, until she faintly heard a muffled grunt from that direction.","The tone sounded very much like Bipo's.","But the distance from there to the stairwell wasn't that close. Daili wasn't sure if she had misheard, so she called out, \"Bipo?\"","\"Madam, what are your instructions?\" came the reply, still in Bipo's voice, with a normal tone.","\"Nothing.\" Daili suspected she had imagined the sound earlier.","Daili was standing in the middle of the bracelet section, with shelves both in front and behind her.","She heard footsteps from both her left and her right. Daili first glanced to the left and saw Nianxia and Bipo wearing cyan (greenish-blue) clothes. The two women were backlit, their faces somewhat more blurred than usual, so she turned to look to the right.","On the right was the shop attendant holding the tray.","Daili naturally turned sideways, facing the attendant and turning her back to her own maids. \"What is it?\"","The shop attendant smiled. \"Madam, I would like to invite you to a place.\"","Daili looked puzzled.","Almost as soon as her words fell, the two women who had already arrived behind Daili acted simultaneously. Their coordination was seamless; one, holding a handkerchief, pressed it over Daili's mouth and nose with both hands, while the other grabbed her hands.","This series of actions was completed almost in an instant. Daili was greatly alarmed and was about to resist when the attendant in front also put down the tray and stepped forward.","From the cloth, Daili smelled a very strange odor, like some kind of plant, or perhaps a mixture. She couldn't quite place it, only knowing that after inhaling twice, she began to feel dizzy and lightheaded.","Her struggling strength gradually weakened.","The noise in her ears slowly faded away; the scene before her eyes blurred into layers of double images that gathered and dispersed. After this happened several times, darkness fell before Daili's eyes.","The attendant in front of her caught her limp body.","Two stood behind Daili, one in front; the three of them sandwiched Daili.","\"Bipo\" cautiously kept the cloth in place for a few more moments before removing it.","The attendant who had been holding the tray earlier was similar in stature to Daili. She picked Daili up and headed west to a bronze mirror, then gave the mirror a light kick with her foot.","Then, this heavy bronze mirror actually slid open from right to left, revealing a passageway with a row of small lanterns hanging from the ceiling. The passage slanted downward, connecting to the rear of the first floor.","There was a person behind the bronze mirror, holding a petite figure; it was this person who had pushed the mirror open.","The young lady he had abducted wore cyan-green clothes, with two carved silver hairpins in her hair and a pair of jade pearl earrings—simple but not plain, the attire of a maid from a wealthy household.","And this young lady, who else could it be but Nianxia, who had gone downstairs to the privy earlier?","The two met and exchanged their burdens deftly, without a word.","The man carried Daili downstairs. The attendant took Nianxia, turned, and headed straight north, arriving at the rest area, where she and another \"Nianxia\" positioned her in front of a low table.","This scene was quite eerie, as if a strand of Nianxia's soul had left her body and was attempting to usurp and harm the main host — a case of the guest usurping the host.","Someone approached from over there—two people.","There was a face eighty percent similar, the same height, the same clothing and hair ornaments, except one Bipo was unconscious, while the other had keen, alert eyes, looking spirited.","The three of them worked together to arrange the unconscious Nianxia and Bipo properly, fed each of them a few pills, and then let down the curtain.","Immediately, \"Nianxia\" and \"Bipo\" walked to the stairs. One went down, and halfway, said to Hu Bao guarding the stairwell: \"Sergeant Hu, the shop is promoting tea beverages. Madam tried some and found it quite good. Could you trouble someone to go to the South Bamboo Tea House in the east of the city to buy a few jars of honey tea?\"","It was Nianxia speaking. Hu Bao was about to agree when he heard Bipo's voice from above.","\"Madam says to buy ten jars.\"","\"Oh, then buy ten jars. My apologies for the trouble.\" Nianxia amended.","Upon hearing this, Hu Bao called over a soldier from outside and sent him on the errand. He was unaware that at that very moment, behind this jewelry shop, a donkey cart was waiting.","A young lady in white waited by the cart. Seeing the man bring Daili down, she hurriedly opened the cargo box on the donkey cart.","The man placed Daili inside the box, then stood motionless beside the cart, gazing at the person in the box.","\"Madam Dai truly has remarkable beauty, like a fairy from the heavens. Such bearing is perfect for entering our Green Lotus Sect.\" The woman in white couldn't help but reach out and stroke Daili's face. Then she took out a small porcelain vial, poured out a black pill, and fed it to Daili.","No need to swallow; the pill slowly dissolved upon entering her mouth.","After completing this, the two spread the pre-prepared straw over Daili. Once the straw was laid, they covered it with a layer of burlap.","The donkey cart slowly drove out of this alley, heading east.","The guard, ordered to buy honey tea, was walking along the bustling street when he suddenly heard a donkey braying behind him.","It was common for carts to come and go on the main street. When he heard the sound, the soldier edged a little further inward. A donkey cart overtook him, its hooves clip-clopping toward the east city gate.","At all four city gates—east, south, west, and north—guards inspected those entering and leaving. The military guards were jointly composed of soldiers from the Northern Region and from Qingzhou, each side providing half the force.","This donkey cart reached the east gate, queuing to await a simple inspection.","Two soldiers stepped forward then. They exchanged a glance with the man driving the cart, their eyes holding an undisclosed fanaticism. The woman in white sitting in the back compartment got down and let one of the soldiers search the box.","That man only went through the motions.","Inspection passed, clearance granted.","After exiting the city, the donkey cart traveled about half a li before meeting up with a horse team stopped by the side of the official road.","In these times, horses were precious. Merchants traveling to various places for business mostly rode donkeys; the wealthier ones might keep horses. But even if they kept them, they were horses of very ordinary quality. Horses were a strategic resource, and fine-bred horses were, in a sense, not in circulation.","However, this merchant caravan was equipped with tall, sturdy horses, each one glossy and well-fed, with bright, spirited eyes—clearly fine steeds bred for speed.","The donkey cart halted. The woman in white alighted swiftly and lifted Dalì from the back compartment. \"We must be quick. They can't hold out much longer over there.\"","Soon, the merchant caravan changed direction and headed north.","North, towards the Jin River.","Inside the city, at the Jinfengyu Jewelry Store.","The guards sent to the east city to buy honeyed tea had been back for over half an hour, yet Hu Bao still didn't see anyone come downstairs.","Lady Dai rarely lingered in one place for so long...","After some thought, Hu Bao decided to go up. But before he could finish climbing the stairs, a figure appeared at the top.","\"Captain Hu, the weather is getting warmer. The lady suffers in the summer heat and fancies some sweet melon.\" It was Nianxia.","Then, a familiar figure stepped out beside Nianxia. \"The lady says she saw an old man selling melons at the north street entrance on the way here. His melons looked quite good. She wants his. Could you trouble Captain Hu to send someone?\" said Bipo.","Before Hu Bao could respond, as if musing to herself, he heard Bipo whisper to Nianxia:","\"This shop is truly nice, even having a resting area. I reckon the lady will visit often from now on.\"","Finally, Bipo smiled and said, \"Captain Hu, we entrust this to you.\"","Hu Bao retreated. \"It's nothing, just my duty.\"","A guard was dispatched on the order, and Hu Bao continued to wait.","Perhaps it was Hu Bao's imagination, but the trip seemed to take longer than he expected. A round trip to the north street entrance should take at most half an hour, yet it felt like the guard was gone for ages.","It wasn't until the guard returned, panting and out of breath, that Hu Bao knew it wasn't just his imagination.","It wasn't half an hour. It was a full hour.","According to the guard, the old man selling sweet melons at the north street entrance had already packed up his stall. Left with no choice, he had to search for melons elsewhere.","But, oddly enough, sweet melons, usually not hard to find, were nowhere to be seen that day. He visited several large markets and came back empty-handed each time. In the end, he only managed to buy a few from a peasant woman.","Hu Bao strode out of the shop and looked up at the sky.","It was already the end of the Shen hour.","Soon, it would be the You hour, when the sun sets.","The end of the Shen hour. Perhaps because Lady Dai had left at the end of the Shen hour last time, Hu Bao felt an inexplicable aversion to this particular time.","Just then, two young maidens, accompanied by formidable-looking servants, entered the store together. They were clearly from wealthy families. They bypassed the first floor entirely and went straight upstairs.","\"Eh? Why isn't there a single shop assistant on the second floor? Where did everyone go?\" A voice tinged with surprise drifted down.","Hu Bao felt as if he had been struck on the head.","There were supposed to be shop assistants upstairs; otherwise, Nianxia wouldn't have mentioned the shop serving promotional tea. So why were there none now?","Immediately, Hu Bao disregarded all else and bounded up the stairs two or three steps at a time.","His first action upon reaching the top was to search for Dalì.","When he spotted the familiar silhouette behind the curtained-off resting area, his heart settled, but he soon realized something was wrong—","There seemed to be only two figures inside the curtain.","\"Lady Dai,\" Hu Bao called.","There was no response from within.","\"Lady Dai, I beg your pardon.\" His heart pounding wildly, Hu Bao swiftly drew aside the curtain. The sight before him made his vision darken.","There were only Nianxia and Bipo, both with their eyes closed. Lady Dai was nowhere to be found."]},{"number":67,"title":"Chapter 67","paragraphs":["Qin Residence, in the study.","Qin Shaozong was listening to a debriefing. It had been several days since taking over Bai Ri City. A batch of the original Yanzhou officials had been replaced, and deciding how to fill the vacant positions was a delicate art.","This campaign had been a joint effort between two forces. Although Qingzhou was not the main force, they had contributed. It would be unreasonable not to give them even a small share of the spoils.","\"...My Lord, Bai Ri City is fronted by Bai Ri Pass. That pass is strategically important, easy to defend and hard to attack. We absolutely cannot concede Bai Ri City. If Qingzhou pushes for it, at most we can cede a few other counties in Yanzhou instead,\" Nalan Zhi said.","Qin Shaozong: \"Wugong's words are reasonable.\"","After discussing two other matters, the meeting was drawing to a close. Qin Shaozong glanced at the sky outside the window.","Brilliant sunset clouds spread across the entire firmament. As time passed, a shadow appeared on one side of the sky. The areas of light and dark were distinct, as if a corner had been swallowed by a giant beast.","\"Let's stop here for today. We'll discuss other important matters tomorrow,\" Qin Shaozong said to the assembled group.","Everyone bowed with hands clasped and left the study one after another.","Qin Shaozong also rose from his seat, intending to return to the main courtyard.","She should be back by this time. There were still three fish she caught yesterday in the water vat in the courtyard. Finishing them all tonight would be perfect.","But just as he stepped out of the study, he saw someone rushing towards him. Urgent reports were common, but when he saw who it was, the curve of Qin Shaozong's lips flattened.","\"My Lord...\" Hu Bao's face was pale. Kneeling under that icy gaze, he said, \"Lady Dai is missing.\"","His brown pupils constricted to pinpoints for an instant. Qin Shaozong strode forward, grabbed Hu Bao by the collar with one hand, and hauled him up. \"When? How did she disappear?\"","A string in Qin Shaozong's mind was vibrating, shaking him until his blood churned and his eyes turned crimson.","His first thought was that she had run away again.","The promise of \"forever\" she gave him that night was merely a stratagem, never meant to be kept.","Thinking back carefully now, the first time he brought it up, she said she needed a month to seriously consider it. He agreed, so the matter was postponed. Later, when he brought up the old matter again at night, she was evasive. From beginning to end, she never actually said \"yes.\"","She had deceived him again!!","The collar tightening around his neck was uncomfortable, but Hu Bao reported without a moment's pause: \"Between the end of the Hour of the Horse and the end of the Hour of the Monkey. At that time, Lady Dai went to a jewelry store called 'Gold Meets Jade.' The shop assistant said the second floor was full of ladies, including some unmarried young maidens, and asked me to wait on the first floor...\"","Hu Bao reported every detail, including how he guarded the staircase without leaving, how Nianxia and Bipo twice asked him to buy honey tea and sweet melons, hinting that their mistress was resting and that's why she hadn't come downstairs, the surprise of the new customers later, his rush upstairs to find both maids unconscious, and most importantly, the fact that Dai Li had vanished into thin air.","Speaking in one breath and having run back, Hu Bao was panting. Filled with self-blame and guilt, he would have knelt again if Qin Shaozong weren't holding him up.","\"This subordinate failed in his duty. Please punish me, Lord.\"","Qin Shaozong suddenly released his grip. Punishment was the last thing on his mind now. He immediately raised his voice to summon guards: \"Pass the order! Seal the city. Seal Bai Ri City for me!\"","As he strode out, Qin Shaozong said coldly, \"What about the two maids who followed her? They attend to her day and night, watching over her closely. They couldn't possibly be unaware of her plans. If they refuse to talk, use torture.\"","But Hu Bao said, \"My Lord, those two are still at the jewelry store. Somehow, they remain unconscious. Pinching the philtrum, wiping their faces with cold water, or even stimulating other acupoints with needles haven't been able to wake them. It's as if... they were drugged.\"","Qin Shaozong's temples throbbed. Fire surged in his chest, burning his internal organs with pain.","It seemed her preparations this time were unusually thorough. Had she learned from last time's lesson?","Very good. Just wonderful!","Qin Shaozong quickened his pace: \"Notify Ding Congjian. Have him come with me. Last time, a female shop assistant from the silk shop covered for her. This time it must be related to the jewelry store staff. Are the shop assistants under control?\"","Hu Bao kept up. \"They have all been detained and are under watch.\"","Qin Shaozong couldn't wait a moment longer. He was originally headed to the stables to get his own horse, but after turning a corner in a side corridor, all the rage that had been rushing to make him vomit blood was suddenly doused by a bucket of cold water.","Qin Shaozong abruptly stopped, his gaze fixed unblinkingly on the tall, slender figure not far away.","Qin Yanzhou seemed to sense something and turned his head to look at Qin Shaozong. His face showed no expression, but a hint of barely perceptible confusion flickered in his eyes.","Qin Shaozong stood rooted to the spot.","She treasured her son more than her own eyeballs. There was absolutely no reason for her to leave alone while leaving her son behind in the residence.","Was this going against expectations, deliberately leaving in separate groups? Or was there foul play from the beginning, and it had nothing to do with her?","Hu Bao also saw Qin Yanzhou, and his face changed color.","How much Dai Li cherished this son she had regained, they all knew. Logically, it shouldn't be...","\"Keep this confidential for now. Don't let that boy know. Send people to watch him secretly, around the clock. Guard the perimeter of his courtyard at night. I need to know his every move,\" Qin Shaozong said in a low voice.","If it was the former scenario he suspected, the other party would certainly make a move soon and would definitely go to reunite with her. Following the trail would surely reveal her whereabouts.","But if it was the latter...","Qin Shaozong's eyes darkened frighteningly.","The distance wasn't close. Qin Yanzhou didn't hear the conversation between the two men. He only saw Qin Shaozong say something, then lead his men away in a frantic hurry.","The young man withdrew his gaze, not particularly concerned.","\"Clatter, clatter, clatter—\"","Hooves beat against the bluestone paving stones still bathed in the last glow of dusk. The dust stirred up by one set of hooves hadn't even had time to settle before being stamped back down by another.","Several groups of riders split up and went their separate ways.","Teams were sent to each of the four city gates—east, south, west, and north—to seal the city while questioning the guards about the general situation of people leaving the city that day.","Furthermore, people were sent to the Household Registration Office to obtain the census records, then immediately began door-to-door inspections without pause. Meanwhile, the group led by Qin Shaozong himself arrived at the front of 'Gold Meets Jade.'","The tall man reined in his red steed, Chijiao, and dismounted.","The northern soldiers guarding the front of the shop all bowed with clasped hands. Qin Shaozong strode inside without a sideways glance.","Inside the shop, three shop assistants were being held separately. Only after Qin Shaozong arrived did the guards bring them together.","\"My Lord, these are all shop assistants. They were attending to customers on the first floor earlier,\" Hu Bao said.","The shop assistants were pale and trembling.","One of them, his knees giving way, knelt directly on the floor. \"Your Excellency, this humble one only started working here ten days ago. This humble one knows nothing!\"","The other two also chimed in.","One said he had only been in the shop for seven days, the other said eight days; in short, they had both arrived recently.","\"Where is the shopkeeper?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","\"Lord, at that time, there were only these three young assistants on the first floor. They said the shopkeeper had gone out at noon. Before leaving, he had ordered an assistant named Liu to mind the shop, and this Liu...\" Hu Bao pointed at the middle assistant, \"...is him.\"","This person was the very one who had spoken up first earlier, claiming to have been hired only ten days prior.","Qin Shaozong's gaze swept over him coldly and sharply, making the man shiver. However, Qin Shaozong did not question him further for now and proceeded upstairs first.","Second floor.","Nianxia and Bipo were still in the rest area, having barely moved from their spots. Ding Lianxi, carrying his medicine chest, was bustling about. After setting down the chest, he took their pulses.","Qin Shaozong surveyed this floor.","There were quite a few shelves, arranged neatly at equal intervals, each section clearly demarcated. At first glance, it was no different from any other jewelry shop.","But after walking a few steps inward, Qin Shaozong quickly discovered the secret of the \"louvered\" shelves.","The area near the staircase entrance was much higher; one had to go down a few steps to reach the shelf level. Earlier, standing at the staircase entrance, he could see the people behind the shelves through the latticework of the wooden frames.","He could clearly see where the other person was moving and what they were doing, every single action. However, if one stood among the shelves and looked out, they couldn't see anything at all.","Qin Shaozong closed his eyes.","There was no need to wait until tonight to verify whether that brat had made a move; he could now be certain that someone had abducted her. Relying on her own strength alone, it was absolutely impossible for her to have orchestrated all this without his knowledge.","As if confirming his thoughts, someone called out, \"Lord, there's a hidden passage here.\"","Qin Shaozong's eyes snapped open, and he followed the sound.","A bronze mirror, used for adjusting attire and viewing jewelry, had been pushed aside, revealing a narrow, downward-sloping passage. A row of small lanterns hung in the passage, but the candles inside had burned out, not emitting the slightest glimmer of light.","Looking down from the entrance, this pitch-black corridor resembled a long serpent with a gaping maw, ready to devour any passerby.","Qin Shaozong descended the passage and found himself in the backyard of the first floor.","A small courtyard led to a back door, which connected to a rear alley. From that alley, one could turn onto the main street leading to all four city gates.","\"Lord, those young assistants might just be decoys,\" Hu Bao said in a low voice.","Having arrived only a few days ago and knowing nothing when questioned—what else could they be but decoys prepared to deal with the situation?","\"Investigate the information on this shop,\" Qin Shaozong left the order and exited through the back door.","Summer rains were plentiful, and a light rain had fallen last night. The rear alleyway wasn't very wide, and the walls on both sides blocked the sunlight, making this place cooler and gloomier than the outside.","The bluestone bricks used for paving became patchy here—some areas were paved, others were not.","Qin Shaozong lowered his gaze to the ground.","Both donkey and horse dung could be used as fertilizer after processing. Therefore, if such things appeared on the main streets, they would be collected.","Of course, some people preferred not to let others benefit; believing that \"fertile water should not flow into another's fields\" (i.e., don't let outsiders reap the benefits), they would hang a bag behind their donkey and replace it when it was full.","Currently, this rear alley was clean, with no trace of donkey or horse dung on the ground, as if no carriage had ever passed through here.","But it was only 'as if.'","Qin Shaozong spotted some faint hoof prints. He walked over and examined them carefully. \"A donkey cart.\"","Donkey carts were far less conspicuous than horse carriages. In the commandery, households owning donkeys numbered at least in the hundreds.","Moreover, with a hidden passage, special shelves, and temporarily hired assistants... Since the other party was willing to go to such great lengths to set up this scheme, they must have ensured a successful outcome in one move.","They definitely wouldn't lack even a few horses.","Though he was extremely reluctant to admit it, Qin Shaozong knew in his heart that there was over a fifty percent chance she had already been moved elsewhere...","Qin Shaozong's expression turned extremely grim.","\"Lord, the two maidservants have regained consciousness,\" a guard reported.","Without a word, Qin Shaozong turned and went back upstairs via the passage.","Ding Lianxi was packing his chest. Seeing Qin Shaozong, he cupped his hands respectfully. \"My lord, these two most likely ingested pills made from henbane seeds. I have already cleared the henbane's effects from their systems. However, while henbane is easy to counteract, 'dumb grass' cannot be neutralized quickly.\"","Qin Shaozong paused. \"'Dumb grass'?\"","Ding Lianxi nodded. \"Yes. They ingested dumb grass and will be unable to speak for a while.\"","Nianxia and Bipo were now awake. Seeing Qin Shaozong's terrifying expression and surrounded by a circle of armed guards, their faces turned as pale as gold paper.","Both women tried to speak, but when they opened their mouths, no sound came from their throats. They immediately broke into a frantic sweat.","\"If you can't speak, then write it down,\" Hu Bao said, then realized his mistake.","The likelihood of maidservants being literate wasn't high.","\"Can you read?\" Hu Bao amended his question.","Sure enough, both women shook their heads.","The atmosphere seemed to freeze. Everyone looked at Qin Shaozong, awaiting his instructions.","Qin Shaozong looked at the two women, his eyes like sharp blades. \"I will ask questions. You answer. Nod for yes, shake your head for no. If I later discover you have lied...\"","Before he could finish, both women were already kowtowing, their foreheads thumping loudly against the wooden floorboards.","Qin Shaozong asked, \"Did you lose consciousness upstairs?\"","Bipo nodded.","Nianxia shook her head. She pointed downstairs and even mimicked the action of relieving herself.","Hu Bao beside them exclaimed in shock, \"Impossible! I clearly saw you go upstairs!\"","Nianxia waved her hands frantically and then raised a hand as if swearing an oath.","Qin Shaozong twisted the thumb ring on his finger, his gaze dark and unreadable.","Hu Bao had joined the Northern Army before coming of age and had served for twenty years now. His entire family was in Yuyang. He couldn't possibly betray him.","These two maidservants were selected in Ying Commandery, screened repeatedly. Ying Commandery was hundreds of kilometers from White Sun City and was previously under a different jurisdiction. Moreover, the selection of maidservants happened almost immediately after Madam drew the dragon-bone waterwheel, within less than twelve hours. There was no time for them to set up a scheme.","Plus, with the hidden passage downstairs, if she had been drugged in the privy, she could indeed have been brought back upstairs via the passage.","Hu Bao wasn't lying, and the maidservants weren't lying either.","Qin Shaozong looked at Hu Bao. \"Are you certain the person you saw was really her?\"","Hu Bao nodded. \"Certain. Putting aside height and appearance, even the clothing and hairstyle were identical.\"","Upon hearing this, Nianxia's tears welled up. She kowtowed repeatedly and gestured frantically with her hands, utterly frustrated by her current inability to speak.","Qin Shaozong asked again, \"Do you have any memory of buying honeyed tea?\"","Both women shook their heads; they had no memory of it.","\"When was the first time she asked you to buy honeyed tea?\" Qin Shaozong asked, turning his head to Hu Bao.","Hu Bao had been guarding the staircase and was not sensitive to the passage of time, so he called over the errand-running guard.","The guard reported thus: \"The honey tea was bought at the end of the Hour of the Horse, the sweet melon at the end of the Hour of the Goat.\"","\"She was already gone by the end of the Hour of the Horse.\" Qin Shaozong expressionlessly removed the jade thumb ring, now crisscrossed with cracks. \"Send men to the four city gates. Ask them how many donkey carts left the city during the Hour of the Goat.\"","The guard accepted the order and left.","Qin Shaozong lowered his gaze to Nianxia and Bipo. \"Before entering this jewelry shop today, did anything unusual happen? For instance, did anyone stop the carriage or approach her on their own initiative?\"","The two maidservants shook their heads again.","Nothing unusual had occurred. Everything was as normal.","It was precisely because of this that Bipo and Nianxia felt a creeping dread in their hearts. It was over. No one could vouch for their innocence...","\"Take them back to the manor first, post guards to keep them under strict watch. Also, send someone to the Census Office to investigate the owner of this 'Gold Meets Jade' shop. Find out who he is, his ancestral hometown, his family members, and when he took over this shop.\" After leaving these instructions, Qin Shaozong turned and walked toward the staircase without looking back.","He went downstairs, mounted his horse with practiced ease, the hem of his black robe flaring in a sharp arc. Before it had even settled completely, Red Serpent, having felt the sting of the whip, charged forward.","White Sun Pass had fallen, and White Sun City was undergoing a transfer of power. Like Qin Shaozong before him, Nangong Xiong was now pondering how to secure more key positions for his own men.","Before he could even decide how to broach the subject, he heard a soldier report that the Marquis of Wu'an had come to his door.","Nangong Xiong was greatly surprised, thinking to himself that his little schemes had only just begun to take shape, yet Qin Changgeng was already at his doorstep. Could that fellow actually divine the future?","And it was already the Hour of the Rooster, wasn't it? Looking outside, only a faint glimmer of light remained in the sky. What matter was so urgent for Qin Changgeng?","Composing himself, Nangong Xiong went out to greet his guest. Upon entering the main hall, he was inwardly startled.","Qin Shaozong had not taken a seat!","One must know that when he went to see Fan Tianshi, this man hadn't even bothered to rise to greet him, sitting arrogantly in his chair with an air of utmost importance. Yet now he was standing, waiting for Nangong to appear.","For a moment, Nangong Xiong felt rather flattered, but this feeling came quickly and faded just as fast.","From the moment he entered, the other man's icy, even murderous gaze shot straight at him. If looks could turn into blades, he would likely be in several pieces by now.","Nangong Xiong frowned with displeasure. \"Qin Changgeng, what kind of look is that? When did I offend you?\"","Qin Shaozong stared fixedly at him. \"When will Nangong Qingzhou return my person to me? If he returns her, what would it matter if I gave you this White Sun City?\"","Nangong Xiong was first stunned, then pressed urgently, \"What do you mean, 'return your person'? Who? Who are you talking about? Give me a name, and I promise I'll catch her and drag her right before you!\"","But Qin Shaozong suddenly turned and walked out.","Nangong Xiong sprinted after him. \"Qin Changgeng, don't leave! Make it clear to me, who are you looking for? Hey, hey, have you eaten dinner? Why not stay and eat at my residence? We can drink and sing, and discuss White Sun City in detail.\"","Qin Shaozong said nothing, only quickened his pace, leaving the residence in moments.","Red Serpent was pacing before the gate and snorted upon seeing his master emerge.","Qin Shaozong swung onto the horse, but before he could raise his whip, the horse's reins were seized by another hand—it was Nangong Xiong, who had chased him out.","\"Qin Changgeng, explain your words clearly. What do you mean, 'return her, and White Sun City is yours'?\" Nangong Xiong's heart was itching unbearably.","Qin Shaozong suddenly laughed. \"I just saw you were itching for the city, scratching your heart and lungs, so I was joking with you.\"","Nangong Xiong was dumbfounded, then immediately began cursing furiously. \"Qin Changgeng, you scoundrel! You actually made a fool of me! Do you not know what it means that 'a true man's word, once spoken, cannot be overtaken even by a team of four horses'?\"","\"I know. That's why I added a precondition, didn't I?\" Qin Shaozong brushed aside the hand holding the reins. \"No need to get angry over such a small thing. Alright, go back and have your meal. I'm returning to my manor.\"","Nangong Xiong nearly spat out a mouthful of old blood.","This fellow plays a trick on someone and then blames them for getting angry? Is there no justice in the world? Qin Changgeng is so arrogant, just wait, he'll get his comeuppance one day!","Qin Shaozong raised his whip and urged his horse on. Red Serpent carried him swiftly into the distance. Only after leaving Nangong's residence did the ease and nonchalance he had worn on his face finally vanish, like the last bit of light in the sky, utterly swallowed by gloom.","It doesn't seem like Qingzhou's doing. Then who on earth is it?"]},{"number":68,"title":"Chapter 68","paragraphs":["Qin Estate, Study.","\"Lord Marquis, we have uncovered something. The proprietor of 'Jin Feng Yu' is surnamed Zhao. His ancestral home is in Guiyang, Sizhou, and he currently resides in Qing Lane in the east of the city. He came to Bai Ri City to make a living ten years ago. According to neighbors, his wife took their young son back to her parents' home to visit ten days ago and has not yet returned.\"","In the study, the assembled generals who had just learned of Dai Li's disappearance collectively drew a sharp, hissing breath.","\"Ten years ago?\"","\"The wife leaves first, he follows later. This is a case of the building being emptied of people!\"","\"What manner of demon is behind this? Could it be remnants from Yanzhou seeking revenge for that scoundrel Fan Tianshi?\"","\"Impossible. Seeking revenge on a woman is not the act of a true man. Furthermore, the two maidservants attending Lady Dai are still alive; only Lady Dai herself is missing. If it were revenge, wouldn't a single stroke of the blade be simpler? Why take her?\"","\"Could it be Qingzhou?\"","At this point, Qin Shaozong spoke, \"I previously tested Nan Gongxiong; his reaction seemed genuine, like he knew nothing.\"","The room fell silent.","They never doubted the Lord Marquis's accuracy in judging people. In the years since the Lord Marquis fully took command of the Northern Army, every single hidden spy he had rooted out was a correct identification—not one innocent person was wrongly accused.","\"Lord Marquis, the brothers investigating the city gate guards have returned.\" Bai Jianping, having received the summary, strode into the room. \"In the early Wei hour (1-3 PM), among the four city gates—east, south, west, and north—only the west gate had no donkey carts leaving the city.\"","Qiao Wangfei's brow twitched. \"We only eliminated one, leaving east, south, and north. That's still too broad. This information isn't very useful!\"","Feng Feng turned to look at the sheepskin map nearby, stroking his chin. \"Not necessarily. Bai Ri City connects east to Bai Ri Pass, and further east lies Qi Jiang County, which we previously captured. The south is Red Horn Peak. Anyone leaving through the south gate would inevitably head towards Lu Chuan County, which lies southwest and adjacent to Red Horn Peak, as that's the only inhabited place south of Bai Ri City. Then there's the north. Bai Ri City borders the Jin River to the north, with a ferry crossing. One can travel east or west by boat.\"","\"In my humble opinion, heading north to the Jin River is the most likely, followed by south, then east. After all, the east is already the Lord Marquis's territory,\" Feng Feng concluded.","Mo Yanyun recalled a past event. \"Last time, Lady Dai traveled by boat to Tai Ping County. Could they be taking the water route again this time? Although villains are at work, the convenience remains the same. Simply put, water travel is more convenient than land and harder to intercept.\"","Qiao Wangfei said hesitantly, \"What you say makes sense, but what if they are trying to do the opposite? Could they guess what we are thinking and intentionally head east instead?\"","His words caused another silence to fall over the room.","\"That Merchant Zhao came here ten years ago. That's a deeply buried spy. Who's to say there aren't spies elsewhere?\" Qiao Wangfei whispered.","Another group of guards came to report.","\"Lord Marquis, all the relay hostels in the commandery have been searched. No unidentified women checked in today.\"","\"Lord Marquis, the owner of that tea house in the east city indeed knows Merchant Zhao, but he claims it's merely an acquaintance, with no deep friendship. He said that on a certain day half a month ago, Merchant Zhao took the initiative to visit, proposing to promote his tea house. Such an unsolicited benefit, the owner naturally didn't refuse. When the owner asked Merchant Zhao what his conditions were, the latter only said he would tell him later, but there has been no further word until today.\"","\"Lord Marquis, the old man selling melons has been found. He said that at exactly noon, a man with dark skin and an ordinary face suddenly came, bought all his melons, so the old man packed up early and went home.\"","\"Exactly noon?\"","Hu Bao murmured, \"That was before Madam's carriage had even reached 'Jin Feng Yu'. Calculated, it was just as her carriage passed that old man's melon stall.\"","The guard continued his report: \"This subordinate visited other melon vendors in the city. Some said a woman bought all their melons, others said it was a man. The accounts vary and are conflicting. However, one point is the same. All these vendors said the buyer requested home delivery.\"","\"Home delivery? Then there must be an address! Who owns that residence?\" Qiao Wangfei hurriedly asked.","The guard looked towards Qin Shaozong behind the long desk, his tone becoming more cautious. \"Lord Marquis, that residence is an empty house. It was put up for sale half a year ago and still has no owner. The melon vendors could enter because someone bribed the property agent for the key to temporarily open the door. And the person who bribed the agent left Bai Ri City a few days ago.\"","The study fell quiet once more, everyone frowning in worry.","The house was borrowed, the person has already fled.","Another lead has gone cold.","Mo Yanyun was puzzled. \"Their target was Lady Dai, right? Why go to such great lengths to buy all the melons in the city?\"","\"Time.\" Qin Shaozong held a tiger-shaped brush rest, his long fingers gently stroking its back. \"They wanted to obscure Hu Bao's perception of time.\"","Hu Bao had been guarding the staircase entrance and couldn't see the sky outside. Based on his initial knowledge of the melon seller's location, he felt this trip would take at most half a shichen (an hour).","When the soldier didn't return for a long time, Hu Bao would only think his own judgment was off. Because besides that old melon seller, one could still buy melons a bit further down the road.","After Bai Ri City was captured and its defenses replaced, Hu Bao's subconscious believed more firmly that the city was peaceful and nothing would happen.","Hu Bao lowered his head in shame. \"Lord Marquis, this subordinate failed in his duty. Please punish me.\"","Qin Shaozong did not speak.","He could not concern himself with punishment now. The urgent priority was to find her...","\"They abducted her, they must have arranged a carriage. From here to Lu Chuan County, by carriage it takes two days and one night.\" Qin Shaozong assigned the task. \"Qiao Wangfei, take a team and set off south immediately for Lu Chuan County. Inspect all caravans you encounter along the way. Once in Lu Chuan County, post people at all four city gates to strictly inspect every carriage entering afterwards.\"","Lu Chuan County belonged to Yanzhou. Now that Fan Tianshi had been executed, his reach could extend there directly.","Qiao Wangfei cupped his hands in acknowledgment. \"As you command!\"","Qin Shaozong looked at Feng Feng. \"Feng Feng, you lead men through Bai Ri Pass to Qi Jiang County. Do as Qiao Wangfei does.\"","He paused, remembering something. \"I recall there's a ruined temple west of Qi Jiang County. Don't miss that spot either.\"","Feng Feng accepted the order.","Qin Shaozong then assigned Mo Yanyun, ordering him to lead troops to search the west.","Yes, still search to the west. Even though no donkey carts passed through the west gate in the early Wei hour, they would not neglect this direction.","Mo Yanyun received the order and left with the other two.","Having dealt with the east, south, and west directions, Qin Shaozong pointed to the two remaining Xuan Xiao Cavalry squad leaders. \"Bai Jianping, Wei Qing, each of you take a team to the Jin River. Bai Jianping heads west along the river, Wei Qing follows the river east. Leave a group of men at every ferry crossing you reach. Have these soldiers inspect cargo at that crossing and keep an eye out for women with a figure similar to the Lady's. Don't neglect the river itself either. Randomly stop vessels for inspection. Those unwilling to comply, arrest them directly.\"","The two men accepted their orders and left.","Only Qin Shaozong, Hu Bao, and Nalan Zhi remained in the study.","Nalan Zhi then spoke: \"To replace Lady Dai without anyone noticing would require an extraordinary amount of manpower and resources. Master, the one behind the scenes who has the capability to set up such a scheme must possess considerable power. If it wasn't Qingzhou or Yanzhou, then I have a speculation in mind.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"Wugong, speak freely.\"","Nalan Zhi said seriously: \"Master, regarding the previous matters of the divine signs and the nursery rhymes, perhaps Yanzhou was not the only one involved. Think back to why we marched south in the first place.\"","Qin Shaozong was slightly taken aback.","He had known from the start that there was something suspicious about the divine signs. Whoever benefited the most was likely the mastermind behind it. Since the divine signs and nursery rhymes occurred before the war, he naturally assumed it was related to Fan Tianshi, that it was Yanzhou's doing.","With Fan Tianshi's death, he considered the matter closed. But now, Nalan Zhi's words suggested another possibility.","Qin Shaozong lowered his gaze, his fingertips tapping rapidly on the desk as his thoughts swiftly rewound.","Like rewinding a tape, first came the sudden appearance of the divine signs and nursery rhymes, then the breakdown of the tripartite meeting, followed by him leading troops to Guoyun County, and finally receiving the invitation from Nangong Xiong.","The letter at the time said that on the eve of the alliance between Yanzhou and Qingzhou to jointly attack the Qinglian Sect, the alliance became precarious due to the death of a Yanzhou general...","Qin Shaozong's pupils constricted, \"The Qinglian Sect?\"","Nalan Zhi nodded, his expression grave as he said: \"That is precisely my speculation. Initially, Yanzhou and Qingzhou formed an alliance. Later, their alliance became shaky, and you, Master, led your army south to ally with Qingzhou. After your involvement, the situation became two against one, isolating Yanzhou. Especially after you later shot and killed his legitimate eldest son, it is not impossible for Fan of Yanzhou to switch sides.\"","He paused before adding a final reminder: \"Master, you must not forget that Fan of Yanzhou's relationship with the Qinglian Sect has always been ambiguous.\"","This last statement was not unfounded.","After Qin Shaozong became the heir of the Qin clan, he immediately began cultivating spies, a process that had lasted over a decade. These individuals were later dispersed across various provinces, becoming his eyes and ears.","These agents had once sent back messages stating that Fan Tianshi had frequently traveled to Huai'an County in recent years, each time returning with some beautiful concubines.","Well, that was all.","As for whether there were any substantial transactions involved, the spies could not uncover. Moreover, Fan Tianshi had not visited Huai'an County in the following years, so it could only be described as an \"ambiguous relationship.\"","Qin Shaozong was silent for a moment. \"Fifty years ago, the Qinglian Sect heavily supported the rebellious prince's attempt to usurp the throne. After the prince's defeat, they were severely crippled. Perhaps learning a lesson, they have not appeared openly in the decades since.\"","Nalan Zhi nodded. \"Indeed, they have not been on the open stage. They lie dormant among the common people, blending into the lowest levels of society. But Master, just because ants are tiny and hard to see without stooping down, one should not overlook the capability of the entire colony. A thousand-mile dike can be destroyed by an anthill, let alone other things.\"","Qin Shaozong pinched the bridge of his nose. \"It was my oversight.\"","This Qinglian Sect thing really hadn't registered much with him. As the Guardian Deity of the Northern Border, his prestige in the northern regions was exceedingly high.","As the saying goes, 'Where the wind blows, the grass bends.' Qin Shaozong himself intensely disliked Taoist priests and Buddhist teachings. Seeing this, the officials and common people of the north naturally followed suit. Even if they worshipped Buddha or participated in religious activities, they did so secretly, never flaunting it before him.","Over time, the presence of the Qinglian Sect in the Yuyang area became almost negligible, no different from ants. Qin Shaozong grew accustomed to this and did not take the Qinglian Sect, which lacked a formal armed force, seriously.","But as Nalan Zhi said, ants that are hard to see without stooping down can sometimes deliver a fatal blow.","\"Huai'an County.\" Qin Shaozong gripped the tiger-shaped brush rest. \"Hu Bao, go convey my military order. Have the Xuanxiao Cavalry mobilize tonight. Tomorrow, they will accompany me to Huai'an County.\"","The Qinglian Sect is merely a religious sect, without the authority to openly conscript soldiers. Such a force, even if it gathered troops, would not be particularly formidable.","One unit of the Xuanxiao Cavalry would be sufficient.","Hearing his tone, Nalan Zhi knew he was determined to go.","It couldn't be dissuaded, nor was there any need to try.","Hu Bao was just about to cup his hands in salute when he suddenly heard hurried footsteps from outside.","Someone rushed in: \"My Lord!\"","The voice arrived before the person. Upon entering, the man said: \"My Lord, the spy in Huai'an County has just sent word. On the seventeenth, he saw a large number of carriages leaving the Tianhe Estate. A day later, even the gatekeeper's figure was nowhere to be seen. The spy scaled the wall to enter and found the estate completely empty.\"","The Tianhe Estate was currently the only confirmed Qinglian Sect stronghold that had been discovered. Judging by its scale, one could even say this Tianhe Estate was the core of the Qinglian Sect's operations in Huai'an County.","And the \"seventeenth\" mentioned by the guard was the third day after Qin Shaozong's successful surprise attack on the Yanzhou military camp.","\"They fled?!\"","Qin Yanzhou had been waiting in the main courtyard.","He knew his mother had gone out to the market at noon and might have dinner outside. So, after the usual dinner time had passed and Dai Li had not returned, Qin Yanzhou ate first.","By the time he finished his meal, only a faint glow remained in the vast sky. Soon, he thought, it would be completely dark.","With the onset of night came the curfew. Pedestrians returned home, shops closed, and there was nowhere left in the city to wander.","Qin Yanzhou looked towards the moon gate. It was quiet, showing no sign of anyone's return.","The young man rose from his seat, intending to go out alone to search for her, when he heard footsteps.","The steps were hurried and somewhat heavy—definitely not a woman's gait.","The ripple of anticipation in Qin Yanzhou's eyes settled back into calmness.","The newcomer was indeed a man. Seeing him in the courtyard, the guard stopped at the moon gate: \"Young Master, the Lord requests your presence in the study.\"","\"I have matters to attend to outside the estate,\" Qin Yanzhou simply stated.","The guard understood his implication and could only say: \"This matter concerns Lady Dai, who has not yet returned to the estate.\"","Qin Yanzhou's expression changed slightly. Without further discussion, he changed direction and headed for the study.","Whether in Guoyun County, Qijiang County, or now in Baiyi City, Qin Yanzhou had never once set foot in the study, the core of power. This was his first time.","Upon entering, he saw the floor in disarray.","Many items were scattered beside the long desk: rolled bamboo scrolls, wax seals, writing brushes, and other objects. It looked as if the master had recently flown into a rage, taking it out on the innocent furnishings.","Nothing and no one in this estate, except for his mother, could stir his emotions. But at this moment, looking at the scattered debris, Qin Yanzhou felt an inexplicable twitch in his brow.","The man behind the long desk had a dark, somber expression, the aura around him frighteningly oppressive.","Qin Yanzhou met his gaze directly. \"I wonder what matter the Marquis of Wu'an seeks me for.\"","\"Your mother went out to the market today and was secretly abducted by villains,\" Qin Shaozong stated bluntly, then proceeded to concisely explain the course of events.","Qin Yanzhou's perpetually impassive face now resembled a glacier struck by a tremendous force, fissured with countless cracks. At this moment, questioning the guards for their negligence was utterly meaningless. He demanded sharply, \"Who is responsible?!\"","\"Fan Tianshi has been eliminated. The Yanzhou faction is leaderless, scrambling to flee; they couldn't possibly have the capacity to plan this. I've also probed Qingzhou; it likely wasn't Nan Gongxiong's doing. My personal suspicion falls on the Qinglian Sect.\" As he spoke these words, Qin Shaozong's gaze remained fixed on the young man seated across the desk.","A chill shot up from the soles of Qin Yanzhou's feet, exploding within his mind and causing his frame to sway slightly.","In that instant, numerous conjectures flashed through his heart, only to be replaced by a single, resolute decision.","Qin Shaozong's tone was unreadable. \"You are her son; you have the right to know this, which is why I'm telling you. But there's no need for you to involve yourself. I have already dispatched men to search in all four directions. You will wait here. Spare her the worry of not finding you upon her return.\"","\"As her son, how can I stand idly by while my mother is in peril?\" Qin Yanzhou directly refuted him. Leaving only those words behind, he turned and strode swiftly away.","Qin Shaozong's expression darkened. He barked at Hu Bao, \"Stop him! He is not to leave the estate!\"","Hu Bao, accepting the order, immediately gave chase.","The front courtyard of the study instantly became a scene of commotion as guards, following commands, joined Hu Bao in surrounding Qin Yanzhou.","While the clash raged outside, the atmosphere inside the study grew heavy and tense.","Qin Shaozong took a deep breath, as if speaking to himself or to Dai Li, who was not present. \"That boy might have backing. He cannot be allowed to return.\"","Nalan Zhi, having known Qin Shaozong for over twenty years, spoke up after Hu Bao's departure. \"My lord suspects Yanzhou has support behind him?\"","Qin Shaozong countered, \"Does Wugong not think so?\"","Nalan Zhi fell into a rare silence for a moment.","Qin Shaozong stated calmly, \"Nine years ago, the heavens were unkind. Plagues of insects arose, leading to a great famine where the fields yielded no harvest. That boy left his mother ten years ago and only arrived at the Fan residence seven years ago. Where was he during those three intervening years? I do not believe a helpless, orphaned child could have survived alone.\"","Of course, there was more to it than that.","Bai Jianping had privately confided that when he crossed blades with the young man, he sensed his martial arts foundation was exceptionally solid, and his movement techniques showed distinct schooled refinement.","Fan Tianshi adopted orphans to raise as hounds. While he would hire instructors to train them, he certainly wouldn't invest wholeheartedly. It was a process of survival of the fittest; only those who remained would receive his undivided attention and instruction.","This meant the orphans typically needed two years, or even longer, before they received truly unreserved teaching. Their foundations were seldom exceptionally solid.","Everyone has their own secrets. She had hers, and her son had his.","Before, when she was by his side, he could afford to turn a blind eye to such matters.","Now, he could no longer do so."]},{"number":69,"title":"Chapter 69","paragraphs":["When Daili regained consciousness, what met her eyes was a plain-colored bed curtain with faint peony patterns on it. It didn't look like an ordinary thing.","When she first woke up, Daili's head was dizzy, as if a rolling pin had stirred vigorously in her brain several times. Her memories were scattered, here and there.","Moreover, she wondered if it was just her imagination, but she felt that the couch beneath her seemed to be swaying.","\"Madam, you're awake,\" suddenly someone spoke.","It was a very strange voice, neither masculine nor feminine, completely unfamiliar to her.","Daili gave a start. Invisible ropes instantly extended outward, pulling back and piecing together her fragmented memories. The previous scenes emerged clearly in front of her eyes.","The jewelry store, Nianxia and Bipo, the maid with the tea tray...","Daili suddenly sat up. But perhaps it was because she got up too abruptly or for some other reason. After sitting up, she felt dizzy and fell backward. However, before she could fall, she was held up.","\"Madam, be careful.\"","Only then did Daili see clearly the person who had just spoken.","With willow-leaf eyebrows and almond eyes, the person in front of her was dressed in white, with a quiet and gentle temperament, like a graceful beauty stepping out of a painting of ladies. But her voice was extremely heroic, with a sharpness completely different from her appearance.","\"Who are you? Why did you kidnap me here?\" Daili pushed away the hand that was holding her.","It was impossible not to be anxious at this moment. She had disappeared without saying a word to Zhouzhou. Her son must be extremely worried.","But when talking to such a stranger, it was most taboo to show one's weakness. Only the high-ranking military generals in the northern region knew that she had found her son. Before figuring out who these people in front of her were, Daili would never expose any extra information.","Seeing Daili's defensiveness, the white-clothed woman smiled slightly. \"Madam, there's no need to be so on guard. We are the lay believers of the Puhua sect, the tonsured monks. People usually call me Xiuniang. Madam can also call me that.\"","Daili was stunned.","Lay believers of the Puhua sect? Tonsured monks?","This title sounded so much like...","\"Are you the Qinglian Sect?\" Daili asked in surprise.","Xiuniang nodded with a smile. \"Yes, Madam has indeed heard of us.\"","Daili's eyelids twitched.","Well, the Qinglian Sect that Qin Shaozong wanted to wipe out, and she actually ran into them?","\"Why did you kidnap me?\" Daili frowned.","\"Marquis Wuan is vulgar and forced Madam to be his concubine. Madam is well-versed in strategies and has the talent to govern the country. It's really a disgrace for you to be just a favored concubine. Our master pities Madam for being in a difficult situation and can't bear to see you being buried. So he found a way to take you away from Baori City,\" Xiuniang explained.","Daili slowly lowered her eyes, covering the darkness in them.","This person who called herself Xiuniang could say the word \"forced\", which meant that the other party must know that she had once fled from Nankang County. Pretending to be stupid with Xiuniang at this moment would only raise the other party's suspicion.","Showing a little hesitation on her face, Daili didn't respond to her words. Instead, she said, \"I'm a bit hungry.\"","There was a window in her room. The sunlight outside the window boldly shone into the room, casting large bright patches of light.","It was daytime.","She hadn't had dinner last night, so it wasn't a lie to say she was hungry now.","\"Let me help you up,\" Xiuniang reached out her hand again.","Daili didn't refuse this time because she noticed that there was something wrong with her body. It had been a while since she woke up, but she still couldn't muster any strength, and there was a strange taste in her mouth.","\"Did you give me something to eat?\" Daili asked anxiously.","Traditional Chinese medicine was profound, and so was pharmacy. She was very worried that she had taken poison and would have to rely on them to detoxify later.","Daili had lain down fully dressed last night. Now, all she needed to do was straighten the folds of her clothes and put on her shoes. Xiuniang bent down to put on her shoes. During this process, her eyes inevitably fell on Daili's embroidered shoes again.","The shoes were made of brocade, with moon-white mother-of-pearl pieces on the surface, shining brightly in the sun. There was a large and plump pearl inlaid at the toe of the shoe, emitting a soft glow. It was obviously a rare treasure.","Xiuniang lowered her eyes upon seeing this. \"You had a tiring journey yesterday. We were worried that Madam would be exhausted on the way, so we fed Madam a calming pill.\"","Daili was skeptical. \"Is that all?\"","Xiuniang was like handling a large doll. She first helped Daili, who had already put on her shoes, to turn to the side, and then helped her tidy up her loose hair. \"Of course. Madam is our master's honored guest, so we naturally need to treat you with courtesy.\"","Within half a meter was an intimate distance. Daili wasn't used to strangers getting close, especially when she couldn't see the other person at the moment. She suppressed her discomfort. \"Who is your master?\"","\"Madam will know later,\" Xiuniang only said.","After simply helping Daili tie up her hair and wash up, Xiuniang helped her out of the room. When they reached the door, Daili pushed away her hand. \"I can walk by myself. I can manage slowly.\"","Xiuniang didn't force her.","Daili had suspected that the couch was swaying before. Now, when she walked out onto the corridor deck and saw the surging river, she realized that they were really on a boat.","There were green mountains on both sides of the river, and a few boats were floating on the river. The view was extremely broad. The wind carrying the moisture of the water blew on her face, bringing a bit of freshness. The sunlight danced on the river, creating layers of broken golden light.","Normally, people would feel relaxed and happy when viewing such a scene.","Daili was the exception.","Looking at the flowing river, she was extremely anxious. There was only one Jinshui River flowing from west to east near Baori City. Now that the boat was going upstream, she was heading west.","To the west was the territory of Yanzhou.","With one night and half a day, going upstream by boat was enough to travel dozens of miles.","\"Madam, please,\" Xiuniang stood outside the corridor, keeping Daili away from the railing.","Daili withdrew her gaze and followed her to the main hall.","The main hall filled with the fragrance of agarwood was empty. There was no one there at the moment. Daili casually sat down in front of a table.","It was just a short walk through a side corridor deck from the room to the main hall. When she sat down, Daili clearly felt that her heart rate was abnormally high and she was very tired. She guessed it was because the medicine hadn't been completely metabolized yet.","So when Xiuniang asked someone to bring up the soup cakes, Daili ate them all up, not even leaving a drop of the soup.","Seeing that Daili had a good appetite, the smile on Xiuniang's face deepened. \"What else would Madam like to eat?\"","Daili said, \"Please give me a glass of water. Not tea, but cooled boiled water.\"","\"Please wait here for a moment,\" Xiuniang left the main hall.","Not long after she left, Daili heard footsteps. The person approaching walked steadily, neither too fast nor too slow, with a natural air of calmness.","Soon, a tall and slender figure entered from the outside.","The young man was dressed in white. His face was handsome, and the flowing cloud robe with embroidered cranes and gold-trimmed edges suited him perfectly. As he walked, the wide sleeves of his white robe fluttered slightly, like the wings of a white crane spreading out. In the agarwood fragrance filling the room, he looked extremely ethereal.","Diting","Meeting Daili's eyes, he showed a gentle smile. \"Did Madam sleep well last night?\"","Daili thought to herself that this person must be doing it on purpose. He had given her medicine, making her unconscious, and then asked her if she had slept well.","He was testing her personality right from the start.","\"It's neither good nor bad,\" Daili said indifferently.","With her face set in an aloof expression, she was still astonishingly beautiful, exuding an air of haughty coldness and a strong sense of distance.","Diting's gaze lingered on Daili's eyebrows for a moment, but was distracted by the cinnabar mole on her forehead. When he regained his senses, the fleeting thought had vanished without a trace.","\"Marquis Wu'an keeps a tight rein on his wife. I had no choice but to resort to this measure. I hope the lady will understand,\" Diting said as he took a seat opposite her.","\"How should I address you, sir?\" Daili asked.","Diting lifted his hand to move the small stove and placed the pottery pot on it. \"I'm Diting. The lady can just call me Diting.\"","Daili seemed to be deep in thought.","Diting was the mount of the Bodhisattva Ksitigarbha, a auspicious beast that protected its master. Compared to \"Xiuniang\", the meaningful name \"Diting\" was obviously closer to the core of the group.","Daili said, \"I heard from Xiuniang that you thought I had the talent to govern the country, so you brought me out of Bairi City. But I wonder where this great talent of mine comes from?\"","Diting let out a soft laugh. \"The lady need not be modest. I know that the refined salt was your work. There's also the dragon - bone waterwheel. Although it's widely rumored that the lady obtained it from a hermit surnamed Ma, this hermit...\"","Here, Diting shook his head. \"Can't be found.\"","Daili slightly raised her finely - arched eyebrows. \"Are you so sure it was me? The salt lake in Ying County was previously occupied by a salt smuggler surnamed Li. Why couldn't it be that the smuggler had just figured out how to make refined salt, but unfortunately, before he could make it public, Marquis Qin got there first and took it?\"","Diting shook his head with a smile. \"It couldn't be him.\"","His words were so definite that Daili suddenly remembered that after the great victory at Taohua Ridge, at the bonfire feast, Qin Shaozong had said that Li Zan's power had grown at an unusual speed, and there might be a mystery behind it.","Now, it seemed that the mystery was sitting right in front of her.","Daili turned to look out of the window. The sun was shining brightly, and it was a beautiful day. \"Yes, the refined salt was indeed my work. But I think there's a misunderstanding. As the saying goes, everyone has their own area of expertise. Just researching refined salt has exhausted all my energy in the first half of my life. I really can't live up to your praise of 'talent to govern the country'.\"","\"Does the lady really want to stay by Marquis Wu'an's side forever? Marquis Wu'an has an inauspicious fate. He has a shallow relationship with his relatives. In the past, his parents, elder brother, sister - in - law, and wife all died one after another because of him. Moreover, the marquis has never been interested in women. He's not a good match. Not to mention that he had an agreement with the Wei family, his late wife's maternal clan, in his early years. If he wants to remarry, he can only marry a woman from the Wei family,\" Diting looked at the woman opposite him.","She was wearing a smoke - purple peony - patterned round - collar ruqun. Her figure was graceful, and she was the most beautiful among the crowd. Her peach - blossom - like eyes had slightly upturned tails, and there was a hint of laziness in her flowing eyes, showing a different kind of calmness from young girls.","The room was brightly lit, but she was even more eye - catching.","\"The lady is as beautiful as a national treasure. Now, the marquis is very enthusiastic about the lady. But has the lady ever thought about the future? With the agreement with the Wei family, the marquis won't marry you. As beauty fades, love will wane. This is the way of love and hatred. He's always been cold - hearted towards women. The lady should find another way out,\" Diting said as he saw the water boiling and slowly picked up the pottery pot.","\"Don't I know that I should find a way out? But the world is so vast, and the situation is turbulent now. Everywhere is full of dangers. I don't know where to go,\" Daili lowered her eyes, hiding the dim light in them. \"The marquis, although he has many flaws, once promised me something.\"","Back in Nankang County, Mo Yanyun had helped her search for Zhouzhou all over the county. Later, in the north, he had even issued a notice to search for the child in every state.","It all traced back to Nankang County.","\"Is the lady referring to the marquis's promise to find your son?\" Sure enough, Diting guessed what Daili meant.","Daili nodded accordingly.","\"The marquis can do it, and so can we,\" Diting put some dried melons into the teacup. \"The lady asked where to go. I can try to give you an answer.\"","Daili suddenly looked up, directly ignoring his latter words. \"Is it true? You can also find my son for me?\"","Her black eyes were like peach blossoms in March, extremely bright, like the floating light on the surface of a stream under the sun.","Diting lowered his eyes, avoiding her gaze. \"Of course it's true. Our believers in the Green Lotus Sect are countless and are distributed all over the world. We have people in Jiaozhou in the south and in the north. If the sect issues an order, it's not impossible to find your son.\"","\"So, the way out you're talking about is for me to join the Green Lotus Sect?\" Daili made it clear.","\"Flowers bloom towards the Buddha, praying to be reborn in the Western Pure Land,\" Diting's smile was sincere, even with a kind of fanatical piety. \"The so - called mud comes from the beginning of chaos. Lady, both you and I can be the purifiers of the mud.\"","Maybe it was the red - alert instinct deeply ingrained in her bones, and the strong repulsion towards the cult's ideas. Daili looked at the man in front of her, and a layer of goosebumps rose on her back.","But on her face, Daili showed a bit of hesitation and then changed the topic. \"Where is the ship going?\"","Diting said, \"To Tianshui County.\"","Daili frowned when she heard this.","Previously, when she was idle in the mansion, she had looked at the map. If she remembered correctly, Tianshui County was already beyond the border between Sizhou and Yanzhou and was completely within the territory of Sizhou.","Sizhou was so far away from Zhouzhou.","She didn't want to live under someone else's roof, and she did want to leave. But it definitely wasn't the kind of leaving that would separate her from her son.","\"What's the lady worried about?\" Diting suddenly asked.","Daili didn't hide it. \"Naturally, I'm afraid of getting out of the frying pan and into the fire. Although Marquis Wu'an is vulgar and sometimes unreasonable, in his mansion, I only need to serve him, and I have good food and accommodation. I'm afraid that if I go to another place, not only will the living conditions be poor, but I'll also have to serve several guests at once.\"","Probably not expecting her to be so direct, Diting was stunned for a moment and then shook his head with a smile. \"Of course not. The lady is our honored guest. We won't force you.\"","Daili's hair stood on end because she somehow sensed an underlying meaning.","An honored guest, not forced.","But if she didn't cooperate, then she wouldn't be an honored guest...","Perhaps they had prepared a lot of supplies in advance. For three consecutive days, when passing by a ferry, the ship didn't stop to replenish supplies.","Daili watched the green mountains on both sides of the river receding. There was a fire burning in her heart, making her restless. Every hour, she was getting farther away from Zhouzhou.","Just as she was thinking about how to make the ship dock, the ship actually slowed down and stopped.","Soon, Daili found out why the ship had stopped.","\"Sir, there are several floating boats on the river ahead. From afar, there are guards with swords. They look like officials. They're inspecting passing ships.\""]},{"number":70,"title":"Chapter 70","paragraphs":["When Xiuniang said this, Daili and Diting were playing chess in the main hall.","\"Checking passing ships?\" Diting raised an eyebrow.","Xiuniang nodded, \"It's most likely the Marquis of Wu'an's men.\"","They were sailing upstream. Their ship, a two-story tower boat, carried at least ten people that Daili had seen, plus considerable supplies stored earlier, so their speed was truly not fast.","Traveling along the bank on horseback could indeed reach the upstream area first.","Diting pondered for a moment, then smiled at Daili across the chessboard. \"I must ask you, madam, to return to your room for a short nap.\"","Daili's eyelids twitched.","Not just return to her room, but return to her room for a nap.","Did he intend to knock her out, or continue giving her that drowsiness-inducing medicine?","\"You're worried I want to return to the Marquis of Wu'an?\" Daili rose from her seat. Her smoky purple dress had been changed; today she wore an emerald green one from Bishan.","Green accentuated fairness, and in the brightly lit hall, her skin seemed to glow. Daili looked down at Diting from her standing position. Her beauty was already striking, and now, looking down at him, there was an aggressiveness not usually seen in her. \"There's no need for that. The Marquis of Wu'an is merely a floating log to me. If there is better timber elsewhere, why wouldn't I abandon him?\"","Diting was about to speak when she continued:","\"Of course, I know you certainly aren't at ease. This time, I can cooperate with you as a gesture of my sincerity. But don't expect it next time.\"","Daili met his eyes directly. \"With ships intercepting and checking nearby, if I truly intended to return to him, I could have just rushed out suddenly moments ago and vaulted over the railing into the river. If you tried to fish me out, the commotion would surely draw attention. If you didn't, I can swim and could have made my way to them myself.\"","Diting was momentarily taken aback, not expecting Daili to even mention jumping into the river.","However, her words weren't false.","\"Alright,\" he replied with a gentle, warm smile.","Daili turned and went back to her room.","Out of sight, Daili slowly let out a breath.","She could swim, but barely—a clumsy doggy paddle. Forget being a swift river swimmer; even staying afloat for a few minutes in a calm swimming pool required a life ring.","Jump into the river? What a joke. She valued her life; Zhouzhou was waiting for her return.","Daili followed Xiuniang to another room.","Under Daili's watchful eye, Xiuniang gripped the edge of the bed platform and, with a forceful pull, lifted the entire plank to a ninety-degree angle.","Beneath the plank revealed another space, lined with bedding. It wasn't large, just enough for one person to lie down.","The outer-facing side of the wooden panel was carved with intricate, overlapping lattice patterns at both ends. The interlocking grids blocked the line of sight but allowed air to pass through.","Xiuniang took out a small lotus-patterned vial and poured a single black pill into her hand.","\"Madam, please.\"","Daili took the pill but didn't swallow it immediately. \"How long will this one make me sleep?\"","Xiuniang: \"Half a day, six hours.\"","Daili first sat down inside the hidden compartment, then, in front of Xiuniang, swallowed the pill.","She swallowed it dry. Her throat was narrow, and it caught for a moment. A strange bitterness spread in her mouth, making Daili grimace.","The pill took effect in less than half a minute. In her growing drowsiness, Daili heard the sound of the plank being lowered back into place.","In the last fleeting moment of consciousness, Daili thought this pill worked incredibly fast, more effective than sleeping pills. If it were in modern times, it would sell out instantly.","Xiuniang carefully arranged the bedclothes. She then took a pillow and quilt from a nearby clothing chest, placed them on the bed, and slightly ruffled the quilt to create the illusion that someone had recently slept there. She also took a ruqun skirt from the chest and casually hung it on a nearby clothes rack.","After completing all this, Xiuniang closed the door and left.","Meanwhile, two tower boats had flanked Diting's vessel, pinning it in the middle.","Someone shouted from the deck: \"River bandits have been rampant recently, disguising themselves as merchant ships to harm the people. The authorities are now conducting inspections. We expect your cooperation.\"","It was a notification, not a request for a reply.","After this perfunctory statement, several rope-attached iron hooks were thrown from the opposite sides, accurately catching the wooden railings. Once loosely secured, a long wooden plank was lowered with a thud, forming a narrow bridge.","The plank was about fifteen feet long with no railings on either side, yet the men opposite, skilled and bold, stepped onto it without hesitation.","Planks were lowered from both sides simultaneously, and men crossed over in sync.","Eight men from each side, sixteen in total boarding the ship.","\"Where is the owner of this vessel?\" the centurion Lin Wu called out loudly.","Diting emerged from the main hall at that moment. \"I haven't heard about river bandits on the Jin River, but if the authorities are inspecting ships, there must be a reason. How may I cooperate, sir?\"","Lin Wu saw a man in his early twenties, seemingly just of age, dressed moderately well but whose speech seemed somewhat brash—likely a young master from some family traveling for experience.","Lin Wu: \"State your family background.\"","Diting: \"My ancestral home is in Donghai County, Xuzhou. I am the fifth son of the Donghai County Deputy Magistrate, Kong Lishen. I set out from Xuzhou half a year ago to travel, visited Qingzhou, Yanzhou, and was planning to see Sizhou, passing through...\"","\"Enough,\" Lin Wu cut off his lengthy explanation. \"How many people are on your ship?\"","Diting: \"Twenty.\"","\"Did this ship of yours dock at the Nine Precepts Ferry?\" The \"Nine Precepts Ferry\" Lin Wu mentioned was precisely the sloped ferry north of the city they had used during the day.","Diting nodded without hesitation. \"Naturally. When traveling afar, one docks at every ferry. Sir, is there something amiss with the Nine Precepts Ferry?\"","\"Bring your travel permits,\" Lin Wu said, waving his hand. His guards immediately scattered.","The tower boat had two stories and was somewhat worn. Compared to the lower deck, which was closer to the water and less airy, the upper deck offered a better view. Therefore, on such ships, the masters usually resided on the upper level while servants stayed below.","Soon, a stack of travel permits was brought over.","Lin Wu examined them one by one. The group was from Xuzhou, and the permits contained information from there, mostly from Donghai County, with a few from neighboring counties.","\"Sir, while I don't know how I've become associated with river bandits, I assure you I am a law-abiding citizen. Here is also a letter bearing the official seals of my father and his superior. Please have a look.\" Diting produced a letter.","Lin Wu took it and examined it.","Perhaps to minimize trouble for his son during travels, the letter was written earnestly and stamped with many red seals at the end.","It bore both the official and private seals of the county magistrate and the deputy magistrate. The paper wasn't new, with deep creases, suggesting it had been unfolded many times.","Lin Wu inspected it carefully, confirming it was genuine, but he didn't immediately call off the search.","Several guards went to the upper deck, inspecting each cabin room by room. The occupants had already heard the commotion and gone out. The rooms now appeared empty at a glance. Every clothing chest large enough to potentially hide a person was opened.","Room after room was checked, but nothing was found.","They then withdrew.","They shook their heads at Lin Wu.","Lin Wu tossed the letter back to Diting. \"Stand down.\"","The team withdrew as swiftly as they had arrived. In the blink of an eye, the visitors had departed the ship.","Diting watched their retreating figures, a faint smirk curling his lips.","There would be no problems whatsoever.","Because the letter was genuine, the official seal was authentic, and every detail on the identity pass was verifiable—one could indeed trace a real person matching its description.","...","On the neighboring vessel.","After standing down, one of the guards muttered, \"That ship had a few rooms that smelled rather pleasant earlier. I wonder what incense they were burning.\"","His companion chuckled. \"People have their tastes for fragrances, and those young masters are the most fastidious of all. Probably some high-grade stuff.\"","\"True enough.\"","This minor exchange remained between the two men and was soon forgotten.","White Sun City.","\"My Lord, just as you anticipated, the young master has slipped out of the manor under cover of night,\" reported Hu Bao.","It had been three days since Lady Dai's disappearance.","Centered on White Sun City, the Lord had dispatched search parties in all directions—Luchuan County to the south, Qijiang County to the east, Luoxing County to the west, and Jinshui to the north. Not a single area was overlooked.","Over these past few days, they had stopped hundreds upon thousands of carriages and intercepted and searched countless vessels. Checkpoints were strictly enforced at all city gates, meticulously inspecting every entering and exiting vehicle.","The situation even escalated to the point where Governor Nangong, upon receiving news, enthusiastically joined the search efforts.","One could say that for this manhunt, Qing Province and the Northern Territories were working in tandem. With their combined forces, logically, not just a living, breathing person, but even a small cat should have been unearthed.","Yet, there was nothing.","Lady Dai remained missing, as if she had vanished from the face of the earth the moment she disappeared from \"Gold Meets Jade.\"","The Lord's expression grew darker by the day, the oppressive atmosphere thickening. Everyone in the manor was ten thousand times more cautious, terrified of provoking his wrath at this critical juncture.","While the Lord was displeased, the young master under house confinement was anything but quiet. He schemed and struggled daily against his guards, having nearly dismantled several courtyards and almost lifted the roof tiles.","Yesterday, the Lord had ordered the surveillance to be slightly relaxed, leaving a gap for escape.","Sure enough, the young master fled that very night.","Qin Shaozong sat behind the long desk, his face like still water. \"Since the boy slipped away at night, he will surely wait for daylight to exit the city. Ensure sentries are placed at all four city gates and locations like the Nine-Caution Ford. I must know which direction he heads.\"","That boy had backing.","Initially, he thought his wife had been kidnapped by the Blue Lotus Sect. But later, he considered adding another suspect to the list.","For instance, the forces behind that boy.","Because upon learning of Lady Dai's disappearance, the boy's behavior had been highly unusual. He repeatedly insisted on leaving, determined and decisive, as if he already had a target in mind.","Since the other party refused to disclose the truth, he had no choice but to let him go and secretly follow this young wolf cub.","Dai Li was still on the boat.","On the seventh day of the voyage, the ship docked, not because they had reached their destination, but to send people ashore for supplies.","Once replenished, the ship set sail again.","Another five days passed—twelve days in total since Dai Li boarded. The ship finally docked. Dai Li had traveled from White Sun City on the border of Yan and Qing Provinces, crossed the boundary into Si Province, and arrived at a ferry crossing outside Tianshui County in Si Province.","\"My lady, let us disembark,\" Xiuniang said, handing Dai Li a wide-brimmed hat with a veil.","Stepping out of the cabin, Dai Li saw Diting. At first glance, she thought she had mistaken the person.","His style of dress had changed completely, no longer ethereal and immortal. He now wore a purple-gold \"Facing the Sun\" crown and a sapphire-blue robe with a curved hem, patterned with subtle gourd designs—the very picture of a dashing young master from a wealthy family.","Even his face was not the one Dai Li remembered.","At a quick glance, he seemed a different person altogether. But upon closer inspection of his features, one could see only minor alterations had been made. A tiny difference created a vast divergence in impression. The feeling he now projected was entirely different.","One was a mystic, the other a rich young master.","\"My lady does not recognize me?\" Diting said with a smile.","Dai Li stared fixedly at his face, inexplicably stirred by a strange thought. But before she could grasp it, the man before her spoke again:","\"My lady will grow accustomed after a few more glances. The world is descending into chaos. When traveling abroad, it's best to be prepared.\"","Dai Li snapped back to attention. \"The way you say that makes it sound like you've offended many people out there.\"","Diting made a gesture of invitation. \"In this world, some revere us as deities, honoring and loving us; naturally, others despise us as demons, wishing to eradicate us. Caution ensures a long life. Only by staying alive can we fulfill the mission entrusted to us by the Unborn Venerable Mother: to deliver the common people from their suffering.\"","Dai Li walked ahead of him down the gangplank, not letting him see the expression on her face.","\"For our travels, I must ask my lady to temporarily pose as my elder sister. Your surname is He, given name Hua. You are recently widowed, childless, and have returned to your family to rely on your younger brother,\" Diting explained.","As soon as he finished speaking, the woman in front of him suddenly turned and extended her hand toward him, palm upturned.","Diting raised an eyebrow.","\"My identity pass?\" he heard her say.","Dai Li spoke as if it were the most natural thing. \"Since we are upstanding citizens, and since you can provide specific details, there must be a pass. Let me see it.\"","Diting didn't move.","Everyone around him took their cue from him. Since he remained still, Xiuniang and the others did not move either.","Dai Li continued on her own. \"During these past two weeks on the ship, I've determined you are easier to get along with than Lord Wu'an. Until I find my son, staying anywhere is the same. You are a decent option. Once we enter the city, I'll give you a gift.\"","At the last sentence, a glint of interest flashed in Diting's eyes. \"What exactly does my lady's gift refer to?\"","Dai Li gave a faint, ambiguous smile. \"Similar to what's in the Northern Territories, yet not entirely the same. We are now in Si Province. Qin Changgeng's arm, however long, cannot reach here. I am alone, without funds, without connections, and unfamiliar with the roads. Where could I possibly go if I left you?\"","Diting glanced sideways at Xiuniang, who understood. She took a small wooden tablet from her pouch and handed it to Dai Li.","Dai Li took it and examined it.","It indeed read \"He Hua,\" with details like place of origin and an official seal. It was nearly identical to the one she had previously tricked out of Yun Rong.","A shallow smile spread in Dai Li's eyes. Although she had said she just wanted to \"see\" it, once the pass was in her hands, she openly tucked it into her own sleeve, clearly with no intention of returning it.","Diting let out a soft chuckle, unsurprised.","They disembarked at the ferry crossing. To Dai Li's surprise, a carriage was already waiting there.","They boarded and entered the city.","Tianshui County was somewhat smaller in scale than the average county. But no matter how small a place, with boundless means, one could create a gilded nest.","For instance, the residence where Dai Li was now staying.","The exterior looked quite old, not very large in area, and even showed signs of years of neglect and decay, but inside was a different world altogether. It wasn't a garish, unrestrained luxury of gold and jade carvings, but an elegance decorated with great care and thought.","Pavilions, terraces, and towers were arranged in a proper, orderly manner, with the main courtyard leading directly to a rear garden. The garden was filled with imposing strange rocks and exotic flowers and plants competing in full bloom. Water had been channeled to form a pond, upon which jade-colored koi even spouted water to create a small waterfall. To call it a masterpiece of nature's craft would not be an exaggeration.","As Daili looked around, she marveled inwardly at the capabilities of the Green Lotus Sect—luxurious pleasure boats, horse-drawn carriages, and now this residence hidden within the city.","She just didn't know where all the money came from.","It was possibly from the middle and lower classes.","Wealthy merchant believers made large donations, while the cloth-clad commoners with meager means gave what little they could, coin by coin. Each contributed according to their ability, gathering sand to form a dune, eventually creating a breathtaking sea of sand.","They had moved into the residence at noon, and not even half an hour had passed before Diting came looking for her.","The young man stood at the doorway of her room, blocking a large portion of the slanting sunlight that streamed inside, leaving a small part of his face hidden in shadow and unseen.","Compared to Qin Shaozong's heavy, battlefield-hardened aura of authority, Diting was quieter, like deep, still waters running profound.","\"Madam, I've come for the gift,\" he stated bluntly, without preamble.","Daili smiled. \"You are truly one who worries about the nation and its people. Then you will surely like this item.\"","Diting's movements paused slightly.","The way she said it, could it be...","\"The Recluse Scholar Feng truly existed. Back then, he entrusted me with taking two things out. The dragon-bone waterwheel was one. The remaining item is the curved-shaft plow. Compared to the straight-shaft plow currently in use, which requires two oxen to pull, this one is much lighter and more efficient, increasing productivity by more than double while saving the labor of one ox.\" Daili observed his expression closely.","Although the man wore a disguise, perhaps due to his relative youth, his emotions weren't completely concealed. At this moment, Daili clearly saw him freeze for a moment.","She was inwardly delighted.","Compared to the saltpeter that could bring immense wealth, the curved-shaft plow was obviously not valuable. First, like the dragon-bone waterwheel, it was the type of thing that could be copied once seen, with no real technical secrets. Second, it was a farming tool.","This destined its users and most direct beneficiaries to be the lowest-tier tenant farmers and small landholders.","If the Green Lotus Sect relied on donations from followers for its wealth, unless every single believer led an ox to plow fields, this improved version of the straight-shaft plow—which wouldn't appear historically until the Tang Dynasty—wouldn't bring immediate, tangible benefits.","Fine, even if every believer used the curved-shaft plow, it would take at least a year to see results.","After all, crops need time to grow, don't they?","Just as Daili thought he might get angry, the man before her instead smiled and said, \"This item is excellent. Thank you, Madam.\"","Daili raised an eyebrow. \"You really like it?\"","\"Naturally. The Unborn Venerable Mother is compassionate and merciful. Our Green Lotus Sect also takes delivering all living beings as its responsibility. We share the worries and the joys of the common people under heaven.\"","By the end, Diting's words carried a pointed meaning. \"Madam, it's just that this road is long and fraught with difficulties. Not only are dark clouds covering the sky above, but fierce tigers and jackals block the path. If one merely follows the old rules, great deeds will certainly be hard to accomplish. For the sake of future equality and freedom, for the soul's eventual ascension to the Pure Land, all sacrifices are worthwhile. You have contributed to saving the people; the deities will protect you.\"","The teasing smile slowly faded from Daili's face.","She suddenly realized that the Green Lotus Sect's ability to stand unshaken for a hundred years, with followers spread across the land, was no simple feat. It could even be called highly sophisticated.","This era emphasized the Mandate of Heaven, meaning the deities bestowed supreme authority upon the monarch, who was thus destined to rule.","The Green Lotus Sect worshipped the Unborn Venerable Mother, believing she was the true creator. And the Unborn Venerable Mother advocated for the equality of all and the pursuit of rebirth in the Pure Land. This essentially bypassed the \"monarch.\"","The two ideologies were inevitably in conflict. The latter challenged imperial authority and traditional ethics, but it was certainly popular among the lower classes.","Without sufficient material foundation, grand talk of universal equality is mere fantasy. Therefore, whether it's the Mandate of Heaven or the Green Lotus Sect's equality and bliss, if you peel back the layers to see the essence, both use religion to serve political ends."]},{"number":71,"title":"Chapter 71","paragraphs":["As a city behind the dangerous pass, Bairi City has many merchants who think the official road into the pass is not wide enough and will directly take the Jiujie Ford.","It often rains in summer, and now it's drizzling in the sky. But the rain can't dampen the enthusiasm of the boats in the Jiujie Ford area at all.","The boatmen are enthusiastically soliciting passengers, and the pedestrians who want to board the boats are trying to bargain to save one or two coppers.","A tall and slender figure in a straw raincoat jumped off the donkey cart neatly. After throwing the fare to the coachman, he headed straight for the boats docked by the shore without looking back.","From another donkey cart behind, someone immediately followed. Some boatmen also glanced in this direction and quietly moved their boats.","There were quite a few people at the ferry in the early morning. Qin Yanzhou scanned the area with his eyes, identified a group of boats going west according to the direction of the bows, and then randomly picked a less - crowded one to board.","\"Go to Jinlin Ford. Set off immediately.\" Qin Yanzhou didn't ask about the price and directly threw a money bag over.","The boatman took the heavy money bag and immediately beamed with joy. He didn't take other passengers anymore and courteously invited Qin Yanzhou to board the boat.","The boat set sail.","As this boat headed west, several other boats also left the shore at the same time.","*","In Tianshui County, Sizhou.","\"Have you heard? The Unborn Venerable Mother couldn't bear to see our farmers suffering, so she sent down a divine oracle and bestowed a divine object on the divine envoy.\"","\"Yes, I've heard. That thing is similar to the straight - shaft plow, but it's much easier to use than the straight - shaft plow. I heard that it only takes the strength of one ox to pull the plow, and the other ox saved can be used to plow other fields.\"","\"The sect has issued a notice, calling on believers to go to the temple to pay homage and give thanks on the first day of the lunar month.\"","\"We must give thanks. My hen just laid a clutch of eggs. I'll take the eggs there on the first day.\"","\"Eggs won't do. The sect previously issued a notice that items are not circulated in the upper realm. It only accepts silver money. You should sell the eggs for money and then donate the money to show your respect. By the way, I've saved a lot of money for my son's betrothal gift. Anyway, he won't get married until the year after next. I'll use his betrothal gift to pay homage to the Unborn Venerable Mother first.\"","\"Didn't the sect say that donations to show one's sincerity should be done according to one's ability? Are you really going to use your son's betrothal gift?\"","\"I'm his father. Why can't I use it? I'll save it back later.\"","...","Daili stood by the street, listening to the two passers - by whispering and lost in thought.","She didn't expect that the Qinglian Sect would promote the curved - shaft plow by means of \"divine oracle from heaven\". It has to be said that the Qinglian Sect, which has believers all over the country, indeed has many smart people.","The curved - shaft plow can't bring in silver money, but through such promotion, it can bring prestige and further attract the common people at the bottom.","And according to what they said, the believers are called to go to the temple to pay homage on the first day of the lunar month. Then, besides the believers, the so - called \"divine envoy\" in their mouths will probably also be present in the temple at that time.","\"Madam?\" the Xiuniang beside her said.","Daili came back to her senses and directly asked her, \"I just heard that there will be a ceremony on the first day. Will you participate at that time?\"","The Xiuniang nodded, \"I'll go to preside over it. Are you interested, Madam?\"","A flash of lightning went through Daili's mind. Immediately afterwards, a bold plan emerged like a floating log half - buried in the water, with an invisible hand pulling out the buried part.","Suddenly, the floating log shot upwards and finally emerged from the water with a \"plop\".","\"I've never seen it before. I'm really interested,\" Daili heard her heart pounding wildly. \"Can I go to the temple with you on the first day of the lunar month?\"","Xiuniang nodded. \"We'll set off the day before the first day. There will be no one in the mansion at that time. I was going to take you with us anyway.\"","Daili smiled and said she was looking forward to it.","Then the group turned into a rouge shop. There were many things sold in the shop, such as facial creams, lipsticks, flower ornaments, eyebrow pastes, as well as lead powder and rice powder that came in different prices.","Just the facial creams alone included peach blossom rouge, safflower rouge, apricot blossom rouge, hibiscus rouge and so on.","There were so many things that they had to be placed on several shelves.","Daili quickly glanced at the eyebrow paste on the edge of the shelf, then picked up the small basket provided by the shop and started a shopping spree.","She wanted this facial cream and that lipstick. Just like a crazy shopper, she took one of each kind.","It was the first time for Xiuniang to see someone buy things like this. But thinking about the valuable shoes and clothes Daili wore before, she guessed that Daili might have been unrestrained when she was with the Marquis of Wuan.","Before they left, the master only told her to watch over Daili and didn't say anything else. Now that the lady just bought a lot of things, it didn't seem unacceptable.","So Xiuniang kept silent.","Daili had been paying attention to Xiuniang out of the corner of her eye. Seeing that she didn't say anything, Daili reached out to a certain shelf and took the items from left to right.","When she put the small jar on the far side into the small basket, Daili's heart was pounding like a drum. For a moment, she even had an illusion of hearing a thumping sound hitting her eardrums.","All the other things were just for show. Only this box of eyebrow paste was the most important.","After leaving the rouge shop, Daili went to other places. It was almost sunset when she and Xiuniang and the others headed back to the mansion.","They returned fully loaded.","When Daili came back, she saw a carriage driving out of the mansion. It was a horse - drawn carriage. The man driving it wore a cap and was strong and powerful. He also carried a knife.","This kind of attire didn't seem to belong to the servants of an ordinary wealthy family. Instead, it looked like that of an official.","\"Madam?\" Xiuniang called out in a low voice.","Daili lowered the curtain and said bluntly, \"That carriage just now looks like it belongs to the government office. You should get on good terms with those people. Otherwise, if you fall from power one day, Qin Changgeng will definitely take revenge on me. After all, there was the dragon - bone waterwheel before, and then my disappearance. Now that the curved - beam plow has appeared, he might suspect that I'm involved.\"","These words were just for the occasion, but when she mentioned Qin Shaozong, Daili's thoughts wandered a little.","If she could escape successfully this time, she would go back to Yanzhou, but she wouldn't go directly back to the Qin Mansion. She and Qin Shaozong were from different eras, and they were bound to have many conflicting ideas.","Just their views on marriage and love were as different as ice and fire, and they were destined not to get along. Moreover, there were so many old scores that couldn't be settled, so it was better not to bother.","Hearing this, Xiuniang smiled and said, \"Madam, you can rest assured. Sizhou is very safe.\"","Daili pretended not to care much on the surface, but her mind was working non - stop.","Sizhou is very safe?","Why is it so safe? Could it be that the governor of Sizhou is on their side?","Daili had no answer.","She had dinner outside. After returning to the mansion, Daili dismissed the maids on the pretext of being tired and wanting to go to bed.","Outside the window, the sky had already darkened. Inside the room, there was only a tiny bean-sized lamp. The light was not bright, but it didn't prevent Daili from rummaging through her spoils of the day right after closing the door.","The facial creams in this era were quite small, about half the size of an egg. The boxes were exquisitely made, and one could easily hold three or four of them in one hand.","Daili rummaged through them and found that box of black paste. She carefully dug out a piece from it and kneaded it into a granular shape, which was the same size as the black pills she had eaten before.","There was once a trend of black lips among women. So, in fact, the black paste was lip balm. Naturally, there was oil in the lip balm to ensure that the lips wouldn't dry when applied.","Now, holding the small black pill she had kneaded by hand, Daili chose a suitable distance from the fire and started to roast this small black pill.","While roasting, she would occasionally blow on it artificially.","After about a quarter of an hour, Daili stopped.","After a series of \"wind and sun exposure\", the hardness of the previously slightly soft small black pill had significantly increased. And its surface had also solidified, no longer leaving black marks on one's hand when touched like before.","Daili did the same thing again and kneaded two more black pills, making a total of three. It wasn't that she didn't want to knead more, but there was only so much of the black paste left, and she had other uses for the rest.","Looking at her dirty fingers, Daili dipped the tips of her fingers into the teacup to clean them. After they were thoroughly cleaned, the water in the cup became pitch - black and turbid.","Picking up the cup, Daili walked to the potted plant placed in the corner of the room and poured the black - colored water on the side against the wall.","The mud was gray - yellow, and it wasn't obvious after pouring the black water on it.","She took the cup back and looked at it under the bean - sized lamp. Seeing that the inside of the cup was stained black, Daili then picked up the teapot to add water and thoroughly washed it clean.","There was no one else in the room except Daili.","She did this series of actions very slowly. In sharp contrast, her heart had been pounding since the moment she kneaded the small black pill.","She had to succeed in one go!","If she failed, not to mention getting a second chance, her situation later would definitely be worse than it was now.","Lying on the couch, Daili calculated the days. There were still seven days until the first day of the lunar month. She only had seven days left to carry out this scheme of \"switching the prince with a commoner\".","...","The next day.","When she woke up from sleep, the sun was shining brightly outside the window. The flowers and leaves in the courtyard were dotted with water droplets, and there were also wet marks on the stone bricks on the ground. It had rained a light shower before dawn.","Maybe because Daili had gone on a big shopping spree outside the mansion yesterday, Xiuniang, the embroidery woman, had caught a glimpse of the daily life of the \"favorite concubine of the marquis\". After breakfast, she took the initiative to ask.","\"Madam, do you still want to go out and stroll in the market today?\" Xiuniang asked.","Daili thought for a moment and said, \"Since you're called Xiuniang, are you particularly good at needlework?\"","Xiuniang modestly replied, \"I can't say I'm really good. I can just barely make it look decent.\"","\"Can you teach me? I want to learn.\" Daili seemed to have suddenly become interested.","Xiuniang naturally agreed. However, when the maidservant fetched the needles and thread, she casually asked, \"I've heard that many families arrange for their daughters to learn needlework. Why didn't you learn it before, madam?\"","This was true.","Whether they were the daughters of wealthy families or those of common people, girls had to learn needlework from a young age. They embroidered wedding dresses as well as other clothes. For poorer families, they had to use the embroidered items to exchange for money.","Daili: \"I used to be lazy. I thought that if a matter could be solved with silver, why should I do it myself? My family always let me have my way.\"","If someone else had said these words, Xiuniang would surely have thought that this person was spoiled and ignorant.","But the face in front of her was so striking, as gorgeous as spring flowers and as bright as the moon. Coupled with her nonchalant tone, things somehow seemed perfectly natural.","Xiuniang murmured, \"...Indeed.\"","While teaching Daili, she asked again, \"Madam looks like someone nurtured in a water town. Is your ancestral home in Yangzhou?\"","\"Of course not. My ancestral home is in Cangwu, Jiaozhou.\" Daili repeated the same story and then said, \"Do I need to thread it through here? I don't think it's right. Let me have a look at it.\"","For the next four days in a row, Daili asked Xiuniang to teach her needlework. On the surface, she seemed calm, but in fact, she became more and more anxious day by day.","Four days had passed. There were only three days left, and time was running out. Unfortunately, she still hadn't found an opportunity.","This courtyard was inhabited by her, Xiuniang, and two other maids. Nominally, the three of them served her, but in fact, they were there to keep an eye on her.","However, perhaps because she had behaved very obediently these days, one of the maids would occasionally leave. No one knew what she was busy with, but in any case, she wouldn't stay by her side all the time.","Daili had been waiting for an opportunity but couldn't get one. Seeing that time was running out, she was extremely worried. Just when she was hesitating whether to change her method -","A turning point appeared.","The turning point came on the fifth day.","That morning, after Daili got up, she found that one of the two maids was missing again. At that time, she didn't care and thought that the maid had just gone to do some errands as usual and would come back soon.","But later, Daili never saw her.","After breakfast, she continued to learn needlework from Xiuniang. Around the beginning of noon, a person rushed in and whispered to Xiuniang, \"Xiuniang, the carriage of the Third Young Master has arrived.\"","The governor of Sizhou had recently passed away due to an illness. He had left in a hurry and hadn't had time to arrange many things, leaving his three sons to fight for power. The \"Third Young Master\" mentioned by the person was Xie Yuanxiu, the third son of the governor of Sizhou.","The room was very quiet. Since Daili and Xiuniang were sitting close to each other, Daili also heard this not - so - quiet whisper.","Xiuniang paused and put down the needle and thread in her hand. \"Madam, there is an honored guest coming today. I'll go out for a moment and come back soon. If you have anything to do, you can call Caoxiang to serve you.\"","Daili felt as if a ray of light had broken through the chaotic sky, which made her heart surge with excitement. She tried to speak in a calm tone. \"All right. You go and attend to your business first. Don't worry about me. I seem to have grasped some tricks these days. I'll try by myself first.\"","Xiuniang smiled and agreed. Then she called Caoxiang over and gave her a few instructions, mainly telling her to serve well.","After Xiuniang left, only Daili and Caoxiang were left in the room.","Daili deliberately waited for a while before turning to look at Caoxiang. \"I'm a bit bothered by the summer heat. Go to the kitchen and cook a pot of mung bean and lily soup for me.\"","After saying this, Daili turned back and continued to hold the needle and thread.","Caoxiang hesitated for a moment but finally agreed.","Daili pricked up her ears to listen to the footsteps. When she couldn't hear them anymore, she immediately put down the needle and thread and went to the window to look out.","Caoxiang had gone out, and the courtyard was empty at this moment.","Daili quickly took out the small brocade bag from the box, stuffed it into her pocket, and was about to go out. But as soon as her front foot stepped over the threshold, she stopped.","Oh, almost forgot something.","Daili quickly went back, took out a cloth rabbit from under the pillow. After taking this little thing with her, she went out again.","This courtyard was in a \"pin\" - shaped structure. Daili lived in the largest room at the innermost part. On the left side were the rooms of Xiuniang, and on the right side, Caoxiang and another maid lived together.","Daili came to the left and quickly pushed the door.","As expected, the door was not locked.","After Daili went in, she closed the door behind her and immediately began to look for Xiuniang's small porcelain bottle.","On the boat back then, Xiuniang took out the small porcelain bottle from her pocket and carried it with her at that time. But Daili didn't think that after she had \"submitted\" to the Green Lotus Sect and told Diting about the curved - beam plow, Xiuniang would still carry the medicine with her all the time.","After all, although the porcelain bottle was small, it was quite heavy.","Xiuniang's room was not very big and was divided into an outer and an inner part. As Daili walked straight into the inner part, her eyes quickly scanned the surroundings.","The decoration of the outer room was very ordinary. There were calligraphy and paintings hanging on the wall, a incense burner and a vase in the corner. There was a low chair beside the long table, and there were cups, teapots and cups on the table. In addition, there were several storage boxes.","It was nothing special, quite similar to Daili's place.","Pushing aside the beaded curtain, Daili entered the inner room. There was a couch and several stacked cabinets in the inner room.","Putting herself in Xiuniang's shoes, Daili first lifted the pillow. Unfortunately, there was nothing under the pillow. After putting the brocade pillow back in place disappointedly, she turned her target to the bedside cabinet.","\"Creak——\"","The cabinet door opened, and Daili's pupils suddenly tightened.","She found it!","But not exactly. Because the cabinet was densely filled with medicine bottles.","They were arranged very neatly. Each bottle outside was different. Different colors, different patterns. It could be said that except for the shape of the bottle and the stopper on the top, everything else was different.","It was easy to know that each type represented a different kind of medicine.","Daili was a bit stunned.","So many?","She carefully recalled the pattern on the small porcelain bottle at that time. It seemed that there was a lotus flower on it. Wait, was it a lotus or a mountain magnolia?","It seemed to be a lotus.","Daili fixed her eyes on a small bottle with a lotus pattern, quickly took it out, pulled out the wooden stopper, and poured out the contents.","The black pills rolled out with a gurgling sound. Daili picked up one and brought it close to her nose to smell it carefully.","Yes, this was the smell!","Daili quickly took out three pills, then stuffed three self - made black pills into it and shook it specially to mix them well. She neatly put the porcelain bottle back in place, even adjusting the angle to be exactly the same as before.","Daili closed the cabinet door and stood up.","The task was accomplished. It was time to retreat.","However, just as her happy mood was just beginning to sprout like a little spring bud, Daili suddenly heard footsteps.","She was in the inner room. For her to hear the footsteps, it meant that the person was already very close.","As if to confirm Daili's guess, she heard the sound of the door opening with a \"creak\".","At that moment, a thunderbolt exploded in Daili's mind.","Someone had come in."]},{"number":72,"title":"Chapter 72","paragraphs":["The room Xiuniang lived in did have windows, but they were not particularly large. Furthermore, if she tried to climb out the window at this critical juncture, the person outside would likely hear the noise and enter before she even made it halfway out.","If that happened, it would be absolutely impossible to explain herself.","Xiuniang had said earlier that she was stepping out for a moment and would be right back. Surprisingly, she had not been lying.","She really was quick...","Dai Li's blood raced, her heart leaping into her throat. This uncontrollable physiological reaction made her subconsciously raise a hand to touch her face.","Fortunately, it was not too hot.","Dai Li hurriedly took two deep breaths. At the same time, she dug a small object out of her pocket and conspicuously placed it right beside Xiuniang's brocade pillow.","Only after doing all of this did she turn to walk out, straightening her back and trying hard to feign a calm and composed demeanor.","Outside, whether the person had noticed she was not in her own room or had sensed something amiss with the door, whoever was pushing it open quickened their pace to enter.","Two breaths later, Dai Li and Xiuniang saw each other through a layer of bead curtains. The master of the room stood on the outside, while the guest was in the inner chamber.","The atmosphere suddenly froze.","Dai Li clearly saw Xiuniang's expression change. Taking the initiative, she said, \"Oh, I did not expect you to come back so soon. It seems the surprise I prepared for you is ruined.\"","With that, Dai Li turned back around. Under Xiuniang's watchful eyes, she picked up the plush rabbit she had just placed by the brocade pillow.","\"This is the result of my learning these past few days. Here, it is for you,\" Dai Li said, stuffing the plush rabbit into Xiuniang's hands. \"My embroidery skills are not even a tenth of yours, but you are not allowed to dislike it.\"","Dai Li let her hands drop, her wide sleeves hiding her stiff, ice-cold fingertips. Then, acting as if nothing had happened, she brushed past Xiuniang and walked out.","Xiuniang turned sideways, watching Dai Li's retreating back. Only after the other woman had completely left the room did she look down at the plush rabbit in her hands.","The rabbit was smaller than a woman's palm. Two pieces of red jade were sewn on for eyes, its ears were uneven in length, and its mouth was so small it was almost invisible.","Every part of it looked awkward, but when put together, it had an inexplicably festive charm.","Xiuniang squeezed the rabbit, then turned her gaze toward the bed and the low cabinet in the inner room. Crossing the distance in a few quick strides, she swiftly opened the low cabinet next to the bed.","The small porcelain bottles inside the cabinet were neatly arranged, each with its patterned side facing outward, exactly in the identical posture she had left them.","She had only ever shown Madam Dai one kind of medicine. Xiuniang reached out and took the lotus-patterned bottle, popped out the wooden cork, found a small clay saucer, and poured out all the medicine.","The bottle was not large; it could only hold ten pills. She had previously used two from this particular bottle.","She counted them. There were exactly eight pills. Not a single one was missing.","Xiuniang poured the small black pills back in, then took down another medicine bottle and opened it.","One by one, Xiuniang carefully poured out and checked all the bottles of this type. However, the number of pills in every single one was correct; not a single pill was missing.","Xiuniang subconsciously turned her head to look at the plush rabbit again, the doubt in her eyes deepening.","Could it be that Madam Dai really just came to give her a gift?","But lost in her thoughts, Xiuniang completely forgot about another important matter.","...","Meanwhile.","Back in her own room, Dai Li held a teacup and drank. The cool water slid down her throat, slowly soothing the restless anxiety throbbing within her.","Thank goodness she had prepared an extra plush rabbit, otherwise her cover would definitely have been blown.","Just as she finished having this thought, her right eyelid suddenly began to twitch violently.","There was a folk saying: \"A twitching left eye brings wealth, a twitching right eye brings disaster.\" Dai Li never used to believe in such things, but she could not help feeling guilty right now. Her eyelid started twitching right after she had done something bad, and it was her right eye at that.","\"She could not have found out, right...\" Dai Li felt completely unsure.","She thought the eyelid would only twitch for a moment, but it ended up twitching intermittently for the entire day. It did not even stop by the next morning, leaving Dai Li both irritable and depressed.","Tomorrow was the first day of the lunar month. She had heard Xiuniang mention that the auspicious time for tomorrow's ceremony was set for exactly noon, which meant twelve o'clock.","Tomorrow at dawn, there would surely be many believers leaving the city to climb the mountain and enter the temple. Diting and his group would set off a day early, which meant they would be leaving the city this afternoon during the hour of Wei.","There were still four hours left before they left the city.","According to the information she had gathered so far, believers of the Green Lotus Sect from around Tianshui Prefecture would all rush to Ganquan Temple tomorrow. By then, there would definitely be many carriages at the foot of the mountain.","Wherever there was a way to make a living, there were merchants.","She guessed that there would surely be passenger carriages along the mountain roads or at the foot of the mountain. Since Ganquan Temple was located outside the city, she would not have to go through the city gates again. As long as she successfully made it down the mountain and got into a carriage, she could reach the ferry crossing in just half an hour.","Once she boarded a boat, she could sail east with the current, cross the border between Si and Yan provinces, and disembark at a county on the western side of Yan Province.","By then, it would be inconvenient for anyone to find her.","After going over her plan again, Dai Li's right eyelid was still twitching, making her feel terribly restless. Finally, unable to sit still any longer, she decided to take a stroll in the back garden with the little time she had left before leaving the estate.","As a result of this stroll, her right eyelid stopped twitching, because she seemed to have run smack into the very source of the disaster.","In the back garden, bizarre rocks stood tall and imposing, and jade brocade carp spat gurgling water that sounded like endless fairy music. The surrounding flowers were in full bloom, a riot of vibrant colors. It was truly a beautiful scene.","A gentle breeze brushed past, bringing with it a rich floral fragrance and a hint of alcohol. At first, Dai Li did not know where the smell of alcohol was coming from, until she turned out of the rockery corridor and saw two figures in the waterside pavilion by the pond.","Amidst the half-draped sheer gauze curtains, the two men in the pavilion sat facing each other across a table.","One wore a sapphire-blue cross-collared robe with gold-trimmed edges, exhibiting the demeanor of a wealthy young master that Dai Li was familiar with. The other wore a white jade crown with a continuous bead pattern and a dark cyan brocade robe. He appeared to be around thirty years of age, with long eyes, an aquiline nose, and a gaze as piercing as a torch.","Xie Yuanxiu had been drinking with Diting when he caught a glimpse of a beautiful silhouette stepping out from the corner of his eye.","At that moment, all the exotic flora in the garden seemed to dim, leaving only that graceful, curvaceous figure glowing brightly. Sunlight danced on her emerald-blue dress, and as she walked, a layer of fragmented light, like the iridescence of a seashell, rippled out around her feet.","Seeming to notice his gaze, she looked over.","Thus, the ethereal soul of snow and flowers materialized into substance, and the elegant flower demon took on a true form. This beautiful woman with her fair skin and thick, dark hair commanded absolute allure without uttering a single word.","Clang—","The jade cup slipped from his hand and fell.","The wine spilled across the table, and a few splashed drops dampened Xie Yuanxiu's cuffs.","But right now, he could not care less about wiping it off. He did not even try to hide his loss of composure. With his eyes still fixed on Dai Li, he asked Diting, \"Who is that beautiful lady?\"","Seeing the man across from him staring without blinking, even dropping his cup, Diting knew things had gone terribly wrong.","This Third Young Master Xie had come yesterday to discuss matters and happened to stay overnight at the estate. Because of this, he had specifically instructed Xiuniang to pass a message to Madam Dai, telling her not to leave her courtyard.","If nothing unexpected had happened, Xie the Third would have left after finishing this pot of wine. After all, everything they needed to discuss was settled, and they had another itinerary for the afternoon.","But as luck would have it, an accident happened right at this moment.","\"This woman is not suitable for you, Third Young Master,\" Diting simply replied.","\"Which family is this lady from?\" Xie Yuanxiu pressed.","Diting also turned his head. He saw that Dai Li seemed to realize her presence was inappropriate. After giving them a slight curtsy, she turned and left.","Though she had left, someone was still staring blankly after her.","Diting was about to speak, but he saw Xie Yuanxiu, separated only by a table, abruptly stand up and follow closely after her.","Diting thought to himself that this Third Young Master Xie's strengths and weaknesses were far too obvious. This man was the third son of the provincial governor. If they did not support him, the third son of the Xie family would certainly have no chance at the position of Sizhou's governor.","He was obedient, knew his boundaries, and clearly understood what he relied on to rise to power. Moreover, he was quite religious, making him half a believer of theirs.","In stark contrast, however, this man was quite licentious when it came to women. Whenever he set his sights on a lady, regardless of whether she was from a respectable family or not, he had to have her.","Previously, this flaw hadn't seemed like a concern to him. After all, a person without weaknesses and shortcomings was difficult to control. But who would have thought that now...","Xie Yuanxiu felt as if a wisp of his soul had been snatched away. His chest hummed, and the only thing echoing in his ears was his own heartbeat drumming wildly. He could no longer hear any other sounds.","The last emperor of the previous Great Liang dynasty had exclusively favored the bewitching consort Jiang Ji. For her, he imposed heavy taxes, launched massive construction projects, and even executed Crown Prince Dan, whom he had personally cultivated, all because he was dead set on putting Jiang Ji's youngest son on the throne.","Later generations scoffed at his foolishness, and Xie Yuanxiu used to be one of them. She was merely a woman, as insignificant as grass and duckweed. How could she be worth destroying one's own foundation and ruining an empire meant to last ten thousand generations?","Women were just for playing around with.","But now, the continuous waves of novelty and excitement thrilled him so much that even his soul seemed to tremble, causing Xie Yuanxiu to completely throw his past grand words to the back of his mind.","He hurried after her, walking faster and faster, until his robes even whipped up a gust of wind.","Dai Li was very familiar with that burning gaze, one that looked as if it wanted to devour her whole. When they first met, Qin Shaozong had looked at her exactly like that. Later, he restrained himself considerably, only letting his gaze run wild when they were in bed.","Dai Li was returning the way she came, but just as she walked out of the moongate of the back garden, a figure bypassed her from behind and blocked her path.","The newcomer was about six feet tall, standing a couple of inches taller than Dai Li, with a rather lean physique.","To Dai Li, who used to face Qin Shaozong on a regular basis, the sense of oppression brought by this man was negligible.","\"May I know your fair name, my lady?\" Xie Yuanxiu stared at her unblinkingly.","Dai Li turned her head to look at Diting. With a calm expression, she opened her mouth and said, \"Brother, is this your guest? I am feeling unwell, so please entertain your guest well.\"","It was entirely the tone of a host.","Both Diting and Xie Yuanxiu were taken aback.","Diting nodded helplessly. \"Alright, Sister. If you are feeling unwell, go back to your room and rest. If you don't feel better by this afternoon, I will have Xinglin come and examine you.\"","Dai Li nodded casually, tossing the mess to him, and turned to return to her room.","Xie Yuanxiu wanted to chase after her, but Diting reached out from behind and pressed a hand onto his shoulder.","\"Third Young Master.\" Diting looked like a scholar, but the force of his hand was not light. \"Those who achieve great things know when to stop and do not harbor greed.\"","Xie Yuanxiu understood the warning in his words. The veins on his forehead bulged. \"Sir, if I could have your sister, I would surely cherish and value her. I would seek out all the treasures in the world just to make her smile.\"","Diting withdrew his hand and crossed his arms. \"Not to mention that my sister is already married, but if I remember correctly, you are already married as well, Third Young Master. Your esteemed wife's maternal family is a prominent clan in Xuzhou, and my sister will not be a concubine. This matter is inappropriate. Please do not bring it up again, Third Young Master.\"","Xie Yuanxiu's expression turned ugly.","To Dai Li, her chance encounter with Xie Yuanxiu was nothing more than a minor interlude; the man was just a stranger to her. Once she left Tianshui Commandery the next day, she would never see this man whose name she didn't even know again in this lifetime.","In the blink of an eye, the afternoon arrived. Xiuniang helped Dai Li pack a small travel bag, and they rode out of the city with the convoy.","The carriage wheels rolled over the bluestone bricks and entered the yellow dirt road, leaving the hustle and bustle behind.","Ganquan Temple was located on the northwest side of Tianshui Commandery. Half an hour after leaving the city, Dai Li looked through the carriage window and saw the majestic temple emerging from the green mountains.","Besides their convoy, there were other carriages on the official road.","They were all horse-drawn carriages; there wasn't a single donkey cart in sight.","Upon reaching the foot of the mountain, the mountain road wound upwards. The path had been widened, allowing two carriages to travel side by side. After passing through the snake-like winding mountain road, the path gradually leveled out.","The view suddenly opened up. A massive clearing had been carved out here, and at this moment, quite a few carriages were already parked neatly and orderly upon it.","Seeing this, Dai Li asked Xiuniang, who was in the same carriage, \"Isn't the celebration tomorrow? Why have they come today as well?\"","Xiuniang replied, \"The auspicious hour is right at noon. There are only six hours from daybreak to noon. Wealthy families place great importance on etiquette and have many things to prepare. It is better to arrive at the temple a day in advance. Anyway, there are guest rooms available here for them to stay in.\"","Dai Li didn't voice the question, \"Does it cost money?\" She figured it obviously did, and the price was probably quite steep.","Thinking that Dai Li disliked sharing a courtyard with strangers, Xiuniang said, \"Rest assured, Madam, your quarters are in another location.\"","Taking the opportunity, Dai Li brought up, \"There shouldn't be any forbidden areas in this temple, right? I would like to go for a walk later.\"","Xiuniang replied, \"Any place where pilgrims are not allowed to enter will be guarded.\"","Dai Li nodded.","Their carriage did not park in the clearing next to the temple. Instead, it took a small side path and entered through a side gate. Dai Li consciously memorized the route and noticed that the carriage stopped at a small courtyard on the westernmost side of the temple.","This courtyard was not considered large, just a single-entry courtyard with no back door. Perhaps to create as much of an imposing atmosphere for the temple as possible, the surrounding walls here were exceedingly high, about ten feet tall, and the top was paved with overlapping slanted tiles.","There was a tree in the courtyard. Dai Li visually estimated the distance, and her gaze darkened.","It wouldn't work. Even if she climbed up, she wouldn't be able to reach the edge of the wall.","There were no exits in three directions. If she wanted to get out, her only option was the main gate of the courtyard.","Wait, there were also windows in the room!","Dai Li walked into the small room. \"Has it been a long time since anyone lived in this room? Why is there a smell? Caoxiang, did you bring my fish-and-bird incense burner? Hurry up and light some incense to cover up the smell.\"","Having said that, she raised her hand and pushed open the begonia-patterned window.","As soon as the window opened, the cool breeze from outside rushed in, fresh and refreshing.","Dai Li narrowed her eyes to feel the wind, her gaze looking out the window. Outside were green mountains and verdant forests, and further away were clouds as soft as cotton.","She quietly took a deep breath, as if she could smell the scent of freedom. Dai Li turned her head and asked Xiuniang, \"Xiuniang, how many days will the ceremony last?\"","Xiuniang smiled. \"It won't be a matter of days. It will be less than four hours. After all, the commoners still have to make a living.\"","Dai Li lowered her eyes.","Less than two double-hours, less than four regular hours. She had to leave and descend the mountain before the celebration ended.","No, more accurately, she needed to reach the ferry crossing and board a boat before the celebration ended..."]},{"number":73,"title":"Chapter 73","paragraphs":["Leaving the luggage to the two maids to unpack, Dai Li proposed taking a walk around, with Xiuniang accompanying her.","Without pausing for a breath, Dai Li wandered through numerous areas, exploring the entire ground level of Ganquan Temple.","The traditional Chinese concept of symmetry was brought to its fullest expression in Ganquan Temple. At the very center was the Eight Immortals Shrine; flanking it on both sides were halls and pavilions of varying sizes, along with an equal number of pagodas.","A vast open space stretched out in front of the Eight Immortals Shrine. The front courtyard was exceptionally expansive, with a massive bronze tripod cauldron sitting squarely in the middle for the presiding monks to burn incense.","Standing before the cauldron and looking up, Dai Li saw the towering temple buildings on either side, noticing that the upper levels had windows. If a large crowd of believers were to gather here tomorrow, one could observe the entire scene from up there.","Dai Li withdrew her gaze and continued her stroll elsewhere.","Her small courtyard was on the west side, while the east side housed the guest rooms for pilgrims. The temple couldn't compare to the high-end inns in the city; the guest rooms were packed closely together, and the space inside was quite small.","However, looking at the pilgrims who had checked in early, they all wore bright smiles, clearly thoroughly satisfied.","\"Xiuniang, will you also be attending the ceremony tomorrow?\" Dai Li asked.","\"Generally speaking, all believers are required to attend.\" Xiuniang didn't immediately state whether she was going or not; instead, she asked Dai Li, \"Would you like to attend, Madam?\"","Dai Li hesitated before saying, \"I'm a bit interested, but my novelty wears off quickly. Even if I attend, I won't stay for long. Would it be inappropriate to leave halfway through?\"","Xiuniang thought to herself that it would indeed be inappropriate.","If someone suddenly left when the atmosphere was at its peak, it could easily ruin the believers' mood and provoke their dissatisfaction.","\"It's still early, let's wait and see.\" Dai Li pointed upstairs. \"May I go up?\"","Xiuniang replied, \"Please, Madam.\"","Dai Li went all the way up to the highest floor of the Eight Immortals Shrine in one breath. Looking out from the window here, she could see parts of the temple, the lush green mountains, and the road they had taken to get here.","Fortunately, the dense foliage in the mountains provided plenty of cover, making the path they came from only faintly visible.","Dai Li withdrew her gaze, a plan forming in her mind. When the time came, she would stick to the edges and walk under the trees where they couldn't see her. \"I'm a little hungry. Let's go back.\"","They had left the city in the afternoon. After the carriage ride and the temple tour, by the time Dai Li returned to the western courtyard, dusk had fallen. Brilliant evening clouds spread across the sky like an oil painting.","The practitioners of the Green Lotus Sect did not shave their heads, nor were they required to be vegetarians. Tonight's dinner consisted of millet rice and roasted mutton.","Dai Li didn't like mutton, but she knew she wouldn't have any strength without eating meat. To prepare for the tough battle tomorrow, she ate the small plate of mutton clean.","\"By the way, with so many strangers in the temple and this western courtyard being quite secluded, will there be anyone keeping watch at night?\" Dai Li asked.","Xiuniang nodded. \"Of course. There are two guards stationed at the entrance connecting the western courtyard to the outside all day long. You can rest assured, Madam.\"","The small house Dai Li was currently staying in, together with the adjacent courtyards, formed a layout resembling the Chinese character Pin, shaped like a triangle of three squares. The entrance Xiuniang mentioned was the intersecting path between the top courtyard and the two bottom ones.","\"Very well, then I can be at ease,\" Dai Li nodded.","Dai Li went to bed exceptionally early that night, but perhaps due to nerves, she felt completely sleepless after lying on the bed.","She only had three small pills. If Xiuniang and the other two maids were watching her together, even with the medicine in hand, it would be difficult to use.","Dai Li hugged her quilt and rolled over on the bed.","\"Generally speaking, all believers are required to attend.\" Xiuniang was also a believer. She had to find a way to distract her tomorrow.","After tossing and turning for half the night, Dai Li finally fell asleep.","With things on her mind, she woke up exceptionally early the next day, but someone was even earlier. Dai Li didn't see Xiuniang when she woke up; upon asking, she learned that the other woman had gone to help with the preparations.","Dai Li sought out Caoxiang and the others to chat. \"How many times have you attended the ceremony?\"","One said she had attended once, while the other said she had never attended, adding that the ceremony was unusual and would only be held when something major happened.","Dai Li figured that the two girls had probably only joined the sect a few years ago and were still at the most basic outer level, not yet reaching the rank of handling actual affairs.","\"I've never seen believers making a pilgrimage before. Come out with me to have a look.\" Dai Li's eyes darted around thoughtfully.","The two maids naturally obeyed.","Dai Li deliberately led them out through the courtyard entrance, and sure enough, saw two men standing guard.","They were clad in armor and armed with swords, looking quite imposing.","When Dai Li went out, she was questioned briefly by them. Upon learning that she wanted to see the main gate of Ganquan Temple from the outside, the guards didn't stop her and let her pass.","As she gradually walked further away, Dai Li heard someone whispering behind her:","\"Speaking of which, the divine medicine that is distributed once every half a year should be handed out soon, right? I've been waiting for so long.\"","\"Soon, soon. It'll be distributed next month. I'm really looking forward to it. Every time I take it, I feel exceptionally cheerful and my physical strength doubles.\"","\"I really envy those who have been promoted to Divine Envoys. They can get even more of the divine medicine...\"","As Dai Li walked further away, the discussion behind her became inaudible.","After walking for a while, Dai Li saw the main gate of Ganquan Temple.","The mountain gate stood high. Many commoners in plain clothes passed through on their knees. The stream of people entering the temple was endless; they wore different clothes and came in all shapes and sizes. The only thing they shared in common was the devotion on their faces.","After strolling around outside, Dai Li headed back about an hour before the ceremony was set to begin.","When she returned, Xiuniang was already in the room.","\"Madam, where did you go?\" Xiuniang asked.","\"Just took a casual stroll,\" Dai Li fanned herself with her hand, pretending to be unbearably hot. \"Summer heat is a yang evil, scorching by nature—it truly doesn't deceive. Caoxiang, take some codonopsis, poria, schisandra berries, and ophiopogon tuber, add a few pieces of meat, and boil them for an hour. Stew a small pot of Shen Ling Sheng Mai Soup for me. A pot the size of the one we used for dinner yesterday will do.\"","Seeing Dai Li sit down, looking so exhausted that she didn't want to move another inch, Xiuniang stayed silent for a moment before finally asking, \"Madam, are you still attending the ceremony?\"","Dai Li waved her hand. \"No, I'm exhausted. If I go, it'll take another four hours. I won't be able to endure it; I'd rather rest in the room. You go ahead by yourself and don't worry about me. I'll just stay in the room with the two of them.\"","Xiuniang hesitated, a conflicted expression on her face. \"I'll stay in the room and keep you company.\"","Dai Li quickly replied, \"No need. When I was walking around outside just now, I heard that this ceremony is quite important. Attending more of these grand events will be beneficial for raising your status in the sect. Besides, I don't need you to keep me company. I'm just going to take a nap in the room. If you stay here, I'll only find you too noisy and it'll keep me from sleeping.\"","\"This...\" Xiuniang was clearly tempted.","As a devout follower, she genuinely wanted to attend the ceremony.","Dai Li continued, \"What do you have to worry about? Caoxiang and the others are in the courtyard, and there are guards outside. If I need anything, I can just call out; there are plenty of people around, so we won't be short of you. It's good for you to go take a look. When you come back, you can briefly tell me about the ceremony, and it'll be just as if I had experienced it myself.\"","Xiuniang was persuaded by her words. \"I will go and observe the ceremony. Caoxiang and Mei Xiang will stay behind to serve you. If you need anything, Madam, feel free to call them.\"","Dai Li nodded. \"Of course.\"","The Ginseng and Poria Pulse-Generating Soup took an hour to stew. Dai Li had timed her return perfectly, meaning that right when this pot of soup was done, the ceremony over there would begin.","Xiuniang had left more than fifteen minutes before the ceremony started.","Caoxiang returned carrying the steaming pot. The soup pot was about the size of a grown man's splayed hand, and about ten centimeters deep. It held more than enough to stuff two people, let alone one.","Dai Li heard the tolling of a bell.","Dong, dong, dong. The intervals between each toll were identical. The bell chimes of the ancient temple were distant and lingering.","With these tolls, Dai Li felt as if an invisible string was winding around her heart, loop by loop. With every passing second, her heart was hoisted a little higher.","The ceremony had begun, and so had her countdown.","Four hours. Every second used was a second lost, and there was no telling if any other accidents would occur along the way.","\"Madam, the heat-relief soup is ready,\" Caoxiang said.","The Ginseng and Poria Pulse-Generating Soup was fresh off the stove and still piping hot. Dai Li looked at it with distaste and said, \"This is too hot, how am I supposed to drink it? Go fetch a basin of cold water.\"","Mei Xiang did as she was told.","The water was quickly brought in, and the small pot was set inside to soak.","Once it had cooled to a warm temperature, Dai Li ordered Caoxiang to take the pot out. Then, right in front of the two girls, she scooped a bowl of soup for herself and downed it in one breath.","After finishing that bowl, she drank another.","Only after drinking two consecutive bowls did Dai Li stop. At this point, more than half of the soup still remained in the small pot.","\"Go fetch two more bowls,\" Dai Li instructed.","When the new bowls were brought over, she scooped out two bowls full to the brim, adding plenty of meat to them. \"The two of you, take this soup out to the two guards outside. It's a sweltering day, let's reward them a little. Oh, right, wait by their side and bring the bowls and chopsticks back after they finish eating, so they won't have to leave their posts.\"","The bowls were very full and contained meat, making chopsticks indispensable. It would be difficult for one person to carry everything steadily, so Mei Xiang and Caoxiang went together.","Seeing the two leave the room, Dai Li hurriedly took out a small pouch and poured its contents into her palm. She had slightly processed these small pills last night, slicing each one perfectly in half.","Dai Li originally wanted to pour them all in, but she hesitated as many thoughts flashed through her mind in an instant.","She couldn't put them all in!","She didn't know if this drug would react negatively with the codonopsis root and poria mushrooms. If they counteracted each other and the drug lost its efficacy, the girls wouldn't be affected by drinking it, and she would lose her only chance.","She had to keep a backup plan.","Dai Li picked out two halves, which equaled one whole small black pill. The remaining four halves she poured entirely into the pot.","She had just drank two bowls of soup and served out another two bowls with lots of meat, so there wasn't much soup left now. The soup was warm, which was better for dissolving the medicine than cold water, but not as fast as hot water.","Dai Li quickly stirred with the spoon, using the bottom of the wooden spoon to crush the pills and dissolve the medicine as much as possible.","After a flurry of activity, there was finally no obvious residue visible in the pot. Just then, the sound of footsteps came from outside.","The two girls entered the small courtyard holding the bowls and chopsticks.","Before they even entered the room, Dai Li said to them, \"Go wash the bowls and chopsticks, and I'll serve you a bowl of soup too. There's a little bit left, just enough to split between the two of you.\"","It would be a lie to say Mei Xiang and Caoxiang weren't craving it. Earlier, however long Dai Li had walked outside under the blazing sun, they had accompanied her for just as long. Upon returning, they had been ordered to work without even a sip of water.","\"It seems a bit too much codonopsis was added; it's slightly bitter. Next time, we can put in a little less,\" Dai Li remarked casually at this moment.","The two held their bowls and thanked Dai Li, then drank the soup together.","Dai Li sat in her chair. As they tilted their heads back, her hands resting on her knees couldn't help but slowly clench into fists.","The medicine had a bitter taste, but it couldn't be said to be exactly the same as the bitterness of codonopsis. If these two had taken that kind of pill before, or had been involved in its making, she would definitely be exposed.","Dai Li watched the two unblinkingly, a thin layer of sweat breaking out on her palms.","With her nerves stretched to their absolute limit, scenes seemed to flash before her eyes:","The two girls took only one sip before sharply lifting their heads, stating bluntly that something was wrong with the soup. One stepped forward to subdue her, while the other shouted to the guards outside.","Consequently, the pot was taken away to be kept as evidence. Xiuniang and Diting arrived later upon hearing the commotion and searched her, finding the remaining pills on her person.","It was over, everything was over.","\"Clack.\" The ceramic bowl was placed on the table, emitting a soft sound.","This sound seemed to turn into a heavy punch, smashing the various illusions in front of Dai Li to pieces. Those terrifying images all turned into fragments scattered on the ground, only to be swept away by a sudden gust of wind.","\"Thank you for the reward, Madam,\" the two girls said in unison.","Dai Li snapped back to reality, a layer of cold sweat breaking out on her back. She paused for a moment before revealing a relaxed smile. \"It's just a small matter. Don't just stand there, take a seat. I'm going back to my room for a short nap.\"","With that, she rose from her seat and headed straight back to her room, looking as though she didn't intend to bother with them anymore.","Only after Dai Li was out of sight did the two girls sit down.","Not long after sitting down, Caoxiang began to rub her eyes repeatedly.","For some reason, she felt exceptionally sleepy today. Her eyelids grew heavier and heavier. Finally, the chirping of birds outside the window faded away, her vision went black, and she fell asleep leaning against the soft chair.","About ten minutes later, Dai Li tiptoed out from the inner room. Seeing both of them slumped over in their chairs, she was instantly overjoyed.","It worked!","Dai Li hurried out and took out the remaining two halves of the black pill. Just to be safe, she fed them to the two girls respectively.","After waiting a moment, Dai Li carried Caoxiang, whose physique was closer to hers, into the inner chamber and began to take off her clothes.","Caoxiang's clothes were made of linen, in a completely unremarkable unbleached color. Dai Li swiftly changed into them, then took out the remaining bit of black ointment to apply simple makeup on herself. Once everything was done, she also tucked Caoxiang's money pouch into her pocket.","She didn't just take hers; she didn't spare the one outside either.","Dai Li pushed open the window, took a deep breath, and propped her hands on the windowsill, using the momentum to kick off the ground and climb out the window.","As soon as her feet hit the ground, before she could even steady herself, Dai Li immediately dashed toward a nearby tree and ducked into its cover.","Walking beneath the trees with the canopy as a shield, no one would be able to see her unless they ran into her on the same level.","Dai Li broke into a jog, not daring to waste a single second.","From the moment the bell chimed to signal the start of the ceremony until now, about twenty minutes had already passed. Every remaining minute and second was exceptionally precious.","After running for a distance, Dai Li stopped, panting heavily.","This wouldn't do. Winding her way down the mountain was too slow, and taking the usual path carried the risk of exposure.","She turned to look at the other side. There was no trodden path here; branches and leaves grew wildly, and the vegetation was extremely dense. Heading straight down from here would be more difficult, but it would save a lot of time.","Dai Li picked up a branch to use as a walking stick. Then, she subconsciously reached for her waist, belatedly realizing that the short dagger Qin Shaozong had given her had been taken away.","Without a knife to whittle the branch, she could only make do with it as it was.","Afraid there might be snakes in the dense undergrowth, Dai Li beat the thick patches of grass and leaves with her stick as she descended the mountain. Moving swiftly all the way, she encountered a few minor hiccups, but she ultimately managed to make it down the mountain successfully.","The journey took nearly half the time she had anticipated.","Yet, as she pushed her way out of the thicket, Daili's heart suddenly plummeted, because—","At the foot of the mountain, there was not a single passenger cart in sight.","She had previously assumed that visitors would take donkey carts to Ganquan Temple, and that the carts would wait at the bottom of the mountain for passengers. That way, she could simply hire one to take her to the ferry crossing.","But looking out at the completely deserted expanse, Daili's heart turned ice-cold.","She suddenly realized something. Since Ganquan Temple was only a little over a quarter of an hour's ride from the north city gate, it was entirely possible that the drivers had simply headed back to the city after dropping off their fares.","After all, the trip out of the city was quick; they only needed to head back out a little early when it was time to pick up their passengers."]},{"number":74,"title":"Chapter 74","paragraphs":["There was no one in sight. Let alone a donkey cart or a driver, there were not even a few decent wooden planks lying around. A wave of despair washed over Dai Li.","\"I can't give up. I have no way back,\" she murmured.","With no carriages at the mountain pass leading to Ganquan Temple, Dai Li simply set off on foot.","She hiked out of the temple's mountain roads, heading toward the ferry crossing and the main road outside the city. The time it took to cover this distance completely wiped out the head start she had gained by rushing straight down the mountain, and then some.","Fortunately, after walking a fair distance, Dai Li came across another cart heading for the ferry crossing.","It was a donkey cart.","It was the most ordinary of donkey carts—a small donkey harnessed in the front, pulling a two-wheeled flatbed cart that did not even have an awning. The cart was piled high with goods packed in burlap sacks. An old man sat atop the sacks, holding a small leather whip that he cracked every now and then.","Dai Li ran up without hesitation and flagged down the cart. \"Old sir, I am heading to the ferry crossing. Could you please give me a ride? I won't ride for free; I will pay you for the fare.\"","Never expecting to earn extra silver on this trip, the old man had no reason to refuse. He smiled cheerfully and said, \"Of course. It's just that my donkey is old and doesn't walk very fast. If you don't mind, hop on.\"","Naturally, Dai Li did not mind. She thanked him and nimbly climbed onto the cart, taking a seat on a pile of bulging burlap sacks.","The moment she sat down, the invisible thread constricting her heart finally seemed to loosen a little. Dai Li took two deep breaths, trying to calm the violent pounding in her chest.","But it was of little use; her blood still boiled with anxiety.","Dai Li could not help but look back. As the donkey clopped forward, the ancient temple nestled among emerald peaks was gradually left behind. Due to the shifting angle, it was soon obscured by the lush greenery. Slowly, it vanished from sight entirely.","The old man driving the cart was likely bored, so he struck up a conversation with Dai Li. \"Miss, are you going to the ferry crossing to meet someone or to travel far? If you're meeting someone, there's actually no need. There are carriages at the ferry, and they can catch a ride into the city themselves.\"","\"Traveling far,\" Dai Li replied.","\"You haven't even brought any luggage. Traveling far like that won't be convenient. Could it be you're heading to the neighboring Jiulu County?\" The old man was quite chatty and continued on his own, \"Jiulu County is the closest. It only takes the better part of a day by boat to get there. It's early afternoon now; you can rest on the boat for the night and arrive right on time tomorrow morning.\"","Dai Li asked calmly, \"What is further east of Jiulu County?\"","\"Further east? That would be Xiagu. Xiagu is a larger place, with many merchants coming and going. Oh, you're heading to Xiagu, aren't you...\"","Upon hearing that it was a larger place, a glint of light flashed in Dai Li's eyes.","A larger place meant more inns, more places to hide, and relatively convenient transportation.","\"No, I am heading to Jiulu County,\" Dai Li said aloud.","*","Ganquan Temple.","The ceremony was more than halfway over when a person suddenly hurried over to Xiuniang's side and whispered to her, \"Xiuniang, the guards at the West Courtyard caught a man sneaking into that lady's room.\"","Xiuniang was shocked. \"What kind of scoundrel dares to act so brazenly in the temple? And specifically during the ceremony, no less!\"","The messenger reported, \"The man claims to be a subordinate of the Third Young Master. He says he came under his master's orders to deliver a gift and meant no harm.\"","Xiuniang's expression darkened.","She bore an undeniable responsibility for Dai Li getting entangled with Xie Yuanxiu. If she hadn't carelessly forgotten the master's instructions that day, Madam Dai would never have gone to the gardens.","However, the messenger's next words made Xiuniang's pupils contract, shocking her so much that she nearly cried out.","\"Xiuniang, that lady is not in the room. Her whereabouts are unknown, and both of the maids in the room are unconscious.\"","\"Is this true?\" Xiuniang could not control her volume.","Standing ahead of her, Diting glanced sideways at the sound. Taking in the sight of the pale-faced Xiuniang and the person beside her, his gaze inevitably darkened.","Xiuniang bit her lip hard. \"I need to go back. Go inform Yuping and tell her to come take my place. Hurry!\"","The person accepted the order and retreated.","As he withdrew, Xiuniang also stepped down from her position.","She had originally been standing on the high platform alongside the other members of the Green Lotus Sect, arrayed in an inverted V-formation like a flock of flying geese. However, compared to Diting, who stood at the very front as the absolute core, Xiuniang's position was much further back.","Her stepping down now was hardly conspicuous, especially since the mass of believers below currently had their eyes tightly shut and were prostrating on the ground.","Xiuniang briskly descended from the high platform and entered a secret passage to the side, signaling a few sect members to follow her along the way. The group took the shortest route, rushing hurriedly toward the West Courtyard.","Just as they approached the West Courtyard, while still a short distance away, Xiuniang spotted a man bound tightly with ropes, flanked by two armored guards.","She jogged over, her breathing growing ragged. But without sparing a moment to catch her breath, Xiuniang quickly stepped into the room.","The doors were wide open, and the interior was a complete mess. The desk and small chairs were overturned on the floor, the vase in the corner was smashed to pieces, and a plump, oval incense burner had rolled to the side of the door, completely ignored.","One glance at the scene was enough to tell that the guards had likely heard a commotion, rushed over, and engaged in a struggle with the intruder right inside the room.","In the outer room, on a cushioned chair by the window, the maid Meixiang lay with her eyes tightly shut, looking as if she were sleeping peacefully.","\"Wake her up,\" Xiuniang ordered briefly before heading further in.","Upon entering the inner chamber, she saw that the two panels of the outward-facing window were thrown wide open. Someone lay quietly on the bed, covered by a smoky-purple dress. A portion of the hem had slipped down to the foot of the bed, its subtle peony patterns catching the sunlight from the window and shimmering with a luxurious, costly luster.","The person on the bed was Caoxiang.","Or, more accurately, it was Caoxiang stripped of her outer garments.","Xiuniang stepped forward and patted Caoxiang's cheek. Seeing no reaction, she pinched hard at the girl's philtrum.","Caoxiang remained completely motionless.","\"Xiuniang, it doesn't look like she was knocked out. It looks more like she swallowed a sleeping pill,\" someone beside her noted. \"Did you ever give that lady any sleeping pills?\"","\"No, why would I ever give her something like that?!\" Xiuniang flatly denied it.","Qi Yu had only asked casually, not truly believing Xiuniang would be so careless. However, there was another possibility. \"Did you store the sleeping pills securely? Is it possible they were stolen?\"","\"I have always kept them in a cabinet, and she has never even seen them...\" Xiuniang, who was checking Caoxiang's pulse, suddenly broke off mid-sentence.","She suddenly recalled that Dai Li had, in fact, seen the bottle containing the sleeping pills.","Back on the boat, when they were intercepted by government officials, Madam Dai had to be hidden. Hiding her wasn't enough; she absolutely could not make a sound. Left with no other choice, Xiuniang had given Madam Dai a sleeping pill.","She had watched her pour out that sleeping pill—the lady had seen that bottle!","Xiuniang withdrew her hand from Caoxiang's wrist and stood up abruptly. \"Come with me.\"","Leaving behind only those words, she swiftly exited Dai Li's room and returned to her own. From a small cabinet, she took out a medicine bottle. \"These are waking pills. Take them over and feed them to the maids. Once they wake up, I have questions for them.\"","Qi Yu took the medicine and turned to leave, but Xiuniang called out to stop him. \"Qi Yu,\" she said, \"send a team of men to search the mountain.\"","Qi Yu was a messenger within the cult, not some marginal figure. \"The ceremony is already halfway through. It's hard to say, but she might have already descended the mountain. We might as well send people directly into the city... Right, does she have a pass?\"","Xiuniang remained silent for a moment before finally squeezing out the word, \"Yes.\"","Qi Yu rubbed his forehead. \"What were you thinking? How could you give her a pass! With a pass, she can enter the city and go to the ferry to take a boat. If she leaves Si Province by boat, tracking her down will be a nightmare.\"","\"Take that up with the mister. That pass was given to her under Diting's personal instruction,\" Xiuniang said coldly. \"Let's search the mountain first. Who knows, she might still be hiding here. There is one of her dresses in the next room. Cut a piece off and let the hounds sniff it to see which way she went.\"","Qi Yu was left speechless by her earlier words. Finally, he simply said, \"Fine, I will arrange the mountain search.\"","After he left, Xiuniang shifted her gaze back to the cabinet, an unresolvable doubt lingering in her eyes.","When Madam Dai appeared in her room that day, she was likely trying to steal the sleeping pills; the stuffed rabbit was nothing but a decoy. But Xiuniang had clearly checked the medicine bottles at the time, and not just one—she had checked every single bottle in the entire cabinet. They were packed full of sleeping pills, not a single one missing.","How could this be?","Where did Madam Dai get the sleeping pills?","Refusing to give up, Xiuniang took out all the small medicine bottles containing the sleeping pills, opened them all, and counted them again.","The count was still correct. Not a single pill was missing.","And yet, Caoxiang and Meixiang outside were unconscious. Could it be that they hadn't taken the sleeping pills, but consumed some other drug?","Could someone from the North have come and taken Madam Dai away unnoticed during the ceremony?","But the two guards were still alive. If Caoxiang and Meixiang inside the room had seen a stranger, there was no reason the two girls wouldn't have called out for the guards. Moreover, if someone from the North really had come, there would be no need for the madam to take off her lavish dress...","Xiuniang felt as if she were surrounded by a thick fog, unable to see clearly where exactly things had gone wrong.","An unknown amount of time passed before she was snapped out of her daze.","\"They're awake. Go ask them immediately.\"","Caoxiang and Meixiang had awoken. Looking at the room full of people and hearing them ask when Dai Li had disappeared, the two girls were instantly frightened out of their wits.","\"I-I don't know. After I drank the madam's summer cooling soup, I inexplicably felt exhausted and fell asleep without realizing it. When I woke up again, it was just now...\"","\"Right, the summer cooling soup. I also fell asleep after drinking it.\"","The small table in the room had been knocked over, and the pot that had previously rested on it was shattered into pieces.","Xiuniang crouched down, picked out a relatively large shard from the pile of broken pot pieces, and used her finger to dab a little of the soup from the inner wall.","As soon as her fingertip touched her lips, the confusion in Xiuniang's eyes deepened. She murmured, \"It tastes like the sleeping pills. Someone put medicine in the pot.\"","\"That's impossible. The madam drank it too, two bowls in a row,\" Meixiang blurted out subconsciously.","\"She drank it too? Did she drink it first, or later?\" Xiuniang asked.","Caoxiang chimed in, \"After the summer cooling soup was ready, the madam drank two bowls in one breath. Later, she ordered us to take two bowls out for the two guards. After scooping out those four bowls, the remaining two were given to us.\"","Qi Yu's expression was grave. \"Where did she get the medicine? Who gave it to her?\"","There was one thought he left unsaid: Could there be a traitor within the cult?","Xiuniang read the unspoken implication in his eyes and immediately shook her head. \"No one could have given it to her. When she spent nearly half a month on the boat, I was the one taking care of her personally. Besides me, she hardly spoke to anyone else.\"","Qi Yu pressed, \"What about after arriving in Tianshui Commandery?\"","Xiuniang continued, \"Besides me, Caoxiang and Meixiang were added to attend to her personally. And during these days at the residence, she only went out to visit the market once. We followed her the whole time. She had no contact with anyone else, nor did she act unusually.\"","\"That's strange, then. Where did she get the medicine?\" Qi Yu muttered.","When he joined the cult, Xiuniang was already a member. Her seniority was deeper than his, and she had always been highly valued by Diting. If not for that, he would have suspected Xiuniang of defecting to the enemy.","Xiuniang pursed her lips, choosing not to tell him about the time Dai Li had entered her room alone.","Qi Yu was merely her subordinate; there was no need to explain this matter to him.","Xiuniang asked Caoxiang, \"When was that pot of summer cooling soup brought over?\"","Caoxiang answered honestly, \"Exactly at noon, right when the ceremony started.\"","Xiuniang did a quick calculation on her fingers. The soup was ready exactly at noon, and the time spent drinking it definitely wouldn't have exceeded half an hour. In other words, it had been roughly three hours since Madam Dai left.","Three hours was more than enough time for her to descend the mountain...","Dong, dong, dong—","Suddenly, the sound of a bell chimed.","Both of them were startled.","The ceremony began with the tolling of the bell, and it was supposed to conclude with the tolling of the bell. According to the original plan, the ceremony was scheduled to end in a little over half an hour, definitely not now.","It seemed this matter had already alarmed Diting.","About fifteen minutes later, Diting, dressed in a white Daoist robe and wearing a silver-white mask, rushed over.","He already had a premonition that something major had happened on his way here; otherwise, given Xiuniang's composed nature, she would absolutely not have spoken up during the ceremony while on the high platform.","\"...She's gone?\" Diting's voice suddenly spiked in pitch.","It was a good thing he was still wearing his silver-white mask, or else his loss of composure would have been seen by everyone.","\"Tell me everything, leave no detail out. Hurry,\" Diting's voice lacked its usual unhurried calm.","Caoxiang and Meixiang started from the beginning. They explained that Dai Li had gone out for a stroll this morning and, upon returning, complained about the unbearable heat. She had them stew a pot of ginseng and poria root soup. They shared the soup, and after drinking it, the two of them lost consciousness.","Upon hearing this, Diting asked the same question Xiuniang had asked earlier: when was the soup served?","After receiving the answer, Diting fell silent for a moment. \"Three hours. That's enough time for her to get down the mountain. If she was lucky enough to run into a carriage, it's also enough time to enter the city or reach the ferry crossing.\"","\"Sir!\" Someone hurried in from outside.","The person leading the way was the captain Qi Yu had sent out earlier to conduct the search.","\"We've searched the perimeter of Ganquan Temple, but there's no sign of Madam Dai,\" the captain reported.","Unwilling to give up, Xiuniang asked, \"What about the mountain range in the back?\"","The captain replied, \"We brought the hounds there just now, but they didn't react to the back mountain. On the contrary, at the front of the mountain, they kept pulling toward the bushes, heading straight down the mountain in a straight line.\"","Diting closed his eyes. \"She went down the mountain.\"","Not only did she go down the mountain, but she took a straight path, which saved much more time than following the winding mountain trail.","The young man suddenly opened his eyes. Under everyone's gaze, he walked over to the tied-up gift bearer.","A cold glint of steel flashed, startling the man so much that his face turned deathly pale. He repeatedly pleaded, \"Don't kill me! I'm the Third Young Master's man. I was only acting on orders this time!\"","However, the agonizing pain he expected never came. Instead, the ropes binding him suddenly loosened.","The man froze in stunned disbelief.","Diting sheathed his blade, personally helped the man to his feet, and even smoothed out his collar. \"Take a message to Xie San for me. When I said earlier that my older sister was married, it was true, but I only told half the story. My brother-in-law has perished, and she is now all alone. If the Third Young Master can help me find my sister, who threw a fit and ran away from home, then as her younger brother, I would not object to her making a new friend.\"","The man nodded profusely.","Once the man had left, Diting turned to Qi Yu. \"Take your men and ride for the ferry crossing at once. Do your best to intercept all departing boats. Stop any donkey carts lingering at the docks or making their return journeys, and ask the drivers if they gave a ride to a young woman traveling alone. If they did, use whatever means necessary to make them reveal every detail.\"","He then singled out another person. \"Fanyin, hurry back to the city and find Old Zeng. Tell him to keep a close watch for any movements involving the travel pass under the name 'He Hua'. If anyone uses it to check into an inn, detain them immediately.\"","Once these orders were methodically issued, a group of men withdrew from the small courtyard.","Diting looked toward Xiuniang. \"She has only been in contact with a few of you these past few days, and among you, only you possess the sleeping pellets.\"","This matter had to be thoroughly investigated, as it concerned whether there was a mole within their sect.","His gaze grew increasingly sharp. Xiuniang no longer dared to hide the truth as she had earlier. She was forced to admit that Dai Li had entered her room one day, but added that she had carefully checked afterward and found none of the sleeping pellets in her cabinet missing.","Hearing this, Diting fell silent for a moment before stepping toward her room. He needed to see for himself.","Xiuniang immediately followed.","Back in her room, she took out all the medicine bottles containing the sleeping pellets from the cabinet and lined them up on the table.","Diting instructed her to bring over several small dishes and sort the pellets into them. Dish by dish, the small plates soon covered the table. With a single glance, the exact number of little black pellets in each dish was glaringly obvious.","Looking at it this way, not a single one appeared to be missing.","However, Diting did not let Xiuniang put them back right away. He reached out, picked up one of the small dishes, and used his slender fingers to pinch the pellets one by one, inspecting them meticulously.","The room was dead silent. Neither of them spoke; there was only the occasional soft clink of a ceramic dish being set down.","Suddenly, Diting let out a questioning hum. He pressed down hard, and the little black pellet between his fingers crumbled instantly, leaving a conspicuous smear of black on the man's fair fingertips.","Xiuniang's face drained of color.","Diting, however, revealed a relieved smile.","Excellent. This meant the sect was clean; there was no traitor among them.","The ferry crossing.","Dai Li stepped down from the donkey cart. Just as she was preparing to pay the fare, the faint ringing of bells drifted over from the distance.","By the time the chimes reached the docks, they were barely discernible, and many pedestrians turned a deaf ear to them.","To Dai Li's ears, however, the sound was like a mountain collapsing or a towering tsunami crashing down. It shook her to the core, terrifying her out of her wits and leaving her face completely ashen. \"How can this be...\"","The festival was over.","The festival had ended early. This meant that someone must have discovered her absence."]},{"number":75,"title":"Chapter 75","paragraphs":["\"My lady, my lady? You haven't paid your fare yet.\" Seeing Dai Li in a daze, the old man couldn't help but remind her.","Dai Li suddenly snapped back to her senses. After paying the bill swiftly, she walked briskly toward the ferry crossing.","It was now the early Shen hour, and there were quite a few boatmen soliciting customers at the ferry crossing. Dai Li did not choose a large, sturdy tower ship, but instead walked toward the small boats.","\"Boatman, are you going to Xiagu? I have a close relative there who is gravely ill and running out of time. I must go to see him off on his final journey. If you are willing to set off for Xiagu immediately, how about I pay the fare for five people myself?\" Dai Li didn't dare to offer too high a price, afraid that showing off her wealth would attract jealous eyes.","Hearing the last sentence, the boatman perked up instantly. \"To Xiagu, we leave right now!\"","Dai Li boarded the boat.","The boat was small in size, featuring nothing more than an arched-roof cabin. Inside the cabin, linen cloth was used as a partition, slightly separating it into two sections, forming two inner cabins.","This kind of small boat couldn't carry many people. Including the boatman, it could hold at most five people. If there were any more, it would easily capsize when encountering large waves on the river.","Because of Dai Li's offer, which was tantamount to chartering the entire boat, the boatman didn't take on any other passengers. He pulled in the anchor, pushed hard with the oars, and the boat slowly left the shore.","Dai Li looked inside from the rolled-up linen at the front and saw that the first inner cabin was completely empty. The linen further inside was slightly blown up by the wind, and a sliver of space opening from the middle allowed a glimpse inside.","There was someone in that inner cabin.","Dai Li sat in the first inner cabin.","The boatman sized her up, and seeing her empty-handed, couldn't help but ask curiously, \"You didn't bring any luggage? From here to Xiagu, even if the weather is kind to us, it will take two days and one night.\"","Dai Li showed a helpless expression. \"I didn't have the time to care about that. When I heard the news, my head was just buzzing. By the time I regained my senses, I was already on a donkey cart out of the city, almost at the ferry crossing. Seeing that I at least had my travel pass and some travel expenses, which would barely suffice, I simply decided not to go back.\"","The boatman had a quick mind. Moreover, for someone like him who made a living on a boat all year round, there must be a lot of dry rations on board.","He immediately probed, \"My lady, I have some dry rations on this boat. How about I sell some to you?\"","Dai Li was delighted inwardly; this was exactly like someone handing her a pillow right as she was nodding off. \"Of course, that would be wonderful.\"","Dai Li, who was chatting with the boatman, didn't notice, or rather, couldn't see from her current line of sight, that a sailboat was approaching from not far away.","The linen sail was blown taut by the wind, pushing the boat forward rapidly. As it neared the shore, a burly man rolled up the sail, releasing the wind power and letting the boat slow down.","The boat docked, but before the burly man could set up the wooden plank for connecting to the shore, a slender figure suddenly leaped from the side of the boat, actually jumping directly from the boat onto the shore.","\"Hey, take it easy,\" the burly man said.","That figure walked forward without looking back.","The burly man clicked his tongue in wonder. \"What an agile young man. I wonder which family's young master has come out to gain experience.\"","The two boats crossed paths, drifting further and further apart.","\"Clop, clop, clop—\"","Horse hooves trampled over the yellow dirt road, coming menacingly. A group of horses galloped along the official road, and pedestrians quickly dodged upon seeing them. However, some carriages soon realized that dodging was useless; the other party was coming straight for them.","The rider reined in his horse, looking down at the driver from his high vantage point. The sword at his waist was exceptionally eye-catching.","\"Have you carried a woman traveling alone to the ferry crossing?\" the cavalryman asked.","The donkey cart driver shook his head repeatedly. In these times, one should never argue with an armed man. He answered forthrightly, \"No, I didn't. I went to the ferry crossing in the morning to wait for cargo, and I just finished loading all the goods onto the cart. I haven't seen any woman.\"","The cavalryman then left. This scene was happening everywhere on the official road; all returning carriages were intercepted.","Qi Yu's subordinates scattered to interrogate the carriages returning to the city, and Qi Yu was no exception.","He intercepted a donkey cart, asked the same question as his subordinates, and said, \"...This woman is a wanted criminal. Anyone who can provide clues will be rewarded. Conversely, anyone who harbors her will be guilty of the same crime.\"","The driver shook his head repeatedly and said, \"No, no, I didn't see any woman traveling alone on my way there, I...\"","Before he could finish his words, the driver suddenly felt a movement at the back of the cart. It turned out to be the strange passenger who had paid him the fare jumping off the cart.","\"Qi Yu.\"","Suddenly being called by name, Qi Yu turned his head toward the sound. A flash of bright light reflected directly at him, stinging his eyes and making him squint. It was also at this moment that he realized the donkey cart was carrying another person in the back.","That person wore a black mask, concealing their face, and had a hoarse, rather unpleasant voice.","Qi Yu was stunned and carefully sized up the other party.","Many people in their cult had masks, and those who could obtain a mask were no ordinary cult members. Once the mask was put on, the face could no longer be seen; unless they were close acquaintances, no one would be able to recognize them.","However, it wasn't absolute. Besides the face, one could also listen to the voice. For example, if Xiuniang spoke in her usual voice, she would be very easy to recognize.","And apart from that, there was another person...","\"Mingdeng?\"","Qi Yu dismounted from his horse. \"You're back? You haven't had any news for a while, and I was even thinking of going to look for you. But at that time, Diting said there was no need, and also said you would return sooner or later.\"","Mingdeng did not respond to this, but instead asked, \"You are looking for a woman?\"","The donkey cart driver was not suspicious, so Qi Yu waved his hand to let him go, and then said to the person in front of him, \"Yes, looking for someone. You must know this woman, and maybe you've even seen her before. It is the former favorite concubine of the Marquis of Wu'an, Madam Dai.\"","Mingdeng asked, \"Wasn't she invited to join the cult? Why are you still searching for her everywhere?\"","Qi Yu sighed, \"In a moment of inattention, she found a loophole and slipped away. I heard that on the way back from Bairi City, the Marquis of Wu'an set up quite a few obstacles on the river, attempting to intercept and bring her back. During those rounds of searches, Madam Dai was extremely cooperative. Everyone, including Diting, thought she was sincerely joining the cult. Who could have expected that it was just to make us lower our guard.\"","The young man beneath the mask slowly relaxed his brows. \"She ran away?\"","\"Yes! At the very beginning of the ceremony, she drugged her two personal maids and ran away.\" Qi Yu hadn't stayed until the end, so he didn't yet know where Dai Li's sleeping pills came from. \"Xiuniang said none of her drugs were missing, so I don't know where she got the sleeping pills either. Let's just hope there isn't a mole within our cult.\"","Mingdeng: \"It's hard to say.\"","Qi Yu looked left and right, and as if wanting to do him a favor, whispered, \"You hadn't replied to any messages before, and I noticed that Diting seemed a bit displeased. When you see him, he will definitely ask you for details, so you'd better explain it clearly.\"","In Qi Yu's view, explaining the matter was not exactly simple, but it couldn't be considered fraught with difficulties either.","If he were Mingdeng and had to report, he would definitely say that he went to assassinate the Marquis of Wu'an under the orders of Fan of Yanzhou, but was unfortunately captured. In order to survive, he had no choice but to cooperate with the Marquis of Wu'an and act as his excuse to eradicate Yanzhou.","Although everything was done out of necessity, it ultimately ruined the grand scheme. Qi Yu guessed that he would inevitably suffer some punishment.","Mingdeng seemed entirely unconcerned about this, returning to the previous topic. \"You took your men to the ferry crossing. Are you certain she went there?\"","\"I am not certain,\" Qi Yu said. \"But it has been less than four hours since she descended the mountain. If she enters the city, she will likely stay at an inn tonight. With the Third Young Master's help, if she dares to stay at an inn, we will definitely find her before noon tomorrow.\"","\"The Third Young Master you speak of, is it Third Young Master Xie?\" Mingdeng fell silent for a moment.","\"It is indeed Xie Yuanxiu,\" Qi Yu laughed. \"Coincidentally, this Third Young Master Xie has definitely taken a fancy to Madam Dai. During today's celebration, he even sent someone to sneak into her room to deliver a gift, only to find it empty. Thanks to this little commotion, we realized she had run away.\"","Mingdeng lowered his eyes.","Qi Yu could not see his expression, but looking into those cold, dark eyes, he could only sense the other man's displeasure.","\"I will go with you to the ferry crossing,\" Mingdeng said suddenly.","Qi Yu was stunned. \"You will go with me? That is hardly appropriate. You just managed to return; perhaps you should go back and report on your duties first.\"","\"It will not make much of a difference,\" Mingdeng simply replied.","Qi Yu figured the other man might be trying to make amends for his past mistakes. Since that was the case, it was not his place to say more. He could only call over a subordinate and order him to give up his horse.","They continued toward the ferry crossing.","Along the way, they kept intercepting carriage drivers.","They questioned group after group, turning up empty-handed time and time again, until one instance—","\"...You have seen her?!\" Qi Yu was overjoyed, immediately firing off a string of questions at the old man. \"When was this? What was the situation at the time?\"","If Dai Li were here, she would certainly recognize this apprehended old man as the very driver she had hitched a ride with earlier.","The old man did not dare to hide anything and recounted everything in full detail. Finally, he said, \"...She told me she was heading to Jiulu County.\"","Qi Yu did a quick calculation.","It had already been more than an hour since Madam Dai arrived at the ferry crossing; she must have boarded a boat by now.","\"She is already gone, and the speed of a boat traveling downstream is far beyond what horses can match. We might as well return and report this, then wait for Diting's arrangements,\" Mingdeng suddenly suggested.","Qi Yu thought for a moment and found it reasonable.","Diting had tasked him with tracking down Madam Dai's whereabouts. Now that the mission was accomplished, he really ought to go back and report first.","*","\"...It cannot be Jiulu County.\" Upon hearing Qi Yu's report, Diting shook his head. \"Her words cannot be trusted. Since she also mentioned Xiagu during the conversation, it is highly likely she went to Xiagu.\"","However, after saying this, Diting smiled and shook his head again. \"But we cannot ignore Jiulu County either. Her mind is full of schemes.\"","Xie Yuanxiu was standing nearby.","Ever since he received the message brought back by his servant, he had been overjoyed and had come to visit once again.","It was almost dusk, but Xie Yuanxiu showed no sign of leaving. \"Jiulu County is very close to here. I will send a troop of men to rush over overnight and thoroughly search the inns in the county.\"","\"As for the slightly farther Xiagu, we can take both land and water routes. We will send men on light boats downstream toward the east to enter through the north city gate; meanwhile, another squad will set out from the south of Tianshui Commandery and take the southern route to Xiagu.\" Xie Yuanxiu grew increasingly excited as he spoke. \"With a pincer attack from both the north and the south, your esteemed sister will have nowhere to go and will have no choice but to obediently return home.\"","\"What if she is not in Xiagu, but has gone to a commandery or county further east?\" someone suddenly spoke up.","It was the first time Xie Yuanxiu had heard such a grating voice. He instinctively frowned, feeling his mood thoroughly dampened.","Although the man's words were not without reason, he had just talked about bringing her back home, and this person's remark was like a bucket of cold water poured right over his head.","His earlier excitement instantly dissipated by more than half.","\"It does not matter if she has gone to other commanderies or counties. The believers of our cult are spread across all provinces, and she only has a single travel pass in her possession. Sooner or later, we will know where she is,\" Diting said.","Xie Yuanxiu did not like the phrase \"sooner or later.\" He wished he could find her tonight and share a night of passion with her. Regarding the search, Xie Yuanxiu eagerly offered his suggestions: \"Aside from Xiagu and Jiulu, we naturally cannot overlook the other commanderies and counties to the east.\"","\"The Marquis of Wu'an and Governor Nangong just conquered Yanzhou. If we mobilize troops on a large scale to search for someone at this time, would it not be seen as a provocation by the Northern Territory and Qingzhou?\" Mingdeng asked in a calm tone.","At these words, Xie Yuanxiu froze for a moment.","He had gained the support of the Green Lotus Cult, but his eldest and second brothers were still around, and his position as the Governor of Sizhou was not yet secure. Provoking the Northern Territory and Qingzhou at this time was indeed unwise.","Diting glanced at the person beside him. \"Go in disguise and keep a low profile. It should not be a big problem.\"","Xie Yuanxiu's expression improved significantly. \"I will send men to set out overnight for Xiagu, Jiulu, and other places.\"","Diting nodded.","After exchanging a few more words, Diting asked Xie Yuanxiu to return first. Once the other man and his entourage left, only he and one other person remained in the room.","With no outsiders present, Diting took off the silver-white mask on his face, revealing a casual demeanor rarely seen in front of others. \"Why were you delayed outside for so long this time?\"","Mingdeng replied, \"The Marquis of Wu'an is difficult to deal with. Just making it back took a tremendous amount of effort.\"","\"Are you injured?\" Diting scrutinized him.","The young man wore a black robe and looked travel-worn, yet his posture remained as straight as a pine tree. Just by looking, one could not tell whether he was injured.","Mingdeng said, \"It is nothing serious.\"","\"Diting, I want to lead a team in the search.\"","\"Mingdeng, you stayed by the Marquis of Wu'an's side for so long. What happened during that time?\"","The two voices rang out simultaneously.","Diting raised an eyebrow. \"Why are you taking this matter so much to heart?\"","\"I bear part of the responsibility for Yanzhou being captured. If I had not been taken alive by the Marquis of Wu'an, allowing him to use me as a pretext to crusade against Yanzhou, Fan Tianshi would not have lost his life over this, causing the cult to lose a decent ally for nothing,\" Mingdeng explained.","In truth, compared to the title \"Mingdeng,\" the young man preferred the name his mother had given him: Qin Yanzhou.","*","On the Jin River, the river breeze blew the sails into the shape of crescent moons as the multi-storied ship rode the waves.","A gyrfalcon with white and brownish feathers let out a long cry before tilting its wings and beginning to dive.","A tall figure stepped out from the cabin and casually raised his hand. The gyrfalcon, weighing over four pounds, swooped down and landed on his long arm. The man's bent arm only swayed slightly.","Qin Shaozong single-handedly untied the thin ribbon on the gyrfalcon's leg, retrieved the small bamboo tube attached to it, and then gave his arm a sharp jerk upwards.","The gyrfalcon spread its wings once more, circled once in the air, and landed on the crossbeam of the mast, where it began to preen its feathers.","Hearing the falcon's cry, several men followed him out of the inner cabin.","\"My Lord, is there a message from the front? Have they found her?!\" Mo Yanyun asked impatiently.","The Marquis's secret departure from Bairi City was quite a risky move. Yanzhou had only recently been acquired, and there were countless matters to attend to. Furthermore, right next door was Qingzhou, whose obedience could be genuine or merely a facade.","With the Marquis gone, many orders would not be transmitted in time, and certain vacant positions left by Yanzhou officials might be opportunistically seized by Qingzhou.","But anxiety was useless. Given his superior's temperament, once he had made a decision, not even nine oxen could drag him back.","Qin Shaozong finished reading the letter and said, \"That kid finally disembarked at Tianshui Commandery.\"","\"Tianshui Commandery?\"","Mo Yanyun had a sharp memory for maps and instantly pinpointed its location in Sizhou. \"What is he doing in Sizhou? Could he be someone from Sizhou?\"","Qin Shaozong had never explicitly mentioned that Qin Yanzhou had another faction backing him. However, there was no shortage of shrewd individuals under his command. Ever since he let Qin Yanzhou go and dispatched people to secretly tail him, some had already deduced the underlying implications.","Since they were all comrades, they inevitably gathered around to chat. As they gossiped, everyone eventually figured it out. However, Mo Yanyun was the first to bring the matter up directly to Qin Shaozong's face.","Feng Feng silently shifted his seat, putting some distance between himself and Mo Yanyun.","Qin Shaozong knew exactly what kind of temperament his subordinates had and was well aware of their habit of holding little secret meetings. \"Third Young Master Xie has also appeared in Tianshui Commandery recently, and even paid a visit to the members of the Green Lotus Cult.\"","Feng Feng stroked his chin.","If that was the case, did that not mean there were two different factions operating in Tianshui Commandery?","\"We will reach Tianshui Commandery in three days,\" Mo Yanyun prayed. \"May the Heavens show us some favor and let the winds blow a bit fiercer.\"","After enduring a long and grueling journey on the small boat, Dai Li finally arrived at Xiagu near the end of the noon hour on the third day.","She had always considered herself to have a strong constitution; she never suffered from motion sickness or seasickness, rarely fell ill, and had an excellent appetite. But this time, after stepping off the boat, Dai Li felt as if her soul was still swaying out on the water.","The small boat was light and traveled swiftly downstream, but precisely because of its light weight, it lacked the stability of a larger vessel and was prone to intense bumping and swaying.","Dai Li walked dizzily for a short distance before casually finding a donkey cart to ride into the city.","Xiagu Commandery was truly massive. Even if the enemy knew her destination, it would be impossible for them to dig her out in a short amount of time.","In other words, she was safe for today.","Upon entering the city, Dai Li headed straight for a pawnshop and sold a few pieces of jewelry for some silver. Afterward, she went for a hearty meal to comfort her empty stomach, bought a few necessities, and only then went to pick out a place to stay for the night.","After taking a thoroughly comfortable bath at the inn, she fell into a deep, oblivious slumber.","Fast asleep, Dai Li was completely unaware that during the darkest part of the night, near the end of the Yin hour, several ships had sailed in from the west and finally docked at the northern ferry crossing outside the commandery."]},{"number":76,"title":"Chapter 76","paragraphs":["Daili was too tired. Once her nerves relaxed even slightly, many of her bodily functions went out of control, and she fell into a deep sleep.","She had originally planned to wake up early the next morning at the beginning of the Chen hour, which was around seven or eight o'clock. However, since there were no alarm clocks in this era, and she had automatically tuned out the hustle and bustle outside her window, Daili slept straight through until the end of the Wu hour.","Clutching the quilt, Daili abruptly sat up from the bed. Looking at the angle of the sunlight entering the room, she muttered, \"Oh no, this is bad.\"","The city gates opened at the first light of dawn, which was over three shichen ago. Three shichen, six hours—so much could be done in that time.","Daili didn't dare to delay any further. She immediately got up to wash and dress, and applied some makeup.","The inn she had carefully selected was on the smaller side, with a very average location. In terms of cleanliness and service, it couldn't compare to other establishments.","But it had one aspect that perfectly suited Daili's wishes, which was...","The young attendant at the front desk was quite perfunctory.","When she checked in and paid yesterday, her identification pass remained in her hands from beginning to end.","That lazy young attendant merely lifted his eyelids to take a glance. He was so casual that he didn't even ask her to move the finger that \"accidentally\" covered half of her name.","She was certain he hadn't clearly seen the name \"He Hua\", but that didn't mean she could rest easy.","The sheer number of low-level followers of the Green Lotus Sect was evident from the massive crowd of commoners who attended the grand ceremony on the first day of the month.","They blended into the lowest rungs of society, coming and going without a trace. It was entirely possible that a street vendor was one of them, or even the most ordinary-looking young attendant at a certain inn.","Daili's luggage consisted only of a light, flimsy little bundle containing a few brocade kerchiefs, some hair ointment and face cream, and a few pieces of jewelry. Aside from that, she didn't even have a second set of clothes. As for her silver coins and other small, delicate ornaments, she kept them close to her body, not daring to put them in the small bundle.","She left her guest room and went down the stairs.","Daili thought for a moment and decided to go to the counter to extend her stay. \"I'd like to extend my room for two days.\"","\"Sixty coins,\" the young attendant quoted the price first, taking an extra glance at the bundle on Daili's shoulder. \"My lady, you can just leave your things in your room. Our inn is very safe; no one would dare come here to steal.\"","\"No, I'll carry them myself. The last place I stayed at said the same thing, but I still ended up losing things when I returned to my room,\" Daili refused.","She had thought the young attendant would drop the subject, collect the money, and she would go find some food.","Who would have expected the young attendant to say at this moment, \"Our boss's older brother is no ordinary person. His brother knows many powerful figures with immense influence, as well as countless sworn brothers and sisters of different surnames. Let me put it this way: there are plenty of petty thieves in Xia Valley, but here at our place...\"","The young attendant stuck out a finger and wagged it. \"Thieves wouldn't dare to come.\"","Daili's brow twitched, and an inexplicable sense of foreboding rose within her. \"Countless sworn brothers and sisters? Are you trying to fool me? Even the Peach Garden Oath only bound a few people together.\"","\"Ignorant woman. My boss's older brother is a follower,\" the young attendant snorted.","The current dynasty had not issued any orders banning the sect, so the common people did not keep their mouths shut about it. In fact, many people even took pride in it.","Daili felt a wave of dizziness.","Yesterday, she had scouted many inns until her feet were sore. She never expected that after all her careful selection, she would walk straight into the enemy camp and choose the absolute worst one.","What terrible luck!","No, not exactly. At least she found out early.","The young attendant said the boss's older brother was a follower, not the boss himself. There was a layer of separation here. As long as they hadn't found their way here yet, there was still time...","However, just as Daili thought this, people hurried in from outside. Judging by the footsteps, there was more than one person.","Then someone spoke:","\"Brother, my inn isn't very large. I heard you are looking for a noble person. Why would such a prestigious figure ever take a liking to my small inn?\"","\"You don't need to worry about that. Just give the young attendant a few instructions.\"","With her back to the door, Daili's heart suddenly leaped into her throat, then slowly settled down just a fraction.","It sounded like the boss and his brother.","So only two people came?","\"Please rest assured, Your Excellency. I will absolutely do my utmost to carry out the orders passed down from above.\" It was the older brother's voice.","Daili shuddered. In that instant, she felt the muscles and bones in her entire body twitch. A snake-like chill shot up from her tailbone, eventually wrapping its head around her neck, making the surrounding air feel incredibly thin.","This inn was not large. She remembered that the distance from the door to the counter was only about seven steps.","There were more than two people who had arrived!","There were also people from the Green Lotus Sect, and they had come here.","\"You're right, then I can stay here with peace of mind.\" Daili placed the silver coins in her hand onto the counter. \"I suddenly remembered that I might have left something in my room. I'll go up and check.\"","Having said that, Daili didn't wait for the young attendant to respond. She turned sideways and headed toward the stairs.","The main door and the stairs were not on the same side. Walking toward the stairs meant she wouldn't have to face the people at the door.","The young attendant had also heard the voices, and his attention had long since drifted over there. He instinctively swept the money from the counter into the till, then rubbed his hands together and left the counter to greet them.","As for the young lady staying at the inn?","Oh, if she wanted to stay, she could stay; if not, so be it. Either way, the money for the room wasn't going into his pocket.","Right now, entertaining the boss was more important.","Daili's heart beat like a drum, pounding so hard her eardrums ached, but she didn't dare walk too fast. If she showed even a hint of panic, it would definitely draw their attention. Moreover, she didn't know if the \"Your Excellency\" they mentioned had ever seen her face...","Reaching the foot of the stairs, Daili lifted her foot and began to climb.","The wooden stairs let out soft creaks when stepped on. What would normally be a very ordinary sound now pierced Daili's ears like needles, making every step she took exceptionally difficult.","However, Daili soon realized that she was just being paranoid and had gotten worked up over nothing, because those people hadn't noticed her plain and unremarkable appearance at all.","After turning the corner, Daili stopped in her tracks.","She didn't go upstairs; instead, she hid there to eavesdrop.","\"Where is the registry of yesterday's guests? Bring it out for a look,\" the boss's older brother said.","\"Th-there is no registry. Our inn has always just taken a glance at the identification pass during check-in; we don't record them,\" the young attendant replied, his voice growing quieter and quieter.","\"Nonsense, how can you do things this way!\" the boss's older brother scolded.","For the next brief moment, Daili didn't hear any immediate voices. It was likely the boss pulling his brother aside to whisper something.","Anyway, a moment later, the boss's older brother cleared his throat lightly. \"It's fine if you didn't have one before, but you must have one now. Anyone staying at the inn must have their identification details registered. Go do it right now. Take a small booklet and go door to door...\"","Daili's breath caught in her throat. She didn't dare linger any longer and hurriedly went upstairs.","This small inn had three floors, and Daili's room was at the end of the second floor. She walked quickly back into her room, locked the latch on the door, and then threw open the quilt on the bed.","Grabbing one of the corners, she tied it to the heavy bedpost. Daili used a knot meant for escaping fires, so she wasn't worried that the quilt would suddenly come loose midway due to immense force.","The window happened to be right next to the bed. After tying the knot securely, Daili pushed open the window and looked down.","This inn was small in scale, so naturally, it didn't occupy a prime location like the larger inns. It was situated right in an alley, and the paths connecting to it from several directions were also alleys.","Unluckily, at this moment, a woman carrying a bamboo basket on her arm was passing through the alley.","Having just eaten her fill, she was walking at a leisurely pace.","Dai Li bit her lip, burning with anxiety. Since the woman hadn't left yet, she couldn't lower her makeshift blanket rope right now. But she could already hear footsteps approaching.","It was now the end of the noon hour, a time when not many guests remained inside the inn.","\"Open the door! Is anyone there?\" A knock sounded from outside.","However, it wasn't Dai Li's door being knocked on. She poked her head out to look down again.","The woman had made it more than halfway through and was about to turn out of the alley.","\"Who is it? Why are you knocking at this hour? I don't recall asking for a servant to come to my room.\"","\"An important fugitive has recently entered the city, and the authorities are currently searching everywhere. We hope you will cooperate.\" Dai Li heard an unfamiliar voice.","She guessed this person was the \"Your Excellency\" the innkeeper had mentioned.","Dai Li stared intently below and decided not to wait any longer. She began to lower the rope first. She lowered it gently, and the woman remained completely unaware, not even pausing her steps as she turned out of the alley.","As soon as the woman was gone, Dai Li immediately climbed onto the window sill.","The first floor of this inn was built quite high, over ten feet tall. Dai Li's current distance from the ground was this height, plus the height of the window sill. If she fell from this height and had the bad luck to hit her head, it wasn't impossible for her to be sent straight to her next reincarnation.","Dai Li dared not relax. She gripped the rope tightly with her hands, trying her best to keep her feet perpendicular to the ground as she descended.","...","Second floor.","\"Is anyone there?\" The young servant walked further in and knocked on another door.","He knocked for a moment, but no one answered.","\"Could they have gone out?\" the innkeeper said.","\"Push the door open,\" the innkeeper's older brother said.","None of the guest rooms had exterior locks; to lock the door, one could only slide the latch from the inside. The innkeeper had always been obedient to his older brother, not to mention that when he first opened the inn, his brother had provided part of the funds.","The innkeeper immediately pushed the door open himself.","The room was completely empty.","\"Did they go out? Or is it unoccupied?\" the innkeeper asked the young servant.","\"Oh, oh, this is an empty room, no one is here.\" The previously dazed young servant finally realized, and as soon as he spoke, he received a smack on the head from the innkeeper. He quickly clutched his head and begged for mercy. \"The next one isn't. The room next door is occupied by a lady, and she is definitely inside.\"","\"How do you know she is there?\" the innkeeper's older brother asked.","The young servant didn't overthink it. \"She came downstairs just now. She originally wasn't going to stay, but then she extended her room for another two days.\"","\"Just now?\" someone spoke up.","\"Yes, just now, right when you all first arrived. After paying for the extension, she went upstairs.\" As the young servant spoke, he walked to the door at the end of the corridor and raised his hand to knock. \"Lady, please open the door.\"","There was no answer from inside, nor any sound.","The innkeeper raised his hand to push and found that the latch inside was secured. The door couldn't be pushed open.","\"Lady?!\" The young servant was still knocking. \"Please open the door. An important fugitive has entered the city, and we need to register your travel document information now.\"","The room remained dead silent.","\"Could she have fallen asleep? That shouldn't be, she just came down fifteen minutes ago...\" the young servant muttered to himself.","\"Everyone step aside.\" This meant someone was going to kick the door down.","The innkeeper wasn't too pleased, but seeing his brother's resolute expression and noting that the person beside him was dressed unlike an ordinary civilian, he had to swallow his words of refusal.","Bang!","The door took a tremendously forceful kick. The rather thin latch inside was sent flying, and the two door panels burst open abruptly.","A gust of cold wind suddenly blew in, like a giant, invisible hand ruthlessly plucking at the nerves of the men present.","This guest room wasn't large, with no separation between an inner and outer chamber. Standing at the doorway, one could directly see the bed inside.","And at this moment, everyone clearly saw a blanket twisted into a rope, with one end tied to the bedpost and the other stretching toward the wide-open window.","Two figures dashed forward simultaneously, rushing to the window and sticking their heads out to look.","Outside the window, the unraveled blanket fluttered in the wind. The alley below was completely empty, with not a single shadow of a person in sight.","\"It's definitely her! She was in the room just now!\"","\"She hasn't been gone long, she absolutely couldn't have gone far.\"","Someone vaulted over the window sill with a swift push of their hands, grabbed the blanket rope, and slid down with a whoosh. In the blink of an eye, their feet hit the ground.","The alley had two ends. The man first sprinted toward the end leading to the main street, but the pedestrians on the street all looked perfectly normal, and he didn't see anyone running. He then doubled back to check the other end.","The other end connected to more alleys. Let alone a person, there wasn't even the shadow of a flying bird.","Upstairs.","The innkeeper's older brother was interrogating the young servant. \"What kind of clothes was that lady wearing at the time? What did she look like? Tell me quickly.\"","The young servant stammered, \"Just... just the attire of an ordinary woman. Her face was dark, and she had quite a few black moles on it. She had a habit of keeping her head down, so I didn't see too clearly.\"","...","Dai Li had already slipped away two streets over, but the invisible boulder pressing on her chest remained entirely unmoved, still suffocating her.","They had caught up to her; this entire area was unsafe.","Yesterday, she had gone to many places and wandered through most of Xia Valley. Now, having left that area, she wouldn't be stumbling around blindly like a headless fly.","After walking continuously for three streets and confirming she had put a good distance between herself and the inn, Dai Li turned and entered an eatery.","This eatery only had one floor and no private rooms; all the diners ate in the main hall. As it was well past the usual mealtime, there were only a handful of people inside, just a sparse scattering of patrons.","Dai Li didn't deliberately choose the darkest corner, but she did sit near a corner with her back facing the entrance.","After ordering a bowl of noodle soup, Dai Li began to ponder her next move. The biggest problem right now was her travel document. Reaching into her pocket, she pulled out a wooden tablet and looked down at it.","Name: He Hua","Dai Li stared at these two words for a long time, and suddenly, the corners of her mouth slowly curled up.","She had it!!","\"Lady, your noodle soup is here.\" The servant brought over the noodle soup.","With the path ahead much clearer, and given that Dai Li was indeed hungry, she ate this meal with exceptional relish, even ordering an extra serving of sesame flatbread afterward.","After finishing her lunch, Dai Li didn't head outside but instead walked toward the eatery's kitchen. The kitchen was located in the backyard, an area that was logically off-limits to idlers. Just like right now, the servant stopped Dai Li.","\"Please stop here, lady. That's the kitchen over there, it's not open to the public,\" the young servant said.","Dai Li replied, \"I don't intend to go into your esteemed establishment's kitchen to cause trouble. I only wish to borrow one item for a minor use. I won't use it for free; I'll borrow it for fifteen minutes and offer you ten coins in return. How about it?\"","Fifteen minutes, ten coins.","The servant was completely dumbfounded. He worked hard all day in the shop to earn twenty-five coins, and this single offer was nearly half a day's wages for him.","\"What item do you wish to borrow, lady?\" the servant hurriedly asked.","Dai Li smiled and said, \"A knife. I'd like to borrow a small knife from your shop.\"","Just saying it wasn't enough. She took a handful of silver coins from her coin purse. \"I wonder if you could do me this small favor? I will stay right here in the shop and won't take it away. In fifteen minutes, I will definitely return it in perfect condition.\"","The servant stared at the money in her hand, his mind racing. Ten coins. He could keep half and give the other half to Cook Liu, who would most likely be willing to lend the knife.","\"Alright, please wait a moment, lady,\" the servant agreed.","Soon, he returned with a small knife. \"Will this one do?\"","Dai Li handed him the money and took the knife. \"It is perfect. Thank you.\"","Returning to the main hall, Dai Li sat in a corner this time, her back still facing the entrance.","With the knife in one hand and the small wooden plaque in the other, she deliberately tucked the back half of the plaque into her sleeve, exposing only the section with the name.","Then, Dai Li got to work.","The name was He Hua. She planned to add a grass radical to the top of the character He, changing it to the word for lotus.","The character Hua was difficult to alter, so Dai Li simply left it alone and instead added an extra character at the end. Her physical strength was limited, and she could not wield the knife for long, so she chose a very simple character: just the word for scholar.","New name: Lotus Scholar.","The name sounded rather strange, but there were plenty of peculiar names in this era. Given her limited resources, she had no other choice but to make do with it.","Dai Li was extremely cautious while altering and adding the characters. In this era, the regulation of travel passes was very strict. Those caught peddling forged passes would, at best, be beheaded on the spot; at worst, they would suffer severe physical torture before being sent to meet the King of Hell.","Of course, forged passes were not easy to create anyway. The official seals stamped on them were complex and meticulous, not something that could be casually faked.","She had said she would borrow the knife for a quarter of an hour, and exactly a quarter of an hour it was.","A quarter of an hour later, Dai Li returned the knife. She then rubbed black ointment into the scratches, seamlessly forming the new handwriting.","Mission accomplished!","Dai Li relaxed her brows in relief.","They knew she was in the Xia Valley, so the ferry crossings and the various city gates would certainly be guarded. Since that was the case, she might as well stay in the city for a while and wait for the heat to die down before leaving."]},{"number":77,"title":"Chapter 77","paragraphs":["On the Jin River, the wind slowed down, and consequently, the wind-powered ships also reduced their speed.","The gyrfalcon flew in from the west once more. After a slight shift of its sharp raptor eyes, it locked onto a room with an open window on the first floor of the tower ship.","Tilting its wings, the white and brown shadow descended from the sky like lightning.","With a whoosh, the falcon landed on the window sill. It let out a cry, then folded its wings, waiting for someone to approach.","In the main hall, several people who were brewing tea and chatting stopped simultaneously. Feng Feng, being closest to the window, took the initiative to go over and remove the small bamboo tube tied to the gyrfalcon's leg.","\"My Lord.\" Qin Shaozong took it from him.","Two days had passed since the last letter, and they were due to arrive in Tianshui Commandery in just one day. Unless there was a major incident, the other side wouldn't be sending letters so frequently.","Qin Shaozong pulled out the silk cloth from inside and unrolled it. Upon reading it, the man froze for a moment. Then, he couldn't help but chuckle softly, his laughter growing louder and louder.","His feelings at this moment were hard to describe. He felt invigorated, smug, relieved, and even harbored a touch of private schadenfreude that he couldn't share with others.","She had run away!","Back then, dissatisfied with him, she had managed to escape from his grasp. Now, evidently dissatisfied with them as well, she had successfully fled once again.","She always managed to make him see her in a new light.","Tianshui Commandery was located on the border of Yan and Si provinces. By heading east, she had left Si Province and returned to Yan Province.","She was moving closer to his direction!","However, as he read further down, the high, amused arc of Qin Shaozong's lips gradually flattened.","Xie Yuanxiu?","This Xie San had actually gotten involved, and even personally led a team across the border into Yan Province to search for her. Could this bastard have seen his wife before...","Qin Shaozong's hand slowly tightened, crumpling the silk cloth into a tight ball in his palm.","His emotional shifts while reading the letter were entirely too obvious. He had been joyous at first, but then his smile faded, and the aura around him became heavy and oppressive.","The surrounding military officers were astonished by this sight.","Ever since Madam Dai had gone missing, the Lord had been in a foul mood. Just now, the gloom had seemingly been swept away, only for his face to darken once again. Was the news sent back good or bad?","Mo Yanyun couldn't help but ask, \"My Lord, what does the letter say?\"","Qin Shaozong didn't answer him immediately. Instead, he loudly summoned a soldier from outside. \"Pass on my orders: turn around immediately and head to Xiagu. Also, tell Wei Qing's ship behind us not to change course with me. Have him take his men to Jiulu County and act according to the situation.\"","The tower ship had several levels and could actually carry quite a few soldiers. However, the northern soldiers were used to marching on land; their horsemanship was unmatched, but on the endlessly rolling rivers, they were full of distress.","Many soldiers simply couldn't handle being on a ship.","Besides the soldiers being unaccustomed to water travel, another issue was that the more people the tower ship carried, the heavier it became, causing it to sail much slower against the current.","Qin Shaozong couldn't wait, so for this trip, the men were divided among ten ships, with each carrying no more than thirty people.","The guard received the order and went down.","The crowd was surprised. \"My Lord, are we not going to Tianshui Commandery anymore? Why is this?\"","\"Could it be that they relocated Madam Dai?\"","\"Or do they have an operation elsewhere, so they took Madam Dai away from Tianshui Commandery?\"","Listening to their varied guesses, Qin Shaozong's anger over learning that Xie San had personally led troops to catch her subsided slightly.","Well, every single one of them had guessed wrong.","\"How could she be compared to an ordinary woman?\" Qin Shaozong chuckled.","The men looked at each other in dismay, truly unable to figure it out. \"Please enlighten us, My Lord.\"","Qin Shaozong smiled and said, \"Madam ran away while they were holding a ceremony. She left Tianshui Commandery all alone. Right now, she might be in Xiagu, or she might be in Jiulu County.\"","Everyone was dumbfounded.","Ran... she ran away?!","After the initial shock, they couldn't help but sigh in admiration in their hearts. As expected of Madam Dai, a true heroine among women!","Xiagu Commandery.","After forging her travel pass, Dai Li's courage grew. She brazenly took to the streets, changing her route to visit a fabric shop to buy herself some clothes.","There was no other way. She currently only had one outfit, and it was still the same set from Caoxiang.","The servant boy at the previous inn had seen her. The people pursuing her would definitely have the boy describe her appearance and clothing. She had to change her look again.","Dai Li didn't dare to go to a large silk shop, worried that looking out of place would only attract more attention. However, after arriving at a small fabric store, she encountered a new problem.","\"Miss, I only sell bolts of fabric here. We don't have ready-made outfits for sale,\" the fabric shop owner explained.","Buying just the fabric was cheaper. Commoners at the bottom of society all knew needlework and preferred to spend their money wisely. Ready-made clothes were much more expensive, not to mention that the seller wouldn't give you the leftover scraps of fabric once the clothes were made.","Dai Li looked disappointed and was about to go look elsewhere.","Seeing that she wanted to leave, the shopkeeper quickly said, \"But making ready-to-wear clothes isn't hard. I know a nimble seamstress, and her three daughters also have excellent embroidery skills. For a simple dress, if the mother and daughters work together to rush it, it can be finished in a day at most.\"","Dai Li was reluctant to wait that long; she wanted to buy ready-made clothes and change into them immediately.","So, she still took her leave of the fabric shopkeeper. But whether it was just her bad luck today, she visited four fabric shops in a row, and none of them sold ready-made clothes.","Dai Li stopped in her tracks. An indescribable feeling prevented her from going to look for another fabric shop.","She retraced her steps and returned to the first fabric shop. \"Shopkeeper, please introduce me to the seamstress you mentioned earlier.\"","The shopkeeper gave her an address, then said, \"Take the fabric to the East Street and look for Madam He. Tell her I recommended you, and she will definitely treat you as an honored guest and won't dare to neglect you. It's just...\"","At the end, the shopkeeper rubbed his hands together. \"Hiring Madam He will require an additional fee.\"","He was certain Dai Li would agree. After all, someone looking to buy ready-made clothes wouldn't be short on a few extra coins, right?","Dai Li nodded in agreement and headed towards the East Street carrying the fabric. Following the address, she successfully found the Madam He the shopkeeper had spoken of.","Three generations were crowded into the small house in the city's poorer quarters. The dwelling was very cramped, so Dai Li didn't go inside. She simply handed over the fabric and a deposit at the doorway, agreeing to come pick the dress up tomorrow.","After finishing this task, Dai Li went to look for another inn.","But she didn't know that shortly after she left the He residence, a group of men who had been sweeping through fabric shops since morning arrived at the store where she had just bought her fabric.","\"...Yes, I've seen her. She left quite an impression.\"","Hearing that harboring a fugitive carried the same punishment, how could the shopkeeper dare to hide anything? He immediately spilled everything like beans from a pod. \"That young lady was in a hurry to buy ready-made clothes. At first, seeing that I didn't have any, she left. About three-quarters of an hour later, she came back. I'm guessing she couldn't find any elsewhere, so she finally decided to seek out the seamstress I recommended.\"","\"What is the name of the seamstress you recommended, and where does she live?\"","The shopkeeper said, \"Madam He on the East Street. She has three daughters. Your honors just need to go to the East Street and ask.\"","After saying this, the shopkeeper asked cautiously, \"May I ask what crime that lady committed? She looked quite ordinary to me, no different from a regular woman.\"","The leader scolded, \"Just cooperate honestly. Why do you have so many questions?\"","This group of men came quickly and left in a hurry. Not long after, the door of Madam He's house was knocked on once again.","At the same time, several teams went to various hostels, inspecting their registration books one by one. The commotion was quite large, and it eventually alarmed the Grand Administrator of Xiagu.","However, just as this Grand Administrator Gao realized that someone was making trouble in his territory and felt displeased, a servant came to report that a distinguished guest had arrived to visit.","\"A distinguished guest? Where is he from?\" Gao You lazily held his wine cup.","The servant replied, \"He is the third son of the Inspector of Sizhou, Third Young Master Xie.\"","Gao You paused, sucked in a sharp breath of cold air, and his expression turned solemn.","It was true that Xiagu, under his jurisdiction, belonged to Yanzhou, but it was located to the west, not too far from Sizhou. The transition of power in Sizhou was closely watched by a multitude of prominent and wealthy families, and Gao You was among them.","Now that the most likely successor to Sizhou had come to his door, he naturally could not turn him away. He had to see what the other party's intentions were.","\"Entertain him well. I will go over after I change my clothes.\"","...","Outsiders had no way of knowing what transpired in the Gao Residence. Many people only knew that a large number of city guards were mobilized in the afternoon, joining forces with several other teams to rush to the various hostels in the commandery.","At the same time, the city's military patrols posted notices in bustling markets all over, claiming that a female thief had recently entered the city and ordering the commoners not to take in any outsiders.","Just posting notices was not enough. The military patrols went in batches to several major gathering places for commoners, which were the urban villages, and spread the word alley by alley.","Xie Yuanxiu walked out of the Gao Residence, took the horse led by his subordinate, and rode to a mansion.","The exterior of this mansion was simple and unadorned, but the inside was extraordinary. Xie Yuanxiu quietly took in his surroundings, thinking to himself that the foundation of the Green Lotus Cult was truly profoundly deep.","They had been in Xiagu for less than twenty-four hours, yet Diting had already managed to secure such a decent residence.","He walked to the door of the main hall and heard a hearty laugh coming from inside. It was Diting smiling and saying \"perfect.\" When he entered, he happened to see a person retreating.","Presumably, that person had just reported some good news.","The moment Xie Yuanxiu thought about how he could get intimate with that beautiful woman as soon as they found her, it felt as though a fire was burning in his heart. He did not even bother to tell Diting about what had just happened and directly asked, \"Is there any news of her?\"","Diting wore a silver-white mask when outside. The mask covered his face down to his upper lip. Hearing this, he curled his handsome lips. \"Indeed there is, and it is good news.\"","But he did not say it directly. Instead, he asked, \"How did Third Young Master's discussion with Prefect Gao go?\"","This was not what Xie Yuanxiu wanted to hear. After a brief reply of \"Not bad, he was very cooperative,\" he hurriedly brought the topic back. \"What good news? Do you know her hiding place? It is getting dark now, and there is no time to delay. We should hurry and invite the Honored Sister to return home.\"","\"Her hiding place is unknown,\" someone suddenly said.","It was still that unpleasant, hoarse voice. Xie Yuanxiu frowned in repulsion, his excitement once again extinguished by a basin of cold water.","He subconsciously turned his head and saw that black figure again. The person was dressed entirely in black and wore a black mask, looking as if he had blended into the gradually darkening sky outside the window.","Even though he had interacted with quite a few cult members, Xie Yuanxiu just found this person to be an eyesore no matter how he looked at him. Furthermore, he could also sense a hidden hostility from the other party.","He had never even met this person before, right? It was truly baffling.","Xie Yuanxiu's excitement was mostly gone. \"Since the Honored Sister's whereabouts are temporarily unknown, what could possibly be considered good news?\"","Diting said, \"She visited a fabric shop, attempting to buy ready-made clothes there. However, the shop did not sell ready-made clothes, so the shopkeeper only sold her some fabric.\"","\"How is this good news?\" Xie Yuanxiu asked anxiously.","Diting smiled and continued, \"Seeing that she was in a hurry to get clothes, the shopkeeper recommended a seamstress on the East Street to her. We sent someone to that seamstress's house and learned that she had arranged to pick up the clothes at the beginning of the You hour tomorrow. With this, does Third Young Master still think it is not good news?\"","Xie Yuanxiu was slightly stunned, and then he was filled with wild joy.","Pick up the clothes at the beginning of the You hour tomorrow?","Since the appointment had been made, as long as they sat and waited for her to walk right into their trap, they would definitely be able to catch her!","...","While the search for her outside was intensifying, Daili had already checked into a hostel.","Yes, she was still staying in a hostel today.","Compared to the one from yesterday, she had specifically chosen a larger one with a better environment today.","Since she was using the name Lotus Scholar anyway, she figured that those people who did things by the book would not be able to wrap their heads around it anytime soon.","Dusk had passed, and the sky was covered with a hazy, dim color. Daili sat by the window, opened it slightly, and observed the main street from the inside.","Pedestrians came and went on the street. There was no shortage of armored soldiers, as well as some people wearing ordinary clothes who would converse with the soldiers.","Those people were dressed differently; some looked ordinary, while others appeared wealthy. They were clearly not from the same family.","Daili looked thoughtful.","Were they cult members? From the looks of it, there were quite a lot of cult members in this Xiagu Commandery.","Daili gently closed the window and returned to lie down on the bed. A single set of clothes was difficult to wash and change out of, so she had to prepare new clothes.","After she went to Seamstress He's place to pick up the clothes tomorrow, she would not go out for the next few days.","Daili lay on the bed and closed her eyes, falling asleep without realizing it. Her sleep quality was usually very good, but tonight she was plagued by endless nightmares.","She kept dreaming that she was caught by the Green Lotus Cult, subsequently locked up, and could never see Zhouzhou again.","Daili woke up with a start in the middle of the night. When she fell back asleep later, she actually had the same kind of dream again. As a result, she woke up the next day feeling listless and did not feel better until the afternoon.","Today, she had an appointment with Seamstress He to pick up the clothes at the beginning of the You hour. Daili did not leave the hostel until nearing the end of the Shen hour.","Seamstress He lived on the East Street, while Daili was on the West Street. They were exactly in two different directions, and it would take about three quarters of an hour to walk there.","Soldiers could still be seen hurrying along the main street, and some pedestrians were discussing the notices in the city.","Daili's footsteps grew slower and slower, and finally, she stopped as she approached the East Street.","Notices had been posted in the city, and the fact that a female thief had entered the city was well known to many people. It was hard to guarantee that Seamstress He had not heard about it. Just like back in the Taiping Commandery, she had stayed at Madam Lin's house, thinking it was absolutely safe, but she was still caught by Qin Shaozong.","She could not go directly.","Daili looked up at the sky. Dusk had arrived. Today's sunset glow was very beautiful, like an unfurled oil painting.","There were a few young children playing with mud at the entrance of the alley, muttering childish words. Daili looked at those children, a gleam of shrewdness flashing in her eyes.","She walked toward them.","...","Knock, knock. The sound of someone knocking on the door came from outside.","Seamstress He's whole body shuddered. She subconsciously turned her head to look at the man beside her, cowering and extremely timid. \"Noble sir, she is here.\"","Xie Yuanxiu stared intently at the door. The shocking fanaticism in his eyes made Seamstress He's blood run cold. \"Go open the door and invite her in.\"","Seamstress He did not dare to disobey.","Creak. The door opened.","However, the expected figure was not outside the door. There were only three little kids standing at her doorway.","\"Madam He, we are here to pick up the clothes ordered yesterday. Here is the final payment for you. Please bring the clothes,\" the three children said in unison.","The sweet, childish voice sounded incredibly endearing. Yet, to Xie Yuanxiu, it felt like stepping off a sheer cliff. His hopes were suddenly dashed, and the immense disappointment caused his normally handsome face to contort.","\"Where is she?!\" Xie Yuanxiu demanded, striding toward the exit.","The few children were frightened by his imposing aura, stammering and too intimidated to speak.","Seeing this, an embroideress hidden in another part of the alley hurried over and crouched down. As a woman, her deliberate use of a gentle tone worked wonders in soothing them.","After just a few words, the children, who had been shivering like quails moments ago, finally calmed down.","The embroideress quickly asked, \"Who sent you here? Where is that person now?\"","\"It was a tall lady with a very pretty voice.\"","\"She said she wanted us to do her a small favor and help her fetch some clothes.\"","\"She also said she'd treat us to sesame flatbreads once we were done. Yes, sesame flatbreads! I'm planning to eat two!\"","Chiming in one after another, the three children explained the gist of what had happened.","The embroideress thought to herself that the woman was truly cautious, actually sending little pawns to test the waters first. She looked up at Xie Yuanxiu. \"Third Young Master, why don't we play along for now and let them take the clothes back?\"","Xie Yuanxiu had recovered from his immense disappointment and was invigorated once more. \"Yes, play along! Playing along is a great idea!\"","...","Dai Li stood at the alley entrance, gazing at the entrance to East Street in the distance. Shortly after, she saw three small figures walk out, the middle one carrying a sack.","Dai Li's gaze shifted behind them. She noticed that after the three children emerged, a woman also walked out of the alley.","The woman was short and dressed in ordinary clothes, carrying a basket on her arm. There was no one else behind her.","Dai Li watched the woman for a moment. Seeing that she was simply walking forward without looking around, Dai Li figured she was most likely just an ordinary passerby.","Suddenly, the woman looked over, and their eyes met across the distance.","A sudden chill shot straight to the top of her head. Dai Li couldn't explain why, but alarm bells violently rang in her mind. Before she could even process the thought, her body reacted faster than her mind, shrinking back into the alley.","\"She's over there!\"","\"Quick, after her!\"","Someone shouted loudly from not far away.","Dai Li's mind buzzed, and she instinctively took off running deeper into the alley. This alley had many forks, and having been here before, she was relatively familiar with the terrain. She should be able to shake them off here.","After taking two consecutive turns, just as Dai Li was about to veer into the lower end of a Y-shaped fork, a figure suddenly darted out from her rear flank—from an even narrower adjacent alley.","The person grabbed Dai Li's arm with one hand and covered her mouth with the other, dragging her into the narrow alley.","Dai Li's pupils shrank in sheer terror. Just as she opened her mouth to bite the hand and simultaneously bent her elbow to strike backward, she suddenly heard—","\"Mama, please don't move, and don't make a sound.\""]},{"number":78,"title":"Chapter 78","paragraphs":["Dai Li froze, thinking she was hearing things. She whipped her head around to look behind her.","Dusk was drawing to a close, its lingering afterglow swallowed layer by layer by the encroaching darkness. As the daylight faded from bright to dim, the outlines of people and objects blurred. The face of the young man standing behind her was mostly shrouded in shadows, but this could not dampen Dai Li's joy.","Zhouzhou!","Qin Yanzhou pulled Dai Li further into the alley. In just a few steps, they reached a cluttered area where a household stored their miscellaneous items. Dai Li guessed its purpose simply because a back door stood right beside it.","The clutter was piled high and in disarray, a jumble of everything imaginable. There were worn-out flat bamboo baskets and a broken vat with a large hole punched through its bottom.","The vat was quite large, standing about half a meter tall, and to Dai Li's pleasant surprise, it was completely empty inside. Feeling a sudden tightening around her waist followed by a swift release, Dai Li found herself deposited inside the vat.","She tried crouching down and discovered that the space inside was just enough to fit an adult woman, as if it had been tailor-made for her.","\"Mother, please bear with hiding in here for a while. I will come back for you later.\" Qin Yanzhou pulled out a piece of sackcloth from who knows where.","With a flick of his wrist, he tossed the sackcloth over the broken vat, covering it. Then, using the rim of the vat for support, he casually draped two pieces of firewood over the top.","After finishing all this, Qin Yanzhou dug out a mask, put it on, and swiftly walked toward the mouth of the alley. Just as he reached the entrance, he ran right into the pursuing guards.","The pursuer hurriedly skidded to a halt. Seeing him coming from this direction, the man concluded that the lady couldn't possibly have escaped down this path. \"Mingdeng, the target has appeared. She just turned into this area.\"","Qin Yanzhou's voice was calm. \"I came from this way and did not spot her.\"","The man did not doubt his words in the slightest; after all, the other's rank was much higher than his own. However, subconsciously, his gaze still drifted past Qin Yanzhou to look at the alley behind him.","It was empty behind him, save for some miscellaneous clutter piled up in the alley.","The houses of commoners were all very cramped, no bigger than the palm of a hand. Being poor, they naturally cherished their belongings, reluctant to throw this or that away. Over time, not only would their homes be filled to the brim, but some of the junk would also spill out and be piled up by their doors.","Many people were already accustomed to this sight.","Qin Yanzhou said, \"She likely went that way. If we fail to catch her this time, she will definitely return to her hiding place from yesterday. Go and inform the Third Young Master, and tell him to guard the exits over there.\"","Three other men were following behind that person. After he went back to deliver the message, the other three charged toward the lower end of the Y-shaped alley.","Once this group left, Qin Yanzhou pondered for a moment before turning around and walking toward the other end of the alley. The other end was also a fork in the road, leading in more than one direction. He similarly turned back another group of pursuers there.","With him maneuvering back and forth, surprisingly, no one else walked down this stretch of the alley for quite a long time.","Hiding in the broken vat, Dai Li heard the footsteps pacing back and forth, and faintly caught the sound of voices.","Her heart pounded violently in her chest, thump, thump, thump. Her head grew hot and her blood raced. She felt as though she could hear the rushing of her own blood, yet her hands and feet were icy cold.","Mingdeng?","Those people called Zhouzhou Mingdeng. They seemed to be very familiar with him.","No, not just seemed, they were definitely very familiar. Zhouzhou was able to make the other party obey him without question, even turning away a whole wave of people with just a single sentence.","Dai Li recalled what her son had once told her: when he first arrived in this alternate world, he was saved by a wealthy family. Later, they encountered bandits and he was accidentally separated from them. He was then taken in by Fan Tianshi, which was how he became the adopted son of that man surnamed Fan.","In his sixth year at the Fan Manor, he reunited with the wealthy family that had initially saved him, and for the following year, he worked for them...","A truth gradually surfacing in her mind made Dai Li clench her jaw tightly.","The wealthy family her son had spoken of was the Green Lotus Cult.","During that great famine nine years ago, Zhouzhou had spent his time within the Green Lotus Cult. He had stayed with them for at least two years.","Two years, plus the entirety of last year, made three years in total. Was three years really enough time for Zhouzhou to climb to a position where he could casually command other cult members?","Especially considering that he was still young during those first two years, and by the final year, he was already Fan Tianshi's adopted son, spending most of his time at the Fan Manor.","Although she didn't want to admit it, at this moment, Dai Li could not help but suspect that her son had not told her the truth before.","She felt anxious and terrified, along with an unspeakable sense of unease.","It was pitch black before her eyes. The footsteps outside faded away, sounding as if everyone had left the area. Yet, Dai Li remained absolutely still. Keeping in mind her son's promise to return, she did not dare to get up on her own.","She didn't know how much time had passed, perhaps fifteen minutes, perhaps half an hour, when the sound of footsteps approached again.","Someone hurried past, and a few words drifted over:","\"She's not here either. Could that person really have escaped?\"","\"Most likely. Besides, the curfew has already started; it's highly unlikely she's still wandering outside.\"","\"Sigh, that's going to be troublesome. After today, she'll definitely lock herself indoors. Let's go, we'll take a quick look at the alley entrance over there...\"","The voices faded into the distance.","Dai Li rejoiced that she hadn't gone out. Otherwise, if they had doubled back, she would have been caught red-handed.","Then came another agonizingly long wait, until Dai Li's taut nerves slowly began to relax, and she even started to feel drowsy leaning against the inside of the vat.","\"Creaaak.\"","The sound of wooden door hinges turning was exceptionally clear in the dead of night. Dai Li jumped in fright. Before she could figure out where the noise came from, she heard people whispering.","\"Those patrol guards seem to have all left.\"","\"It's curfew, of course they have to withdraw. But things have been a bit unsettled lately. Huh, why is there an extra vat by the door? Old Li, when did you get this?\"","\"It wasn't me. I was out running my stall during the day, where would I find the time to pick things up and bring them back?\"","\"This vat is quite big, it's a good find! Hurry up and move it inside.\"","\"You foolish woman, your eyes really are failing you. The bottom of this vat has several large holes broken through it, and the sides are cracked too. It can't hold water at all, what's so good about it? Someone probably just left it by our door temporarily. Let's take a closer look tomorrow, there's no rush. If the patrol guards come back and see us outside, we'll be in big trouble.\"","\"Sigh, you're right. Let's go back inside first.\"","\"Creaaak.\" The door closed.","Hiding inside the vat, Dai Li broke out in a cold sweat from the scare.","If that man and woman had actually tried to lift the vat, she would have been exposed in an instant.","After that little episode, Dai Li didn't dare to fall asleep again. It felt as if a long time had passed, yet also like only a brief moment, before she heard footsteps once more.","The approaching footsteps were very light, like a cat's. By the time Dai Li confirmed she wasn't hearing things, there was movement above her head.","The items casually pressing down on top were moved aside, the sackcloth was lifted, and scattered moonlight spilled into the vat.","\"Mother...\"","The young man, his face fraught with tension, helped Dai Li out.","Having sat with her knees bent for so long, Dai Li's legs had gone numb. But compared to her legs, there was a much more pressing issue right in front of them...","And that was where they were going to stay for the night.","With military guards patrolling the city outside and the heavy dew of the deep night, it was impossible to stay outdoors for the entire night.","Regarding a place to stay, Dai Li had an idea. \"Zhouzhou, I booked a private room at the Shengyang Inn on West Street. I used a travel pass with an altered name to check in. The room is on the second floor, and the window facing the alley isn't closed tightly. It wouldn't be impossible to climb the wall and get back in tonight.\"","Qin Yanzhou was clearly stunned for a moment, then whispered, \"I'm sorry, Mom.\"","It was all because of the Green Lotus Cult that his mother had to hide here and there.","\"Why are you apologizing, silly child? You're not their leader. It's not like you can make them all listen to you, right? Don't take everything upon yourself,\" Dai Li sighed.","Qin Yanzhou said, \"The cult once assigned me an old residence. There are only two servants looking after the house. You can rest there tonight.\"","Dai Li asked him, \"Are those two guarding servants cult members?\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded affirmatively, but then added, \"Those two are the most fringe figures. I've interacted with them a few times; they obey my every word and have always stayed in Xiagu Commandery. They normally don't have contact with anyone else in the cult. I'll just tell them that you are also a follower of the cult and need to stay in seclusion due to a secret mission. They certainly won't be suspicious.\"","Dai Li understood.","This was infiltrating the inside disguised as a cult member—hiding in plain sight right under their noses.","This was a very good proposal. By then, even if they turned the world upside down and wracked their brains, they probably wouldn't imagine she was hiding right inside a Green Lotus Cult house.","There was just one thing...","\"Your proposal is great, but it's too late right now. Going over at this hour would draw too much attention. After all, there are wanted posters all over the city. I'm worried they might get suspicious. It's better to go tomorrow,\" Dai Li said cautiously.","Better safe than sorry.","Her mother-son relationship with Zhouzhou seemed to be known only to the higher-ups in the Northern Territory. She had to keep this tightly under wraps, otherwise she and Zhouzhou would become each other's weaknesses.","Qin Yanzhou listened to Dai Li; whatever she said, went.","Dai Li followed her son away from East Street. Along the way, Qin Yanzhou scouted the path, accurately avoiding all the patrolling guards.","When they arrived at the back street of the inn, Qin Yanzhou said to Dai Li, \"Mom, I'll go take a look first.\"","Dai Li nodded.","In the mere time it took her to nod, she saw the young man who was just standing on the ground leap up. With a raise of his hand, he grabbed onto a slight protrusion on the wall, then did a pull-up using only his arm strength. Pushing off the wall with his feet, his whole body shot up another stretch.","In the blink of an eye, her son, who had just been in front of her, was already up there, poking his head out the window to look at her.","Eyes wide open, Dai Li was speechless: \"...\"","Qin Yanzhou first went to bolt the door, then rummaged through the cabinet for a quilt. After that, he did something somewhat similar to what Dai Li had done before, tossing the quilt down. He didn't tie it directly to the bedpost, because if he did, it wouldn't be long enough.","Dai Li couldn't fly or leap over walls, nor could she do a pull-up, but she still managed to get upstairs in the end.","She went up sitting on a human-powered sling chair.","A tiny oil lamp was lit in the room. The light was very dim, and the surroundings were completely quiet. Dai Li didn't even dare to speak loudly. \"Zhouzhou, do you still have to go back tonight? If you can avoid it, then don't go back.\"","The conditions of this inn were better than the previous one. There was a small couch inside, along with two quilts, perfectly fine for two people to sleep.","But Qin Yanzhou shook his head. \"I have to make a trip back.\"","Dai Li felt disappointed but knew he probably had no choice. \"Alright then, be careful. I won't go out all day tomorrow and will wait for your arrangements.\"","After bidding his mother goodnight, Qin Yanzhou vaulted out the window with a push of his hands.","Dai Li was startled by him and rushed to the window in a few steps. But when she looked down, the quiet alley, faintly illuminated by the moonlight, was completely empty. There was no sign of him at all.","\"This child really is...\"","*","The morning sun rose, and the eastern sky brightened.","The night before last, Dai Li had nightmares all night about being caught, so she hadn't slept well. Last night, although she unexpectedly reunited with her son and they made a rough plan, she still hadn't slept well.","Zhouzhou was a member of the Green Lotus Cult.","Religious organizations were not something you could just leave when you wanted to, especially since her son seemed to have worked his way up from the bottom.","Once reaching a certain level, one would inevitably come into contact with some secrets. If people could come and go as they pleased, the cult would definitely be in chaos. It was hard to say what methods they had to control their members.","Dai Li tossed and turned, and even when she finally fell asleep, she didn't sleep soundly. When she woke up the next day, she had rare dark circles under her eyes.","Not wanting to go downstairs for breakfast, Dai Li spent a few copper coins to have a young servant bring it up. After eating breakfast, Dai Li caught up on her sleep, waiting until around three in the afternoon before Qin Yanzhou finally arrived.","\"Mom, come with me.\" The young man looked a bit anxious.","Dai Li only had one backpack for luggage. She grabbed it and went. \"What's wrong? Are they searching this way?\"","Qin Yanzhou said, \"The hunt for the wanted female thief has swept across the entire Xiagu City, but there's been no movement among the commoner followers. Diting believes you are still hiding in an inn. Today, he ordered an expansion of the search scope. Any woman who used a travel pass with a surname sounding like 'He' to check into an inn must be strictly investigated. They are on their way here; we can't stay in this place.\"","Dai Li gasped.","It seemed the other party had thought of the possibility that she might have altered the name on her travel pass.","Slinging her small bag over one shoulder, Dai Li followed Qin Yanzhou out of the inn. Qin Yanzhou wore a black mask outside. Dai Li didn't walk side by side with him, but trailed a short distance behind, so as to be less conspicuous.","She walked casually down the main road. Along the way, they encountered a few squads of patrolling guards, but the guards were probably busy rushing to the inns, or perhaps they didn't expect her to be so brazen. In short, no one paid her any attention.","Leaving the main street and turning into an alley, the distance between Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou shortened a bit. The mother and son took several turns left and right until the young man in black finally stopped in front of a house.","Qin Yanzhou raised his hand and knocked on the door. Perhaps those inside had been informed beforehand, as the door opened as soon as he knocked.","The person who opened the door was an old man in his sixties, with grizzled hair and wearing linen clothes. Behind him stood a fifteen or sixteen-year-old boy, whose appearance was somewhat similar to the old man's. They looked like grandfather and grandson.","\"Greetings, Divine Envoy,\" the two said, both respectful and excited.","Qin Yanzhou's voice was cold. \"This is another Divine Envoy of the cult. Serve her carefully, and do not neglect her.\"","The grandfather and grandson knelt and kowtowed, repeatedly promising to do so.","A trace of complexity flashed through Dai Li's eyes.","Qin Yanzhou seemed to have other matters to attend to. He didn't stay long. After bringing Dai Li here, he left in a hurry, leaving the mother and son with hardly any time to speak.","This old residence was a single-courtyard house shaped like the character 'Pin'. It didn't take up much space, but although the sparrow is small, it has all the vital organs—it had everything it needed.","Dai Li settled down here.","*","\"Why hasn't she been found yet? Could she have grown wings and flown away?\" Xie Yuanxiu was extremely frustrated.","The inns and residential houses in the city were all being searched. The former was spearheaded by the military patrols, undergoing a complete carpet search; as for the latter, the followers acted upon the news, conducting investigations in secret.","Yet, after such a long time had passed, they still hadn't found her.","No, it could not be said that they had not found her at all. She had shown her face; they had simply lost her trail.","A whole group of men mobilized together, yet they could not even catch a single woman.","Useless, they were all useless!","The messenger kept his head bowed, not daring to face the wrath of the future provincial governor.","Xie Yuanxiu paced back and forth across the main hall again. Seeing Diting still brewing tea, he could not help but say, \"We have already searched the county's inns twice. The second time, as you suggested, we even checked for similar-sounding names, but we still found absolutely nothing. Your esteemed sister is missing, yet as her younger brother, you are not the least bit anxious.\"","Diting tapped his fingers lightly against the low table, feeling equally puzzled in his heart.","He had thought she would stay at an inn, but now they had come up empty-handed.","Could it be that she was not at an inn?","But if she was not at an inn, where could she be? At a critical juncture like this, with wanted posters plastered all over the city, who would dare take her in...","\"Xiagu is not a small place. Perhaps there are other areas we have overlooked. Let us wait and see,\" Diting said.","His voice was calm and unhurried. Hearing this, Xie Yuanxiu's anger subsided slightly, thinking to himself that it made sense.","Let us wait and see; they were not short on time anyway.","Facing the warm sunlight, the burly soldiers deftly lowered the sails. The towering ships lost their wind power and slowed down. Several tower ships lined up in a single row, slowly pulling into the Xiagu ferry crossing.","The Xuanshui Ferry of Xiagu was never short of boats on any given day, but it was rare to see such uniformly built tower ships docking together. The fishermen and carriage drivers on the shore could not help but cast sidelong glances.","Bang, bang, bang—","Long wooden planks were thrown down from the ships, perfectly bridging the hulls and the shore. Under the stealthy gazes of the pedestrians at the crossing, a group of armor-clad brutes filed out from the ships with practiced ease.","Each of them was robust and heavily built, with blades hanging at their waists and eyes blazing like torches. They leaped from the ships to the shore without the slightest wobble, their stances incredibly steady. One look was enough to tell they were trained martial artists.","Qin Shaozong disembarked from the ship. The man looked up at the sky, his brown eyes narrowing slightly.","It was the beginning of the Shen hour. Entering the city and heading to the governor's manor in Xiagu at this time would be just right for dinner.","They could drink merrily and have a proper chat about the affairs of the city, both big and small."]},{"number":79,"title":"Chapter 79","paragraphs":["Gao Manor.","\"Master, a distinguished guest has arrived outside!\" A servant rushed inside, accidentally stumbling and practically rolling into the main courtyard.","At that time, Gao You was leisurely admiring a painting.","The painting was a gift from Third Young Master Xie, created by a great master of the previous dynasty. Very few authentic works of that master had survived to the present day, making it invaluable. Gao You, who loved calligraphy and paintings, treated it as a precious treasure, spending a great deal of time admiring it every day for the past two days.","Interrupted by the servant's hasty arrival, Gao You revealed a look of displeasure. But then, thinking of something, he quickly asked, \"Is it Third Young Master Xie again?\"","Last time, the other party borrowed the military patrol from him and thanked him with calligraphy and paintings. He wondered what he had brought this time.","It was almost mealtime; could he have brought fine wine?","Thinking of this, Gao You suddenly felt delighted and casually picked up the teacup beside him to take a sip.","\"It's not the Third Young Master, it's... the Marquis of Wu'an,\" the servant stammered.","\"Pfft—!\" Gao You spat out a mouthful of tea.","The tea splashed onto his precious masterpiece from the previous dynasty's great master. For a moment, he didn't know whether to mourn the ruined artwork first or panic over the possibility that he was hallucinating.","\"Who? Who did you just say came?\" Gao You's beard trembled.","The servant repeated, \"The Marquis of Wu'an, the Marquis of Wu'an from the North.\"","Gao You gasped loudly, \"Why is that god of death here?\"","The joint effort of the North and Qing Province to conquer Yan Province was closely watched by every governor and magistrate in the commanderies and counties of Yan Province. This battle would determine whether their highest superior would change; they had to pay attention!","With Bairi Pass serving as the frontline defense, they originally thought it would be a protracted war, taking three to four months at the shortest, or up to a year and a half at the longest to decide the victor.","Instead, no sooner had they received the news of the war breaking out than they were informed:","Bairi Pass had fallen!","Setting aside their emotional rollercoaster upon learning of Fan of Yanzhou's lightning-fast defeat, the officials of Yan Province all focused on what would happen next.","Yan Province changing hands meant that the officialdom on their side might be reshuffled.","\"Xiagu is in the western part of Yan Province. Why would the Marquis of Wu'an come here first? Could he have already settled everything in the east?\" Gao You muttered to himself. \"That shouldn't be possible, how could it be that fast?\"","He grumbled under his breath, but his hands moved swiftly to change his clothes. Once properly dressed, Gao You led his sons out to receive the guest.","\"...What? The Marquis of Wu'an is here? What is he doing in Xiagu!\" Xie Yuanxiu's expression changed drastically.","Qi Yu turned a deaf ear to Xie Yuanxiu's question and only said to Diting, \"The Marquis of Wu'an just arrived at the Shen hour and has now directly moved into the governor's manor with his men. Looking at his accompanying soldiers, they are all elites, numbering around two hundred.\"","Xie Yuanxiu silently repeated the number \"two hundred,\" and his heart gradually settled. He had brought four hundred men with him to Xiagu this time. In terms of troop numbers, he had the upper hand over the Marquis of Wu'an.","However, he was still puzzled. \"He dares to come with only over two hundred men? What exactly is he here for?\"","Up until now, Xie Yuanxiu still believed that Dai Li was Diting's biological sister, completely unaware of her relationship with Qin Shaozong.","There was also a round-faced man with squinty eyes in the room. This man's name in the cult was Fanyin. At this moment, Fanyin smiled and said, \"He is here for the same reason you are.\"","This matter could no longer be hidden, so it was better to tell Xie Yuanxiu now.","Xie Yuanxiu froze, taking a long while to recover his senses.","He wasn't stupid, and he was well-informed about the affairs of various provincial governors. Naturally, he knew that in recent months, the Marquis of Wu'an had a highly favored young woman by his side.","Could it be...","His gaze swept over the people in the room, from Diting sitting by the tea table, to the man dressed in black robes who always wore a black mask, then to the squinty-eyed Fanyin, and finally to Qi Yu. The latter slightly turned his head, avoiding Xie Yuanxiu's gaze.","Now, what else could Xie Yuanxiu not understand? \"Diting, she is not your elder sister?!\"","With the lie exposed, Diting showed no sign of panic. \"Whether she is or not is no longer important. What matters is that the Marquis of Wu'an has tracked us down, and we should think about what to do next.\"","Xie Yuanxiu gritted his teeth but was helpless. He could only ask, \"How did the Marquis of Wu'an find Xiagu? Who leaked the news to him? Is there a mole within the cult?\"","It was too fast. They had only been in Xiagu for a few days!","Moreover, Qin Shaozong didn't go to Tianshui Commandery in Si Province but came straight to Xiagu. He must have received information...","Questioning anything else was fine, but at Xie Yuanxiu's last sentence, Qi Yu couldn't hold back. \"Seven years ago, the Marquis of Wu'an planted a sleeper agent under Rong Bingzhou. Planting a mole in the core circle of another province was effortless for him, let alone just having eyes and ears to gather intel. He probably guessed that we were the ones who abducted Lady Dai, so he directly sent a message to his spies in Tianshui Commandery, ordering them to secretly observe our movements.\"","Qi Yu firmly believed that the cult was united as one. Rather than having an inside man, he was more inclined to believe that the Marquis of Wu'an's eyes and ears were spread all over Yan and Si provinces.","\"The Third Young Master's recent troop movements have been quite loud. Dividing the forces by boats and personally leading men to Xiagu, wouldn't that naturally draw their attention?\" Fanyin touched his chin from the side.","A hint of ruthlessness flashed in Xie Yuanxiu's eyes.","Saying this, were they pushing all the blame onto him?","But they didn't consider that if it weren't for their momentary negligence in watching over her, how could she have escaped?","\"Clack.\" A sudden noise broke the silence in the room.","The few people in the room paused and turned their heads to look at Diting sitting by the table. They saw that he had accidentally knocked over his teacup, and a small puddle of tea spilled onto the table.","Diting wore a silver-white mask, so Xie Yuanxiu couldn't see his expression, but his intuition told him that the other party must have been struck by some kind of emotional impact, otherwise, he wouldn't have accidentally knocked over the teacup.","Xie Yuanxiu was about to ask when he heard the other party ask in a calm tone, \"Xiagu belongs to Yan Province. Now that the Marquis of Wu'an has arrived, does the Third Young Master still want to continue?\"","Xie Yuanxiu froze, obviously a bit hesitant.","But thinking of the young woman he had seen in the back garden that day, it felt like a fire was burning in his heart, making it impossible for him to say the words \"forget it.\"","Moreover, if he backed down now, wouldn't it tell the world that he was terrified at the mere mention of the Marquis of Wu'an?","Even if the other party only brought a little over a hundred men this time...","The main hall fell silent, and everyone looked at Xie Yuanxiu.","The veins on Xie Yuanxiu's forehead throbbed and then subsided. \"The Marquis of Wu'an only brought a little over a hundred men, while I currently have hundreds of soldiers. He is the one who should be worried. I will send a message back to Si Province later and mobilize heavy troops overnight. If the Marquis of Wu'an dares to stay here any longer, I will make sure he never returns!\"","Diting said, \"There is no time to lose. Third Young Master, please hurry.\"","These words were true. Xie Yuanxiu immediately left the main hall and went back to write the letter.","After the only outsider left, Diting looked at Qin Yanzhou. \"Mingdeng, when you were in the Qin Manor, how did the Marquis of Wu'an treat you?\"","He didn't speak too plainly, but everyone present understood perfectly.","\"You suspect me,\" Qin Yanzhou's tone was unruffled. \"But what benefit would I gain from betraying the cult and working for him?\"","Diting picked up a brocade handkerchief from the desk and tossed it into a puddle of water. He did not formally declare it a betrayal, merely stating, \"This matter is rather bizarre. The Marquis of Wu'an arrived in Xiagu far too quickly.\"","Even if, as Qi Yu said, Qin Shaozong's spies were scattered throughout the Yan and Si provinces, or even taking a step back and assuming he knew they were the ones who had abducted Lady Dai...","How did the Marquis of Wu'an determine Lady Dai's exact location?","The Green Lotus Sect had countless strongholds. They could hide in Tianshui Commandery, where the grand ceremony was being held, or in their former headquarters in Huaian Commandery.","There were plenty of places. If he had no clues whatsoever, just confirming Lady Dai's whereabouts would have been enough to keep Qin Shaozong running around in circles for half a year.","Yet, of all places, he came straight to Xiagu!","Qin Yanzhou fell silent for a moment before simply admitting it. \"Looking back on it now, my departure back then was indeed a bit too easy. Perhaps his spies in Yanzhou had already discovered my true identity.\"","Diting took off the mask on his face and slapped it onto the desk. He pinched the bridge of his nose. \"Your share of the divine medicine for the next quarter is docked. Any further punishment will be decided by Uncle personally.\"","The young man remained silent, raising no objections.","\"Diting, should we retreat?\" Fanyin asked.","The Marquis of Wu'an had arrived, yet Lady Dai had still not been found. Once she heard the news, she would definitely take the initiative to contact the Marquis.","Once those two parties reunited, given the lessons learned from past mistakes, taking Lady Dai away again would be as difficult as ascending to the heavens.","Qi Yu whispered at this moment, \"I see that Third Young Master Xie is absolutely determined to get Lady Dai, and his military strength far exceeds that of the Marquis of Wu'an. It's still unknown whose hands the prize will ultimately fall into.\"","\"Xiagu belongs to Yanzhou,\" Qin Yanzhou said coldly out of the blue.","Diting's fingertips tapped rapidly against the desk a few times. \"Prepare for both scenarios. We can start making arrangements for the retreat.\"","Gao Manor.","Gao You's face had grown stiff from smiling. He was forcing a smile on the outside, but inside, he was suffering unspeakably.","Before him was the prospective Governor of Sizhou, and behind him was the Marquis of Wu'an. He was merely a lowly prefect, caught in the middle and pleasing no one.","It was a difficult situation, truly difficult.","But after weighing the options, he decided to temporarily lean towards the latter.","It was true that Xie San was the prospective Governor of Sizhou, and it was also true that he had brought troops and arrived menacingly. But at the end of the day, Xiagu belonged to Yanzhou.","What if, after some thought, Xie San decided not to provoke the Marquis of Wu'an and slipped away? What would happen to him then?","Xie San's headquarters wasn't here. He could run, but as the Prefect of Xiagu, Gao You was like a monk who could run away while his temple could not!","\"...Absolutely. Whatever the Lord Marquis commands, this humble official will certainly do his utmost.\" Gao You looked at Qin Shaozong seated above him, revealing a fearful and troubled expression, as if struggling with whether he should say something. \"It's just that there is one thing...\"","Qin Shaozong held his wine goblet and appropriately offered a prompt, \"Just what? Lord Prefect Gao, please speak freely.\"","\"I wouldn't dare hide it from you, Lord Marquis. A few days ago, that Third Young Master Xie from Sizhou came to find this humble official. His words, both explicit and implicit, were all asking me to dispatch the city patrols to find a young woman for him. At the time, I thought since we are neighbors, doing him a small favor would be no trouble at all, so I agreed. But today, hearing your description, Lord Marquis, I personally believe the person you are looking for is seventy or eighty percent similar to the 'lost favored concubine' Third Young Master Xie spoke of,\" Gao You said in a low voice.","He knew very well in his heart that it wasn't just \"seventy or eighty percent\" similar; it was highly likely the exact same woman.","But that wasn't important. What was important was that he needed to use this opportunity to explain his previous actions to the Marquis of Wu'an.","Ignorance is no crime. Previously, I didn't know the inside story, but now that I do, I am determined to abandon the darkness and turn to the light. You can't settle the previous score with me.","Qin Shaozong understood the underlying meaning of his words. He immediately smiled, swirled his wine goblet, and raised his cup to Gao You. \"You don't need to worry about this Xie San. This man won't be staying in Xiagu for much longer.\"","Gao You beamed with joy and hurriedly raised his goblet to drink with him. \"You are absolutely right.\"","As the local overlord of Xiagu Commandery, Gao You's choice of sides determined many things, such as the direction of the city patrols.","Although the patrols were still searching inns and civilian homes for people, it was obvious they were no longer taking orders from Xie Yuanxiu.","Invisible gunpowder smoke spread, and as a single spark was deliberately released, the raging flames exploded with a boom.","\"There's a perfectly good road, yet you insisted on bumping into me. I think you're tired of living.\" Mo Yanyun aimed at the leader of the opposing group, reached out, and shoved him when he was off guard, sending the man sprawling onto his back.","The other man quickly scrambled up, unable to bear the humiliation. \"You're awfully arrogant! The broad road is open to the sky, and we each walk on one side. It was clearly you who bumped into me!\"","\"Not only do you refuse to apologize after bumping into someone, but you're also standing here running your mouth! Brothers, let's show them what we're made of!\" Mo Yanyun was the first to draw his sword.","Seeing that the situation was turning bad, a peddler quickly picked up his carrying pole and slipped away. Pedestrians hurriedly dodged, clearing an open space for the two groups of men.","Swords flashed and shadows of blades danced; blood splattered. The scene instantly descended into total chaos.","On the second floor of a teahouse facing the street, a window was half open. Qin Shaozong stood by the window, looking down and taking in the chaos on the street.","The man's lips were curved, but that icy smile did not reach his eyes.","\"Lord Marquis, I have investigated thoroughly. In the three days since Xie San arrived in Xiagu with his troops, they, along with the city patrols, have searched every inn in the commandery, big and small. In addition, they have posted notices around the city looking for her and sent men to investigate the major commoner residential areas. They've done quite a lot, but they still haven't found any trace of Lady Dai,\" Feng Feng reported.","He was also quite baffled in his heart.","The inns had all been searched, the notices had been issued, and a massive amount of manpower and resources had been sent to search the commoner districts. Such a full combination of tactics had been executed, yet it surprisingly failed to make even a splash.","Could it be that Lady Dai was no longer in Xiagu?","\"She has always been good at hiding. Have someone spread the news that people from the North have arrived in Xiagu, had a very pleasant conversation with the Prefect of Xiagu, and are currently residing in the Prefect's Manor,\" Qin Shaozong said, twisting his thumb ring.","That fox had hidden herself; let's see if this could draw her out on her own.","Feng Feng received his orders and withdrew.","Qin Shaozong watched the chaotic streets, his gaze darkening.","Dai Li had been living in this small courtyard for a day now. It wasn't a long time, so she could endure it; she hadn't taken a single step out of her room. However, even though she hadn't gone out, she was somewhat aware of the commotion outside.","The search for her was still ongoing.","Dai Li would sometimes hear hurried footsteps passing by her door, and occasionally, phrases like \"You few, go ask over there; you guys are in charge of this area\" would drift in.","The houses in this \"urban village\" were built so close together that they were comparable to modern handshake buildings. Sometimes, she could even hear the neighbors talking.","Like right now...","\"It seems there's a new group of people in the city today.\"","\"You must have seen wrong. It's probably still the same ones from a few days ago, or maybe their reinforcements have arrived. Tsk tsk, this is a massive operation. I wonder what kind of female thief is worth having these government officials mobilize so many forces.\"","\"It's not the same group. When I went to the market to buy groceries today, I saw a fight break out. Someone's head was severed from their body, rolling far away, and blood spilled all over the ground.\"","\"A fight broke out? Why are they fighting amongst themselves?\"","\"I told you they weren't from the same group. I secretly kept an eye on them. The men doing the slashing were all clad in matching black armor. Every single one of them was incredibly burly; they looked like elite fighters. Taking on five men at once probably wouldn't be a problem for them. The other squad wasn't as imposing, but they made up for it with agility. Once they saw things going south, some of them sneaked off, probably to call for backup.\"","\"You actually dared to watch that kind of spectacle? Do you have a death wish?\"","\"What's there to be afraid of? They were focused on each other, and their blades were aimed precisely. It didn't look like they were going to take their anger out on innocent bystanders.\"","...","Dai Li stood by the wall, listening to the voices just on the other side, her brow twitching.","Another faction had arrived in the city, and they had even gotten into a conflict?","The previous group was undoubtedly from Sizhou and the Green Lotus Cult. But who could these newcomers be?","A tall, imposing silhouette inexplicably surfaced in Dai Li's mind.","The voices next door spoke up again:","\"Oh, right, I remember now. I heard the other group came from the North and has deep ties with Prefect Xia. They have all taken up residence in the Governor's Manor.\"","\"Oh man, with Prefect Xia covering for them, whoever picked a fight with them is going to suffer.\"","Just as I thought, Dai Li said to herself.","It really was Qin Shaozong...","She paced around the courtyard a few times. Finally, unable to hold back, she waved over the young boy. She was just about to speak when, out of the corner of her eye, she caught a glimpse of a dark figure suddenly vaulting over the wall from outside.","Even though it was broad daylight with the sun shining brightly, Dai Li was still startled. But once she got a clear look at the intruder, her heart instantly settled back into her chest, and joy lit up her face.","However, mindful of the other person in the courtyard, Dai Li could not bring herself to call out to her son directly.","Qin Yanzhou shot her a look, which she understood, and the two of them retreated into the room.","Once the door was closed, Qin Yanzhou kept it brief. \"Mom, the Marquis of Wu'an has tracked us down. He has won over the Prefect of Xiagu Commandery. Now, the city's military patrols and the soldiers he brought with him have merged into one force to deal with Xie San.\"","Dai Li knitted her delicate brows in thought, then suddenly her eyes lit up. \"Zhouzhou, so right now there are two opposing factions in the city, and it is completely chaotic outside, right?\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded in confirmation.","\"The chaos is just what we need! Zhouzhou, how about we take advantage of the mess and make our escape?\" Dai Li said excitedly."]},{"number":80,"title":"Chapter 80","paragraphs":["Leave Xiagu amidst the chaos!","Once this thought emerged, it grew wildly like weeds, quickly occupying Dai Li's entire mind.","It seemed there was no better time than now. When the snipe and the clam grapple, the fisherman profits. She was going to be the fisherman.","But there was another problem. Dai Li quickly glanced at the tightly shut door and lowered her voice by a notch, \"Zhou Zhou, can you leave the Green Lotus Sect freely?\"","Qin Yanzhou was still wearing his mask. Dai Li couldn't see his expression clearly, but she saw his eyes slowly lower.","Dai Li's heart skipped a beat.","Could it be...","Just as she wanted to ask in detail, the young man spoke, \"I can leave. If nothing unexpected happens, a major conflict will break out between the North and Sizhou soon. Mama, when that happens, we will leave amidst the chaos and head south to Yuzhou.\"","Dai Li felt a bit more reassured.","He could leave. Zhou Zhou would head south with her.","Dai Li asked, \"To Yuzhou? Is Yuzhou more peaceful? How does it compare to Chang'an?\"","As the capital of the dynasty, it should be much better than other places, otherwise where would the monarch's pride be?","However, with warlords dividing the land now, the ministers being strong and the ruler weak, it might indeed be true that some places were safer than Chang'an.","Qin Yanzhou explained, \"The Governor of Yuzhou is indecisive and content with his corner of the world. He has always had few conflicts with other provinces. He has a son who is skilled in both pen and sword, with extraordinary strength. Whenever there is an irreconcilable conflict with other warlords, this second legitimate son leads the troops into battle.\"","Dai Li understood. So this Governor of Yuzhou was a conservative peacemaker, but because he had a capable son, he wasn't considered a pushover.","He belonged to the type of \"I'm easy to talk to, but if you really bully me, I'm not powerless to fight back.\"","Dai Li: \"Alright, then we'll go to Yuzhou.\"","\"Mama, this is a human skin mask. I will teach you how to use it.\" Qin Yanzhou took out a small bag from his chest.","There were quite a few things in the bag. Dai Li recognized one of them: fish glue. She had always heard that fish glue was one of the raw materials for disguises, and now it seemed to be true.","Qin Yanzhou seemed very busy. He didn't stay long. After carefully teaching Dai Li how to use the human skin mask, he said, \"The next time I come to find you, it will be time for us to leave. Wait for me.\"","Dai Li agreed.","Qin Yanzhou left.","Dai Li sat on the chair, still holding the small cloth bag in her hand, feeling as if she had forgotten to say something.","She stared blankly at the small cloth bag for a moment, but still couldn't remember. Dai Li simply stopped thinking about it and earnestly fiddled with the fish glue in her hand.","Since she had decided to travel far, besides disguises, there were many other things to prepare.","Clothes, travel expenses, travel pass...","Right, the travel pass!","Although her travel pass had been altered, it still sounded identical to the surname \"He\". If she used this pass to exit the city gates, she might be stopped.","Dai Li fell into deep thought.","*","\"...This is going too far!\" Xie Yuanxiu kicked over the desk in front of him. His nostrils flared, and his eyes were bloodshot, clearly furious.","\"Please calm your anger, Third Young Master.\" A trusted confidant beside him tried to persuade him. \"The Marquis of Wu'an has been acting arrogantly for more than just a day or two. An arrogant army is bound to lose. He will eventually pay the price for his recklessness and flamboyance.\"","Xie Yuanxiu took a deep breath. \"You're right.\"","Turning his head, he asked his confidant again, \"How was the city patrol today?\"","The confidant hesitated for a moment before saying, \"Not very optimistic. Nine out of the ten squads encountered interceptions. It was all the people from the North deliberately picking fights. The remaining squad visited several major inns in the commandery again, searching according to Mr. Diting's new ideas, but still found nothing.\"","Xie Yuanxiu remained expressionless. \"What are the casualties?\"","The confidant: \"Ten dead, fifteen severely injured, and over thirty lightly injured.\"","Xie Yuanxiu clenched his fists tightly, his knuckles cracking loudly. \"Qin Shaozong!\"","\"Third Young Master, Mr. Diting has arrived,\" a servant came to report at this time.","It took Xie Yuanxiu a long while to rein in his anger.","When Diting entered, he saw Xie Yuanxiu standing in the main hall. The desk was overturned, teacups were shattered, and tea spilled all over the floor.","It was a complete mess.","Diting stopped in front of the pile of fragments. \"The summer days are scorching, and the weather is dry. It seems that even Third Young Master's anger is hard to extinguish. However, I have a fire-fighting plan. I wonder if Third Young Master would like to hear it.\"","Xie Yuanxiu's eyes lit up. \"What brilliant plan do you have, sir? Please speak. I am all ears.\"","Diting made a small joke, \"With the hall in such a mess, I'm afraid there's nowhere for Third Young Master to wash his ears.\"","Understanding the underlying meaning, Xie Yuanxiu said, \"This way, please. Let's go to the study to discuss in detail.\"","Inside the study.","After the servants served tea and withdrew, Xie Yuanxiu couldn't wait to ask, \"I wonder how you plan to put out the fire, sir?\"","\"The Marquis of Wu'an arrived in Xiagu the afternoon before yesterday. It's been over a day now. The time isn't very long, but it's enough for him to spread the news and let the whole city know that people from the North have arrived in Xiagu,\" Diting said.","Xie Yuanxiu, solely focused on hearing the brilliant plan, didn't think much of it. \"So what?\"","\"Haven't you noticed that she still hasn't made a move?\" Diting smiled.","It was as if a spring breeze brushed past Xie Yuanxiu, instantly sweeping away all his anxiety and lifting his spirits. \"You mean, she doesn't want to go back!\"","Indeed. If she were willing to go back, she would have returned to the Marquis of Wu'an's side the moment she heard the news. But now that the news had been spread for so long, there was still no movement.","She might not want to go back!","Diting brought up a past event. \"A few months ago, she met the Marquis of Wu'an in Nankang Commandery and was used by him to set up a trap to deceive the Prefect of Nankang Commandery. Dissatisfied with the Marquis of Wu'an, she used a small trick to shake off her personal maid and fled alone by boat to Taiping Commandery. And now, several months have passed. It seems the beauty's original intention remains unchanged.\"","Xie Yuanxiu suddenly felt physically and mentally relaxed, and a different kind of lofty aspiration arose within him.","He hadn't properly interacted with her, which was why she felt she had no other choice. If she experienced his goodness, she would definitely abandon the Marquis of Wu'an and choose him.","Diting continued, \"Right now, neither you nor the Marquis of Wu'an have heavily armed forces by your sides. Prefect Gao You is a key figure. We must win this person over.\"","Xie Yuanxiu frowned, however. \"That's easy to say, but easier said than done. Gao You is an official of Yanzhou. He will definitely obey the orders of the Marquis of Wu'an. Who can blame him, now that Yanzhou has changed owners.\"","\"Third Young Master is mistaken.\"","Diting smiled and said, \"Whether Yanzhou is surnamed 'Qin' or 'Nangong' is still undecided. The Marquis of Wu'an only brought about two hundred people with him on this trip to Xiagu. Who can deny that this isn't a good opportunity? As long as the Marquis of Wu'an dies, the North will fall into chaos. Qingzhou will definitely take advantage of the chaos to bite off a fat piece of meat from the North. By then, Qingzhou will probably only be able to take care of the eastern part of Yanzhou at most. As for the west...\"","\"The west will belong to Sizhou!\" Xie Yuanxiu said excitedly.","The boundaries of each province were set in the past, but in the current situation, who would dare to say it would always be so?","\"It is true that Gao You is the Prefect of Yanzhou and is temporarily taking orders from the Marquis of Wu'an. But has he ever thought about it? Yanzhou is only so big, and the number of commanderies and counties is fixed. The North and Qingzhou won't even have enough time to carve it up between themselves, so how could they leave a position for a mere Gao You?\" Diting said unhurriedly.","Xie Yuanxiu was taken aback, feeling enlightened.","Right, there were only so many important official positions, and they would definitely be replaced by their own people. Gao You, an 'old minister of the previous regime,' certainly didn't have many days left. Rather than sitting and waiting obediently to be replaced, it would be better to take a gamble!","\"Prefect Gao is currently just blinded by dark clouds and cannot see the future clearly. The Third Young Master invited him out to appeal to his emotions and reason with him. At worst, he can promise that if things don't work out, he will allow his entire family to move to Sizhou, and you can arrange another official position for him in Sizhou. I believe he will know what choice to make,\" Diting said.","Xie Yuanxiu was overjoyed. \"You are absolutely right, sir. I will send someone to deliver the message immediately.\"","Diting replied with a smile.","*","Teahouse, a private room on the second floor.","Compared to the Prefect's estate, the Gao Residence, the people of the North had recently preferred to discuss matters in the teahouse.","Situated in a bustling area, the teahouse offered a wide view overlooking the street. Not only did it help them avoid the eyes and ears within the Gao Residence, but it was also advantageous for observing the movements of the city's military patrols.","\"My Lord, there is still no news,\" Mo Yanyun said, his voice lowered.","The news had been released for over a day. Logically speaking, with Sizhou blatantly searching for someone beforehand, any change in the city's current atmosphere should have been enough to spark heated discussions among the commoners during their leisure time.","Many people were discussing it, and a large number were paying attention, yet there was absolutely no sign of Madam Dai.","Mo Yanyun secretly raised his eyes.","His superior stood by the window. The sunlight fell on his sharply contoured face, reflecting not a hint of warmth, only a chilling sharpness and an imposing authority that made one tremble.","\"She is hatching some wicked scheme again.\" Qin Shaozong coldly took off his heavily cracked jade thumb ring.","She had yet to appear, and at this point, what could he possibly not understand? Her wild fox-like heart must have grown restless again, fully intent on running away.","She needed to be taught a lesson!","The jade thumb ring drew a beautiful arc in the air, landing accurately in a small bamboo trash basket not far away. The impact upon landing was somewhat forceful, and the already cracked jade ring shattered into pieces.","\"My Lord, what should we do now?\" Mo Yanyun asked with a bitter expression.","It was not ideal for them to be away from Bairi City for too long. Setting aside the situation in Qingzhou, this place was ultimately too close to Sizhou. Furthermore, they had also clashed with Third Young Master Xie. What if the other party mobilized heavy troops over...","Qin Shaozong, however, said, \"Have Feng Feng and the others come over. Call all of them, don't leave a single one behind.\"","Mo Yanyun was stunned, not understanding why, but he obediently went to pass on the order.","Two quarters of an hour later, all the high-ranking military officers arrived in the room.","Qin Shaozong's gaze swept across the crowd one by one.","These men, who moved like the wind on the battlefield and lived with their lives on the line, now felt their backs stiffen under that gaze which suppressed a volatile temper.","They all stood up straight, and no one dared to speak.","\"Have any of you told anyone else about the mother-and-son relationship between Madam and that boy?\" Qin Shaozong finally spoke.","\"My Lord, we have not intentionally spread this matter. However, after the young master took Mister Nalan as his teacher, some people in the army must have guessed it,\" Feng Feng stated truthfully.","Qiao Wangfei nodded and added, \"The guards on duty at the estate all knew about it at the time. After all, the young master has always lived in the main courtyard with Madam Dai, and the mother and son bear a striking resemblance to each other. It's not difficult to guess that they are related by blood. Later, after the young master's apprenticeship ceremony was completed, a banquet was held in the army, and I heard some soldiers who knew the inside story mention a word or two about it.\"","Qin Shaozong asked again, \"Of the guards who knew the inside story back then, how many have followed me to Xiagu this time?\"","But just as he finished asking, Qin Shaozong corrected himself, \"Never mind. Pass my order to all the squads. From today onwards, it is strictly forbidden to discuss or spread the relationship between Madam and Qin Yanzhou. Violators will be dealt with according to military law!\"","The men were momentarily stunned.","Kuang Ye blinked his puppy-dog eyes and was the first to react. \"My Lord, do you suspect that the young master is a member of the Green Lotus Cult?\"","The forces opposing them were now clear. One was Sizhou, and the other was the Green Lotus Cult.","\"It's not a suspicion; it's a certainty.\" His words were resolute and resounding.","Qin Shaozong's eyes were heavy. \"Fan Tianshi and the Governor of Sizhou do not have deep ties, and the two provinces have been at peace for many years. But a few years ago, Fan Tianshi already had an ambiguous relationship with the Green Lotus Cult. If I were the leader of the Green Lotus Cult, I wouldn't completely trust this noncommittal ally either. Planting an insider in his estate is very common.\"","He just hadn't expected the other party to be so ruthless as to break a twelve-year-old child's legs and throw him at the entrance of the Fan Residence.","These were things Qin Shaozong had found out later, and he hadn't told her. At that time, she could cry until she fainted just from seeing a few extra scars on that boy. If she knew her son's legs had been intentionally broken, her tears would probably flood the entire estate.","Since she had chosen to escape the Green Lotus Cult back then, she naturally wouldn't take the initiative to show her face and draw close to them now.","But if the mother-and-son relationship were known to the Green Lotus Cult, she would absolutely be used and threatened by those with ulterior motives.","The men immediately realized the severity of the matter and assented one after another.","\"My Lord, I once heard a rumor about the Green Lotus Cult. Although I'm not sure if it's true or false, I think it's necessary to tell you,\" Kuang Ye said.","He was different from the others. Kuang Ye had stayed in Bingzhou for seven years. And the governor of Bingzhou didn't loathe spirits, gods, and Daoism like Qin Shaozong did, so he had come into contact with these things more than the others.","Qin Shaozong: \"What rumor?\"","Kuang Ye: \"I heard that the Green Lotus Cult would bestow a kind of miraculous medicine upon certain important cult members. Some say that after taking it, one would feel refreshed, their strength would increase, and it could even prolong life. If one were injured, they would instantly forget the pain.\"","\"Playing tricks to deceive people.\" Qin Shaozong sneered. \"If it could truly prolong life, that prescription would have been offered to the late Emperor long ago, or even earlier to Emperor Wu and the others in exchange for the position of State Preceptor. How could it be the turn of the subordinates to enjoy it?\"","Kuang Ye shook his head, however. \"My Lord, the main point is not the benefits, but the subsequent drawbacks. I heard that if this medicine is taken continuously for a course of treatment, and then rashly stopped afterwards, there is a risk of one's intestines being pierced and stomach rotting.\"","The mockery on Qin Shaozong's face instantly vanished.","The others were all startled.","\"Is this true?\"","\"How is this a miraculous medicine? It's clearly poison!\"","\"Kuang Ye, where did you get this news?\"","Facing everyone's chattering, Kuang Ye spread his hands. \"I said earlier that this is just hearsay. I don't know the specific truth or falsehood of it either.\"","This teahouse had been completely booked by the people of the North. The attendants were not allowed on the second floor. Now, with the sound of hurried footsteps approaching from outside, it could only be their own guards.","\"My Lord, your subordinate has an urgent matter to report.\"","The guard was summoned inside.","\"My Lord, you previously ordered us to secretly keep an eye on Prefect Gao. Just now, he sneaked out. He was wearing hemp clothes and didn't even take a carriage. He left through the side door on an ordinary cargo donkey cart and went to a remote winery in the city,\" the guard reported.","The crowd was in an uproar.","\"Acting so low-profile, it seems the person he is meeting must absolutely not be known to My Lord! If he isn't meeting Third Young Master Xie or someone from the Green Lotus Cult, I'll twist my head off and let him use it as a chair.\"","\"What a Gao You, he has quite a lot of cunning tricks up his sleeve!\"","\"My Lord, this Gao You is dishonest. You clearly hinted to him that if he obediently followed orders, it wouldn't be impossible for him to keep his position as Prefect. I didn't expect him to still dare to pull a stunt like this.\"","\"A man whose heart is not content is like a snake trying to swallow an elephant. Fortunately, My Lord had the foresight to make other preparations in advance.\"","\"It's a pity there was no one in the winery. We don't know what they talked about.\"","The guard from just now said, \"Men have been left near the tavern to keep an eye on Prefect Gao's movements at all times.\"","*","Wearing a straw hat, Gao You emerged from the winery. He glanced left and right at the door, and only after ensuring there was nothing unusual did he quickly climb into his donkey cart.","With a crack of the whip, the donkey trotted off, its hooves clattering all the way to the prefectural governor's manor.","By the time Gao You returned to the manor, the sky had already grown dim. Weighed down by his thoughts, he headed straight for the inner courtyard, intending to unwind and ease his fatigue.","Concubine Ruan was Gao You's favorite concubine. She was a specially trained Yangzhou beauty gifted to him by others in his early years. He doted on her deeply, and over the past dozen years, she had borne him two sons and a daughter.","Delicious dishes and a pot of fine wine were laid out on the low table. However, Gao You was too troubled to eat much; instead, he drowned his sorrows in the wine.","Concubine Ruan continuously poured his drinks, gently asking what was causing him such great distress.","As the alcohol went to his head, Gao You suddenly felt a strong urge to confide in her. Yet, he didn't speak directly about the political situation, choosing instead to use an analogy.","\"...So, what you mean, Husband, is that there are currently two shop owners who both want to hire you as their manager. The first is a newcomer you haven't dealt with before, and the two of them have jointly taken over the shop you originally worked for. The second is a familiar neighboring owner who wants to ally with you to secretly acquire your current shop,\" Concubine Ruan said.","Gao You nodded drunkenly. \"Exactly. If it were you, how would you look at it?\"","\"I come from humble beginnings and don't understand grand principles, but I always remember one saying: 'Man struggles upwards, just as water flows downwards.' A good life is something you must fight for yourself. As long as there is even the slightest chance for things to get better, you cannot miss it! Just like back then, when I fell in love with you at first sight, Husband, I used every bit of skill I had to make sure you kept me.\"","Hidden from Gao You's view, the eyes of his beloved concubine gleamed with an eerie, calculating light."]},{"number":81,"title":"Chapter 81","paragraphs":["The sun rose in the east, and the darkness entrenched in the sky slowly dispersed. At the break of dawn, the side door of the commandery governor's manor opened, and a cart meant for purchasing groceries drove out.","Few people noticed that, compared to usual, there was an extra person on today's cart. The donkey cart headed toward the vegetable market, but halfway there, a person jumped off and hurriedly slipped into a certain courtyard.","Clatter, clatter. Horse hooves pounded against the official road. After traveling day and night, this cavalry troop from Sizhou bypassed Jiulu County and finally arrived at the western outskirts of Xiagu Commandery.","Someone was already waiting to receive them in the western suburbs of the city. The contact was named Li Huairen, one of Xie Yuanxiu's trusted aides.","The cavalry leader was named Ni Chiwen. This man had taken the name of an ancient fierce beast, and his appearance was equally ferocious. With a square jaw, a wide mouth, a dark complexion, and yellowish hair, the muscles on his neck and shoulders bulged like old tree vines. One look was enough to tell he was a man of immense strength.","Commander Ni, I've finally waited for you... Li Huairen quickly stepped forward. After exchanging a few pleasantries with Ni Chiwen, he openly swept his gaze toward the rear.","Li Huairen asked in surprise, Commander Ni, how many soldiers are accompanying you this time? Why does it look a bit scarce?","Ni Chiwen snorted heavily through his nose and said indignantly, When the Eldest Young Master and Second Young Master heard about the troop deployment, they were very unwilling. They united with some of Inspector Xie's former subordinates to exert pressure and withheld a portion of the troops. The cavalry accompanying me this time only numbers a thousand. Oh, right, there are also three thousand foot soldiers led by Vice General Lin trailing behind.","Horses travel fast. The Third Young Master had issued an urgent order, so he didn't dare to delay and led the cavalry to go on ahead.","Li Huairen counted on his fingers. When the Third Young Master originally came to Xiagu, he brought four hundred cavalrymen. Now that Ni Chiwen had arrived, they had a total of one thousand four hundred cavalrymen on their side.","There was just one problem. The Marquis of Wu'an had already entered the city. With many obstacles in the city, there was no difference between cavalry and infantry, unless the opponent was beaten to a pulp and eventually forced to flee out of the city.","Ni Chiwen asked, How many troops does the Marquis of Wu'an have with him?","Li Huairen replied, Around two hundred.","Ni Chiwen immediately burst into loud laughter, his entire demeanor visibly relaxing. I thought he had thousands of troops and tens of thousands of horses this time. It turns out to be only two hundred. Tell the Third Young Master there's no need to be nervous. Even if the foot soldiers behind don't arrive, we have more than enough to handle them.","We thought of deploying troops, and the Marquis of Wu'an naturally thought of it too. It's just a matter of who arrives first. Without further delay, Commander Ni, quickly follow me into the city. We will take the head of the Marquis of Wu'an directly! Li Huairen said.","Inside the city, at a teahouse.","The teahouse had been entirely booked out, completely becoming the stronghold for the northern generals. Both the front and back doors were guarded by soldiers.","A white figure avoided the eyes and ears of the crowd and quietly appeared at the back door of the teahouse.","The guarding soldier was originally a patrol guard of the Qin Manor. Seeing the newcomer, he was immediately startled. Young Master?!","Qin Yanzhou was brief and to the point: I need to see the Marquis of Wu'an.","The attendant dared not turn away the son of Madam Dai, but considering that a while ago the Young Master was raising hell every day and almost tore the mansion apart, he didn't dare to let him in directly either.","The guard simply said, Please come with me.","Entering from the back door, they went upstairs via the back staircase. There were also soldiers guarding the upper floor. Seeing Qin Yanzhou, everyone showed a look of surprise.","Young Master? Bai Jianping came out of a room and saw Qin Yanzhou coming toward him. Why are you here?","As soon as the words left his mouth, he felt it was inappropriate.","Pah, look at what he was saying. Given the Marquis's attitude of treating Madam Dai like the apple of his eye, they would be family sooner or later.","A hand pushed aside Bai Jianping, who was blocking the way. Qin Shaozong emerged from behind him, his calm gaze falling on Qin Yanzhou.","He didn't ask how the boy knew Dai Li's movements back then, nor did he ask why Dai Li had been hiding and not coming out to find them, nor did he demand an explanation of how he followed him to Xiagu. Qin Shaozong got straight to the point: What kind of trouble have you run into, kid?","Qin Yanzhou was just as straightforward with him. My mother was just taken away by Third Young Master Xie's men.","Bai Jianping was greatly shocked. Feng Feng and several others in the room quickly came out upon hearing this, all crowding at the door.","Qin Shaozong's pupils constricted slightly. Where is Third Young Master Xie now?","Qin Yanzhou provided an address on West Street.","Mo Yanyun was outspoken, The previous curved-shaft plow was Madam Dai's masterpiece, right? Your Green Lotus Sect got such a great thing, so why didn't you treat her as an honored guest, instead of letting that Third Young Master Xie run amok?","The other party has troops in his hands, Qin Yanzhou said.","Qin Shaozong didn't speak, but hurried downstairs.","As soon as he left, the surrounding generals immediately followed closely behind, leaving the second floor like a receding tide. The originally crowded doorway instantly became empty.","Qin Yanzhou followed them for a few steps, stopped at the second-floor staircase, and looked down. He saw Qin Shaozong go downstairs and order someone to bring his horse, obviously intending to head to the west side of the city immediately.","A glimmer of light flashed in the young man's eyes. He returned the way he came, heading straight for the back door of the teahouse.","Calculating the time, Sizhou's reinforcements were almost here. He couldn't let the North be caught off guard. Sizhou winning an overwhelming victory would be of no benefit to him or his mother, which was why he had made this trip.","It would be best if they were evenly matched and fought inextricably, so that neither side could spare the energy to attend to other matters.","...","Downstairs.","Qin Shaozong suddenly stopped in his tracks: Mo Yanyun, take Bai Ye with you and secretly follow that kid to see where he goes. It's chaotic right now; he will most likely take the opportunity to leave the city with Madam. Don't make a sound, just follow him secretly. If they discover you, no matter what, you must keep following them.","Suddenly called out, Mo Yanyun accepted the order, turned around, and left.","My Lord, do you suspect the Young Master is lying to us? Feng Feng asked in a low voice.","The guard brought the horse, and Qin Shaozong mounted it. It's not impossible. She is very sharp, and the son she gave birth to is at least half like her. But whether it's true or false, it really is time to settle scores with Third Young Master Xie.","They had arrived in Xiagu later than Xie Yuanxiu. It could be said that they were completely in the dark when they first arrived, not knowing how many troops Third Young Master Xie had hidden in this small commandery.","The previous confrontation was more of a probe to test the opponent's true strength rather than an act of suppression.","It didn't take long, just a day, and they found out.","The opponent did indeed have more men than they did, but not to the extent of overwhelming them, and the combat power of Sizhou's soldiers was far inferior to theirs.","Even if Qin Yanzhou hadn't come looking for him, Qin Shaozong planned to make a move today anyway. Xiagu Commandery was closer to Sizhou. If they dragged this on any longer and waited for the opponent's reinforcements to arrive, it would be very disadvantageous for them.","The riding crop was raised and fell, and the fine horse neighed.","Their group rode in a large formation, causing the surrounding commoners to quickly give way.","And on the way to West Street, Qin Shaozong encountered two guards riding their horses in a hurry.","The two groups of people ran into each other head-on. The guard was pleasantly surprised that he didn't have to run any further. \"My Lord, the reinforcements from Sizhou have arrived outside the city! Garrison Commander Qiao saw them approaching from afar and immediately closed the city gates according to your orders. Just as you predicted, the city gate guards have all rebelled, dead set on letting the Sizhou people in. Fortunately, we kept our wits about us, otherwise, the consequences would have been unimaginable. Right now, Garrison Commander Qiao is leading his men in a fight against them.\"","Qin Shaozong asked, \"How many reinforcements from Sizhou?\"","\"They are all cavalry, looks to be about a thousand men,\" the guard replied.","Feng Feng said furiously, \"That bastard Gao You spoke so nicely before, saying he would serve you like a dog or horse, My Lord. Now he turns around and defects to the enemy camp just like that. He really is greedy. Good thing you weren't fooled by his sweet talk, My Lord.\"","When they were staying at the Gao Manor, Prefect Gao treated them as honored guests. Every detail of their food, clothing, shelter, and transportation was exquisite, and he took every opportunity to flatter the Lord. The Lord had even promised that if he knew what was good for him, he wouldn't be treated poorly in the future.","Even a rat has skin, yet that man has no sense of honor. The scoundrel doesn't know what's good for him!","Feng Feng volunteered himself, \"My Lord, Qiao Wangfei only has about seventy men over there. Please grant me a troop of soldiers, and I will go support Qiao Wangfei.\"","\"The city gates are not the main point. To catch the bandits, first catch the ringleader. Right now, our top priority is to capture Third Young Master Xie.\" Qin Shaozong's gaze swept over their surroundings, keenly noticing that there was already some unusual movement nearby.","At first glance, the pedestrians were still pedestrians, wearing headscarves and coarse linen clothes, carrying long, strip-shaped luggage in their hands or on their shoulders. The peddlers on both sides were mostly squatting or sitting behind their stalls. Even if there were pedestrians doing business with them, their eyes were all restlessly darting in this direction.","Riding on his horse, Qin Shaozong's field of vision was higher than that of ordinary people, and he could faintly see some curved, long pieces of wood hidden behind the stalls.","\"There are archers on both sides!\" Qin Shaozong suddenly raised his voice.","Whether it was the \"pedestrians,\" the \"peddlers,\" or Qin Shaozong's cavalrymen, everyone was startled.","Seeing that the opportunity to shoot from the shadows was gone, the \"peddlers\" on both sides simultaneously grabbed their longbows and sprang up. Meanwhile, the \"pedestrians\" on the street suddenly drew out flashes of white steel from their luggage.","After Qin Shaozong's warning, the cavalrymen closest to the edges quickly dismounted, closed the distance in a single bound, and used their long sabers to suppress the enemy's bows and arrows.","The \"pedestrians\" had no horses and were a level lower than the cavalry; the disadvantage brought by the height difference immediately became apparent.","Drawing his ring-pommel saber from its sheath, Qin Shaozong bent his elbow to raise the blade, then fiercely slashed forward.","The sharp edge of the blade whipped up a fierce gust of wind, carving a clean arc from top to bottom, bringing with it splattering blood and a rolling head.","\"Bang, bang, bang—\"","The windows of the shops on both sides up ahead were forcefully pushed open, and longbows were thrust out from within, aiming at the people below.","At the same time, soldiers poured out from the ground floors. Those on the first floor wielded sabers, while those on the second floor held bows and arrows.","His falcon-like brown eyes took on a cold, metallic hue in the sunlight. The man quickly locked onto a target, tightly squeezing the horse's belly with his legs. The fine steed neighed and, without needing to be whipped, broke into a gallop, charging straight toward the entrance of a fabric shop.","A tall flag stood in front of this fabric shop. The flagpole was about ten feet long, and the flag bore only a single word, \"Fabric,\" its jagged edges fluttering in the wind.","Qin Shaozong grabbed the flagpole with his left hand, the veins on the back of his hand bulging. In an instant, he yanked the flagpole out of the stone base it was embedded in.","Several whistling sounds of wind being pierced came from his side. Qin Shaozong's gaze turned chilling. His left hand, holding the flag, forcefully swung from back to front.","The fluttering flag whipped up a gust of wind, seemingly transforming into an iron eagle spreading its wings in an instant. The extended wings propped up an invisible domain of protection, keeping the outside storm of attacks at bay.","\"Split into small squads and head upstairs to clear out the enemy soldiers!\" Qin Shaozong ordered sternly.","The soldiers who had previously dismounted to deal with the archers moved along the edges, advancing while blocking, hurrying all the way until they reached the enemy positions.","Qin Shaozong glanced back. The street was in complete chaos. The goods the \"peddlers\" had used for their act were scattered all over the ground. The fallen corpses had been trampled to a pulp by horse hooves, and blood seeped into the bluestone bricks, forming a shocking, deep crimson.","\"My Lord, they've stationed troops here. Third Young Master Xie might not be over at the West Street anymore.\" Kuang Ye blocked a flying arrow; it would be a lie to say he wasn't anxious.","For the Lord's westbound journey this time, only three hundred men had traveled with him on the tower ships. And not all of these three hundred men were in Xiagu; three tower ships, which meant ninety men, had gone to Jiulu County with Wei Qing.","They had two hundred and ten men left.","Now that the city's patrol guards had defected, if Third Young Master Xie took advantage of the chaos to hide, they would not only have to deal with the patrol guards but also search for him, which would absolutely overwhelm them.","Qin Shaozong said, \"Whether Third Young Master Xie is there or not, we'll know once we go take a look.\"","He was very interested to see if the address that kid provided was true or false.","A small courtyard in the eastern part of the city.","Dai Li still kept her doors closed and didn't go out. The courtyard was cramped, and her only form of entertainment was eavesdropping by the wall.","And admittedly, she managed to gather quite a lot of information.","Someone said that the higher-ups seemed to have stopped checking the inns and had switched to going door-to-door to inspect household registers. The large-scale sweep was originally meant to find a female thief, but unexpectedly, they dug out some fugitives, which could be considered a lucky stroke.","Someone else said that yesterday they saw quite a few patrol guards patrolling with weapons, but after making a round and coming back, the people were the same, but the weapons in their hands were gone, as if they had been hidden away.","Still others said:","\"Recently, both leaving and entering the city have become much more difficult. My distant cousin who sells sauces transported goods back into the city yesterday, and even the empty boxes had to be inspected. He said he saw many merchants having to undergo a round of interrogation to leave the city. All cargo boxes had to be opened, without a single one left out.\"","\"Sigh, it's not peaceful lately. Best not to go out easily.\"","Hurried footsteps approached, followed by someone shouting, \"Brother, this is bad! A fight has broken out over at the West Street! Word is spreading outside right now telling people not to go out these next few days, lest they get their heads chopped off!\"","\"Another fight? Is it a clash between the two patrol squads? Speaking of which, there was a fight yesterday too, and I heard quite a few heads rolled at the time. But afterwards, those who should withdraw withdrew, and those who should go home went home. I'm guessing the chaos won't last long this time either.\"","\"No! They're really fighting! There are archers inside the shops, shooting arrows left and right. There are also tons of soldiers on the streets. Anyway, it's an all-out war, and blood is flowing like a river.\"","Dai Li pursed her lips.","A fight broke out?","Between Qin Shaozong and that person from Sizhou?","Before Dai Li could listen any further, a white figure flipped over the wall from outside, landing like a cat without making a single sound.","Dai Li: \"!\"","Seeing Dai Li in the courtyard, Qin Yanzhou hurried forward and said in a low voice, \"Mother, the Northern Region and Sizhou have started fighting. I'll go back to the room with you to apply our disguises, then we'll leave through the east city gate and change our route to head south.\"","Dai Li's spirits jolted. Knowing that time was of the essence, she couldn't care about anything else and hurriedly turned around to return to the room with Qin Yanzhou.","About a quarter of an hour later, the mother and son walked out of the house.","Dai Li was wearing ordinary coarse linen clothes. Her complexion was concealed with a specially mixed dark ointment, making it several shades darker than before. A small scar had been added to her face, the curve at the corners of her eyes was pressed down slightly, and a few dark moles were also added to her face.","Qin Yanzhou had also disguised himself. The mother and son looked almost like completely different people.","They did not have much luggage, just one pack each.","Disguised like this, Dai Li did not need to wear a veiled hat and could walk outside openly.","After leaving the small courtyard, the two navigated a series of turns and headed east.","They already lived in the eastern part of the city, not far from the city gates. Perhaps because their path was so unobstructed, Qin Yanzhou brought up what had just happened: \"Mother, on my way back, I ran into Commandant Mo. He followed me, but I managed to shake him off.\"","Dai Li, whose thoughts had been occupied with the Green Lotus Sect, had her train of thought broken. \"He followed you? Did you run into him by accident?\"","\"No, I went to look for the Marquis of Wu'an just now.\"","Dai Li was severely shaken by the bombshell her son had just dropped. \"Why would you go looking for him? Qin Shaozong is an incredibly sharp and deeply calculating man. There is no telling if he...\"","She did not finish her sentence. Suddenly, both mother and son stopped dead in their tracks.","Staring at Mo Yanyun, who was crouching near the city gates just a short distance away, Dai Li instantly felt a sinking sense of foreboding."]},{"number":82,"title":"Chapter 82","paragraphs":["The entire street was soaked in the color of blood. Corpses lay haphazardly across the ground, scattered among broken blades and shattered bows.","The doors of the shops lining both sides of the street were thrown wide open. When the wind brushed past, the dilapidated window shutters were blown inward, groaning under the strain with a heavy creak from their wooden hinges.","Qin Shaozong flicked his blade, sending a thick trail of blood splattering loudly onto the bluestone pavement. He looked up and gazed ahead. The street before him was dead silent, the shop doors shut tight. It was impossible to tell if there was an ambush lying in wait within.","The horse he had previously borrowed from Gao You was dead. The enemy had deployed tripwires and then focused their attacks relentlessly on the beast.","\"My Lord, we are but one street away from that residence,\" Feng Feng said, his eyes also fixed straight ahead.","Looking at it like this, one truly could not discern how many hidden troops lay ahead.","\"Tear down the shop doors to use as shields. Position the archers in the center of our formation and the infantry on the outside.\" Qin Shaozong sneered. \"It is merely the distance of a single street. How could we possibly fail to cross it?\"","As for the enemy's cavalry outside the city, Qin Shaozong paid them no mind whatsoever. The enemy had reinforcements, but so did he; it was just a matter of waiting a little longer.","When Third Young Master Xie's men arrived at the city walls, he would simply close the city gates.","They had no siege ladders or battering rams. Did they really think they could force their way in with just that handful of men outside? It was a pipe dream.","...","The commotion from the earlier slaughter was not small; it could be heard several streets away. Xie Yuanxiu, who was residing in a courtyard pavilion on the West Street, was no exception.","He was not stupid. Upon hearing from his attendants that the Marquis of Wu'an was slaughtering his way over, he immediately ordered a retreat. As for the belongings inside the residence, they took absolutely nothing. Fleeing for their lives was the priority.","\"The Marquis of Wu'an brought no more than two hundred men to Xiagu this time. He has to divide his forces to search for people, keep an eye on the situation at all four city gates, and still keep guards by his side. He needs men everywhere, yet he somehow managed to spare enough hands to find my hiding place?\" Xie Yuanxiu truly felt as if he had seen a ghost.","He had naturally heard of the fearsome reputation of that man from the North. He was incredibly vicious, and facing his wrath head-on was the worst possible plan. Therefore, when he first heard that the Marquis of Wu'an had also arrived in Xiagu, he quickly found a place to hide.","The hiding place was provided by Diting. Logically speaking, it should have been perfectly secure. Even if the Marquis of Wu'an's men came knocking to investigate, they shouldn't have been able to find any clues.","Where exactly did the leak happen? Could Gao You have betrayed him?","That shouldn't be the case. Now that the city gate guards had mutinied, Gao You had no turning back. It was absolutely impossible for him to still be wavering.","Xie Yuanxiu's subordinate also didn't know the reason, but did his best to comfort him. \"Third Young Master, please do not be angry. Fortunately, we prepared a backup plan at the time. We will leave through the back door now, pass through the alleys, and head toward the North Street to lay low for a while. Commander Ni and the others are already outside the city. With Prefect Gao and our men cooperating from within, entering the city is only a matter of time. Once Commander Ni leads his troops here, why worry about not being able to take the head of the Marquis of Wu'an?\"","The subordinate added, \"Furthermore, Commander Ni has always been resourceful. If he cannot enter through the East Gate, he will certainly try the other gates. He will get in eventually.\"","Xie Yuanxiu's expression softened slightly. \"You are right. Let us avoid the brunt of his attack for now. By the way, how many men did Gao You arrange to assassinate the Marquis of Wu'an?\"","The subordinate replied, \"Four hundred men. Plus the one hundred we lent him, that makes a total of five hundred.\"","Xie Yuanxiu gasped. \"Five hundred men still couldn't stop the Marquis of Wu'an? What are they good for!\"","The subordinate was also incredibly anxious.","He had always heard that the Marquis of Wu'an commanded an invincible elite force under his banner, every single one of them a master capable of taking on ten men at once. Could it be that the unit outside was...","Subordinate: \"The back alley is too narrow for carriages to pass. I must trouble the Third Young Master to proceed on foot.\"","Xie Yuanxiu gritted his teeth. \"Let's go!\"","At the same time, at the East City Gate.","Dai Li looked at Mo Yanyun, who was staking out the area not far away, and cursed inwardly. With Mo Yanyun here, could it be that Qin Shaozong had discovered her?","However, Dai Li quickly overturned this speculation.","He probably hadn't found out. She observed him for a moment and saw that Mo Yanyun was solely focused on staring at the caravans leaving the city, not looking anywhere else.","\"Mother, we will leave with the merchant caravan shortly.\" Qin Yanzhou had already made the arrangements.","Dai Li followed his gaze and saw a group of traveling merchants not far away. It was a group of about twenty people with five donkey carts, each packed to the brim.","\"Is that a caravan from the Green Lotus Sect?\" Dai Li asked.","Qin Yanzhou replied, \"Not entirely. Only the lead merchant is a believer. I told him that we would be leaving the city with his caravan shortly, accompanying another divine envoy, which is you, to execute a secret mission, and that we needed to borrow his wife's travel pass.\"","Just by looking at her son's placid expression, Dai Li knew that the merchant had raised no objections to this.","It seemed that the Green Lotus Sect's influence among the common folk was far greater than she had imagined. To think that they would lend out something as important as a travel pass just like that.","\"That Commandant Mo is staking out the city gate,\" Dai Li said in a low voice.","Qin Yanzhou said, \"It doesn't matter. He is the only one familiar with us. The other Northern soldiers rarely see you, so they likely won't recognize you. When the time comes, walk alongside the cart and use it as a shield to block his view. If you are inevitably seen by him, just turn the scarred side of your face toward him. Furthermore, when we go out, I have arranged a diversion to lure the tiger away from the mountain. He will most likely not have the energy to conduct the inspections himself.\"","Perhaps worried that Dai Li was still anxious, Qin Yanzhou spoke more than he usually did. \"Do not worry. From my observations, that Commandant Mo is a bit more slow-witted than the rest. He will not notice.\"","Dai Li didn't know whether to laugh or cry.","As they spoke, the merchant caravan moved forward a distance, passing right by the two of them.","The mother and son joined the group. They did not walk at the front or the rear, but stayed in the middle, pretending to watch over the goods on the carts alongside the others.","Perhaps because they had been notified beforehand, not a single person showed any surprise at the two joining their ranks midway.","Everyone kept their mouths shut and walked forward in silence.","Mo Yanyun was filled with endless regret. The Marquis had sent him to tail them. He had thought it would be a simple task, never expecting the young master to be so deeply hidden and capable. Upon discovering him, the boy had immediately shaken him off.","The Marquis had said that the mother and son might take advantage of the chaos to leave the city. Looking at the young master's previous route, they were undoubtedly heading east.","By staking out the city gate, he should be able to intercept them. In the past, people always said that fools have foolish luck. He hoped that saying would hold true now, allowing him to fish out Madam Dai.","With a bitter expression, Mo Yanyun stared closely at every young woman leaving the city.","At this moment, a merchant caravan arrived. With several donkeys pulling carts and about twenty people, it was considered quite a sizable group.","Seeing that there were a few women in the group, Mo Yanyun swept his gaze over them roughly. Each of them had dark, rough skin and plain features. He walked over to take a closer look at two of them. Before they even opened their mouths, he already knew his hopes were dashed.","Just as he was planning to carefully inspect the remaining women, a sudden commotion erupted not far away.","Mo Yanyun subconsciously raised his head, and that single glance caused his pupils to constrict. He thought he saw that slender, white-clad figure.","The young master was wearing a white robe today!","Could it be that they tried to leave the city but accidentally alarmed the city patrols?","Mo Yanyun immediately sprinted in that direction to chase after them. However, when he reached a crossroad, he was left utterly bewildered once again.","Where should I go?","Ah, it seems I've lost them again...","His head was suddenly pressed down hard. Mo Yanyun cried out \"Ouch\" and clutched his head. \"Bai Ye, what are you doing?\"","The gyrfalcon, its feathers a mix of white and brown, landed on his head, tapped twice with its claws, and then spread its wings to fly east. It flew a distance, circled back, and continued eastward.","Mo Yanyun froze, then his spirits suddenly lifted. \"Are you saying they're over there?\"","He immediately hurried back to the east city gate, grabbed a horse belonging to the city guards, mounted it, and chased after them.","Not long after Mo Yanyun left the city, a squad of Xuanxiao Cavalry led by Kuang Ye arrived and ordered the city gates to be closed.","The heavy city gates slowly shut.","...","After following the merchants out of the city, Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou broke away from the caravan.","Qin Yanzhou had hidden a good horse in the suburbs. The mother and son shared the ride, rushing toward the south at top speed.","It was now the end of the noon hour. They had to reach the ruined temple in the southern city before dark; that ruined temple was their resting place for the night.","After staying a night in the temple, they would travel for a whole day tomorrow to reach a small mountain village. They would spend another night there, travel for one more day the day after, and then reach the border of Yuzhou. There was a small county next to the Yuzhou border. As long as they entered that small county, it would be like a fish returning to the sea.","\"Zhou Zhou, now that you've left with me and the Green Lotus Cult can't find you, will they guess that you've defected?\" Dai Li asked worriedly.","The believers of the Green Lotus Cult were spread across all provinces. The sheer number of people was one thing, but the key was that they were hard to identify. However, communication in ancient times was slow; a piece of information could take half a year or a year to transmit.","Half a year or a year?","Oh, by the time they noticed something was wrong, the two of them would have long escaped. They wouldn't just sit obediently waiting to be caught.","But if the Green Lotus Cult immediately realized that Zhou Zhou had defected, the nature of the situation would be entirely different.","\"Diting had a premonition that the situation was bad and has already left with his people. I told them that I temporarily received a mission from the higher-ups and had to go elsewhere, so no one suspects anything for now,\" Qin Yanzhou said in a low voice.","Dai Li breathed a sigh of relief. \"That's good.\"","By the time the Green Lotus Cult reacted, they would have already reached Yuzhou.","The horse trotted along the official road. After riding for a distance, the people on the road gradually became sparse.","With fewer people, other sounds became more obvious.","Qin Yanzhou suddenly reined in the horse and looked back.","The official road stretched out behind them, the small bend obscured by lush foliage, no longer visible. A breeze brushed past, making the leaves sway in the quiet and peaceful atmosphere.","\"Zhou Zhou, what's wrong?\" Dai Li also turned to look back.","But she saw nothing.","Qin Yanzhou turned his head back. \"Nothing.\"","He continued to ride forward.","However, after some distance, the young man reined in the horse again. This time he did not speak, merely stopping the horse to listen quietly.","Dai Li didn't understand why, but her heart skipped a beat, and an ominous premonition washed over her.","After pausing for a moment, Qin Yanzhou suddenly urged the horse forward.","Dai Li could feel that their pace had quickened, and her heart rose to her throat. \"Zhou Zhou, is someone following us?\"","\"There is one rider,\" Qin Yanzhou said.","Dai Li was taken aback. \"One rider?\"","What could a single person do? To put it bluntly, by the time they went back to report the news and returned, their target would have long vanished.","\"I don't know whose side they are on yet. We'll see in a bit.\" After riding past a bend ahead, Qin Yanzhou quickly reined in the horse and dismounted.","The bushes here were dense. Holding the reins, Qin Yanzhou led the horse carrying Dai Li to the side, trying to let the bushes conceal them as much as possible.","After doing all this, the black-haired young man climbed up the tree above Dai Li's head in a few swift moves, hiding himself within the canopy.","Mo Yanyun couldn't hear the sound of hooves. This time, the pause was longer than before, so long that it seemed the rider had stopped to rest.","Could it be that they had realized he was secretly following them and had abandoned their horse to flee into the mountains?","His heart tightening, Mo Yanyun couldn't care about anything else and hurried his horse forward. At first glance, seeing the official road empty, his heart sank halfway.","But at second glance, he saw Dai Li on horseback, half-hidden in the tall grass not far away.","Their eyes met, and both of them froze for a moment.","Dai Li hadn't expected it to be Mo Yanyun. He had clearly been lured away earlier, yet here he was, back again.","Mo Yanyun's pupils contracted, his eyes revealing shock.","If Bai Ye hadn't reminded him, making him clearly aware that this was Madam Dai, he really wouldn't have recognized her. She looked like a completely different person from before!","\"Madam Dai, the Marquis has been looking for you for a long time. Please come back with me.\" Mo Yanyun was solely focused on quickly persuading Dai Li to return.","Seeing him approach, Dai Li tightened her grip on the reins. \"Save your breath. I'm not going back.\"","\"Why?\" Mo Yanyun didn't understand.","Dai Li looked away. \"No reason.\"","Mo Yanyun dismounted and continued walking toward Dai Li, wishing he could just throw a net over her and drag her back. \"There must be a reason. How could there be no reason? The Marquis...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, alarm bells suddenly rang in the head of Mo Yanyun, a man who spent his life on the battlefield. He instinctively drew his blade and blocked horizontally, intercepting the strike from the young man who had jumped down from the tree.","Mo Yanyun felt a chill on his neck.","If his reaction hadn't been fast just now, his head really would have fallen to the ground.","Dai Li was also startled.","The two men immediately began to fight.","Mo Yanyun only defended and didn't attack. But later, he found that this approach wouldn't work; the opponent's moves were exceptionally fierce, and not attacking would only fuel Qin Yanzhou's aggression.","\"Zhou Zhou, you can't kill this man. Just kill his horse,\" Dai Li said anxiously.","Mo Yanyun was a member of the core circle of the North. If he died by her son's hands, Qin Shaozong would have even more reason not to let them go.","Qin Yanzhou turned his blade, immediately abandoning Mo Yanyun to attack his horse.","Mo Yanyun cursed under his breath and hurriedly moved to block the blade.","A few more moves passed. The horse, frightened, stomped its hooves, looking ready to bolt. Seeing this, Mo Yanyun shouted frantically, \"If you dare to kill my horse, I'll kill yours too! Then none of us will be able to run!\"","Qin Yanzhou's eyes and brows instantly turned cold. He wanted to continue fighting, but Dai Li stopped him again.","Dai Li had been observing for a while. Seeing that it had been only Mo Yanyun from beginning to end, she was certain that he was the only one who had caught up.","Perhaps, as Zhou Zhou had said earlier, the city was already in chaos. Qin Shaozong had only brought a small number of people to Xiagu, and he simply couldn't spare anyone else at the moment.","Well, that made things easier.","Sitting on the horse, Dai Li raised her chin slightly, looking down at Mo Yanyun. \"You just asked me why I am unwilling to go back. Very well, I will tell you plainly now: I refuse to be a concubine. Commandant Mo, now that you know the reason, go back and tell Qin Changgeng. Stop following me.\"","She had never inquired about Qin Shaozong's family affairs. But in this era, how could a man, especially a powerful figure who controlled the entire North, have only one woman?","Qin Shaozong wanted a lifetime with her, but she did not want to be trapped in such a place for a lifetime. Living under someone else's roof, bound by rules, pitifully and pathetically living at the mercy of him and his wife.","Mo Yanyun was dumbfounded and left speechless.","\"Zhou Zhou, he came alone. Just ignore him.\" Dai Li gave the reins a tentative tug.","The horse beneath her let out a snort. Seeing this, Qin Yanzhou quickly grabbed the reins and led the horse out.","Qin Yanzhou swung himself into the saddle and rode off with Dai Li.","Mo Yanyun hastily followed after them.","Qin Yanzhou abruptly reined in his horse again and drew his blade.","Mo Yanyun quickly threw his hands in the air to show he meant no harm. \"The Marquis ordered that if I encountered you, I must follow and ensure your safety. I dare not disobey his command. Please rest assured, Madam Dai, I am merely tagging along and absolutely will not do anything else. If you don't believe me, you can have the young master search me. I swear I have nothing on me that could be used to leave a trail.\"","Dai Li called out softly, \"Zhou Zhou.\"","They were still on the outskirts of Xia Valley, a place where they shouldn't linger. They couldn't afford to keep arguing with Mo Yanyun over this matter.","Qin Yanzhou sheathed his blade and walked over. Mo Yanyun fully cooperated with the search.","After a thorough pat-down, he found nothing suspicious.","There was no cinnabar powder and no specially crafted tracking incense. Aside from the clothes on his back, a saber, a handful of copper coins, and a waterskin, Mo Yanyun had absolutely nothing else on him.","Qin Yanzhou coldly withdrew his hands.","The two horses set off once more.","Listening to the hoofbeats beside them, Dai Li pursed her lips.","They couldn't kill him, nor could they shake him off. It was a good thing Qin Shaozong couldn't spare any more men at the moment, otherwise, they would be in serious trouble...","Still, they had to find an opportunity to lose him.","Mo Yanyun trailed them all the way to a ruined temple in the southern part of the city. By now, the sky had grown dark, and night was fast approaching. He guessed that the mother and son intended to spend the night there.","A gaze as sharp as a blade shot toward him, laced with murderous intent. Mo Yanyun shuddered and quickly said, \"Don't worry, I swear I won't step a single foot out of this temple tonight, except to relieve myself. If you still don't trust me, I can sleep in the deepest corner of the room.\"","After he finished speaking, Dai Li watched as he took the lead and entered the temple, saber in hand.","Old, ruined temples often served as hideouts for bandits and wanted fugitives. These outlaws might have blood on their hands, but such desperadoes were sometimes incredibly perceptive.","The moment Mo Yanyun stepped inside, the vagrants already taking shelter there all shrank back into a corner, lowering their voices to mere whispers.","Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou walked in after him.","Mo Yanyun took the innermost spot, Dai Li settled in the middle, and Qin Yanzhou guarded the outermost position near the entrance.","The cramped, ruined temple was divided into two halves; Dai Li's group occupied the left side, while the other group took the right.","Noticing someone stealthily peeking in their direction, Qin Yanzhou's eyes turned cold, and he stood up, gripping his blade.","Mo Yanyun had been pondering Dai Li's words for the entire journey. Seeing Qin Yanzhou step away, he seized the opportunity to whisper to her, \"Madam Dai, the Marquis's estate hasn't had a mistress for fifteen years. Given how the Marquis treats you, you could absolutely do whatever you please once you move in.\"","Dai Li shot him a sideways glance but said nothing.","As someone who had spent plenty of time in pleasure houses, Mo Yanyun suddenly had a flash of inspiration. \"If you don't like the idea of living in the Marquis's estate, there's no reason you and the young master couldn't live somewhere else outside.\"","Audaciously, he decided to take a completely unconventional approach. \"What I'm about to say might sound utterly absurd, but it comes from the bottom of my heart. If there were ever a pleasure house in this world specifically designed to cater to women, and all of us military men from the North were lined up inside for the ladies to take their pick... well, with our Marquis's impressive physique and handsome face, he would undoubtedly be the top choice of the bunch, wouldn't he?\"","Dai Li: \"...\""]},{"number":83,"title":"Chapter 83","paragraphs":["The twilight was heavy, and a round of fierce fighting had just ceased. The surrounding air was permeated with a stench of blood so thick it almost felt tangible.","Qin Shaozong casually grabbed a piece of coarse cloth to wipe his blood-drenched blade. As the cloth passed over the metal, a sharp, chilling gleam of white instantly revealed itself.","\"My Lord Marquis, we have slain five hundred men in total this time.\" Feng Feng had climbed up from the very bottom to the position of Garrison Commander of the Xuanxiao Cavalry step by step, and he was as meticulous as one could be. \"From what I can tell, the ratio between the city guards and Third Young Master Xie's men is about eight to two.\"","Just as Third Young Master Xie knew exactly how many men they had brought to Xiagu, they had also figured out the enemy's true strength.","Xie Yuanxiu had four hundred soldiers, twice their own number. Coupled with the city guards under Gao You's command, the enemy forces reached a thousand men.","However, not all of these thousand men were thrown into the battle. At the very least, Xie Yuanxiu would definitely keep a portion of them by his side for protection.","\"A quarter of Third Young Master Xie's soldiers are gone,\" Qin Shaozong said lightly.","After fighting from noon until nightfall, the man's face showed no signs of fatigue. The light of the torches reflected in his eyes, resembling the sharp glint at the very tip of a blade.","\"What is the situation at the city gates?\" Qin Shaozong continued to ask.","Feng Feng replied, \"That thousand-man force mainly attacked the east gate. The east gate is being guarded by Lao Qiao, and the patrol guards on the wall have all been replaced by our own men. It is a good thing they are cavalry and did not bring any siege equipment. Unable to break through from the inside, they are now just shouting provocations from below.\"","The Xuanxiao Cavalry was renowned far and wide, but the enemy had never clashed with them before and clearly felt their reputation was exaggerated. Stubbornly refusing to believe the rumors, they thought they could force open the east gate, which was defended by over a hundred Xuanxiao Cavalrymen, with a mere five or six hundred men.","They did not even stop to consider that their city guards lacked basic daily training. Some of the higher-ranking officials had eaten themselves into fat, bloated messes who would lose their breath after running just a few steps. Even their blades were of poor quality.","If the Xuanxiao Cavalry could be defeated by such people, they truly deserved to die.","\"Let them shout. Treat it as nothing more than dogs barking,\" Qin Shaozong said indifferently.","There was no such thing as fighting a war without being cursed at. It was commonplace for enemies to hurl ugly insults during a standoff, greeting one's ancestors and entire family. But the time to strike had not yet arrived; those scores would be settled later.","\"Have Gao You and Third Young Master Xie been found yet?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","Feng Feng lowered his head in shame. \"Not yet.\"","The streets and alleys within the city were twisting and winding, offering far too many places to hide. They simply did not have enough manpower.","\"The enemy's reinforcements are definitely not limited to a single batch of cavalry. In another two or three days, the rest of their reinforcement troops should arrive.\" Qin Shaozong's lips curled into a smirk. \"Let them come!\"","Bairi City was located to the east of Xiagu. The great river flowed eastward, and taking a small boat downstream would be much faster than their journey here.","After roughly pinpointing his wife's location, he had immediately dispatched someone to take a boat back to Bairi City. Calculating the time, it had been over eight days now.","And his own reinforcements would be arriving soon as well.","\"Whoosh—\"","A sudden rush of air swept down from the sky as a majestic gyrfalcon landed on a nearby wooden rack. Its black, agate-like eyes darted around sharply.","\"Ah, Bai Ye is back!\" Feng Feng exclaimed in surprise.","He turned his head to look around, but the street was veiled in the dreary, heavy twilight, and there was no sign of Mo Yanyun anywhere. \"Lao Mo didn't come back?\"","Bai Ye always carried a small bamboo tube on its leg for delivering messages. Qin Shaozong twisted off the wooden lid, only to find that inside...","\"Is this mud?\" Feng Feng looked at the substance Qin Shaozong had poured out.","Qin Shaozong casually kicked aside a corpse blocking his path and walked over to a nearby torch.","The bright light illuminated the handful of mud-like substance in his palm with absolute clarity. It was yellowish-brown and was indeed mud, but mixed within it were obvious traces of ash and some fine, shredded pieces of yellow paper.","\"What is this?\" Feng Feng could not make sense of it.","Qin Shaozong pinched a tiny scrap of the yellow paper between his fingers. \"It looks a bit like yellow paper.\"","Yellow paper—this was an item used for sacrificial offerings.","\"Are there any temples outside Xiagu City?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","Feng Feng actually did know. \"There is one in the southern outskirts of the city, but it has been abandoned for a long time. Lord Marquis, do you suspect that Lao Mo followed Madam Dai into that temple?\"","\"Nine times out of ten, yes.\" Qin Shaozong dusted the mud and ash from his hand.","Feng Feng said with regret, \"It is a pity that we are short on manpower right now. We cannot spare anyone from their posts, nor is it a good idea to open the city gates. Otherwise, we could head straight there and invite Madam Dai back.\"","\"Heading south... they want to go to Yuzhou. Let her roam free out there for a little while longer.\" Qin Shaozong instinctively reached to twist his jade thumb ring but found nothing there. He casually lowered his hand as if nothing had happened.","\"Go back. Return in a few days.\"","The gyrfalcon was released into the air. With a powerful flap of its wings, it swiftly flew toward the south.","A small courtyard in the northern district.","\"Where is Diting? Have you managed to contact Diting yet?\" Xie Yuanxiu paced back and forth across the room.","The oil lamp on the table flickered gently in the draft. Xie Yuanxiu's shadow moved back and forth along with him, occasionally distorted by the wind into bizarre, eerie shapes, resembling a trapped beast brandishing its fangs and claws.","\"We have already dispatched more men to search for him, but there is no news yet,\" his confidant replied.","Xie Yuanxiu could not help but feel a pang of regret.","Back when Diting had arranged for him to stay here, if only he had invited the man to stay with him, he wouldn't be in this situation of not being able to find him.","Gao You was also present. This once-glorious Prefect now did not even dare to return to his own manor. His lips trembled as he asked, \"Third Young Master, when will the reinforcements outside the city be able to enter?\"","It would have been better had he kept his mouth shut. The moment he brought this up, Xie Yuanxiu flew into a rage. \"If it weren't for the fact that your city guards are completely useless, Prefect Gao, how could my cavalry outside the city fail to break in?\"","The city guards, combined with his own men, numbered a full thousand.","Yes, he admitted that the city's terrain provided an advantage, with streets, alleys, and shops serving as cover. But there was absolutely no reason why a thousand men attacking together could not take down the Marquis of Wu'an's mere two hundred men.","It was utterly absurd!","Gao You was rendered speechless, a faint sprout of regret beginning to take root in his heart.","Xie Yuanxiu gritted his teeth and said, \"My thousands of infantrymen will arrive soon. They are bringing battering rams and siege ladders. When they get here, the city gates will surely fall. So what if the Marquis of Wu'an's soldiers are battle-hardened elites? When my great army bears down on the city, we can grind them to death just by exhausting them with sheer numbers.\"","Gao You did not reply; instead, he looked out the window.","The night was pitch black and seemingly endless, as if concealing countless man-eating beasts.","He had constantly heard Third Young Master Xie mentioning \"Diting.\" Just what kind of extraordinary figure was this, that Xie Yuanxiu was so desperate to see him even at such a critical juncture?","And to make matters worse, this \"extraordinary figure\" had gone missing.","The unease in Gao You's heart began to spread.","The morning light broke, and the horizon turned the pale white of a fish's belly. A new day arrived as promised.","Although they had spent the night in a ruined temple, perhaps because their path forward was gradually becoming clearer, or perhaps because all the other occupants of the temple had been chased out, Dai Li slept much more soundly than she had expected.","Upon waking up, Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou continued their journey without a moment's delay.","They no longer tried to drive Mo Yanyun away. Of course, even if they had tried, they would not have succeeded.","No one else had approached the temple throughout the entire night. Not only did Mo Yanyun refrain from harming their horses, but he had even helped dispatch a restless bandit who was itching to make a move.","It was difficult to shake him off now, mainly because he kept a very close eye on his own horse. Furthermore, there was only one official road, and traveling on horseback meant they had no choice but to follow it.","The mother and son could only tacitly allow him to trail behind them.","Walking one after another, they kept a fair distance between them. Even if Mo Yanyun stopped his horse, Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou would not look back to wait for him.","Therefore, neither mother nor son noticed that when Mo Yanyun stopped, a gyrfalcon landed silently.","After traveling for another day, they arrived at Qin Yanzhou's planned second stop: a small mountain village.","The small mountain village was situated halfway up the hills, surrounded by mountains on all sides, with a stream winding through it. There were not many people in the village, only twenty or thirty households. When Dai Li and her group arrived, it was already dusk. The horse hooves trod on the shattered golden sunset, startling the birds resting on the branches.","Strangers rarely visited the village, so when the sound of horse hooves approached, many villagers poked their heads out. However, upon seeing Mo Yanyun with a sword hanging at his waist, they quickly pulled their heads back and shut their windows with a loud bang.","Mo Yanyun was not surprised by this.","The world was becoming increasingly chaotic. These days, ordinary people avoided anyone carrying a sword like the plague. It seemed that Madam Dai and the young master would have to put in a lot of effort to find a place to stay tonight.","Just as he was thinking this, Mo Yanyun saw Qin Yanzhou rein in his horse in front of a house.","He dismounted and knocked on the door. After a short while, the door opened a palm's width, faintly revealing a woman inside. Her hair was coiled in a bun, and she wore hemp clothing—the most ordinary attire.","The distance was a bit far, so Mo Yanyun could not hear what Qin Yanzhou said. But he saw that in just a few words, the previously defensive peasant woman actually opened her door completely on her own initiative, her face full of smiles as she welcomed the two inside.","Mo Yanyun was dumbfounded.","Why was this? Could it be that they knew each other?","He subconsciously wanted to follow them, but just as he took two steps, he saw the young man shoot a sideways glance at him.","He said to the peasant woman, \"That one is not with us.\"","Mo Yanyun: \"...\"","\"Hey, hey, how am I not? We are traveling together!\" With a house to sleep in, Mo Yanyun had no desire to sleep on the streets. Seeing that Qin Yanzhou was unmoved, he hurriedly looked at Dai Li. \"Madam Dai, please have mercy, for the sake of the Lord...\"","The words had reached his lips, but Mo Yanyun made a rare and clever pivot. \"For the sake of Mister Nalan, please let me have a roof over my head tonight.\"","Dai Li pondered for a moment.","Qin Shaozong's man had been following her, which made her very uneasy.","But without making an enemy of the Northern Lands, the only way to shake him off was to wait until they reached the border of Yuzhou, enter the city, and use the crowd to slip away. Zhouzhou said that after leaving this small village, it would only take one more day to reach Yuzhou.","Just endure for one more day!","\"Let him sleep indoors. Zhouzhou, you stay with him.\" Dai Li was worried that Mo Yanyun would do something to the horses.","If he crippled their horses and rode back alone to report the news, it would be troublesome.","Qin Yanzhou nodded.","Xiagu Commandery.","The beautiful and handsome gyrfalcon flew back once again, and Qin Shaozong took out the small bamboo tube tied to Bai Ye's leg.","Last time, it was gray mud and yellow paper scraps. This time, the small bamboo tube contained a small piece of broken tile.","\"A broken tile?\" Kuang Ye looked at the object in Qin Shaozong's hand. He looked gentle, but his words hit the nail on the head. \"Has Madam Dai reached a populated area?\"","A sheepskin map had long been spread out on the desk, clearly showing the terrain and landforms around Xiagu.","To the south of Xiagu was a ruined temple. Further south, until they reached Nanyang County at the border of Yuzhou, there would be no more small towns of any considerable size.","And from the ruined temple to Nanyang County, ordinary travel could not cover the distance in a single day.","They definitely had not reached Yuzhou yet, but Lao Mo had sent back a broken tile, which likely meant they had found a populated area along the way. It could be a village in the mountains, or it could be a hunter living alone in the mountains south of the city.","Qin Shaozong set the broken tile aside and ordered someone to bring two wild hares, feeding them to Bai Ye himself.","The sharp beak pecked off a large chunk of meat at a time, tearing and swallowing, sending bits of meat flying. Before long, the two plump rabbits ended up in Bai Ye's stomach.","\"Go back.\"","After Qin Shaozong released Bai Ye, his gaze remained on the map, but whereas he was looking south before, he was now looking east.","During the day today, the Sizhou soldiers in the city, led by Xie Yuanxiu, gathered the military patrol and launched another battle to seize the city gates.","Xiagu was just an ordinary commandery. Its armed forces had been strengthened somewhat after the emergence of the warlord fragmentation, but the total number of soldiers combined was only a little over seven hundred. Yesterday, the military patrol took the lead and suffered four hundred casualties.","Xie Yuanxiu originally had over four hundred men. Yesterday, a hundred died in battle, leaving about three hundred now. Combined with the remnants of the military patrol, they formed an army of over six hundred men.","As if knowing that with each passing day, the level of danger increased by a fraction, the enemy's offensive was particularly fierce today. They did not divide their forces but focused their fire on the east gate, determined to tear an opening in this corner.","The entire day was a bloody battle.","Qin Shaozong led by example, the ring-pommel sword in his hand hacked until the edge was curled, and blood flowed like a river beneath his feet.","The combined army of six hundred worked together, but they still failed to break through the defense line of the Xuanxiao Cavalry. Towards the end of the battle, the most fragile local military patrol was the first to have deserters.","This desertion was disastrous; the military morale collapsed.","Outside, Ni Chiwen listened to the sounds of killing inside the city, his blood boiling. He was filled with energy and wished he could scale the walls and slaughter everyone inside.","Unfortunately, without scaling ladders and battering rams, their thousand cavalrymen could only stand helplessly outside the city, scratching their heads in frustration as they stared at the tightly shut gates.","\"The sounds of killing seem to have stopped,\" Li Huairen said in a low voice.","It had indeed stopped, but there was no movement at the city gates, and the result was obvious.","Sizhou's second round of siege had returned in defeat.","Ni Chiwen frowned and asked Li Huairen, \"How many soldiers did the Third Young Master lead into the city initially?\"","\"Four hundred,\" Li Huairen said hesitantly. \"They fought a battle yesterday, and another one today. I'm afraid all the men have been wiped out.\"","Ni Chiwen irritably grabbed a handful of his hair. \"That's terrible. We can only wait for the infantry to arrive from behind. But if we drag this out any longer, there's no guarantee that the Northern Lands' reinforcements won't arrive as well.\"","Li Huairen maintained an optimistic attitude about this. \"It shouldn't be that bad. The Marquis of Wu'an has only been in Xiagu for less than four days. Even if he sent someone back to Bairi City on the day he arrived in Xiagu, traveling far by boat takes time. After returning to the army, assembling troops and horses also takes time, not to mention the journey here. Just relax, the next ten days are a safe period.\"","\"In five days, we will send scouts to the eastern road to gather intelligence. We will definitely be able to find out the whereabouts of the enemy's reinforcements.\"","The night had grown to its darkest. A thick, heavy darkness dyed the entire sky, covering both the bright moon and the myriad stars.","If one looked down from high above, in this pitch-black night where one could not see their own fingers, a faintly discernible fire dragon appeared on the ground.","This long-galloping fire dragon came from the east, winding its way along the official road. It did not rest day or night, moving at an extremely fast speed, continuously rushing past several commanderies and counties.","After a long and arduous journey, this illustrious and renowned cavalry finally saw their target city in the distance.","\"Extinguish the torches.\" With a single command, all the torches were put out.","The cavalry slipped into the darkness like ghosts. The majority stayed where they were, while only a small detachment continued forward, stealthily making their way to the foot of the city wall.","Bai Jianping, who was on guard duty at the east gate, suddenly heard a few bird calls. He was exceptionally sensitive to the cries of birds and beasts, even able to discern the emotions within them. Now, hearing this familiar bird whistle, he immediately shuddered.","His sleepiness dissipated, instantly replaced by a fierce surge of excitement.","He looked down from the city walls, straining his eyes until he finally managed to spot a few cavalrymen in the dark night. Bai Jianping replied with a bird whistle, signaling for the men to wait quietly. He then immediately turned back to report the good news of the reinforcements' arrival to Qin Shaozong.","\"...My Lord, I request to join the vanguard!\" Bai Jianping, Feng Feng, and several others rubbed their hands together, itching for a fight.","\"Feng Feng, you will guard the city. Bai Jianping, you will come with me,\" Qin Shaozong ordered. With that, he led ten soldiers carrying heavy burlap sacks out of the city.","The eastern gate quietly opened a narrow crack. Qin Shaozong and his men filed out to rendezvous with the main army.","\"Distribute the burlap. Pass down my orders: muffle the horses' hooves with the cloth and rest in place for two shichen. We depart at the Hour of Yin. Once we move out, absolute silence is required.\" The orders spread through the ranks like wildfire.","The ten heavy sacks from earlier were filled with strips of burlap, which were quickly handed out and wrapped securely around the horses' hooves.","The Xuanxiao Cavalry had traveled tirelessly under the stars and moon, and they were truly exhausted. Now given the order to rest, the soldiers fell asleep the moment they hit the ground. Soon, a chorus of snores rose from the surroundings.","Qin Shaozong's steed, Crimson Dragon, was also brought over. In the darkness, the majestic large red horse snorted and let out a soft whinny, delighted to be reunited with its master.","Qin Shaozong patted the horse's head.","While everyone else rested, Qin Shaozong sat beneath a tree with his arms crossed, his eyes closed to conserve his energy. He did not sleep; instead, he silently counted down the time remaining until the Hour of Yin.","The Hour of Yin, the final stretch before dawn, when the night was at its darkest and thickest. It was the absolute perfect time for a sneak attack.","The enemy would never expect his cavalry to reach Xia Valley tonight. Completely off guard, they would be no different from lambs waiting to be slaughtered.","Time slowly slipped by, and before long, the Hour of Yin arrived.","A bird whistle pierced the air, and the Xuanxiao Cavalry roused at the sound. After a brief rest, these elites, whose physical endurance far surpassed that of ordinary soldiers, were once again brimming with vigor.","Qin Shaozong vaulted onto his horse. Just before they set off, he cast a glance toward the south.","Let her enjoy her freedom for one more day."]},{"number":84,"title":"Chapter 84","paragraphs":["West of the city.","Tonight was the second night Ni Chiwen's cavalry had been camped outside the city. It had not been long, but he was exceptionally anxious. Because after the next day, their logistical supplies would be completely exhausted.","During their rapid march, he had assumed they could enter the city immediately, so he had only brought a day and a half's worth of dry rations. Now, the food was gone, and they could not enter Xiagu. He was caught in a dilemma.","Ni Chiwen had no choice but to consider leading his army back.","He had to go back; they were out of food.","But that was a matter for tomorrow. Tonight, he would at least get a good night's sleep.","In the middle of the night, Ni Chiwen, who was sleeping directly on the ground, was jolted awake. He was using his saddle as a pillow and his cloak as a blanket, making do as best as he could.","Precisely because he was sleeping on his side with his head resting on the saddle, Ni Chiwen, a rather light sleeper, was awakened in the middle of the night by a rumbling sound coming from beneath his ear.","At first, he thought it was thunder, assuming the summer sky was about to rain, but after he rolled over and lay flat on his back, the rumbling disappeared.","Oh, it was not thunder.","Closing his eyes and just about to fall back asleep, Ni Chiwen suddenly felt as if his temple had been struck by a heavy hammer. His mind reeled, and in a massive wave of horror, he sprang up into a sitting position.","He quickly pressed himself back to the ground, listening closely with his ear.","There was indeed a rumbling sound, like ten thousand horses galloping together. But just by listening, he could not tell if it was coming from the east or the west.","Ni Chiwen woke up Li Huairen and asked him, \"Besides us, did the Third Young Master notify any other allies to join the campaign against the North?\"","\"What other allies? No...\" Li Huairen replied groggily.","Ni Chiwen gasped, then hurriedly roared at the top of his lungs, \"Everyone up! Enemy attack!\"","His voice rang like a massive bell, jolting a group of soldiers awake.","The soldiers, roused from their slumber, shuddered in unison.","What? Where is the enemy attack?","Did they not say the northern reinforcements would not arrive for at least another ten days?!","One by one, they sat up, but all the movements around them were from their own people. Looking out into the vast, hazy night, there was clearly no firelight.","Enemy attack? It must be a mistake.","With their nerves tensing and then relaxing, many began to yawn incessantly. Some, seeing that everything was peaceful, even fell straight back down to sleep.","Ni Chiwen flew into a rage. \"Whoever dares to go back to sleep will be dealt with by military law!\"","The soldiers opened their eyes again, but Ni Chiwen did not need to say anything more, because they all heard the commotion.","A muffled sound came from the east, rolling in like crashing waves, its momentum growing increasingly terrifying as it drew nearer.","This time, without Ni Chiwen having to repeat himself, the Sizhou soldiers were all struck with terror.","There really was an enemy attack!","The Black Valiant Cavalry was equipped with the best horses from the North. Especially after Qin Shaozong conquered the Northern Kingdom, all the fine-breed horses there had fallen into his hands. The absolute best of the best, carefully handpicked, were now all with the Black Valiant Cavalry.","As for the Sizhou side, they had all previously assumed the northern reinforcements would not arrive for at least a few days. Well then, since that was the case, they were not in combat readiness.","To sleep more comfortably, everyone had taken off their saddles to use as pillows.","Taking them off was easy, and sleeping on them was relatively comfortable. But now, the surrounding light was dim, with only a few fire braziers placed on the periphery to ward off wild beasts. Quickly putting the saddles back on was no easy task.","Just finding their horses and seeing the buckles was a massive undertaking.","Since they had already been exposed, Qin Shaozong simply roared, \"Follow me and kill!\"","Under the dark night, this black-armored cavalry seemed to transform into a pack of wolves. The strong, ferocious wolves charged into the flock of lambs, frantically tearing at their prey with fangs and claws.","Screams rose and fell in succession. Bright red blood splattered, spilling onto the ground and seeping into the soil, dyeing it a macabre hue.","Heads rolled, their faces frozen in expressions of wide-eyed terror.","Ni Chiwen was frantic, organizing a counterattack while simultaneously searching for the enemy commander.","The wind picked up in the night, blowing apart the continuous dark clouds and revealing the full moon.","Bright moonlight descended upon the world once more. Across a distance, Ni Chiwen spotted a man not far away, a red cape billowing behind him.","The man had a towering, imposing figure and rode an exceptionally robust jujube-red horse. As the moonlight cascaded down, his helmet, adorned with golden Taotie patterns, cast a small shadow over his face.","Ni Chiwen could only vaguely make out the man's sharply contoured profile: prominent brow ridges, a straight nose, and a sharp, smooth jawline that resembled an unsheathed blade.","Suddenly, the man in the distance looked over.","Those brown eyes seemed tinged with the eerie green of a ferocious wolf. In the next instant, Ni Chiwen saw the corner of the man's lips curl up.","After Qin Shaozong led his troops charging into the enemy camp, he had been searching for the Sizhou general the entire time.","To catch bandits, first catch the ringleader. What was the point of killing the underlings? He had to take out the leader first.","Initially, Qin Shaozong thought he would have to search for quite a while. After all, the lighting was not bright, and they did not have military tents, so he could only look slowly.","As it turned out, the moon came out, and someone not far away was staring right at him, with a red cape lying at his feet.","Qin Shaozong curled his thin lips. \"Heaven is helping me!\"","The Chijiao horse shared a telepathic connection with its master. Rearing its hooves, it kicked away a Sizhou soldier blocking the path and charged straight toward Ni Chiwen.","Qin Shaozong raised his long spear and delivered a strike.","The silver spear clashed with the broadsword. One man was mounted on horseback, wielding a silver spear from a commanding height; the other stood on the ground, gripping a broadsword with both hands.","Ni Chiwen's arms went numb from the impact, but before he could even catch his breath, the second strike arrived. Although the silver spear only had the spearhead as its point of attack, an inch longer meant an inch stronger. Right now, he was completely being beaten one-sidedly.","As Qin Shaozong advanced, the gleaming spearhead was like a snake bearing venomous fangs, swift and agile, making Ni Chiwen's heart tremble incessantly.","One advanced, one retreated. In the blink of an eye, Ni Chiwen's back hit a tree trunk.","There was nowhere left to retreat.","Ni Chiwen thought to himself that this was bad, just as he saw the red-tasseled spearhead striking again. With no room to retreat, he could only grip the hilt with one hand, hold the long blade horizontally, and support the back of the blade with his other hand to block.","Clang!","The spearhead struck the flat of the blade. The point that received the immense force began to crack, and the fractures rapidly spread across the entire blade.","Crack. Something shattered.","Ni Chiwen's pupils suddenly widened. His gaze, which had been fixed straight at the man in front of him, shifted down slightly, landing on the silver spear that was now connected to his throat bone.","A trail of bright red trickled from the corner of his mouth. He opened his mouth but could not make a single sound. He could only watch helplessly as the man in front of him pulled his arm back, taking the silver spear that had pierced his throat along with it.","Qin Shaozong coldly watched Ni Chiwen fall to the ground. Drawing the ring-pommel sword at his side, he cleanly severed his head. Then, he picked it up from the bottom with his silver spear and hoisted it high. \"Your leader is dead! Those who surrender will be spared!\"","Under the moonlight, Ni Chiwen's hoisted head caught the eyes of many.","Everything around them came to a standstill. Suddenly, with a few clangs, someone dropped their weapon first.","More and more people surrendered. Qin Shaozong ordered his men to light fires for illumination.","Soon, the firelight flared up, casting its glow on the black-armored northern soldiers. Each of them was bathed in blood, like ferocious wolves baring their bloodstained fangs.","The night raid was a blitzkrieg; it came fast and ended fast. After a tally, only four out of ten Sizhou soldiers remained. Their horses had scattered in fright, so a good number of those were left behind.","Qin Shaozong confiscated all the weapons and horses of the surrendered soldiers, then singled out the commander of the Southern Garrison. \"Bai Jianping, lead three hundred men to escort these captives back to the city first. Afterward, lead your troops out of the city and head west along the official road of Sizhou.\"","Bai Jianping's heart gave a jolt.","Head west, along the official road of Sizhou?","Did the Marquis intend to swallow the reinforcements trailing behind Sizhou in one fell swoop?","Qin Shaozong reorganized his troops and marched west without a moment's pause. He indeed planned to strike while the iron was hot and devour the rest of the Sizhou army behind them.","This cavalry unit had not even set up camp, meaning they must have force-marched to the western suburbs. Behind such a vanguard, there was bound to be an infantry battalion dragging along supplies.","A victorious battle had thoroughly ignited the soldiers' blood. Why not ride the momentum and take down the forces behind them?","The Black Valiant Cavalry swiftly split into two, with the main force following Qin Shaozong westward. He did not know exactly how far away the Sizhou infantry was, but since the Sizhou cavalry had already arrived at the western suburbs two days prior, they couldn't be far.","Indeed, they were not far. After just a two-hour rapid march, as the sky grew faintly bright, Qin Shaozong spotted the encampment in the distance.","Tents were pitched one after another. To Qin Shaozong, they looked somewhat like the meat buns his wife had invented. Thin skin and generous filling—just a light slash, and one could taste the savory meat inside.","The man curled his lips into a smile, his eyes filled with sheer excitement.","...","By the time Bai Jianping escorted the captives back to the city and hurried over with his three hundred men, the battle was surprisingly already over.","Broken halberds were planted at an angle in the ground, and longbows lay with snapped strings. Some military tents had collapsed, their surfaces splattered with streaks of blood. The ground was a mess; the wooden frames originally used to hold fire basins were scattered in pieces, having long lost their original shape.","There was no need to even mention the sheer number of corpses; this entire stretch of land had changed color. Meanwhile, the granary area, previously managed by the Sizhou army's cooks, had now changed hands.","Qin Shaozong did not burn the granary. Instead, seeing that the situation was dire, the Sizhou side had attempted to set it on fire so the enemy wouldn't benefit, but unfortunately for them, they were stopped midway.","Seeing Bai Jianping arrive, a soldier hurriedly came forward. \"Garrison Commander Bai, we roughly estimate the enemy had about three thousand men. This time, our army killed over half of them, and we captured more than two hundred heads of cattle and sheep, as well as three hundred shi of grain...\"","Bai Jianping found it strange. Why report these things to him? \"Where is the Marquis?\"","\"The Marquis took a squad and headed south. He said he was going to pick up Madam Dai, and left everything here entirely in your hands,\" the soldier replied.","Bai Jianping was stunned and blurted out, \"The Marquis left that quickly?\"","He had just devoured the Sizhou infantry—before even fully swallowing them, he had hurried off to another place.","Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou left the small mountain village at the break of dawn, continuing their journey south.","Mo Yanyun was still following them, but just as they left the village, he realized his horse... had a problem.","His horse was suffering from severe diarrhea, to the point of exhaustion. Its legs grew weak, and it walked slower and slower.","At first, Mo Yanyun tried to turn the tide, but his efforts ended in failure. His horse eventually collapsed to the ground, foaming at the mouth.","Watching the single horse ahead rapidly pull away from him, Mo Yanyun broke into a panicked sweat. \"Hey, how can you not play by the rules of martial virtue!\"","As soon as the words left his mouth, he realized something was wrong.","He had secretly tipped off the Marquis, which wasn't exactly keeping his word either. Wait, they tampered with his horse—could it be that they had discovered his little tricks?","\"Madam Dai, please wait!\" Mo Yanyun roared.","The two people ahead turned a deaf ear. Their horse trotted further and further away, and in just a moment, it was nothing but a small silhouette.","Mo Yanyun felt as if he had been struck by lightning, his heart turning to ashes. \"It's over, it's over, I'm going to lose them again...\"","It was different from last time. Last time, they were not far from the city, and he could just walk back. But this place was a whole day's journey from Xiagu. By the time he endured untold hardships to get back to the city, those two would have long disappeared without a trace.","So Madam Dai did it on purpose, right? She specifically chose to make her move in this barren wilderness.","Oh, well, it wasn't exactly a barren wilderness. At least there was a village behind him; she had at least left him an out.","Since the horse couldn't be ridden anytime soon, Mo Yanyun scratched his head in frustration and finally decided to walk back to the village to borrow a donkey.","Madam Dai and the young gentleman were sharing a single horse. Even if it was a fine steed, its speed wouldn't be as fast as a solo rider. If he borrowed a donkey to chase after them, though he certainly wouldn't catch up, at least he wouldn't be left stranded in place.","The idea was beautiful, but when Mo Yanyun returned to the village, he discovered...","No one would lend him a donkey.","To the villagers, he was a stranger. How could they easily lend him such an important piece of property as a donkey?","As for buying a donkey, he didn't have enough money, making it impossible to purchase one.","Mo Yanyun broke down. He trudged heavily back to the sick horse. Recalling the herbs Mr. Ding had given him when he was ill before, he muttered to himself, \"I'll just treat a dead horse as a living one. Otherwise, there's nothing else I can do.\"","He opened his eyes wide and searched through the surrounding grass.","Believe it or not, he actually found a familiar-looking plant. He immediately fed it to the horse and then used his waterskin to pour water down its throat.","Mo Yanyun waited and waited. Two hours passed, then four hours passed...","After the golden sun reached its zenith, it slowly began to slant toward the west.","Just as Mo Yanyun was on the verge of despair, his horse—whether it had recovered from eating the herbs or simply pulled through on its own—finally regained some vigor.","Mo Yanyun quickly mounted the horse and continued his pursuit south along the official road.","Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou had already traveled quite a distance. It was now early afternoon. If nothing unexpected happened, they would cross the border of Sizhou and enter Nanyang County in four hours.","As long as they entered Yuzhou, it would be absolutely impossible for Qin Shaozong to brazenly send troops to search for them.","Summer weather was like a child's face, changing at the drop of a hat. Just moments ago, the bright sun had been hanging high in the sky, but now a thick, heavy dark cloud suddenly drifted over. It looked like it was going to rain.","Dai Li looked up at the sky, only to unexpectedly spot a bird circling overhead.","Its feathers were white with a touch of brown. Though it was far away, Dai Li estimated that the bird's wingspan was over half a meter.","Over half a meter was considered a medium size in the avian world.","Dai Li kept her head tilted upward for quite a while, prompting Qin Yanzhou to look up as well.","\"Zhou Zhou, is it just my imagination, or has it been hovering right above us this whole time?\" Dai Li murmured.","Birds were much faster than horses. Unless there was food, birds of prey generally wouldn't circle in the same spot. This bird was incredibly strange.","Qin Yanzhou watched it for a long time. \"That looks like a Haidongqing.\"","At these words, Dai Li's face paled. \"A Haidongqing? Zhou Zhou, are you sure?\"","Qin Yanzhou said yes.","\"This is a bird of prey only found in the northeastern regions. We're about to enter Yuzhou territory; logically, it shouldn't be here. Has Qin Shaozong caught up to us, or is it a gyrfalcon raised by the people of the Green Lotus Cult?\" Dai Li said nervously.","Before Qin Yanzhou could answer, a faint memory surfaced in Dai Li's mind. \"I think I've seen it before. This is the gyrfalcon raised by Qin Shaozong!\"","What else was there to misunderstand? Mo Yanyun must have brought this Haidongqing along with him.","\"Zhou Zhou, it seems we'll have to brave the rain and press on,\" Dai Li said gravely.","Heavy rain would weigh down a bird of prey, and rarely would any avian brave such a downpour. They had to make their escape now, while the gyrfalcon was grounded.","Once they reached the city and melted into the crowd, the bird would definitely lose their trail.","Qin Yanzhou lowered his voice to comfort her, \"Mother, please do not worry. From what I have gathered, the Sizhou infantry, equipped with battering rams and scaling ladders, is set to arrive at Xiagu today. The Marquis of Wu'an has so few men at his disposal that he will surely be overwhelmed; he will have no energy to spare for anything else. We have already shaken off Mo Yanyun. Once we are inside the city walls, we will be able to lose this gyrfalcon overhead as well.\"","Dai Li murmured her agreement.","Her son's reasoning was sound. Yet, for some inexplicable reason, the lingering unease in her heart only grew heavier, as though something terrible was about to happen..."]},{"number":85,"title":"Chapter 85","paragraphs":["Dark clouds loomed overhead, yet the rain held back until the moment Dai Li and Zhou Zhou arrived in Nanyang County.","Nanyang was merely a county, and its scale could not compare to that of a prefecture. The mother and son arrived just as the curfew was beginning. Unable to worry about anything else, they found the nearest inn to stay for the night.","Dai Li used travel documents identifying her as a merchant's wife, while Zhou Zhou had his own. They booked two adjacent rooms. After having dinner in the main hall, they returned upstairs.","Zhou Zhou followed Dai Li into her room first, carefully inspecting every corner to see if the accommodations truly lived up to the \"first-class\" standard the young attendant had boasted about.","Dai Li stood by the window, leaning out to look. \"Zhou Zhou, that gyrfalcon, Bai Ye, is still there.\"","\"Time was tight today, so I couldn't deal with it. Tomorrow, I'll find a bow and shoot that bird down,\" Zhou Zhou said, already forming a plan.","Dai Li nodded in agreement.","Just then, two attendants entered carrying wooden tubs filled with water. This was an additional service Dai Li had requested when they first checked in. By the time they finished dinner downstairs, the water was ready.","\"Mother, I'll keep watch for you outside the door,\" Zhou Zhou said as he stepped out.","Dai Li waved a hand. \"No need. You've been exhausted all day; go back to your room and rest. These rooms are close together. If anything happens, I'll just shout.\"","Zhou Zhou hesitated for a moment before finally nodding.","Once everyone had left, Dai Li began to undress for her bath. Staying in a farmer's house in a small village the night before had been a blessing—simply having a roof over their heads and not sleeping on the streets was good enough. One couldn't ask for more.","As for the night before that, there was no need to even mention it; the environment of the ruined temple had been far worse.","But that was all in the past. Now, she and Zhou Zhou had entered Yuzhou and were finally out of Qin Shaozong's territory. Once they dealt with that gyrfalcon, Bai Ye, she and her son would head further south. Ideally, they would pick a small county neighboring a prefecture where the provincial governor resided.","When the time came, they would buy a small house, plant some flowers, and raise a cat or a dog.","Zhou Zhou was nineteen this year; he was old enough to start dating girls. No, that wasn't how it worked here. Here, it was all about parental commands and matchmakers. The process was quite different, but there would be a way...","Dai Li placed a warm towel over her face and let out a contented sigh.","***","Mo Yanyun rode his half-dead horse alone along the mountain path. He hadn't set out again until the afternoon and had traveled until deep into the night, barely reaching the vicinity of Nanyang County.","Suddenly, Mo Yanyun heard a low rumbling.","At first, he thought it was thunder, but a moment later, he realized it was clearly the sound of galloping hooves.","He was currently at a crossroads. Ahead lay Nanyang County, behind him was the road he had come from, and the third path was the official highway leading northwest.","Mo Yanyun muttered to himself, \"It seems to be coming from the northwest. Who would be traveling at night at this hour? Could it be reinforcements from Sizhou trying to bypass the area to reach the east of Xiagu City? But that doesn't make sense. If they wanted to bypass it, they could do it anywhere. Why take such a long detour?\"","Regardless of whether it made sense or not, he quickly dismounted and led his horse into the nearby bushes, doing his best to hide.","\"Well, thank goodness it's dark. I shouldn't be noticed.\" Mo Yanyun began to wait.","Within moments, the troop arrived.","The night was pitch black, making it impossible to see exactly who was leading them, but he could make out the general shape of the force. The cavalry was swallowed by the darkness, their powerful horses galloping with a grand momentum. The soldiers were all clad in uniform black light armor.","Mo Yanyun stared blankly.","Something was definitely wrong. The more he looked, the more familiar they seemed.","Suddenly, he shuddered. This looked like his own lord's cavalry!","Mo Yanyun immediately jumped out and shouted, \"Xuanxiao Cavalry, wait!\"","The cavalry moved with incredible speed. By the time Mo Yanyun shouted, only the tail end of the troop remained. As his voice fell, someone at the very front reined in their horse and ordered a halt. The entire column quickly came to a stop.","Mo Yanyun hurried forward on his horse. Before he had gone far, a towering, imposing figure gradually became clear in the darkness.","Mo Yanyun was shocked. \"My Lord? Why have you come...\"","\"Where is my wife?\" Qin Shaozong asked in a deep voice.","Mo Yanyun felt as if his throat had been suddenly seized. His mouth hung open, but no sound came out; he couldn't utter a single word.","\"Mo Yanyun.\"","Mo Yanyun wanted to cry but had no tears. \"My Lord, I lost them. At first, Lady Dai let me follow, but after staying a night in a small village... no, yesterday morning, I realized my horse was unwell. It seemed to have been poisoned. I couldn't keep up with Lady Dai and the young master.\"","As he spoke, the atmospheric pressure around them plummeted. Mo Yanyun sensed danger and quickly finished his explanation:","\"The gyrfalcon, Bai Ye, shouldn't have been discovered yet. At least, everything was normal until my horse had its accident. Furthermore, Nanyang County is just ahead. Lady Dai and the young master are sharing one horse, so they definitely aren't moving fast. I suspect they entered the city around the end of the Shen hour yesterday. Time was tight; even if they noticed Bai Ye, they probably wouldn't have had time to deal with it yet.\"","For the first time, Mo Yanyun felt his brain working at lightning speed.","He carefully observed his superior. He noticed that while the man's expression hadn't exactly softened, the terrifying pressure from before had dissipated slightly.","Qin Shaozong simply said, \"Keep up on your own.\"","Mo Yanyun's face fell.","Keep up?","His horse was in such a state; he couldn't keep up!","But Qin Shaozong clearly had no intention of coddling him. After leaving those words, he turned his horse around.","This location was not far from Nanyang County. An hour later, Qin Shaozong arrived outside the walls.","Whether it was a prefecture or a county, all city walls were thicker at the bottom and narrower at the top, built with a certain slope rather than being perfectly vertical. The difference lay in the fact that prefecture walls were higher and smoother, like those in Xiagu. County walls, however, were shorter, and due to lax supervision, there were many gaps and protrusions between the bricks. Nanyang County was a prime example of the latter.","The former was difficult to scale, while the latter provided numerous footholds. Without interference, a daring person could climb the wall quite rapidly.","Qin Shaozong looked up at the height of the wall.","It was a bit over twenty feet, not quite thirty. Not very high at all.","Mo Yanyun, who had swapped horses with one of the Xuanxiao Cavalry, caught up. He volunteered, hoping to make up for his failure. \"My Lord, I wish to lead a few men up to open the gates.\"","Qin Shaozong granted permission.","In the darkness, a dozen figures flipped off their horses in unison. With swift strides, they reached the base of the wall and began to climb with practiced ease.","They clung to the wall like geckos, focused only on moving upward without looking back. Within moments, the dozen figures reached the top one after another.","A brief commotion broke out atop the wall, but it was quickly silenced.","A short while later, the relatively light city gates slowly creaked open.","***","Dai Li was sleeping in the middle of the night when she was suddenly startled awake by a crack of thunder. The summer was hot, so she hadn't closed her window before going to bed. Now, the wind was howling inside, rattling the window shutters and making the wooden hinges creak.","The sound was truly irritating. Dai Li listened for a moment before she couldn't take it anymore and got up to close the window.","The thunder rumbled loudly, sounding as if it were trying to tear through the sky. Purple lightning danced across the clouds, connecting to form a massive, terrifying web that seemed intent on catching every stray soul beneath it.","Dai Li glanced toward the roof across the way. The gyrfalcon, Bai Ye, which had been perched there earlier, was gone.","It had probably gone to seek shelter from the rain.","Dai Li closed the window and lay back down in bed. But before she could drift into a deep sleep, she thought she heard a knock at the door.","It was urgent, a sound that sent an inexplicable chill through her heart in the middle of the restless night.","\"Mother...\"","Dai Li’s eyes snapped open. It wasn’t an illusion or a dream; it was Zhou Zhou calling for her from outside.","She scrambled out of bed to open the door.","As the wooden hinges creaked open, Dai Li saw Zhou Zhou standing there. \"Zhou Zhou, what is—\"","Before she could finish her question, he cut her off.","\"The Marquis of Wu'an's men have found us. There are many of them, and they're already downstairs.\" A rare, visible flash of anxiety flickered in Zhou Zhou's eyes.","Dai Li froze, the color draining from her face instantly.","They were staying on the second floor. She hadn't noticed anything earlier, but now that her son had mentioned it, she realized the commotion downstairs was far too loud. On a night when everyone should have been sound asleep, the lights below were blazing, and voices were echoing.","The mother and son stood on the second-floor landing. The guesthouse was designed with a high ceiling, leaving part of the first floor open to view from above. From their vantage point on the stairs, they could see everything happening below.","At that moment, the guesthouse doors were flung wide. Two soldiers in black armor stood guard at the entrance, while two small oil lamps flickered on a table, their flames dancing in the draft.","The man leading them stood over eight feet tall. Clad in black armor and a crimson cloak, his massive silhouette loomed like an insurmountable mountain under the dim light. His dark red cloak flared with sharp, lethal edges as he moved, resembling a blade that had just drank its fill of blood.","Dai Li’s pupils trembled.","It wasn't just Qin Shaozong's subordinates. He had come in person.","The man on the first floor seemed to sense something and abruptly looked up.","Dai Li was standing in the shadows; logically, he shouldn't have been able to see her. Yet, when that piercing, scorching gaze landed on her, she felt for a moment as if she were being enveloped by violent, searing lava.","The wildfire in his eyes transformed into a great tiger with its jaws agape, desperate to tear her apart and devour her.","It was over. He had definitely seen her.","Dai Li’s legs felt weak.","\"Mother, I'll take you...\"","Dai Li grabbed her son’s arm, her grip tight and brook no argument as she pulled the young man back toward his own room. \"Zhou Zhou, don't come out later. Leave everything to me. I'll handle him.\"","\"No,\" the youth replied without a second thought, shaking his head.","\"Listen to me!\" This was the first time since their reunion that Dai Li had used such a stern tone with him. \"If we appear together, it will only fuel his rage. Now is not the time to add oil to the fire. Zhou Zhou, be good. Stay in your room.\"","Dai Li patted her son’s arm, softening her voice. \"It’s alright. I know what I’m doing. Don’t worry.\"","Without waiting for Zhou Zhou to say another word, Dai Li backed out of his room and pulled the door shut behind her. Before she could even turn her head, a dark shadow lunged into her peripheral vision.","The heavy pressure radiating from the man—a ruler who had fought his way through seas of blood—felt like the sharpest of blades, sending shivers of terror down her spine.","Dai Li remained frozen in the motion of closing the door.","After a few tense heartbeats, she finally turned around and forced a gentle smile. \"The Marquis has arrived.\"","She acted as if nothing were wrong, her tone casual, as if everything—her being kidnapped by the Lotus Sect, her subsequent escape, her silent flight south to Yuzhou with her son—had never happened.","She didn't cry to him about her grievances or anger, nor did she show any fear at being \"caught red-handed.\"","She was trying to whitewash the situation.","The fire that had been smoldering in Qin Shaozong’s heart suddenly flared up as if doused in oil. It burned so fiercely that his very organs ached, screaming for release.","The veins on the man's forehead bulged as he let out a cold, mirthless smile. \"I used to think my wife possessed the heart of a bear and the gall of a leopard. Now it seems you certainly have the gall, but whether you have a heart is another matter entirely.\"","The door wasn't very soundproof, and Dai Li didn't want to talk in the hallway.","She stepped forward and took Qin Shaozong’s arm. \"What are you saying, My Lord? Circumstances were beyond my control; many things were forced upon me. Let’s not stand out here. Come inside with me.\"","A faint, familiar fragrance wafted toward him. The mockery on Qin Shaozong’s face faded, replaced by a cold, unmoving expression.","Dai Li continued to pull at his arm, trying to lead him forward. However, because Qin Shaozong was far taller and heavier than her, she couldn't budge him.","Realizing she couldn't move him, Dai Li let go. \"My Lord must be parched after traveling through the night. Why don't I pour you a cup of tea?\"","She turned back toward her own room. As she walked, she heard his heavy footsteps following her.","Bang! The door was slammed shut.","Her waist tightened as she was suddenly scooped up. After a dizzying whirl, her back hit the cold wooden door panel, with him looming over her.","The man, still in his black armor, looked even more imposing. Outside, lightning flashed and thunder roared, the light flaring and fading. Yet, Dai Li couldn't see a single ray of light. She was caged by him, pinned against the door, her every breath filled with his thick, masculine scent.","\"Why didn't you come to find me in the city? Why did you secretly head south with that boy?\" Every word sounded as if it had been ground between his teeth before being spat out.","He was volatile, reeking of gunpowder and rage.","Dai Li thought to herself that things were looking grim. It seemed she wouldn't be able to smooth this over. She lowered her eyes, ready to admit her fault while simultaneously shifting the blame onto the Lotus Sect. \"I'm so sorry. It was the Lotus Sect; they gave my son a mission that required a long journey. I didn't feel comfortable letting him go alone, so I insisted on going with him. I did consider informing you, but knowing your enmity with the Lotus Sect, I...\"","\"Liar!\"","The force of those two words left Dai Li stunned.","She quickly looked up, staring at Qin Shaozong in shock. Her red lips parted, but no words came out.","Qin Shaozong stared at her intently. Even in the dim room, he didn't miss a single one of her expressions.","After being tricked by her once in Nankang Commandery, he had realized this little fox was an expert at deception. She mixed truth with lies and knew exactly when to play the victim.","Just now, when she lowered her eyes and spoke so piteously, that familiar feeling returned. It was harder to ignore than the thunder outside, making his head throb.","She was unparalleled at acting obedient and playing the victim, and she was quick to admit her faults—but she never, ever changed.","If there were a next time, he was certain she would do it again!","Qin Shaozong’s temples throbbed. Seeing her part her lips as if to speak again, he simply reached out and gripped her chin, forcing it up.","If nothing good came out of that mouth, then he wouldn't let her speak at all.","He leaned down and kissed those red lips ruthlessly.","Dai Li knew he was always aggressive in matters of passion, but this was the first time she felt a distinct \"cruelty\" behind that aggression. She was pinned completely against the door, unable to move, unable to even make a sound.","The dark fire that had been bottled up in Qin Shaozong’s chest for days finally found its outlet, surging forth with overwhelming power.","It swept through her, biting and pillaging, his tongue lashing through her mouth.","Dai Li was forced to tilt her head back. She couldn't see herself, but she could feel that he had left faint teeth marks on her lips and tongue.","A thin thread of silver escaped and trailed down, first pooling in a small spot, then slowly expanding until a small patch of her clothes was damp.","Attempting to quell the raging wildfire, Dai Li stood on her tiptoes and wrapped her arms around his neck, trying to soothe his fury with her own surrender.","Outside, thunder rumbled and lightning snaked across the sky like wild dragons. Inside the room, the air was filled with the incessant, heart-stirring sounds of a deep, wet kiss.","The sky, which had been heavy and oppressive all day, finally broke into a torrential downpour. The rain hammered down, a deafening deluge that blurred out the rest of the world.","While it was cool outside, the temperature within the room seemed to climb higher with every passing second. Dai Li felt as if she were being swallowed whole. She tilted her head back, her breathing ragged and her eyes clouded with a thin, shimmering mist.","She turned her face away, but he refused to let her go.","With one hand clamped around her waist, he used his sheer strength to hoist her up. His other muscular arm slid down the curve of her hip and hooked under her thighs, lifting her until she was practically seated upon his arm.","There was a height difference of nearly eight inches between them. While he had been kissing her just moments before, Qin Shaozong hadn't even stood up straight. Now, with Dai Li’s feet dangling off the floor, he pinned her firmly against the door.","The sudden sensation of being airborne startled Dai Li, and she instinctively grabbed onto his arms. He was still wearing his light armor, and the metal over his shoulders was cold and hard. Unable to get a firm grip, she instead reached for the crimson cloak draped over his back, clutching the fabric tightly.","He moved to kiss her lips again, but Dai Li, still gasping for air, instinctively turned her head to the side.","Qin Shaozong paused for a moment. Then, moving down from her flushed lips, he pressed his mouth against the pale, delicate skin of her neck.","His canines grazed her, nipping and licking at the tender flesh."]},{"number":86,"title":"Chapter 86","paragraphs":["Mo Yanyun stood firmly in front of Qin Yanzhou’s door, speaking with earnest persistence. \"...Young Master, is our Northern Territory not good enough? Why must you insist on staying with the Lotus Sect? They are a pack of hypocrites who do nothing but harm. They constantly use gods and Buddhas as a front to swindle people everywhere; they are by no means a righteous path.\"","\"Move!\" Qin Yanzhou had no desire to waste words with him.","Outside, the lightning flashed and thunder roared with a deafening rumble, making it impossible for him to hear what was happening in the room next door.","The less he could hear, the more anxious he became, his heart burning with worry.","Yet the door was blocked, and he couldn't get out.","Mo Yanyun continued his sermon-like chatter. \"Lady Dai is in our Northern Territory; we all treat her with the utmost reverence. If she told us to catch a chicken, we wouldn't dare chase a dog. Jewels, fine jades, silks, satins, powerful servants, or beautiful maids—what has she asked for that our Marquis hasn't given?\"","Indeed, Mo Yanyun believed that Lady Dai and her son had slipped out of the city entirely under the instructions of the Lotus Sect. Because Summer Valley was no longer safe, they were being moved to another stronghold according to orders.","As for why Lady Dai would submit to the Lotus Sect, it was easy to understand—her young son was being held there, leaving her with no choice.","It never occurred to him that Lady Dai was completely unaware of any \"detention,\" and that her departure was a choice to leave both the Northern Territory and the Lotus Sect behind.","Qin Yanzhou was irritated beyond measure.","Ever since he had opened his door, this giant of a man had been nagging him for over half an hour. The words rolled back and forth like a broken wheel, an endless, chanting drone.","Now that his mother was with the Marquis of Wu'an, it was clearly inappropriate for him to strike the man's subordinate. He couldn't hit him, and he couldn't curse him away.","\"Shut up!\"","Mo Yanyun kept babbling: \"Aya, Young Master, listen to me...\"","While Qin Yanzhou’s room was noisy, the adjoining chamber was filled with a different kind of heat.","The bath barrel Lady Dai had used earlier had not been taken out, and water was now splashed everywhere.","Some had spilled directly onto the floor, some lent a shimmering wetness to the black armor discarded on the ground, and some had soaked into a dark red cloak.","Clothes were strewn all over the room. Beside the black armor lay a lady’s thin apricot-colored chemise. The closer one got to the bed, the fewer water stains there were, but the more clothes—especially women’s garments—cluttered the path.","The dragons of lightning flashing outside the window were the only source of light. Occasionally, as a bolt streaked past, the interior of the room would be illuminated for a fleeting second.","In those moments, the room was bright, save for a dark shadow coiled upon the bed.","The man was tall and imposing, with broad shoulders and a narrow waist. He knelt on the bed, his back to the outside, pinning a figure into the corner. The lightning highlighted the scarred, dark skin of his back. At this moment, with his forceful movements, the firm muscles of his back and waist tensed into fluid lines.","The sound of swallowing was exceptionally clear in this small space—ravenous, as if he wished he could devour her whole, flesh and bone.","\"Dai Li.\" He rarely called her by her full name.","Hearing those two deep syllables, Dai Li felt her scalp tingle for some reason. That sense of foreboding grew heavier, like a wet blanket stifling her.","\"I am asking you one last time,\" Qin Shaozong’s voice was hoarse and heavy. \"Did you head south on your own because you wanted to leave, or did the Lotus Sect really give that boy a mission?\"","\"Wuuu...\" Dai Li attempted to muddle her way through.","Qin Shaozong gave a light tsk and reached out to cup the lower half of her face. \"Speak. Stop trying to play dumb with me!\"","Her face was truly small; he could nearly cover it with one palm. Held by the chin in his hand, she looked so delicate.","Her lips were a vivid red and somewhat swollen; the tip of her nose and the corners of her eyes were flushed. Against the small cinnabar mole on her forehead, her jade-white skin was strikingly pale where it wasn't red, and her eyes were as dark and glossy as polished obsidian.","The colors were so exquisite and vibrant that it was likely no one else in the world could suit his tastes more perfectly.","However, the more Qin Shaozong looked at her now, the more furious he became. His heart, liver, lungs, and kidneys—every part of him burned with agitation.","This vixen was full of schemes. With one roll of her eyes, she could come up with eight hundred tricks. When she was caught doing something bad and couldn't deceive him, she would start playing the fool.","His calloused long fingers curled slightly and then straightened, probing into her red lips to pinch that soft, crimson tongue. \"If you won't talk, do you no longer want your tongue?\"","With a foreign object in her mouth, Dai Li instinctively wanted to bite down, but she jolted awake halfway through the thought.","Her eyelashes were damp with a bit of moisture, looking somewhat misted. She lifted her eyes to look at the man before her, whose expression remained grim. She didn't bite him; instead, she lightly brushed the tip of her tongue against his finger.","\"I want it,\" she murmured, the words blurred and sweet.","\"My Lady’s ability to sail with the wind is truly unrivaled; it fills me with admiration.\" Qin Shaozong let out a sharp, angry laugh. He withdrew his hand, deliberately using his glistening fingers to rub against her lips. \"This trip south—was it entirely because you wanted to leave?\"","The conversation had circled back to the original question.","How could Dai Li admit to that? \"...No.\"","Qin Shaozong sneered. \"Still lying. You truly don't know what's good for you.\"","Outside, purple light streaked across the sky like a giant tiger wreaking havoc in the heavens. With a casual swipe of its claws, several bolts of purple lightning surged for thousands of miles.","The thunder in the firmament was deafening. The interior was not as loud as the commotion outside, but it was far from quiet.","The plain curtains on either side of the bed were not drawn. In the flickering purple light, the two figures shifted between shadow and clarity.","Dai Li arched her back, grasping the hollowed-out bed frame. She tried to scratch the wooden crossbeam with her nails, but finding it impossible to leave a mark, she turned to grab the pillow beneath the frame instead.","She whimpered while clutching the pillowcase until it was a wrinkled mess. \"I really didn't lie to you...\"","\"Did you want to escape yourself, or was it a mission from the Lotus Sect? Tell the truth.\" He didn't believe her for a second.","Dai Li’s cheek rubbed against the quilt, her face flushed and her eyelashes clumped together from the moisture. She was being worn down by his \"interrogation\" and knew he was convinced she had wanted to run away on her own, refusing to hear anything else.","She was forced to confess.","\"It was... my own idea.\" Dai Li’s voice was barely audible. Once she finished that sentence, she began calling his name in a soft, pleading tone, saying every sweet thing she could think of. These endearments were much louder than her previous words.","The thunder roared outside, but Qin Shaozong heard both sentences clearly. The man laughed from sheer rage. \"So that is to say, when My Lady first saw me today, she lied to me?\"","Dai Li thought to herself that this was obvious, but since the man was currently in a towering rage, she didn't dare stroke the tiger's whiskers further. She could only whisper, \"I was wrong.\"","The veins on Qin Shaozong’s forehead throbbed.","She was still like this—avoiding the main issue and focusing on the trivial, never changing. He couldn't help but raise his hand and deliver a sharp \"smack.\"","Dai Li’s pupils suddenly contracted. It didn't hurt much, but the sound was very loud, occurring during a brief lull in the thunder. Her sense of shame spiked in that instant, fearing that the sound had pierced through the wall and reached the room next door.","Dai Li was exhausted and tried to lay back down stealthily.","\"You refuse the easy way and insist on the hard way. Behave.\" He raised his hand and gave her another smack.","\"What did My Lady promise me before? Setting aside what came later, you were the one who personally agreed to the initial one-year pact, were you not?\" After finishing his sentence, he gave her another one.","At first, Dai Li bit the corner of the quilt and whimpered. Later, she found that if she didn't respond, he would sometimes give her two smacks for every sentence he spoke.","Dai Li was going mad.","\"...It was I who promised.\" Having no other choice, she could only admit it.","Behind her came another cold sneer. \"Breaking your word, going back on your promises, and burning bridges once you've crossed them!\"","He spoke these three phrases slowly, but the force behind each was heavy, delivered through gritted teeth. With every phrase that fell, he gave her a sharp \"smack.\"","\"Of everything I promised Lady Dai, which have I failed to do? At the very beginning, when there was no news of that brat, did I not send men to Yangzhou?\"","\"...Yes.\"","He smacked her again and asked once more, \"Later, when we learned the boy had appeared in Yangzhou ten years ago, after I reached an agreement with you, did I not do as I said? Did I not issue search orders to every province and organize an inspection team for you to travel across the lands?\"","\"...Yes.\"","Outside, a sudden crack of thunder erupted. The roar of the thunder completely overlapped with the sound of the \"smack,\" the former swallowing the latter whole.","Though she had been hit several times, Dai Li pretended she hadn't heard a thing, practicing a form of self-deception. \"Qin Changgeng, I was wrong.\"","Qin Shaozong could not bear to hear her admit fault right now; it was like pouring oil on a fire. The more he heard it, the more furious he became.","Since the moment he found her, she had admitted fault many times. But every single time, it was because she saw the situation was turning against her; she apologized only to escape, a mere formality without a shred of sincerity.","He ignored her apology and continued coldly, \"Later, when we found your son, that brat had stirred up a mess of trouble. He offended Yanzhou, Qingzhou, and several smaller factions. Was it not I who settled every single one of those matters for him?\"","\"...Yes,\" Dai Li replied, her eyes shimmering with tears.","He did not stop his movements.","The sound was truly too shameful for Dai Li to bear. She had exhausted all her sweet words, yet the man showed no intention of stopping.","She broke into a frantic sweat and, in desperation, grabbed a random garment and draped it over her head.","Out of sight, out of mind; if she couldn't see it or hear it, it wasn't happening.","Qin Shaozong gave a cold huff and reached out to pull the clothes away. \"If you dare to do it, you must dare to face it. Since you had the courage to break our contract and flee without a word, why do you lack the courage to face the consequences now? I have never broken my word to you, yet you have played me for a fool time and time again. It is true that the Lotus Sect committed evils, but it is also true that you wanted to use the opportunity to burn your bridges. So you simply went with the flow to make your escape, is that not so?\"","The pillowcase Dai Li was biting on had long been stained with damp patches of varying shades.","Seeing her silence, that shameful sound rang out twice more.","Dai Li’s eyelashes trembled. At this juncture, she truly couldn't argue her way out. Now, she only prayed that this chapter would end quickly and that he would stop dwelling on her lies.","No matter what he said, she agreed.","\"Yes,\" she murmured muffledly, begging him once more to stop hitting her.","Qin Shaozong, however, asked on his own accord, \"When I told you back then to stay by my side forever, you said you would give me an answer in a month. Had you already planned to use that as a stalling tactic?\"","\"...Yes.\"","Qin Shaozong gritted his teeth and gave her another smack. \"Do you dare to do it again in the future?\"","\"I dare,\" Dai Li answered instinctively.","After giving that affirmative answer, Dai Li dithered for a moment, realizing too late that she had misspoken. \"No, that’s not...\"","Qin Shaozong could no longer remember how many times he had been driven to the point of a dizzying rage by her tonight.","Fine. It seemed she hadn't listened to a single word he said; she only wanted to hurry up and deal with him.","Good. Very good. She truly was in need of a lesson!","\"Qin Changgeng, I didn't mean that just now,\" Dai Li said anxiously.","She hadn't expected to lose her head and misspeak, giving him a handle to use against her. As soon as those words fell, she realized he was gradually shifting his focus.","His touch moved along her waist, descending from top to bottom, finally landing on a tiny point. \"You said it yourself; how could it be false?\"","A fire threatened to burn in Qin Shaozong's eyes. \"If those words don't count, and so many other words don't count, then how am I to tell which of your words will be true or false in the future?\"","\"Only that sentence doesn't count, everything else is true,\" Dai Li cried, a fresh wave of tears welling up instantly.","His fingertips were covered in thick calluses, very rough to the touch. Usually, even a light brush felt coarse; how could he deliberately toy with such a delicate place?","Qin Shaozong wasn't listening. He couldn't listen to another word.","Dai Li truly couldn't hold it in anymore. She reached back, trying to push him away, but before she could even touch him, he seized her wrist.","His palm was hot and heavy, like a red-hot shackle. Caught in his grip, Dai Li was unable to move.","\"If you dare to run again, I'll break your son's legs!\" Qin Shaozong said savagely.","She could agree to anything else he said, and she could endure it by closing her eyes and waiting for it to pass, but she had a violent reaction to this one sentence. \"You hit me, and now you want to hit Zhou Zhou! Then wouldn't I have suffered all this for nothing?\"","She began to struggle, no longer willing to cooperate with him.","Qin Shaozong pinned her down, holding her firmly beneath him. \"I won't hit Qin Yanzhou.\"","Dai Li paused.","Qin Shaozong guided her hand downward, finally resting it on her own stomach. Dai Li's flat belly could no longer maintain its original state.","\"If you dare to run again, we'll have one. When he grows up, I'll break both his legs.\"","\"Qin Shaozong, you pervert!\"","Qin Shaozong raised a long eyebrow. \"What does 'pervert' mean?\"","\"It's... it's a compliment... stop rubbing, I can't take it anymore, wah...\"","Qin Shaozong didn't believe a single word. \"It seems your bad habit of lying won't change one bit. Very well, the road is long; we shall correct it slowly.\"","As if remembering something, Qin Shaozong added, \"If you agree to a few things, I will tell you something important regarding that brat and the Lotus Sect.\"","The moment he finished speaking, Dai Li said impatiently, \"I agree, I agree to anything.\"","The fire in Qin Shaozong's chest began to churn again. \"Glib-tongued woman. Let me tell you, Dai Li, even if you flee to the ends of the earth, I will find you.\"","Outside the window, lightning flashed and thunder roared. Rain poured down in torrents. The flags used by the merchants to attract customers rattled in the wind, and the night remained restless until dawn.","*","The magistrate of Nanyang County was surnamed Mi, and his given name was Gao. Mi Gao was a diligent magistrate who liked to handle government affairs personally.","Before dawn today, a servant rushed in to report, \"My Lord, a troop of cavalry opened the North Gate under the cover of night.\"","The words \"cavalry\" and \"under cover of night\" combined were enough to make Mi Gao gasp.","\"Who are they?\" Just after asking, Mi Gao muttered to himself, \"I heard there was fighting over in Yanzhou, but that's not right either. Didn't they say the war in Yanzhou was over? Besides, they can fight their wars, but why come to Yuzhou?\"","After his rambling, Mi Gao asked again who the newcomers were.","The servant shook his head, saying he didn't know. \"After that cavalry unit opened the city gates, they went straight to a guesthouse in the north of the city. The entire troop checked in and there has been no movement since.\"","The reason he was only reporting now was that the guards at the North Gate had all been tied up. The night watchmen and patrols they encountered were also detained without exception, and they were only released at daybreak.","Mi Gao paced the room. \"They released the men? It seems they mean no harm. If they truly wanted to seize the city, they could have killed them and crept into my manor under the cover of night. Which guesthouse are they at? Have the horses readied; I must pay them a visit.\"","...","When Dai Li woke up, the day was already bright outside.","She was still lying on the couch, staring blankly at the plain canopy above. Her memory was a bit muddled, and she didn't know what day or year it was.","It took a good while for the events of the previous night to come flooding back.","Qin Shaozong had tracked her down.","Dai Li let out a low, miserable groan and instinctively yanked the nearby duvet over her head. But she had barely been under for two seconds before she threw the covers aside again."]},{"number":87,"title":"Chapter 87","paragraphs":["Last night, she had signed a slew of humiliating treaties. The memories were too painful to dwell upon, and just as Dai Li was attempting to block them out, the bedroom door opened.","The hinges of this guesthouse door were in poor condition; opening and closing them produced an unavoidable, sharp creak. Now, that sound struck like a bolt of thunder, instantly jolting Dai Li back to her senses.","The door was pushed open, and a tall figure stepped inside.","Dai Li stole a glance at Qin Shaozong. Her expression remained calm, and she didn't bother to stop him. Last night, her poor silk camisole had been used as a rope and was now a wrinkled mess. Dai Li rolled over, turning her back to the outside of the bed to face the wall.","A sudden bout of perfectionism took hold as she tried to smooth the creases out of the silk.","After a few strokes, it looked presentable enough, and Dai Li began to dress.","The thin ribbons had just looped around her neck, but before she could tie the knot herself, two large, dark-toned hands took over.","Dai Li paused for a moment, then allowed him to help.","Qin Shaozong stood by the couch, towering over her. Looking down from his height, he easily took in the stunning view before him.","Her skin was like congealed cream, her neck elegant and fair. Her ink-black hair flowed like a cloud over her snowy back, where intense red marks trailed down from her nape like clusters of blossoms—or perhaps like inescapable thorns entwining her.","The thin silken cords wound through his fingers. This was the first time Qin Shaozong had ever done such a thing for a lady.","It was a novel experience, and a pleasant one at that.","He tugged the ribbons, preparing to tie the knot, but the woman in front of him suddenly shifted. She placed a hand on the camisole, appearing as though she wanted to pull it down slightly, while looking back at him with dissatisfaction. \"It's too tight.\"","Only when she turned did he see that it was indeed too tight.","The ends connected to the thin straps had been pulled up too high. However, rather than focusing on the garment, his gaze lingered on her.","The lush, snowy curves filled the silk camisole, dotted with red marks, vibrant and rich in color. She was naturally radiant and exquisite, with pitch-black eyes and watery red lips. At this moment, she looked like a peony soaked in water, possessing an indescribable languor. Even as she glared at him imperiously, she appeared charming and breathtakingly beautiful.","Qin Shaozong loosened the long fingers holding the cord. \"Is this better?\"","The camisole slid down a bit. Dai Li turned back to face away from him, letting him continue with the ribbons. \"Tie it.\"","In a place where Qin Shaozong couldn't see, Dai Li twisted her fingers and began to ponder the future.","He seemed quite peaceful this morning, his expression no different from usual, as if her unauthorized trip south had been smoothed over.","But Dai Li knew everything was only \"as if.\" By the end of last night, she couldn't even remember how many shameless things she had promised him. Knowing Qin Shaozong, he would certainly hold her to them. Furthermore, in certain respects, he likely wouldn't trust her again...","To be honest, Dai Li didn't know what to do now. She couldn't break free, and she couldn't run away.","With no other choice, she decided to wave the white flag for now and see what the future held. For the time being, she would just drift along.","After he had taken his time helping her into her undergarments, Dai Li went to look for her outer robes. Her clothes from yesterday had been torn, but a set of new garments now sat by the bed.","The midnight-blue silk shimmered in the sun-drenched room. When she lifted it by the collar, the smooth fabric unfurled like flowing water.","Dai Li let out a hum of confusion. \"Where did these clothes come from?\"","Small counties rarely had large-scale silk merchants; they might sell fabric, but not necessarily ready-made clothes—and these were clearly no ordinary garments.","\"The magistrate of Nanyang came to visit me this morning, intending to gauge my intentions. I asked him for a few things,\" Qin Shaozong said, leaning against the bedpost and watching her dress.","Having his city gates forced open by cavalry in the middle of the night had terrified the local official. He had come to the guesthouse at the crack of dawn to beg for an audience. Upon learning that Qin Shaozong was merely \"passing through\" and leaving today, the magistrate, a man named Mi, became incredibly sycophantic, insisting that if there was anything he could do, Qin Shaozong shouldn't hesitate to ask.","Since the offer had been dropped in his lap, Qin Shaozong didn't stand on ceremony and took several items from Magistrate Mi.","\"What did you ask for?\" Dai Li asked casually.","\"A carriage, two sets of clothes, and...\" He paused here, and as expected, she turned her head, her gaze sweeping toward him from the corner of her eye.","\"The medicine Madam wanted.\"","Dai Li froze, her eyes instantly lighting up. She turned to look at him directly, a bright smile gracing her face. \"Ah, the Lord is truly as meticulous as a hair, so thoughtful and thorough in his actions.\"","She was smiling like a flower, but the corners of Qin Shaozong's mouth slowly sank. After everything that happened last night, the dark fire that had nearly been extinguished flared up again.","Even though he knew rationally that she was unwilling and had no intention of bearing another child, seeing her so happy about birth control still infuriated him.","She had been willing to have a child for someone else—and for a man she had quarreled with, no less.","What was so good about that man? How much property did he own? Did he have more power than Qin? Why was she willing to carry that man’s bloodline but refused even to consider him!","Seeing his expression darken, Dai Li knew exactly what Qin Shaozong was thinking. But she had made it clear long ago: this was a matter of principle and was not up for negotiation.","Once dressed, Dai Li left the room.","It would be a lie to say she wasn't nervous about going out. Although the thunder had been loud last night and could mask many sounds, it hadn't been constant.","If a certain moment hadn't been covered and the sound had drifted outside or to the next room, it would be incredibly embarrassing...","The entire guesthouse had been booked out, and the owner had been living in fear since last night.","First, a troop of cavalry had arrived. Then, just as dawn broke, the County Magistrate himself showed up. That was the highest official in their region, someone who didn't appear easily, yet he had come to this small guesthouse today.","What shocked him even more was the magistrate’s attitude—he was extremely respectful, acting as if he were a mere servant.","In the owner's mind, the only person higher than a magistrate was a Governor. Could it be that a Governor from another province was staying in his shop?","He served them with fear and trepidation, secretly speculating. Finally, around mid-morning, there was movement upstairs.","The owner peeked up, hoping to catch a glimpse of the Governor's majestic bearing, only to have his entire attention captured by a silhouette in midnight blue.","The ladies from ancient scrolls and the legendary beauties of literature seemed to suddenly come to life in that moment. As she slowly descended the stairs, she glowed like a shimmering pearl or radiant jade; the hall seemed to brighten significantly.","The owner stared blankly, filled with confusion.","The people who checked in last night were clearly all men. When did such a lady enter his shop?","Could she be a fox spirit in disguise?","A sharp, cold gaze shot toward him—authoritative and deep. Though it held little emotion, it made the owner shiver, and he instinctively looked away, not daring to stare further.","Dai Li saw her son while she was still on the stairs.","The young man was sitting on the ground floor with Mo Yanyun and the others. Hearing footsteps, Qin Yanzhou looked up.","Despite the distance, Dai Li could see the worry in her son's eyes. She gave him a reassuring look, signaling that everything was fine.","Everyone else had already eaten breakfast except for Dai Li, who had woken up late. Shortly after she sat down, food was served. She was starving and began to eat.","Mo Yanyun secretly stole a glance at his superior.","It was strange. Clearly, the Lord had been in a good mood this morning, radiating the refreshed satisfaction of a man well-sated. How had his temperament taken such a sharp turn for the worse in such a short time?","Mo Yanyun’s gaze shifted stealthily to the side. Looking at Dai Li this time, he felt a sense of admiration that bordered on total worship.","When the news of Lady Dai’s betrayal first broke, the Lord had been livid, his fury bordering on the uncontrollable. It wasn't an exaggeration to say that Mo Yanyun had feared for Lady Dai’s life; after all, she was the first person to ever successfully deceive the Lord time and again, and it was obvious he cared for her deeply.","And yet, here they were. Lady Dai was perfectly fine, and the young master had not been made a scapegoat. Not a single hair on the heads of mother or son was missing.","It seemed the Lord’s great storm of rage had been exactly like the heavy rain last night—it poured violently, but once it was over, it was gone.","The clouds had parted, and the sun was out.","Mo Yanyun hissed a breath through his teeth, thinking to himself that if he ever accidentally messed up in the future, it might not be a bad idea to ask Lady Dai to intercede for him.","If Dai Li could have heard Mo Yanyun’s inner thoughts, she would have refuted them on the spot.","What did he mean, \"perfectly fine\"? She was anything but!","It was just that the place where she had received her \"punishment\" wasn't something she could easily talk about with others.","After the meal was finished, the group left the relay station.","Dai Li saw a carriage parked at the entrance. The curtains were rolled up and the door was open, revealing the interior. It looked clean and tidy, furnished with a small desk and a padded chair.","She climbed inside and slowly lowered herself onto the chair.","Several layers of soft cloth had been spread over the seat, making it much softer than usual. Dai Li let out a slow, cautious sigh of relief.","It wasn't bad; in fact, it was better than she had expected.","But just as she relaxed, a familiar, imposing figure entered the carriage. This carriage only had a single row of seating; the desk in front was fixed against the front window, leaving no room for a second row.","Dai Li watched as Qin Shaozong came toward her.","He didn't speak, simply standing before her. Dai Li hesitated for a moment before finally scooting to the side to make room for him.","Qin Shaozong’s expression softened slightly. He reached back to close the carriage door and sat down beside her.","The carriage wasn't actually small. If nothing else were placed next to the seat, there would be more than enough room for two people to sit side-by-side. However, the carriage’s previous owner had been a man of meticulous tastes and had installed a small cabinet next to the seat.","With the cabinet taking up space, the seating was less spacious than usual.","Qin Shaozong stood over eight feet tall with a frame much broader than the average man. The moment he sat down, the chair became cramped, forcing Dai Li’s thigh to press firmly against his.","Once he was settled, the carriage began to move.","Dai Li turned her head to look out the window. The small town was bustling during the day; pedestrians came and went, and vendors cried out their wares. It was the picture of a perfectly ordinary, peaceful life.","Only a day ago, she had been planning how to live her future life, thinking about how to decorate her little house and what color kitten or puppy she should raise...","In less than a day, most of those choices were no longer hers to make.","Seeing Dai Li staring fixedly outside, Qin Shaozong let out a cold mental sneer.","This little fox still hasn't given up.","\"My Lady.\"","Hearing his voice, Dai Li turned her head. She saw him holding his hand out, palm up. \"The travel permit. Give it to me.\"","Her permit was kept in a small cloth pouch. He must have seen it when she changed her clothes earlier.","He wouldn't take it himself; he insisted on her handing it over personally.","Under his expressionless gaze, Dai Li pulled the pouch from her sleeve, slowly loosened the drawstring, and pulled out a small wooden tablet.","She placed the wooden tablet in Qin Shaozong’s hand.","He flipped it over to look at the front.","Name: Hua Wenxiu.","Qin Shaozong studied the tablet for a moment before suddenly asking, \"Is that all?\"","Dai Li’s breath hitched slightly.","The man’s long, well-defined fingers tapped the wooden tablet, then brushed over the \"Name\" column. His tone was so calm it was unnerving. \"After My Lady fled Sweetwater County and arrived in Xiagu, you spent a period of time hiding alone. During that time, the Lotus Sect turned the world upside down looking for you. Wanted posters were plastered all over the city; it wouldn't be an exaggeration to say they searched every inch of Xiagu. Where was My Lady staying then?\"","The fact that she could enter Xiagu successfully meant she must have had a permit on her.","That boy had been sent back by him later. Calculating the time, the boy had just arrived in Sweetwater County before being diverted, so it was unlikely she had met up with her son there.","It had to be Xiagu.","For her to hide while the whole city was being searched meant there was likely something wrong with that permit.","And don't even suggest that the Lotus Sect wouldn't realize she had forged one. As soon as she ran, they would have meticulously reviewed everything she had done recently. It wouldn't be hard to find a hidden permit.","But now, the permit in his hand showed no signs of tampering.","Dai Li had already reached a point of \"giving up.\" When she pulled the permit from the pouch just now, she had grabbed one at random.","She had been careless, but she hadn't expected Qin Shaozong to be so observant.","This man’s mind was too sharp; he had pieced everything together from the smallest clue. Thinking about what he had done to her because of her lies and broken promises, Dai Li’s backside gave a phantom throb of pain. She didn't dare make up any more stories and reluctantly pulled another wooden tablet from the pouch.","Qin Shaozong took it and saw at a glance that there was something suspicious about the \"Name\" section.","Two of the characters in \"Lotus Scholar\" looked off. Upon closer inspection, it was clear they had been altered. The man gave a soft click of his tongue. \"Dishonest again.\"","Dai Li remained silent, keeping her eyes fixed on her own lap.","*Crack.* The sound of splintering wood came from beside her.","Dai Li couldn't help but peek. She was startled to see those two sturdy wooden tablets crushed into splinters in his palm.","He reached his hand out the carriage window and opened his large palm. The fragments, large and small, were instantly swept away by the wind.","Qin Shaozong withdrew his hand. Looking at his empty palm, Dai Li sighed inwardly.","Not even the dust remained.","\"Move over a bit,\" Dai Li grumbled, feeling uncomfortable. She intentionally tried to push him.","Qin Shaozong’s eyebrows arched slightly. He didn't speak immediately because he noticed something different in her tone.","Except for when they were in bed, she usually addressed him with formal titles, remaining polite and maintaining a clear distance. When she wanted to annoy him, she would even pointedly call him \"My Lord,\" which was as irritating as could be. But now...","From this blunt, unceremonious sentence—completely devoid of formal titles—Qin Shaozong heard a hint of resignation.","His mood suddenly brightened. His previous displeasure and anger vanished instantly, and he yielded to her pressure, shifting slightly to the side.","Reaching out a long arm, Qin Shaozong pulled her into his embrace. \"It’s all the fault of that local magistrate. He filled the carriage with useless, decorative junk, wasting all the space.\"","Dai Li was speechless. The man had taken someone else’s carriage and now he was complaining about it. \"We’re lucky to have a carriage at all.\"","His hand moved down from her shoulder, brushing over her waist and following the smooth curve until it rested just above her hips. \"My Lady, how effective was Ding Congjian’s medicine?\"","Suddenly, a memory flashed through her mind. Ignoring everything else, Dai Li asked, \"Qin Changgeng, you said before that you’d tell me something about Zhou Zhou and the Lotus Sect. What was it?\"","Qin Shaozong leaned back against the padded chair. \"A bit of hearsay. Whether it’s true or not remains to be seen.\"","\"True or not, tell me first,\" Dai Li said urgently.","Whenever it concerned her son and the Lotus Sect, she was always desperate for information.","Qin Shaozong didn't keep her in suspense. \"I’ve heard that the Lotus Sect makes certain important believers consume something called 'Divine Medicine.'\"","Before she could even hear the rest, the mere words \"divine medicine\" made Dai Li straighten up abruptly. \"What?!\"","Qin Shaozong's hand moved up to soothe her back. \"This medicine is said to have both benefits and drawbacks. Let's set aside the benefits for now. Some say its drawback is life-threatening; if one stops taking it abruptly, it will cause one's intestines to rot and belly to rupture.\"","No thunder from last night was as shocking and terrifying to Dai Li as Qin Shaozong's words at this moment.","He seemed to say something else afterward, something about the veracity of the rumors, but in this moment, Dai Li couldn't hear any of it.","The phrase \"intestines rotting and belly rupturing\" seized her entire mind and drained all color from her face.","\"It can't be... I... I clearly asked Zhou Zhou. At the time, Zhou Zhou said one could leave...\" Dai Li murmured.","She had asked her son, right there in that small courtyard.","Back then, she had been suspicious that a large sect like the Qinglian Sect might have methods to control people, and she asked him if one could leave the sect freely.","Her son had said, \"One can leave.\"","Thinking back on it now, Zhou Zhou had only said one could leave; he hadn't answered her other questions.","He had evaded the issue, playing a game of words with her.","Dai Li felt both a heart-wrenching pain and a bewildered helplessness.","Ten years, a full ten years.","It seemed that the long stretch of time had filled the space between her and her son Zhou Zhou with an undue amount of estrangement."]},{"number":88,"title":"Chapter 88","paragraphs":["Qin Shaozong saw that Dai Li was about to get up after speaking. His long arm tightened, pinning her back onto the soft chair. \"A few moments won't make a difference. We will discuss this matter after we return to Xia Valley.\"","Dai Li sat back in the chair, but she was trapped in a mire of anxiety and unease.","\"Those so-called divine medicines are mostly just smoke and mirrors. How could something have the effect of prolonging life while also causing one's intestines to rot, and even forcing a person to take it regularly by threatening such a fate? It sounds far too far-fetched; the rumors are likely untrue.\" Qin Shaozong spoke of the matter with utter disdain.","Dai Li pursed her lips and remained silent.","Qin Shaozong took one of her hands, squeezing her pinkish fingertips. \"If my Lady is worried, let Ding Congjian feel the boy's pulse once we return and have him take a careful look. Ding Congjian comes from a family of physicians spanning generations. His father and his grandfather, who is now in his seventies, are both exceptionally skilled. No matter how rare the ailment, they have the cure to make it vanish.\"","A long silence followed his words before Qin Shaozong finally heard her soft \"Mm,\" followed by, \"Thank you.\"","Those two words grated on Qin Shaozong's ears. \"There is no need for thanks. If my Lady truly wishes to thank me, then behave yourself in the future. Stop spending all your energy thinking about running away.\"","Dai Li turned her head to glare at him, her lips still pressed tight.","One look at her expression and Qin Shaozong understood everything.","Fine. She was still defiant. Likely, her current submission was only because she had been caught and had no way out, forcing her to accept her fate for now. That mind of hers, full of schemes and \"wicked water,\" had never once run dry.","\"What? Did I say something wrong?\" Qin Shaozong challenged her, determined to straighten out her bad habits and wayward thoughts. \"Dai Li, I can grant you anything, except for one thing.\"","Whether it was the treasures she desired or the things she wished to do, he could find them for her and arrange everything. He could even personally pave the way for her son’s future, ensuring the boy a lifetime of wealth and status.","Except for one thing: she could never leave him.","This was his bottom line. Above that line, no matter how she acted out—even if she poked a hole in the heavens—he would be there to patch it up for her.","Dai Li knew exactly what he was referring to, but she had no heart to argue with him. \"The Lord is right in everything he says.\"","Qin Shaozong’s lip twitched. Her voice was pleasant enough, but the words she spoke were enough to provoke a man to death.","When Dai Li had first left Xia Valley, she had shared a horse with Qin Yanzhou, traveling at a modest pace. Now, on the return journey, they traveled by carriage. The speed of the carriage was roughly the same as two people on one horse, and they arrived at the small mountain village just as dusk was falling.","They stayed in the villagers' homes just as they had before, paying them in silver.","Because they paid generously, the villagers were all smiles. Some even took the initiative to bring out chickens and geese from their homes to slaughter. Providing good food and meat meant another payment, and the offcuts that the nobles wouldn't eat would allow the villagers to feast themselves.","In the approaching night of dusk, the small mountain village was unusually lively.","Children ran about laughing, and the villagers beamed with joy over their unexpected income. The Xuanxiao Cavalry, for their part, were relaxed, having won the battle and being on the verge of returning home.","Everyone, that is, except Mo Yanyun.","Mo Yanyun had been agonizing the entire way. Ever since he had heard Dai Li’s reasoning in the eastern suburbs, he had initially felt as though he had been struck by lightning, unable to believe it.","However, thinking back on it carefully, it was completely understandable! Lady Dai was brilliantly talented, possessed peerless beauty, and had a gentle temperament. It was only logical and fair for her to demand to be the primary wife.","What woman wouldn't want to be the legitimate wife? It was just as no common soldier didn't dream of being a commander.","Unfortunately, the Marquis and the Wei family had a prior agreement. The Marquis’s word was as heavy as a thousand gold pieces; in over thirty years, he had never broken a promise made to another.","This was a difficult knot to untie.","But if he didn't tell the Marquis, and Lady Dai attempted another escape in the future, it would be considered a dereliction of duty on his part as a subordinate...","\"Mo Yanyun.\"","Mo Yanyun was squatting on the ground, holding a wild flower and plucking its petals, muttering under his breath, \"Tell him, don't tell him, tell him, don't tell him...\"","\"Mo Yanyun.\"","Mo Yanyun jolted, instinctively springing to his feet with his legs together and his back ramrod straight. \"Present!\"","Qin Shaozong looked at his subordinate’s strange behavior, his narrow brown eyes squinting slightly. \"I'll give you the time it takes for a cup of tea to cool. Explain yourself.\"","Mo Yanyun cried out in his heart that he was doomed. The Marquis must have heard his indecision just now.","Fine then. No need to pluck petals anymore; the Marquis had made the decision for him.","Mo Yanyun swallowed hard, not daring to keep silent. \"My Lord, when I pursued Lady Dai out of the city and was discovered by her in the eastern suburbs, I tried to persuade her to return with me. She refused, and at the time, she said...\"","By the end, his voice dropped about eight decibels. \"She said she didn't want to be a concubine.\"","Of course, as for the words he had used to persuade Lady Dai in the ruined temple, he wouldn't breathe a word of them even if he were beaten to death.","Qin Shaozong was silent for a moment. \"And?\"","Mo Yanyun shook his head hurriedly. \"Nothing else. Lady Dai only said that one sentence.\"","Qin Shaozong glanced at the petals scattered all over the ground. \"There is nothing to be conflicted about. In the future, if it concerns her, do not hide anything. Report directly to me.\"","Mo Yanyun plucked up his courage to ask, \"That matter... how does the Lord view it?\"","\"It is only human nature,\" Qin Shaozong said calmly. \"If you were a lady, you wouldn't want to be just a concubine either.\"","Mo Yanyun scratched his head. That was true enough, but what he really wanted to know was how the Marquis planned to handle the situation.","However, even asking \"how he viewed it\" had been an overstep; he didn't dare ask anything further.","*","On the other side, during the leisure time before dinner, Dai Li was taking a walk through the small village with her son.","Two members of the Xuanxiao Cavalry followed the mother and son at a distance—close enough to keep an eye on them, but far enough not to intrude.","Dai Li walked aimlessly.","She had so many things she wanted to say to her son, but because there was so much, it had piled up like layers of silt and sand, blocking the exit and leaving her not knowing where to begin.","Qin Yanzhou could sense his mother’s mood; she was heavy-hearted, panicked, and at a loss.","He assumed Dai Li was upset about being caught, so he comforted her in a low voice. \"Mama, the failure of this trip south was an accident. We had the timing and the location, but we lacked the final piece of luck. I didn't expect the Marquis of Wu'an's reinforcements to reach Xia Valley so early, ending the war ahead of schedule. It's also my fault for not dealing with that gyrfalcon sooner, allowing it to bring word to the Marquis of Wu'an. But don't be discouraged. If it didn't work this time, we'll just wait for the next. Next time...\"","As Qin Yanzhou spoke, he caught sight of the glint of tears in Dai Li’s eyes.","A shimmering layer of moisture was clearly visible in the sunset, looking so full that it seemed as though a single blink would send the teardrops falling.","The young man’s face, usually devoid of expression, now crumbled like a fracturing mountain, revealing an undeniable panic.","Last night, the thunder had been deafening and the rain had poured almost all night long. The noise in the next room had been muffled by the rain and thunder, making it almost inaudible. But when his mother had come downstairs this morning, her face clearly bore traces of exhaustion, while the Marquis of Wu'an had looked triumphant and hadn't even offered a word of reprimand regarding his attempt to take his mother south.","Though he had no experience with women in that regard, Qin Yanzhou was no fool. It wasn't hard to guess what had happened in the room next door last night.","His mother was crying—she had been humiliated beyond endurance!","A murderous intent surged in his eyes, and at that moment, his hatred for the Marquis of Wu'an reached its peak.","But in the next instant, he heard Dai Li say, \"It has nothing to do with Qin Shaozong, and I wasn't thinking about our journey south just now. I just... my heart aches for Zhou Zhou.\"","The young man froze, the murderous intent in his eyes instantly stilled and dissipated.","Once the conversation started, the rest followed naturally.","Dai Li said softly, \"Sometimes I can't help but think about those ten years—the hardships you faced, the things you went through. I try to guess how you managed to survive. Sometimes I even dream about the year of the great famine, dreaming of you as a tiny child being caught, and they wanted to kill you for your meat. The famine was so great that people exchanged their children to eat... and the one being exchanged was my son. Zhou Zhou, I’m not telling you this to burden you. I just feel like I haven't been a competent mother.\"","\"No!\" Qin Yanzhou shook his head frantically. \"There is no better mother than you.\"","He didn't remember much from his early years; his memories only started becoming clear when he was four or five. Before that, there were only fragmented pieces.","His father had been a civil aviation captain and was rarely home. His only impressions of his father were a tall silhouette and the warmth of a large palm resting on his head.","But his memories of his mother were countless.","Those memories were like wildflowers scattered across a mountain. If he plucked one at random, it might become his mother sitting in the audience at kindergarten, smiling and holding a camera as she watched him perform alongside other parents.","It might turn into a picture of him sitting on the floor at home, playing with a toy car, while not far away, his mother worked on a laptop by the sofa.","Or it might become another scene: him playing with his friends in the neighborhood, returning to his mother’s side drenched in sweat, where the beautiful woman would hand him a water bottle. After watching him gulp down the water, she would take out a handkerchief to wipe his brow.","These wildflowers connected to form a hidden oasis, a sanctuary that resisted the terrifying sandstorms of life and allowed his scarred self to find a brief moment of rest years later.","Dai Li gave a bitter smile. \"I don't deserve to be called 'good.' I left you to wander here alone for so long as a child. We finally reunited, and after only a few days of peace, you have to go on the run with me.\"","\"Being with you is a good life to me,\" Qin Yanzhou said without hesitation.","The distress in Dai Li's heart reached its breaking point, and she blurted out, \"You left the Lotus Sect. They know you've defected, and not only is there a bounty on your head, but they certainly won't give you that medicine anymore! Is having your intestines rot away still considered a 'good life'?!\"","Qin Yanzhou's pupils contracted sharply, his lips trembling. \"Mom...\"","\"Why didn't you tell me? Parents should be a child's support, not their burden. My child has suffered enough. I only want you to be safe and sound from now on. I don't need you to make that kind of sacrifice for me, Zhou Zhou.\" The tears in Dai Li's eyes finally fell.","Hearing about that matter from Qin Shaozong's mouth was no exaggeration—she truly felt as if the sky was falling.","She had thought that after those ten years, once she and Zhou Zhou were reunited, the days ahead would be the sweetness after the bitterness. Even if they weren't wealthy or as comfortable as they had been in the modern world, it would surely be better than those ten harrowing years.","But she hadn't expected the Lotus Sect to have such a hold on him, and she certainly hadn't expected her child to hide it from her...","Over the years, Qin Yanzhou had almost no one he could talk to openly. Having gone so long without arguing with anyone, he could only say anxiously, \"It’s not a sacrifice! As long as you are happy, Mom, I am willing to do anything.\"","As Dai Li's heart twisted with pain, a surge of anger rushed to her head. \"Does that medicine not have side effects? If that isn't a sacrifice, what is!\"","Qin Yanzhou was speechless.","In the blink of an eye, a fresh trail of hot tears rolled down Dai Li's face. \"I know you want me to be happy, and you want me to live well in this era. But Zhou Zhou, if your body is ruined by that medicine and you don't have long to live... I'm telling you, just as I could jump off that bridge back then, I can take a knife to my own throat when that day comes.\"","Qin Yanzhou's body jolted. His face went blank for a moment, but his eyes reddened first.","Her son was already much taller than her. Dai Li could no longer easily pat his head as she did when he was small, so she could only pat his shoulder.","\"Zhou Zhou, I am so sorry I wasn't by your side for those ten years. I understand ten years is a long time—long enough for a child who relied on his mother for everything to grow into a man who stands on his own. Perhaps you aren't used to telling me everything anymore and have your own secrets and concerns. I can understand that; growing up is a process of becoming independent.\"","Dai Li wiped away a tear. \"But you cannot gamble with your health and your life. Those are not things to be trifled with.\"","\"Mom, it’s not that serious. My intestines won't rot,\" Qin Yanzhou said stiffly.","Dai Li didn't feel relieved at all, because she heard another meaning behind those words.","Her son had indeed taken the Lotus Sect's poison.","It made sense. He had been making a living within the Lotus Sect; when the medicine was given to him, several pairs of eyes would have been fixed on him, making sure he swallowed it—they might have even handed him water to wash it down.","Zhou Zhou had no choice.","Qin Yanzhou said hurriedly, \"Mom, I didn't take much of that medicine. Even if it felt okay for a short time after taking it, I knew it was bad stuff. When no one was watching me, I didn't take it.\"","Dai Li paused, the heavy stone pressing on her heart loosening slightly. Just as she was about to speak, a soldier in the distance called out that dinner was ready, summoning them to eat.","Dai Li took a deep breath, slowly calming her emotions. \"I heard that the military doctor in the North, Ding Congjian, is highly skilled. When we get back, Zhou Zhou, you must let him check your pulse.\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded in agreement.","Dai Li turned with him and walked back the way they came. \"As for leaving, let's not think about it for now.\"","Qin Yanzhou turned to look at his mother, but he could only see the woman's calm profile.","When the mother and son returned to the small house, dinner was already served. One table was set inside, and several more were set outside.","The conditions of the farmhouse were limited. There were no elegant low tables; instead, they used tall, wide tables where several people dined together.","There were three people at Dai Li's table.","The space was not large, so they sat close to one another. Looking up, one could clearly see the expressions on the others' faces.","Qin Shaozong sat beside Dai Li, holding his bowl in one hand and chopsticks in the other. His gaze drifted toward the woman beside him from time to time.","The afterglow of the sunset slipped through the wooden window, scattering golden fragments across the floor. A few stray beams landed on Dai Li's skirt, shimmering with a brilliant golden light. She looked as if she had been born from the light and would eventually dissolve back into the sunset.","Sensing his gaze falling on her too frequently, Dai Li turned to look at him, her eyes filled with confusion.","She was asking him what he was looking at.","She had just been crying; her eyes were bright as if washed with water, and the corners of her eyes were tinged with a flush of red, like rouge. However, her expression was somewhat weary, her spirits low.","Qin Shaozong guessed she must have gone to ask her son about the Divine Medicine. Between this mother and son, neither was easy to worry about. \"Ding Congjian’s medical skills are not bad, and his father and grandfather were even better. Besides that, there are other, more unconventional ways to handle it.\""]},{"number":89,"title":"Chapter 89","paragraphs":["Dai Li was instantly attracted by his last sentence.","An unconventional approach?","What kind of unconventional approach?","Unfortunately, after Dai Li asked, Qin Shaozong just said leisurely, This is not the place to discuss important matters. I will tell you after we go back, Madam.","Dai Li suddenly understood. The house they were staying in now was still the same one from before. The reason Zhouzhou was able to easily stay here back then was because of his identity as a divine envoy of the Qinglian Cult.","It was indeed inappropriate to discuss how to cure the poison administered by the Qinglian Cult here.","Dai Li stopped asking.","After staying in the small mountain village for the night, the group set off again early the next morning.","Today, Qin Shaozong also rode in the carriage with Dai Li. No one dared to ride his big red horse, so its reins were loosened to let it run along with the procession on its own.","Inside the carriage.","Not long after the carriage set off, Dai Li asked him, Qin Changgeng, the unconventional approach you mentioned yesterday, how do we take it?","She had been thinking about it all along.","Qin Shaozong smiled and said, Madam, have you been thinking about this all night? Asking so early in the morning.","Can't I ask? Dai Li was dissatisfied.","Alright, of course you can. Qin Shaozong took Dai Li's hand. The sleeve of his midnight blue robe slipped down a little with his movement, revealing a section of an empty, fair wrist.","Qin Shaozong lowered his eyes, his gaze falling upon it, feeling that it was too plain.","Other women wore gold and silver, but she only had an ordinary wooden hairpin on her now. He guessed that on her journey south, she had pawned her previous jewelry for money.","Dai Li saw that after he said you can, there was no further sound.","What was wrong with this person, keeping people in suspense.","Her fine eyebrows knitted together. She pulled her hand, trying to withdraw it, but failed. That large, dark hand tightened a little. It didn't hurt her, but it prevented her from retreating.","The Qinglian Cult has existed for over a hundred years. Perhaps at first, they only had a few people who held multiple roles, telling fortunes while dabbling in talisman water and divine medicines. But after a century of development, they have established various departments with clear divisions of labor. There must be a specific group of people dedicated to developing that so-called divine medicine, Qin Shaozong finally spoke.","Dai Li's knitted brows relaxed a little. Indeed.","If it had stood for a hundred years without falling, even a small workshop could develop into a large corporation.","Since that boy can take the divine medicine, it shows he is not a marginal figure in the cult. In that case, it's not impossible for him to know the hiding place of the drug maker.","Speaking of the latter part, Qin Shaozong's thin lips curled up, and a terrifying ruthlessness appeared in his eyes. Capture these people and interrogate them with severe torture. Are you afraid we won't get a formula or an antidote out of them?","He had his own set of interrogation methods in the North. Except for those specially trained as assassins, ordinary people could not withstand such cruel torture.","Dai Li suddenly realized, This really works!","This matter should be done sooner rather than later. Although Zhouzhou had tricked Diting into carrying out another mission, lies had a time limit, especially since her son might be a minor backbone member in the cult.","As time passed, it would easily arouse suspicion.","Dai Li couldn't wait to lift the carriage curtain and called out to the young man who was not far from the carriage at this time, Zhouzhou, come here for a moment.","Hearing the voice, Qin Yanzhou turned his head. Seeing his mother calling, he rode his horse over.","The carriage curtain was rolled up. Riding on the horse, Qin Yanzhou was much taller overall. Looking down through the carriage window, he happened to see his mother's held hand.","That large, dark hand had its five fingers spread out, inserted between her pale fingers, interlocking with them tightly, holding her hand firmly in his own.","It was truly an eyesore.","Qin Yanzhou looked away expressionlessly, and his gaze softened when he looked at Dai Li. Mother, what is it?","Unable to pull her hand away, Dai Li had to turn sideways with her hands behind her back to look at her son. Zhouzhou, do you know the developer of the divine medicine? What is that person's name, and where are they?","Anxious, she asked three questions in one breath.","Qin Yanzhou paused and instantly guessed the follow-up. He didn't ask anything else, but simply recalled, People in the cult generally use code names instead of their real names. The person who makes the medicine is called the Divine Physician. I often saw him when I was still in the cult, but after I went to the Fan residence, I never saw him again.","Dai Li's heart skipped a beat.","Never saw him after going to the Fan residence?","Her son had stayed in the Fan family for seven years, didn't that mean the last time he saw the Divine Physician was seven years ago?","Qin Yanzhou continued, The Divine Physician is a thin old man with a narrow face, half-white hair, thick lips, and long ears. He has an ordinary appearance, no different from an ordinary old man. As for the location, the Qinglian Cult has countless strongholds. Liudao is busy with affairs and rarely stays in one place for long. The few times I saw the Divine Physician, he came to pay his respects on the orders of Liudao.","Dai Li was surprised and doubtful. Liudao? The Divine Physician takes orders from him. Who is he?","Liudao is the uncle of Diting and Baixiang. This person is the current head of the Qinglian Cult, Qin Yanzhou said.","Dai Li frowned deeply.","Diting looked to be in his early twenties, but he already had a large entourage and great pomp in the cult. She had felt he had a significant background at the time, but she didn't expect him to be a prince of sorts.","Not staying in one place for long, this is hard to handle, Dai Li muttered.","What's so difficult? A lazy voice came from behind.","Dai Li turned her head. Isn't it difficult? They are fighting a guerrilla war.","Qin Shaozong applied some force to his hand, making Dai Li, who was leaning on the carriage window, sit properly back in her chair. He looked straight at the young man outside the window. After returning to Xiagu this afternoon, you list out all the Qinglian Cult strongholds you currently know, and I will dispatch people to rush there immediately.","Any old man who matched the description, regardless of whether he was the Divine Physician or not, would be captured first.","Qin Yanzhou said, Not all the strongholds are in the North and Yanzhou.","Qin Shaozong chuckled lightly. So what? It's just capturing a few people, not attacking their provincial governor's office. Could it be that other provincial governors will declare war on me because of this?","His demeanor was arrogant and extremely insolent, but it had to be said that it made a lot of sense.","Especially now that Yanzhou had recently been defeated, the North's momentum was booming and unstoppable. Anyone with a bit of brains would not confront them head-on at this critical juncture.","Qin Yanzhou was silent, unable to find words to refute.","Then it's settled. Qin Shaozong made the final decision. After saying this, he raised his long arm and pulled down the rolled-up carriage curtain, isolating the inside of the carriage from the outside.","Dai Li was speechless.","After a day of traveling, at the end of the Shen hour, Dai Li returned to Xiagu.","Coming back again, Dai Li's mood was quite complex, but her sighing lasted for less than half a quarter of an hour before she had no time to be melancholy.","Qin Yanzhou was concentrating on writing. Mulberry paper was spread out on the desk, and the ink-dipped wolf-hair brush moved smoothly and gracefully on the paper, quickly listing out place names one by one.","Dai Li stood aside, becoming more alarmed the more she looked.","This, there were so many...","There were fewer in the North, but the places outside the North were densely packed. They were not necessarily in commanderies or counties; many were also outside the cities. Each stronghold was pinned on the map like a thumbtack, pulled by invisible threads to form a large, spread-out net.","After a long while, Qin Yanzhou finally stopped writing. This is all I know. Mother, I have something I want to tell you.","Hmm? Dai Li's eyes were still on the paper.","She had looked at the map booklet earlier, roughly scanning the various provinces, commanderies, and counties. Now she found that most of these strongholds were concentrated around Yongzhou.","Yongzhou, the location of Chang'an.","\"Mom, I want to join the Northern Army,\" Qin Yanzhou said.","Dai Li abruptly raised her head, her face full of shock. \"Zhouzhou, why do you suddenly want to join the army? Joining the army here isn't like in modern times. Here, you really have to go to the battlefield. Besides, the medical conditions in this era are very primitive. If you get injured on the battlefield, an infection could easily cost you your life.\"","At first, she was just responding to her son's words, but as she went on, her worries grew heavier, leaving her with a deep frown.","Her son wanted to join the army.","He had just broken free from the Green Lotus Cult not long ago. After risking his life for them, he now wanted to enlist and risk his life for Qin Shaozong. What kind of nonsense was this!","She was a hundred times reluctant in her heart, but her child had grown up. As a parent, she couldn't just take control of everything like she did when he was little.","Suppressing her frustration, Dai Li asked him, \"Zhouzhou, why do you have this idea of joining the army?\"","Suddenly, a flash of insight crossed her mind. \"Is it because of me?\"","Seeing the young man before her fall silent, Dai Li understood everything. She immediately said anxiously, \"Zhouzhou, my greatest wish is for you to be safe and sound. Weapons on the battlefield have no eyes. If you accidentally get into a mishap and lose an arm or a leg, how do you expect Mom to live the rest of her life?\"","Qin Yanzhou's eyes were stubborn. \"Mom, I've grown up. I'm already a man. It should be me protecting you, but instead, I've caused you to worry about me because of those things. It is my failure as a son. I can repay the Marquis of Wu'an's favor myself. Isn't he trying to conquer the world? I can be his vanguard.\"","\"What vanguard!\" Dai Li rarely lost her temper to this extent. \"Who gave you permission to risk your life for Qin Shaozong?\"","...","Meanwhile, on the other side.","After the Black Valiant Cavalry arrived in Xiagu and wiped out one thousand of Sizhou's cavalry and three thousand infantry in a surprise attack, the battle had come to a close.","The Governor of Xiagu, Gao You, and the third son of the Sizhou Governor, Xie Yuanxiu, had originally been hiding in a certain residence on the city's North Street. Once the Black Valiant Cavalry completely took over Xiagu Commandery, they conducted a thorough search under Qin Shaozong's orders.","With thousands of men searching the city simultaneously, it didn't take much time at all to flush them out of hiding.","As for the treacherous Gao You, Qin Shaozong directly gave him a quick death. Tearing up the weeds by the roots, he didn't even spare Gao You's several sons.","As for Xie Yuanxiu, Qin Shaozong personally broke three of his ribs and both of his hands. He didn't kill this man immediately; keeping him alive still had its uses.","After dealing with these matters, Qin Shaozong returned to the main courtyard, thinking of having dinner with Dai Li. However, the moment he stepped inside, he heard a sentence:","\"Who gave you permission to risk your life for Qin Shaozong?\"","It was her voice.","She had a very easygoing temperament. Even towards the lowliest of maidservants, she spoke softly and gently. In all the time he had spent with her, he had never seen her fly into such a rage.","But now, that voice, usually as gentle as water, carried a seething anger, like boiling water about to overflow with scalding steam.","The guards stationed by the main courtyard didn't even dare to breathe too loudly.","The argument inside was fierce. They had caught a sentence or two, and even heard Lady Dai address the Marquis directly by his full name.","Calling someone by their full name, unless it was a superior addressing a subordinate, was universally regarded as disrespectful.","The guards wished they could plug their ears. But before the argument inside had even finished, the Marquis himself had arrived.","Qin Shaozong merely paused his steps slightly, then strode inside as if he hadn't heard a thing.","Dai Li was already so angry that she had stood up from her seat. Mother and son were both standing by the window, faintly forming a standoff. Just as she was about to continue speaking, a dark figure entered the corner of her eye.","Swallowing her words back down her throat, Dai Li took a deep breath. \"We will talk about this later.\"","Qin Yanzhou did not speak.","They sat around the table for dinner. Dai Li ate this meal in particular silence, only opening her mouth to speak when Qin Shaozong asked if the strongholds of the Green Lotus Cult had been written down.","After the meal, the young man holding the roster of strongholds left with Qin Shaozong.","Watching the backs of the two leaving, Dai Li pressed the center of her brows with a headache.","After that departure, it wasn't until bedtime that Qin Shaozong finally returned.","Gao You had just been dealt with today, and his estate had not yet been cleared out. Therefore, Dai Li and her group were temporarily staying in an estate that had been listed for sale.","The main courtyard was not large. Dai Li's meager, almost negligible luggage had been brought into the master bedroom by Qin Shaozong.","The implication was obvious: she was sleeping here tonight.","Dai Li didn't say anything; she would stay wherever he arranged. However, she went to bed early today. By the time Qin Shaozong returned, the lights in the room had already been extinguished.","He pushed the door open and entered. Without lighting a lamp, he undressed by the moonlight filtering through the unlatched window.","Sleeping on the inner side of the bed, Dai Li opened her eyes upon hearing the noise, but quickly closed them again in the darkness.","Stripped down to his inner garments, Qin Shaozong casually draped his leather belt and other items over the clothes rack before getting into bed.","Summer nights were often stiflingly hot. The blanket was very thin, but Qin Shaozong didn't bother covering himself at all. The breathing beside him was uneven; he knew she wasn't asleep yet.","The man turned on his side, reached out, and scooped the person beside him into his arms, along with the thin blanket draped over her.","The room was dark, lit only by the natural little lamp of moonlight by the window lattice. The moonlight stretched inward, becoming very dim by the time it reached the bed.","Yet, Qin Shaozong seemed to have eyes capable of night vision. After pulling her close, he first kissed Dai Li's earlobe, then leaned against her ear and whispered, \"That boy told me just now that he wants to join the army.\"","Dai Li had unexpectedly fallen into a furnace. Before she could push this oversized furnace away, she heard those words.","Dai Li's eyes snapped open. \"Absolutely not!\"","\"He is your son. My lady has the final say in this matter. Without your nod of approval, I guarantee that no unit in the North will dare take him onto the battlefield,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Dai Li had just breathed a sigh of relief when she heard him continue:","\"It's just that the boy managed to endure ten years on his own, which proves his resilient character. He is not someone meant to remain in a small pond. Moreover, with his past experiences in the Green Lotus Cult and the Fan Manor, asking him to live a conventional, rule-abiding life now would likely be difficult.\"","Before Dai Li could get angry, Qin Shaozong added the second half of his thought: \"Over these past few days, I've observed that he's somewhat withdrawn. He is so young, yet he lives like a little old man with no desires or demands, rarely opening up to others. Although the military has strict discipline, the camaraderie between brothers-in-arms is the easiest thing to build. If my lady worries about the blind weapons on the battlefield, why not place him in the military's rear?\"","Dai Li's eyes widened slightly.","The voice pressed against her temple continued, \"Find him an idle position to burn off his energy. It doesn't matter how well he does. It will satisfy the boy's demand to join the army while putting my lady's mind at ease. It's the best of both worlds, saving you mother and son from an unhappy fallout. What do you think, my lady?\"","The more Dai Li listened, the more she felt it was a viable idea. She also realized that she had previously fallen into a misconception, directly equating joining the army with going to the front lines.","There were many positions in the army. The logistics cooks were part of the army, and serving as a military advisor like Nalan Zhi was also being part of the army. He didn't necessarily have to tie his head to his waistband and charge into battle with a blade to kill enemies.","\"Hey, that's a good idea!\" Dai Li became happy, the frustration that had been pressing on her chest all evening gradually dissipating.","Hearing her relaxed tone, Qin Shaozong also hooked the corners of his lips, kissing her hair at the temples intermittently. \"Happy now?\"","He had some unshaven stubble on his jaw, which felt prickly when he pressed close. Dai Li turned her head away and reached out to push him. \"It's hot. Go sleep over there by yourself.\"","Qin Shaozong laughed in exasperation.","She absolutely could not change that awful habit of hers of burning bridges the second she got what she wanted."]},{"number":90,"title":"Chapter 90","paragraphs":["Behind the mountain gate of Longxing Temple.","Behind the temple lay a bamboo forest, beside which a stone pool had been dug to channel spring water from the mountain. The babbling stream, accompanied by the chirping of birds in the woods, conveyed an indescribable sense of tranquility and peace.","Deep in the bamboo forest stood a hexagonal pavilion with upturned eaves. Inside the pavilion, there were stone tables and chairs, and on the stone table rested a chessboard made of Kunshan jade.","A man sat by the table, holding a Kunshan jade chess piece, playing against himself.","Suddenly, a bird took flight, soaring straight into the sky, breaking the peace of the bamboo forest. It turned out that someone had hurried over, startling the birds. The man went straight ahead and finally stopped in front of the pavilion.","\"Sir, a letter from Diting.\" The servant presented a letter sealed with wax.","The sound of the Kunshan jade chess piece falling stopped. Liudao looked up, took the letter, and scanned it rapidly.","Before today, Diting had also sent several letters in succession.","The letters reported many things, including successfully abducting Madam Dai in the beginning, her escaping during the grand ceremony, Mingdeng's return, their pursuit to Xiagu Valley along with Third Young Master Xie, the arrival of the Marquis of Wu'an, and his persuasion of the Governor of Xiagu Valley to join forces against the Marquis of Wu'an...","In the previous letter, Diting told him of his intention to persuade the Governor of Xiagu Valley.","But now, Diting said in the letter that he had a bad premonition about the situation and wanted to leave Xiagu Valley. At the same time, the letter also said that he had stopped giving Mingdeng the divine medicine for a quarter, and begged him to be lenient when Mingdeng returned from his mission, considering that Mingdeng had worked hard even if he had no merits.","Reading to the end, ripples appeared in Liudao's eyes, which were usually as deep as an ancient pool.","Mingdeng returning from his mission? Who gave him a mission?","Mingdeng had always been a rather special existence in the cult. He had picked him up personally. At first, he didn't know if he was frightened or what, but for a long time, he was like a mute, unable to speak.","He was only slightly younger than Diting and Baixiang, so he just raised the three of them together.","Mingdeng only took orders from him, Diting, and Baixiang. Baixiang had gone to Sizhou on his orders a while ago to help the third son of Governor Xie of Sizhou ascend to power, and later changed his route to Yongzhou.","Baixiang had Baixiang's mission, and generally wouldn't contact Mingdeng privately midway.","But this possibility couldn't be ruled out...","Tapping his slender fingers lightly on the table twice, Liudao said, \"Bring pen, paper, and sealing wax.\"","The servant waiting at the side moved at the sound and returned with the items shortly after.","Using the chessboard as a desk, Liudao immediately wrote a letter by hand, sealed it himself, and handed it to the servant. \"Set off immediately and deliver it to Baixiang at top speed.\"","The man cupped his hands and received the order.","After the servant left, Liudao picked up a chess piece again. Just as he was about to place it down according to his previous train of thought, he suddenly realized that the situation on the entire chessboard had changed.","His white pieces had unknowingly fallen into a dangerous position.","Liudao's hand fell, and the long chain of Buddhist beads wrapped around his wrist a few times clattered onto the stone table. His hand fell a bit heavily, and the sound was abrupt.","*","More than ten cavalry squads set out from Xiagu Valley, heading in four directions: east, south, west, and north, galloping to various places.","Some cavalry squads' destinations were close to Xiagu Valley, and they arrived in less than a day. They took out a piece of paper from their pockets and found a house hidden in the city according to the specific location on it.","Knock knock.","The unknowing master of the house opened the door and was startled by a group of burly men.","\"Who are you? Hey, why are you coming in? What exactly are you going to do?\"","Inside, an old man came out upon hearing the sound, but before he could speak, two burly men came over, grabbed him from the left and right, and directly carried him out the door.","The old woman turned pale with fright. \"Where are you taking my husband?\"","A guard said, \"Don't worry, it's just a routine interrogation. If there's nothing unusual, we guarantee to send him back in one piece.\"","Such a scene occurred in different places soon after.","*","Xiagu Commandery, Qin Residence.","Last night, Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou had a disagreement. Today, before lunch, Qin Shaozong rushed back from the military camp to eat with the mother and son.","The small round table was filled with dishes, both meat and vegetarian, as well as mung bean soup to cool down the summer heat.","The vegetarian dish was the most ordinary cold mixed vegetables, and the meat dishes were Dai Li's favorite steamed fish and boiled river shrimp, plus a plate of roast mutton.","They picked up their chopsticks and began to eat.","Dai Li picked up a river shrimp for her son. \"Zhouzhou, I thought about it last night, and joining the army isn't entirely impossible. There are no high schools or universities here. If you want to study at your current age, you can only follow a private tutor. Mr. Nalan is a military advisor and will often stay in the army. If you follow him, you will inevitably come into contact with military affairs.\"","When saying these words, Dai Li didn't avoid Qin Shaozong, who was beside her. He could listen if he wanted to; anyway, he couldn't possibly understand everything.","Qin Yanzhou was slightly startled, not expecting his mother to change her tune so quickly.","His gaze couldn't help but shift to the side, quickly glancing at a certain person with a normal expression, who lowered his eyes, picked up a piece of roast mutton with jade chopsticks, and was focused on eating the meat, as if he hadn't heard his mother's words just now.","Qin Yanzhou withdrew his gaze. \"Thank you, Mom.\"","Dai Li smiled. \"Why thank me? We're a family.\"","Qin Shaozong, who was eating mutton with his head down, suddenly blurted out, \"So Madam also knows that families don't speak two languages. When did you learn that?\"","Dai Li's eyelids twitched, knowing he was referring to the \"thank you\" she had said to him in the carriage the day before yesterday. She played dumb. \"A great immortal came to me in a dream last night, and I learned it on the spot.\"","\"Now that Madam uses it with ease, it seems you've learned it.\" Seeing that she had eaten almost one side of the steamed fish, Qin Shaozong raised his chopsticks to pick up the fish body, intending to flip it over.","As a result, the fish bones were steamed a bit soft and rotten. Halfway through the flip, the back half broke off.","Qin Shaozong held half of the fish in his chopsticks, unable to attend to the other half. Just then, another pair of jade chopsticks reached over, flipped the fallen fish tail over as well, and after flipping it, conveniently picked away a large piece of fish meat from the fish tail.","The fish meat dipped in sauce was delicious and juicy. As soon as it entered Dai Li's mouth, she narrowed her eyes in satisfaction. Suddenly, she noticed the man beside her looking at her.","Steadily, without blinking, his gaze seemed to be mixed with something heavy.","Dai Li only glanced at him and then looked away, thinking to herself that this person was sometimes truly baffling. But soon, she put this to the back of her mind and brought up another matter. \"Qin Changgeng, can you have someone forge an iron wok? I want to use an iron wok to stir-fry dishes in the future.\"","In this era, iron was very precious and mostly used for weapons. The government also strictly controlled iron. Production determined everything. The production of iron had not yet gone up, which destined iron woks not to fly into ordinary people's homes like pottery cauldrons.","Without an iron wok, there could be no stir-frying.","Life had to go on no matter what, and she had to treat herself and Zhouzhou better.","\"Alright, I'll have someone deliver it tomorrow,\" Qin Shaozong readily agreed, and then asked, \"Did every household in the Peach Blossom Spring where Madam lived before use an iron wok?\"","Qin Yanzhou, who had been eating with his head down, paused slightly.","Dai Li nodded and said yes.","Qin Shaozong only asked this one question and didn't ask anything else.","After the meal, Qin Shaozong left the main courtyard and went to the study.","In the study, besides Bai Jianping and Qiao Wangfei, who were still in the military camp, everyone else was present.","Qin Shaozong called out a name. \"Mo Yanyun, lead a team to escort Third Young Master Xie back to Sizhou.\"","Mo Yanyun first cupped his hands to accept the order, and only after taking the task did he ask: \"My Lord, why keep this man alive?\"","Xie Yuanxiu, along with the Green Lotus Sect, previously plotted against Madam Dai, and later mobilized troops to besiege the city, attempting to take the Lord's life. Based on the Lord's usual way of doing things, it stands to reason he should not let him off.","\"The tendons in both his hands have been completely severed. Even if they are reattached in the future, he will be nothing but a cripple.\"","Qin Shaozong sneered, \"And do you think that when he returns to Sizhou, he can really command everyone's obedience like before? Just based on what he did to his two older brothers for the sake of rising to power, it is enough for the latter to skin him alive and tear him apart.\"","Power struggles have always been chillingly ruthless. They can cause family members to turn against each other and siblings to kill one another. No matter how good a relationship is, once the words power struggle are involved, it can never return to its pure beginnings.","Qin Shaozong: \"Sending him back is nothing more than earning a good reputation.\"","Kuang Ye heard other information from his superior's words. \"My Lord, you do not plan to march on Sizhou? Why is this? The Governor of Sizhou has just died of illness, and Sizhou is currently in a chaotic period of power transition. Coupled with Third Young Master Xie taking the initiative to invade earlier, we have every reason to raise an army against Sizhou.\"","Feng Feng also nodded repeatedly.","That was indeed the logic.","Qin Shaozong, however, said, \"If I had taken Yanzhou on my own, that would be one thing. But we allied with Qingzhou. The old debts have not been settled yet, and adding new ones will only make them snowball. It is hard to guarantee that Nangong Xiong will not have malicious intentions under the lure of heavy profits, secretly teaming up with other provinces to play the mantis stalking the cicada, unaware of the oriole behind.\"","The few men were momentarily speechless.","True, swallowing Yanzhou required time to digest. Trying to immediately swallow Sizhou right after might cause them to choke.","\"There is no need to stay long in Xiagu. We will set off to return to Bairi City the day after tomorrow.\" Qin Shaozong flipped open the booklet of Xiagu's officials. \"This Deputy Governor surnamed Ding is usable. Promote him to the position of Governor, and have him temporarily manage the entire Xiagu Commandery in place of Gao You.\"","After giving a series of orders, Qin Shaozong finally said, \"Feng Feng, have someone cast an iron pot and deliver it before noon tomorrow.\"","Feng Feng, who was called out, initially braced himself for a serious task, but the result was just him being asked to cast a pot. He agreed first, then asked, \"My Lord, what is the use of this iron pot?\"","\"Madam said she wants to use an iron pot to stir-fry dishes from now on,\" Qin Shaozong said.","The men were all slightly stunned.","Stir-frying with an iron pot?","Unheard of, and a bit extravagant. But since it was Madam Dai who said it, she must have her reasons.","Feng Feng's thoughts could not help but wander. \"Could it be that cooking with an iron pot is beneficial to the body?\"","The others laughed at his absurdity.","Qin Shaozong was noncommittal.","After they finished laughing, Qin Shaozong began to shoo them away. \"Go do what you need to do, do not just stand here.\"","The crowd filed out.","After they left, Qin Shaozong took out paper and brush from the side of the desk and wrote a letter in one breath.","After sealing it with wax, he called in his personal guard from outside and ordered, \"Ride with all haste, deliver this letter to Yan San, and tell him to make sure this matter is handled properly.\"","The guard cupped his hands: \"Yes.\"","Qin Shaozong watched the guard's back, his brown eyes darkening.","The Yan family was something he had personally propped up. For this matter, he could not trust anyone but Yan San.","A fast horse set out from Xiagu, traveling day and night to the Ying Commandery in the north. By the time Yan San received this secret letter, several days had passed.","\"Commandant Yan, a letter from the Lord.\" The guard presented the letter and relayed Qin Shaozong's oral message. \"The Lord commands you to ensure this matter is handled properly.\"","Before the letter was even opened, an oral message was added. Yan San furrowed his brows, knowing that what was written in this letter must be a matter of utmost importance.","He broke the wax seal and took out the letter.","There were not many words on the letter, but they made Yan San's pupils shrink slightly, and shock surged in his eyes.","He froze for a moment before recovering.","The guard was still at the door, and Yan San said to him, \"I have read the letter. Go back and tell the Lord that I will definitely handle this matter with the utmost caution, and ask him to rest assured. Go now, and close the door on your way out.\"","The guard received the order and left.","Only Yan San was left in the room. He took out a piece of mulberry paper, ground some ink, and then picked up a brush to write down names one by one.","Wei Congmu, Wei Conglin, Wei Congsen.","The direct Cong generation of the Wei family only had three male descendants. And these three were all brothers of the Lord's late wife.","Yan San's gaze roamed among the three.","The eldest, Wei Congmu, was the current Chief Clerk of Yuyang Commandery; the second, Wei Conglin, was in the military, serving as a Section Commandant; the third, Wei Congsen, held no official position.","Yan San's fingers tapped quickly on the desk a few times, the tip of his brush hovering between the second and third brothers. His mind quickly flashed through their personalities, past experiences, their wives' family backgrounds, as well as their status within the Wei family and how much they were valued by their parents.","A drop of black ink fell between Wei Conglin and Wei Congsen.","Yan San looked at the stained paper, and finally with a stroke of his brush, he circled a name along with that ink mark. He then immediately wrote lines of small characters below this name.","These words connected together, forming an invisible large net, silently approaching an unaware person.","After a long time, Yan San stopped writing. He read this paper a full three times to ensure it was smooth and flawless, and only then did he light the oil lamp and personally burn the paper.","\"Have Yan Qingsheng come over,\" Yan San said to the guard outside.","The latter took the order.","Soon, a young man in an indigo robe arrived at the door of the study.","Yan Qingsheng was in his early twenties, with facial features somewhat similar to Yan San's, but he had a pair of dimples on his face, making him quite endearing when he smiled. \"Uncle, what orders do you have for your nephew?\"","\"I need to go out for a trip, the date of return is undecided. Ying Commandery is left to you,\" Yan San said concisely.","Yan Qingsheng's expression changed slightly. \"Uncle, leave Ying Commandery to me? How can that work? Recently, spies from all sides have been making a comeback. Without you holding down the fort, I am afraid I will not be able to handle it.\"","Yan San said calmly, \"The foundation has already been laid, just keep everything as usual. Qingsheng, you must learn to be independent. I cannot manage everything for you forever. The Lord will not heavily rely on someone who panics when faced with trouble and lacks their own judgment.\"","Yan Qingsheng took a deep breath. \"Nephew understands. During the time you are away, I will guard Ying Commandery well. But Uncle, what matter is so urgent that it requires you to go personally?\"","Yan San only said it was an important matter and said nothing else.","He lowered his eyes to look at the ashes on the table, thinking to himself that after this matter, the situation in the Lord's mansion that had been maintained for over ten years was going to be broken."]},{"number":91,"title":"Chapter 91","paragraphs":["Bairi City.","After a tiring journey, Dai Li followed Qin Shaozong back to Bairi City.","Having been separated from Nianxia and Bipo for nearly two months, the two maids wept tears of joy upon seeing Dai Li again.","Seeing their expressions of mingled remorse and overwhelming shame, Dai Li merely comforted them by saying she had not suffered. She was too embarrassed to admit that, later on, she simply had not wanted to come back.","The very first thing Dai Li did upon returning to Bairi City was take her son to see Ding Lianxi.","The Green Lotus Cult was hostile to the Northern Army, and Qin Shaozong himself harbored a deep disgust for religious sects and talks of ghosts and spirits. Therefore, during the consultation, Dai Li only said, Mr. Ding, my son accidentally ingested a poison while we were away. I heard that once this drug is taken, one must take an antidote regularly, otherwise it will cause their intestines and stomach to rot away. Please, sir, could you check his pulse?","Ding Lianxi immediately turned serious. Young Master, please sit down and extend your right hand.","Qin Yanzhou did as he was told.","Ding Lianxi began to feel his pulse.","Dai Li watched from the side, her heart rising into her throat as Ding Lianxi's brows gradually furrowed. After a long while, seeing him withdraw his hand, she hurriedly asked, Mr. Ding, how is my son...","When she spoke, her voice carried an unconscious tremble.","Madam Dai, the Young Master's pulse is calm and steady. Please forgive my lack of skill, but I cannot detect any signs of poisoning, Ding Lianxi replied.","Dai Li felt a wave of dizziness wash over her.","How could there be no abnormalities?","Zhouzhou, tell Mr. Ding in detail what happened last night, Dai Li said to her son.","When she woke up this morning, she noticed her son was looking unwell and asked if he had not slept well the night before. It was meant to be a casual question, but it led her to unexpectedly discover that something was wrong with him.","After some probing, Zhouzhou finally told her that he had felt unwell during the night.","Severe ringing in his ears, dizziness, and abdominal pain.","Dai Li's immediate reaction was that the poison was acting up.","The abdominal pain started late last night around midnight and lasted for two hours. Around three in the morning, I heard a buzzing sound in both ears... He paused for a moment before adding, It sounded a bit like insects flapping their wings.","The color completely drained from Dai Li's face.","Around four in the morning, I felt dizzy and lightheaded for about half an hour, as if I were floating in the clouds. But after five o'clock, when dawn broke, everything returned to normal, Qin Yanzhou explained, detailing everything.","Ding Lianxi's expression grew solemn. He asked Qin Yanzhou to extend his hand again and took his pulse a second time.","This time, the pulse-taking lasted even longer than before. Afterward, Ding Lianxi carefully examined Qin Yanzhou's eyes, ears, mouth, and nose, but the result remained the same.","Ding Lianxi looked deeply ashamed. Madam Dai, I cannot find anything unusual. The Young Master's pulse is slightly floating, but it is autumn now, so it is normal for the pulse to be a bit more restless than usual.","Mother, I am fine. Everything went back to normal after dawn, Qin Yanzhou comforted her.","Ding Lianxi pondered for a moment. How many times has the Young Master experienced these symptoms recently?","Qin Yanzhou: Roughly once every ten days, always at night.","Ding Lianxi frowned in amazement. To be this regular is truly unheard of. Madam Dai, I am powerless and cannot see the root of the problem. Perhaps when we return to Yuyang, I can introduce the Young Master to my grandfather.","Dai Li naturally agreed, thanking him repeatedly. By the way, Mr. Ding, my son just mentioned hearing the sound of insects flapping their wings. Is it possible... that there are bugs inside his body?","In Dai Li's understanding, things like Gu bugs only existed in television shows or novels.","In history, the most famous record of such unorthodox practices was the Wugu witchcraft scandal during the reign of Emperor Wu of Han. However, that was merely Liu Che's belief that someone was cursing him with sorcery. Setting aside the involvement of wooden puppets, the mere fact that it was based on his belief made it highly subjective; whether it actually happened or not is hard to say.","But the Great Yan Dynasty, where Dai Li currently found herself, did not exist in the history she knew. Although the general environment was similar to the Qin and Han dynasties, it was not entirely the same. For instance, items like stirrups had appeared ahead of time.","Therefore, was it possible that some bizarre and mystical things also existed in this era?","Ding Lianxi sighed. We cannot rule out the possibility, but for the specifics, I will need my grandfather to take a look.","Then I will leave it to Mr. Ding to help make the connection when the time comes, Dai Li thanked him once again.","You are too polite, Madam Dai.","Dai Li's thoughts drifted, wondering when they could return to Yuyang. If Qin Shaozong was not going back so soon, could she take Zhouzhou there first to seek medical treatment?","...","While Dai Li was taking her son to see Ding Lianxi, Qin Shaozong was receiving a guest in the main hall.","Nangong Xiong had come knocking.","He disliked tea and much preferred wine, so Qin Shaozong had wine brought up, and the two drank merrily together.","Qin Changgeng, you were gone for over a month, and I guarded White Sun City perfectly for you. How about it? I am quite the loyal friend, aren't I? Nangong Xiong said, gripping his wine goblet.","Qin Shaozong raised his cup to him. Naturally, you are.","Nangong Xiong laughed. When I invited you south to form an alliance, I had made up my mind to weather the storms with the North, so I naturally wouldn't break our pact. However, business is business. Qin Changgeng, you slaughtered every male member of the Fan family, and my future son-in-law died by your hands. You destroyed my son-in-law, so shouldn't you compensate me with a new one?","Hearing this, Qin Shaozong knew the man hadn't come simply to drink with him.","Qin Shaozong invited him, It is almost mealtime. Why don't you dine at my estate?","Nangong Xiong had deliberately arrived right at mealtime specifically to eat at the Qin estate and prolong their conversation. Then I will respectfully accept.","Qin Shaozong ordered his attendants to prepare the food.","Just as he turned back, he heard Nangong Xiong continue, Neither of your two sons is married. What would be the harm in just picking one to give to me?","This was laying his cards completely on the table.","The hand holding Qin Shaozong's wine goblet paused slightly. Yunce is my elder brother's son. Back then, my brother and sister-in-law passed away one after another, leaving behind a five-year-old boy and a two-year-old girl. As the saying goes, when a person is gone, the tea cools. There were many opportunists within the clan and outside who bullied the helpless orphans. So, I had them acknowledge me as their father, just to stop others from bullying them openly or in secret.","Hearing this, Nangong Xiong thought to himself: Since they acknowledged you as their father, you are still the one who has the final say in their marriages.","But Yunce was already old enough to remember things back then, and he had a very deep affection for my brother. At first, he was unwilling to accept my proposal. I had to explain the situation to him and promise that when he reached adulthood, if he wanted to change it back, he could openly be his biological father's son and go back to calling me uncle. That was the only way it worked, Qin Shaozong said.","Nangong Xiong was greatly astonished. Are you serious? Qin Changgeng, you aren't tricking me, are you?","How could acknowledging a father be something you could just do and undo so casually?","Why would I trick you? In the Qin clan's genealogy, the two siblings are still recorded under my brother's name. Qin Shaozong let out a soft scoff, then fell silent for a moment. I feel indebted to my brother. How could I forcibly steal his children?","Nangong Xiong muttered, \"How old is he again? When is his coming-of-age ceremony?\"","Qin Shaozong replied, \"He is nineteen and will be crowned this winter.\"","Nangong Xiong's mind raced. What he valued was Qin Shaozong's power. If this eldest son were to acknowledge his biological father, marrying his daughter to him would be completely useless.","Thus, Nangong Xiong changed his tune and asked, \"What about the younger one? I haven't heard of your son being betrothed.\"","Qin Shaozong lazily swirled his wine goblet, watching the liquid ripple inside. \"The moment he was born, his mother arranged a childhood betrothal for him.\"","Nangong Xiong inhaled sharply. \"Which family?\"","\"A lady from his mother's side of the family,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Qin Shaozong was the second son of the Qin family. Initially, the entire Qin clan centered around his older brother, who had married into the prominent Jiang family of Yuyang.","When it was his turn to marry, his father told him that the Wei and Wu families were planning an alliance through marriage. If the Qin family ignored this, the Wei family would be won over by the Wu family.","The Qin and Wu families were blood enemies. First, there was the death of an heir at the other's hands, and later, a fierce struggle for the position of provincial governor. The two families fought bitterly.","Meanwhile, the Wei family was one of the major clans in Yuyang.","Seeing the impending Wu-Wei alliance, Father Qin and the clan elders could no longer sit still. Realizing they still had a legitimate second son, they simply pushed this younger son forward to marry into the Wei family.","Given the situation at the time, both the Qin and Wu families were courting the Wei family. Knowing they had nothing to fear, the Wei family adopted a very high and mighty stance.","Later, the Wei family astutely sensed that this son-in-law from the Qin family was likely no ordinary man. Striking while the iron was hot, at the hundred-day banquet celebrating the birth of their maternal grandson, the Wei daughter who had married into the Qin family took the lead in arranging a childhood betrothal between her son and a girl from the Wei family.","Of course, Qin Shaozong only told half the story, leaving out some of the unexpected turns that happened later.","Nangong Xiong frowned deeply.","Of the two sons, it was uncertain if the older one could even be kept, and the younger one's marriage was already settled, which meant he was also off the table.","Suddenly, a flash of inspiration crossed Nangong Xiong's mind. \"Right, I heard that Nalan Wugong recently took in a disciple named Qin Yanzhou. In the past, so many capable and ambitious men tried to become Nalan Wugong's disciple, only to return in failure. How did this Qin Yanzhou become the exception? His surname is Qin. I remember you once said that Quanjie is a child of the Qin family who was abducted in his youth and eventually ended up under Fan Tianshi's command. Could it be that this Qin Yanzhou is actually Quanjie? And now he has simply abandoned his past, changed his name, and presented himself anew to the world.\"","As he spoke, he stroked his chin and murmured, \"The name Qin Yanzhou sounds somewhat familiar for some reason...\"","The hand with which Qin Shaozong was swirling his wine goblet suddenly stopped.","It had to be said that to become a powerful provincial warlord, Nangong Xiong truly had his extraordinary qualities.","Nangong Xiong had been observing Qin Shaozong all along, and seeing his reaction, he chuckled. \"It seems my guess is correct. You previously said he was the son of an old friend. Who is this old friend? A man or a woman?\"","Nangong Xiong's last question was just a casual remark, but unexpectedly, the man beside him shot him a sidelong glance and actually said, \"Nangong, you talk too much today. Are you drunk on wine?\"","\"The old friend is a woman?!\" Nangong Xiong exclaimed in surprise.","His mind instantly spun through several possibilities. A child of the Qin family, an old friend... Could it be that this old friend was an old flame of Qin Changgeng, and that boy was the son she secretly gave birth to?","\"My younger brother has a legitimate daughter. She is fifteen, beautiful, and has a gentle disposition. What do you think about betrothing her to Qin Yanzhou?\" Nangong Xiong probed.","The fact that Qin Changgeng was willing to spend so much effort cleaning up that boy's mess showed that he valued him exceptionally. The future of the eldest son was still undecided, and the second son no longer had a chance. Therefore, it was better to first secure Qin Yanzhou, whose identity was temporarily unclear but certainly wouldn't be too bad.","Although his younger brother's status was not as high as his own, and his niece was not as beautiful as his daughter, their family background was still prominently established; it would not be a disgrace to him.","Qin Shaozong's tone was cold. \"Not interested.\"","If he dared to promise that boy's hand in marriage, her merely tearing the roof off would be getting off lightly. She would likely just take her son and run away from home again without a second thought.","Nangong Xiong was about to press the matter, but at that moment, the army cooks brought in the meals. As soon as they entered, Nangong Xiong subconsciously sniffed the air, catching a very overpowering and rich aroma.","Fragrant, truly fragrant!","\"What delicacies are we having today?\" Nangong Xiong's attention was immediately diverted.","\"Stir-fried mutton with Sichuan peppercorns, along with a fish soup simmered from pan-fried fish,\" Qin Shaozong replied with a smile.","The two men ate at separate low tables, each served an identical portion.","When the clay dishes were presented on the table, the usually alcohol-loving Nangong Xiong forgot the fine wine in his cup for the very first time, staring unblinkingly at the meat in front of him.","It was no exaggeration; the aroma was absolutely mouth-watering.","He didn't stand on ceremony with Qin Shaozong. Picking up his jade chopsticks, he grabbed a piece of meat and stuffed it into his mouth.","At that moment, the rich flavor danced across his taste buds, shocking Nangong Xiong so much that his pupils contracted. He marveled greatly, \"This makes life in the mortal realm worth living!\"","He then turned and asked, \"Qin Changgeng, where did you conjure up such a delicacy?\"","\"My wife ordered the kitchen to make it.\" Qin Shaozong also picked up his chopsticks.","Nangong Xiong paused his chewing, inexplicably recalling the woman who had followed Qin Shaozong on his military campaign, along with certain rumors. \"Does that lady have the surname Dai?\"","Qin Shaozong nodded, not denying it.","\"Tsk, you sure are lucky.\" Nangong Xiong felt a twinge of sourness in his heart. The dragon-bone water wheel was such an incredible invention; farmers all over the realm were deeply grateful to the Northern Lands because of it.","Originally, Nangong Xiong had timed his visit right at mealtime, planning to eat and negotiate simultaneously. He had been determined to grab one of Qin Shaozong's sons today to take back as a son-in-law. However, once he started eating, apart from those initial few sentences, he spent the entire time with his head buried in his food, eating ferociously and unable to spare a moment to say another word.","Taking this all in, Qin Shaozong felt as if he were looking at his past self. He couldn't help but smile, his thoughts drifting far away.","Returning to the city today, she would probably take that boy to find Ding Lianxi right away. He wondered what the outcome would be.","The meal concluded.","Nangong Xiong was still left wanting more. His stomach was full, but his appetite had not diminished in the slightest. Having just finished this meal, he was already anticipating the next. \"Qin Changgeng, how did Lady Dai cook this mutton to make it so incredibly fragrant? Tell me the recipe.\"","Qin Shaozong replied, \"I won't tell you.\"","Nangong Xiong thought he had misheard. But looking at the man again, his face was completely relaxed, and the corners of his mouth held a smirk that made one's fists itch to punch him.","Right, he hadn't misheard. That fellow Qin Changgeng was doing it on purpose.","Nangong Xiong voiced his dissatisfaction, \"It's just a delicious dish. Why should a grown man be so stingy over it?\"","Qin Shaozong said, \"This recipe is managed by my wife. Nangong, if you really want to know, why not find some precious treasures that ladies love? If she is pleased upon seeing them, she might just tell you.\"","*","Yuyang Commandery.","Qin Shaozong's ancestral home was in Youzhou. As the core of Youzhou, Yuyang Commandery had grown far more prosperous than other regions as Qin Shaozong's power and influence became increasingly prominent.","Many powerful and prominent families gathered here, with the Qin, Jiang, Wei, Zou, and Cai families enjoying the greatest prestige, standing as top-tier powerful clans.","A few years ago, there was also the Wu clan. Unfortunately, they suffered a series of defeats in their power struggle against the Qin clan and were ultimately forced to withdraw from Yuyang's aristocratic circle.","Several great, prominent families were rooted in Yuyang like intertwining vines. One family would be bound to another by marriage, while that family would share deep, complex ties with yet another.","Naturally, where there were good relationships, there were also bad ones.","Frictions, both great and small, were a constant among the clans. Major conflicts arose over official positions, military merits, and land, while minor disputes involved the younger generation showing off their wealth or fighting over women.","Today, a playboy from the Zhang family might beat up a young master from the Li family. Tomorrow, the Sun family might throw a lavish banquet for friends and relatives, deliberately excluding a certain family just to humiliate them.","Incidents of all sizes emerged one after another, providing the local commoners with fresh gossip every few days. Recently, however, a rather significant event shook Yuyang Commandery.","Wei Conglin of the Wei family, after drinking with his friends, accidentally beat a man to death.","The victim was no stranger. It was Cai Pei, a scion of the Cai family and a commandery commandant, who had recently had a bitter falling out with Wei Conglin.","As luck would have it, the relationship between the Cai and Wei families was already quite poor to begin with."]},{"number":92,"title":"Chapter 92","paragraphs":["The discord between the Cai and Wei families dates back more than three generations.","Back then, the Cai patriarch's full sister married a Wei family scion. This young Master Wei had a fiery temper and would often beat his wife in a fit of rage.","The Cai daughter endured it for five years until she could bear it no longer. She secretly sent a message to a loyal retainer who had once been infatuated with her but was forced to transfer away after her marriage.","Upon hearing the news, the loyal servant arrived and disguised himself as a bandit on the official road, killing Master Wei. He then fled the Wei family with the Cai daughter and her pair of young children.","Originally, everything should have ended there. After all, the group of Wei family members present at the time were all killed, and the carriage was driven off a cliff, creating the illusion of an out-of-control fall. Three mutilated corpses were even arranged at the bottom.","But man proposes, God disposes. No one expected a hunter to witness everything, and this hunter was unexpectedly found by the Wei family.","That was a big deal. The Wei family exploded and demanded an explanation from the Cai family.","At that time, the patriarch of the Cai family had recently been replaced by the Cai daughter's full brother. Because of the large age difference between the siblings, the Cai patriarch treated his sister like a daughter. Seeing the Wei family come to the door, demanding the Cai family hand over the person and personally execute him, how could he submit? Not only did he refuse to hand him over, but he also bluntly stated that Master Wei had a flawed character and deserved to die, and that his family's retainer was merely carrying out justice on behalf of heaven.","When these words were released, it was a disaster, infuriating the Wei family.","The deceased Master Wei was of the direct line and had considerable ability. In their view, apart from the minor flaw of being prone to anger, this person was definitely a pillar of the Wei family, and could even rank in the top five of the massive Wei clan.","The discord between the Cai and Wei families, from that moment on, was like a broken mirror that would continue to bump and scrape in the future.","For the next two generations, there were no more marriages between the younger generations.","Setting aside this old grudge, the recent drunken murder case was no small matter.","The official position of Commandery Commandant was slightly higher than that of Division Commandant.","In other words, Wei Conglin, a subordinate, had actually beaten his superior to death.","According to the laws of the Great Yan, an official who committed patricide or murdered a superior should receive sixty lashes and be sentenced to having his head shaved, wearing an iron collar, and pounding grain for building city walls for five years.","This meant that he would first be beaten sixty times with a whip or wooden board, have all his hair and beard shaved off, wear a highly insulting iron collar around his neck, and then be sent to build city walls.","\"...Father, these sixty lashes will cost your son his life! The people in charge of criminal law include members of the Cai family. They will definitely have someone beat me to death.\" Wei Conglin knelt before his father.","His younger brother, Wei Congsen, was very helpless. \"Second Brother, why were you so impulsive? If you couldn't get along with Cai Pei, just cursing a few words would have been enough. Why did you beat him to death? The Cai family finally managed to raise a Commandery Commandant, and now he's gone. They will never let this go.\"","\"I-I did beat him, but I didn't strike to kill! How could I possibly beat someone to death?\" Wei Conglin felt extremely wronged.","His older brother, Wei Congmu, coldly scoffed. \"You just beat a servant to death after drinking last year. How many times have I told you that drinking ruins things, and told you to drink less, but you just wouldn't listen.\"","Wei Conglin said in a low voice, \"That day was Zou Yude's birthday banquet. I've always had a good relationship with him, so naturally I had to be there. With the atmosphere so lively, it's inevitable that I drank a little too much. Cai Pei's death is also strange. Who knows if he didn't already have poor health...\"","\"Crash.\"","Someone at the head of the table smashed a teacup, and Wei Conglin hurriedly hushed.","Father Wei looked at his second son with disappointment. \"The clan spent a lot of effort cultivating you to push you to the position of Division Commandant, thinking that you would be promoted another level in a few years. But look at you, causing trouble outside. You haven't helped the family much, and now you've got your father worrying about wiping your ass.\"","Feeling the overt and covert accusatory gazes on him, Wei Conglin felt suffocated.","The authority of a Division Commandant was not low. Outside, he could get whatever he wanted, and there were plenty of people flattering him. Now, returning home to be reprimanded, even his third brother, who held no official position, dared to covertly accuse him.","\"Father, although my sister has been gone for fifteen years, the Marquis of Wu'an hasn't remarried all these years. In the end, the relationship between the Qin and Wei families is far beyond what other prominent families can compare to. Could we have someone go to the Qin family and pull some strings? If the Qin family steps forward, the Cai family will definitely not dare to act recklessly,\" Wei Conglin suggested.","As soon as these words came out, the study fell silent for a few breaths.","Father Wei pinched the bridge of his nose. \"Have Lady Cheng go to the Qin family to find Qinian. Lady Cheng is Qinian's aunt. She has frequently visited the Qin family over the years. It couldn't be more appropriate for her to act as a bridge.\"","Just as these words fell, the panicked voice of a servant came from outside. \"Master, many people from the government office have come, saying... they want to take Division Commandant Wei away for interrogation.\"","\"Outrageous! They actually came to our home to arrest someone!\"","This was an arrest.","\"Quickly find Fifth Sister!\" Wei Conglin said to his younger brother.","*","At the same time, the Marquis of Yuyang's Residence.","\"Uncle Yan, why are you back? Are you here to tell me that Father has relented and is summoning me to the front lines?\"","The sixteen-year-old youth was dressed in a red and black mixed martial arts outfit. The lower half of his face resembled his biological father, but his eyes were more like his biological mother's—pitch black, with somewhat blunt and round inner corners.","He had a chair but refused to sit on it, preferring to sit on a wooden chest, swinging his legs, with a piece of grass of unknown origin dangling from his mouth.","Before Yan San could speak, the youth continued talking to himself, \"The injuries I suffered in the Northern Kingdom have been healed for hundreds of years. Old Mr. Ding also checked me out, and there's nothing wrong. They all say father and son are the best soldiers on the battlefield. It makes no sense for Father to go on this expedition without taking me along.\"","\"Third Young Master, the Marquis wants you to go to the military camp in the suburbs,\" Yan San said.","Qin Qinian, who had been lazy and scattered, suddenly perked up. He spat out the grass in his mouth. \"Really? Don't fool me. Last time I secretly went to the military camp and was discovered, Eldest Brother punished me by making me copy books, just as Father said. Oh my, whenever I look at a book, my head spins and swells. Those words are like dancing; it's better to just beat me up.\"","Yan San: \"I'm not lying to you. There's just one thing: the Marquis wants you to follow my arrangements in the military camp, and you are not to return to the residence for a short period of time.\"","Qin Qinian leaped down from the chest. \"Listen, listen, listen, I'll listen to Uncle Yan for everything. Let's go right now. I'm going to be a great general in the future. If I'm a step late, who knows, I might become one a day later.\"","Yan San didn't say anything else, merely leading the person away.","An hour after they left, a carriage hanging a wooden plaque of the Wei clan arrived at the Qin residence.","This carriage was not unfamiliar to the Qin residence. The guards at the gate knew why the person in the carriage had come. Usually, she would be allowed in directly after being announced, but today the guard said:","\"The Third Young Master left the residence an hour ago and is not here now.\"","The lady was surprised. \"Qinian is actually not here. Did he say when he would return?\"","The guard shook his head.","\"Alright, then I'll come back tomorrow.\"","*","Longxing Temple, behind the mountain gate.","A servant hurried over. \"Sir, this is a reply from White Elephant.\"","Liudao sat by the window in the room. Many things were spread out on the desk in front of him, the most numerous being small boxes, small in volume, similar to a lady's rouge box.","\"Put it on the desk,\" Liudao said calmly.","The servant put down the letter and left the room.","Liudao unscrewed one of the small boxes, revealing that it was filled to the brim with yellow powder. He used a small wooden spoon to scoop out a little, first placing it into a clay bowl.","Before Liudao could open another small box, footsteps sounded from outside.","A tall, slender white figure walked in from outside. \"Uncle, I have returned.\"","The newcomer was Diting.","Seeing the items on Liudao's desk, he raised his eyebrows slightly. \"You are making new medicine again.\"","Speaking of \"medicine,\" Diting's expression gradually grew heavy. \"Uncle, I heard that the Marquis of Wu'an has been arresting people lately. His men are active everywhere in Yanzhou, Qingzhou, and the Northern Territories, and they have captured quite a few of our key members. It is truly strange. How did the Marquis of Wu'an learn the locations of our strongholds?\"","Recently, things had been very turbulent within the cult.","The impact from the Northern factions was especially massive. The North dispatched troops to arrest people, charging straight at the strongholds and catching them accurately every single time, almost as if they knew in advance!","\"We have a spy,\" Liudao said with a mild expression.","Diting froze, his face changing drastically. \"A spy? What spy could know our stationed points in such detail?\"","\"Back then, the Marquis of Wu'an followed Mingdeng to Xia Valley.\" Liudao only said this one sentence.","Diting subconsciously replied, \"Uncle, you suspect Mingdeng? Impossible! He came to the Green Lotus Cult at the age of ten. Over the years, he has gone through thick and thin for us. He had never come into contact with the Marquis of Wu'an before. How could he betray us just because of one small act of mercy from the other party? Not to mention, Mingdeng has been taking the divine medicine all these years. If he leaves us, where would he get the medicine?\"","Liudao pointed at an unopened letter on the desk with a small wooden spoon. \"I did not assign any mission to Mingdeng. This is a letter that White Elephant just delivered. You may open it yourself.\"","Hearing this, Diting reached out to take the letter and quickly broke the wax seal. He read it rapidly.","The more he read, the more bizarre his expression became.","At that time, Mingdeng had told him that he received a newly assigned mission from above and had another place to go, so he would not travel with them.","He had not thought much of it then, only assuming that his uncle had given Mingdeng another task. He never expected that this was not the case.","Now White Elephant said he was unaware, and everyone in the cult who could command Mingdeng stated that they had never issued any orders. Could it really be...","\"Why is this? He has stayed in the cult for nine years. How could he switch sides just because of a few words from the Marquis of Wu'an? Did the Marquis of Wu'an feed Mingdeng some kind of bewitching potion?\" Diting was greatly puzzled.","Liudao set down the wooden spoon and fiddled with the prayer beads on his wrist. \"I also thought about it for a long time, and then I remembered something. A while ago, the North issued a missing person notice to merchants all over the world, looking for a nine-year-old boy.\"","This matter had been reported previously.","However, for such a trivial matter of finding someone, especially a child with the surname Qin, Liudao, like many others at the time, assumed that the Marquis of Wu'an was searching for a lost child of the Qin clan.","He had only glanced over it casually back then and handed it over to his subordinates to keep an eye out.","It was only recently, due to Mingdeng's betrayal, that he focused much of his attention on the North and ordered his men to compile all major and minor events in the North over the past year.","Thus, that missing person notice was presented to his desk once again.","\"The North was previously looking for a boy named Qin Yanzhou. Qin Yanzhou, that was Mingdeng's original name,\" Liudao said, fingering his prayer beads.","Diting's pupils suddenly contracted. \"Are... are you sure?\"","Liudao did not speak, but turned his head to look out the window.","Today the weather was clear and bright, the sky as blue as crystal, and a gentle breeze blew by, presenting a peaceful scene.","Liudao's thoughts slowly drifted back to nine years ago.","Nine years ago, a great famine ravaged the various provinces like a plague. He was taking Diting and White Elephant from Yangzhou back to Yanzhou. While passing through Yangzhou, he saw a child who had escaped.","Yes, escaped. Behind him, a skinny, skeletal man was chasing him.","The child held a small knife in his hand, and there was blood on the blade. The man behind him ran with a limp, most likely injured by the boy.","The man roared ferociously, saying that once he caught him, he would chop him into eight pieces, peel off his skin, and hack his bones into sections to make soup.","An ordinary, yet not so ordinary scene.","He did not act immediately at the time, only watching as the skinny man caught up and tackled the child to the ground. The two engaged in a life-and-death struggle on the dirt. He saw an astonishing ruthlessness burst forth from the filthy child's eyes as he narrowly kept hold of the knife and plunged it into the skinny man's chest.","At that moment, he knew this child was a good prospect. He picked the child up, brought him into their group, and took him back to the cult.","At first, the child was like a mute and did not speak. When asked where he came from, where his ancestral home was, or who was in his family, he answered nothing.","Later, after a few months, the little mute finally opened his mouth, only stating that his name was Qin Yanzhou.","Everyone in the cult had a codename. He personally gave the child the name Mingdeng, making him abandon his past.","However, he never expected that after nine years, this abandoned past would eventually turn into an invisible rope, pulling the once wandering child back.","\"Uncle...\" Diting was uncharacteristically dumbfounded. \"Mingdeng is actually the son of the Marquis of Wu'an?!\"","He was surnamed Qin, and the missing person notice came from the North. If he was not the son of the Marquis of Wu'an, how could he switch sides after meeting the other party just once?","\"No, that's not right.\" Diting suddenly shook his head as if struck by lightning. \"Uncle, he might not necessarily be the son of the Marquis of Wu'an.\"","Liudao frowned. \"Why do you say that?\"","Diting said solemnly, \"I spent some time with Madam Dai. When I first met her, I vaguely felt she was somewhat familiar, but I could not pinpoint where that feeling came from. But now, with hindsight, I realize it came from Mingdeng! Mingdeng's eyes and brows look exactly like hers.\"","Liudao was stunned. \"Madam Dai?\"","Diting continued, \"Uncle, the salt stones and the dragon-bone waterwheel came from the hands of Madam Dai. Looking back, the North's missing person notice was issued precisely from Ying Commandery. The two events happened almost simultaneously. I guess Madam Dai very likely made a deal with the Marquis of Wu'an. It's just...\"","Speaking towards the end, Diting clearly hesitated. \"Why were they looking for a nine-year-old child? According to logical deduction, she should know that Mingdeng is already nineteen years old.\"","\"We cannot rule out that it is a smokescreen,\" Liudao stopped fiddling with his prayer beads. \"No matter what, Mingdeng having a connection with Madam Dai is a good thing for us.\"","Bairi City, the Qin Residence.","Dai Li left Ding Lianxi's courtyard with her son, her heart heavy. Illness should be treated early. If Ding Lianxi had no solution, they could only return to Yuyang.","\"Mother, I don't feel unwell right now,\" Qin Yanzhou followed closely by his mother's side.","Dai Li's worry did not diminish. \"You might not feel unwell now, but it is hard to say for the future. I will go find Qin Shaozong and talk to him about returning to Yuyang.\"","\"Mother, I heard that Governor Nangong has arrived. The Marquis of Wu'an is probably still receiving guests at this moment,\" Qin Yanzhou said.","Dai Li paused her steps. \"Is that so? Then let's go eat first.\"","...","After the meal.","Dai Li checked the sky. The rainy summer had passed, and the chilly autumn was settling in.","The closer it got to winter, the shorter the days and the longer the nights became. When they were having dinner, the sky had still been covered with brilliant sunset hues, but by the time they finished eating, the sky had mostly darkened.","\"I'm going to the main hall for a bit,\" Dai Li couldn't sit still.","However, just as Dai Li reached the entrance of the courtyard, a tall figure happened to turn into the entrance at that exact moment, and the two bumped right into each other.","Qin Shaozong reached out and pulled her into his embrace. \"Madam is so hasty, where are you rushing off to?\"","Seeing that the person she wanted to find had delivered himself to her door, Dai Li was naturally happy and stated matter-of-factly, \"To find you.\"","Qin Shaozong paused in surprise, a deep smile spreading in his eyes. \"You came looking for me? Could it be, my dear wife, that you are...\"","He turned the woman in his arms around and guided her inside. Just as he was about to lean in close and whisper something completely shameless to her, he looked up, only to see an expressionless young man standing right there in the courtyard.","Qin Shaozong: \"...\""]},{"number":93,"title":"Chapter 93","paragraphs":["Qin Shaozong paused slightly, but the hand around Dai Li's waist did not loosen. He simply swallowed the words that had reached his throat and changed to another sentence, \"Has Madam eaten?\"","\"I've eaten.\"","Dai Li got straight to the point. \"This afternoon, Zhou Zhou and I went to see Mr. Ding for a consultation. Mr. Ding said he couldn't figure it out and suggested Zhou Zhou go find his grandfather. Qin Changgeng, I want to take our son to Yuyang Commandery first.\"","She did not ask him when he would return, but directly stated that she wanted to go ahead first.","Qin Shaozong replied, \"In a few days, I will return to Yuyang together with Madam.\"","Dai Li frowned anxiously. Her son said the affliction would act up every ten days, and she did not want to wait a moment longer. \"How many days is a few days? How about this, we split up. Zhou Zhou and I will go first, and you can return after you finish your business.\"","After she finished speaking, Dai Li belatedly realized that her son had followed her out of the room. She suddenly felt the large hand on her waist become exceptionally hot.","She quietly tried to push his hand away, but failed. That dark hand was like cast iron, firmly clamped on her waist.","Qin Yanzhou looked away. \"Mother, I'm going back to my room first. Good night.\"","\"...Good night, Zhou Zhou,\" Dai Li said, feeling very awkward.","Qin Yanzhou turned and went into his own room. Only after he entered the room did Qin Shaozong take Dai Li back to their room.","There were no lamps lit in the room; only a few fading embers of the dusk lingered by the window.","Qin Shaozong turned around, trapping her between himself and the door. He lowered his head and kissed the small red mole on Dai Li's forehead. \"Wait two more days. In two days, Madam will depart with me to return to Yuyang.\"","He had just been drinking in the main hall, and now his breath was full of the smell of alcohol as he spoke. Dai Li wrinkled her nose and turned her head away. \"Two days is a bit long.\"","Qin Shaozong could never stand her showing distaste for him. He immediately pinched her chin with two fingers and turned her back. \"It's not long. When the time comes, Madam and I will travel day and night, with the infantry following behind. We can make up for the time.\"","Dai Li still frowned. \"I still want to...\"","The rest of her words were swallowed by him before she could finish.","The taste of alcohol exploded in her mouth, surging fiercely like a tsunami. Dai Li's pupils trembled slightly. The other party came menacingly, as if he hadn't eaten enough at the banquet, and was now opening his appetite to gorge himself.","The soft red was hooked, and the greedy tiger found the hidden delicacy, smacking his lips loudly as he ate, as if to extract all the flavor from the very marrow.","Unlike any partner Dai Li had ever dated before, Qin Shaozong would not close his eyes at times like this.","He always looked at her without blinking. Not only did his arms have to encircle her, but his gaze also locked onto her tightly, guarding his meat like a tiger or wolf, allowing no one else to snatch it, nor allowing her to be distracted.","The room was unlit, and the man's light brown eyes were pitch black at this moment, like a bottomless dark pool.","Even though she hadn't been drinking, Dai Li was forcefully intoxicated by his aura. By the time she came to her senses, she was already on the bed, her outer garment lying not far away by the edge of the bed.","Click.","The soft clinking of beads was exceptionally clear in the night.","Dai Li only felt a cold sensation on her wrist, as if something was wrapped around it. She raised her hand. The surrounding light was not very bright, and she could only faintly see a touch of unusually vibrant blue-green.","\"What is this?\" Dai Li moved her wrist.","Qin Shaozong mumbled with soft flesh in his mouth, \"Nangong came to the manor to dine. After taking a bite of the meat stir-fried in the iron wok, he was greatly amazed and couldn't stop thinking about it, attempting to ask for the recipe. I told him this was Madam's masterpiece, and if he wanted to know, he should bring some treasures for you to look over. Upon hearing this, that fellow couldn't wait a single moment and had people return to his manor, directly bringing over several large chests of jewelry. Madam, take a look, do they catch your eye?\"","Dai Li turned her hand.","The object was not heavy, seemingly some kind of beaded bracelet.","After saying that, Qin Shaozong snorted lightly, showing a bit of disdain. \"There are not many treasures in Qingzhou and Yanzhou. Wait until Madam returns to Yuyang with me, I will let Madam see other treasures. For now, we'll just make do with these.\"","Though his mouth spoke of disdaining the other's gifts, his movements did not stop. He produced a long necklace from who knows where and continued to drape it over Dai Li.","The lack of oxygen in her brain, coupled with the intoxicating smell of alcohol, made Dai Li's thoughts two beats slower than usual. She didn't even resist when he lifted her hands and waist.","It took a good while for Dai Li to realize that she had become a Christmas tree.","The cold bead chain slipped through her open undergarment, feeling icy and smooth. Dai Li reached out and touched it. She couldn't see, but the texture was nice. Considering this man picked it out from several chests of jewelry, it was likely no ordinary item.","It was true that she liked collecting jewelry, but who wants to wear a body full of accessories in bed!","\"No, these will poke me if I roll over.\" Dai Li tried to take them off.","Qin Shaozong grabbed her wrist, stopping Dai Li's movements. \"Just look at them first, take them off after you're done looking. Back in Nanyang County, what did Madam promise me?\"","As if reminding her not to forget, his other hand patted her perky and plump side.","Dai Li was speechless.","She had discovered that this man had some particular quirks in bed.","He was suddenly in high spirits, acting on a whim, wholly focused on dressing Dai Li up.","Not only on her neck and hands, but Qin Shaozong also took two gold bracelets and slipped them on her, pulling a necklace down to use as a waist chain. He also hung thin gold chains in other places.","After roughly finishing the decorations, Qin Shaozong stood up, scooped Dai Li up with one arm, letting her sit on his left arm, and carried her off the bed just like that.","Her feet couldn't touch the ground at all, she couldn't get down, and she had nothing to lean back on. Afraid of falling, Dai Li had to hook one arm around his neck.","Qin Shaozong carried her around the room, picked up two items, and then went to the vanity mirror.","\"Madam, light the lamp.\"","Something was stuffed into Dai Li's hand. She felt it out to be a piece of flint and a small iron block.","In this era, let alone lighters, even the initial version of lighters, fire sticks, hadn't appeared yet.","When people wanted to start a fire, they generally used the method of obtaining fire with golden flint and stone flint. The former utilized sunlight, while the latter used flint, a type of phosphorus-containing siliceous stone, striking it against iron tools to manually create fire.","There was a soft chair in front of the vanity mirror. Qin Shaozong sat down, and then let Dai Li sit on his lap.","A lamp stand stood quietly in front of them. Dai Li held the things in her hand. She had never used this contraption before, and combined with her lack of enthusiasm, her attempts to strike a fire were sporadic. It took a long while before she managed two clicks.","Qin Shaozong patted her. \"Don't dawdle. The sooner you finish looking, the sooner we go back to rest.\"","Speaking of this, Dai Li found her motivation. She tilted her head slightly, dodging the heated kisses on her earlobe. \"Give it a rest for a moment.\"","\"You do your thing, I'll do mine, we won't interfere with each other,\" Qin Shaozong said, taking that round, snow-white earlobe into his mouth.","Dai Li shuddered, and then felt a rough sensation slither under the hem of her clothes like a snake. It measured inch by inch, growing upwards like a vine, and then turned into spreading fallen leaves to support her.","Focusing her attention, Dai Li struck the stone two more times, finally seeing sparks fly out.","But having motivation is one thing, whether she can use it is another. Not knowing if her method was wrong, Dai Li struck it a few times, but not a single imperceptible spark landed on the wick.","\"Qin Changgeng, did you give me a fake flint?\" Dai Li let go and quit.","\"Nonsense, let me teach you, Madam.\" Qin Shaozong withdrew his hand from her clothes, instead wrapping her two hands separately, teaching her hand in hand how to use the flint.","\"Click,\" the force was much greater than Dai Li's previous strikes. With just that one strike, the wick was lit.","\"See, it's done. What's so hard about it?\" Qin Shaozong smiled.","Dai Li pursed her lips in dissatisfaction, thinking to herself that a fire stick was still easier to use, only needing a blow to work.","Thinking of the fire stick, her thoughts couldn't help but drift further away. It was now autumn, and the weather was getting colder day by day.","Yuyang Commandery was in the north, where winters were even colder. Using a flint to start a fire would definitely hurt her fingers, and it would be inconvenient for eating hotpot or roasting meat. It would be better to make a batch of fire sticks. Then she, Zhou Zhou, Nianxia, and Bipo could sit around the stove and eat hotpot.","The hotpot was already floating in front of her eyes when a sudden chill on her chest pulled Dai Li back to reality.","Her bodice was loose, and after the long amber necklace wrapped twice around her neck, the largest rabbit-shaped amber in the middle was hidden in the high snow-white.","The bean lamp flickered, and the bronze mirror in front reflected a bright light, with gold and silver intertwining to outline a luxurious and elegant beauty.","The knot of the bodice was close at hand. Qin Shaozong leaned closer, biting the knot with his sharp canine teeth, and then tilted his head to the side.","The smooth silk slipped down.","Under the bean lamp and in the bronze mirror, other more vivid and bright colors were added to the snow-white scroll. Dai Li raised her hand to pick up the fallen bodice, her fingertips barely touching the apricot-colored undergarment, when suddenly she was lifted up by him.","Originally sitting sideways, she was now sitting straight, facing the bronze mirror and leaning against his back.","As she slowly sat down, Dai Li's breathing slightly paused, her waist tense, completely unable to care about picking up the fallen bodice.","Qin Shaozong's breathing sank heavily with her tightening, and he opportunely reached out to rub the small of her back.","The pool water was rippled by a not-so-gentle wind, pushing away layer by layer, revealing the murmuring flowing water.","The mirror reflected a beauty like a flower demon, with snow-white flower branches wrapped in gold and silver ribbons, jade, various agates, amber, and turquoise adorning the delicate branches everywhere.","\"Does Madam like it?\" He personally decorated it one by one, measuring it carefully again, unable to put it down.","\"Don't wear it here, Qin Shaozong, you pervert.\" Dai Li's face was flushed, and she was not honest in doing things. She raised her hand to take it off, but her wrist was caught by him again.","\"Earlier, Madam said this was a compliment. It seems you really like it,\" he laughed in a low voice.","Occasionally, strong winds and huge waves would crash over, causing the flower branches to tremble, and even the rabbit-shaped amber deep in the canyon was turned out.","\"These things from Qingzhou are still a bit inferior.\" After he had enough of his addiction, he took them off for her one by one, picking them up with his mouth, and then hugged her back to the bed to continue the second half.","Only a faint light remained in the lamp in front of the mirror box, looking as if it would go out in the next breath. The dim light fell on the bodice left behind by its owner.","The warm-colored undergarment glowing with a faint light lay quietly on the soft chair. The bodice was a bit wrinkled, but it was not difficult to see the beautiful peony embroidered in the middle.","And in the center of the peony's heart, a different dark color bloomed, as if accidentally wet by a water stain.","The candlelight suddenly went out, but the movement in the room had not yet stopped.","*","Qin Shaozong said they would wait two more days before setting off back to Yuyang, and he meant two days.","Two days later, he left Kuang Ye in Bairi City to wrap things up, and amid Nangong Xiong's cursing, he led a group of people and Dai Li to set off first.","Bairi City was in Yanzhou, and Yuyang was in Youzhou. To go from Yanzhou to Youzhou, they had to cross Jizhou, which covered a considerable area.","Jizhou had already been swallowed by Qin Shaozong in his early years, and now passing through this area was like returning to his own home, with unimpeded progress all the way.","Normally, Qin Shaozong would stay in various commanderies of Jizhou for a few more days to check on the work of each commandery in the state, but now it was purely rushing.","They marched almost entirely during the day, and at night, if they encountered a commandery or county, they would settle down in the city; if not, they would continue their journey.","On the way back, a not-so-small incident occurred.","The matter began when they came to a place called Dahong County. Dahong County was not large, and there were only a few inns in the county, which could be counted on one hand.","Qin Shaozong went directly to the most expensive one, waved his hand, and booked the entire inn.","After having dinner downstairs, Dai Li went upstairs to rest. On the way back to Yuyang Commandery, she slept in the same room with Qin Shaozong. When she came up, Qin Shaozong was still downstairs.","Nianxia and Bipo stayed in the next room. After Dai Li washed up, there was no place where they needed to serve, so she let them go back to their room to rest.","Although there were fewer mosquitoes and insects in autumn than in summer, in the current weather, which was not as hot and stuffy as summer, Dai Li still smoothly put down the plain curtain.","As a result, as soon as the plain curtain hanging on the wooden hook dispersed, a piece of silk cloth gracefully fell down.","It was a very plain-colored silk cloth, looking very clean, so clean that no one would feel that picking it up would dirty their hands.","Dai Li bent down to pick it up, and when the distance narrowed, she found that there were words on this silk cloth.","It read: The medicine of Yanzhou can only be cured by me.","Dai Li's pupils suddenly shrank. At that moment, her heart seemed to be caught off guard by a hidden poisonous snake, and the seemingly corrosive venom stung her heart.","She stood there in a daze, staring closely at the silk cloth.","Where did the silk cloth come from, and how could it be placed in her room so coincidentally?","Yes, the believers of the Green Lotus Sect were spread across all states, and it was not surprising that they had people in the commanderies and counties of Jizhou. There were people from the Green Lotus Sect in this inn, and they accurately calculated the room she would stay in.","No, those were not the main points.","The main point was, could the poison on Zhou Zhou really only be cured by the Green Lotus Sect?","Dai Li only felt a rolling pin stirring vigorously in her brain, shaking her eardrums and making her dizzy. Unable to stand, her legs gave way and she fell to the ground.","Qin Shaozong ended his conversation with Mo Yanyun within a quarter of an hour after Dai Li went upstairs. \"It's getting late, let's go back to our rooms and rest.\"","He turned and went upstairs, walking all the way to the best room in the inn, pushing the door open and entering.","The door wasn't locked, and the light wasn't out.","The room was divided into an inner and an outer room. Qin Shaozong had just called out to his wife when he turned his head and saw Dai Li sitting on the floor beside the bed in the inner room.","The man's gaze sharpened, and he stepped forward in three strides, scooping her up. \"Why are you sitting on the floor? Did you hurt your foot again?\"","\"No, no...\" Dai Li was like waking up from a nightmare, clutching the silk cloth tightly, so hard that her knuckles turned white.","Qin Shaozong instantly noticed the thing in her hand. He wrapped Dai Li's cold hand in his palm, and then skillfully took the plain-colored silk cloth.","The eight characters on the cloth were written in cinnabar, bright and eye-catching. This color would normally be festive, but at this moment, it carried an ominous sign.","A chilling ruthlessness flashed through his brown eyes. The man clenched his large hand, instantly crushing the silk cloth into a ball. \"Although these scare tactics are clumsy, they are highly effective. My lady, do not fall for their treacherous scheme. In four days, we will arrive in Yuyang. When the time comes, I will accompany you to pay a visit to the Ding family.\""]},{"number":94,"title":"Chapter 94","paragraphs":["The night was already very deep, and Dai Li lay on the couch, completely sleepless.","As soon as she closed her eyes, she saw those eight glaringly red characters; if she thought about them too long, the edges of the writing seemed to drip blood.","Unable to sleep, Dai Li wanted to change places, but she was held tight by the long arm wrapped around her waist.","Every time she shared a bed with Qin Shaozong, he liked to hold her before falling asleep. Previously, Dai Li had good sleep quality, and after struggling a few times without success, she would slowly fall asleep.","But today she couldn't sleep and felt annoyed. Now, being blocked even when trying to turn over, that fire mixed with irritation sizzled upwards.","Dai Li attempted to push away the hand on her waist. First push, it didn't budge; second push with more force, still didn't budge. She then knew that Qin Shaozong wasn't asleep either.","\"So restless, Madam has been tossing and turning on the couch all night,\" he spoke.","Dai Li remained silent.","Qin Shaozong continued, \"That piece of silk only had eight characters and no other information. Madam, just wait, they will contact you again.\"","After obtaining the silk, Qin Shaozong didn't send anyone to investigate who left it.","Because it was meaningless.","The Green Lotus Sect had too many followers; the commoners at the bottom were ignorant and uncultivated, as easy to manipulate as puppets.","Even if they caught someone, so what? The clues going further up would definitely break. Besides, this was Ji Province, and they were currently rushing back to Yuyang at full speed. They couldn't stay in Ji Province for a long time just to investigate an upstream source that they likely wouldn't find.","Dai Li opened her eyes, \"They know Zhou Zhou and I are mother and son.\"","Back when the North made a big show of looking for people, blowing notices to various provinces like a gale, the Green Lotus Sect likely connected the missing person notices with the dragon bone waterwheel, or even the suddenly appearing refined salt.","After multiple lines overlapped, they locked onto her.","Zhou Zhou was picked up by the Green Lotus Sect; it couldn't be ruled out that he had told them his name at the very beginning.","\"That sect leader probably wants to use the antidote to the rare poison as a threat to make Madam submit to him and work for him. Over in Yuyang, I previously sent people back to protect Ding Lianxi's family. But those aren't important; what is Madam thinking now?\" His voice was calm, with no discernible emotion.","Dai Li naturally knew the Green Lotus Sect's intentions as well. As for what she thought...","Her mind was a mess.","On one hand, she clearly knew that whoever could send her son to a treacherous place like the Fan Residence was definitely not a good person. Maybe Zhou Zhou had also been bullied when he was in the Green Lotus Sect before.","But on the other hand, if the antidote was only within the Green Lotus Sect, she had no choice. She absolutely could not watch her son die from poison.","\"Let's wait until we return to Yuyang and see,\" Dai Li avoided the topic.","To this, Qin Shaozong didn't press for details, but just scooped the woman who wanted to move to the other side to sleep back to him, stroking her back. \"The North is vast, with many medicinal herbs, and countless merchants traveling north and south. Old Mr. Ding also spent several years in places like Jiao Province in his early years; his experience and medical skills are far beyond ordinary physicians. There will always be a way to solve it.\"","After a long time, Dai Li finally said, \"I hope so.\"","Closing her eyes again for a moment, Dai Li opened them once more. \"Qin Changgeng, when we return to Yuyang Commandery, I won't live in your Marquis Residence. Zhou Zhou and I will live outside.\"","With things on her mind, a hint of fire inevitably spilled into her tone.","Qin Shaozong heard it. He was silent for a long time, ultimately not grabbing her fox tail to take her back at this moment. \"Okay.\"","With things weighing on her mind, Dai Li didn't sleep well the whole night. The next day, she lacked energy and basically spent the daytime catching up on sleep in the carriage.","For four consecutive days, their travel speed increased a bit.","Later, passing through other commanderies and counties, Qin Shaozong didn't deliberately avoid the well-conditioned relay stations in the commanderies and counties because of the silk.","They stayed however they should stay.","Later, they indeed received other notes, uniformly using plain white silk as the base, written on with cinnabar.","[The Marquis of Wu'an is not your best choice.]","[Our sect's doors are always open for you.]","There was not a single specific piece of information; they were all just stoking the fire. Seeing them made Qin Shaozong furious, and finally, unable to hold back, he left three Xuanxiao Cavalrymen behind to deal with the underlings.","After a long trek, this procession that set out from Bairi City finally arrived at Yuyang when the sun was high in the sky.","As the core of You Province, Yuyang's city gates were naturally built to be more majestic than other commanderies and counties.","The quaint city bricks were neatly stacked, presenting a vicissitude and magnificence baptized by time under the sunlight. It was like a silent guardian, looking down upon this small piece of heaven and earth, quietly watching merchant caravans come and go, and cavalry enter and exit.","It was now noon, and the pedestrians and caravans entering and exiting the city were especially numerous.","The sound of horse hooves came, and many people turned their heads at the sound. What entered their sight was a cavalry unit clad in black armor.","Sunlight fell on the black armor, reflecting a blade-like sharpness. The horses they rode were all exceptionally sturdy; one could tell at a glance that aside from being of excellent breed, they were fed top-quality fodder.","\"Is this... the Marquis has returned?!\"","\"Hey! It's definitely the Marquis. I recognize his big red horse mount. It's just, why don't I see his figure? Could he be in the carriage?\"","\"I heard he previously led troops to crusade against the salt smugglers, and later was invited to the South. Now returning not on horseback but in a carriage, could he have been injured in the South?\"","\"It's not impossible. Swords flash and shadows of blades fall on the battlefield; who knows where one might get hurt. Otherwise, when fighting the Northern Kingdom previously, the Third Young Master wouldn't have been severely injured.\"","\"It hasn't been peaceful in the commandery lately. That captured Chief Commandant of the Wei family escaped from prison, saying something about the Cai family using private torture on him. The latter denied it and flew into a rage, bringing people to catch him back.\"","\"Tsk tsk, not to mention the fighting here, the Wei family over there is saying a certain Cai family son neglected his duties. They are determined to go against them. It's really causing a huge uproar in the city. With the Marquis returning to Yuyang to recuperate this time, I fear his ears won't get a moment of peace.\"","\"Indeed. It's a pity I have to travel far, otherwise I would definitely watch the rest of this good show.\"","...","Other merchant caravans entering and exiting the city had to be inspected, but when it came to the Xuanxiao Cavalry, the city guards recognized a few platoon leaders and let them pass directly.","Sitting in the carriage, Dai Li listened to the town's clamor, and her heart gradually settled down.","They had finally arrived in Yuyang.","Dai Li lifted the curtain to check the sky, turned her head and said to Qin Shaozong,","\"It's noon now. Qin Changgeng, can you send someone to the Ding family to give a heads up first, and we'll formally go over around early afternoon.\"","Let alone in ancient times with heavy rules, even in modern times visiting friends, one should inform the other party in advance. Dropping in suddenly is very presumptuous in any era.","Qin Shaozong: \"Yesterday Hu Bao arrived in Yuyang ahead of time to arrange everything. After returning to the residence for lunch, I will go to the Ding family with Madam.\"","Dai Li nodded.","This highly anticipated procession did not return to the Marquis Residence, but came to another mansion. Entering from the main gate, the carriage drove all the way to the main courtyard before stopping.","Dai Li got out of the carriage. Just as she looked up, she was startled by a row of young women dressed as maids standing not far away. She paused slightly, turning her head to look at the man beside her. \"Don't tell me these young women are all going to stay in the courtyard.\"","Qin Shaozong corrected her, \"They are staying in the residence, but not entering the main courtyard. Aside from the main courtyard, other places in the residence also need hands. Madam, just see if they are pleasing to the eye; if not, we can change for another batch.\"","Seeing Daili hesitate, he added in a low voice, \"They have all been thoroughly checked. Neither they nor their families follow any religion.\"","Daili looked at the maidservants standing a few steps away.","There were ten in total.","They wore uniform attire, neat and clean. Some were younger, around sixteen or seventeen, while others were older, perhaps in their forties.","Everyone was extremely nervous, afraid of being singled out as unsuitable.","\"Let them stay for now, we'll see how it goes,\" Daili said. She recalled the long carriage ride into the estate just now; the residence had to be quite expansive.","The maidservants' faces immediately lit up, and they expressed their endless gratitude.","Wealthy households offered great benefits; even the scraps that slipped through their fingers were enough to feed them for a long time. Not to mention that the master of this estate was the Marquis of Wu'an, the renowned God of War guarding the northern borders, the uncrowned king of Yuyang and the entire North.","Qin Shaozong said, \"Let's eat first.\"","...","In another courtyard.","Feng Feng watched Mo Yanyun sit down, stand up, and pace endlessly around the room, muttering something under his breath.","\"Lao Mo, what's wrong with you? Why are you acting like you've got bugs biting you ever since we entered the estate?\" Feng Feng asked.","His voice was not quiet, but Mo Yanyun didn't hear him at all, still immersed in his own world.","Feng Feng called out \"Lao Mo\" again, but the latter still didn't react, continuing to pace back and forth.","Seeing this, Feng Feng quietly walked over to listen.","\"I'm doomed, I'm doomed. Madam Daili actually did it... I'm doomed. This stupid mouth of mine, never knowing when to shut up. Why did I have to spout such nonsense?\"","Feng Feng raised an eyebrow. \"Lao Mo, what are you muttering about all by yourself? What's doomed?\"","Mo Yanyun jumped in fright. If he had a furry tail, it would definitely be standing straight up right now, bristling all over.","Having worked together for so many years, how could Feng Feng not tell that something was wrong? He immediately threw an arm around Mo Yanyun's shoulders like a good buddy. \"Lao Mo, did you do something you shouldn't have?\"","It would have been better if he hadn't brought it up. Now that he did, Mo Yanyun suddenly felt the blade hanging over his head sway, the rope holding it creaking under the strain.","\"N-no, what could I possibly have done?\" Mo Yanyun looked away.","Feng Feng laughed at him. \"Still denying it? You're even stuttering. Don't say I didn't warn you as a brother. The Marquis is incredibly sharp; how could he not see that something is off about you? Tell me, what kind of trouble did you stir up this time?\"","Mo Yanyun shook his head vigorously.","Feng Feng clicked his tongue. \"Why don't you trust me? Think about all the times I've given you ideas in the past. Ask yourself, didn't they all work out perfectly?\"","Mo Yanyun hesitated.","Feng Feng had the worst background among them, but out of all the garrison commanders, no one had a sharper mind. He was full of clever ideas and often helped them solve their problems.","In the past, whenever Mo Yanyun encountered a difficult problem, he liked to discuss it with Feng Feng, and the results were always excellent.","\"What are you so worried about?\" Seeing that he still wouldn't speak, Feng Feng grew even more curious. Changing his tactic, he decided to play hard to get. \"Fine, if you don't trust me, you don't have to tell me. Just make sure you keep your wits about you when you're around the Marquis later. Stay on high alert and don't let him notice anything. It's rare for us to return to Yuyang, so I need to go home and see my wife and little daughter. My baby girl can walk now, I wonder if she still remembers me.\"","Seeing him about to leave, Mo Yanyun, who had been hesitating, immediately pulled him back. \"I didn't say I wouldn't tell you. What's the rush?\"","Feng Feng smiled but said nothing.","Mo Yanyun gritted his teeth. \"This is no ordinary matter. I'll tell you, but you must not tell anyone else.\"","Feng Feng agreed immediately.","Mo Yanyun coughed lightly. \"Come closer.\"","\"So secretive.\" Feng Feng leaned in anyway.","Mo Yanyun whispered in his ear.","Feng Feng's expression shifted rapidly—from bizarre to shocked, to terrified, to impressed... A series of emotions flashed across his face.","Feng Feng swiftly shoved Mo Yanyun away and walked out the door without looking back. \"Lao Mo, I didn't hear anything just now, and you didn't say a word to me today. I'm going home to see my daughter. See you around.\"","Mo Yanyun was dumbfounded. By the time he recovered and tried to call out, Feng Feng had already vanished without a trace.","\"Feng Feng, you bastard!!\" Mo Yanyun cursed loudly.","Just as he finished cursing, Bai Jianping walked in. \"I heard you yelling from far away. Lao Mo, what are you cursing about?\"","Mo Yanyun huffed angrily, \"That guy Feng Feng said he'd help me solve a problem, but the moment I finished telling him, he ran off.\"","Bai Jianping's interest was piqued immediately. \"There's a problem he can't solve? Quick, tell me. I can definitely solve it.\"","He and Feng Feng had been secretly competing for a long time, and he always felt that he was a bit smarter than Feng Feng.","Mo Yanyun was half-skeptical. \"Come closer.\"","Bai Jianping leaned in without hesitation.","Mo Yanyun whispered.","Bai Jianping's eyes widened in sheer shock. He too bolted for the door without looking back, acting exactly as if a dog were chasing him out of the room. \"Lao Mo, I just remembered I haven't fed my dog. I'm going back to feed the dog. I didn't hear a word you just said.\"","With that, without waiting for a reply, Bai Jianping took off running.","Mo Yanyun stood frozen.","Not long after he ran out, Qiao Wangfei came in. Qiao Wangfei asked in confusion, \"Lao Mo, what did you do to Old Bai?\"","\"I ran into some trouble. That guy clearly said he would help me solve it, but he ran away as soon as he heard it. It's truly infuriating.\"","\"What is it? Tell me, I'll help you.\"","...","The main courtyard.","Perhaps due to special instructions, there was actually a small round table in the main courtyard, and they gathered around it for lunch.","Lunch consisted of stir-fried pork, steamed egg custard, and fish soup. It couldn't be called a lavish feast; they were just everyday home-cooked dishes.","The fish was first pan-fried in an iron wok, then stewed in an earthen clay pot with tofu. The resulting fish soup was a milky white. Finally, it was sprinkled with chopped green onions. The tender green paired with the milky white made it incredibly delicious.","Even though Daili was preoccupied with visiting the Ding family that afternoon, she surprisingly drank an extra bowl of soup and ate nearly half the fish from the stew.","Seeing that her appetite was much better than yesterday, Qin Shaozong simply instructed Nianxia to make the fish soup again tonight. He looked at Daili, \"Madam actually reminds me of some old matters.\"","\"Hmm?\" Daili hummed through her nose.","Qin Shaozong glanced at her completely empty soup bowl and smiled. \"In my early years, I once traveled to the south. When they eat, they love having soup. A meal is incomplete without it, exactly like you, Madam.\"","Daili couldn't refute this. She really did love drinking soup, and Zhou Zhou liked it too. Even her former colleagues would stew soup at home whenever they had the time. However, there were other reasons as well. \"It's probably due to the climate differences. The south is hot and humid, so people sweat easily. Drinking soup helps replenish hydration.\"","After saying this, Daili realized something. \"Did you think I was lying to you when I said my homeland was in Qiantang?\"","\"Not at all. Madam's daily habits and accent cannot be faked.\" Seeing that there was about one bowl of soup left in the pot, Qin Shaozong casually ladled it out for her. \"Finish the fish soup. Once you're done, we'll head out to the Ding family.\"","During the past few days of travel, she had been eating like a bird every day, and had lost some weight compared to when they were in White Sun City.","Daili had originally wanted to give the soup to her son, but he had already ladled it into her bowl. Since she had already eaten from this bowl, she couldn't give it to anyone else.","After a pause, Daili eventually picked up the bowl and drank it slowly.","Once Dai Li finished her drink, the group was just about to head out when Hu Bao rushed over to report.","\"My Lord, Wei Congmu, the Chief Administrator of the Commandery, is outside requesting an audience.\"","Qin Shaozong stopped in his tracks."]},{"number":95,"title":"Chapter 95","paragraphs":["The Xuanxiao Cavalry's distinctiveness was too high, and the Red Flood Dragon was also running outside carelessly. As long as one paid attention, it wasn't hard to find out about Qin Shaozong's return to the city.","The people of the Wei Residence must have also heard the news.","Qin Shaozong said to Hu Bao, \"Tell Wei Congmu that I'm not free today.\"","He only said he wasn't free today, without even the polite \"come back another day.\"","Hu Bao was his personal guard. As soon as he heard it, he knew what his superior meant and immediately bowed to take the order to pass the message.","Dai Li knew nothing about the major families in Yuyang. Qin Yanzhou had heard of them. Hearing this, he turned his eyes to look at Qin Shaozong, but could only see the man's expressionless side face.","When they came back, Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou took two separate carriages. Dai Li and Qin Shaozong shared one, and Qin Yanzhou took one by himself.","Now when they go out, it's the same.","There was no intention of avoiding at all. The two carriages came out of the main gate one after another. When they came out, they happened to meet the carriage with the wooden sign of \"Wei\" hanging on it.","Hearing Hu Bao's message, Wei Congmu was extremely anxious. He tried to ask Hu Bao for a free time, but the latter kept his mouth shut and didn't reveal any information.","Fine, since this is the case, he will come back tomorrow. It's always a good thing that the Marquis of Wu'an returned to Yuyang. With him holding down the fort, a single word from him would definitely make the hateful Cai family not dare to cause trouble again.","It's a pity that Qi Nian hasn't been seen during this period of time, otherwise communicating with his nephew and having him mediate in the middle would get twice the result with half the effort.","As a result, Wei Congmu went out on foot and was about to go back to his residence, but suddenly heard a domestic servant remind him in a low voice that two carriages drove out of the residence.","Carriages?","Those who can ride in carriages are definitely not ordinary figures, let alone coming out of the main gate of the residence.","Could it be...","Wei Congmu quickly lifted the curtain and saw that it was actually Hu Bao driving the carriage, and his guess was instantly verified. He immediately straightened his clothes, got down from the carriage, blocked in front of Hu Bao's carriage, and bowed deeply to him.","Wei Congmu was the Chief Clerk of Yuyang Commandery, so when he opened his mouth, he said, \"This humble official congratulates the Lord on the triumphant return of his mighty army. The Lord wins every battle and captures every objective, always successful. I imagine the descent of the Martial Star to the mortal realm would also be of such a heroic posture. After this battle, the bandits large and small in the north are all terrified, scattering and fleeing, not daring to wreak havoc everywhere again. It is the fortune of the people of Ying Commandery to be protected by the Lord.\"","Although the person blocked the front of the carriage, what he said were words of congratulation, so it was not easy to directly drive him away.","Seeing the curtain move slightly, Wei Congmu quickly moved from the front to the side of the curtain. Sure enough, the next moment the curtain was lifted, revealing that face that showed more and more pressure as time flowed.","\"It's just a small matter, not worth mentioning,\" Qin Shaozong merely said.","Wei Congmu didn't expect the other party to only say this one sentence. By right, the Marquis of Wu'an already knew that he had previously visited the residence, and at this time, he should at least exchange a few pleasantries with him and ask him what he came for.","Seeing that the other party seemed to want to put down the curtain, Wei Congmu had no choice but to get straight to the point: \"I wonder when the Lord will be free. This humble official has some important matters and would like to ask for your guidance.\"","\"What matter?\" Qin Shaozong asked directly.","Wei Congmu's face twitched. There were people coming and going around, and maybe there were a dozen pairs of ears pricked up. How could that matter be said on the street?","Dai Li was still riding in the carriage provided by the magistrate of Nanyang County. There was only a single row of seats in the carriage, and she sat next to Qin Shaozong.","When he was talking to the person outside the carriage, Dai Li sat quietly. Her person was there, but her thoughts had been wandering for a while. She was thinking about the Green Lotus Sect and seeking medical treatment.","Until—","Qin Shaozong reached over and wrapped Dai Li's hand in his palm. In the cooling autumn, his hands were very warm, like a hot water bottle.","Dai Li returned to her senses for a moment, but she had gotten used to his occasional small movements these days, so she didn't react much.","Qin Shaozong pinched her fingertips.","Dai Li turned her head to look at him, but still didn't react much.","Qin Shaozong rubbed her palm with his rough thumb pad.","The woman's palm was delicate and soft. When that touch, like fine feathers and also like sandpaper, brushed past, Dai Li felt as if she had been touched by an invisible electric current. A tingling itch ran along her arm to her spine, and then up to her head.","As the back of her neck tightened slightly, she suddenly understood what Qin Shaozong meant.","This person wanted her to make a sound.","But Dai Li just didn't want to do what he wanted. If he didn't want to talk to that Wei family member, he could just tell the other party directly. Why use her as a shield?","She wouldn't do it.","Dai Li pulled her hand back, unwilling to let him hold it. Qin Shaozong didn't let go and continued to scratch her palm.","Even while she struggled, his strength was controlled very well. Dai Li always felt that there were fine feathers sweeping her palm, making that itch reach straight to her heart.","Dai Li was angry. How could this person be like this!","Immediately, she used her other hand to grab his fingers and pry them outwards, attempting to make that thick, tiger-paw-like large palm stretch out again.","Dai Li was fully concentrated and didn't notice that as she struggled more and more with him, she was no longer sitting with her back against the soft chair as before. She turned her body slightly and came out of the shielding area where Qin Shaozong used his body as a barrier.","Outside the carriage.","Wei Congmu had made up his mind to tactfully decline and leave this matter until tomorrow. As a result, when he looked up, he suddenly saw a piece of hibiscus-colored clothing.","It was a very gentle and graceful color, widely loved by young ladies. It could not be ruled out that some young gentlemen in the south who posed as lovers of culture also loved it very much. But in the rough north, almost no men would dress like this.","Before Wei Congmu could be surprised, the next moment, half of a lotus-like jade face poked out from behind the black robe.","Skin as white as snow, a little bright red mole between the eyebrows. The beautiful concubine lowered her eyes. Her eyelashes were thick and black, and the arc from the inner corner to the outer corner of the eye was extremely smooth and beautiful. When the curve reached the outer corner of the eye, it slightly tilted up, like a beautiful little feather fan.","As if noticing his gaze, she suddenly raised her eyes.","Those eyes were like a pool of clear water. When looking at him, they were cold and clear. It was clear that she didn't carry much emotion, but it made people feel distant, cold, and unapproachable, as if it were a graceful peony growing on a high platform, which could only be looked up to but not touched.","While Wei Congmu was stunned, that half of the jade face had disappeared.","Seeing Wei Congmu stunned, Qin Shaozong frowned, \"I'm not free today, and I have to go busy first. Please do as you please, Chief Clerk.\"","After saying that, the carriage curtain fell, blocking Wei Congmu's gaze. Hu Bao almost simultaneously raised his horsewhip and spurred the horse forward.","Wei Congmu stood blankly on the spot.","The Marquis of Wu'an shared a carriage with a young lady? And knowing that he came to visit and ask for an audience, and even after stating bluntly that he had important matters, he still left him behind and rode away with the young lady.","When did the Marquis of Wu'an become such a person who didn't know the severity of things? Who is that beautiful concubine? When did such a beauty exist in the north...","Perhaps there was a deviation from his past cognition, Wei Congmu felt inexplicably uneasy at this moment.","Inside the carriage.","Dai Li finally pried his hand open. After accidentally making eye contact with Wei Congmu just now, she knew that Qin Shaozong's certain goal might have finally been achieved.","Dai Li glanced at him sideways and said nothing.","Later when going to the Ding family, she still needed to use him, so it was not appropriate to argue with him at this time.","Dai Li didn't speak, but Qin Shaozong took the initiative to say, \"The one just now was the Chief Clerk of Yuyang, and also the eldest son of the middle generation of the Wei family. The Qin and Wei families used to be related by marriage. I married the legitimate daughter of the Wei family, but Lady Wei had a weak body and died of illness less than two years after giving birth to a son.\"","Dai Li was stunned.","This was her first time learning about Qin Shaozong's family background, and it was told to her by the man himself.","Qin Shaozong spoke of the past, \"When Lady Wei passed away from illness, the Qin family happened to be in a precarious situation and needed support from outsiders. At that time, the Qin family sought out Lady Wei, promising heavy profits in exchange for their help. The Wei family agreed, but worrying that they would drift apart from the Qin family in the future, they proposed marrying another daughter of the Wei family to me.\"","Daili's curiosity was piqued. \"Did you marry her?\"","Although she had only been interacting with Qin Shaozong for a little over half a year, she was absolutely certain that he was an extremely domineering man.","If you wanted this kind of person to bow his head and obediently follow orders, his rebellious nature would likely flare up, and he would deliberately go against you.","On the other hand, it was hard to say. After all, he was a son of the Qin family. With his current status, he would likely become the core focus of the Qin family's cultivation later on.","Enjoying the family's resources meant he also had to bear the corresponding responsibilities. Perhaps he would have agreed to the matter proposed by Lady Wei at that time.","Qin Shaozong sneered, \"At that time, there were no unmarried legitimate daughters of marriageable age in the Wei family's main branch, so they wanted to marry off a concubine-born daughter from the main branch to me.\"","Promising heavy profits was already enough compensation, and adding a marriage alliance... well, that would have been fine too. After all, marrying anyone was still a marriage, and it could just be considered as continuing the good relations between the two clans.","But the result was that they told him there were no legitimate daughters, only a concubine-born one.","It was simply going too far!","His older brother had already passed away by then, and as the second son, he had been promoted to heir. If he married a concubine-born daughter of Lady Wei, how would the other prominent families view the Qin clan?","Looking at his expression, Daili already knew the answer. \"It seems you didn't.\"","\"They actually knew it was impossible too; bringing it up was merely a probe,\" Qin Shaozong said lightly.","If he agreed, the Wei family would naturally be delighted. If he refused, they could take a step back and make a relatively less excessive demand, which, given the situation at the time, he would find hard to reject.","Daili's eyes flickered. Thinking of the important matter the person had just mentioned, and connecting it to Qin Shaozong's attitude, she felt that Qin Changgeng probably already knew about that important matter, but he simply didn't want to handle it.","However...","\"Why are you telling me all this?\" Daili was baffled.","Qin Shaozong said meaningfully, \"My lady will have to know eventually.\"","Perhaps to make it convenient to treat Qin Yanzhou, the residence Daili moved into was not far from the Ding family's home.","After the two chatted for a few sentences in the carriage, it came to a halt.","They had sent someone ahead to inform them, so the main gates of the Ding manor were currently wide open. Ding Lianxi, who had returned with the convoy today, was standing in front of the gate with his parents and grandfather.","Qin Shaozong stepped out of the carriage first and reached out a hand, bringing Daili down as well.","\"Welcome, Your Grace.\"","\"Welcome, Your Grace.\"","Daili saw two men who looked somewhat similar to Ding Lianxi standing beside him. One was older than the other, but both were in excellent spirits.","The old man, who was in his seventies, had greying hair, a lean face, and gentle, clear eyes. He actually possessed an air of transcendent, immortal-like grace.","\"Elder Ding, there is no need for such formalities,\" Qin Shaozong personally helped Ding Lianxi's grandfather up. \"I have come today entirely for the illness of my young son. I hope you will do your utmost later and hold nothing back.\"","Daili paused, unable to resist looking at Qin Shaozong. The young man standing beside Daili also couldn't help but look at the man in front of them.","Qin Shaozong stood before the two of them. He was very tall, with a straight back and broad shoulders, looking like a mountain that could shield them from the wind and rain.","Even though he knew why his lord had come, hearing these words still made Ding Lianxi reveal a look of astonishment.","His young son?","The young master was the Marquis's son? Something seemed wrong...","After a moment of shock, the Ding family members quickly invited them inside.","Since they were anxious to seek medical help, they got straight to the point. The people in the main hall did not sit separately but gathered around a small table. Qin Yanzhou sat on one side of the table, and Ding Lianxi's grandfather, Ding Luying, sat on the other.","Qin Yanzhou described his condition to the old man in detail, including how the attacks felt, the frequency of taking the medicine, the color and smell of the pills, and even the age at which he first started taking them.","Hearing her son say he had been taking this kind of medicine since he was ten years old, Daili's vision went dark for a moment. A long arm wrapped around her waist at just the right time, holding her up and preventing her from collapsing.","Qin Shaozong glanced at the pale woman in his arms and instructed a maid nearby, \"Go pour a cup of hot tea.\"","Ding Lianxi didn't dare turn his head, only daring to steal glances from the corner of his eye. He thought to himself that the words of that stingy miser Jin Duole might actually have some accuracy to them.","The Marquis's estate might truly be undergoing a massive change.","\"...The first time I took that medicine, my heart beat very fast at first. My body grew hot, my mind became hyperactive, and it felt like a hot fire was burning in my blood. The second time I took the medicine was two months later. The symptoms were the same, except that in the end, all the heat seemed to converge in my abdomen.\" As Qin Yanzhou said this, he devoted a fraction of his attention to observing Daili beside him.","Seeing his mother's strange expression, he couldn't help but purse his lips.","Ding Luying, seeing him stay silent for a long time, took the initiative to ask, \"Young Master, what happened next?\"","For a healer, the greatest worry was a patient who wouldn't cooperate and hid things.","Daili was also anxious listening to this and called out to her son.","Only then did Qin Yanzhou continue his explanation.","Ding Luying asked, \"Young Master, do you have any of the medicine you previously took left over?\"","Qin Yanzhou shook his head.","Ding Luying didn't say anything further, only asking him to extend his hand so he could take his pulse.","Time slowly ticked by. No one in the main hall spoke, and it was so quiet you could hear a pin drop.","Daili felt as if layer upon layer of wet cloth was covering her face. Heavy and stifling, it smothered her nose, making every breath she took exceptionally difficult.","\"It is the Crimson Gall,\" Ding Luying said, withdrawing his hand.","Although Daili hadn't heard the rest yet, at this moment, those invisible cloths were suddenly lifted away significantly, and her breathing became smoother.","This old gentleman knew what it was!","This was much better than not being able to figure it out at all.","Ding Luying stroked his greying long beard. \"The Crimson Gall is a type of Gu worm that feeds on Cold Food Powder. And the pills you took previously, Young Master, were very likely Cold Food Powder.\"","Daili froze. She didn't even hear the maid who brought the hot tea calling her in a low voice.","Cold Food Powder.","Some people might not be very familiar with this name, but its other name was absolutely well-known to the world: Five Minerals Powder.","Five Minerals Powder was originally a traditional Chinese medicine prescription for treating stroke and typhoid fever, but it was later abused and became a death warrant for many.","Ding Luying continued, \"Cold Food Powder should not be used in large quantities. Those who take it for a long time are prone to confusion, tinnitus, palpitations, and a series of adverse symptoms.\"","Daili knew all of this.","Basically, no one who consumed Five Minerals Powder met a good end. With excessive minerals accumulating in the body, and perhaps even trace amounts of heavy metals, it would be a miracle if one could live a long and peaceful life.","Daili hurriedly asked, \"Elder, you just said that the Gu worm called Crimson Gall feeds on Cold Food Powder. Does that mean the residual accumulation of Cold Food Powder in my son's body is not much, and the worm and the host have reached a balance?\"","Ding Luying replied, \"I can only say it is a precarious balance. If the Crimson Gall is starved for a long time, it secretes a venom. All of the young master's previous discomforts were caused by this venom.\"","Qin Shaozong took the teacup from the maid's hands, stuffed it into Daili's hands, and said casually, \"Then just continue taking the Cold Food Powder to feed the worm so it stops causing trouble.\"","Daili couldn't help but glare at him.","Is Cold Food Powder something one can consume so recklessly?","\"My Lord, this method is ill-advised. Cold Food Powder is a drug, after all, and every drug harbors a trace of poison. Over the years, the young master's foundation will inevitably suffer lasting damage,\" Ding Luying said, shaking his head.","Qin Shaozong replied, \"Then we extract it.\"","Ding Luying fell silent for a moment. \"A Red Gall parasite has a lifespan of twenty years. Whenever its life nears its end, or when it starves to the brink of death, it enters an entirely new state. It begins to frantically devour its host's flesh and blood, attempting to convert them into nourishment to prolong its own life. If left unchecked, within half a year, the host's intestines and stomach will be gnawed clean through, and they will die in agonizing torment.\"","As those last words fell, Daili's heart seized in a painful spasm.","\"Then... old sir, do you have a way to remove the parasite?\"","Ding Luying knitted his hoary brows. \"There is a way. However, from what this old man can see, the Red Gall was implanted in the young master's body at a very early age. Coupled with what appears to be a highly irregular feeding pattern, its lifespan has been cut significantly shorter than others of its kind. It has already entered its final, frenzied stage, and has been in it for quite some time.\"","Daili opened her mouth to speak, but only a breathless gasp escaped her lips.","Qin Shaozong then said, \"Since there is a way, I must trouble you to go ahead and extract the parasite, old sir.\"","Ding Luying replied, \"The extraction itself is not difficult. The problem lies in the vast array of medicinal ingredients required. Some of these herbs grow in the south, while others are found in the west; they are scattered far and wide. And the young master's Red Gall only has three months left.\""]},{"number":96,"title":"Chapter 96","paragraphs":["Without delay, Ding Luying had a servant fetch paper and a brush, and began writing down the medicinal ingredients right then and there.","He did not write it all in one breath. Instead, he paused frequently, sometimes frowning in thought before continuing, and occasionally going back to cross out a certain herb after some deliberation, replacing it with another.","Daili watched with her heart in her throat.","Although the old gentleman didn't say it explicitly, she could sense that he hadn't helped anyone remove a Gu worm in recent years, perhaps even for over a decade.","Otherwise, why would he need to think so much?","Please, please don't write down the wrong ingredients. A tiny error could lead to a disastrous outcome...","It took about half an hour just to finish the first sheet of mulberry paper.","Ding Luying switched to a new sheet and continued.","Qin Shaozong picked up the first page. He was not well-versed in Chinese medicine, so he was merely counting at this point. There was a total of fifteen herbs on the paper; some sounded familiar, while others he didn't recognize at all.","Hu Bao, come over and make a copy, Qin Shaozong called out to Hu Bao, who was waiting outside.","Hearing this, Hu Bao sat down to the side, picked up a brush, and began to write.","Daili held a teacup in her hands. The warm tea was held until it lost its heat and turned cold, without its owner taking a single sip.","Qin Shaozong tapped the outside of the cup with a bent finger. Seeing that the tea was completely cold, he smoothly took it from her and handed it to a maid. Go change this for a fresh one.","The maid withdrew.","Qin Shaozong said in a low voice, Madam, do not worry too much. Ever since Xianshi became well-known among merchants across the world, traders coming to the North have been in an endless stream. These are just medicinal herbs; even if there are many types, it doesn't matter. We will manage to gather them all.","But there are only three months left, Daili said, fraught with anxiety.","Because that Chidan worm had an irregular diet, its lifespan was much shorter than others of its kind. It only had three months left, and if they couldn't successfully extract it, it meant Zhou Zhou also had only three months to live.","However, right after she spoke, Ding Luying shook his head. Madam, the Chidan has three months left, but the young master cannot wait that long. At the latest, all ingredients must be ready in two and a half months, leaving the remaining half month for the worm removal process.","Daili's face instantly paled significantly.","It wasn't three months; there were actually only two and a half months to prepare the medicine.","She suddenly remembered something. Back when they were passing through Dahong County in Jizhou, she received a message from the Qinglian Sect for the first time.","The medicine of Yanzhou can only be resolved by us.","They didn't say poison, nor did they say worm. The other party used the word medicine.","At the time, she thought this word meant poison, and that avoiding the direct term was a euphemism to gloss over the severity. But looking back now, it didn't just refer to the Gu worm; it also referred to the medicinal ingredients.","The other party had calculated that she would bring her son to the Ding family for medical help, knew the lifespan of the Chidan inside Zhou Zhou, and even anticipated that the required herbs would be scattered far and wide, making a two-and-a-half-month collection period likely insufficient.","That was the reason behind the arrogant phrase, can only be resolved by us.","Thinking about it this way, when her son initially secretly refused to take those divine medicines, the other party probably saw it all along but never exposed it from start to finish.","They let it happen, using it as a punishment for his capriciousness.","Daili gritted her teeth, her heart bleeding with hatred. From north to south, the distance is more than a thousand miles. A round trip, plus the time needed to find the herbs...","As she spoke, Daili became somewhat dazed. If only there were airplanes here, traveling back and forth between the north and south in a single day wouldn't be a problem.","Her voice was not loud. Only Qin Shaozong and the maid returning with fresh tea heard her.","Hearing this, the maid looked up in astonishment. Just as she glanced at Daili, a sharp, cold gaze from the side fell upon her. In that instant, it felt as if a biting winter wind had brushed her face, making her hair stand on end.","The maid hurriedly lowered her head, not daring to look further. The weight in her hands lightened as the teacup was taken away.","Qin Shaozong said, You may leave.","Suddenly, a teacup was placed in Daili's hands. The tea was at a perfect, warm temperature. The heat transferred over, warming her icy fingers until they felt cozy.","Qin Shaozong spoke to her again, After Xianshi was introduced, merchants from the Great Yan, and even foreign traders from the Western Regions, frequently visited the North. It isn't cost-effective to come with empty carriages, so they inevitably bring many goods up north. Some items might be sold out along the way, but many are transported all the way here. Southern medicinal herbs might not be impossible to find in the North.","Daili lowered her eyes, looking at the gently swaying liquid in the cup. With his reassuring words, the restless heart in her chest finally settled down a bit.","Suddenly, a flurry of footsteps echoed from inside, and a person hurriedly emerged from the inner side corridor.","He was dressed simply, clearly a servant.","Master...","Seeing that there were quite a few people in the main hall, and that three generations of the host family were present, the servant immediately realized that distinguished guests had arrived at the estate.","He suddenly became hesitant, but subconsciously took two steps forward. Clearly, the matter he needed to report was extremely important in his mind.","We will discuss other matters later, Ding Lianxi said initially.","The servant hesitated and whispered, But the guard captain inside said this matter is urgent and ordered me to report it without fail.","Ding Lianxi shuddered.","The guard captain inside meant the Xuanxiao Cavalry.","Back when they learned that the young master had been afflicted with a strange poison, the Marquis had dispatched a squad overnight to rush back to Yuyang, tightly protecting the entire Ding household.","These guards arrived just in time. Almost a few days after they took their posts, the Ding family faced their first brazen nighttime assassination attempt.","The Xuanxiao Cavalry were all highly skilled and successfully cut down all the assassins. After that night, blatant assassinations decreased, occurring only once more, followed by a frequent series of minor accidents.","What is it? Ding Lianxi asked.","The servant said, Somehow a stray cat slipped into the kitchen. It took a bite of the fish bought today and collapsed in convulsions.","As the servant spoke, Daili, holding her teacup, didn't react in time. She was still in the mindset of Zhou Zhou should be saved, let me have some tea to calm my nerves, and lowered her head to take a sip.","As a result, just as the tea entered her mouth and before she could swallow, a large, dark hand suddenly reached over and spread open, cupping her cheek. Forcing Daili to lower her head, long fingers applied pressure through her skin and pried her jaws open.","Because her head was lowered, the tea flowed out before it could reach her throat.","Daili spat the tea all over Qin Shaozong's hand. Because they were standing close, some of the tea also splashed onto his black robe and boots.","His movement was incredibly fast, and he also knocked over the teacup in Daili's hand. The tea Daili spat out hit the ground almost at the same time as the teacup.","Clang! The cup shattered on the floor, the sound exceptionally abrupt in the main hall.","Qin Yanzhou was sitting with his back to Daili and didn't know she had just been drinking tea.","However, having earlier heard Qin Shaozong ask the maid to bring tea, and then hearing the Ding family servant's report, his first reaction was to turn around and look at Daili. He happened to see the scene of Qin Shaozong forcing her jaws open and her spitting water all over his hand.","The originally tense young man relaxed a little, but still asked, Mother, did you swallow any?","Daili also realized the tea might be poisoned. She pushed Qin Shaozong's hand away and coughed reflexively a couple of times. No, I didn't have time to.","Qin Yanzhou relaxed completely.","Beside them, Ding Lianxi was left dumbfounded. Not only him, but neither his parents nor his grandfather had recovered their wits; they all stared in astonishment at Daili and Qin Shaozong, whose robes were now stained with water.","Under the gaze of many, Qin Shaozong turned a blind eye. He calmly took a handkerchief from the pouch at Dai Li's waist, wiped the tea from his hands, and brushed off his robe.","He called Ding Lianxi by his courtesy name, asking, \"Congjian, do poisonings like this happen often?\"","Ding Lianxi quickly snapped back to attention, \"Not often. Counting just now, it has only happened twice before. The Ding family has practiced medicine for generations and is highly sensitive to the scent of medicinal herbs. If anything else is added to our food, we can notice the anomaly just by smelling or taking a small sip. Moreover, after some herbs are steamed or boiled, their toxicity is far less potent than before.\"","Dai Li said thoughtfully, \"So poisoning is useless against you.\"","If it wasn't aimed at the Ding family, then it was aimed at... them.","The Green Lotus Sect knew they would seek medical help immediately upon arriving in Yuyang, so they staged this?","Dai Li looked down at the shards on the floor, thinking that the tea was probably not poisoned; the poisoned item was likely just the fish. As for the cat, it was deliberately let into the Ding residence.","This was a reminder, or rather, a warning.","Qin Shaozong suddenly whispered to Dai Li, \"Madam, the people of the Green Lotus Sect harbor evil intentions and are full of tricks. They are by no means on the righteous path.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","By the time the servants had cleaned up the broken cup, Old Mr. Ding had finished writing down all the medicinal herbs.","A full three pages. The latter two pages didn't have as many varieties as the first, but perhaps due to their high value, the less common herbs on the latter pages had their specific quantities marked.","Ding Luying put down his brush, \"Young Master, starting tomorrow, I will administer acupuncture for you every other day to suppress the Chidan's activity as much as possible.\"","Qin Yanzhou stood up and bowed deeply to the old man in front of him, \"Thank you, Old Mr. Ding.\"","It wasn't proper to stare at that beautiful lady, but it was fine to look at this young man. Ding Luying had lived for many years, but this was the first time he had seen such a handsome young man.","Perhaps because he had practiced martial arts for a long time, his movements were vigorous, his back was straight, and his temperament was tough. Even though his face was as flawless as jade, there was not a trace of effeminacy.","Like a sharp, beautiful blade.","No one dislikes beautiful things and people, so Ding Luying was quite accepting of treating him.","Removing the parasite wasn't difficult for him; the hard part was gathering all the medicinal herbs. If the treatment was delayed due to incomplete ingredients, he couldn't be blamed.","However, there was one thing he had to explain in advance...","Ding Luying said seriously, \"Marquis, the breeding conditions for a Gu worm like Chidan are quite harsh and uncommon. The reason I know of it is because fifty years ago, I traveled south to Jiaozhou with my elders and happened to learn about it in a small mountain village. As for where that village is now, I can no longer remember.\"","After fifty years, many memories had faded.","Especially for a medical fanatic like Ding Luying, he remembered what he had learned, but if you asked him the exact location, who taught him, or who else was around, he had forgotten it completely.","But looking at the young master's current condition, that small mountain village back then likely had followers of the Green Lotus Sect, or even served as a high-level hideout.","Qin Shaozong understood his implication: \"No matter. Old Mr. Ding only needs to focus on removing the worm.\"","...","The discussion of important matters came to a temporary close. At sunset, Qin Shaozong, Dai Li, and her son left the Ding residence.","With the incident of the poisoned cat, the Ding family didn't dare ask them to stay for dinner.","They could taste the poison, but that didn't mean others could. When dining with such distinguished guests, they would surely have to invite them to take the first bite. If anything happened, they couldn't escape the blame.","Qin Shaozong had no intention of eating at the Ding residence anyway. The manor had prepared a fresh fish soup for her, and he missed the stir-fried pork. They would go home and eat their own food.","When they left, the entire Ding family saw them to the door. Qin Shaozong first helped Dai Li onto the carriage. Just as he was about to board, he seemed to notice something and sharply turned his head.","About sixty or seventy feet away, a man wearing a cross-collared short jacket and a headband met Qin Shaozong's gaze.","Probably not expecting to be suddenly discovered, and by the Marquis of Wu'an himself, the man was startled and instinctively turned his head away.","His exaggerated movement only served to give himself away.","With the cat poisoning fresh in his mind, Qin Shaozong was furious. \"Hu Bao, catch him.\"","Hu Bao had also seen the man. Without a word, he dashed over. Seeing this, the man immediately fled, but Hu Bao caught up and sent him crashing to the ground with a flying kick.","Hu Bao dragged the man back in less than a minute. Qin Shaozong didn't even look at him, boarding the carriage without a word.","The carriage wheels rolled over the setting sun as it returned to the Qin Manor.","Upon returning, Qin Shaozong called Jin Duole over. \"Jin Duole.\"","The heavy utterance of his name made the refined military instructor's heart skip a beat.","His superior treated military and civil officials differently. He would casually call out the full names of the former and even curse at them sometimes, but for the latter, he usually used their courtesy names.","Calling him by his full name right off the bat was something Jin Duole hadn't experienced in a very long time.","Jin Duole immediately turned serious. \"Marquis, what important matter do you have to command?\"","Qin Shaozong placed the three sheets of mulberry paper on the desk. \"For these three lists of medicinal herbs, spare no manpower or financial resources. They must be fully collected within two months. Do you understand?\"","When he said this, Qin Shaozong spoke slower than usual, emphasizing the words \"financial resources\" and staring unblinkingly at Jin Duole, revealing a rare solemnity and seriousness.","Jin Duole's narrow eyes widened slightly, instantly realizing that for this task, the Marquis would not tolerate his usual stinginess. He quickly bowed and replied, \"This subordinate understands. Please rest assured, I will strictly follow your orders this time.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"Report back to me in ten days. Go and send Qiao Wangfei in.\"","Jin Duole agreed, took the lists, and left in a hurry.","A moment later, Qiao Wangfei entered. \"Marquis, you were looking for me.\"","As winter approached, the sky darkened faster. The sunset had been brilliant when they returned, but now the sky was mostly dark.","The tall and sturdy man sat behind the desk. The afterglow slipped in through the window and fell diagonally across him, using his straight nose as a dividing line between light and shadow. \"Madam once saved your life. Do you remember?\"","Qiao Wangfei immediately said, \"I will never forget her life-saving grace.\"","Qin Shaozong took out another list.","Unlike the complete list given to Jin Duole, if Ding Luying were here, he would definitely recognize that this list consisted entirely of herbs not found in the North.","Qin Shaozong spoke openly, \"Some of the herbs on this list grow in the South, while others are in the East or West. They are all needed to treat the Madam's son's stubborn illness. Tomorrow, go to the army and select a group of soldiers, and lead them yourself to collect the herbs. I don't care what methods you use—whether you buy them from merchants along the way or split up to go to where the herbs grow. In short, you must return with the collected herbs in at most seventy days.\"","Qin Shaozong knew well that besides leveraging gratitude, he had to provide incentives. \"When you return, you will be rewarded with five hundred taels of silver, a grand mansion, and a hundred acres of fertile land. The soldiers who travel with you will each receive fifty taels, and for every herb collected, their reward will increase by ten taels each.\"","Nowadays, a single cow costs no more than two taels of silver. A two-courtyard house in a small county town sells for a mere twenty taels.","Fifty taels is a massive fortune to many people, yet Qin Shaozong was essentially giving away the equivalent of two houses right off the bat.","Not to mention the five hundred taels Qiao Wangfei stood to receive.","Qiao Wangfei knew his superior had always been generous and never mistreated those of merit. However, this was the first time such a large sum of silver had been promised before the task was even accomplished.","\"My lord, you need not reward me with silver. I owe Lady Dai my life, and I am more than willing to run errands for her,\" Qiao Wangfei said hastily.","The ray of sunset that had slipped into the study gradually faded, and the face of the man behind the desk was swallowed by the shadows. \"Take it since it is given to you. Go now. Leave the city and return to the suburban barracks to select your men before the curfew. You depart first thing tomorrow morning.\"","Hearing the unquestionable tone in his voice, Qiao Wangfei cupped his hands in obedience. \"This subordinate will do his absolute utmost to complete the mission, so as not to fail Lady Dai's great kindness.\"","Qin Shaozong left the study and entered the main courtyard, arriving just in time as dinner was being served in the room. The delicious, savory aroma of fish soup drifted out, whetting the appetite.","Qin Shaozong quickened his pace. Without needing anyone to invite him, he took a seat right next to Dai Li.","Seeing him arrive, Dai Li reached for the soup ladle. Before her fingertips could even touch the wooden handle, a pale, scarred hand reached over.","\"Mother, let me.\"","Dai Li smiled, not stopping her son from helping to serve the soup.","Qin Yanzhou first served a bowl for Dai Li, then ladled one for Qin Shaozong, and finally served himself.","Just as the soup bowls were set down, approaching footsteps sounded from outside. It turned out to be Hu Bao.","\"My lord, the man who was spying on us earlier claims to be a servant of the Wei family. How should we deal with him?\"","As he finished speaking, Dai Li could not help but cast a glance at Qin Shaozong."]},{"number":97,"title":"Chapter 97","paragraphs":["Previously, Dai Li didn't know about the Wei family, but after hearing him mention it in the carriage, she knew now.","The Qin and Wei families were related by marriage. Even though the Wei family's daughter had passed away from illness over ten years ago, with the Qin family's growing power, the Wei family must have kept in constant contact with them over the years. Their relationship was certainly closer than that of other prominent families.","As for sending someone to observe in secret, Dai Li guessed it might be related to the \"important matter\" mentioned by the Commandery's Chief Clerk during the day.","These thoughts spun in her mind, but Dai Li just treated it all as gossip. His affairs had nothing to do with her.","Holding the fish soup her son had served her, Dai Li leisurely blew on it, brushed aside the chopped green onions on top, and slowly drank the soup.","The freshly stewed fish soup was incredibly delicious, with shredded ginger added. In this cooling autumn season, a bowl of fish soup warmed her entire stomach.","\"Detain this person for a period of time first. Keep a strict watch and do not let him contact the outside world.\" Qin Shaozong's long fingers tapped twice on the desk. \"Next time, there's no need to report matters concerning the Wei family during mealtimes.\"","Hu Bao paused for a moment, bowed with cupped hands to receive the order, and retreated.","The Wei Family.","Wei Congmu and his third younger brother, Wei Congsen, waited in the main hall, occasionally looking toward the main gate.","They had waited from early afternoon until sunset. They had drunk over a dozen pots of tea, made several trips to the latrine, paced back and forth in the main hall over a dozen times, and even played several games of chess.","From the bright sunshine, to the sun setting in the west, and finally to the complete descent of night, they still had not seen the figure of their servant returning.","\"Eldest brother, the curfew has arrived. Logically speaking, he should have returned by now. But there is still no sign of him. Could something unexpected have happened? Could he have been discovered?\" Wei Congsen said worriedly.","Hearing this, Wei Congmu looked anxious, but gradually, his anxiety settled into deep thought. \"At that time, I sent someone to secretly follow the Marquis of Wu'an, and found that they went to the Ding family. I waited outside for half an hour and still didn't see them come out, so I left someone behind to wait. The Ding family has practiced medicine for generations. With the Marquis of Wu'an staying at the Ding family for so long, could it be that he really suffered severe injuries in the south?\"","Wei Congsen gasped, taking in a breath of cold air. \"Now that the Marquis of Wu'an has detained our man, does it mean he is unwilling to let the news leak? To make him this cautious... Eldest brother, could it be that the Marquis of Wu'an doesn't have much longer to live...\"","Wei Congmu's body trembled.","The more Wei Congsen spoke, the more he felt it was possible. \"I heard that when the Marquis of Wu'an led the army into the city today, he didn't ride a horse either. When did he become the kind of man who would choose a carriage over riding a horse? He has been going to the battlefield with his father and brothers since he was a teenager. In the past, even when injured, he would still ride his horse back to the city, never willing to show weakness. How could a habit of decades suddenly change?\"","\"But when I saw him today, his voice didn't sound weak. I stood by the carriage and took a glance inside; his complexion was normal, and there was even a beautiful concubine in the carriage. No matter how you look at it, he doesn't seem like someone with one foot in the grave.\" Despite saying this, the doubts in Wei Congmu's heart continued to deepen.","\"Could the beautiful concubine be a smokescreen? I've never heard of him traveling with a beauty before,\" Wei Congsen guessed.","Wei Congmu stroked his beard, finding it hard to make a decision for the moment. \"But that young woman is indeed as beautiful as a celestial fairy. Let alone within Yuyang Commandery, I'm afraid there is no one who can surpass her in the entire North.\"","Wei Congsen hadn't seen her and felt his eldest brother was exaggerating.","What kind of person was the Marquis of Wu'an? While he certainly appreciated beauty like any other man, he was fundamentally an extremely rational man, even quite cold towards women.","In his early years, he once had a favored concubine surnamed Han. At that time, the Wei family's daughter had already died of illness, and there was no main wife in the estate, making her the most prominent figure. In terms of the allowances for the women in the estate, Concubine Han ranked second, closely following Second Lady Qin.","However, it was later discovered that this woman was a hidden spy sent by Ji Province.","As for how it was discovered, it was because Concubine Han delayed sending messages to Ji Province. Ji Province sent another group of people to investigate, accidentally exposing their tracks, which led to Concubine Han being exposed.","It was rumored that the reason Concubine Han took no action was because she later fell in love with the Marquis of Wu'an and was unwilling to continue hurting him as Ji Province's hidden blade.","The Marquis of Wu'an hated betrayal and deception the most, nor did he like women interfering in his political affairs. After the fact that Concubine Han was a spy was exposed, she disappeared from the Marquis's estate.","Some said the Marquis of Wu'an remembered their past affection and couldn't bear to kill her, merely driving her out of the estate; others said Concubine Han died. From the moment the spy matter was exposed, her identity was no longer just a woman, but an inside agent for Ji Province.","And when it came to dealing with inside agents from other provincial factions, the Marquis of Wu'an naturally had his own set of protocols.","Wei Congmu said, \"It is still too early to draw conclusions now. We'll observe again tomorrow.\"","Upon observing, Wei Congmu saw the Marquis's estate acquiring medicinal herbs with great fanfare.","Soldiers poured out in full force, heading to various medical clinics in the commandery to massively purchase medicinal herbs.","In addition to this, merchants coming to the North were not spared either. Any merchant caravan carrying medicinal herbs was stopped. The soldiers took a list to make their selections first, then left behind silver and money before swaggering off.","Medicinal herbs flowed into the Ding family's residence like water.","At the same time, a carriage drove out from the Ding family. Someone saw that the driver was a personal guard from the Marquis's estate. In the moment the carriage curtains were blown up by the wind, some people also said they saw that old gentleman from the Ding family with the most exceptional medical skills.","This was a huge deal. Rumors immediately spread throughout the commandery, and people became panic-stricken.","Some people stated with absolute certainty that the Marquis of Wu'an had been hit in a vital spot by a poisoned arrow on the battlefield, which was why he didn't ride a horse when entering the city, but stayed in a carriage the whole time.","Others said that the Marquis of Wu'an was indeed injured, but his life was not in danger, and his unwillingness to ride a horse was simply because he wanted to accompany the beautiful concubine inside the carriage.","Opinions varied widely, and there was no definitive conclusion.","Many people turned their attention to the Marquis's estate, observing the actions of the two young masters. And amidst all these open and secret gazes, a carriage drove out from the Marquis's estate.","\"My Lord, the Eldest Young Master requests an audience,\" Hu Bao reported.","When Hu Bao arrived, Qin Shaozong was in the main courtyard, looking over a list together with Dai Li.","Qin Shaozong said, \"Let Yunce come over.\"","Hearing about the Eldest Young Master, and then hearing him directly ask the person to come over, Dai Li said to Qin Shaozong, \"I'll go check on Zhou Zhou.\"","Just as she stood up, her arm was grabbed by a large, dark hand. Qin Shaozong pulled her back, and Dai Li sat back down on the chair, ending up even closer to him than before. \"Madam, do not go disturb Old Mister Ding. In case it distracts him and he accidentally inserts the needle in the wrong place, having to redo the needle is a minor issue, but that boy being mistakenly pricked in the wrong acupoint is a major matter.\"","Dai Li immediately showed her dissatisfaction. \"You absolutely must not say things that doubt a doctor's medical skills in front of the old gentleman. No, actually, you shouldn't ever say such things again.\"","It was already not easy for him to agree to treat the illness, yet he dared to doubt the man's medical skills!","Qin Shaozong chuckled, \"Alright.\"","Dai Li still wanted to leave. This time, she didn't look for other excuses, but stated it plainly, \"Your eldest son is coming to see you. It's inappropriate for me to continue staying here. I'll go take a stroll in the back garden.\"","Qin Shaozong didn't let go. \"What is inappropriate about it?\"","Dai Li struggled with her hand a bit. \"You father and son haven't seen each other for a long time. You definitely have a lot to talk about, and it might even involve military secrets. I won't get involved.\"","\"Madam is already my advisor. What secrets are there that you cannot listen to?\" Qin Shaozong curled his lips.","Dai Li choked on her words for a moment.","Qin Shaozong added, \"You have even become good friends with Nalan Wugong. He has not talked politics with you any less, has he? And as for Qiao Wangfei and the others, you told them to interact more with that boy and take him along for morning exercises, and they agreed faster than you could blink. Tell me yourself, Madam, where have you not meddled?\"","Dai Li was speechless.","Back then, she used the strategist as an arrow to poke him, never expecting it to become a boomerang one day.","\"Then I have other important matters to attend to.\" Dai Li stood up again.","Qin Shaozong leaned lazily against the soft chair, resting one hand on the armrest to prop up his chin, while his other hand held onto her tightly. \"The important matters Madam speaks of, could they be tinkering with the broken grass and tree bark you had people collect this morning?\"","Dai Li was speechless once more.","How could reeds and paper mulberry bark sound so awful coming out of this man's mouth?","Dai Li clicked her tongue lightly. \"Qin Changgeng, do not underestimate these things. Using them as materials, you will only need to blow a single breath to start a fire.\"","The principle of the fire starter was to preserve a spark by depleting oxygen. Both paper mulberry bark and reeds contained rich fibers, making them excellent combustibles. As soon as new oxygen entered the bamboo tube, the spark would instantly flare up.","It was a pity that sweet potatoes had not yet appeared, otherwise sweet potato vines would have worked even better.","Once the fire starter was invented, having hot pot and barbecue would be much more convenient in the future.","...","Not far away, at the entrance of the main courtyard.","Qin Yunce stopped in his tracks, wondering for a moment if he was dreaming. Otherwise, why would he hear a young woman directly calling his uncle by his courtesy name, and his uncle, instead of being angry, actually wearing a rare smile on his face?","\"Eldest Young Master, please,\" Hu Bao said, gesturing with his hand.","His voice not only snapped Qin Yunce back to reality but also alerted the two people sitting by the window in the main room.","Qin Yunce composed himself and entered the courtyard at a steady pace, then stepped into the main room. He stopped a few steps away from the long desk, cupped his hands, and bowed. \"Your son pays his respects to Father, and congratulates Father on your triumphant return.\"","The young man stood sideways to the sunlight, wearing a white robe with a gold-trimmed crossed collar, his figure appearing quite thin.","\"Yunce is here.\" Qin Shaozong pulled Dai Li back to the seat beside him, making her sit with him.","Qin Yunce raised his head, then lowered his gaze. With great restraint, he avoided looking at Dai Li and instead focused on Qin Shaozong's hand resting on the desk. \"Father, there have been many rumors in the commandery recently, all saying that you were injured on the battlefield and are now in critical condition. Do you need your son to send people to stop these rumors?\"","Before seeing the man himself, he had indeed been deeply worried, fearing that his uncle was truly severely injured as the rumors claimed, perhaps even at death's door.","But just now at the courtyard entrance, he had clearly heard his uncle speaking with a strong and resonant voice, even having the mood to joke with a young woman. It was definitely nothing serious.","His heart settled back into his chest.","While Qin Yunce spoke, Dai Li observed this young man, who was wearing a white robe similar to her son's.","He must have inherited his father's physique, being quite tall, around eight chi. His posture was rather lean, and his face carried an unhealthy pallor, making it hard to tell if he was recovering from a recent illness or had been frail since birth.","Dai Li felt that he only resembled Qin Shaozong around the nose; the rest of his features bore no trace of him.","Compared to Qin Shaozong's ruggedness and sharpness, the young man's appearance was much gentler. His skin was pale, his contours soft, and his features far less aggressive.","If Qin Shaozong was a mighty longsword that had just drunk blood and awed all directions, the young man was like a porcelain cup illuminated by the morning sun, somewhat fragile, somewhat warm, and possessing a touch of leisurely elegance. He gave off a very comfortable impression, completely devoid of any invasiveness.","Qin Shaozong was fully aware of the matters outside. \"There is no need to worry about the rumors for now. Let the storm brew for a few more days.\"","After briefly brushing over the outside situation, Qin Shaozong brought up another topic. \"Have members of the Wei family visited the Qin residence recently?\"","Qin Yunce nodded. \"Before your return, they came a total of four times. The first two times, Aunt visited looking for Qinian. Seeing that Qinian was not there, she went back. The third time, Eldest Uncle came to visit, and he spoke to me about the conflict between Second Uncle and the Cai family. The fourth time Eldest Uncle came to the door again, I did not see him.\"","A few days ago, the conflict between the Cai and Wei families had caused an uproar in the city. Disputes between prominent families were common, and Qin Yunce initially thought nothing of it.","Until, his younger brother, who had been grounded by their uncle for a long time and forbidden from stepping into the military camp, suddenly went to the suburban barracks, and was even brought there by Yan San. Not long after his brother left the estate, Aunt Wei came to the door looking for Qinian.","Qin Yunce acutely sensed an unusual atmosphere.","This premonition rapidly intensified when his brother did not return to the city for a period of time afterward, so he began to intentionally or unintentionally avoid contact with the Wei family.","When they sent greeting cards, he claimed to be ill and refused to see them. Since he had never been very healthy anyway, claiming illness did not seem abrupt.","\"You do not need to pay attention to the Wei family's affairs. I have my own arrangements,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Qin Yunce smiled and nodded. Just as he was about to say something, a gust of wind blew in from outside, and he could not help but cover his mouth and cough, taking a long time to stop.","Qin Shaozong frowned. \"How is your health recently? Old Mr. Ding is in the estate now. Have him take a look at you later.\"","Qin Yunce slowly exhaled. \"Thank you for your concern, Father. I am completely fine. Coughing when exposed to the wind is an old ailment; wearing more clothes will suffice. Moreover, I have been continuously taking the warm tonic prescribed by Old Mr. Ding previously, so there is no need to trouble him again.\"","Qin Shaozong also knew that this nephew's poor health was not a matter of just a day or two.","His eldest sister-in-law went into labor early with her first child, and Yunce was born prematurely, making his constitution weaker than ordinary children.","Later, his blood brother died in battle on the battlefield. While he was busy dealing with the traitors to avenge his brother, he failed to notice, and his eldest sister-in-law, who had been childhood sweethearts with his brother and deeply in love after marriage, committed suicide for love.","The nephew, who was already old enough to remember things at the time, suddenly lost both parents. He suffered from insomnia and continuous high fevers, narrowly surviving. From then on, he completely became a medicine pot.","Qin Shaozong insisted, \"It is better to have a look. He is in the estate anyway. Since you are already here, stay for dinner today before going back.\"","Qin Yunce obediently nodded.","Qin Shaozong changed the subject and suddenly introduced Dai Li. \"Madam, this is Qin Yunce, my eldest son. He is nineteen, the same age as that boy Qin Yanzhou. You can just call him Yunce.\"","Then he looked at Qin Yunce. \"This is my Madam, surnamed Dai, as in the distant mountain Dai. You must not be disrespectful to Madam in the future.\"","Qin Yunce was shocked. Putting aside the myriad of thoughts that flashed through his mind at that moment, he simply cupped his hands and bowed to Dai Li again.","Qin Shaozong's hand was still resting on Dai Li's arm, as heavy as a thousand catties, not giving her the slightest chance to stand up.","Dai Li fully accepted Qin Yunce's bow without returning it at all.","Later, when Qin Yanzhou returned from his treatment, he saw an extra person in the courtyard. Through introductions, he learned that it was Qin Shaozong's eldest son. The two younger generation members met for the first time and exchanged greetings.","Just as Dai Li had expected, her son was very indifferent and spoke pitifully little. It was rare for him to meet someone of the same age, but he showed no intention of making friends, treating it entirely as just knowing the name of one more person.","Dai Li sighed in her heart.","The four of them sat around the table and had dinner together.","That evening, after a comforting bowl of fish soup, Qin Yunce rode his carriage back to the Marquis Manor, a pleasant warmth lingering within him.","As night fell, the glowing lanterns of countless households flickered out one by one.","In the dead of night, when the world was swallowed by a single blanket of darkness, a silhouette vaulted over the wall as nimbly as a cat, slipping silently into the estate where Dai Li resided."]},{"number":98,"title":"Chapter 98","paragraphs":["The figure seemed quite familiar with the layout of the mansion. After vaulting over the wall, he headed straight for the main courtyard without pausing for a moment.","Tonight, it was Bai Jianping's turn to lead the night watch. Knowing he had to stand guard, he had intentionally slept his fill during the day, so he was full of energy now that night had fallen.","Unable to sit idle, he led his men on a patrol around the premises. Just as he turned the corner of a long corridor, he caught a glimpse of a dark shadow darting past from the corner of his eye.","Alarm bells instantly rang in Bai Jianping's head.","An assassin!","This assassin was incredibly bold, actually daring to scale the walls and attempt an assassination right here in Yuyang, the Marquis's own stronghold.","Hah, what arrogance! Today, he would show this fool that even nine lives wouldn't be enough to spare him!","Bai Jianping immediately drew his longsword and charged over. \"How dare you cause trouble in your grandpa's mansion! Die, you scoundrel!\"","Bai Jianping took the lead; the soldiers holding torches couldn't keep up with his speed. In the darkness, his longsword swept out with a wind-breaking force, but the figure nimbly ducked to evade the strike.","Bai Jianping let out a cold snort. Just as he was about to slash again, he suddenly heard—","\"Uncle Bai, don't hit me, it's me!\"","Bai Jianping shuddered and forcefully halted his attack, stumbling as he withdrew his sword. At that moment, the soldiers bearing torches arrived from behind.","The firelight dispelled the darkness, illuminating the young man's rebellious face, which still carried a hint of childishness.","\"Third Young Master, why are you here? Didn't the Marquis tell you to stay at the military camp in the outskirts?\" Bai Jianping gasped after speaking. \"The city gates are already closed at this hour. Don't tell me you scaled the city walls to get in?\"","\"My father is dying, how could I not come?\" Qin Qinian tossed back these words as he hurriedly ran toward the main courtyard.","Bai Jianping froze. By the time he reacted and tried to say it wasn't true, the boy had already disappeared from sight.","He suddenly felt a headache coming on. Knowing this was a huge misunderstanding, he couldn't help but mutter, \"Why do all these young masters like to climb over walls at night? Young Master Qin has done it twice, and the Third Young Master is no stranger to it either.\"","*","Main Courtyard.","When he heard the sound of footsteps outside, Qin Shaozong, who was resting on the bed, woke up. In just a few breaths, his mind became completely clear.","For someone to come rushing to report at night like this, it must be something urgent. Could it be that something happened to the Ding family...","There was no knock on the door; the intruder vaulted directly through the window. The moment his feet hit the floor, the man on the bed snapped his eyes open, swiftly sat up, and reached for the small cabinet beside the bed.","There was a short dagger on top of it.","His fingertips had just brushed against it. Before Qin Shaozong could draw the blade, the intruder suddenly let out a wail:","\"Your son is unfilial, your son is late! Father, you must hold on. Eldest Brother definitely doesn't want to inherit your title at such a young age. Father, tell your son who did this...\"","Qin Qinian had been smelling medicine all the way here. After climbing through the window, grief overcame him, and he couldn't hold back his tears.","His mother had passed away before he was even two years old, so he had no memory of her face.","His father was an important and busy man, spending little time raising them and disciplining them strictly. But this did not stop them from watching their mountain-like father achieve great merits time and time again. When he stood before them like an insurmountable benchmark, profound admiration and filial love bloomed from the bottom of their hearts.","Yet now he was told that this great mountain was about to collapse! How... how could he accept this...","Qin Qinian threw himself onto the footstool by the bed, ready to tend to his sick father. However, in the darkness, his hands pressed against a firm and muscular calf.","Qin Qinian was stunned.","Before he could figure out what was going on, the long leg broke free from his grasp and immediately delivered a kick to his shoulder. The kick was not light; it sent Qin Qinian tumbling backward.","\"You truly are an unfilial brat,\" Qin Shaozong said, the veins on his forehead bulging.","Having just gone through a session of lovemaking tonight, Dai Li was exhausted and had fallen asleep the moment her head hit the pillow. Yet, halfway through her slumber, she was jolted awake by an earth-shattering howl.","At first, she thought it was an assassin who had sneaked into the room and, upon being caught, was begging Qin Shaozong for mercy to spare his life.","But as she groggily listened to the rest, Dai Li realized it wasn't an assassin.","The flint clicked, and an oil lamp was lit in the room.","Qin Shaozong looked at the young man a short distance away. He was dressed in a black and red martial outfit, his face was smeared with dirt, and a few stray blades of dry grass were stuck in his hair. A fire of irritation flared up in Qin Shaozong's heart.","He wasn't dead yet, but this little brat was already acting like he was mourning at a funeral.","Qin Qinian remained sitting on the floor, staring blankly at Qin Shaozong a few steps away.","His father was wearing only a pair of black trousers, his upper body completely bare. The faint light of the lamp fell upon him, clearly highlighting the defined muscles of his chest and abdomen, as well as his two strong arms. His dark skin was cast in a bronze hue by the firelight, faintly gleaming with a robust vitality.","He sat imposingly by the bed, gripping a short dagger in his hand, exuding a murderous aura like an enraged tiger whose rest in the forest had been disturbed.","There was not a single wound to be seen on him; only faint red marks that looked like scratches were visible on his body.","After blinking blankly, Qin Qinian's grief vanished, instantly replaced by overwhelming joy. \"Father, you're fine! That's wonderful, the rumors outside were all false!\"","\"Get out,\" Qin Shaozong said with a dark expression, setting down the dagger.","Qin Qinian didn't want to leave. His father had been away from Yuyang for nearly a year, and he had so much to say to him.","Dai Li had been abruptly woken up in the middle of the night by a loud voice wailing right off the bat, making her head buzz. Having her sleep interrupted naturally put her in a bad mood. Seeing that these two didn't seem likely to quiet down anytime soon, Dai Li simply decided to chase them out.","\"Qin Changgeng, go talk outside. I want to sleep.\"","A woman's voice suddenly rang out in the room, causing Qin Qinian's eyes to widen in shock.","His father was actually sharing a bed with a woman?","What shocked him even more followed right after. A snow-white bare foot extended from behind the bed curtains, kicked lightly a couple of times, and finally planted itself against the side of his father's waist.","The ankle, which bore bright red marks, tensed with visible small veins, clearly exerting no small amount of force as she single-mindedly tried to kick the man out.","Qin Shaozong turned slightly, grasped Dai Li's calf, and tucked it back under the quilt. \"My lady, go back to sleep. I will return shortly.\"","Dai Li rolled over and looked out through the light, sheer bed curtains. She saw a figure sitting on the floor. His face wasn't clear, but judging from his loud, hoarse voice, he was likely still going through puberty.","Probably fifteen or sixteen years old. In modern times, that would be the age of someone just starting high school.","Qin Shaozong stood up from the bed. Too lazy to put on a shirt, he simply walked over, grabbed the back of Qin Qinian's collar with one hand like he was picking up a cat, and dragged him toward the door.","\"Father...\" Qin Qinian's voice was much quieter than before.","Creak. The door opened.","Qin Shaozong was just about to toss the boy out, but unexpectedly, another person was standing in front of the door.","A tall, slender young man stood with his back to the moonlight, bathed in a cold and aloof aura. He held a sword in his hand, looking astonishingly sharp and icy.","He had come to catch a thief.","Over there, the mansion guards led by Bai Jianping arrived holding torches. The firelight instantly illuminated this small area of the main courtyard, lighting up the dirt-covered Qin Qinian and the scantily clad Qin Shaozong, who carelessly laid bare a body covered in marks.","Bai Jianping knew he had arrived late and pleaded guilty to his superior. \"This subordinate failed to stop the Third Young Master in time just now. Please forgive me, Marquis.\"","Qin Shaozong tossed the person in his hands outside. \"Disturbing people's sweet dreams deep in the night. If you have something to say, say it tomorrow. Qin San, next time you enter a room, knock on the door. If you dare to climb in through the window again, I will break both of your legs.\"","Lifting his long, narrow eyes, Qin Shaozong swept his gaze over the crowd. \"Nothing is wrong, everyone go back.\"","Bai Jianping cupped his hands in obeisance and led the men away.","Qin Qinian's mood swung wildly. It was good that his father was fine. As for being kicked and tossed out just now, he had thick skin and tough flesh since childhood; to him, it didn't hurt or itch at all.","\"Bang.\" The door to the main room closed.","Without a target, Qin Qinian had to withdraw his gaze. It was only then that he saw an unfamiliar face.","The moonlight fell upon that jade-like face, as if reflecting a delicate and flawless jade carving. His features were handsome, possessing the awe-inspiring aura of a military man.","Qin Qinian was stunned as he looked, and his voice couldn't help but soften a bit. \"Who, who are you?\"","Hearing him being called \"Qin San\", Qin Yanzhou knew this was Qin Shaozong's third son. The scene from just now flashed through his mind, and right now, he didn't want to speak to this son of the Marquis of Wu'an at all.","Qin Yanzhou turned around expressionlessly and returned to his room.","\"Hey, hey, don't leave!\" Qin Qinian subconsciously followed him.","*","Inside the main room.","Qin Shaozong got back into bed and scooped Dai Li, who had rolled to the other side wrapped in the blanket, back into his arms.","Dai Li was still awake. Hearing the \"Hey, hey, don't leave\" from outside, she couldn't resist saying to Qin Shaozong, \"Qin Changgeng, this son of yours is like a beagle.\"","\"What is a beagle?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","Dai Li fell silent for a moment.","How should she explain this? She couldn't very well say that a beagle was a type of dog, implying his son was like a dog.","\"Madam?\" Suddenly not getting a reply, he started to tease her.","Dai Li turned her head, only letting his kiss land on the side of her face, while reaching out to push him. \"A beagle is a type of energetic, very noisy, and frequently howling... creature.\"","Qin Shaozong raised his long eyebrows slightly, pondering what kind of thing howled like that, but couldn't figure it out.","However, that boy Qin Qinian was indeed noisy, and he had a loud voice. Since he was little, he ran wild everywhere. Climbing trees to dig out bird nests today, climbing onto the roof to rip off tiles tomorrow; even beatings couldn't make him behave.","Qin Shaozong said in a deep voice, \"That boy's biological mother is Lady Wei. The Wei family has recently stirred up trouble and wants to use the Qin family's hands to settle it. They attempted to contact Qin San to act as a middleman. I threw him into the military camp ahead of time and forbade him from returning to the city to prevent the Wei family from contacting him. Qin San probably heard some rumors, thought I was injured, and hurried back from the outskirts late at night.\"","Dai Li's expression shifted slightly.","She didn't know if it was an illusion, but she seemed to hear a storm brewing in the first half of Qin Shaozong's words.","He said the Wei family stirred up trouble. Although Dai Li wanted to enjoy the gossip, the Wei family was a sensitive topic, so she didn't take the initiative to ask what trouble they had caused.","\"Go to sleep.\" Dai Li shrank back into the blanket.","Qin Shaozong chuckled softly.","*","Having slept late last night and waking up once in the middle, Dai Li slept until the sun was high in the sky today before getting out of bed.","By the time she was fully dressed and walked to the outer room, she heard someone talking outside:","\"What's your name? Why are you here?\"","\"Hey, hey, you look really handsome, only slightly worse than me. Your martial arts are truly not bad. Could it be that you're my father's guard?\"","\"But that's not right either. Why would a guard live in the main courtyard?\"","\"What's with the scar on your neck? Was it from killing enemies on the battlefield? I have several on my back too, a full seven inches long.\"","\"Why aren't you saying anything?\"","The familiar, raspy drake-like voice kept ringing out incessantly.","Veins popped out on Qin Yanzhou's forehead. Unable to bear it any longer, he said, \"Stop being so noisy.\"","Qin Yanzhou felt a bit of regret in his heart. Had he known this person was so difficult to deal with, he absolutely wouldn't have sparred with him during morning practice, no matter what Bai Jianping and the others said.","As soon as he spoke, Qin Qinian actually became even happier.","He knew his own voice wasn't pleasant to listen to. Now that he had met a \"kindred spirit,\" it was hard not to be happy.","...","Dai Li came out of the room and saw two figures standing at the entrance of the courtyard from afar.","Her son was dressed entirely in white, expressionless, still wearing a \"strangers keep away\" demeanor.","The youth beside him, wearing a black and red color-blocked martial arts outfit, was more than half a head shorter than him.","Compared to Qin Yunce, Dai Li felt that this young boy was more similar to Qin Shaozong. The lower halves of their faces were about seventy percent alike. It was just that the inner corners of the boy's eyes were a bit rounder, making him look more like some kind of small animal with wet eyes that would wag its tail.","She hadn't guessed wrong last night. The young boy looked to be around sixteen years old, exactly the age of being lively and restless.","He seemed to be a social butterfly, and also appeared to have some military habits ingrained in his bones. Right now, he kept wanting to put his arm around Zhou Zhou's shoulders, but every time he reached out, her son accurately dodged him.","Hearing the sound of the door opening, the older and the younger both looked over at the same time.","Dai Li saw a subtle change on her son's iceberg-like face. He rarely showed a bit of gloominess, and his eyes carried a different kind of meaning: Mom, can I hit him?","Dai Li: \"...\"","Qin Qinian knew last night that there was a lady in his father's room, but he hadn't seen her in person. Now, seeing Dai Li for the first time, he completely froze in place.","The lady not far away was dressed in a fragrant-leaf-red crossed-collar ruqun. She had a red dot between her eyebrows, and her skin was like first snow, beneath which flushed a vibrant, life-filled rosy complexion.","She was born with an extremely outstanding pair of peach-blossom eyes. Her gaze rippled, resembling a touching ripple under the setting sun, and also like a speck of frost over a raging fire, making it hard for people to approach her easily.","\"Mother, did he disturb you?\" Qin Yanzhou shook the person off and walked toward Dai Li.","Dai Li shook her head. \"No, I slept until I woke up naturally today.\"","Qin Qinian was snapped back to his senses by the address \"Mother\". He looked at Dai Li, then at Qin Yanzhou. After going back and forth like this twice, he was shocked to realize that their facial features were extremely similar, as if cast from the same mold.","This lady was actually mother and son with this guy who was so good at fighting!","\"Your mother is so young and beautiful!\" Qin Qinian said involuntarily.","Qin Yanzhou's gaze shot over like ice, but seeing that he was just purely amazed and full of praise, with no lustful greed in his eyes, he restrained his sharp aura.","Dai Li patted her son's arm, telling him not to be impulsive.","She had already met his eldest son Qin Yunce and had even accepted his greeting. Right now, facing another younger one, she just treated him like an ordinary child. \"Have you two had breakfast yet?\"","Both of them said they had eaten.","Qin Qinian was still looking at Dai Li, his gaze filled with unconcealed curiosity, feeling that this favored concubine was very unusual.","Not only did she stay overnight in his father's room, she even dared to use her feet last night. The key was that after kicking someone, she was actually safe and sound.","Dai Li simply pretended not to notice. \"Are you not returning to the military camp today?\"","Qin Qinian was astonished. \"How did you know I came from the military camp?\"","Dai Li didn't hide it. \"Your father said so.\"","Qin Qinian felt even more that Dai Li was unusual, but he answered truthfully, \"Father told me to stay in the manor for the time being.\"","\"Then you have nothing to do.\" Dai Li guessed he was also bored out of his mind, otherwise he wouldn't have caught Zhou Zhou and kept talking continuously. \"Since you have nothing to do, how about you come with me to make a casing for a fire starter?\"","\"What is a fire starter?\" Qin Qinian was puzzled.","Dai Li explained to him, \"You can understand it as an upgraded version of a flint. When you need to make a fire, you just need to blow gently to ignite the flame.\"","Hearing this, Qin Qinian's expression changed drastically. \"My father absolutely despises all this superstitious nonsense. I strongly advise you to mend your ways immediately. Otherwise, when he throws you out of the estate, you won't even have a place to cry.\"","Qin Shaozong returned just in time to overhear Qin Qinian blabbering this entire speech."]},{"number":99,"title":"Chapter 99","paragraphs":["Dai Li stood in front of the main room's door, facing the courtyard entrance. The two juniors faced her, their backs to the entrance.","Only she saw Qin Shaozong.","Across the distance, their eyes met lightly in the air.","There was no point in arguing with a kid of high school age. Although his tone wasn't great, his words could barely be considered a reminder, so Dai Li didn't say anything and just raised an eyebrow at Qin Shaozong.","\"Qin Qinian!\"","A heavy voice dropped from behind. Based on his years of experience getting into trouble and being beaten, Qin Qinian's back instantly stiffened, and his scalp went numb.","When his father called him by his full name, he was usually in for a disaster.","Qin Qinian reflexively spun around with a whoosh, his momentum instantly weakening. \"Father, I...\"","\"If I hear such bastardly words again, you won't need to go to the military camp anymore,\" Qin Shaozong said expressionlessly.","Qin Qinian was shocked. If he had just shown a drastic change in expression, revealing dissatisfaction and condemnation upon hearing Dai Li's \"heretical\" remarks earlier, now his face turned completely pale with fright.","This sentence terrified Qin Qinian more than the threat of breaking both his legs last night.","His father had always been a man of his word, doing exactly what he said. In all his years, he had never seen his father break a promise.","If he could say it, he would definitely do it.","Not letting him go to the military camp in the future?","He was someone who wanted to become a great general. Not letting him practice martial arts and lead troops was worse than killing him.","Terrified and anxious, Qin Qinian immediately hurried forward, muttering, \"Father, I know I was wrong, please don't forbid me from going to the military camp.\" He wanted to reach out and pull the corner of Qin Shaozong's clothes, but felt that this action was too much like a child acting spoiled, which was highly inappropriate.","Finally, his knees gave way, and he knelt in front of Qin Shaozong. \"Father, your son knows his mistake.\"","Qin Shaozong looked down at him from above. \"Are you apologizing to me?\"","Qin Qinian understood the underlying meaning of his words and hesitated for a moment.","One kneels to heaven, earth, ancestors, and parents. He could kneel to Qin Shaozong without hesitation, but he couldn't soften his knees for one of his father's favored concubines.","He lowered his head, stood up from the ground, walked up to Dai Li, and gave her a deep bow. \"I'm sorry. I spoke rudely just now, please don't take it to heart.\"","\"Alright,\" Dai Li smiled.","Looking at Dai Li's curled lips, Qin Shaozong remembered what his youngest son had just said, and he couldn't help but let out a cold scoff in his heart.","Kick her out of the manor, and she would have nowhere to cry?","Hah, he feared that the moment he let her out, she would laugh out loud right at the manor's gates, and then take that boy Qin Yanzhou and leave Yuyang that very day.","Qin Shaozong: \"Qin San, run twenty laps around the manor after the Shen hour today.\"","Qin Qinian quickly nodded.","As long as his father didn't mention forbidding him from stepping foot into the military camp, anything was fine.","Qin Shaozong looked at Dai Li, \"Madam, this is my third son, Qin Qinian, aged sixteen. This boy is full of energy and very noisy. I hope you will be patient with him. If you really can't stand him, a beating is fine too.\"","Full of energy and very noisy. These were exactly Dai Li's original words from last night, but only the two of them knew this.","Dai Li looked away.","Then, Qin Shaozong introduced Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou to Qin Qinian, casually mentioning that Qin Yunce had already come to pay his respects yesterday. His underlying message was to tell him to behave himself in the future.","Hearing that Dai Li's surname was \"Dai\", Qin Qinian blurted out, \"You are not a lady of the Wei family?\"","Dai Li was baffled. \"No.\"","Qin Qinian frowned and muttered, \"That shouldn't be...\"","He had never seen his father treat a woman like this, let alone formally introduce her to his eldest brother and him, and order him to pay respects to her in the exact manner a junior would greet an elder.","No matter how he looked at it, his father seemed to have some intention of taking a wife.","But his father had made a promise in his early years that his second wife must be a woman from the Wei family. If she wasn't a lady of the Wei family, wouldn't that mean she couldn't...","\"She will not be surnamed Wei,\" Qin Shaozong said lightly.","Dai Li didn't understand what riddle this father and son were playing at. Unable to figure it out, she simply stopped thinking about it and returned to the original topic of the fire starter. \"Zhou Zhou, come with me to make the fire starter.\"","She had strolled around the manor yesterday and found it excessively large, bigger than any place she had lived in Guoyun County or Bairi City.","In the back garden, besides flowers and jagged rocks, there was unexpectedly a small bamboo grove, and a square pavilion within it. What Dai Li had her eye on now were the bamboos in the grove.","She thought Qin Shaozong had returned to the main courtyard because he had business with his son, so she only called Zhou Zhou. But after she and her son walked out of the main courtyard, footsteps sounded from behind.","Dai Li turned around.","\"I have nothing to do, so I will go with you, Madam.\" Qin Shaozong took long strides and caught up with Dai Li in just a few steps, walking shoulder to shoulder with her.","Dai Li didn't mind.","Alright, come if you want. There will be an extra laborer later.","The group of four left the main courtyard, headed straight for the back garden, and walked into the small bamboo grove.","Bamboo is an evergreen plant. Even now, in the cool breezy autumn, except for the slightly yellowing leaves, it was mostly emerald green.","Dai Li walked around the bamboo grove and picked one of moderate thickness. \"This one is suitable. Break this one off.\"","Hearing this, Qin Yanzhou was about to draw his sword, but before the short blade was fully unsheathed, a voice popped up from the side:","\"Let me do it, let me do it!\"","Qin Qinian was very excited. The sixteen-year-old boy didn't know the meaning of quiet, nor did he understand a low profile; he was solely focused on showing off.","Dai Li pressed her son's arm, pushing the partially unsheathed blade back in.","Qin Qinian walked up to the bamboo Dai Li had chosen and started chopping away vigorously. As he chopped, his mouth didn't stop either.","This time, he didn't dare say anything about heretical ways anymore, and just asked, \"Lady Dai, you mentioned earlier that the fire starter only needs a blow to catch fire. Why is that?\"","Catching fire with just a blow—was it a breath of fairy magic?","Dai Li explained to him, \"Because fire needs oxy... needs air to burn. After covering it with a lid, the fire will die down to just sparks. Blowing on it is equivalent to adding fuel to the fire again, so the fire can burn up.\"","Qin Qinian was like a curious baby, \"Why won't those sparks completely extinguish?\"","\"Naturally, because of the materials,\" Dai Li answered.","Qin Qinian: \"Then what materials are needed?\"","Dai Li: \"Silvergrass flowers, paper mulberry bark, rosin, sulfur, and saltpeter, among other things.\"","Both saltpeter and sulfur are combustion-supporting, while the highly flammable rosin acts as an adhesive, binding the materials together.","\"If I bring all these to you, can you make a fire starter right away?\" Qin Qinian was itching with curiosity.","He felt that lighting a fire with just a blow was too mystical, and he wished he could see a fire starter today.","Dai Li poured cold water on his enthusiasm: \"Not quite. The silvergrass flowers and paper mulberry bark need to be processed for seven days. These two started drying yesterday, so we still have to wait six more days.\"","If there were a microwave or an oven, baking the materials would only take a few minutes. But if those two things existed, there would be no need for a low-end lighter like a fire starter.","Qin Qinian let out an \"Oh,\" his interest dropping a bit, but he quickly added, \"Then when you make the fire starter, can I come and see?\"","Dai Li said he could.","\"Why do you know so much?\" Qin Qinian continued to ask.","Dai Li: \"It's written in books.\"","Qin Qinian shrank his head almost imperceptibly. \"Then you are quite amazing to be able to read so many books. I can't do that; I can only be a great general.\"","\"Cut it here, it needs to be about this long,\" Dai Li gestured.","\"No problem!\"","While the two were talking, Qin Shaozong leaned against another thick bamboo stalk with his arms crossed, watching the three of them with a curled lip.","Qin Yanzhou standing to the side with a sword at his waist, Qin Qinian working hard to whittle the bamboo, and her, looking down at the bamboo with lowered eyes.","The cool autumn breeze blew through the square pavilion, lifting the hem of her sweetgum-red dress. The vibrant color looked like a warm, dazzling fire in the woods, radiating an endless stream of warmth and brightness.","Despite his chatter, Qin Qinian's movements were very swift. In just a few strokes, he chopped down the bamboo stalk Dai Li had pointed out, stripped away its leaves, and finally cut it into many small sections according to her instructions.","Dai Li took one to examine and said to Qin Qinian, \"Cut another small piece here to make a lid. Then, make a hole in the top of the lid. Don't make it too big; about the size of a soybean is enough.\"","The purpose of the hole was to preserve the spark. After all, if no air could get in at all, the tinder would go out.","\"Alright,\" Qin Qinian agreed readily.","The bamboo stalk was quite long. Cutting it into many small sections and turning each one into a little bamboo tube with a lid was no small task.","There was a square pavilion nearby, furnished with a stone table and chairs. Servants cleaned the furniture daily, ensuring they were spotless and looked brand new.","The group now moved their workspace into the pavilion.","There were quite a few small bamboo joints, about twenty or so. Qin Yanzhou also joined in the task of making the little bamboo tubes.","Both of the younger generation were skilled with knives. Working together, it did not take them long to fit all the little bamboo tubes with lids.","\"Everything is ready. Now we just have to wait for the silvergrass and paper mulberry bark to finish drying in the sun,\" Dai Li said, placing the small bamboo tubes into a basket.","Qin Qinian asked anxiously, \"Do we really have to wait six days? Would five days work?\"","\"No,\" Dai Li shook her head.","\"Alright. Father will not let me go out anyway.\" After saying this, Qin Qinian belatedly looked at Qin Shaozong, who was playing with a bamboo tube nearby. \"Father, why have you grounded me here?\"","He was still unaware that the Wei family had been looking for him several times.","Qin Shaozong seemed displeased. \"You are sixteen years old and still so flighty. What kind of behavior is this? You need to temper your character. Tomorrow, your eldest brother will also come to stay at the manor for a while. You will study with him.\"","Clack. The man tossed the little bamboo tube in his hand back into the basket.","The sound was not loud, but to Qin Qinian, it sounded like a bolt from the blue, followed by the sky collapsing.","Dark clouds gathered over Qin Qinian's head. He deeply regretted bringing the matter up.","If his father told him to stay in the manor, he should have just stayed. Why did he have to get to the bottom of it and ask why? He had really brought this upon himself.","Indeed, just as Qin Shaozong had said, Qin Yunce arrived in a carriage the next day.","Unlike the last time when he just had a simple meal, this time Qin Yunce brought his luggage. He rode in one carriage, followed by two other carriages carrying his belongings.","Many prominent families were watching openly and secretly. The more they observed, the more alarmed they became by the situation.","The Marquis of Wu'an had kept his doors firmly shut, and the trend of purchasing medicinal herbs was growing stronger, even spreading beyond Youzhou.","The eldest son of the Marquis of Wu'an even brought his luggage into the manor to tend to the sick. Some said his third son had also returned to the city overnight and had been staying in the manor to care for the sick without taking a single step outside.","Apart from the daughter who had married into another commandery, both sons had returned to tend to the sick.","This situation did not look good!","But regardless, since the other party lacked medicinal herbs, they had to show some gesture. Therefore, the major prominent families rummaged through their private storehouses, taking out the best medicinal herbs to send over.","The herbs were delivered, but naturally, they did not get to see anyone, nor could they pry out even the slightest bit of information.","Days passed one by one. In the blink of an eye, six days had gone by. Suddenly, a rumor sprang up from nowhere, saying that the Marquis of Wu'an had narrowly escaped death and his condition was gradually improving.","Some also said that since he had overcome the crisis, they should go and offer their congratulations. Regardless of whether they could see the Marquis of Wu'an in person, they needed to make their presence known again! They had to let him know they were constantly concerned about his safety.","Upon reflection, everyone felt this made sense.","Especially the Cai family, who had recently been fighting fiercely with the Wei family. They immediately opened their storehouse again, took out gifts, and set out in their carriages.","Qin Manor, the main courtyard.","\"Lady Dai, today is the sixth day!\"","Dai Li had just finished breakfast when she heard a raspy voice shouting outside.","The voice was unpleasant, but it was incredibly loud. Before the person had even stepped through the moon gate, the sound had already reached the main courtyard.","\"Hey, why are you pulling me? Your mother is definitely up by this time.\"","Dai Li walked out the door of the main room and saw two teenagers, one tall and one short, walking over from a short distance away.","The taller one seemed to want the shorter one to shut up, nudging him in the chest with his elbow in an attempt to distract him.","Seeing this, the shorter one suddenly got energetic. He stopped talking, immediately raised his hands to block, and began sparring with his companion as they walked. In just a few steps, they had exchanged several moves.","It was Qin Yanzhou who saw Dai Li first. He immediately stopped his hands. \"Good morning, Mother.\"","Hearing his voice, Qin Qinian also stopped at once and respectfully bowed to Dai Li with folded hands. \"Lady Dai.\"","He was holding a bag in his hand. As he bowed, the cloth bag hung down from his grip, and then was lifted slightly as he straightened up.","\"The weather has been quite nice these past few days. Not a single drop of rain has fallen, so the items are ready to be collected,\" Dai Li said, her gaze falling on the cloth bag Qin Qinian was carrying.","Sure enough, after she spoke, the youth happily opened the bag. \"I brought them all over.\"","The small bamboo tubes from before were kept in a little basket in the main room. As for the rest, such as the pine resin and sulfur, they had been stored elsewhere with the raw materials.","Now, Qin Qinian had brought everything over.","Dai Li said, \"Come inside.\"","Dai Li asked Qin Qinian to place everything on the table.","After being washed, repeatedly pounded, and sun-dried, the silvergrass and paper mulberry bark had formed a very stiff grass cake.","The pine resin, sulfur, and saltpeter had all been ground into powder. Dai Li sprinkled them over the grass cake and began to roll it up.","She rolled it up and then stuffed it into a small bamboo tube.","\"Is this all it takes?\" Qin Qinian craned his neck to watch from the side.","Whenever he unconsciously leaned too close to Dai Li, Qin Yanzhou would quickly reach out, grab the back of Qin Qinian's collar, and pull him away a bit.","Dai Li replied, \"It is done. Bring a piece of flint to light it.\"","Qin Qinian did not have any flint on him, so he immediately went to look for some upon hearing her request. Not finding any in the outer room, he entered the inner chamber.","But upon entering, he belatedly realized that this room bore very heavy traces of male presence.","A black robe and a leather belt with an animal-head buckle were casually draped over a wooden stand. In one corner of the room stood a sword rack, upon which rested a ring-pommel sword about five feet long.","In front of the dressing mirror were many wooden boxes, which were clearly a lady's jewelry boxes. On the table lay the lady's beautiful hairpins, alongside a jade archer's ring that was obviously worn by a man.","There had never been a moment when Qin Qinian realized more clearly that his father shared a bed day and night with a lady, their lives so intertwined that even the subtlest traces of their daily routines were mixed together.","There was an oil lamp on the small cabinet, with a piece of flint resting beside it. Qin Qinian withdrew his gaze, picked up the flint, and went outside.","Dai Li was not very skilled at using flint, so she simply let Qin Qinian light the fire.","With a sharp clack, sparks leaped onto the tinder roll.","Silvergrass and paper mulberry bark are incredibly rich in fiber. After being dehydrated, sun-dried, and mixed with sulfur and other materials, they ignite at the slightest touch.","Dai Li instructed, \"Just put the cap straight on.\"","Qin Qinian did as he was told. He swiftly capped it, and the flames were instantly extinguished.","Dai Li took the fire starter tube from his hand. She first peered through the small hole at the top, then pulled the cap back off.","Because it had been burned just moments ago, the tinder at the mouth of the bamboo tube was now covered in a charred black layer. Dai Li handed the fire starter to Qin Yanzhou and said, \"Zhou Zhou, come blow on this.\"","Qin Yanzhou paused for a moment, a faint glimmer lighting up his eyes. Under their watchful gazes, he took a breath and blew out.","As the current of air swept over it, the previously charred spot grew redder and redder until finally, like a blooming little firework, it burst into a warm, bright flame with a soft poof.","Qin Qinian was completely dumbfounded. It took him quite a while to finally stammer, \"It... it really can start a fire!\"","Qin Yanzhou was also stunned. When he came to his senses, he quickly turned to look at Dai Li. His eyes were shining, and the corners of his mouth curled up slightly. \"Mom, it lit.\""]},{"number":100,"title":"Chapter 100","paragraphs":["The main hall.","Qin Yunce was receiving guests. This was the third batch of visitors today, and the arrivals were from the Cai family.","Cai Yuan came to the Qin residence this time not only to offer gifts and express loyalty, but also for another matter.","Cai Pei of the Cai family died at the hands of Wei Conglin. Cai Pei was the Commandery Commandant they had painstakingly trained. That was a Commandery Commandant, the right-hand man of the Commandery Governor, with immense real power.","And just like that, he was gone.","There was still no news on who would fill the vacant position of Commandery Commandant.","Today, Cai Pei's eldest legitimate brother, Cai Yuan, paid a visit, both to seek justice for his younger brother and to see if he could bring this \"flower\" back to the Cai family.","However, the Marquis of Wu'an was ill, and it was the Eldest Young Master Qin who received him. To be honest, Cai Yuan was unsure of the outcome, but he still had to cry and complain as necessary.","So Cai Yuan first solicitously inquired about the Marquis of Wu'an's \"injuries,\" expressing his concern with utmost sincerity, and then, with tears streaming down his face, he tearfully recounted the crimes of the Wei family to Qin Yunce.","\"...Eldest Young Master, that Wei Conglin is insane. He actually dared to commit insubordination and murder his superior! According to the laws of the Great Yan, an official who murders his superior should receive sixty lashes and be sentenced to head-shaving, wearing an iron collar, and pounding grain for five years.\" Thinking of his brother's death, two lines of tears ran down Cai Yuan's face.","\"Originally, everything should have been dealt with according to the law, but the Wei family kept delaying handing him over, pushing it off time and again. Later, they were forced by the law and had no choice but to let Wei Conglin be imprisoned. But even so, they sent people to look after him in prison, making Wei Conglin comfortable, as if he were on vacation at a relay station.\"","\"Eldest Young Master, there is a saying, 'A prince who violates the law commits the same crime as a commoner.' Besides, Wei Conglin isn't even a prince; at most, he's a royal relative! My Cai family has closely followed the Marquis all these years. Could the Marquis, for the sake of the Cai family's loyal service, ask the prison officials to handle this impartially?\"","Midway through his speech, Cai Yuan could no longer sit still. He rose from his seat, lifted his robe, and knelt before Qin Yunce.","After finishing his words, he even knocked his head against the ground, performing a grand bow.","Sitting at the head, Qin Yunce looked at Cai Yuan below, remained silent for a moment, and seemed to sigh helplessly.","This sigh made Cai Yuan tremble with fear, afraid that Qin Yunce would later tell him to be forgiving wherever possible.","\"This matter involves the Commandery Commandant and the Division Commandant. It is of great importance, and it is difficult for me to make a decision. It just so happens that my father is in good condition today. Why don't you come with me to see him?\" Qin Yunce said.","Cai Yuan was stunned, and when he reacted, he was overjoyed. \"Good, good, good. Thank you, Eldest Young Master.\"","\"Follow me.\" Qin Yunce rose from his seat.","He led Cai Yuan out of the main hall, walked through a long corridor, and finally arrived at a courtyard with a very strong smell of medicine.","\"Commandant of Agriculture Cai, please wait here for a moment. I will go in and announce you first,\" Qin Yunce told him.","Cai Yuan nodded repeatedly.","He watched Qin Yunce go inside and waited anxiously outside. After about half a cup of tea's time, Qin Yunce came out of the pavilion courtyard.","Qin Yunce gestured with his palm, \"Commandant of Agriculture Cai, you may go in now. However, my father should not be exposed to the wind at this time, so please stand in front of the hanging curtain to speak with him, and do not enter the inner room.\"","Cai Yuan hurriedly straightened his clothes and hat, while saying, \"Understood. I will definitely keep the Eldest Young Master's reminder in mind.\"","He went inside. As soon as he entered, he smelled a strong odor of medicine. The inner room was piled high with medicinal herbs. Some were placed in cabinets, some on stacked multi-tiered wooden shelves, and there were even nails on the walls in the four corners of the room, hanging packets of medicine that hung straight down.","Cai Yuan had long known that Qin Shaozong was seriously injured. Seeing this now, he was not surprised, only thinking to himself that the rumors outside were true.","He stopped in front of the hanging curtain of the inner room. Regardless of whether the person inside could see him, he bowed deeply to the hanging curtain. \"This humble official, Cai Yuan, pays respects to the Marquis, congratulates the Marquis on his triumphant return, and wishes the Marquis peace and good health. This humble official shouldn't have disturbed you during your recuperation, but some people are truly using the Marquis's prestige to bully others. It's too much...\"","He appropriately brought a crying tone into his words, as if he had been driven to a dead end and was filled with grief and indignation.","\"Yunce has already mentioned a thing or two to me about this matter just now.\" A deep male voice came from inside.","Cai Yuan was slightly startled. Judging solely from the voice, the Marquis of Wu'an's vitality was still quite strong.","Could he be forcing himself despite his illness?","The man whom Cai Yuan thought was struggling to hold on was currently sitting boldly and confidently in front of a long desk, holding a booklet that had just been sent back from another province.","Outside, when Cai Yuan heard Qin Shaozong say that he had mentioned a thing or two, he suddenly felt it was highly necessary to recount the matter again.","So he tearfully complained to Qin Shaozong.","In the room, Qin Shaozong was doing two things at once. After the crying and complaining outside finished, he said, \"It is indeed wrong for Wei Conglin to murder his superior...\"","A bright light burst forth in Cai Yuan's eyes, but just as he was looking forward to what would follow, a coughing sound suddenly came from inside.","Cai Yuan's heart suddenly hung high.","A moment later, the person in the inner room stopped coughing, followed by a period of silence, seemingly trying to catch his breath.","Inside the room.","Qin Shaozong picked up a wolf-hair brush, quickly wrote a reply, and then set the small booklet aside.","After dealing with two letters in a row, the man finally spoke. \"The Wei family has indeed been somewhat carried away in their actions these past few years. Cai Yuan, as the Commandant of Agriculture, you are in charge of military agricultural colonies and grain cultivation. The Northern Army has consumed a great deal of grain and fodder in the campaign against the salt smugglers and the battle in Sizhou. Pay close attention to this year's autumn harvest.\"","Cai Yuan's pupils slightly contracted.","In officialdom, many things were not stated too clearly; a hint was enough. If there wasn't the first sentence about the \"Wei family,\" just hearing the second half, Cai Yuan would have thought the Marquis of Wu'an was urging him in his work.","But connecting the context, Cai Yuan immediately understood the implied meaning. The Marquis of Wu'an wanted him to start with the military agricultural colonies and cause trouble for the Wei family.","The amount of information contained here was too large, making Cai Yuan's head spin.","The Qin and Wei families were related by marriage. The Marquis of Wu'an had been a widower for fifteen years without remarrying. Outsiders, out of respect for this connection, usually yielded three points to the Wei family.","However, now, the Marquis of Wu'an himself had revealed a different intention.","It seemed the relationship between the Qin and Wei clans was not as good as it appeared. It made sense; as the Third Young Master Qin grew older, the Wei family had indeed become somewhat arrogant and conceited over the years.","Qin Shaozong continued, \"As for the matter of Cai Pei, let's put it on hold for now. I will deal with it after a while when my condition improves. You can go back first; I need to rest.\"","The order to leave had been given, and Cai Yuan did not dare to stay. He could only cup his hands again, say some auspicious words, and then leave the room.","Cai Yuan had entered with joy and excitement, but came out weighed down by anxiety.","The Marquis of Wu'an said that the matter of Cai Pei would be put on hold for now and dealt with later?","Combining the two sentences, did whether the outcome after the delay depend entirely on his effectiveness as the Commandant of Agriculture?","...","Inside the room.","The man who had just said he needed to rest finished processing the small booklet on the desk, got up, and left, showing no intention of resting at all.","He headed towards the main courtyard. After walking a distance, just as he reached the entrance to the main house's courtyard, he suddenly heard a high-pitched voice drifting out from inside—","\"What's the difference between this and summoning wind and rain? Lady Dai, you are too amazing!\"","The drake-like voice was highly recognizable, both loud and emotionally excited. It was the voice of his youngest son.","Qin Shaozong raised his long eyebrows and quickened his pace. Just as he entered the courtyard, he heard that gentle female voice:","\"The difference is still quite big. I have no way of summoning wind and rain.\"","Dai Li thought to herself that these two were not on the same level at all.","Calling the wind and summoning the rain, artificial rainfall.","The earliest artificial rainfall was in the mid-twentieth century. The gap between then and now was merely an airplane that could soar up to nine thousand meters and some dry ice.","From the corner of his eye, Qin Qinian caught a glimpse of a dark figure walking in from outside. He turned his head to look, and his eyes immediately lit up. Grabbing a fire stick, he ran out happily.","\"Father, look at this!\"","Qin Qinian held the object up in front of Qin Shaozong. \"The fire stick Lady Dai just made. It's quite magical; it only takes a single breath to ignite. When we are marching and fighting outside, lighting a fire will be so much more convenient.\"","Although flint wasn't hard to use, if they encountered wet wood or cloth, it definitely wouldn't light.","A fire stick was different; it could ignite with just a blow.","\"Father, watch.\" Qin Qinian pulled off the cap and blew a long breath at it, demonstrating for Qin Shaozong right then and there.","The charred head of the bamboo tube slowly turned red, and finally, under Qin Shaozong's gaze, a ball of fire burst forth with a whoosh.","Astonishment flashed through his brown eyes. Qin Shaozong took the fire stick from his son's hands. He had just seen Qin Qinian remove the cap and then blow air, so he put the bamboo cap back on and took it off a moment later.","The flame had disappeared.","But when a current of air brushed past, the sparks suddenly reappeared and quickly grew into a small flame.","Qin Shaozong abruptly raised his head to look at the main room.","The doors of the main room were wide open. She sat by the desk, currently talking to that boy Qin Yanzhou.","Sunlight slanted into the room, sweeping an extremely beautiful stroke of color onto the floor. That touch of color stretched all the way until it touched the woman's skirt, which spread out like flower petals, painting it with brilliant, multicolored hues.","Seeming to sense his gaze, the woman in the room turned her head.","Her eyes were pitch black, like black pearls soaked in a cold spring, clear and translucent, even more moving than the light diffusing on the floor.","Dai Li only felt an exceptionally burning gaze land on her. She tilted her head and met those brown eyes. She paused for a moment, then looked away as if nothing had happened, simply pretending she hadn't seen the emotion in his eyes.","Dai Li was talking to her son.","Today was the eighth day since they had returned to Yuyang Commandery. On the very day they returned, they had gone to the Ding family to seek medical treatment.","On the second day, Ding Luying came to perform acupuncture on Zhou Zhou.","Not counting the acupuncture session they were going to have later today, since arriving in Yuyang, her son had already received acupuncture from the old gentleman three times.","Dai Li asked, \"You've already had three acupuncture treatments. Compared to before, Zhou Zhou, did you feel a bit more comfortable on the night the Gu worm acted up?\"","She remembered her son saying that every ten days, there would be one night where he felt particularly unwell, with dizziness, ringing in his ears, and abdominal pain, making it completely impossible to sleep.","Qin Yanzhou nodded. \"It's a bit better. My head isn't as dizzy, and the sound of the insects chirping and fluttering their wings is much softer.\"","He didn't mention any improvement in his abdominal pain. Dai Li knew that this aspect had likely not changed. Her heart ached, yet she was helpless.","\"Mother, acupuncture can't achieve results overnight. It's already better than before,\" Qin Yanzhou comforted his mother.","\"The fire stick you made is quite ingenious,\" Qin Shaozong said as he entered the room.","Just as Qin San had said, when used in marching and fighting, this item could prove immensely valuable on rainy days. Moreover, being just a small stick, it was very light and extremely convenient to carry.","Dai Li said casually, \"Did you think I was lying to you before? It is naturally much more convenient than flint.\"","Only replying to Qin Shaozong with this single sentence, Dai Li's topic shifted back to her son. \"Old Mr. Ding should have arrived at the manor. Zhou Zhou, I'll go over with you.\"","The previous times, Dai Li had also escorted her son to get medical treatment, and today was no exception.","Dai Li had initially thought that Qin Shaozong returned to the room because he had business, but after she and her son left the main courtyard, she heard footsteps behind them.","Dai Li turned her head and saw the father and son following behind. The man behind her quickened his pace upon seeing her look back, and in the blink of an eye, he was walking side by side with her.","The corridor wasn't narrow, so three people walking side by side couldn't be considered crowded. But as they walked, Qin Yanzhou fell behind and walked with Qin Qinian.","Qin Shaozong didn't speak, and neither did Dai Li.","Behind them, Qin Qinian was chattering away with Qin Yanzhou. No, it couldn't really be called a conversation; it was a long, one-sided output from him, asking about this and that. The latter was extremely annoyed by him, responding with a word or two as if they were made of gold.","As if encouraged, Qin Qinian continued to pester Qin Yanzhou with talk.","Dai Li's eyelashes slowly lowered.","The golden sun was behind them, casting the figures of all four forward. Walking in pairs, each pair had one shadow that was longer and the one beside it shorter, possessing a similar harmony.","When Dai Li arrived at another small courtyard, Old Mr. Ding had just arrived.","\"Marquis.\" Ding Luying cupped his hands and bowed to Qin Shaozong. As he bent down, he concealed the astonishment in his eyes.","Counting today, he had come to the Qin manor a total of four times to perform acupuncture on that young master. And out of those four times, the Marquis of Wu'an had actually personally accompanied him three times.","\"Old Mr. Ding, there is no need for such formalities.\" Qin Shaozong gently supported the man back up. \"I leave Yanzhou in your hands.\"","Acupuncture required taking off one's clothes, and sometimes bloodletting was done depending on the situation. Having outsiders present would interfere with the doctor's work, so it was inconvenient for Dai Li to follow them inside.","\"Father, what illness does Qin Yanzhou have?\" Qin Qinian hadn't been able to figure it out for several days.","Previously, he thought those medicinal ingredients were for his father, used to sustain his life, but later he discovered that wasn't the case at all.","The one who needed the medicinal ingredients was someone else entirely.","Qin Shaozong cast a sidelong glance at his younger son, knowing that this boy's mouth had no filter, just like Mo Yanyun. Furthermore, he was naturally active, and it was hard to guarantee that he wouldn't sneak out later, unable to bear the loneliness.","\"He wasn't focused while practicing martial arts and accidentally sustained internal injuries,\" Qin Shaozong casually made up an excuse.","As soon as these words fell, Dai Li's dissatisfied gaze shot over.","Qin Shaozong: \"...\"","Fine, not a single bad word could be said about her precious son.","...","With a blade of grass dangling from his mouth, Qin Qinian wandered aimlessly around the manor.","He was so idle that he was panicking, so idle that his entire body felt uncomfortable.","His father had issued a ban, forbidding him from leaving the manor. Fine, if he couldn't go out, he wouldn't go out. He would play inside the manor.","But after a few days of wandering around all the places he could, Qin Qinian gradually began to feel bored.","He thought to himself what a pity it was. It was a pity that Qin Yanzhou, whose martial arts were very impressive, had to be treated for an illness and couldn't fight him without holding back. Otherwise, he couldn't even imagine how thrilling it would be.","\"If I don't spar with Qin Yanzhou, I can at least find those squad leaders of the Xuanxiao Cavalry, right?\" Qin Qinian muttered. Immediately, he changed direction and headed towards another courtyard.","Most of the high-ranking military officers under Qin Shaozong's command had their ancestral roots in Youzhou.","They had their own houses in Yuyang, but everyone knew that it was currently a special period—the Marquis was critically ill, so everyone was temporarily staying here.","Even if they left the manor to return to their own homes, they generally wouldn't stay for long.","Qin Qinian went to two courtyards in a row, only to find them empty. He secretly thought it was strange; if Uncle Bai and the others weren't staying in their own courtyards, where did they go?","Qin Qinian continued walking forward and vaguely heard some movement ahead.","\"Please save me! Ever since I moved in here, I haven't had a single peaceful night's sleep. Every day, as soon as I close my eyes, I start having nightmares, dreaming that the matter has been exposed.\"","\"Lao Mo, you deserve it! Who told you to run your mouth?\"","\"I... I didn't know Lady Dai would take it seriously...\"","Hearing this, Qin Qinian pricked up his ears.","Lady Dai took it seriously? Took what seriously?","Something wasn't right. Was there actually something in this manor that he, the future Great General, knew nothing about?"]}]);
